   "book_page": "百五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二 (鹿兒島)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Satsuma / Kagoshima (鹿兒島藩): land assessment and fiscal totals",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka and major fiscal aggregates",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the land-and-fiscal page (fascicle 2) for the Satsuma domain, entered under its castle-town name Kagoshima (鹿兒島藩). It records a 草高 (assessed yield) of 869,594 koku, broken into 775,364 koku of productive land and 29,487 koku of loss-adjusted land, with 261,057 koku of current rice on hand (現石) — the totals explicitly exclude Ryūkyū tribute. Alongside the grain figures it lists Satsuma's signature trade goods, above all sugar (砂糖) at 5,092,825 units, along with paper mulberry (楮), raw wax (生蠟), and tea seed, plus a miscellaneous tax in copper coin (雜稅銭) of 159,796."
  },
  {
   "id": "satsuma_demographics",
   "sequence": 2,
   "domain_canonical": "薩摩藩",
   "domain_en": "Satsuma",
   "domain_hi_name": "鹿兒島藩",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 89,
   "page_side": "R",
   "table_number": 2,
   "book_page": "百五十二",
   "image": "images/upper_p089_right.jpg",
   "page_topic": "demographics — population, households, shizoku / ashigaru-and-below counts",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二 (高知) — 鹿兒島藩データ",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Satsuma / Kagoshima (鹿兒島藩): population and status classes",
   "page_summary_en": "This page gives Satsuma's demographic register: a total population (人口) of 896,808 in 174,528 households (戸數), split into 469,468 men and 427,340 women. Of these, 43,119 households and 192,949 persons are 士族 (samurai households) — an unusually high roughly 22% share, reflecting Satsuma's rural-samurai (gōshi) system — while the 足輕以下 (foot-soldier-and-below class) accounts for 107,738 households and 579,405 people. A separate Ryūkyū sub-block records its tribute rice (8,669 koku) and its own households and population. The register is large enough that it runs on from the Satsuma leaf onto the adjacent Kōchi (Tosa) page."
  },
  {
   "id": "satsuma_military",
   "sequence": 3,
   "domain_canonical": "薩摩藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鹿児島藩",
   "domain_en": "Satsuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p163_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 163,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百貳",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八 (鹿児島)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Satsuma / Kagoshima (鹿兒島藩): officials and military (undisclosed)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "officers + military, with explicit non-disclosure annotation",
   "page_summary_en": "In the officials-and-military volume (fascicle 8), Satsuma's entry is a blank: under the ○鹿兒島藩 domain-boundary marker the register carries only the phrase 書ナラス (\"not disclosed\"). The troop counts printed to the right of that marker — 1,568 rank-and-file, 1,106 officers, 464 corps members, and the councillor tallies — belong to the neighbouring Kanazawa domain that shares this leaf, not to Satsuma. Where nearly every other domain itemised its forces, Satsuma reported nothing, making it the most opaque military presence in the 1870 survey."
  },
  {
   "id": "choshu_kokudaka",
   "domain_canonical": "長州藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山口藩",
   "domain_en": "Chōshū",
   "image": "images/upper_p193_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 193,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 (山口)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Chōshū / Yamaguchi (山口藩): land assessment and taxes",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka components + combined high",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the land-and-tax page (fascicle 5) for the Chōshū domain, entered under its capital Yamaguchi (山口藩). It records a 草高 (assessed yield) of 369,411 koku plus an 外高 (new-field uplift) of 618,593 koku, giving a 合高 (combined assessment) of 988,004 koku. The main land tax (正租) is stated as 206,910 koku of current rice (現米) together with 116,190 in copper coin, supplemented by a miscellaneous rice tax (雜稅米) of 14,553 koku and smaller taxes in silver and on wax and coal. Chōshū's population figures appear on the facing page.",
   "sequence": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "choshu_demographics",
   "domain_canonical": "長州藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山口藩",
   "domain_en": "Chōshū",
   "image": "images/upper_p193_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 193,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 (山口)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Chōshū / Yamaguchi (山口藩): households and status classes",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "status-class households + population (with M/F)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page is Chōshū's status register (not a full commoner census), laid out in two horizontal bands. The upper band gives 17,714 households (戸數) and a population (人口) of 66,463, with status sub-counts including 3,000 士族 (samurai) households and 11,589 persons, 3,991 卒族 (lower-retainer) households and 10,362 persons, and 6,157 陪臣 (rear-vassals). The lower band records religious and outcaste groups — 1,165 Buddhist temples (寺院), 92 mountain ascetics (山伏), and 2,675 穢多 (outcaste-caste) households — each population figure carrying its own male/female split.",
   "sequence": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "choshu_officials",
   "sequence": 6,
   "domain_canonical": "長州藩",
   "domain_en": "Chōshū",
   "domain_hi_name": "山口藩",
   "image": "images/lower_p204_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 204,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（山口）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Chōshū / Yamaguchi (山口藩): senior officials",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Chōshū (Yamaguchi) senior domain officials: governor and the three councillor ranks with named appointees",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the opening (right-hand) page of Chōshū's entry in the officials-and-military volume (fascicle 9), marked by the ○山口藩 domain-boundary symbol. Read right to left, it names the domain's senior officialdom: one 知事 (governor), Mōri Motonori; two 大参事 (senior councillors); five 権大参事 (provisional senior councillors); and seven 少参事 (junior councillors), each rank listing its count and its named appointees. The small rifle-corps block of 80 men (銃隊) printed to the right of the ○山口藩 marker is a military overflow belonging to the preceding domain that shares this leaf, not to Chōshū. The junior-councillor list and the full military register continue onto the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "choshu_military",
   "domain_canonical": "長州藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山口藩",
   "domain_en": "Chōshū",
   "image": "images/lower_p204_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 204,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九 (山口)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Chōshū / Yamaguchi (山口藩): army and navy",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "army + navy (17 battalions, 4 warships)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries Chōshū's military register (fascicle 9), a striking contrast to Satsuma's blank entry. The land force is 17 infantry battalions (拾七大隊) of 433 men each — 7,361 infantry in all — with 6½ artillery batteries and one 93-man cavalry company. The navy is four wooden steam warships, each listed with its earlier foreign name: 第一丁卯丸 (ex-Penta), 第二丁卯丸 (ex-Asonda), 鳳翔丸, and 乙丑丸 (ex-Conchin). The domain-boundary marker and the senior officials are on the facing right half; the tail of the 権少参事 (provisional junior councillor) roster also appears here.",
   "sequence": 7
  },
  {
