   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（高知）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — end of Tosa (山內藩) and opening of Kameoka (龜岡藩)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Tail of Tosa's demographic register (a small supplementary household/population block) ending at the ○山內藩 boundary marker, then the opening kokudaka/tax columns of the next domain, ○龜岡藩 (Kameoka).",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half of leaf 155 (fascicle 2) spans a domain boundary. At its right edge the ○山內藩 marker closes the Tosa (Yamauchi) entry with a small supplementary block of just 602 households and about 2,810 people, broken out by samurai and lower-retainer households, shrines, and temples — this is a minor tail, not Tosa's main population, which appears on the facing page. The rest of the leaf is the opening of the next domain, ○龜岡藩 (Kameoka), a 50,000-koku domain: it records a 草高 (assessed yield) of 57,204.7 koku (including a 7,204.7-koku new-field addition), a main land tax (正租) of about 24,461 koku, and a miscellaneous rice tax of about 3,864 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "tosa_military",
   "domain_canonical": "土佐藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高知藩",
   "domain_en": "Tosa",
   "image": "images/lower_p163_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 163,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百貳",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八 (鹿兒島・高知)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Tosa (高知藩): officials roster",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "officials — the named officer hierarchy",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the officials roster (役人) of Tosa domain (高知藩), the Yamauchi domain, in the eighth fascicle of the survey. Where the preceding Satsuma entry named no one, Tosa lists its whole hierarchy: a 知事 (governor), Yamauchi; the 大参事 (senior councillor) Fukao Hiroto; the 権大参事 (junior senior councillor) Gotō Jozan; the 少参事 (junior councillor) Saitō Yakuma; and a long run of 権少参事 (provisional junior councillors) beginning with Konami Gorō and including men who would become national figures, Kataoka Kenkichi and Tani Tateki. The roster and Tosa's combined land-and-sea force of 9,000 (海陸兵員) carry on across the following leaves — the same army the demographics page splits into 6,600 standing (常備) and 2,400 emergency (非常) troops.",
   "sequence": 11
  },
