   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Tosa (高知藩), then Yamauchi and Kameoka",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials-and-military boundary page: tail of Kōchi (Tosa), then the start of Yamauchi (Tosa-Shinden) and Kameoka",
   "page_summary_en": "A boundary leaf in the eighth fascicle carrying three domains in succession. On the right it completes the officials roster of Tosa (高知藩) — seven councillors, among them Iwasaki Yatarō, the founder of Mitsubishi — and gives Tosa's combined land-and-sea force of 9,000 (海陸兵員). That troop figure prints to the right of the next ○ marker but belongs to Tosa, the domain sharing this leaf, not to what follows. The ○山内藩 marker then opens the Yamauchi (Tosa-Shinden) domain, listing its 知事 (governor) and 大参事 (senior councillor) and a standing army of 89 (常備兵). Finally the ○龜岡藩 marker begins the Kameoka domain of Tanba, whose officials continue onto the next page."
  },
  {
   "id": "asao_lower_p044_right",
   "sequence": 15,
   "domain_canonical": "浅尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "淺尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Asao",
   "image": "images/lower_p044_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 44,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（淺尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 6 (Asao)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Anshi domain administrative summary (tail) and Asao domain kokudaka (head)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of Fascicle 6 spans two domains: it completes the administrative summary of Anshi Domain (安志藩) and opens the entry for Asao Domain (浅尾藩), whose block begins at the ○淺尾藩 circle-marker. The Anshi fields (right of the marker) record 82 temple clergy (男42 + 女40), 8 shrine-priest households, 21 temples, 47 villages, 12 outcaste (eta) households, and 50 troops (10 of them officers), followed by its officials — a vacant governor (知事) line, 1 senior councillor (大参事), 2 acting senior councillors (権大参事), and a note that junior-councillor (小参事) posts are omitted as low-grade appointments in a small domain. The Asao fields (left of the marker) give a base assessment of 10,000 koku (per the 1869/巳-year survey), a revised addition of 98.93874 koku for a total of 10,098.93874 koku, and a rice land-tax of 3,574.92098 koku. The eta population is printed as 17 (十七) but its male/female split (36 + 34) sums to 70, indicating a 十七/七十 transposition in the movable-type print."
  },
  {
   "id": "asao_lower_p044_left",
   "sequence": 16,
   "domain_canonical": "浅尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "浅尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Asao",
   "image": "images/lower_p044_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 44,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（浅尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Asao)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Asao Domain: population, households, temples/shrines, outcaste groups, and tax totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf records the 1870 Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表, fascicle 6) survey figures for Asao Domain (浅尾藩, a small Bitchū domain). It reports 1,642 households and a population of 6,674 (3,550 male, 3,124 female) across 16 villages, together with 26 Buddhist temples (36 monks, 2 nuns) and 133 Shinto shrines. Small status-group populations are listed separately: 7 shrine-attendant households (20 persons), 96 eta households, and 39 onbo households. Fiscal totals are 3,907.07 koku of rice (合米) and 833.11 ryō of money (合金), with a principal money levy of 764 ryō and miscellaneous taxes of 100.68 koku and 67 ryō. (The eta population's printed total, 311, does not match its male+female subtotal of 211 — an internal inconsistency in the source.)"
  },
  {
   "id": "asao_civil_tail",
   "sequence": 17,
   "domain_canonical": "浅尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "淺尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Asao",
   "image": "images/lower_p045_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 45,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（浅尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 6 — Asao (淺尾藩): closing civil fields",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Closing fields of Asao domain's vol-2 civil register: status-class populations, kokudaka, and the five-year-average tax breakdown.",
   "page_summary_en": "This right leaf holds the closing fields of the preceding domain, Asao (淺尾藩), in the sixth fascicle of the survey; there is no ○ domain-boundary marker here, so Saga has not yet begun — its ○佐嘉藩 marker and land figures fall on the facing left page. Reading right to left, the columns record Asao's status-class populations — no 非人 (outcastes); 98 士族 (samurai) households totalling 403 persons; 72 卒族 (foot-soldier) households totalling 100 persons — followed by its land assessment (草高, assessed yield, about 10,005 koku; 現石, current rice on hand, 4,139 koku) and a five-year-average tax breakdown (正税, main tax, of 3,921 koku of rice plus 764 ryō in cash; 雑税, miscellaneous tax, of 114 koku of rice). Two bracketed notes from the 1928 reprint mark that the survey was taken in the Kōgo year (1870) and that the following lines had stood in red ink in the manuscript margin."
  },
  {
