   "pdf_page": 45,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六 (佐嘉)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 6 — Saga (佐嘉藩): land assessment and tax",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka via 'two-mouth combined / 5-yr average' + main tax",
   "page_summary_en": "The land-assessment and tax leaf for Saga domain (佐嘉藩), recorded in the sixth fascicle. Saga states its yield with an unusual phrasing, 貮口合平均 (the two-part combined figure, five-year average): 724,739 koku, formed from a base 高 (kokudaka) of 211,519 plus a 新田高 (new-field assessment) of 513,580 — Saga led the Edo period in reclaiming new paddy, so its real yield far outran its roughly 357,000-koku formal rating. The main tax is given as 213,478 koku of land-tax rice (正租米) and 217,789 koku of tax-collected rice (取納現米), together with a silver tax of 444.1 kanme (with its rice-equivalent 但米 of about 4,441 koku) and a small miscellaneous gold tax of 10 ryō.",
   "sequence": 18
  },
  {
   "id": "saga_demographics",
   "domain_canonical": "佐賀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐嘉藩",
   "domain_en": "Saga",
   "image": "images/lower_p046_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 46,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六 (佐嘉)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 6 — Saga (佐嘉藩): population and products",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "population totals (with M/F) + products",
   "page_summary_en": "Saga domain's (佐嘉藩) population totals and trade goods, in the sixth fascicle of the survey. It records 68,710 戸數 (households) and a total population (人員) of 354,450 — 183,517 male and 170,933 female — of which 5,273 are 士族 (samurai) households. The products block lists Saga's output with quantities, including the famous Hizen coal (石炭, 36,000,000 kin), Arita and Imari ceramics (陶器, over 20,000 bales), 92,719 koku of rice, tea, wax, sōmen, sake, and dried shrimp, alongside a cash figure of 99,831 kan-mon. The samurai and foot-soldier person counts continue on the facing left leaf.",
   "sequence": 19
  },
  {
   "id": "saga_status",
   "domain_canonical": "佐賀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐嘉藩",
   "domain_en": "Saga",
   "image": "images/lower_p046_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 46,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六 (佐嘉 → 佐倉)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 6 — Saga (佐嘉藩): status classes, then Sakura (佐倉藩)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "status-class persons + Sakura-han boundary marker",
   "page_summary_en": "The left leaf of Saga's (佐嘉藩) demographic spread, giving the status-class person counts that complete the totals on the facing page, in the sixth fascicle. It records 23,823 士族 (samurai) persons; 9,369 卒 (foot-soldier) households and 43,488 persons; 1,032 monk (僧) households and 4,412 persons; and 195 shrine-personnel (社人) households and 850 persons — each with its own male/female split — together with a note that the number of shrines was not specified (社數不詳). The neighbouring domain, Sakura (佐倉藩), a Hotta domain in Shimōsa, begins alongside.",
   "sequence": 20
  },
  {
   "id": "saga_officials",
   "sequence": 21,
   "domain_canonical": "佐賀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐賀藩",
   "domain_en": "Saga",
   "image": "images/lower_p226_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 226,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九 （佐賀）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Saga (佐賀藩): officials roster",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Saga domain officials (fascicle 9): the ○佐賀藩 boundary marker and Saga's councillor roster (governor heading, vacant senior councillor, provisional senior councillor and three further councillors), preceded on the right by the tail of the Ashikaga (足利藩) officials block.",
   "page_summary_en": "The leaf that opens Saga domain (佐賀藩) in the ninth fascicle, the officials and military register — note that this register writes the name 佐賀, where the civil fascicles used 佐嘉. The ○佐賀藩 marker is the domain boundary: everything to its left is Saga, everything to its right belongs to the preceding domain, Ashikaga (足利藩). Saga's officials, read right to left from the marker, are a 知事 (governor) heading with no appointee named here (Saga's governor was a Nabeshima), a 大参事 (senior councillor) post recorded as 欠員 (vacant), a 権大参事 (provisional senior councillor) Nakano Takumi, and three further councillors, Ikeda Yaichi, Fukae Sukeemon, and Chō Gen'ichi. To the right of the marker stands the close of the Ashikaga block, ending with a note that its troops were not ascertained (兵隊審ナラス) — a remark about Ashikaga's forces, not Saga's. Saga's own army appears on a later leaf, not on this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "saga_military",
   "domain_canonical": "佐賀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐賀藩",
   "domain_en": "Saga",
   "image": "images/lower_p227_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 227,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百三十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九 (佐賀 → 佐倉)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Saga (佐賀藩): army",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "military — Saga's six-battalion army (2,972 / 36 guns)",
   "page_summary_en": "Saga domain's (佐賀藩) army, in the ninth fascicle's military register; its ○佐賀藩 marker and officials roster stand on the facing page, while the force itself is recorded here. Saga fields six battalions (六大隊) totalling 2,972 troops — 864 officers (士官), 180 artillery soldiers (砲士), 1,440 infantry (兵士), 108 artillery privates (砲卒), 260 infantry privates (兵卒), and 120 bandsmen (樂卒) — with 36 cannon (大砲). A note records that the roster of junior officials and below was withheld (少参事以下書ナラス).",
   "sequence": 22
  },
  {
   "id": "nomura_upper_p182_right",
   "sequence": 23,
   "domain_canonical": "野村藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "野村藩",
   "domain_en": "Nomura",
   "image": "images/upper_p182_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 182,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（野村）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Domain Regulations Survey), Fascicle Four — Nomura",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nomura domain: land tax, products, and the household and status register",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf, printed book page 338, carries the fascicle-four return for Nomura domain and shows no maru-marker anywhere, so all fourteen columns belong to Nomura; the ○野村藩 marker that opens the entry stands on the preceding leaf, book page 337. The rightmost data column completes the kokudaka breakdown begun there, adding 600.846 koku of kaidedaka to the komidaka of 34.466 koku and the new-field assessment of 2,721.363 koku already recorded against a total assessed yield of 13,089.007 koku; the land tax (正租) then follows at 3,904.204 koku of hulled rice, with a note that 259.566 koku of miscellaneous taxes is counted inside that figure and a half-size gloss at the foot of the column stating that the sum is entirely revenue actually collected. Seven products are listed — tea, dried sea cucumber, salted sea-cucumber entrails, hijiki, arame, wakame and ino shellfish — followed by the declaration that no tax is levied on them. The register of people closes the leaf: 1,755 households and 8,431 persons, of which shizoku 77 households and 275 people (137 male, 138 female), sotsu 64 households and 124 people (67 male, 57 female), corvée conscripts 45 people, samurai servants 28 people (11 male, 17 female), and shrine households 13 with 49 people (26 male, 23 female); these counts reconcile exactly with the commoner, outcaste and temple figures on the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "nomura_upper_p182_left",
   "sequence": 24,
   "domain_canonical": "野村藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "野村藩",
   "domain_en": "Nomura",
   "image": "images/upper_p182_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 182,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（野村）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Survey Table, Fascicle 4 (Nomura)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nomura domain: religious houses, commoner and outcaste population, districts and villages, and a detached Mikawa parcel",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the fascicle-4 return for Nomura domain and carries no maru-marker, so all twelve columns belong to Nomura. It closes the status-by-status count of households and people — 28 temple households with 93 residents, no Shugendō practitioners, 9 eta households with 29 people, 7 hinin households with 21 people, and 1,557 commoner households with 7,767 people (3,912 male, 3,855 female) — then gives the domain's 95 shrines, its 28 temples plus one additional hall, and its 4 districts and 26 villages. Together with the status counts on the facing page these reconcile exactly to Nomura's totals of 1,755 households and 8,431 people. The three left-hand columns record a detached holding: the Yamada-village portion of Senpuku-ji's former shogunal vermilion-seal land in Atsumi district, Mikawa province, assessed at 122.03 koku (of which 4.63 koku is new field) and returning 31.29982 koku of hulled rice as a five-year average."
  },
  {
   "id": "nomura_kokudaka",
   "sequence": 25,
   "domain_canonical": "野村藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "野村藩",
   "domain_en": "Nomura",
   "image": "images/upper_p183_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 183,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四 （野村）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Nomura (野村藩): civil register",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Civil register (land tax, households, population with commoner/temple and M/F breakdown) of the small Nomura domain.",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page is the complete fascicle-4 civil register for the very small domain of 野村 (Nomura). It records a main tax (正税) of about 6.86 koku of rice plus 3 kanmon of cash, 45 households (戸數), and a population (人員) of 207. Under 内 (of which), that total divides into 2 Buddhist temple houses with 4 monks and 43 commoner houses holding 203 people, and the 203 commoners split into 106 male (男) and 97 female (女). The whole leaf belongs to Nomura alone; there is no ○ domain-boundary marker."
  },
  {
   "id": "nomura_lower_p199_left",
   "sequence": 26,
   "domain_canonical": "野村藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "野村藩",
   "domain_en": "Nomura",
   "image": "images/lower_p199_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 199,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "○野村藩",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Nomura (野村藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "officials_and_military",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fascicle-9 officials-and-military entry for Nomura (野村藩), which opens at the ○ domain-boundary marker. Its ranked establishment runs from a governor (知事) and one senior councillor (大参事) down through two junior senior councillors (権大参事) and three junior councillors (少参事), each listed with the appointee's name. The forces are given as two infantry platoons of 87 men (兵隊) and an artillery unit of six guns and 40 gunners (砲隊). The columns to the right of Nomura's ○marker belong to the previous domain sharing this leaf, Nobeoka (延岡藩) — the tail of its junior-councillor names overflowing leftward — not to Nomura."
  },
  {
