   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 (熊本)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Kumamoto (熊本藩): land assessment and taxes",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka (formal vs real) + sundry taxes + male population",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-5 land-and-tax register for Kumamoto (熊本藩), the Higo domain of the Hosokawa house. Its formal rating (高) was 540,000 koku, but the real assessed yield (草高) is recorded at 786,016 koku — a new-field uplift of 246,016 koku noted under 但内 (of which). The main tax (正税) comes to 304,838 koku, with sundry taxes (諸税) in rice (73,363 koku), salt (1,965), gold (2,615 ryō), and 503,469 jin of wax-tree berries (櫨實), the raw material for Higo's celebrated vegetable-wax industry. The male population (男人口) of 361,024 is entered here; the female count and grand total appear on the demographic pages."
  },
  {
   "id": "kumamoto_demographics",
   "sequence": 28,
   "domain_canonical": "熊本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "熊本藩",
   "domain_en": "Kumamoto",
   "image": "images/upper_p184_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 184,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 (熊本)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Kumamoto (熊本藩): male population by status",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "population by status class (male)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page breaks Kumamoto's male population down by status class, and — unusually — the domain registers its commoners in full. The largest groups are farmers (農, 278,846) and the sotsu class (卒族, 37,219), followed by merchants (商, 18,738), samurai households (士族, 8,050), former rear-vassals (從前陪臣, 8,259), clergy (僧侶, 3,167), and eta or outcaste persons (穢多, 3,495), together with smaller groups, all summing to the 361,024 male total. The total female population (女人口, 355,783) and the female samurai count (士族女, 8,000) also print here; the female-by-class breakdown and the grand totals appear on the facing leaves."
  },
  {
   "id": "kumamoto_demographics_female",
   "sequence": 29,
   "domain_canonical": "熊本藩",
   "domain_en": "Kumamoto",
   "domain_hi_name": "熊本藩",
   "image": "images/upper_p184_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 184,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（熊本）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Kumamoto (熊本藩): female population and totals",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kumamoto female-side status-class population, with treasure-persons, grand total population, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the female (女) half of Kumamoto's status-class population register, continuing the male-side breakdown on the facing page. Reading right to left it gives female counts for each group — sotsu class (卒族, 34,514), former rear-vassals (從前陪臣, 7,608), farmer houses (農家, 278,584), merchant houses (商家, 18,153), and eta or outcaste persons (穢多, 3,578), among others — followed by a treasure-persons category (物寳人, 3,183), the grand total population (人口合) of 719,990, the total household count (戸數) of 148,852, and 4,281 domain-retainer households (藩士). The whole leaf is Kumamoto's; there is no ○ domain-boundary marker."
  },
  {
   "id": "kumamoto_households",
   "sequence": 30,
   "domain_canonical": "熊本藩",
   "domain_en": "Kumamoto",
   "domain_hi_name": "熊本藩",
   "image": "images/upper_p185_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 185,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 （熊本）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Kumamoto (熊本藩): households, shrines, and ships",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "household counts by social category, plus shrine/temple, governor's-family, and steamship registers",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-5 page tallies Kumamoto's households (軒) by social category. Reading right to left it counts soldier-class houses (兵卒, 15,118), former rear-vassals (從前陪臣, 3,815), farmers (農, 114,510), merchants (商, 6,965), shrine households (社家, 277), Buddhist temples (寺院, 1,240, of which 86 draw a domain stipend), blind persons (盲人, 573), and eta or outcaste households (穢多, 1,352). The left margin adds 19 stipended Shinto shrines (神社), the governor's family (知事家族, 10 persons — 5 male, 5 female), and the domain's three steamships (蒸氣, 三艘), each given with its foreign and Japanese names and country of build. The entire leaf is Kumamoto's, with no ○ domain-boundary marker."
  },
  {
   "id": "kurume_kokudaka_households",
