   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 （久留米）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Kurume (久留米藩) opens: land, taxes, and households",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Opening of the Kurume (久留米藩) civil register — domain rank, land yield, taxes, and household counts — with a short Kumamoto (Higo) sailing-ship tail above the boundary marker.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries a domain boundary. At the top right, to the right of the ○久留米藩 marker, sits the tail of the previous domain, Kumamoto (Higo): its two sail-rigged ships (風帆船, 二艘), each named with its origin and build. Left of the marker, the entry for Kurume (久留米藩) opens with its civil and economic data — a formal rank (本高) of 210,000 koku, an assessed yield (草高) of 366,272 koku, a main tax (正税) of 117,280 koku, and miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 72,685 kan (of which 8,551 is product tax). The total households (戸數) come to 50,037, broken down under 内 into 45,727 directly-administered commoner houses plus samurai (士族, 948), sotsu, eta, shrine-servants, hinin, and temple houses."
  },
  {
   "id": "kumamoto_officials",
   "sequence": 32,
   "domain_canonical": "熊本藩",
   "domain_en": "Kumamoto",
   "domain_hi_name": "熊本藩",
   "image": "images/lower_p200_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 200,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（熊本）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Kumamoto (熊本藩): officials roster",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Kumamoto-han officials roster (governor and councillor ranks) with the domain's military-section header",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the officials page of Kumamoto's fascicle-9 entry, opening at the ○熊本藩 domain-boundary marker. Kumamoto's establishment is given as four ranked headings with headcounts — one governor (知事), four senior councillors (大参事), five provisional senior councillors (権大参事), and six junior councillors (少参事) — with the appointees' names listed below in columns, beginning with 松井新次郎 as governor. The far-left 兵隊 (troops) heading opens the military section, whose corps and warship figures continue onto the facing leaf. The small run of names to the right of the ○熊本藩 marker belongs to the preceding domain sharing this leaf, not to Kumamoto."
  },
  {
   "id": "kumamoto_military",
   "sequence": 33,
   "domain_canonical": "熊本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "熊本藩",
   "domain_en": "Kumamoto",
   "image": "images/lower_p200_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 200,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九 (熊本)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Kumamoto (熊本藩): army and navy",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "army + six-ship navy",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-9 leaf records Kumamoto's disclosed forces: a samurai corps (士隊) of two battalions (576 men), a rifle corps (銃隊) of four battalions (1,152), and an artillery corps (砲隊) of 288 gunners with 24 French-pattern guns — roughly 2,016 troops in all. Its navy is notably large: six vessels, mostly foreign-built steamers, including 萬里丸 (ex-Cosmos White, French), 凌雲丸 (ex-Granada, British iron), and 奮迅丸 (ex-Felicia), plus a sailing ship (風帆船) and two more steamers. The ○熊本藩 marker and the named officials sit on the facing leaf, while the ○久留米藩 marker at the left begins the next domain, Kurume."
  },
  {
