   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（金澤）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Kanazawa (金澤藩): population, temples, and standing army",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Kanazawa (Kaga) population, religious institutions, retainer-class register, and standing army",
   "page_summary_en": "This facing half of Kanazawa's (金澤藩) fascicle-2 entry opens at the ○金澤藩 domain-boundary marker at the far left; the whole leaf is Kanazawa's own data. Reading right to left it records the directly-governed population (人口, 26,064), 3,247 Shinto shrines (神社) and 2,330 Buddhist temples (寺院), and the samurai-and-soldier households (士卒族戸數, 16,780) with their population of 37,793 (19,008 male, 18,785 female). The left third lays out Kanazawa's standing army: 12 infantry battalions totalling 5,076 men (戎兵), one cavalry squadron (騎兵, 165), an artillery regiment (砲兵, 270), an engineer corps (工兵隊, 572), and a baggage and transport corps (輜重隊, 89)."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanazawa_kokudaka",
