   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二 (金澤)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Kanazawa (金澤藩): land assessment, demographics, and taxes",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka + headline demographics + main taxes",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle 2 (civil and economic) entry for Kanazawa (金澤藩), the Maeda house and the largest non-Tokugawa domain in Japan — the famed 'million-koku Kaga.' It records a 草高 (assessed yield) of 1,353,353 koku, of which the productive base (込高) is 1,025,020 and reclaimed new field (新田改出高) accounts for 328,333, with a main rice tax (正租米) of 633,134 koku alongside substantial coin taxes. The headline population figures also print here — 戸數 (households) 198,811 and 人口 (population) 997,669 (male 498,585, female 499,084), the largest counts in the survey — of which 士族 (samurai households) number 7,797 and 28,683 persons, a modest share against nearly a million residents. The retainer sub-classes and religious establishment continue on the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanazawa_demographics",
   "sequence": 36,
   "domain_canonical": "金澤藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "金澤藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanazawa (Kaga)",
   "image": "images/upper_p088_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 88,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二 (金澤)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Kanazawa (金澤藩): retainer classes, clergy, and military summary",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "retainer/dependent sub-classes (with M/F) + religious establishment + military summary",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Kanazawa's (金澤藩) demographic entry, breaking the wider population into its sub-classes: 卒族 (lower samurai) 27,038 persons in 9,703 households, 中間小者 (attendants and menials) 5,938 in 2,699 households, and the outcaste classes (藤内等) 11,695 in 2,243 households. It then records the religious establishment — 神社 (Shinto shrines) 407 with 1,799 shrine personnel, and temples with 13,326 monks — each population column carrying its own male/female split (for example, 卒族 14,655 men and 12,383 women). A summary of the domain's reformed army appears alongside: five infantry battalions (步兵) and three artillery units (砲兵), an officer cadre of 1,106 and 1,568 rank-and-file troops (兵卒), plus two steamships and three sailing vessels."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanazawa_officials",
   "sequence": 37,
   "domain_canonical": "金澤藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanazawa (Kaga)",
   "domain_hi_name": "金澤藩",
   "image": "images/lower_p162_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 162,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（金澤）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Kanazawa (金澤藩): officials and army (shared leaf)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain-boundary page: the preceding domain's junior-councillor tail and full standing army, then the ○金澤藩 marker and Kanazawa's senior officials (knowledge-governor and councillors)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf, from the fascicle 8 officials-and-military register, sits across a domain boundary marked by the ○ before 金澤藩. Because the columns read right to left, the material to the RIGHT of that ○marker belongs to the PRECEDING domain: the close of its officials roster (少参事 11, 権少参事 8) followed by its full standing army — twelve infantry battalions of 5,076 men, one cavalry platoon (160 troops, 165 horses), an artillery regiment of 279 men, an engineer corps (工兵隊) of 572, and a transport corps (輜重隊) of 89. To the LEFT of the ○marker Kanazawa's own entry begins: Knowledge-Governor (知事) Maeda Yoshiyasu, Senior Councillor (大参事) Shinohara Kanroku, and Provisional Senior Councillor (権大参事) Rikuhara Shintarō, with a lower register of further councillors and a vermilion addendum, dated the twelfth month of the snake year, adding two more names."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanazawa_military",
   "sequence": 38,
   "domain_canonical": "金澤藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "金澤藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanazawa (Kaga)",
   "image": "images/lower_p162_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 162,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八 (金澤)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Kanazawa (金澤藩): junior officials and army corps",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "junior-official roster + disclosed corps",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fascicle 8 (officials and military) entry for Kanazawa (金澤藩). Its senior officials and the ○金澤藩 boundary marker appear on the facing leaf; this half holds the junior-official roster — 少参事 and 権少参事 (Honda Shigurehei and eight others) — together with the disclosed army: five infantry battalions (步兵, 320 riflemen each) and three artillery units (砲兵, 144 men each). The personnel totals recorded with the entry are 1,568 rank-and-file troops (兵卒人員), 1,106 officers and officials (士等役員), and 464 corps members (隊士), plus four councillor counts summing to 47."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumaki_kokudaka_open",
   "sequence": 39,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴牧藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "○鶴牧藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p155_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 155,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四 （鶴牧）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Tsurumaki (鶴牧藩): land assessment and taxes (shared leaf)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Opening of Tsurumaki domain's civil register: kokudaka, land/cash taxes, received-koku, and household count, with the preceding domain's military roster overflowing to the right of the boundary marker.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle 4 (civil and economic) entry for Tsurumaki (鶴牧藩), a small fudai domain of the Mizuno house in Kazusa, its ○鶴牧藩 boundary marker sitting mid-page with its 15,000-koku official omotedaka gloss. Everything to the LEFT of that ○marker is Tsurumaki's: a 草高 (assessed yield) of 19,910 koku given as a five-year average (1864–1868), a main rice tax (正租米) of 8,896 koku with a cash component, a miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of about 111 kan, a small received-koku figure (受領高) of 25.2 koku tied to two temples, and 戸數 (households) of 4,757. To the RIGHT of the ○marker the preceding domain's military roster overflows onto this leaf: the 振武隊 (169 men), 先進隊 (212), 壯進隊 (224), and an artillery corps (砲隊) of 30, totalling 737 men — these belong to the previous domain, not to Tsurumaki."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumaki_kokudaka",
   "sequence": 40,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴牧藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumaki",
   "domain_hi_name": "鶴牧藩",
   "image": "images/upper_p156_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 156,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（鶴牧）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Tsurumaki (鶴牧藩): population and household counts",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsurumaki domain population, household counts by status, and clergy/shrine/village/troop tallies",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle 4 (civil and economic) entry for Tsurumaki (鶴牧藩), the Mizuno house's small fudai domain in Kazusa. Reading right to left, it gives household counts (114 士族 samurai households, 101 卒族 lower-samurai households, 75 temples) and a total 人口 (population) of 20,586 (male 10,563, female 10,064), broken down by status: 561 samurai-class persons, 341 lower samurai, 61 shrine attendants, 65 temple residents, and small numbers of mountain ascetics, shrine officials, diviners, and blind-guild members. It closes with 19 神社 (Shinto shrines), 64 villages (村數), and three platoons of troops (兵隊) of forty men each, noting explicitly that the governor's family and any warships are not recorded. This is a single-domain leaf, with no ○ boundary marker."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumaki_officials",
   "sequence": 41,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴牧藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "○鶴牧藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p192_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 192,
   "page_side": "R",
