   "book_page": "百四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（和歌山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Wakayama (和歌山藩): land, taxes, and population",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Wakayama (Kii) domain land assessment, tax, product-tax revenue, households, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This is Wakayama domain's (Kii, a major Tokugawa-collateral house) fiscal and demographic entry in the second fascicle, opened by the ○和歌山藩 boundary marker at the right. It records an assessed yield (草高) of 539,469 koku plus a small newly reclaimed-field yield (新田高), the regular land tax (正租) in rice, gold, and cash, miscellaneous taxes (雜税) including salt (鹽), and a product tax (産物税) of about 28,743 ryō of gold. It closes with 108,245 households (戸數), a population (人口) of 458,826 (232,646 male / 226,180 female), and an additional 5,326 outcaste (穢多) households."
  },
  {
   "id": "wakayama_lower_p161_left",
   "sequence": 52,
   "domain_canonical": "和歌山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "和歌山藩",
   "domain_en": "Wakayama (Kii)",
   "image": "images/lower_p161_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 161,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（小見川、和歌山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Omigawa (小見川藩) and Wakayama (和歌山藩): officials",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (governor and councillor ranks) for Omigawa and the opening of Wakayama, from the fascicle-8 administrative-personnel survey.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is an officials leaf from the eighth fascicle, and it holds the boundary between two domains. The upper block belongs to Omigawa (小見川藩), a small Shimōsa domain: its governor (知事) and five councillor-rank posts are listed with headcounts, its named appointees run in a column headed by governor Nukada Daigorō (額田大五郎), and a troop figure (兵隊) of 93 is given with a note that troops were recorded but no personnel detail. Below the ○和歌山藩 boundary marker begins Wakayama (Kii); only the start of its officials appears here — a governor (知事), one senior councillor (大参事), and three junior-senior councillors (権大参事). Everything to the right of the ○和歌山藩 marker belongs to the preceding Omigawa entry, so only the three left-hand columns and the marker itself are Wakayama's."
  },
  {
   "id": "omigawa_upper_p085_left",
   "sequence": 53,
   "domain_canonical": "小見川藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小見川藩",
   "domain_en": "Omigawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p085_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 85,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小見川）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Omigawa)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Close of Ōtawara's fascicle-2 entry and the opening of Omigawa's",
   "page_summary_en": "Most of this leaf finishes the fascicle-2 entry for Ōtawara domain, whose marker stands on the facing recto: 608 shizoku and 149 sotsu; four outcaste blocks (hinin 8 households/36 persons and 2 households/7 persons; eta 11 households/67 persons and 9 households/50 persons), each with its male and female split; 27 temples staffed by 16 monks and a further 13 persons alongside 3 nuns; 119 villages; and shrines entered as 未詳, not ascertained. The maru-marker ○小見川藩 then opens Omigawa domain, and its first four fields print here: kusadaka 10,476.0201 koku, taka 10,000 koku, komidaka 476.0201 koku, and a regular land tax of 2,259.53349 koku of rice. Taka plus komidaka reconciles exactly to the kusadaka figure, and three of the four outcaste blocks reconcile exactly to their male and female components. The one inconsistency is in Ōtawara's rightmost hinin block, where the printed population of 36 exceeds its 18 male and 15 female components by three."
  },
  {
   "id": "omigawa_upper_p086_right",
   "sequence": 54,
   "domain_canonical": "小見川藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小見川藩",
   "domain_en": "Omigawa",
