   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（小見川）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Omigawa (小見川藩): taxes, population, and villages",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Omigawa domain (小見川藩) civil/fiscal survey: land tax, misc tax, households, population by status, temples/shrines, eta, villages.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is Omigawa domain's (小見川藩, an Uchida-family domain of about 10,000 koku in Shimōsa Province) civil and fiscal entry in the second fascicle; the running header and the closing village note naming 小見川村 identify it. There is no ○domain-boundary marker on this leaf — the data flow as a single continuous domain. It records a main land tax (正租) of 589,812 mon in cash, miscellaneous taxes (雜税) of rice and cash, 1,621 households (戸數), and a commoner population (人口) of 8,264 (4,071 male / 4,193 female). It also gives 80 samurai and lower-samurai households (士卒族, of which 74 are 士族 and 6 are 卒) totaling 288 people, 43 Buddhist temples (寺), 27 shrines (社), 6 outcaste (穢多) households, and 24 villages (村)."
  },
  {
   "id": "omigawa_lower_p161_left",
