   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（小見川、和歌山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Omigawa (小見川藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Omigawa (小見川) officials + troops — shares the Wakayama-opening leaf",
   "page_summary_en": "This is Omigawa domain's (小見川藩, Shimōsa) officials-and-military block from the eighth fascicle, on a leaf it shares with Ōtawara to the right and the opening of Wakayama to the left. It lists the domain's councillor ranks by headcount — one senior councillor (大参事), two junior-senior councillors (権大参事), one junior councillor (少参事), and one provisional junior councillor (権少参事) — together with a troop figure (兵隊) of 93. Omigawa printed no governor's name on this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "hiroshima_lower_p095_left",
   "sequence": 56,
   "domain_canonical": "廣島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "廣島藩",
   "domain_en": "Hiroshima",
   "image": "images/lower_p095_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 95,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（廣島）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hiroshima (廣島藩): land assessment",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hiroshima domain fascicle-7 landholding: total/remaining kokudaka, district and village counts, plus household, shrine, eta, and warship notations.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the landholding register for Hiroshima domain (廣島藩) from Fascicle 7 of the survey; its figures read to the left of the ○廣島藩 domain-boundary marker. It records a gross assessed yield (惣高) of 488,024.24735 koku — including 12,433.15575 koku of newly reclaimed fields (新田) and an iron-mine levy (鐵山役高) of 582.972 koku — and, after 456.9244 koku of tax-exempt land (除地) is set aside, a residual yield (殘高) of 487,567.32295 koku. The holding spans Aki and Bingo provinces across 868 villages (村數), with 22 Shinto shrines (神社), a governor's household (知事家) of 3, and an outcaste (穢多) population of 13; warships are noted as not recorded. A marginal variant copy gives an alternate gross total of 485,714.12515 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "hiroshima_lower_p096_right",
   "sequence": 57,
   "domain_canonical": "廣島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "廣島藩",
   "domain_en": "Hiroshima",
   "image": "images/lower_p096_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 96,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（廣島）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hiroshima (廣島藩): fiscal totals",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hiroshima domain fiscal totals (fascicle 7): land after deductions, land tax, miscellaneous tax, cash revenue, remaining koku, and grand total, followed by a variant-edition (別本) recomputation of the same figures printed in the original book's margin.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Hiroshima domain's (廣島藩) fiscal accounts in Fascicle 7; it carries no ○ boundary marker, so all figures belong to Hiroshima. The main block records internal assessed land (内高) of 2,133.3459 koku, a residual yield (殘高) of 483,580.77925 koku, the regular land tax in rice (正租) of 242,999.4185 koku, miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 12,390.225 koku, cash revenue (錢) of 86,018.928 kan, and a grand total (合〆) of 254,422.4051 koku. A note explains that the following six lines were written in the margin of the original book, introducing a variant edition that re-reports the land tax (242,032.18 koku), miscellaneous tax (14,509.009 koku), cash (66,097.765 kan), its rice equivalent (此米, 861.939 koku), and a variant grand total of 258,370.366 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "hiroshima_lower_p096_left",
   "sequence": 58,
   "domain_canonical": "廣島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "廣島藩",
   "domain_en": "Hiroshima",
   "image": "images/lower_p096_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 96,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（廣島）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hiroshima (廣島藩): population and households",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hiroshima domain demographics (population by status class, household counts, temples/shrines, outcaste dwellings) and product-tax revenue.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Hiroshima domain (廣島藩) in Fascicle 7 with its demographic register; it carries no ○ boundary marker, so all figures belong to Hiroshima. It gives a total population (人口) of 914,157 (468,180 male / 445,977 female) and 185,104 households (戸數), with samurai households (士族, 1,780) and foot-soldier households (卒族, 4,730) broken out separately, alongside the samurai population (9,536) and foot-soldier population (23,046). The page also counts 999 Buddhist temples (寺院), 507 shrine-priest families (社家), 2,737 shrine officiants (社務人), and 5,028 outcaste dwellings (非人穢多小屋). The printed page number in the bottom margin is 169."
  },
  {
   "id": "hiroshima_lower_p242_right",
   "sequence": 59,
   "domain_canonical": "廣島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "廣島藩",
   "domain_en": "Hiroshima",
   "image": "images/lower_p242_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 242,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百六十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（廣島）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Hiroshima (廣島藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-9 officials-and-military register: the tail of Shizuku domain (senior councillors + a 3-platoon force) to the right of the ○廣島藩 marker, then Hiroshima's councillor establishment (大参事 2, 権大参事 1, 少参事 4, 権少参事 4) with appointee names and its 6,000-man / 10-battalion army.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf holds the officials-and-military register (職員・兵隊) for Hiroshima domain (廣島藩) from Fascicle 9. To the left of the ○廣島藩 boundary marker is Hiroshima's own entry: a councillor establishment of two senior councillors (大参事), one associate senior councillor (権大参事) with three more under selection, four junior councillors (少参事), and four associate junior councillors (権少参事), together with named appointees, and a military strength of 6,000 troops (兵員) organized into ten battalions (大隊). The columns to the right of the marker belong to the previous domain sharing this leaf, Shizuku (志筑藩): its senior councillors and its small force of one platoon of standing troops (常備兵) and two platoons of reserve troops (非常兵), not Hiroshima's."
  },
  {
   "id": "okayama_upper_p064_right",
   "sequence": 60,
   "domain_canonical": "岡山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡山藩",
   "domain_en": "Okayama",
   "image": "images/upper_p064_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 64,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（岡山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Okayama (岡山藩): land, tax, and population (opening)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Boundary page: tail of Numata domain's civil register (right of the marker) and the opening land/tax block of Okayama domain (left of the ○岡山藩 marker), Fascicle 2.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a boundary leaf in Fascicle 2 of the survey where the ○岡山藩 marker opens the Okayama domain (岡山藩) entry. To the left of the marker are Okayama's opening figures: a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 454,117.20 koku (of which 15,000 koku were split off to Ikusaka domain), a base assessment (高) of 315,200.03 koku, reclaimed new-field yield (新田改出高) of 138,917.17 koku, regular land-tax rice (正租米) of 186,911.31 koku, and miscellaneous-tax rice (雜税米) of 1,387.49 koku. Because the text reads right-to-left, the columns to the right of the ○岡山藩 marker — 41 temples (寺), 123 villages (村數), and the outcaste household and population counts (穢多戸數 215 / 穢多人口 1,012; 非人戸數 13 / 非人人口 58) — belong to the previous domain, Numata (沼田藩), not Okayama. The printed page number is 102."
  },
  {
   "id": "okayama_upper_p064_left",
   "sequence": 61,
   "domain_canonical": "岡山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡山藩",
   "domain_en": "Okayama",
   "image": "images/upper_p064_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 64,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（岡山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Okayama (岡山藩): tax reconciliation and population",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Okayama domain fascicle-2 continuation: land-tax/kokudaka reconciliation (with koku apportioned to the Ikusaka sub-domain) and the samurai/commoner household-and-population breakdown.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Okayama domain (岡山藩) in Fascicle 2; it carries no ○ boundary marker, so all figures belong to Okayama. The right half completes a land-tax and yield reconciliation, with a grand total (合) of 188,298.79 koku, 723.55 koku lost to flood and drought (水旱減石), and portions of the actual koku (現石) and land tax apportioned off to the Ikusaka sub-domain (生坂藩), leaving a remainder of about 183,246 koku (殘高). The left half records households and population by status: samurai (士族) 2,711 households and 9,738 persons (5,304 male / 4,434 female), foot-soldiers (卒族) 3,026 households and 7,799 persons (5,820 male / 1,979 female), and commoners (庶人) 77,489 households. The printed page number is 103."
  },
  {
   "id": "okayama_lower_p148_left",
   "sequence": 62,
   "domain_canonical": "岡山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡山藩",
   "domain_en": "Okayama",
