   "pdf_page": 51,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（鳥取）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Tottori (鳥取藩): land, population, and status",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Tottori domain civil/economic profile (fascicle 2): rice yield, households, population with male/female and status breakdowns, shrines/temples, and one warship.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf holds the civil and economic profile of Tottori domain (鳥取藩) from Fascicle 2, opened by its ○ boundary marker with a former assessment (元高) of 320,000 koku. It records an assessed rice yield (合米) of about 206,359.7 koku, 147,510 households, and a total population of 714,022 (363,776 male / 350,246 female). An internal breakdown gives the samurai-and-foot-soldier class (6,432 households; 30,645 persons), shrine-priest families (社家), and temples (寺). Village and shrine counts are marked as not recorded, the governor's family is noted as unrecorded (知事家族不記), and the domain reports one warship (艦壹艘), the Boshin-maru (戊辰丸)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tottori_upper_p051_left",
   "sequence": 64,
   "domain_canonical": "鳥取藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鳥取藩",
   "domain_en": "Tottori",
   "image": "images/upper_p051_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 51,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（鳥取）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Tottori (鳥取藩): yield and tax revenue",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Tottori domain fiscal survey (Fascicle 2): assessed yield, branch-fief sub-allotments, tax revenue in rice and silver",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Tottori domain (鳥取藩), the Ikeda house's holding in Inaba and Hōki, in Fascicle 2; it carries no ○ boundary marker, so all figures belong to Tottori. The right block records a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 428,169.70 koku, three branch-fief allotments held by Ikeda kinsmen (30,000 / 4,500 / 20,000 koku), and 14,710.255 koku of permanently uncultivable land (永荒). The left block gives the five-year-average tax revenue — regular land-tax rice (正租米) of 156,284.052 koku, fixed-rate rice (定免米) of 164,720.944 koku, miscellaneous-tax rice (雜税米) of 523.706 koku, and silver (銀) of 516.658 kanme — together with a 3,000-koku received fief (受領高) in the Ōyama area of Hōki."
  },
  {
   "id": "tottori_upper_p052_right",
   "sequence": 65,
   "domain_canonical": "鳥取藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鳥取藩",
   "domain_en": "Tottori",
   "image": "images/upper_p052_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 52,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（鳥取）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Tottori (鳥取藩): new-field tax and demographics",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Tottori domain land-tax revenue (new fields, regular/fixed-rate/miscellaneous rice, copper cash) and household/population figures with samurai (shizoku) and foot-soldier (sotsu) status breakdowns.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Tottori domain (鳥取藩), which administered Inaba and Hōki provinces, in Fascicle 2. It records the new-field tax base — reclaimed fields (新田) of 516.893 koku, regular land-tax rice (正租米) of 1,220.545 koku, fixed-rate rice (定免米) of 1,312.025 koku, miscellaneous-tax rice (雜税米) of 3.5 koku, and copper cash (錢) of 81 kan — alongside demographic totals of 79,881 households (戸數) and a population (人口) of 371,640 (191,093 male / 180,547 female). A breakdown (内譯) then splits out the samurai (士族: 1,710 households / 8,605 persons) and foot-soldier (卒族: 7,456 households / 24,205 persons) populations by sex. The printed foot-soldier male and female sub-totals do not sum to the printed total, an inconsistency left as it appears in the source."
  },
  {
   "id": "tottori_upper_p052_left",
