   "book_page": "二百六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（鳥取）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Tottori (鳥取藩): officials",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Tottori domain officials (governor and councillors) opening its fascicle-8 entry, preceded by the tail of Tokushima domain's military overflow.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a Fascicle 8 page, the fascicle that records domain officials and military strength. The ○鳥取藩 marker opens Tottori domain's entry, and its roster of officials (職員) fills the lower part of the leaf: the governorship (知事, no name printed here), a grand-councillor rank (大参事) with three appointees, an acting grand-councillor rank (権大参事) with two, and a junior-councillor rank (少参事) with two. The material to the right of the ○鳥取藩 marker is the tail end of the previous domain sharing this leaf, Tokushima (徳島藩): its last official plus its troop counts of 1,619 soldiers (兵士) and 2,579 rank-and-file (兵卒). Those troop figures belong to Tokushima, not Tottori."
  },
  {
   "id": "horie_upper_p049_left",
   "sequence": 68,
   "domain_canonical": "堀江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "堀江藩",
   "domain_en": "Horie",
   "image": "images/upper_p049_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 49,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（堀江）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 1 (Horie)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Horie domain kokudaka composition and 1864-68 average tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of pdf page 49 (printed page 73) opens with the last three fields of the preceding entry, Honjō domain (本庄藩): 91 shrines, a note that the governor's family was not recorded and that the domain held no warships, and a force of 197 riflemen and 235 rank-and-file soldiers, all printed to the right of the ○堀江藩 marker and therefore belonging to Honjō. Everything left of the marker is Horie domain (堀江藩) in Tōtōmi, whose nominal kusadaka of 10,006 koku is itemised on this leaf as 5,484.70838 koku of present assessed yield (including newly opened fields re-entered on the register) and 4,521.21162 koku of village land the domain merely expected to bring under cultivation by degrees. The revenue block, explicitly a five-year average from 1864 to 1868, records 1,792.02329 koku of regular land tax rice, a 388.18309 koku nobemai surcharge, 718 kan 302.74 mon of ei-cash from barley sales converted at 8 ryō per koku to 89.78784 koku, and miscellaneous taxes of 12 ryō 2 bu 1 shu plus 149.16 mon converted to 1.620275 koku. Those four items sum to the printed total of 2,271.6144275 koku of current rice, matching the components to five decimal places."
  },
  {
   "id": "horie_upper_p050_right",
   "sequence": 69,
   "domain_canonical": "堀江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "堀江藩",
   "domain_en": "Horie",
   "image": "images/upper_p050_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
