   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（堀江）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Horie (堀江藩): civil register",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Horie domain civil register: shrine/temple land, households, population by status, villages, shrines, Shugendo, governor's family",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half-page is the complete civil register (Fascicle 1) entry for Horie domain (堀江藩), a tiny (~10,000-koku) Tōtōmi domain; the running header reads 藩制一覧表第一（堀江） and the block closes with the governor's-family field. It records 15 koku of shrine and temple land (社寺領) — a 10-koku Kashima Myōjin shrine and a 5-koku Shukurō-ji temple, each with its rice tax — and a total of 1,605 households (戸數) and 7,678 people (人口). Status sub-counts follow for the combined shi–sotsu class (士卒族) at 77 households and 298 people, shizoku (士族, samurai households) at 70 households and 203 people, sotsu (卒, lower retainers), and temples (寺) at 30 with a clergy population of 57. It also gives 18 villages, 4 shrines, 3 Shugendō houses, and a five-person governor's family, with an editorial note that the number of shrines is uncertain and that no warships are recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "horie_lower_p141_left",
   "sequence": 70,
   "domain_canonical": "堀江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "堀江藩",
   "domain_en": "Horie",
   "image": "images/lower_p141_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
