   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Tokushima (徳島藩): assessment and tax revenue",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Tokushima domain: assessed kokudaka, land-tax (genmai), and cash/product tax revenue (Fascicle 2 civil/fiscal register).",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page opens Tokushima domain's (徳島藩) entry in Fascicle 2 (第二) of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran, headed by the ○徳島藩 domain-boundary marker. It is the fiscal core of the register: an assessed yield (草高) of 442,735 koku, a land tax stated in current-rice terms (現米) of 218,481 koku, an of-which (内) five-year-average figure of 41,675 koku covering the 1864–1868 remissions, and a balance (差引) of 202,840 koku after deductions. Cash and product taxes (諸税諸産物金) come to 28,158 ryō, with a rice-equivalent (此米) of 3,519.725 koku. A marginal note explains that a great flood cut the actual revenue collected to the 26,034-koku figure shown alongside."
  },
  {
   "id": "tokushima_upper_p051_right",
   "sequence": 72,
   "domain_canonical": "徳島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "徳島藩",
   "domain_en": "Tokushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p051_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 51,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（鳥取）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Tokushima (徳島藩): demographic totals (shared leaf)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Tokushima demographics (shares the Tottori-opening leaf; Tokushima's tail continues here)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens Tottori's entry with the ○ domain-boundary marker and its assessed-yield figure, but the bulk of the page — read right-to-left, to the right of that marker — is the demographic tail of the previous domain sharing the leaf, Tokushima (徳島藩). The Tokushima figures recorded here are a combined rice total (合米) of 206,359.725 koku, 147,510 households (戸數), and a population (人口) of 714,022, split into 363,776 male (男) and 350,246 female (女). Status counts follow — shi–sotsu households (士卒族戸數) at 6,432 with a population of 30,645, shizoku households (士戸數) at 2,100, and sotsu households (卒戸數) at 4,332 — along with Shinto-priest households (社家戸數), temples (寺), temple monks (寺僧) and nuns (寺尼), and one warship (艦). These belong to Tokushima, not Tottori."
  },
  {
   "id": "tokushima_lower_p142_right",
   "sequence": 73,
   "domain_canonical": "徳島藩",
