   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Kajiyama (加知山藩): demographic tail (shared leaf)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kajiyama demographics (shares the Yonezawa-opening leaf; Kajiyama's tail continues here)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens Yonezawa's entry with the ○ domain-boundary marker and its assessed-yield figure, but the bulk of the page — read right-to-left, to the right of that marker — is the demographic tail of the previous domain sharing the leaf, Kajiyama (加知山藩). The Kajiyama figures recorded here cover temple clergy (寺人口, 138 people), Buddhist halls (堂), yamabushi mountain ascetics (山伏, 2 households and 9 people), eta and hinin outcaste households (穢多非人戸數, 13 households and 49 people), shizoku households (士族戸數, 122 households and 417 people), and sotsu (卒族), together with 117 shrines (神社), 30 villages (村數), one rifleman unit (銃兵), and 2 cannon (大砲). These belong to Kajiyama, not Yonezawa."
  },
  {
   "id": "kajiyama_lower_p173_right",
