   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Yonezawa (米澤藩): assessment and demographics",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yonezawa domain civil register: temple/shrine and status-group population and household counts, villages, riflemen and cannon, and the grass-yield (kusadaka) grand total.",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page belongs to Yonezawa domain (米澤藩), marked by the ○米澤藩 domain-boundary marker and the running header 藩制一覧表第三（米澤）, in Fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. Read right-to-left, it records temple, shrine, and status-group counts — temple clergy of 138, yamabushi ascetics (山伏), eta and hinin households, shizoku (士族, samurai households) of 122 households and 417 people, sotsu (卒), 117 shrines and 78 temples, and 30 villages — most with an inner male/female (内男/女) breakdown. It also gives the domain's military strength (a rifle platoon of about 70 men and 2 cannon with their artillerymen) and the grand total assessed yield (草高) of 147,248.723 koku, alongside a reclaimed and added-land figure (外込高新田高改出高) of 28,818.872 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "yonezawa_upper_p111_right",
   "sequence": 78,
   "domain_canonical": "米澤藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "米澤藩",
   "domain_en": "Yonezawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p111_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 111,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三 （米澤）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Yonezawa (米澤藩): land total and tax yield",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yonezawa domain (Fascicle 3), continued: land-total (合高), five-year-average yield (物成) and its rice/purchased-rice/gold components, and the regular- and miscellaneous-tax figures in rice, silver, and coin.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Fascicle 3 fiscal register for Yonezawa domain (米澤藩); the two ○ markers here open internal sub-sections of Yonezawa's own entry, not a boundary to a neighboring domain. It records the samurai-reclaimed and newly-opened land (諸士開高并新開高, 108,681 koku), the combined land total (合高, 284,748 koku), and the five-year-average tax yield (物成, 85,452 koku), the last broken into a rice component (米, 54,398 koku) and a gold component (金, 70,968 ryō). The tax section gives the regular land tax (正租) as 41,735 koku of rice (正租稅米) plus 556 kan of silver (正租銀), and the miscellaneous tax (雜稅) in rice (2,217 koku), coin (16,408 kan), and silver (191 kan), with purchased rice (買米, 10,445 koku) between the two blocks."
  },
  {
   "id": "yonezawa_upper_p111_left",
   "sequence": 79,
   "domain_canonical": "米澤藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "米澤藩",
   "domain_en": "Yonezawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p111_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 111,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（米澤）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Yonezawa (米澤藩): product taxes and tax totals",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yonezawa domain — fascicle-3 product-tax commodities (wax, safflower, cotton, ramie, charcoal), their ryō tax-equivalents, and the summary land-tax totals (regular + miscellaneous tax).",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Yonezawa domain's (米澤藩) Fascicle 3 entry, listing the domain's taxable products alongside their value in tax. Reading right to left, it records the miscellaneous corvée tax (諸役稅, 33,459) and quantities of charcoal (炭, 21,365), safflower (紅花, 264), cotton (綿, 69), blue ramie (靑苧, 14,698), and wax-tree berries (山蠟實, 700, with a village figure of 8,900), each followed by a small-print note converting the commodity into its ryō tax-equivalent. A standalone ○ labeled 取合如上 (\"the reckoning is as above\") opens the summary block, which gives the five-year-average regular tax (正租) of 41,735 koku of rice and the miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 2,217 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "yonezawa_upper_p112_right",
   "sequence": 80,
   "domain_canonical": "米澤藩",
