   "pdf_page": 112,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（米澤）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Yonezawa (米澤藩): money taxes and product quantities",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yonezawa domain miscellaneous taxes (silver/copper-cash duties) and product-tax quantities (charcoal, ramie, silk floss, safflower, purchased rice, wax berries)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Fascicle 3 economic register for Yonezawa domain (米澤藩). The right-hand columns give money taxes in silver (銀, 191) and copper-cash (錢, 16,408 kan), followed by a large charcoal (炭) figure of 21,365 kan. An 外 (\"besides\") divider then introduces a block of product-tax quantities, each with its commodity name at the column foot: purchased rice (買米, 10,445 koku), safflower (紅花, 264), silk floss (眞綿, 69), ramie (青苧, 14,698), and two grades of wax berry (山蠟實 700, 里蠟實 8,900). The block closes with a miscellaneous-duty gold tax (諸役稅金, 33,459)."
  },
  {
