   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Yonezawa (米澤藩): population and households",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yonezawa domain demographic register: total population with sex split, plus household counts by status group (samurai/sotsu, clergy, outcastes), religious buildings, and a miscellaneous copper-coin tax figure.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf holds the demographic portion of Yonezawa domain's (米澤藩) Fascicle 3 entry. It records a total registered population of 127,277 (人員), split 64,977 male (男) and 62,272 female (女), with sub-populations for samurai households (士族, 15,801 persons / 3,425 households) and lower retainers (卒族, 22,438 persons / 3,308 households). Household and religious-establishment counts follow: 23,440 households (戸數), 361 Shinto shrines (神社), 179 Buddhist halls (佛閣), plus tallies for shrine families (社家, 50), temples (寺院, 434), mountain ascetics (修驗, 219), guild houses (座等, 15), and the outcaste groups eta and hinin (穢多非人, 117). A miscellaneous coin tax (錢) of 25,978 kan 873 mon appears in the far-right column."
  },
  {
   "id": "yonezawa_upper_p113_right",
   "sequence": 82,
   "domain_canonical": "米澤藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "米澤藩",
   "domain_en": "Yonezawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p113_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 113,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（米澤）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 3 (Yonezawa)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yonezawa: religious and outcaste population counts, then the domain's military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 200 of the upper volume, fascicle 3, continues the entry for Yonezawa domain (米澤藩) with no domain marker on the page. The upper part finishes the population-by-status list: Shinto priestly houses 118 persons (72 male, 46 female), Buddhist temple clergy 983 (711 male, 272 female), Shugendō practitioners 710 (406 male, 304 female), 座等 22, and the eta/hinin outcaste statuses 665 (341 male, 324 female); a bracketed note repeats the same 665 persons as the kawaramono and adds that they occupy 117 households. The field label 村數 (village count) is printed with no figure beside it. An editorial note, （以下十三行原朱書）, marks the next thirteen lines as vermilion additions to the manuscript: the standing force on the French system, comprising a Unjū corps of 15 platoons with 92 staff and artillery of four and a half sections with 33 staff, and then the reserve, an infantry force of six battalions with 222 staff, with sub-notes fixing 60 men to a platoon, two platoons to a company, five companies to a battalion, and two guns to an artillery section."
  },
  {
   "id": "yonezawa_lower_p173_left",
   "sequence": 83,
   "domain_canonical": "米澤藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "米澤藩",
   "domain_en": "Yonezawa",
   "image": "images/lower_p173_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 173,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（米澤）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Yonezawa (米澤藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials and military establishment of Yonezawa domain (fascicle 8: 職員兵隊)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the officials-and-military page for Yonezawa domain (○米澤藩) from Fascicle 8 of the survey. The top band gives the military strength as 52 troops (兵隊, 五拾貳員) and the administrative ranks: a governor (知事, no count printed), 3 senior councillors (大参事), 3 junior senior councillors (権大参事), and 6 junior councillors (少参事). Below, in the standard two-register layout, ten named appointees hang beneath their rank headings, read right to left: 都筑利義, 大坪誠之, 毛利安積, 千坂嘉遜齋, 新保新, 大瀧新藏, 庄田惣五郎, 三潴清藏, 黒井繁邦, and 小川源太郎. The entire page belongs to Yonezawa; no other domain appears."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshii_upper_p116_left",
   "sequence": 84,
   "domain_canonical": "吉井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉井藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshii",
   "image": "images/upper_p116_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 116,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（吉井）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, table (fascicle) 3 — Yoshii",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yoshimi's retainer and troop tail, then Yoshii's land assessment and tax head",
   "page_summary_en": "The leaf carries the close of Yoshimi domain's fascicle-3 entry and the opening of Yoshii's. On the right, Yoshimi reports 372 people in the retainer class (201 male, 171 female), made up of 274 shizoku (132 male, 142 female), 94 sotsu (65 male, 29 female) and 4 further persons attached to those two ranks; the categories 社家, 寺院, 穢多 and 非人 are printed but left without figures. Yoshimi's armed strength is given as 7 commanders and post-holders plus 30 rank-and-file soldiers, with 45 peasant-soldiers counted separately. Left of the ○吉井藩 marker, Yoshii is assessed at 10,000 koku with an additional komidaka of 1,494.2983 koku; the printed combined total of 11,494.2993 koku exceeds the sum of its own two parts by 0.001 koku. Yoshii's regular land tax, described as a five-year average drawn from the sixth-month survey of 1870, is 1,982.01428 koku of rice plus 1,365 ryō 3 bu and 104 mon 6 fun 4 rin, with miscellaneous taxes of 25 ryō and 69 mon 6 fun 2 rin."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshii_upper_p117_right",
   "sequence": 85,
   "domain_canonical": "吉井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉井藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshii",
   "image": "images/upper_p117_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 117,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（吉井）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Yoshii (吉井藩): tax, households, and population",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Civil register (kokudaka, tax, households, status-group population, shrines/temples) for Yoshii domain — tail of the record",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf holds the Fascicle 3 civil register for Yoshii domain (吉井藩), a small holding of roughly 10,000 koku in Kōzuke province; the outer-margin running header reads 藩制一覧表第三（吉井）. The record continues from the preceding leaf and shows no ○ boundary marker, so all content here belongs to Yoshii. It records present rice (現米, about 1,982 koku), a combined land-and-miscellaneous tax in gold (金, about 1,390 ryō), 111 households (戸數) split into 81 samurai (士族) and 30 lower-retainer (卒族) households, and a total population (人員) of 111 with the same 81/30 status split. The shrine, temple, village, and troop fields are left blank or marked 不分明 (unclear)."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshii_lower_p176_left",
   "sequence": 86,
   "domain_canonical": "吉井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉井藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshii",
   "image": "images/lower_p176_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 176,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八 （吉井、高鍋）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Yoshii (吉井藩) and Takanabe (高鍋藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment (fascicle 8): Yoshimi overflow, Yoshii (no data), and Takanabe",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 8 officials-and-military leaf, read right to left, spans three domains. The four rank columns at the far right — 2 junior senior councillors (権大参事), 1 junior councillor (少参事), 1 junior junior councillor (権少参事), and 30 riflemen (銃兵) — sit to the right of the ○吉井藩 marker and belong to the previous domain, Yoshimi (吉見藩), whose entry opened on the facing leaf, not to Yoshii. The ○吉井藩 (Yoshii) heading carries the note 審ナラス (\"not investigated\"), so Yoshii itself records no counts. The rest of the page is Takanabe (高鍋藩): 2 senior councillors (大参事, appointees 城勇雄 and 黒水鷲郎), 1 junior senior councillor (権大参事, appointee 坂田蒡), and a military of rifle infantry (銃兵) in 5 platoons of 64 plus 1 artillery unit of 54 gunners with 6 cannon (大砲)."
  },
  {
   "id": "takamatsu_upper_p117_left",
   "sequence": 87,
   "domain_canonical": "高松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高松藩",
   "domain_en": "Takamatsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p117_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 117,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高松）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Takamatsu (高松藩): land assessment and tax",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takamatsu domain land-assessment and tax totals (kokudaka, reclaimed land, regular and miscellaneous tax)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Fascicle 3 entry for Takamatsu domain (高松藩), marked by the ○ boundary marker before the header ○高松藩. It records the domain's fiscal base: an assessed yield (草高) of 120,000 koku, additional and newly-reclaimed land (込高・新田高改出高) of 85,387 koku, and a grand total (〆) of 205,387 koku. The regular tax (正税) is given as 98,262 koku of rice (正税米) and 9,662 koku of barley (正税麥), with a miscellaneous tax (雜税) of 21,351 ryō and a small vermilion-seal exempt-land (朱印地) figure of 975 koku; a marginal note flags that the following lines were written in vermilion in the original manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "takamatsu_upper_p118_right",
   "sequence": 88,
   "domain_canonical": "高松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高松藩",
   "domain_en": "Takamatsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p118_right.jpg",
