   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高松）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Takamatsu (高松藩): population by status and military",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takamatsu domain population-by-status counts (commoners, Shinto/Buddhist clergy, outcaste groups, with male/female splits) and the domain's 1870 military establishment.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Fascicle 3 civil register for Takamatsu domain (高松藩), giving by-status population counts with male/female splits: commoners (平民) 268,238 (男 138,798 / 女 129,440), shrine households (社家) 1,016, Buddhist clergy (僧) 1,711, nuns (尼) 4, eta (穢多) 4,293, and hinin (非人) 1,479. It then records the domain's military establishment as surveyed in the 11th month of 1870: a total of 2,153 troops, itemized by rank and type, together with 40 platoons of infantry and 4 artillery companies of 8 boat-guns each. All data on this leaf belong to Takamatsu; no domain boundary appears."
  },
  {
   "id": "takamatsu_lower_p177_right",
