   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（高松）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Takamatsu (高松藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Takamatsu domain officials (governor and councillors) and military strength (infantry and artillery)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Takamatsu domain (○高松藩, Sanuki province) entry in Fascicle 8, the survey's roster of officials (職員) and troops (兵隊). It heads the domain with the governor (知事, whose name is not printed here) and the councillor ranks: five senior and acting-senior grand councillors (正權大參事) and eight senior and acting-junior lesser councillors (正權少參事), of which five posts are filled and three vacant. The military lines record an infantry (步兵) of 40 platoons at 40 men each — about 1,600 men — and an artillery (砲兵) of 4 companies. Seven named appointees, from Ōkubo Kanō through Sakuma Kumazō, hang in columns below; only Takamatsu appears on this leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "sogano_upper_p148_left",
   "sequence": 91,
   "domain_canonical": "曾我野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "曾我野藩",
   "domain_en": "Sogano",
   "image": "images/upper_p148_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 148,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（曾我野）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Soganō)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Sonobe's troop establishment, then Soganō's assessed yield and tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "The right half of the leaf finishes Sonobe Domain's entry with its 兵隊 (troop) establishment, bracketed by an editorial note that the five lines stood in red ink in the original: one battalion commander who superintends civil and military affairs, two army inspectors, platoon and half-platoon commanders raised separately from shizoku and sotsu, seven head drill instructors and nine assistants, two armoury officers, thirty-six middle-grade and forty-two lower-grade fighting men, twelve drummers, and forty upper, one hundred twenty-six middle and eighty-four lower sotsu riflemen — 410 men in all. The maru-marker ○曾我野藩 then opens Soganō Domain, a 10,000-koku house whose lands lay in two widely separated provinces, Shimotsuke at 4,785.5918 koku and Kawachi at 5,265.121 koku. Against those assessments Soganō returned 535.6685 koku from Shimotsuke and 2,464.7435 koku from Kawachi in regular land tax and miscellaneous imposts, rice and cash reckoned together — 11.2 percent of assessed yield in the one province against 46.8 percent in the other. The two provincial assessments sum to 10,050.7128 koku, some fifty koku above the round 10,000-koku kusadaka printed at the head of the entry."
  },
  {
   "id": "sogano_upper_p149_right",
   "sequence": 92,
   "domain_canonical": "曾我野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "曾我野藩",
   "domain_en": "Sogano",
   "image": "images/upper_p149_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 149,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三 （曾我野）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Sogano (曾我野藩): population, households, and status groups",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Sogano domain population, household, and status-group totals with a two-province combined tax figure (Fascicle 3 civil register).",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page is a totals page from the civil register (Fascicle 3) of the small Sogano domain (曾我野藩); it continues the entry and carries no ○ domain-boundary marker of its own. It records an aggregate population (人員) of 10,612 in 1,794 households (戸數) and a two-province combined assessed yield (草高) of 3,000.412 koku. The population is broken out by status group: 170 samurai (士, 69 households), 99 lower retainers (卒, 28 households), 10,235 commoners (平民), 6 nobles (華族), 61 outcasts (非人), and no eta (穢多), alongside 72 Shinto shrines (神社), 29 Buddhist clergy (僧), and 12 shrine officiants (社務人). A troop figure (兵隊) of 166 is also given."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsu_upper_p149_left",
