   "pdf_page": 149,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Tsu (津藩): land assessment and tax",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsu domain (津藩) landholding, tax, and revenue register from the 1870 Hansei Ichiran civil fascicle 4.",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page carries the complete land-and-tax entry for Tsu domain (○津藩), the seat of the Tōdō house in Ise, in Fascicle 4 of the survey. It records a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 299,334.818 koku and a higher total yield inclusive of newly opened fields (高) of 323,950.002 koku, from which a portion is split off to the Hisai (久居) sub-domain, leaving a residual (殘而) of 270,950.002 koku. The tax figures follow: a regular land tax (正税) of 124,906.121 koku given as a five-year rice average (Rat through Dragon years), a miscellaneous tax (雑税) of 1,544.981 koku, and a small monetary levy in gold (金)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsu_upper_p150_right",
   "sequence": 94,
   "domain_canonical": "津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "津藩",
