   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四 （津）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Tsu (津藩): revenue, households, and population",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsu domain civil data (fascicle 4): revenue totals, kokudaka accounting, population, households, and status-class counts with male/female splits",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the right half of the Fascicle 4 civil spread for Tsu domain (津藩, Ise province); no new ○ marker opens here, so every column continues Tsu's own record. The fiscal cluster gives a combined rice total (合米) of 126,451.102 koku, a gold-to-rice conversion (此米) of 87.512 koku, and their grand total (合) of 126,538.614 koku. The demographic cluster records 52,513 households (戸數) and a total population (人口) of 247,682, broken out by status class: 7,917 samurai (士族), 6,889 rural samurai (郷士族), 1,956 lower retainers (卒族), 28 imperial-tomb keepers (御陵守), 698 shrine officiants (社務人), and 1,336 Buddhist clergy (僧)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsu_lower_p190_right",
   "sequence": 95,
   "domain_canonical": "津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "津藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsu",
   "image": "images/lower_p190_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 190,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（津）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Tsu (津藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Officials and military (fascicle 9): Tsu domain personnel counts and appointee roster, with Sonobe overflow",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Tsu domain (○津藩) entry in Fascicle 9, the survey's roster of officials and military. It records Tsu's personnel and troop counts: 197 military-administration officials (兵制諸官員), a samurai corps (士隊) of 563, locally-settled soldiers (土著之兵士) numbering 971, 1,334 infantry privates (兵卒), and 48 reserve troops (豫備兵). Below, the appointee roster names councillors of the ruling Tōdō house and their deputies. The troop figure of 166 and the three names printed to the right of the ○津藩 marker belong to the preceding domain, Sonobe (園部藩), which shares this leaf — not to Tsu."
  },
  {
   "id": "yachi_upper_p202_right",
   "sequence": 96,
   "domain_canonical": "谷地藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "谷地藩",
   "domain_en": "Yachi",
   "image": "images/upper_p202_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 202,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 （谷地・松江）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Yachi (谷地藩) and the opening of Matsue (松江藩)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Civil-register (F5) tail of Yachi domain and the opening kokudaka block of the neighbouring Matsue domain — a two-domain boundary half-page.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a boundary half-page in the civil register (Fascicle 5) that carries two domains. Most of the columns close out Yachi domain (○谷地藩): 85 temple and hermitage residents (寺庵寮), 132 shrines (神社), 4 districts (郡), 53 villages (村), 52 households (戸數), and a samurai-and-retainer population (士卒) of 150 (83 men, 67 women); its assessed yield is noted as undetermined because Yachi is an internal sub-portion of the parent house. At the left the next domain begins with the ○松江藩 marker, opening Matsue with a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 245,341.159 koku, from which 65,331.391 koku is deducted as a loss allowance."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsue_upper_p202_left",
   "sequence": 97,
   "domain_canonical": "松江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松江藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsue",
   "image": "images/upper_p202_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 202,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（松江）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Matsue (松江藩): tax and revenue",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsue domain's tax and revenue totals (land tax, miscellaneous tax, shrine/temple lands, transit dues) plus the household count",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left half of Matsue domain's fiscal entry in the civil register (Fascicle 5), continuing from the facing page. It records the domain's tax accounts in koku: a gross land-tax figure (正) of 180,009.768 koku, of which 5,155.555 koku is newly reclaimed land (新田); a regular land tax (正税) of 104,657.636 koku; a miscellaneous tax (雑税) of 19,581.039 koku; and their combined total (合) of 124,238.675 koku. Shrine and temple lands (社寺領) come to 6,940.816 koku (1,134.289 shrine, 5,806.527 temple). The page also gives 67,944 households (家數) and separately levied transit and commercial dues (諸運上) of 59,768.5 ryō."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsue_upper_p203_right",
   "sequence": 98,
   "domain_canonical": "松江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松江藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsue",
   "image": "images/upper_p203_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 203,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松江）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Table, Fascicle 5 (Matsue)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsue population, status-group households and shrines",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-5 return for Matsue Domain (松江藩) in Izumo, giving the domain's population and its status-group breakdown. Total population is 295,521 — 152,925 men and 142,304 women, plus 292 hinin whose sex the survey does not break out. Household counts run 951 shizoku, 1,256 sotsu, 638 shrine houses, 732 temples, 966 hachiya-eta and 152 hachiya-hinin; the matching head-counts are 9,924 shizoku, 9,693 sotsu, 3,410 shrine people, 1,986 temple people, 4,395 hachiya-eta and 292 hinin, each split by sex and, for the first four groups, by the number of servants within each sex. The leaf closes with 1,872 shrines, three transport vessels of 1,460, 1,400 and 1,000 koku capacity, and a note that the governor's own household was not recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsue_lower_p208_right",
   "sequence": 99,
   "domain_canonical": "松江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松江藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsue",
   "image": "images/lower_p208_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 208,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（松江）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Matsue (松江藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (san'ji ranks) and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This page from Fascicle 9 gives the officials and military establishment of Matsue domain (松江藩, the Matsudaira house of Izumo). Below the governor it lists the councillor ranks with the number filled: senior councillors (大参事) 2 posts, 1 filled; deputy senior councillors (権大参事) 5 posts, 4 filled; and junior councillors (少参事) 4 posts, 3 filled — with eight appointees named in columns beneath. The military side records an infantry (歩兵) of 40 platoons at 25 men each, an artillery (砲兵) of 4 batteries plus 34 men, a cavalry (騎兵) of 1 platoon of 24 horsemen, and a grand total of 1,850 troops (兵員), with no warships but two transport vessels of 1,460- and 1,400-koku capacity. This is a continuation leaf, so no ○ marker appears; the domain is named in the running header."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuoka_upper_p218_right",
   "sequence": 100,
   "domain_canonical": "福岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p218_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 218,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（福岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Fukuoka (福岡藩): population, status groups, and kokudaka",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukuoka domain (福岡藩) civil register: population by status, villages, kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page opens the Fukuoka domain (○福岡藩) entry in the civil register (Fascicle 5). It records a population of 12,805 broken down by sex, together with the status-group populations: 507 samurai (士族), 365 lower retainers (卒族), 139 shrine households (社家), 39 temple residents (寺), and 65 outcasts (穢多), each with a male/female sub-count. The page also gives 29 villages, notes that the governor's family and warships are not recorded (不記), and states the assessed yield (草高) of 473,100 koku plus a newly reclaimed-field yield (新田高) of 98,041 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuoka_upper_p218_left",
   "sequence": 101,
   "domain_canonical": "福岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p218_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 218,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（福岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Fukuoka (福岡藩): taxes, households, and population",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukuoka domain: aggregate kokudaka, land/miscellaneous taxes (rice, soybeans, silver, copper cash), household counts by status class, and total population with male/female split.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left half of Fukuoka domain's entry in the civil register (Fascicle 5). The fiscal columns give a combined assessed yield (合高) of 571,141 koku and the principal land tax (正租) — 206,066 koku of rice, 26,940 koku of soybeans (大豆), and 133,750 monme of silver — plus a miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 128 koku of rice, 271,140 monme of silver, and 41,800 mon of copper cash. The demographic columns record 67,557 households (戸數) by status class — 1,749 samurai (士族), 5,171 lower retainers (卒族), 416 Shinto priests (神職), 772 Buddhist clergy (僧徒), and 3,700 leather-worker outcasts (皮多) — and a total population (人員) of 366,330, split into 185,320 men and 181,010 women."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuoka_upper_p219_right",
   "sequence": 102,
   "domain_canonical": "福岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p219_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 219,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（福井）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Fukuoka (福岡藩): population and status groups",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukuoka demographics (shares the Fukui-opening leaf; Fukuoka's tail continues here)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens Fukui's entry in the fifth fascicle (第五), a civil and demographic register, but the bulk of the page — read right-to-left, to the right of the ○福井藩 boundary marker — is the population tail of the preceding domain, Fukuoka (福岡藩). It counts Fukuoka's status groups: 6,769 士族 (samurai households, 3,480 male and 3,289 female), 26,005 卒族 (lower retainers, 14,564 male and 11,441 female), 4,052 神職 (Shinto priests), 1,999 僧徒 (Buddhist clergy), and 21,485 皮多 (kawata leather-worker outcastes). It also notes one Western-rigged working vessel (運用舶). The figures beginning at the ○marker and continuing onto the facing leaf belong to Fukui."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuoka_lower_p214_right",
   "sequence": 103,
   "domain_canonical": "福岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p214_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 214,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（福井）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Fukuoka (福岡藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Officials (權大參事 / 少參事 / 權少參事) and military establishment (three shizoku battalions, seven sotsu battalions, 16-gun artillery corps, grand total 4,272 men, plus one Western-style vessel) — the closing portion of Fukuoka domain's fascicle-9 entry, followed by the ○福井藩 boundary marker opening Fukui.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the closing portion of Fukuoka domain's (福岡藩) entry in the ninth fascicle (第九), which lists domain officials and military strength. The officials block records six 権大参事 (provisional senior councillors), two 少参事 (junior councillors), and two 権少参事 (provisional junior councillors), with the appointees' names hung in two registers beneath each rank. The 兵隊 (troops) section gives three battalions raised from 士族 (samurai households), an artillery corps of sixteen guns, and seven battalions raised from 卒族 (lower retainers), for a grand total (総計) of 4,272 men, together with one Western-style vessel (軍艦). At the bottom left the ○福井藩 boundary marker begins the next domain, Fukui — its own figures start at the marker and run onto the facing leaf, so everything to the right of the marker is Fukuoka's."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukui_upper_p219_right",
   "sequence": 104,
   "domain_canonical": "福井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福井藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukui",
   "image": "images/upper_p219_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 219,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（福井）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Fukui (福井藩): kokudaka and status groups",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukui domain civil register: status-group populations (with male/female splits), shrine/temple land, one Western-style ship, and total kokudaka.",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half-page is the opening of Fukui domain's (○福井藩) entry in the fifth fascicle (第五), a civil register. Read right-to-left it gives the status-group head-counts, each split into 男 (male) and 女 (female): 6,769 士族 (samurai households), 26,005 卒族 (lower retainers), 4,052 神職 (Shinto clergy), 1,949 僧徒 (Buddhist clergy), and 21,485 皮多 (kawata outcastes). It further records a total assessed yield (草高) of 336,194.0396 koku, 100 koku of vermilion-seal shrine land (朱印地神社), and 694.919 koku of tax-exempt temple land (除地寺領), notes that the governor's family was not registered (知事家族不記), and lists one Western-style operational vessel (運用舶), its name not given."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukui_upper_p219_left",
   "sequence": 105,
   "domain_canonical": "福井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福井藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukui",
   "image": "images/upper_p219_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 219,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（福井）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Fukui (福井藩): taxes, produce, and households",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukui domain civil register: land-tax totals (main/misc/grand-total current rice), product-tax items, and household counts by status group.",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-page continues Fukui domain's (福井藩) entry in the fifth fascicle (第五). The tax columns are given in 現米 (current rice): a principal land tax (正租) of 109,414.8966 koku, a miscellaneous tax (雑税) of 3,221.9277 koku, and their combined total (都合) of 112,636.8245 koku, followed by product levies on 奉書紙 (fine official mulberry paper, 230,000 sheets), 切石砥石 (cut stone and whetstones), 午房種 (burdock seed), and 鎌幷菜切 (sickles and vegetable knives). The household section gives 66,384 total 戸數 (households), broken down by status: 887 士族 (samurai), 1,439 卒 (lower retainers), and small counts of shrine and temple households — 28 社家 (shrine-priest families), 638 寺 (temples), 22 山伏 (mountain ascetics), 81 道場 (training halls), 66 庵 (hermitages) — plus 46 穢多 and 130 非人 (outcaste groups). This is a single-domain leaf, with no boundary marker."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukui_upper_p220_right",
   "sequence": 106,
   "domain_canonical": "福井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福井藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukui",
   "image": "images/upper_p220_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 220,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福井）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle Five (Fukui)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukui domain population by status, with shrines and the governor's household",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the population return of Fukui domain from fascicle five of the Hansei ichiran. The head figure is 284,935 persons, split 141,272 male and 143,663 female, and the 内 breakdown that follows itemises the non-commoner statuses: 4,819 shizoku, 7,326 sotsu, 154 in shrine-priest households, 2,644 temple residents, 158 yamabushi, 285 in dōjō preaching halls, 72 in hermitages, 191 eta and 467 hinin. Three further entries close the block: 17 shrines, a bracketed governor's household of six (three male, three female), and a bracketed note that no warships are recorded. Every male-plus-female pair sums exactly to its printed total, and the hermitage entry prints a bare 男 with no figure beneath it, glossed by the note 但尼僧 — all seventy-two residents are nuns."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukui_lower_p214_left",
   "sequence": 107,
   "domain_canonical": "福井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福井藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukui",
   "image": "images/lower_p214_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 214,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（福井）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Fukui (福井藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (governor and councilors) and military strength for Fukui han",
   "page_summary_en": "This is an officials-and-military page from the ninth fascicle (第九) for Fukui domain (福井藩), whose head is a member of the Matsudaira (松平) family. The appointment roster records one 知事 (governor) and the councillor grades below him — 4 大参事 (senior councillors), 3 権大参事 (provisional senior councillors), and 5 少参事 (junior councillors) — with the appointees' names set in two horizontal registers under each heading. At the left the 兵隊 (military) block gives Fukui's forces as 11 infantry companies totalling 737 men (歩兵) and one artillery unit of 53 men (砲兵)."
  },
  {
   "id": "mito_lower_p069_right",
   "sequence": 108,
   "domain_canonical": "水戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "水戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Mito",
   "image": "images/lower_p069_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 69,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（水戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Mito (水戸藩): boundary leaf with Yunagaya census",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Boundary page: end of Yunagaya-domain civil census (temples, outcastes, total population with sex split, priests, ascetics, monks, nobility, shrines, soldiers) followed by the ○Mito domain marker and Mito's 350,000-koku headline kokudaka.",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half-page in the seventh fascicle (第七) is the boundary leaf where Mito domain's (水戸藩) entry begins: the ○水戸藩 marker sits near the left edge, and Mito's headline assessment of 高三拾五萬石 — a kokudaka (assessed yield) of 350,000 koku — begins there and continues onto the facing leaf. Read right-to-left, all the census columns to the right of the ○marker belong to the preceding domain, Yunagaya (湯長谷藩), a small Iwaki domain whose entry began on the prior leaf. Those figures record 46 寺 (temples), 5 行屋 (ascetic lodges), 115 穢多 (outcaste houses), a total registered population of 7,766 (3,931 male and 3,835 female), 38 社家 (shrine-priest families), 6 修験 (Shugendō ascetics), 29 僧 (monks), 5 華族 (nobility, 2 male and 3 female), 6 社 (shrines), and 72 兵員 (soldiers)."
  },
  {
   "id": "mito_lower_p069_left",
   "sequence": 109,
   "domain_canonical": "水戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "水戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Mito",
   "image": "images/lower_p069_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 69,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七 （水戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Mito (水戸藩): land assessment and taxes",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mito domain assessed koku (kokudaka), land totals, and tax receipts split between Hitachi and Shimotsuke provinces",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-page covers Mito domain (水戸藩) in the seventh fascicle (第七), recording its land assessment and tax receipts across two provinces. The current assessed yield (當高) of the main Hitachi (常陸) holding is 325,606.037 koku including new fields, of which 20,000 koku was administered by the sub-fief steward Nakayama Bitchū-no-kami; the Shimotsuke (下野) portion adds 18,652.845 koku. Related figures give a base assessment (高) of 297,875.297 koku, new-field additions (新田高) of 9,077.895 koku, and an aggregate holding (合高) of 306,953.192 koku. The tax columns record principal land tax as 42,805.909 koku of rice (正租米) and 28,297 ryō of cash (正租金), while the miscellaneous-tax block (雑税納高) breaks out 3,148.06 koku of 稗 (barnyard millet) alongside separate cash and rice sums for Hitachi and Shimotsuke."
  },
  {
   "id": "mito_lower_p070_right",
   "sequence": 110,
   "domain_canonical": "水戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "水戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Mito",
   "image": "images/lower_p070_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 70,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（水戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 7 (Mito)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mito demographics, religious institutions, status groups, retainers and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf (printed page 116) carries the tail of Mito domain's fascicle-7 civil register, opening with the remaining miscellaneous taxes — 144.493 koku in barnyard millet and 332 ryō 2 bu plus 204 mon in cash — before turning to the demographic block. Mito reports 43,475 households and a population of 254,877 (129,374 male, 125,503 female) across 478 villages, alongside 465 shrines staffed by 2,047 shrine personnel and 208 temples housing 773 monastic residents. The two outcaste status groups are enumerated separately, 655 eta (359 male, 296 female) and 710 hinin (387 male, 330 female); the hinin total carries a printed 「マヽ」 sic-note because the source's own male/female split sums to 717, not 710. The leaf closes with 6,559 domain retainers and 3,815 troops, followed by a two-line addendum written in vermilion in the original manuscript recording 1,362.98 koku of shrine land held outside the village assessment."
  },
  {
   "id": "hikone_lower_p098_right",
   "sequence": 111,
   "domain_canonical": "彦根藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "彦根藩",
   "domain_en": "Hikone",
   "image": "images/lower_p098_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 98,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（彦根）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hikone (彦根藩): kokudaka and tax revenue",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hikone domain land assessment, tax revenue (rice, gold, copper-cash), and totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half-page opens Hikone domain's (彦根藩) entry in the seventh fascicle (第七), a fiscal register, marked by the ○彦根藩 boundary marker with a base assessment (本高) of 200,000 koku noted beside it. It records a gross assessed total (惣高) of 203,887.99 koku including new-field re-surveys, then the tax revenues: principal land tax (正租) of 83,026.042642 koku of rice and 2,248 ryō of gold, and miscellaneous taxes (雑税) of 10,562.823156 koku of rice, 348 ryō of gold, and 9,319.0975 kan of copper cash. Combined totals (合計) and a current-rice figure (現米) of 94,030.0263938 koku close the block. A marginal note dates ten of the lines to the first month of 1871 and records that the governor's family was not registered (知事家族不記)."
  },
  {
   "id": "hikone_lower_p098_left",
   "sequence": 112,
   "domain_canonical": "彦根藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "彦根藩",
   "domain_en": "Hikone",
   "image": "images/lower_p098_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 98,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（彦根）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hikone (彦根藩): itemized taxes and temple land",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hikone domain fiscal register (fascicle 7): continuation of the tax-revenue itemization (內譯), giving the principal land-tax rice and cash, miscellaneous-tax rice and cash, cash coin (錢), and a supplementary block for shrine/temple vermillion-seal land (社寺領朱印地) in Ōmi, Musashi and Shimotsuke provinces.",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-page continues Hikone domain's (彦根藩) fiscal register in the seventh fascicle (第七) under the heading 内訳 (itemized breakdown). The main columns give the principal land tax in rice (正租米) of 83,026.042642 koku and gold (金) of 2,248 ryō, the miscellaneous tax in rice (雑税米) of 20,562.823156 koku and gold of 348 ryō, and 9,319.0975 kan of copper coin (銭). A separate block for shrine- and temple-held vermilion-seal land (社寺領朱印地), spread across Ōmi, Musashi, and Shimotsuke provinces, records an assessed yield (高) of 1,660.10575 koku, its rice equivalent (此米) of about 441 koku, its cash equivalent (此金) of 931 ryō, and an actual yield (物成米) of 729.21652 koku, with a marginal note of forest in three places and 2 tan of dry field."
  },
  {
   "id": "hikone_lower_p099_right",
   "sequence": 113,
   "domain_canonical": "彦根藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "彦根藩",
   "domain_en": "Hikone",
   "image": "images/lower_p099_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 99,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七 （彦根）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hikone (彦根藩): produce taxes and temple land",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Tail of Hikone's fiscal register: miscellaneous produce/grain taxes (barley, soybean, hulled rice, millet), the copper-cash and eiraku-money miscellaneous levy, plus a marginal shrine/temple-land (社寺領) supplementary listing with its combined-provinces kusadaka and a note that the yield equals the main-text total.",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half-page closes Hikone domain's (彦根藩) fiscal register in the seventh fascicle (第七). Read right-to-left, the main columns record the domain's miscellaneous produce and grain taxes: a copper-cash levy (銭) of about 33,979 mon and an eiraku-money charge, together with small grain dues of 籾 (hulled rice, 40.13004 koku), 稗 (barnyard millet, 13.7158 koku), 大豆 (soybean, 6.54341 koku), and 麦 (barley, 15.8678 koku). A parenthetical note flags the following seven lines as a separate shrine-and-temple-land survey (社寺領) entered in the original margin: these give a combined assessed yield (草高) of about 1,660 koku across the three provinces of Ōmi, Musashi, and Shimotsuke, along with small entries for forest (山林) in three places and a yield reconciliation."
  },
  {
   "id": "hikone_lower_p099_left",
   "sequence": 114,
   "domain_canonical": "彦根藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "彦根藩",
   "domain_en": "Hikone",
   "image": "images/lower_p099_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 99,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七 （彦根）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hikone (彦根藩): households and population",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hikone domain household and population register: total households, samurai/soldier/temple/shrine/outcaste household counts, and total population with status and male/female breakdowns.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the demographic register (Fascicle 7) for Hikone (彦根藩), the Ii family's domain in Ōmi province. The right-hand block records 42,145 households (戸數), broken down by status: 817 upper-rank samurai (上等士族), 434 lower-rank samurai (下等士族), 2,707 sotsu or lower-retainer households (卒族), 115 shrine-priest families (社家), 498 Buddhist temples (寺), and small outcaste counts (48 hinin 非人 and 897 eta 穢多). The left-hand block gives a total population (人口) of 177,518 persons — 88,216 male (男) and 89,302 female (女) — itemized by status, including 5,066 upper samurai, 1,542 lower samurai, 6,494 sotsu, 222 shrine attendants (社人), and 2,129 Buddhist clergy (寺侶)."
  },
  {
   "id": "hikone_lower_p100_right",
   "sequence": 115,
   "domain_canonical": "彦根藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "彦根藩",
   "domain_en": "Hikone",
   "image": "images/lower_p100_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 100,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（彦根）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Hikone)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hikone domain — civil and fiscal returns (households, land tax, kokudaka, population)",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation page for Hikone domain (彦根藩) in fascicle 7, covering the domain's directly-held territory (御領リ地). It records 5,078 households (of which 36 are dōjō / training halls), an assessed gross yield (草高) of 34,278.92 koku, regular land tax of 10,232.56445 koku and miscellaneous tax of 1,496.4262 koku in rice (combined rice total 11,728.9907 koku), and cash taxes of 32.1875 + 64.125 ryō combining to 96.375 ryō. It also lists the governor's household (10 persons: 3 male, 7 female) and an eta population of 5,407 (2,708 male, 2,699 female). Shrines are entered only as a territorial notation, with 3 shrine-buildings (identity uncertain) and 88 temples noted separately."
  },
  {
   "id": "hikone_lower_p243_left",
   "sequence": 116,
   "domain_canonical": "彦根藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "彦根藩",
   "domain_en": "Hikone",
   "image": "images/lower_p243_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 243,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百六十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（平戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Hikone (彦根藩): officials and military, opening of Hirado (平戸藩)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "officials and military (fascicle 9): tail of Hikone's officials roster and military figures, plus the opening of Hirado",
   "page_summary_en": "This officials-and-military page (Fascicle 9) reads right to left and carries two domains. Most of the leaf belongs to Hikone (彦根藩): a short military tail continuing from the facing page (infantry and artillery units, 砲兵) followed by Hikone's roster of councillors, arranged under four rank headings — 大参事 (senior councillor), 権大参事 (junior senior councillor), 少参事, and 権少参事 — each topping a column of named appointees. The ○平戸藩 boundary marker (○ marks the start of a new domain) then opens Hirado (平戸藩), given here only as counts — 2 大参事, 5 権大参事, and 1 公議人 (assembly delegate) — before its entry continues on the next page. Everything to the right of the ○平戸藩 marker is Hikone, not Hirado."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitotsubashi_lower_p110_left",
   "sequence": 117,
   "domain_canonical": "一橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一橋",
   "domain_en": "Hitotsubashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p110_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 110,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（一橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions (Hansei ichiran), Table 7 (Hitotsubashi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hitotsubashi domain: assessed yield, land and miscellaneous taxes, cash levies, population and households",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the fascicle-7 (藩制一覧表第七) data block for Hitotsubashi domain (一橋藩). It records a total assessed yield (合高) of 119,428.62958 koku plus 613.241 koku of newly-opened paddy (新田高), followed by five-year-average tax figures: a main land tax of 40,082.4818 koku of rice together with its 2,444.96396-kan cash (永) portion, and miscellaneous levies of 1,310.8015 koku (諸税米), 33.693 koku soybeans, 14.3466 koku perilla, 363 ryō in gold, a second eisen entry of 619.34835 kan, and 111.6 kan of copper cash. The domain's population is 115,228 (58,381 male, 56,847 female) living in 25,705 households. The page carries the printed page number 197."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitotsubashi_lower_p111_right",
   "sequence": 118,
   "domain_canonical": "一橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Hitotsubashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p111_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 111,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（一橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 (Hitotsubashi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Revised household & population census, Hitotsubashi domain",
   "page_summary_en": "A demographic addendum leaf for 一橋藩 (Hitotsubashi) from fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran. Per a marginal vermilion note copied from an attached slip (掛ヶ紙), it records the revised commoner counts (23,570 households; 106,251 persons) alongside the samurai (士族: 1,217 households / 5,154 persons), foot-soldier (卒族: 447 / 1,154) and Shinto-priest (神職: 74 / 316) populations. These combine into grand totals (總合) of 25,234 households and 112,559 persons (男 57,075 / 女 55,488), excluding the priests. The page carries no maru-marker and belongs entirely to Hitotsubashi."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitotsubashi_lower_p111_left",
   "sequence": 119,
   "domain_canonical": "一橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Hitotsubashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p111_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 111,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（一橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey, Fascicle 7 (Hitotsubashi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Religious institutions and outcaste/marginal-status population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Hitotsubashi (一橋藩) demographic tables of the Hansei Ichiran (Fascicle 7), enumerating religious institutions and hereditary marginal-status (\"senmin\") groups. It records 470 Buddhist temples (3 on tax-exempt land) housing 668 people (22 on exempt land), and 139 halls/hermitages housing 12 people. It then breaks out outcaste-group households and populations: eta 1,119 households / 6,105 people (3,101 male, 3,004 female); chasen 46 households / 205 people; onbō (crematory workers) 17 households / 67 people; and ban-hinin (guard-hinin) 30 households / 130 people. A vermilion editorial note flags the following lines as marginal annotations transcribed from an affixed paper slip. Printed page 199."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitotsubashi_lower_p112_right",
   "sequence": 120,
   "domain_canonical": "一橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Hitotsubashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p112_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 112,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（盛岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hitotsubashi (一橋藩) tail, opening of Morioka (盛岡藩)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Civil register (fascicle 7): tail of Hitotsubashi domain's temple/shrine/village counts, then the ○Morioka boundary marker and Morioka's kokudaka.",
   "page_summary_en": "This civil-register half-page (Fascicle 7) sits on a domain boundary and reads right to left. Most of the leaf completes the demographic and religious tally of Hitotsubashi (一橋藩), whose entry runs off the preceding pages: 311 Shinto priests (神職), 452 Buddhist temples (寺院) plus a few on tax-exempt land (除地), 703 shrines (神社), 320 villages (村數), 123 halls and hermitages (堂庵), and notes that the governor's family is not recorded and that there are no warships. The ○盛岡藩 boundary marker (○ marks the start of a new domain) then opens Morioka, the Nanbu family's domain, whose only figure here is its assessed yield (草高) of 130,000 koku; Morioka's remaining data continue on the following pages."
  },
  {
   "id": "morioka_lower_p112_left",
   "sequence": 121,
   "domain_canonical": "盛岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "盛岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Morioka",
   "image": "images/lower_p112_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 112,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七　（盛岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Morioka (盛岡藩): assessed yield, land tax, and product taxes",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Morioka domain kokudaka, land-tax and miscellaneous-tax revenue (rice, soybeans, gold, cash), and product taxes (hinoki boards, charcoal).",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fiscal opening (Fascicle 7) for Morioka (盛岡藩), the Nanbu family's domain in the northeast; there is no ○ boundary marker here, so the whole leaf is Morioka. It records a combined assessed yield (合高) of 160,923.932 koku — including a 516.286-koku internal write-off for flood and waste land and a 30,923.932-koku newly reclaimed increment (新田改出) — and then the regular land tax (正租) in rice (69,927.04 koku), soybeans (大豆, 1,623.93 koku), gold, and cash. It also lists a miscellaneous tax (雜稅) in gold and cash and product taxes in cypress boards (檜柾, 180,000 sheets) and charcoal (炭, 420 bales). A marginal note explains that in the Tora and Tatsu years a five-year fixed-exemption average was applied because of crop failure."
  },
  {
   "id": "morioka_lower_p113_right",
   "sequence": 122,
   "domain_canonical": "盛岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "盛岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Morioka",
   "image": "images/lower_p113_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 113,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七 (森)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Morioka (盛岡藩) population, opening of Mori (森藩)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "人口 (population / demographics), plus opening kokudaka and land-tax columns of the next domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This civil half-page (Fascicle 7, demographic register) carries two domains, split by the ○森藩 boundary marker (○ marks the start of a new domain) at center. The columns to the right of the marker complete Morioka's (盛岡藩) demographics: a total population (人口) of 117,527 — 61,314 male and 56,213 female — plus its eta (穢多) counts (31 households, 189 persons) and a directly administered-land tally of 24,515 households, all under a 'not surveyed in detail' notation. To the left of the marker begin the fiscal figures of neighbouring Mori (森藩): an assessed yield (草高) of 12,500 koku, an additional 1,774.64306 koku, a combined total (合高) of 14,274.64306 koku, and land-tax rice (正租米) of 5,165.59044 koku averaged over 1864–1868."
  },
  {
   "id": "morioka_lower_p245_left",
   "sequence": 123,
   "domain_canonical": "盛岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "盛岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Morioka",
   "image": "images/lower_p245_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 245,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百六十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Morioka (盛岡藩): officials and troops, Hitotsubashi (一橋藩) overflow",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (councillor ranks) and troop strength, fascicle 9",
   "page_summary_en": "This officials-and-military page (Fascicle 9) carries two domains. The ○盛岡藩 boundary marker (○ marks the start of a new domain) opens Morioka near the center: everything to its left is Morioka's data. Morioka records its councillor establishment — 1 大参事 (senior councillor), 2 権大参事, 7 少参事, and 11 権少参事 — but declines to state its troop strength, printing instead a note that the 兵隊 (troops) are to be investigated and reported at a later date. The columns to the right of the marker belong to the previous domain sharing this leaf, Hitotsubashi (一橋藩), whose officials overflow from the facing page: its 703 soldiers (兵士), an assembly delegate (公議人), and a full roster of ten senior administrators (参政)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p013_left",
   "sequence": 124,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p013_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 13,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Izuhara / Tsushima (嚴原藩): land-tax revenue",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Annual land-tax revenue of Izuhara (Tsushima) domain: rice, converted-rice, and cash valuations",
   "page_summary_en": "This is an opening page of Fascicle 1 for Izuhara, the Sō family's domain on Tsushima (嚴原藩), its header stamped with an Imperial Library seal (帝國圖書館藏書). The page reports the domain's annual land tax: a rice (米) figure of 337.848 koku and a converted-rice subtotal of 26,799.187 koku, given as a five-year average of the tax across the domain's holdings on the Kyushu mainland, together with three cash valuations in gold (金) — 43,311, 11,172, and roughly 13,337 ryō. Interlinear notes value the domain's barley (麥, 7,218.597 koku) and mainland soybeans (大豆, 1,862.1198 koku) at a reckoning of about 6.5 ryō per koku. No assessed yield (草高) figure is printed in this Fascicle-1 register."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p014_right",
   "sequence": 125,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p014_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 14,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Izuhara / Tsushima (嚴原藩): fiscal totals and Korea-trade goods",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tsushima (Izuhara) domain fiscal totals and the opening of its Korea public-trade goods list",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Izuhara / Tsushima (嚴原藩) entry in Fascicle 1, giving the domain's fiscal totals. It records grand totals (都合) of 27,137 koku of rice and 64,822 ryō of cash, followed by an itemized breakdown (内) of the components — rice, cash, barley (麥), and soybeans (大豆), each with a cash-equivalent conversion — drawn from a five-year average of miscellaneous taxes collected in the domain's Kyushu jurisdiction. Below are a net shortfall in actual rice (差引不足 現米, 6,727 koku) and a cash surplus (金, 3,437 ryō). The lower-left opens the ○公貿易 heading, beginning the register of goods received each year from Korea through the official trade, starting with white rice (白米, 16,620 bales)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p014_left",
   "sequence": 126,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p014_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 14,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Izuhara / Tsushima (嚴原藩): Korea-trade commodities",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tsushima (Izuhara) domain — Korea-trade commodities and their rice/silver conversion values (continuation)",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page continues Izuhara / Tsushima's (嚴原藩) account of goods received each year through the official Korea trade (公貿易 with Chosŏn), begun on the facing page. Rather than a household or land register, it is a commodity ledger: each line is a traded good with a quantity and, for the major items, a silver or copper-cash conversion value and a small inline exchange-rate note. The goods listed include kōboku tribute cotton (公木, 33,245 bolts), soybeans (大豆) and azuki beans (小豆), kudzu and hagi-bark ropes, bent nails, folded floss, large straw mats, and raw ramie, along with rice subtotals for goods exchanged for rice. There is no ○ boundary marker on this leaf — all of it is Tsushima."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p015_right",
   "sequence": 127,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p015_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 15,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Izuhara / Tsushima (嚴原藩): Korea-trade imports",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tsushima Korea-trade imports: itemized list of goods received from Korea with silver-equivalent valuations",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a further page of the Izuhara / Tsushima (嚴原藩) entry in Fascicle 1, listing goods received each year from Korea through the domain's official trade (公貿易). Each line names a commodity, its quantity, and an equivalent value (代) in silver monme (匁) with a per-unit conversion rate. The items shown here include ginseng (人參), tiger and leopard pelts (虎皮・豹皮), white cloth, pongee, and cotton, oiled cloth, writing brushes and ink sticks, split stakes and boards, sail matting, large bamboo, and straw; a summary line values eleven of the miscellaneous articles (十一品) at about 3,652.5 monme of silver. There is no ○ boundary marker on this leaf — all of it is Tsushima."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p015_left",
   "sequence": 128,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p015_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 15,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Tsushima/Izuhara (嚴原藩): Korea-trade goods and their silver values",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tsushima (Izuhara) domain — continuation of the Korea-trade (公貿易) commodity list: itemized goods received annually from Chosŏn with their silver-equivalent (代銀) valuations, plus grand-total and two internal subtotals.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Tsushima (Izuhara) domain's trade register in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran, listing the goods received each year through the domain's 公貿易 (official trade with Korea). Read right to left, each column names a commodity — wax-coated wrappers, cloth packs, oiled and hat paper, oil, walnuts, pine nuts, dried chestnuts, jujubes, and figured mats — paired with its 代銀 (silver-equivalent value) and per-unit conversion notes. The final columns give a grand total silver equivalent of about 14,692,657 monme together with two 内 (of-which) subtotals. Because the page tallies only goods and their monetary value, it carries no population figures or land assessment."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p016_right",
   "sequence": 129,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p016_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 16,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Tsushima/Izuhara (嚴原藩): traded commodities and appraised values",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Products / trade goods (産物) register for Izuhara (Tsushima) domain — continuation listing commodities with quantities and appraised values (代)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf belongs to Tsushima (Izuhara) domain's trade register in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran, listing commodities each with a quantity and an appraised silver value (代). Entries include white rice (about 6,393 bales), pepper (3,100 kin), sappanwood dyewood (7,005 kin), alum, Japanese vermilion, and patterned paper (1,800 sheets), followed by finished luxury goods — maki-e lacquered mirrors, trays, and inkstone boxes, a portable field bath, and a small gold folding screen. A short inset note explains that the accompanying silver and rice cover the costs of escorting shipwrecked drifters, staffing the Korean checkpoint, and other official-trade sundries."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p016_left",
   "sequence": 130,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p016_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 16,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Tsushima/Izuhara (嚴原藩): copper imports from the Korea trade",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tsushima official Korea-trade (kōbōeki) copper imports: silver-value prices and quantities, with an explanatory note on the abolished copper guild",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Tsushima (Izuhara) domain's trade register in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran, itemizing the copper obtained through the domain's 公貿易 (official trade with Korea). Each entry pairs a silver value in kan-monme with a copper product and quantity: a nested copper wash-basin set, 荒銅 (crude copper) of 26,900 kin, and three grades of 吹銅 (refined copper) — 11,000 kin, 6,500 kin, and 3,629 kin. Interlinear notes explain the freight and expense reckoning and record gifts allotted to the Korean interpreter-officials; a further memorandum notes that the former mountain-works and copper-guild purchasing arrangements had been abolished, upsetting the domain's copper-trade projections. Two grand totals in cash close the page."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p017_right",
   "sequence": 131,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p017_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 17,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一 （嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Tsushima/Izuhara (嚴原藩): Wakan and checkpoint expenses",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tsushima (Izuhara) domain sundry expenditures: Wakan-and-two-checkpoints expense block, itemized rice/cash breakdown, and the opening of the drifted-persons relief expense item",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Tsushima (Izuhara) domain's expense accounts in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran. It records the ○和館兩關所入費 block — the running costs of the Wakan (the domain's Japanese trading factory at Pusan in Korea) together with its two barrier checkpoints — totaling 56,618 ryō in gold plus a small silver remainder, resolved into a rice component of about 819 koku and a cash component of 815 kan. A 此小譯 (breakdown of the above) then itemizes the sub-amounts, with notes explaining that the money covers stipend-rice, brushes, ink, paper, oil, and wax, and the year-round upkeep of officials posted at the checkpoints and the Wakan. At the far left the next item, expenses for shipwrecked drifters and their rice rations, is opened and continues on the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_upper_p017_left",
   "sequence": 132,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p017_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 17,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Tsushima/Izuhara (嚴原藩): castaway-relief and repatriation expenses",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tsushima domain (嚴原藩): itemized breakdown and explanatory notes for special expenditures on castaway relief and Korea repatriation / Nagasaki ship costs",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Tsushima (Izuhara) domain's expense accounts in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran. Under the heading 此小譯 (the itemized breakdown of this), it records special outlays in rice (米, in koku) and copper cash (錢) tied to the domain's diplomatic role: provisions and shipboard costs for hosting drifting castaways (漂民), collecting them from Nagasaki, and repatriating them by ship to Korea. The total castaway-relief expense comes to about 94 koku of rice and 13,809,074 in cash, with further lines for the Nagasaki pickup, the Korea repatriation, and relief for castaways from other domains. Explanatory notes qualify each pair of figures and cross-reference earlier lines."
  },
  {
   "id": "izuhara_upper_p022_left",
   "sequence": 133,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/upper_p022_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 22,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（嚴原）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 1 (Izuhara)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Izuhara households, population by status, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf continues the fascicle-1 return for Izuhara (Tsushima) domain; no maru-marker appears on it, so the whole page belongs to the domain named in the running header. It opens with a rice allowance of 271.91743 koku, explained by a note that the amount was granted through the several commissioners in charge, then gives the domain aggregates: 13,975 households and a population of 66,624, split 34,160 male and 32,464 female. Three status groups are broken out with 外ニ (\"in addition\"): 1,837 samurai households holding 10,960 people, 1,082 sotsu households holding 4,102, and 173 shrine-attendant households holding 910 — in each case the male and female sub-counts sum exactly to the group total. Under the heading 對馬國 (Tsushima Province) the page closes with 191 shrines and 287 houses of temples and blind monks, with a split-line note that the domain's holdings in the Hō-Hi provinces are recorded separately."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsushima_lower_p121_left",
   "sequence": 134,
   "domain_canonical": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "嚴原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsushima",
   "image": "images/lower_p121_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 121,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八　職員　兵隊",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Tsushima/Izuhara (嚴原藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials and military establishment of Izuhara (Tsushima) domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the officials-and-military page for Tsushima (Izuhara) domain in Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran, whose ○ domain-boundary marker and columns fill the whole leaf. The upper register prints the standard rank headings in descending order — 知事 (governor), 大参事, 権大参事, 少参事, and 権少参事 — with a note that the appointees' personal names are not recorded here, and the faint name columns hang beneath. The military block gives 兵員 (total troops) of 478 men, 歩兵 (infantry) of 6 platoons, and 砲兵 (artillery) of 2 sub-platoons."
  },
  {
   "id": "nishio_upper_p043_right",
   "sequence": 135,
   "domain_canonical": "西尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Nishio",
   "image": "images/upper_p043_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 43,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（西尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Nishio (西尾藩): land assessment, population, and status groups",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Civil register: land yield, tax revenue, households, population, and non-commoner status populations (temple/shrine, outcast) for Nishio domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the civil register for Nishio domain (西尾藩), a Matsudaira domain in Mikawa province, in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran. It records the domain's actual combined tax rice (現合米) of 23,668.8474 koku, its copper-cash and gold tax figures, a 戸數 (household count) of 12,083 houses, and a total 人口 (population) of 52,078, split into 25,327 men and 25,792 women. The lower portion breaks out the non-commoner status groups: temple and hermitage clergy (寺庵, 232 houses, with a nested tally of priests, nuns, mountain ascetics, and lay devotees), the 穢多 outcast group (28 houses, 103 people), the 非人 outcast group (24 houses, 83 people), and 社家 (Shinto shrine households, 24 houses with 147 shrine people)."
  },
  {
   "id": "nishio_lower_p137_right",
   "sequence": 136,
   "domain_canonical": "西尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Nishio",
   "image": "images/lower_p137_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 137,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（西尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Nishio (西尾藩): junior councillor ranks",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (shokuin) — assistant-councillor ranks for Nishio han",
   "page_summary_en": "This is an officials page for Nishio domain (西尾藩) in Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran, continuing the roster from the preceding leaf. It carries only the later councillor ranks — 権大参事 (senior provisional councillor), 少参事 (junior councillor), and 権少参事 (junior provisional councillor) — the governor and senior councillor having appeared earlier, so this leaf shows no ○ domain marker and no governor's surname. The 権大参事 rank lists 12 named appointees; 少参事 gives 7, with a note that one man was dismissed and another appointed in the fifth month; and 権少参事 gives 10. No military figures appear on this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "nihonmatsu_upper_p043_left",
   "sequence": 137,
   "domain_canonical": "二本松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "二本松藩",
   "domain_en": "Nihonmatsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p043_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 43,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（二本松）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Nihonmatsu (二本松藩): land assessment and tax revenue",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Nihonmatsu domain kokudaka, actual-rice tax, cash revenue, and miscellaneous taxes; plus the tail-end demographic/status block of the preceding domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This civil register opens the Nihonmatsu domain (二本松藩) entry in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran, marked by the ○ domain-boundary marker at ○二本松藩. Nihonmatsu's own figures, to the left of the marker, give a 草高 (assessed yield) of 50,000 koku, an actual-rice figure of 11,839.2381 koku, collected cash revenue (収納金) of 3,949 ryō 1 bu in gold plus about 28 kan in copper, and miscellaneous taxes (諸税金) of 150 ryō 3 bu in gold plus 1,186 kan in copper. Everything to the right of the ○ marker — the village count, samurai and foot-soldier households, and the population with its 士族 (samurai households) and 卒 (foot-soldier) breakdowns — is the closing block of the previous domain sharing this leaf, not Nihonmatsu."
  },
  {
   "id": "nihonmatsu_lower_p137_left",
   "sequence": 138,
   "domain_canonical": "二本松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "二本松藩",
   "domain_en": "Nihonmatsu",
   "image": "images/lower_p137_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 137,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（二本松）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Nihonmatsu (二本松藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials and military (職員兵隊) — Nihonmatsu domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the officials-and-military page for Nihonmatsu domain (二本松藩) in Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran, the only domain on the leaf, opened by the ○二本松藩 boundary marker. Reading right to left, the rank headings run from 知事 (governor) down through 大参事 (senior councillor, one person), with the governor Niwa Yoshinari (丹羽至善) named in the lower band and eight further appointees listed for the junior ranks. The military entry records 兵員 不記 (troop count not recorded), with a note explaining that only the cadre from the battalion commander down to the first-rank flank guards — 51 persons — is enumerated, so the domain's full army strength is not disclosed."
  },
  {
   "id": "nihonmatsu_lower_p138_right",
   "sequence": 139,
   "domain_canonical": "二本松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "二本松藩",
   "domain_en": "Nihonmatsu",
   "image": "images/lower_p138_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 138,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（庭瀨）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 8 (Niwase)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page (職員及職制, personnel and office-structure) records domain officials and military strength. Most of the page belongs to Nihonmatsu Domain (二本松藩): its office-structure counts appear in the upper register — 2 deputy senior councilors (權大參事), 3 junior councilors (少參事), a deputy junior councilor post (權少參事, no count printed), 30 standing troops (常備兵) and 30 reserve troops (豫備兵) — while its named personnel fill the lower register: six senior councilors (脇屋舍, 平山外衞, 廣瀨七郎左衞門, 崎田傳, 梅原新吾, 千賀正雄) and three public assemblymen (公議人: 森安靜夫, 德田金雄, 三宅礼). The maru-marker ○庭瀨藩 opens the entry for Niwase Domain (庭瀨藩) to its left, showing only the governor post (知事) and 3 deputy senior councilors (權大參事) before the entry continues on the following page. The printed page number is 252."
  },
  {
   "id": "obama_upper_p066_left",
   "sequence": 140,
   "domain_canonical": "小濱藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小濱藩",
   "domain_en": "Obama",
   "image": "images/upper_p066_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 66,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小濱）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey Table No. 2 (Obama)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Obama kokudaka, tax rice, and products; Oizumi (Shonai) military overflow",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Obama domain's entry in Fascicle 2 of the Hansei Ichiran (1870 Dajokan domain survey). Left of the ○小濱藩 marker, Obama reports a gross assessed yield (kusadaka) of 106,599.3482 koku (original assessment, new fields, and reassessed output combined), regular tax rice of 130,102 bales 3 to 7 sho 1 go (4 to per bale), and, under 'various products and taxes,' lacquerware worth 564 ryo, 90 kanme of arrowroot starch, 14,576 kan 24 me of candles, and 8,750 nails; the 高 (yield) field prints with no figure. Right of the marker, the tail of the preceding Oizumi (Shonai) entry overflows onto the page: 34 shrines and temples, 35 rifle platoons of 40-60 men each, 4 artillery units, and 4 further units of 30 attached gunners apiece."
  },
  {
   "id": "obama_upper_p067_right",
   "sequence": 141,
   "domain_canonical": "小濱藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小濱藩",
   "domain_en": "Obama",
   "image": "images/upper_p067_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 67,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（小濱）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Obama (小濱藩): products and miscellaneous tax",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Obama domain — products/specialty-goods output and miscellaneous tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half-page belongs to Obama domain (小濱藩) and comes from Fascicle 2 of the survey, which records each domain's economy. Reading right to left, it lists the domain's specialty outputs: 油 (oil) at 1,239.98 koku, 魚漁 (fisheries) valued at 25,469 ryō, 銅 (copper) at 173 units, 石灰 (lime) at 334,737 bales, and 生糸 (raw silk) at about 1,305 kanme, the silk noted as tax-exempt on a five-year average. It then records miscellaneous cash receipts, including a 雜税金 (miscellaneous tax) of 20,696 ryō and a 5,210-ryō toll on freight passing the Tsuruga-road gate (敦賀道之口通荷運上). A far-left column gives the domain's 戸數 (household count) of 23,886."
  },
  {
   "id": "obama_upper_p067_left",
   "sequence": 142,
   "domain_canonical": "小濱藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小濱藩",
   "domain_en": "Obama",
   "image": "images/upper_p067_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 67,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（大垣）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Obama (小濱藩): population and status groups",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Obama demographics (shares the Ogaki-opening leaf; Obama's tail continues here)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the entry for the next domain, Ogaki, with its ○ domain-boundary marker and land figures, but the bulk of the page — everything to the right of that marker, read right to left — is the demographic close of the previous domain, Obama (小濱藩). It records a 人口 (population) of 105,957 (52,713 male and 53,244 female), the 士族 (samurai households) at 475 households and 4,237 persons, and the 卒族 (lower-retainer households) at 249 households and 1,975 persons, each with male and female splits. It also counts 484 神社 (Shinto shrines) and 634 寺 (Buddhist temples), with a temple clergy population of 681 men and 272 women plus 12 尼 (nuns)."
  },
  {
   "id": "obama_lower_p150_right",
   "sequence": 143,
   "domain_canonical": "小濱藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小濱藩",
   "domain_en": "Obama",
   "image": "images/lower_p150_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 150,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（小濱）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 8 (Obama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Obama domain officials with Ōizumi military-establishment overflow",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page opens the Obama (小濱藩) block in Fascicle 8 of the Han-sei Ichiran. To the LEFT of the ○小濱藩 marker stand Obama's civil offices — 知事 and 権知事 (both printed without a count or name), 大参事 (2 members, with the names Muramatsu Samon and Sakai Shūkichi at the foot), and 権大参事 (3 members, currently 4 in all) — closing with the two kōgijin (公議人) delegates Sōma Kitarō and Toimiya Hazama. The columns to the RIGHT of the marker are military entries overflowing from the previous domain, Ōizumi (the renamed Shōnai domain): 35 rifle platoons at 40–60 men each, a 4-company heavy assault corps (大破隊; 4 guns and 24 gunners per company = 16 guns and 96 gunners), and 4 companies of attached riflemen at 30 men each (120). The printed book page number is 276."
  },
  {
   "id": "obama_lower_p150_left",
   "sequence": 144,
   "domain_canonical": "小濱藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小濱藩",
   "domain_en": "Obama",
   "image": "images/lower_p150_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 150,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（小濱）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 8 (Obama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Obama domain officials roster (fascicle 8): junior councillors",
   "page_summary_en": "The left leaf of the Obama-domain (小濱藩) fascicle-8 (officials) entry, continuing the appointee roster. A top band carries two rank headings — 少參事 (junior councillor), whose column notes five members (五員) plus a subsidiary count 同四員, and 權少參事 (acting junior councillor), counted at three (三員) in a warichu below — while the appointees' names hang in a lower band. Eleven officials are named, reading right to left: 都築平六郎, 行方百太郎, 糟谷寸斗平, 池田艮三, 武久權十郎 (the five 少參事); 山川貞藏, 須田鍵五郎, 寺田純藏 (the three 權少參事); and 原田顯藏, 針谷八十吉, 成田其一, whose rank heading falls on the adjoining leaf. No maru-marker appears, so the whole leaf belongs to Obama; the printed page number is 二百七十七 (277)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ogaki_upper_p067_left",
   "sequence": 145,
   "domain_canonical": "大垣藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大垣藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p067_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 67,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（大垣）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Ogaki (大垣藩): kokudaka and establishment",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ogaki domain (大垣藩): population, status-group households, temples/shrines/ascetics, military establishment, and kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 2 civil register opens the entry for Ogaki domain (大垣藩), marked by the ○ domain-boundary marker and annotated with a true assessed yield of 100,000 koku. It records the domain's 草高 (assessed yield) as 131,106.43158 koku, given with notes that it includes newly reclaimed and resurveyed land and is stated as a five-year average. The register also notes Ogaki's military establishment: a two-battalion, English-style army and an eight-gun artillery unit."
  },
  {
