   "pdf_page": 68,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（大垣）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Ogaki (大垣藩): tax accounts and population",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ogaki domain fiscal register: land-tax rice, miscellaneous-tax rice, cash and silver tax, an editorial ◎ block giving the flood-adjusted average figures, additional received stipend, tax-rice subtotal, household count, and population with a male/female split.",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 2 fiscal page covers Ogaki domain (大垣藩) in Mino province. The right-hand block gives the registered figures: 正租米 (land-tax rice) of 51,069.41 koku, 雜稅米 (miscellaneous-tax rice) of 34.31 koku, and a 金 (cash tax) of 7,161 ryō plus a small amount of 銀 (silver). A double-circle ◎ block to the left restates these as a flood-adjusted average — land-tax rice of 49,392.78 koku — with a note that severe flooding in the Tiger and Dragon years left the earlier figure short. The page also records an 外受領高 (additional received stipend) of 405 koku, identified as land of the Nangū shrine at Miyashiro in Fuwa district, along with 242 家 (households), of which 38 are shrine households, and a 人口 (population) of 979 (466 male, 513 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ogaki_upper_p068_left",
   "sequence": 147,
   "domain_canonical": "大垣藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大垣藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p068_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 68,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二 （大垣）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Ogaki (大垣藩): temple-land register",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ogaki domain temple-lands register: grants, tax rice, and temple demographics",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-page continues the Fascicle 2 entry for Ogaki domain (大垣藩) with a register of 寺領 (temple landholdings). Reading right to left, it lists four temples — 金蓮寺 (Konren-ji), 妙應寺 (Myōō-ji), 乙津寺 (Ottsu-ji) in Kagashima, and 阿願寺 (Agan-ji) in Higashijima — each with its 受領高 (received grant), the 租税米 (tax rice) levied on it, a household count, and a resident population broken into men, women, and 僧 (monks). Konren-ji, for example, is recorded with a 35-koku grant, 17.37 koku of tax rice, 43 households, and 194 residents; the grants for the other three run from 10 to about 55 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "ogaki_upper_p069_right",
   "sequence": 148,
   "domain_canonical": "大垣藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大垣藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p069_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 69,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大垣）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table 2 (Ōgaki)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōgaki domain households and population, with supervised former-hatamoto fief parcels",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of Ōgaki domain's entry in Table 2 (households and population). The page first closes an itemization of former hatamoto fiefs under the domain's temporary supervision: one parcel of 4 households (1 temple) and 21 residents (9 male, 8 female, 4 monks), and a parcel at Norimatsu village, Katagata district assessed at 520.888 koku with 135.167 koku tax rice, noted as the former holdings of Uemura Umenosuke and Maeda Shinpachirō. The domain totals follow: 18,320 households and 78,667 people, though the printed male-female split (40,527 / 38,350) over-adds that total by 210 — an inconsistency in the source itself. A status breakdown lists 589 shizoku households (3,115 people), 653 sotsu households (2,640 people), and 14 Shinto-priest households (81 people)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ogaki_lower_p151_right",
   "sequence": 149,
   "domain_canonical": "大垣藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大垣藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p151_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 151,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大垣）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Ogaki (大垣藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Ogaki domain officials (governor and councillors) and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 8 page covers the officials and military of Ogaki domain (大垣藩), opened by the ○ domain-boundary marker (○大垣藩). The officials section lists the domain governor (知事, with no appointee named here), one 大参事 (senior councillor, Ōhara Zesui), two 権大参事 (acting senior councillors, Takaoka and Ōhara Susumu), and one 少参事 (junior councillor, Onozaki Kurao), with the appointees' names set in a lower register. The military figures give a 銃隊 (rifle corps) of six platoons totalling 360 men, a 砲隊 (artillery corps) of 8 cannon, and 77 砲臺守衞士 (battery-guard soldiers)."
  },
  {
   "id": "oshi_upper_p071_right",
   "sequence": 150,
   "domain_canonical": "忍藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "忍藩",
   "domain_en": "Oshi",
   "image": "images/upper_p071_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 71,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（忍）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 2 (Oshi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Oshi domain: assessed yield and five-year-average tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Oshi domain (忍藩) entry in fascicle 2 of the Hansei ichiran. The domain's nominal assessment (本高) is 100,000 koku, while its surveyed gross yield (草高), which the source says includes newly opened paddy and re-surveyed increases, is 141,752.47387 koku. Tax receipts are given as a five-year average covering 1864 to 1868: regular land tax in rice (正租米) of 34,633.6714 koku plus 12,541.76809 kan of eisen cash (a rice equivalent of 1,567.721 koku at 8 kan per koku), miscellaneous tax in rice (雜税米) of 2,514.5654 koku plus 3,964.4167 kan (495.5021 koku), and a head-money levy (丁錢) of 454.067 kan (5.9123 koku). A compilers' note records that the eight lines that follow stood in vermilion in the manuscript original; the first two of them appear here and give a separate 正租 of 39,126.2674 koku and 11,411.59029 kan of eisen."
  },
  {
   "id": "oshi_upper_p071_left",
   "sequence": 151,
   "domain_canonical": "忍藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "忍藩",
   "domain_en": "Oshi",
   "image": "images/upper_p071_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 71,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（忍）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Fascicle 2 (Oshi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Oshi domain tax receipts (five-year averages) and shrine/temple grant total",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Oshi domain (忍藩) fiscal entry in fascicle 2. The first five columns close an eight-line block that the Meiji compilers note was written in red ink in the original manuscript: miscellaneous tax rice 2,597.4934 koku, ei cash 2,469.98988 kanmon, gold 476.625 ryō, silver 7,453.064 monme, and chōsen coin 454.067 kanmon, all stated as five-year averages. The total current revenue (合現) is printed as 39,217.4222 koku, with a compiler's parenthetical noting that the itemized components actually sum to 39,217.3722 koku — a 0.05-koku discrepancy they preserved as found. An \"extra\" (外) block records 635.7 koku of grants received by 5 shrines and 28 temples, collected as 112.6054 koku of regular tax rice, 23.0625 ryō in gold, and 39.28708 kanmon in ei cash."
  },
  {
   "id": "oshi_upper_p072_right",
   "sequence": 152,
   "domain_canonical": "忍藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "忍藩",
   "domain_en": "Oshi",
   "image": "images/upper_p072_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 72,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（忍）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Oshi (忍藩): households and population",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Oshi domain (Musashi) civil register: currency reserves, household counts by status, temples/shrines, and population by status with male/female splits",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 2 civil register covers Oshi domain (忍藩) in Musashi province. It records the domain's cash reserve of 202 kan and its 銀 (silver) holdings, then breaks the 戸数 (households) — 24,654 in all — into 士族 (samurai) at 458, 卒族 (lower retainers) at 1,180, shrine families at 64, 寺 (temples) at 430, 修験 (Shugendō practitioners) at 10, and the 穢多 and 非人 (outcaste) groups. It then gives a 人口 (total population) of 113,070 (56,907 male, 56,163 female), with separate populations for the samurai, lower-retainer, and shrine-family classes, each split by sex. A few of the printed status figures do not add exactly to their stated totals; these are minor arithmetic inconsistencies carried over from the original."
  },
  {
   "id": "oshi_upper_p072_left",
   "sequence": 153,
   "domain_canonical": "忍藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "忍藩",
   "domain_en": "Oshi",
   "image": "images/upper_p072_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 72,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（大洲）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Oshi (忍藩): status-group populations",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Oshi demographics (shares the Ozu-opening leaf; Oshi's tail continues here)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the entry for the next domain, Ozu, with its ○ domain-boundary marker and land figures, but most of the page — everything to the right of that marker, read right to left — is the demographic close of the previous domain, Oshi (忍藩). It records the 穢多 (outcaste) population at 2,723 (1,386 male, 1,337 female), the 非人 (outcast) population at 42 (23 male, 19 female), the population on shrine and temple lands at 473 (233 male, 240 female), and the 寺 (temple) population, along with a small governor's household and a shrine tally."
  },
  {
   "id": "ozu_upper_p072_left",
   "sequence": 154,
   "domain_canonical": "大洲藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大洲藩",
   "domain_en": "Ozu",
