   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（大洲）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Ozu (大洲藩): land assessment and population",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ozu domain civil/economic register: land assessment, troops, governor's household, villages, shrines, and outcaste/religious populations",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 2 civil and economic register opens the entry for Ozu domain (○大洲藩) in Iyo province, with the ○ domain-boundary marker set to the left of all the data columns, so every field to its right belongs to Ozu. It records the domain's 草高 (assessed yield) as roughly 60,906 koku, of which the 内田高 (paddy-field yield) is 36,473.4 koku. The page also gives the domain's 兵隊 (troops) as 14 platoons of about 40 men each, a small governor's household of 3 persons, a shrine count of 2,083, and outcaste populations of 2,723 穢多 (eta) and 42 非人 (hinin), among other village and religious figures."
  },
  {
   "id": "ozu_upper_p073_right",
   "sequence": 155,
   "domain_canonical": "大洲藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大洲藩",
   "domain_en": "Ozu",
   "image": "images/upper_p073_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 73,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（大洲）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Ozu (大洲藩): land-tax accounts and households",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ozu domain land-tax accounts: dry-field koku, crop yields (rice/soybean/sesame), cash miscellaneous tax, paddy/dry-field breakdown, and samurai-class households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 2 land-and-tax page continues the entry for Ozu domain (大洲藩) in Iyo province. Reading right to left, it records the 畑高 (dry-field assessment) of 24,432.6 koku with its tax-rate note, then a crop-and-cash block of 實米 (actual rice) 25,087.1 koku, 豆 (beans) 11,923 koku, 胡麻 (sesame) 222.1 koku, and a 雜稅金 (miscellaneous cash tax) of 195 ryō. It goes on to a 用高 (allotted yield) of 9,268.9 koku with a Niiya-branch note, a 殘リ用高 (remaining allotted yield) of 51,637.1 koku, and a paddy-versus-dry-field breakdown. The page closes with the 士卒族戸數 (samurai and lower-retainer households) at 1,245 and a 人口 (population) of 5,018 (2,541 male, 2,471 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ozu_upper_p073_left",
   "sequence": 156,
   "domain_canonical": "大洲藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大洲藩",
   "domain_en": "Ozu",
   "image": "images/upper_p073_left.jpg",
