   "pdf_page": 153,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大村）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 8 (Ōmura)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Ōzu domain — han officials (少参事/権少参事) and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page carries the closing portion of the 大洲藩 (Ōzu) entry in Fascicle 8 (officials and military) of the Hansei Ichiran. Ōzu lists 4 Junior Councillors (少参事) and 4 Acting Junior Councillors (権少参事), with all eight officials named in full (瀧野佐衞, 山路侯齋, 杵志弓, 菅八藏; 中村惇, 玉井俊次郎, 垂水小平司, 窪田文彦). Its military establishment comprises a rifle corps of five companies (銃隊 第一〜五番) plus one artillery battery (大砲 壹隊), together numbering 730 troops (此兵員七百三拾人). The circle-marker ○大邨藩 at the far left opens the next domain, Ōmura, whose own data continues on the following page; the running header names 大村 as provenance. The printed page number is 二百八十二 (282)."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameyama_upper_p092_left",
   "sequence": 160,
   "domain_canonical": "龜山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p092_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 92,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（龜山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Kameyama)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Kameyama land assessment and tax receipts, with Karatsu military overflow",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Kameyama domain entry in fascicle 2 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran. Kameyama's gross assessment (草高) is 75,418.9818 koku, made up of a base assessment of 60,000 koku plus 15,418.9818 koku of newly reclaimed and re-surveyed land (込高新田改出高); the two components sum exactly to the stated total. Regular land tax comes in two forms, 24,404.6762 koku of rice and 3,091 mon in cash, while miscellaneous taxes are recorded as 100 bales of rice, qualified by the note that the amount varies from year to year; the itemisation that follows credits 12 bales to village tea and mulberry levies and 86 bales to levies on newly opened woodland and bamboo thickets, with the remaining 2 bales appearing on the next leaf. The three columns printed to the right of the ○龜山藩 marker are the tail of the preceding Karatsu entry: an infantry battalion of 360 men (sixty to a platoon, six platoons to a battalion), an infantry reserve of 80, and an artillery company of 30 with a reserve of 31."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameyama_upper_p093_right",
   "sequence": 161,
   "domain_canonical": "龜山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p093_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 93,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（龜山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Kameyama (龜山藩): population, households, and minor rice levies",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Kameyama domain civil register: population by status (total / shi-sotsu / shizoku / sotsu with male-female splits), household counts, temples and shrines, and three minor rice transport/land taxes.",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page is the civil register (fascicle 2) for Kameyama domain (龜山藩); the running header at the right margin reads 藩制一覧表第二（龜山）. It records a total population of 41,924 (男 21,093 / 女 20,831) in 8,790 households, of which the samurai-and-foot-soldier segment (士卒) numbers 3,667 people in 726 houses, broken down into 士族 (samurai households) 270 / 1,373 and 卒 (lower retainers) 456 / 2,294. Religious counts are 212 temples (寺, including hermitages) and 33 shrines (神社). Three short columns on the right list minor rice levies (米): a 2-bale dyers' license tax, a 4-bale tax on Wakamatsu incoming-ship wholesalers, and a 4-bale tribute on retainers' fallow upland fields. The bottom-margin page number is 160."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameyama_upper_p093_left",
   "sequence": 162,
   "domain_canonical": "龜山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p093_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 93,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（川越）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Kameyama (龜山藩) tail, on the Kawagoe-opening leaf",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Kameyama demographics (shares the Kawagoe-opening leaf; Kameyama's tail continues here)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the entry for Kawagoe domain (its ○ marker and land assessment), but the bulk of the page — read right to left, to the right of that marker — is the demographic tail of the previous domain, Kameyama (龜山藩). The Kameyama figures shown here cover its religious and status populations: shrine-priest families (社家) 202 people (男 104 / 女 98), monks and nuns (僧尼) 671 (男 427 / 女 244), 743 shrines (神社), and mountain ascetics (修驗) in 11 households / 40 people, followed by a small military note of 8 troops (兵隊) and 3 cannon-corps officers (大砲隊役員)."
