   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the Fascicle 2 (第二) civil and fiscal entry for Kasama (笠間藩), a roughly 85,000-koku domain in what is now Ibaraki, opening with its ○ domain-boundary marker. Reading right to left, it records the 士族 (samurai households, 571) and 卒族 (foot-soldier households, 447) with their populations, along with a two-part 兵隊 (troop) count of 597 regular and 212 reserve men. The fiscal columns give an assessed yield 草高 (kokudaka) of 85,310.6648 koku, and, as five-year averages, the 正租 (regular land tax) of 16,273.6368 koku of rice plus 6,596.28 kan in cash, and the 雜稅 (miscellaneous tax) of 553.4329 koku of rice plus 923.73 kan in cash."
