   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Kasama's (笠間藩) Fascicle 2 civil register, with no ○ domain-boundary marker of its own, so the whole half-page belongs to Kasama. It records a total population of 44,046 (22,800 male, 21,246 female) across 7,425 households in 197 villages, together with 238 Buddhist temples (147 of them uninhabited). It also breaks out the 士族 (samurai households, 310) and 卒族 (foot-soldier households, 443) with a samurai population of 3,255, along with 穢多非人 (outcaste) and 社家 (Shinto-priest) households. A right-hand rice subtotal 右合 of 25,187.8892 koku closes the fiscal columns; the 神社 (shrine) heading is printed but left blank here."
