   "page_summary_en": "This is the left continuation of Takasaki's (高崎藩) Fascicle 3 civil register; it carries no ○ domain-boundary marker of its own, since the marker and 知事 (governor) heading sit on the facing leaf. The right-hand columns give the combined revenue total 合 broken into rice (32,699.52 koku), 永 cash, gold, and copper coin, followed by a 産物税 (products tax). The left-hand columns record the demographic register: 20,972 total households, 58 shrines, 330 temples, 1,444 士族 (samurai households), 201 卒族 (foot-soldier households), and smaller counts of shrine families, Buddhist halls, and mountain-ascetic temples. Several entries carry interlinear notes citing the 1870 ninth- and tenth-month surveys."
