   "page_topic": "Population and household register by status group (Takasaki domain)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Takasaki's (高崎藩) Fascicle 3 status register; it has no ○ domain-boundary marker or 知事 (governor) name, marking it as an interior page. It carries two parallel breakdowns. The persons-by-status register gives a total 人員 (population) of 97,550, with 2,815 士族 (samurai), 1,251 卒族 (foot-soldiers), 91,066 平民 (commoners), and smaller counts of shrine priests, temple clergy, mountain ascetics, and others, most split into male and female subtotals. The households-by-status register records 18,530 commoner households (including 16 that migrate seasonally to Kishū), 11 ferryman households, and 264 穢多 (outcaste) households."
