   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the civil register (人別) for Tatebayashi domain (館林藩), opened by the ○ domain-boundary marker at the ○館林藩 heading. Reading right to left, it lists small population sub-classes with male and female detail — physicians (医師) 28 and one kengyō, mountain ascetics (山伏) 28, ferrymen (渡守) 66, blind persons 4, one shrine maiden (巫女) and four nuns, and an eta (穢多) population of 1,287 (693 male, 594 female). It then records 735 troops (兵), 93 villages (村), and the land figures: an assessed yield (草高) of 60,000 koku, a new-field uplift (外高) of 53,851.7 koku, a combined assessment (合高) of 113,851.7 koku, and a regular land tax in rice (正租米) of 12,337.4 koku given as a five-year average."
  },
