   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tatebayashi domain: population by status, households, temples/shrines, and miscellaneous-tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This civil-register leaf for Tatebayashi domain (館林藩) records the miscellaneous tax (雑税) — 1,826.6 koku in rice plus cash — followed by the domain's household and population accounts. It gives 15,868 households (戸数), 105 shrines (神社) and 290 temples (寺院), and a breakdown by status: samurai households (士族) 293, lower retainers (卒族) 618, shrine-priest families (社家) 43, commoners (平民) 14,551, mountain ascetics (修験) 18, crematory attendants (煙亡) 19, eta (穢多) outcastes 406, and hinin (非人) 21. The final column gives a total population (人員) of 75,057, split into 37,859 male and 37,198 female. Several entries are dated to the first month of 1871 (辛未正月)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tatebayashi_upper_p122_left",
