   "pdf_page": 160,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（中村）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle Four (Nakamura)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Status-group households and population; shrines, districts, and the farmer/artisan/merchant counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 294 of fascicle four continues the household-and-population return for Nakamura (Sōma) domain in Mutsu. No maru-marker appears anywhere on the leaf, so the whole page belongs to 中村藩. The sheet records 554 sotsu households holding 3,426 people, 67 shrine-officiant households (467 people), 124 Shugendō households (467 people), 114 monastic households (311 people), 5 eta households (56 people) and 15 hinin households (117 people), together with 105 shrines and 3 districts. Three further lines, which the compiler marks as having been written in vermilion in the original, give the commoner counts: 6,480 farming households with 43,355 people, 100 artisan households with 595 people, and 243 merchant households with 1,374 people. The rightmost column carries a population of 13,453 (6,670 male, 6,783 female) whose label and household count printed on the preceding page."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagao_upper_p160_left",
   "sequence": 185,
   "domain_canonical": "長尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagao",
   "image": "images/upper_p160_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 160,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（長尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Table Four (Nagao)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nagao domain land assessment and five-year-average tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the fascicle-four entry for Nagao Domain (Awa Province, modern Chiba) with the maru-marker ○長尾藩, and records its land assessment and tax yield. The nominal assessed yield (草高) is 40,000 koku, with a further 10,255.20227 koku of supplementary assessment (込高). Under the heading \"five-year average,\" the regular land tax (正租) is 12,539.02854 koku of rice plus 2,039,169.646 mon in cash, and the miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) are 1,823.57041 koku plus 1,049,735.812 mon; the printed combined total, 14,362.59895 koku and 3,088,905.458 mon, reconciles exactly with both component pairs. The product tax (産物稅) accounts for the whole of the miscellaneous rice tax at 1,823.57041 koku, with 49,735.812 mon of cash attached to it. A single column standing to the right of the marker, 兵隊六百二十七人）, closes a parenthesis opened on the facing half-page and reports 627 troops for the preceding domain, Nakamura."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagao_upper_p161_right",
   "sequence": 186,
   "domain_canonical": "長尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagao",
   "image": "images/upper_p161_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 161,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（長尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Nagao (長尾藩): households and population by status",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nagao domain (長尾藩) civil register — households, population, and status-group / clergy / outcaste-adjacent breakdowns with male-female splits",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the right-hand half of a fascicle-4 civil-register leaf for Nagao domain (長尾藩), a small Kazusa domain identified here by its running header; because this is a continuation leaf, no ○ marker or governor's name is printed. The columns record total households (戸数) of 12,275 and a total population (人員) of 70,850 (35,056 male, 35,794 female), followed by per-group counts with male and female splits: monkey-showmen (猿牽), constables (長吏), shrine-priest families (社家), temples (寺, 333 sites and 320 persons), temple-land peasants (寺領百姓, 282 houses and 1,482 persons), samurai (士族) 310, lower retainers (卒族) 268, and foot-soldiers (兵卒) 153, each with a dependent-family (家族) breakdown. The facing left half of this leaf carries the neighbouring domain of Nagaoka (長岡藩)."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagao_lower_p194_right",
   "sequence": 187,
   "domain_canonical": "長尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagao",
   "image": "images/lower_p194_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 194,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（長尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Nagao (長尾藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "officials_and_military",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-9 leaf (職員兵隊, officials and military) covers Nagao domain (長尾藩), opened by the sole ○ marker on the page at ○長尾藩. Nagao's military is recorded as 161 standing troops (常備兵) and 155 reserve troops (准備兵). Its officials roster runs across two registers — a compact surname-and-rank block on the right (Honda and Masuda as senior councillors 大参事; Shigetomi, Kameda, Ishii, and Okumura as junior councillors 少参事) and a fuller full-name block on the left, headed by a senior-councillor column carrying the editorial note that the following seven lines were originally written in vermillion (以下七行原朱書). The 兵隊 figure of 627 troops printed to the right of the ○長尾藩 marker belongs to the previous domain sharing this leaf, not to Nagao, whose troops total 316."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagaoka_upper_p161_left",
   "sequence": 188,
   "domain_canonical": "長岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagaoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p161_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 161,
   "page_side": "L",
