   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（長岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Nagaoka (長岡藩): land, revenue, and households by status",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nagaoka domain civil register: kokudaka, five-year-average current rice, miscellaneous tax, and household/population breakdown by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-leaf records the fascicle-4 civil register for Nagaoka domain (長岡藩), opened by the ○ marker at ○長岡藩. It gives an assessed yield (草高) of 24,000 koku, a five-year-average current-rice figure (現米) of 22,993.4, and a miscellaneous-tax rice figure (雑税現石) of 614.3 koku. The bulk of the leaf is a household count (戸数) broken down by status group: samurai (士族) 607 houses (including one kazoku 華族 house), foot-soldiers (卒) 1,122, rural commoners (在方) 3,901, townsmen (町方) 1,813, temples (寺) 80, shrine-priest families (社家) 10, and eta (穢多) 2. The total population (人員) and the eta-hinin count are left blank or marked indeterminate (不分明)."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagaoka_upper_p162_right",
   "sequence": 189,
   "domain_canonical": "長岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagaoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p162_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 162,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（長島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview Table, Fascicle 4 (Nagashima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Population by status group (Nagaoka) and opening assessed yield (Nagashima)",
   "page_summary_en": "The leaf closes Nagaoka domain's fascicle-4 population return and opens Nagashima's. Reading right to left, Nagaoka's status counts run kazoku 8, shizoku 3,173 (m 1,508 / f 1,665), sotsu 5,052 (m 2,456 / f 2,596), rural commoners 18,460 (m 9,320 / f 9,140), town commoners 8,242 (m 3,888 / f 4,352), shrine-priest households 41 (m 22 / f 19), Buddhist clergy and households 223, and eta 15 (m 7 / f 8), followed by a count of 8 Shinto shrines; the eight status figures sum to 35,214 persons. Two figures do not reconcile: the town-commoner split falls two short of its total and carries a printed マヽ (sic) mark beside the total, and the kazoku split as printed reads 男三人 / 女八人 against a total of 八人. To the left of the ○長島藩 marker the Nagashima block opens with an assessed yield of 18,301.718 koku, glossed by a two-line note as the total for Nagashima and its new fields in Kuwana district, Ise province."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagaoka_lower_p194_left",
   "sequence": 190,
   "domain_canonical": "長岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagaoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p194_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 194,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（長岡、長島）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Nagaoka (長岡藩) and Nagashima (長島藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "officials_military",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-9 officials-and-military leaf names both Nagaoka and Nagashima in its running header. The primary domain is Nagaoka (長岡藩), whose ○ marker opens the block: its army (兵隊) is recorded as 828 troops, its officials headcount (官員) is undisclosed (不詳), and its named appointees run through the senior councillors (大参事: Makino Tanomo 牧野頼母, Mishima Okuchōrō, Kobayashi Torasaburō), the acting senior councillors (権大参事: Nagino Kahei, Akita Motome, Hara Ichihei, Takebe Seizō), and longer junior-councillor rosters. The note printed to the right of the Nagaoka marker (以上大参事以下姓名届留守官) belongs to the previous domain, Nakamura (中村藩), on the facing leaf. At the far left, the ○長島藩 marker opens the next domain, Nagashima, whose own officials continue on the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "oka_upper_p069_left",
   "sequence": 191,
   "domain_canonical": "岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Oka",
   "image": "images/upper_p069_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 69,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Overview of Domain Administration, Table 2 (Oka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-2 civil/fiscal block: end of Ōgaki entry, opening of Oka entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes the Ōgaki 大垣藩 entry in fascicle 2 of the Hansei Ichiran and opens the Oka 岡藩 entry. Ōgaki's tail records 306 temples with an attached population of 1,805 (1,080 male, 725 female), 756 shrines, 7 counties, with village count and outcaste (eta/hinin) numbers marked \"not ascertained\" (シレス), followed by parenthetical notes: no warships possessed, a governor's family of five, an infantry battalion of 600 men (60-man platoons, plus 105 officers and 150 laborers besides), and a 144-man artillery company (48-man squads, with 61 officers and 90 laborers). The ○岡藩 marker gives Oka's base assessment as 70,440.17 koku, and its block begins with a gross assessed yield of 91,844.62378 koku (inclusive of komi-daka and new-development yield), regular tax rice of 51,221.906 koku stated as a five-year average from 1864 to 1868, and miscellaneous tax rice of 1,180.791 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "oka_upper_p070_right",
   "sequence": 192,
   "domain_canonical": "岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Oka",
   "image": "images/upper_p070_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 70,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle 2 (Oka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Regular land-tax breakdown and household/population registers of Oka Domain",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Oka Domain (Taketa, Bungo Province) entry in Fascicle 2. A red-ink block in the original manuscript, flagged by an editorial note, totals the regular land tax at 52,402 koku 6 to 9 shō 7 gō and breaks it into rice (32,788.735 koku), rice commuted to cash (4,950.747 koku, equal to 28,801 ryō 2 bu plus 24 mon in ei-cash), and rice paid in soybeans (13,482.424 koku, equal to 18,875.393 koku of soybeans); the printed components sum to 51,221.906 koku, 1,180.791 short of the printed total. The page then records 17,657 households and a population of 77,574 (39,244 male, 38,330 female), with a status breakdown giving 354 shizoku households of 2,295 persons (1,106 male, 1,189 female) and 1,273 sotsu households."
  },
  {
   "id": "oka_upper_p070_left",
   "sequence": 193,
   "domain_canonical": "岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Oka",
   "image": "images/upper_p070_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 70,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey Table, Fascicle 2 (Oka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Oka domain status-group census, shrines and temples, villages, and military strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Oka domain (Bungo province, Nakagawa house) entry in fascicle 2. The page completes the status-group census: the soldier-class (sotsu) population of 4,104 (2,269 male, 1,835 female), 141 shrine-official households with 617 persons recorded, 71 temples with 548 persons, 21 shugen (mountain-ascetic) households with 109 persons, 23 blind performers (zato), 116 eta households with 643 persons, and 7 hinin households with 51 persons. It then records 2,786 shrines, a village count marked \"not ascertainable,\" no warships, a governor's family of seven, and a force of two infantry battalions (a note explains six platoons form a battalion) plus one artillery unit. The printed shrine-official population of 617 conflicts with its own male/female split (328 + 389 = 717), an arithmetic slip in the source itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "oka_lower_p151_left",
   "sequence": 194,
   "domain_canonical": "岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Oka",
   "image": "images/lower_p151_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 151,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Oka (岡藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "officials_and_military",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 8 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) records the officials and military establishment of Oka (岡藩), the Nakagawa family's domain in Bungo province. The ○ domain-boundary marker opens Oka's entry mid-leaf, and its roster of 官員 (administrative officials) runs leftward from there: a 大参事 (senior councillor, 1), 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 4), 少参事 (junior councillor, 2), and 権少参事 (acting junior councillor, 1); the 知事 (governor) heading is printed but names no appointee. Read right-to-left, the officials and troop figures to the RIGHT of the ○岡藩 marker — a lone 権少参事 appointee together with 歩兵 (infantry, one 600-man battalion) and 砲兵 (artillery, one 144-man battery) — belong to the previous domain sharing this leaf, not to Oka."
  },
  {
   "id": "kano_upper_p096_left",
   "sequence": 195,
   "domain_canonical": "加納藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "加納藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanō",
   "image": "images/upper_p096_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 96,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（加納）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 3 — (Kanō)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kanō domain — assessed yield, five-year-average land and miscellaneous tax, and products",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Kanō (加納藩) entry in Fascicle 3 of the Han-sei Ichiran, the 1870 Dajōkan survey of the domains, and carries the printed book-page number 167 of the bound upper volume. Kanō's assessed gross yield (草高) is 32,000 koku, with a further 3,856.6342 koku entered under 外, the two totalled as a 合高 of 35,856.63402 koku. Averaged over five years the domain collected 11,656.487 koku of land tax in hulled rice (正租 現米) and 1,396.27415 koku of miscellaneous tax (雜税), and those two figures sum exactly to the printed total of 13,052.76115 koku. Two products are recorded: roughly 8,000 bolts of fine crepe cloth (縮細) and roughly 300,000 umbrellas (傘), the latter the oiled-paper umbrella trade of the Gifu area in which the Kanō castle town sat."
  },
  {
   "id": "kano_upper_p097_right",
   "sequence": 196,
   "domain_canonical": "加納藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "加納藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanō",
   "image": "images/upper_p097_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 97,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（加納）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Kanō)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Temple lands, cotton-stripe output, and households/population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Kanō (加納) entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran; no maru-marker appears anywhere on the leaf, so every column belongs to Kanō, and the running head in the right margin names Kanō as well. It records temple lands of 412.685 koku with a five-year average yield of 130.6103 koku of rice, plus four additional woodland tracts, and cotton-stripe output of roughly 30,000 bolts of santome-jima and 53,500 bolts of Yūki-jima. The household and population block that follows gives 317 shizoku households holding 1,488 people (719 male, 769 female), 71 sotsu households holding 207 people (98 male, 109 female), and 5,387 commoner households holding 23,970 people (11,817 male, 12,153 female). Summed across the three status groups the domain returns 5,775 households and 25,665 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "kano_upper_p097_left",
   "sequence": 197,
   "domain_canonical": "加納藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "加納藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanō",
   "image": "images/upper_p097_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 97,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（加納）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Three (Kanō)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kanō Domain: household and population returns by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Fascicle Three return for Kanō Domain in Mino, carrying the status-by-status household and population counts that begin on the facing leaf with the shizoku, sotsu and peasant figures. It records 681 townsman households with 2,706 people (1,312 male, 1,394 female), 101 Buddhist temples housing 393 people (238 monks, 134 women, 21 lay residents, with three hermitages and three nuns noted separately), 15 shrine-priest households with 71 people, a second temple entry of 173 households, 258 people under the bare label 姓, four eta households with 15 people, and 48 hinin households with 263 people. The leaf closes with the domain totals of 6,305 households and 27,656 people, with one kazoku household of seven persons printed under 外ニ and therefore standing outside those totals, and with the districts-and-villages count returned as 未詳, not ascertained. Every male and female sub-count reconciles exactly with its printed total, while the household components run three over the printed 6,305."
  },
  {
   "id": "kadano_lower_p167_left",
   "sequence": 198,
   "domain_canonical": "加納藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "加納藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanō",
   "image": "images/lower_p167_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 167,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（加納）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Kanō (加納藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "officials_and_military",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) opens the entry for Kanō (加納藩) with its ○ domain-boundary marker, then gives its officials roster: a 知事 (governor), 大参事 (senior councillor, 1), 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 2), and 少参事 (junior councillor, 3). Read right-to-left, the material to the RIGHT of the ○加納藩 marker belongs to the previous domain sharing this leaf, Kasama (笠間藩): its named 知事 (governor) and its full military establishment of seven unit types — scout, artillery, sharpshooter, and volley-fire companies, plus first-, second-, and third-class guard companies of 61, 51, and 52 men. That Kasama military does not belong to Kanō."
  },
  {
   "id": "kano_lower_p168_right",
   "sequence": 199,
   "domain_canonical": "加納藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "加納藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanō",
   "image": "images/lower_p168_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 168,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（加納）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration (Hansei ichiran-hyō), Fascicle 8 — Kanō",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Kanō domain officials roster and military strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle 8 page records the administrative officials and military establishment of Kanō domain (加納藩, Mino province) as of the 1870 (Kōgo) survey. The summary counts give one senior councillor (大参事), two acting senior councillors (権大参事), two junior councillors (少参事), and three acting junior councillors (権少参事), together with an infantry force of three platoons (兵隊三小隊, headcount not ascertained) and an artillery corps of sixteen men (大砲兵隊十六員). The lower register names seven officials — 篠原長, 川上實, 片岡靜, 小島勳, 小林更平, 安達信夫, and 杉浦兵四郎 — arranged under the four council ranks. The named roster lists only seven individuals against the eight positions implied by the summary counts, a minor internal discrepancy within the source entry."
  },
  {
   "id": "takada_upper_p119_right",
   "sequence": 200,
   "domain_canonical": "高田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高田藩",
   "domain_en": "Takada",
   "image": "images/upper_p119_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 119,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Three (Takada)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takada domain land assessment, land tax and miscellaneous tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Takada domain entry in fascicle three of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran and reports the domain's land assessment and its tax income. Takada's assessed yield (kusadaka) is 150,000 koku; a separate line adds 4,104.158 koku of re-survey increment and newly opened fields, giving a combined assessment of 154,104.158 koku. The regular land tax came to 94,382.2852 bales of rice and 135.143 bales of soybeans, of which 29,908 ryo 3 bu 1 shu plus 375 mon was taken in cash, while miscellaneous taxes brought 1,370.02806 bales of rice and 6,600 ryo 3 bu 2 shu plus 900 mon. Three further lines, marked as written in vermilion in the original manuscript, record 1,460.451 koku of tax-exempt shrine and temple land, 1,569.088 koku of shrine and temple fiefs, and 154 shrine sites and 42 temples holding vermilion-seal land; the domain contained 31,422 households."
  },
  {
   "id": "takada_upper_p119_left",
   "sequence": 201,
   "domain_canonical": "高田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高田藩",
   "domain_en": "Takada",
   "image": "images/upper_p119_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 119,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Fascicle 3 (Takada)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takada domain: shrines, temples, status households and population by status with male/female splits",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf, printed page 213 of fascicle 3, continues the Takada domain (高田藩, Echigo) return begun on the facing page; no maru-marker appears here, so every column belongs to Takada. It records 1,407 shrines and 557 temples, and households by status: 609 shizoku, 1,238 sotsu, 91 shrine-priest (社家), 23 shugendō, 306 eta and 30 hinin. The total population is given as 168,776 (82,170 male, 86,606 female), of which 155,569 were commoners, 4,439 sotsu, 4,032 shizoku, 2,292 clergy, 1,688 eta, 509 in shrine-priest households and 146 hinin, and the domain is credited with 134 villages. The seven status populations sum to 168,675, leaving 101 people unaccounted for — most likely the shugendō households, whose 23 dwellings are listed but whose population is not."
  },
  {
   "id": "takada_lower_p177_left",
   "sequence": 202,
   "domain_canonical": "高田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高田藩",
   "domain_en": "Takada",
   "image": "images/lower_p177_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 177,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（高田）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Takada (高田藩): officials",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (職員) — Takada domain administrative appointees",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) is the officials (職員) page for Takada (高田藩), the single domain shown, marked by its ○ domain-boundary marker. The 知事 (governor) line carries no name or count and is noted as 審ナラス (not disclosed); the domain reports 大参事 (senior councillor, 5) and 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 6), with a 権少参事 (acting junior councillor) heading standing atop a roster of eleven named appointees. No military figures appear on this leaf — it is purely a roster of names, with troop data falling on the adjacent pages."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuyama_upper_p150_left",
   "sequence": 203,
   "domain_canonical": "津山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "津山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p150_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 150,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 4 — Tsuyama (津山藩): land assessment and civil register",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Civil register (kokudaka, land tax, vessels, temples/shrines, outcaste and clerical populations) — Tsuyama domain opening on this leaf, with the tail of the previous domain Tsu on the right.",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 4 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) is a civil register that opens the entry for Tsuyama (津山藩) at its ○ domain-boundary marker. Tsuyama's land figures give a 高 (base assessment) of 100,000 koku, a 込高新田改出高 (reclaimed and re-surveyed add-on) of 4,576.913 koku, a 草高 (total assessed yield) of 104,576.913 koku, and a 正租 (main land tax) of 41,967.4508 koku of rice, averaged over five years. Read right-to-left, the fields to the RIGHT of the ○津山藩 marker are the tail of the previous domain, Tsu (津藩): its 兵卒 (troops, 1,647), one steamship and one sailing vessel, 579 villages, 1,247 temples, 1,122 shrines, 1,564 hinin and 9,098 eta (each with a male/female split), and 52 nuns — closed by a submission note dated the 11th month of 1870. Those Tsu counts belong to Tsu, not Tsuyama."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuyama_upper_p151_right",
   "sequence": 204,
   "domain_canonical": "津山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "津山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p151_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 151,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（津山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Tsuyama)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsuyama miscellaneous taxes, transit dues, households, population and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fourth-fascicle return for Tsuyama Domain (津山藩) in Mimasaka, with no domain marker printed on it: the block opens on an earlier leaf and runs on to the facing one. On the fiscal side it records miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) of 914.6478 koku of rice and 409 ryō 1 bu 1 shu in cash, the cash figure carrying a note that it is the amount surveyed in the eleventh month of 1869, followed by transit and business dues (諸運上) reported in three columns: 479 ryō 1 bu 1 shu, 42,882.9056 koku of rice, and 1,888 ryō with 643 mon 7 fun 2 rin in ei-currency. On the demographic side it gives 2,006 commoner households and 8,111 persons (3,846 male, 4,265 female, likewise dated to the eleventh month of 1869), and outside that count 364 shizoku households with 1,666 persons, 163 sotsu households with 640 persons, and 33 shrine households with 84 persons. The military entry is one battalion, glossed as a company of 60 men plus 40 officers, together with four cannon manned by 48 men and 16 officers."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuyama_lower_p190_left",
   "sequence": 205,
   "domain_canonical": "津山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "津山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p190_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 190,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（津山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Tsuyama (津山藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (councillors) and military establishment of Tsuyama-han",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) records the officials and troops of Tsuyama (津山藩), the single domain shown, marked by its ○ domain-boundary marker. Officials are listed by rank — 大参事 (senior councillor, 2), 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 2), and 権少参事 (acting junior councillor, 11) — with appointee names hung in columns below the headings; an inline note reads 少参事以下不詳 (junior councillor and below: not detailed). The 兵隊 (troops) line reads 一大隊但一小隊六十人 — one battalion, with each company comprising sixty men. No gun, cannon, warship, or total-strength figures are printed here."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuwano_upper_p151_left",
   "sequence": 206,
   "domain_canonical": "津和野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "津和野藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuwano",
   "image": "images/upper_p151_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 151,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（津和野）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Tsuwano)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsuwano's assessed yield, households and population, after Tsuyama's temple, outcast and troop tail",
   "page_summary_en": "The sheet carries the tail of Tsuyama domain's fascicle-four record and then opens Tsuwano's. Right of the ○津和野藩 marker, Tsuyama reports 178 temples and 41 hermitages housing 284 people (202 monks and 82 male servants), 64 temple row-house tenements with 168 residents (90 male, 78 female), 905 eta and hinin households holding 4,535 people (2,416 male, 2,119 female), and a bracketed force of one rifle battalion of 600 men and an artillery corps of 48, with 16 staff officers besides; a note dates the returns to the eleventh month of the Snake year, that is Meiji 2. Left of the marker, Tsuwano reports a nominal assessment of 75,060.6489 koku, an average deduction of 18,385.1479 koku across the five years from the Boar year to the Hare year, and receipts of 26,770.52692 koku over the same span. Its 15,918 households hold 68,679 people (36,113 male, 32,566 female), of whom 967 are shizoku (478 male, 489 female) living in 219 households. The printed book page is 277."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuwano_lower_p191_right",
   "sequence": 207,
   "domain_canonical": "津和野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "津和野藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuwano",
   "image": "images/lower_p191_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 191,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（津和野、土浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Tsuwano (津和野藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (職員) and military (兵隊) — Fascicle 9: Tsuwano domain full officials roster + its 6-platoon force, plus the opening of Tsuchiura domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) is headed for Tsuwano and Tsuchiura and carries two domains. Tsuwano (津和野藩), opened by its ○ domain-boundary marker, fills most of the page: a 知事 (governor, unnamed here), a 大参事 (senior councillor) marked 欠員 (vacant), 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 3), 少参事 (junior councillor, 7), and 権少参事 (acting junior councillor, 3); its force is 六小隊 (six platoons of sixty men, 360 total), with a note of 40 additional sub-officials. At the far left the ○土浦藩 marker opens Tsuchiura (土浦藩) with its 大参事 heading and first four appointees; that roster continues on the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuchiura_upper_p152_right",
   "sequence": 208,
   "domain_canonical": "土浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "土浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuchiura",
   "image": "images/upper_p152_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 152,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（土浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (Tsuchiura)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsuwano status populations, shrines, temples and troops; Tsuchiura kokudaka opening",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of this page close out Tsuwano Domain's fascicle-4 entry. It records 3,292 sotsu (1,809 male, 1,483 female) in 1,018 households, a separately counted eta population of 584 (312 male, 272 female) in 117 households, 246 shrines with 94 shrine-priest houses holding 395 people, and 120 temples holding 480, followed by a military line of six platoons of fifty men with a printed total of 330. A closing note states that the foregoing was submitted in the first month. The maru-marker ○土浦藩 then opens Tsuchiura Domain, whose assessment prints a 草高 of 110,083.0404 koku made up of a base 高 of 95,000 koku and 15,083.0404 koku of newly opened fields recorded on re-survey, with a further 1,593.0637 koku carried as landless assessment. The running header names Tsuchiura even though most of the printed columns still belong to Tsuwano."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuchiura_upper_p152_left",
   "sequence": 209,
   "domain_canonical": "土浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "土浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuchiura",
   "image": "images/upper_p152_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 152,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（土浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 4 (Tsuchiura)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsuchiura land tax, households, population, shrines and temples, troops and samurai counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-4 return for Tsuchiura Domain (Hitachi Province), with no maru-marker on the page and the running header naming Tsuchiura. The fiscal block records regular land tax (正税) of 24,262.115 koku of rice plus 4,747.890559 kan in cash (永), and the standing assessed rate (右之定免) of 31,190.4018 koku plus 4,096.80048 kan; a preceding 内 note itemises 4.9 koku differing by tax-rate (斗代違高) and 34.625 koku struck off by cadastral resurvey (檢地減高). The demographic block gives 13,053 households and a population of 72,277 (36,676 male, 35,601 female), together with 378 shrines and 319 temples housing 383 clergy (315 male, 68 female). The status and military counts follow: 1,414 samurai and foot-soldier troops, 368 peasant militia, 2,796 shizoku in 513 households, and 1,186 sotsu; two warichu notes date the tax figures to the tenth day of the tenth month of the Kanoe-uma year (1870) and the population figures to the eleventh month of the Snake year (1869)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuchiura_lower_p191_left",
   "sequence": 210,
   "domain_canonical": "土浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "土浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuchiura",
   "image": "images/lower_p191_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 191,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（土浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Tsuchiura (土浦藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (councillors) and military establishment of Tsuchiura domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) continues the entry for Tsuchiura (土浦藩), the 90,000-koku Tsuchiya-family domain in Hitachi province, the single domain shown here. The 知事 (governor) heading carries no surname (the governor's name appeared on the preceding leaf); the councillor ranks run right-to-left as 大参事 (senior councillor, 2), 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 1), 少参事 (junior councillor, 2), and 権少参事 (acting junior councillor), with appointee names hung below each heading. The military entry records 大隊貳隊 (two battalions), qualified by a note that 47 men make one platoon and six platoons make a battalion. A marginal caretaker-official report dated the 6th month of 1870 attaches to a separately listed 大参事 at the far left."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuyama_upper_p203_left",
   "sequence": 211,
   "domain_canonical": "松山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松山藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p203_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 203,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五　（松山）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Matsuyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsuyama domain land assessment, tax revenue, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the entry for Matsuyama Domain in Iyo Province, whose territory the survey records as ten districts containing 313 villages. The gross assessed yield (草高) stands at 157,184.977 koku, against which the domain collected 103,480.7 koku in land tax (正租) and 7,176.7 koku in miscellaneous taxes (雑税), for a combined 110,657.4 koku; a further 16 ryō 2 bu 2 shu and 711 ryō 1 bu 2 shu were taken in cash under the same two heads, and the domain reports no shrine or temple lands. The household count is 50,487, of which 833 are samurai (士族) households, 2,868 are foot-soldier (卒族) households, and a further 850 belong to the quasi-samurai and kachi category (准士徒士族). A compiler's note printed beside the tax total records that the original manuscript gave the sum as five to rather than the four to printed here, and asks whether the two fractional remainders were combined into the extra to."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuyama_upper_p204_right",
   "sequence": 212,
   "domain_canonical": "松山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松山藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p204_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 204,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Matsuyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Population, status breakdown, and shrine/temple households of Matsuyama domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the demographic close of the Matsuyama domain entry in fascicle 5 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. It records a total population of 211,882 (108,720 male, 103,162 female) and itemises the non-commoner statuses beneath the 內 marker: 4,645 shizoku, 4,079 junshi/kachi shizoku, 5,580 sotsu, 1,278 shrine people, 1,124 temple people (of whom 8 are eta monks), 341 hinin and 9,302 eta — 26,349 in all, leaving 185,533 commoners unenumerated. The household register printed to the right gives 267 shrine-priest households, 344 temples (3 of them eta temples), 1,873 eta households and 174 hinin households, and the page closes with 2,604 shrines and a parenthetical note that the governor's family numbers four (two male, two female). Every male-plus-female pair on the page sums exactly to its printed total."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuyama_lower_p208_left",
   "sequence": 213,
   "domain_canonical": "松山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松山藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p208_left.jpg",
