   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（松山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Matsuyama (松山藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (chiji / sanji ranks) and military establishment for Matsuyama domain, with a naval-vessel note overflowing from the preceding domain (Matsue).",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) is opened by the ○松山藩 marker, so the domain shown is Iyo-Matsuyama (松山藩), the Hisamatsu-Matsudaira house. The 知事 (governor) heading carries no printed name; the councillor ranks are 大参事 (senior councillor, 3), 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 3), and 少参事 (junior councillor, 3), with nine appointee names hung in columns. The military entry gives 歩兵 (infantry) as 30 platoons of 75 men each (2,250), 砲兵 (artillery) as 3 units of 43 gunners plus 10 officers each (129), and 船ナシ (no ships). Read right-to-left, the naval note 千石積 一艘 (one 1,000-koku-capacity vessel) printed to the RIGHT of the ○松山藩 marker belongs to the previous domain sharing this leaf, Matsue (松江藩), not to Matsuyama."
  },
  {
   "id": "himeji_lower_p100_left",
   "sequence": 214,
   "domain_canonical": "姫路藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "姫路藩",
   "domain_en": "Himeji",
   "image": "images/lower_p100_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 100,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（姫路）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Himeji) — running header",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Himeji kokudaka (opening entry) + Hikone temple/shrine-land households & population (continuation)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a boundary page in fascicle 7 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran: it closes Hikone domain's entry and opens Himeji's. The right two-thirds continue Hikone's temple- and shrine-land tabulation (管轄内社寺領地戸口): 5,169 total households and 21,421 people (男10,551/女10,870, including 154 monks and 310 temple clergy), sub-divided into shrine-land (211 households / 759 people, with 20 Shinto priests, 4 shrine-maidens, 5 monks, 4 nuns) and temple-land (334 households / 1,776 people, with 176 monks and 4 nuns). To the left of the ○姫路藩 marker begins Himeji domain: nominal assessed yield (草高) of 150,000 koku plus an additional 61,224.081 koku from new-field re-survey, for a combined total of 211,224.081 koku, followed by the five-year-average heading. Printed book page is 百七十七 (177)."
  },
  {
   "id": "himeji_lower_p101_right",
   "sequence": 215,
   "domain_canonical": "姫路藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "姫路藩",
   "domain_en": "Himeji",
   "image": "images/lower_p101_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 101,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（姫路）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 — Himeji",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Himeji domain — land tax, miscellaneous levies, and product taxes",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Fascicle 7 fiscal entry for Himeji domain (姫路藩). It records the domain's regular land-tax rice (正租米) of 87,437.108 koku, followed by miscellaneous tax rice (雜稅米) broken into three named levies — petty imposts/komononari (小物成) 702.009 koku, commercial dues/unjō (運上) 338.663 koku, and mountain-district dues (山方運上) 6.93 koku. Under a 諸產物稅 (product-tax) header, four domain products are each paired with their tax: bleached cotton (晒木綿, ~540,000 tan → 2,055 ryō), salt (鹽, >280,000 koku → 69.003 koku of rice), tanned leather hides (~28,000 pieces → 179 ryō), and stone (~5,700 pieces → 149 pieces in kind, equal to 0.61 koku of hulled rice). The printed book-page number is 178."
  },
  {
   "id": "himeji_lower_p101_left",
   "sequence": 216,
   "domain_canonical": "姫路藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "姫路藩",
   "domain_en": "Himeji",
   "image": "images/lower_p101_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 101,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（姫路）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 7 (Himeji) — outer-margin running header (provenance)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Himeji domain household & population statistics by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Himeji domain (姫路藩) entry in fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran, tabulating households and population by status group. It records 51,489 total households and a population of 222,661. The itemized status households are: 706 samurai (shizoku) households with 4,030 persons (1,925 M / 2,105 F); 1,402 foot-soldier (sotsu) households with 4,582 persons (2,433 M / 2,149 F); 273 boatmen-and-fixed-guard households with 1,095 persons (592 M / 503 F); 118 bureau-servant/substitute-hire households with 789 persons (468 M / 321 F); and 135 shrine-family (shake) households with 488 persons (262 M / 226 F); plus 647 temples. No domain marker appears on the page, so every figure belongs to Himeji (the block opens on the facing page with the ○姫路藩 marker)."
  },
  {
   "id": "himeji_lower_p102_right",
   "sequence": 217,
   "domain_canonical": "姫路藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "姫路藩",
   "domain_en": "Himeji",
   "image": "images/lower_p102_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 102,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（姫路）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Register, Fascicle 7 (Himeji)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Himeji special-status population, shrines, and governor's household",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Fascicle-7 demographic register for Himeji Domain (姫路藩). It records special-status populations — temple residents 1,650 (clergy 893, male 213, female 544), shugendō practitioners 65 (ascetics 17, male 20, female 28), eta 11,389 (male 5,757, female 5,632), and hinin 109 (male 54, female 55) — together with structural counts: 2,307 eta households, 1,059 shrines, 19 shugendō sites, and the governor's household of 3 (male 1, female 2). Village count and hinin household count are both marked \"not recorded\" (記セス). A three-line red-ink marginal note reconciles the household total: the original combined figure of 51,948 households becomes 52,548 when summed by category, so the 1,059 shrines are subtracted to follow the breakdown."
  },
  {
   "id": "himeji_lower_p102_left",
   "sequence": 218,
   "domain_canonical": "姫路藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "姫路藩",
   "domain_en": "Himeji",
   "image": "images/lower_p102_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 102,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（平戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Hirado) — running header",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Himeji five-year-average land-tax account and shrine/temple-land yield; opening of Hirado (kokudaka)",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of the page completes Himeji Domain's fascicle-7 fiscal entry as a five-year-average (五ヶ年平均) tax account: regular land-tax rice (正租米) of 1,234.488 koku, miscellaneous-tax rice (雜稅米) of 13.497 koku, and a cash tax (錢) of 10.756 kan whose rice equivalent (此米) is 0.134 koku, summing to a combined tax rice (合米) of 1,248.119 koku. It also records shrine- and temple-land yield (社寺領高) of 2,665.856 koku, with an additional 16.66 koku reckoned in, and notes that Himeji holds no ships (船ナシ). Below the ○平戸藩 maru-marker the page begins Hirado Domain, giving its nominal assessed yield (草高) of 61,700 koku and a heading for newly-reclaimed-field re-survey yield. The printed book-page number is 181 and the running header reads \"Fascicle 7 (Hirado).\""
  },
  {
   "id": "himeji_lower_p243_right",
   "sequence": 219,
   "domain_canonical": "姫路藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "姫路藩",
   "domain_en": "Himeji",
   "image": "images/lower_p243_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 243,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百六十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（姫路）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Himeji (姫路藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Officials and military (職員兵隊) — Hikone tail + Himeji",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表) is headed for Himeji (姫路藩), opened by its ○ domain-boundary marker. To the LEFT of the marker is Himeji's own entry: its officials are noted as 官員不詳 (not disclosed), and its military totals 288 兵士 (soldiers) and 576 兵卒 (rank-and-file troops) in 6 and 12 platoons respectively, plus 168 砲手 (gunners) and 54 樂手 (bandsmen). Read right-to-left, the columns to the RIGHT of the ○姫路藩 marker belong to the previous domain sharing this leaf, Hikone (彦根藩): its 少参事 (junior councillor, 2), 権少参事 (acting junior councillor, 3), a foot-soldier force of 36 platoons, and 2 artillery batteries of six guns each. That Hikone material does not belong to Himeji."
  },
  {
   "id": "hiji_lower_p109_left",
   "sequence": 220,
   "domain_canonical": "日出藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "日出藩",
   "domain_en": "Hiji",
   "image": "images/lower_p109_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 109,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（日出）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Hiji)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hiji domain regular land tax, miscellaneous tax, and household/status counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a continuation page for Hiji domain (日出藩, Bungo province, Kyushu; Kinoshita house) within fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran. The regular land tax (正租) is rice 8,906.0237 koku plus soybeans 1,584.274 koku, which sum exactly to the total regular tax (正租合高) of 10,490.2977 koku recorded here as a red-ink marginal note; the soybean levy is separately valued at 8,064 ryō 1 bu (at ~5 ryō 1 shu per koku) and re-expressed as 1,008.055 koku of rice at 8 ryō per koku. Miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) comprise rice 473.9329 koku and cash 112 ryō 1 bu plus 13 mon (ei). The domain has 4,712 households, of which 195 shizoku, 261 sotsu, 39 shrine families, 10 Shugendō yamabushi, and 9 blind monks, along with 47 temples."
  },
  {
   "id": "hiji_lower_p110_right",
   "sequence": 221,
   "domain_canonical": "日出藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "日出藩",
   "domain_en": "Hiji",
   "image": "images/lower_p110_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 110,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（一橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Hitotsubashi section)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hiji domain population by status and religious estate; Hitotsubashi kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page completes the Fascicle 7 demographic block for Hiji domain (日出藩, Bungo province): a total population of 20,925 (10,649 male, 10,276 female), broken out into 946 shizoku, 1,044 sotsu, 201 shrine attendants (社人), 127 Buddhist clergy (寺侶), 46 mountain ascetics (修驗山伏), 37 blind monks (盲僧), and an eta (outcaste) population of 177 persons living in 44 households, together with 125 Shinto shrines; the domain governor's own household is expressly not recorded. At the far left a maru-marker opens the Hitotsubashi domain (一橋藩) section, whose scattered holdings across eight provinces are noted in a warichu and whose nominal assessed yield (kusadaka) is given as 118,815.38858 koku. The male/female splits and the eta population column read directly from the scan were absent or transcribed incorrectly in the prior dataset. The running header names Hitotsubashi (provenance) even though the bulk of the data belongs to Hiji."
  },
  {
   "id": "hiji_lower_p245_right",
   "sequence": 222,
   "domain_canonical": "日出藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "日出藩",
   "domain_en": "Hiji",
   "image": "images/lower_p245_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 245,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（日出、一橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Hiji (日出藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Officials (shokuin) and troop strength (heitai) for three domains: the tail of an unnamed preceding domain, then Hiji (日出藩), then the start of Hitotsubashi (一橋藩)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表), read right-to-left, is headed for Hiji and Hitotsubashi and carries three domains. The central and dominant block is Hiji (日出藩), opened by its ○ domain-boundary marker: 大参事 (senior councillor, 1), 権大参事 (acting senior councillor, 2), 少参事 (junior councillor, 2), and 兵隊 (troops) of 5 platoons — 2 士族 (samurai) platoons and 3 卒 (foot-soldier) platoons. The rightmost columns are the tail of the domain immediately preceding Hiji: its 権大参事 (3), 少参事 (3), 権少参事 (3), named appointees, and 兵隊 (troops, 160 persons); because this troop figure sits to the RIGHT of the ○日出藩 marker, it belongs to that preceding domain, not to Hiji. At the far left the ○一橋藩 marker opens Hitotsubashi (一橋藩), whose 執政 (regents) begin here and continue onto the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuoka_upper_p217_left",
   "sequence": 223,
   "domain_canonical": "松岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p217_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 217,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（松岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Matsuoka)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsuoka miscellaneous taxes, administered-land total, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the middle of Matsuoka domain's fascicle-5 return, continuing without a break from the facing page, where the ○松岡藩 marker stands; no marker appears here, so every figure belongs to Matsuoka. The rightmost column completes the previous entry by converting the cash part of the regular land tax into rice at 8 ryō to the koku, giving 83.32793 koku. The miscellaneous-tax (雜税) group follows: 133.815 koku of barnyard millet reckoned at half a koku per ryō, worth 33.45375 koku of rice, plus 867.236 ryō in cash, worth 108.4045 koku — both conversions reconcile exactly at the stated 8-ryō rate. The leaf then records 4,049.60493 koku of administered land, 301.42 koku of shrine and temple land, and 2,842 households, of which 121 are shizoku, 105 sotsu, 23 shrine-family, 16 temple and 8 outcaste; a further 239 shrine sites are listed separately."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuoka_upper_p218_right",
   "sequence": 224,
   "domain_canonical": "松岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p218_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 218,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（福岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Matsuoka (松岡藩): demographics",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsuoka demographics (shares the Fukuoka-opening leaf; Matsuoka's tail continues here)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf sits on the boundary between two domains in Fascicle 5 of the survey, which records population and household figures. At the lower left it opens the entry for Fukuoka (福岡藩) with that domain's ○ (domain-boundary marker) and land figure. But read right-to-left, everything to the right of that marker is the closing demographic block of the preceding domain, Matsuoka (松岡藩): a total population of 12,805, with 士族 (samurai households) numbering 507 persons and 卒族 (lower-samurai households) 365, alongside 139 Shinto-priest and 39 temple residents, 65 in the outcast (穢多) group, and 29 villages. The Fukuoka data proper continues on the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuoka_lower_p213_left",
   "sequence": 225,
   "domain_canonical": "松岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsuoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p213_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 213,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（松岡、福岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Matsuoka, Fukuoka)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of fascicle 9 records the reorganized 1869-70 官制 (office system) and troop returns for two domains. Matsuoka (Hitachi province, Nakayama house) lists a governor, Nakayama Nobuakira, together with three senior councillors (大參事, of whom Ōta Shin and Ishikawa Hiroki are named), two acting senior councillors (權大參事, Fujita Ryōzō named) and four junior councillors (少參事, Matsumura Gio named); its troops number 78 shizoku and 47 sotsu, 125 men in all. Fukuoka's block opens at the foot of the page with one governor and five senior councillors, all five of whom are named: Kuroda Kazuyoshi, Kōri Narimi, Yano Yasuo, Ogawa Ujio and Tachibana Masuzane. At the top right, above the Matsuoka marker, the military return of the preceding domain, Mariyama, spills across the gutter: 17 soldiers and one platoon of 40 rank-and-file."
  },
  {
   "id": "shonai_upper_p065_right",
   "sequence": 226,
   "domain_canonical": "大泉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大泉藩",
   "domain_en": "Shōnai (Ōizumi)",
   "image": "images/upper_p065_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 65,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（大泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Okayama (岡山藩): demographics",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Okayama domain population and household breakdown by status group, grand totals, shrines/temples, and one warship (Fascicle 2 demographics).",
   "page_summary_en": "This page comes from Fascicle 2 of the survey, the demographic register, and carries the closing portion of the Okayama domain (岡山藩) entry. The ○ (domain-boundary marker) for the next domain, Ōizumi (大泉藩), appears at the lower left, so every column to the right of it belongs to Okayama. It records a commoner population of 328,341 (172,475 male, 155,874 female), broken down by status group: Shinto-priest households and population (642 households, 2,772 persons), 709 temple clergy, mountain-ascetic (山伏) households and population (105 / 323), and outcast (穢多) households and population (993 / 9,128). The grand totals are 85,431 households and 358,827 persons, and the domain reports 701 shrines, 464 temples, and one warship."
  },
  {
   "id": "oizumi_upper_p065_left",
   "sequence": 227,
   "domain_canonical": "大泉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大泉藩",
   "domain_en": "Shōnai (Ōizumi)",
   "image": "images/upper_p065_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 65,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey Table, Fascicle 2 (Ōizumi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōizumi (Shōnai) yield, taxes, households, population",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle-2 fiscal and demographic block for Ōizumi domain (the renamed Shōnai domain, Dewa; castle town Tsuruoka). The page records a gross assessed yield (草高) of 120,000 koku and a regular rice tax (正租米) of 68,013.99853 koku, flagged in small print as a five-year average. Under miscellaneous taxes (諸雜稅) it itemizes 2,362.31353 koku of rice, 1,151 ryō 2 bu in gold with a small silver remainder, 2,564 kan 662 mon of copper cash, 95.797155 kanme of wax, 25.257654 kanme of lacquer, 3.6 koku of salt, and 100,000 sheets of dried squid. The page closes with 14,744 households and a population of 79,934 (40,122 male, 39,812 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "oizumi_upper_p066_right",
   "sequence": 228,
   "domain_canonical": "大泉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大泉藩",
   "domain_en": "Shōnai (Ōizumi)",
   "image": "images/upper_p066_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 66,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table 2 (Ōizumi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Status-group and religious households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Ōizumi (Shōnai) domain entry in fascicle 2. Beyond the commoner totals reported on the preceding page, the domain lists as additional categories 48 eta/hinin households (296 persons), 930 shizoku households (5,392 persons), and 930 sotsu households (9,705 persons), each with a male/female split. A religious block headed 神社 records 526 temples (population printed as 1,604, though its own male/female components print as 1,416 and 558), 128 shrine-priest households with 673 persons, 181 shugen households with 283 persons, and 4 miko households with 16 persons. A parenthetical note states a received grant of 1,752.88343 koku, of which 1,452.31116 koku is actual rice."
  },
  {
   "id": "shonai_lower_p149_right",
