   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Okayama (岡山藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Okayama domain officials (councillors and administrative ranks) and standing military force, at the boundary with the Ōizumi domain entry.",
   "page_summary_en": "This page belongs to Fascicle 8 of the survey, which lists domain officials and military strength. Although the running header names the Ōizumi (大泉藩) section, the ○ (domain-boundary marker) for Ōizumi sits in mid-page, so everything to its right is the entry for the preceding domain, Okayama (岡山藩). It names eight councillors (議員) under the administrative ranks 少参事 (junior counsellor) and 権少参事 (acting junior counsellor), and gives Okayama's standing army as seventeen rifle battalions (銃隊) and four artillery emplacements (砲隊), totaling 7,862 men. To the left of the marker, the 知事 (governor) heading opens the next domain, Ōizumi."
  },
  {
   "id": "oizumi_lower_p149_left",
   "sequence": 230,
   "domain_canonical": "大泉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大泉藩",
   "domain_en": "Shōnai (Ōizumi)",
   "image": "images/lower_p149_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 149,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Domain Survey), Fascicle 8 (officials & military register), Ōizumi (Shōnai) section — running header / provenance",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials — councillor ranks and roster",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left (continuation) page of the Ōizumi (大泉 = the 1869 rename of Shōnai/庄内) Domain's officials entry in Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran. It records four councillor ranks with headcounts — Grand Councillor (大参事) 2, Acting Grand Councillor (権大参事) printed as 5 but corrected by an interlinear note to 4, Junior Councillor (少参事) 5, and Acting Junior Councillor (権少参事) 2 — followed in the lower band by the thirteen named officeholders. The roster of thirteen names matches the corrected sum 2+4+5+2 exactly, confirming that the 権大参事 count is four rather than five. The ○大泉藩 marker and the governor (知事) that open the entry are on the facing right page (p.149 recto), not on this leaf; the inner-margin figures give the provenance header 藩制一覧表第八（大泉）and reprint page number 275."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirosaki_lower_p097_right",
   "sequence": 231,
   "domain_canonical": "弘前藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "弘前藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirosaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p097_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 97,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（弘前）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Hirosaki (弘前藩): land assessment and taxes",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-7 boundary page: tail of the previous domain's population/religious/warship fields, then the head of Hirosaki-han's (弘前藩) fiscal block (kokudaka, land tax, totals, households).",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a boundary leaf from Fascicle 7 of the survey, which records each domain's land assessment, taxes, and household totals. The ○ (domain-boundary marker) here reads ○弘前藩, opening the entry for Hirosaki (弘前藩) at an original assessment of 100,000 koku. Everything at and to the left of that marker is Hirosaki's own fiscal block: 草高 (assessed yield) of 274,482 koku including reclaimed land, 正租 (regular land tax) of 130,854.5 koku as a five-year average, miscellaneous taxes in rice and cash, combined grand totals, and 50,162 households (戸數). The five columns to the right of the marker — clergy, outcast population, shrines, the governor's family, and warships — are the closing fields of the previous domain, whose own entry falls on the preceding leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirosaki_lower_p097_left",
   "sequence": 232,
   "domain_canonical": "弘前藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "弘前藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirosaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p097_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 97,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（弘前）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Hirosaki)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Population, status counts, temples/shrines, and Boshin reward-rice (弘前藩)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the fascicle-7 population/household block for Hirosaki domain (弘前藩) in Mutsu. It records a total population of 278,842 — a printed figure the 1928 reprint flags with a マ (\"sic\") mark, since the male 142,085 + female 136,657 split actually sums to 278,742 (100 fewer). Of the population it breaks out shizoku 12,469 persons, sotsu 10,215, shrine-people (社人) 799, and temple-clergy (寺侶) 726, each with its own male/female split, and notes that eta/hinin were not recorded. Household counts give 2,066 shizoku, 2,261 sotsu, 269 temples and 117 shrine-households; the domain has 873 shrines, holds no warships, and receives an imperial reward-rice (御賞典米) of 2,500 koku tied to a perpetual 10,000-koku grant plus a 10,000-koku-per-year three-year grant."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirosaki_lower_p242_left",
   "sequence": 233,
   "domain_canonical": "弘前藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "弘前藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirosaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p242_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 242,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（弘前、彦根）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Hirosaki, Hikone)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle-9 entry for Hirosaki domain (Tsugaru, Mutsu) with its councillor establishment and its troop strength. Hirosaki reports 2 senior councillors (大參事), 3 acting senior councillors (權大參事), 4 junior councillors (少參事) and 4 acting junior councillors (權少參事) — thirteen men, each named in the columns printed beneath the counts, among them Nishidate Tōru, Sugiyama Ryūkō, Nishidate Kosei and Kusumi Taiso. Its forces are given in a two-register note under 兵隊 as 2,057 heishi and 1,449 heisotsu, 3,506 men in all. A second maru-marker mid-leaf begins Hikone domain, whose first two grades appear here: 1 senior councillor (Shinno Kosetsu) and 3 acting senior councillors (Kimata Kan, Tanaka Ō, Nishimura Jūzō), the entry continuing on the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "mori_lower_p113_left",
   "sequence": 234,
   "domain_canonical": "森藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "森藩",
   "domain_en": "Mori",
   "image": "images/lower_p113_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 113,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七 （森）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Mori (森藩): population and taxes",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mori Domain (森藩) civil statistics — continuation: retainer-class households/populations, domain kokudaka taxes (soybean, misc-tax rice, gold, ei), total households, and population with male/female splits",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left, continuation half of the two-page Fascicle 7 entry for Mori (森藩), a small domain of about 12,500 koku in Bungo Province held by the Kurushima (久留島) family. Its ○ (domain-boundary marker) and header open on the facing right half, so this half carries no marker and is read right-to-left as a continuation. It records Mori's population of 14,244 (6,839 male, 7,405 female) and, by status, 128 士族 (samurai households) with 720 persons and 130 卒族 (lower-retainer households) with 726 persons, for 2,645 households (總戸數) in all. The tax yields follow: soybeans of 1,205.278 koku, miscellaneous-tax rice (雜稅米) of 262.216 koku, gold of 245 ryō, and a small cash (永) figure of 17.122."
  },
  {
   "id": "mori_lower_p114_right",
   "sequence": 235,
   "domain_canonical": "森藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "森藩",
   "domain_en": "Mori",
   "image": "images/lower_p114_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 114,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（森）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle 7 (Mori)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mori han religious populations, temple/shrine counts, outcaste households, governor's family, villages, and warships",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a continuation leaf of the 森藩 (Mori Domain, Bungo province) entry in Fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran, with no domain marker; the running header (Fascicle 7, Mori) identifies the block and all columns belong to Mori. It records small religious and marginal populations: the shrine-office (社務) community numbers 11 households and 71 persons (39 male, 32 female), and the Buddhist-temple clergy 20 temples with 70 persons (33 male, 37 female). Outcaste groups are minimal — 穢多 3 households / 20 persons (7 male, 13 female) and 非人 2 households / 12 persons (printed as 5 male, 7 female, which MASTER has recorded with the sexes reversed). The page also lists 10 Shinto shrines (plus 14 auxiliary, 10 subordinate, and 13 minor shrines), the governor's household of 5 (3 male, 2 female), notes that the village count was not recorded (記セス), and reports no warships (艦ナシ); the leaf is printed page 204."
  },
  {
   "id": "kokura_lower_p143_right",
   "sequence": 236,
   "domain_canonical": "香春藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "香春藩",
   "domain_en": "Kokura (Kawara)",
   "image": "images/lower_p143_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 143,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（香春）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Kōharu / Kokura (香春藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-8 officials-and-military boundary page: Tottori's overflow (權少参事 officials + army) at right, and the start of Kōharu's block at left.",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a Fascicle 8 leaf recording domain officials and military strength, sitting on the boundary between two domains. The ○ (domain-boundary marker) reads ○香春藩, so the block to the left of it opens the entry for Kōharu (香春藩): a governor (知事), one senior councillor (大参事), four acting senior councillors (権大参事), and a force of forty-six companies totaling roughly 2,700 men. Everything to the right of the marker is the overflow of the preceding domain, Tottori (鳥取藩): its 権少参事 (acting junior counsellor) rank with six named appointees, and its army of ten battalions (3,734 men) plus an artillery corps (砲隊) of 240 men."
  },
  {
   "id": "numata_upper_p063_right",
   "sequence": 237,
   "domain_canonical": "沼田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "沼田藩",
   "domain_en": "Numata",
   "image": "images/upper_p063_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 63,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（沼田）",
   "page_header_en": "Overview of Domain Administration, Table 2 (Numata)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ryūgasaki block tail (households, shrines, temples, villages) and Numata kokudaka and land-tax block",
   "page_summary_en": "The right half of this leaf closes out the Ryūgasaki block begun on the previous page and opens the Numata block. Ryūgasaki's tail records 26 additional sotsu (foot-soldier) households with 76 persons (39 male, 37 female), 17 watchmen-hinin households with 36 persons (23 male, 13 female), 93 Shintō shrines served by 17 priest households of 73 persons (38 male, 35 female), 40 Buddhist temples with 57 residents (49 male, 8 female), and 45 villages. After the ○沼田藩 marker, Numata reports a gross assessed yield of 44,154.21279 koku, broken down into the listed 35,000 koku and 9,154.21279 koku of added-in yield, a regular land tax in rice of 12,899.9788 koku, and a regular tax on dry fields of 2,490 ryō in gold plus 5 mon 8 bu in eisen."
  },
  {
   "id": "numata_upper_p063_left",
   "sequence": 238,
   "domain_canonical": "沼田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "沼田藩",
   "domain_en": "Numata",
   "image": "images/upper_p063_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 63,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（沼田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Survey of Domain Administration), Table 2 (Numata)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Numata domain tax-rice totals, households, and status-group population",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Numata domain entry in fascicle 2. The tax account closes here: miscellaneous tax rice of 1,731.8468 koku, a cash tax of 502.41738 ryō converted at 8 ryō per koku into 62.80217 koku, and a further conversion of 417.34505 koku priced at the 1864-1868 five-year average, bringing total tax rice to 15,111.97282 koku. The domain counts 9,804 households and 42,499 people (22,007 male, 20,492 female), of which samurai households number 280 (1,167 people) and sotsu households 229 (598 people). The page closes with 510 Shinto shrines served by 21 shrine-attendant households of 82 people, and a bare heading 成物高 (produce yield) with no value printed on this leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "numata_lower_p148_right",
   "sequence": 239,
   "domain_canonical": "沼田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "沼田藩",
   "domain_en": "Numata",
   "image": "images/lower_p148_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 148,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八 （沼田）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Numata (沼田藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (chiji and sanji ranks) and military strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the officials-and-military page (Fascicle 8) for Numata (沼田藩) in Kōzuke Province. In its two-register layout, the upper band gives the administrative ranks — a governor (知事), two senior councillors (大参事), two acting senior councillors (権大参事), and five junior councillors (少参事) — with the appointees' names in the lower band; the governor's slot carries no printed name, and the nine listed names fill the councillor rolls exactly. At the left the military entry records a garrison of 251 troops (兵隊) organized as three and a half platoons, noted at 66 men per platoon including officers. This is a clean single-domain leaf, with no ○ (domain-boundary marker) and no overflow from a neighbor."
  },
  {
   "id": "otawara_upper_p085_right",
   "sequence": 240,
   "domain_canonical": "大田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōtawara",
   "image": "images/upper_p085_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 85,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大田原）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Two (Ōtawara)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōtawara land assessment, grain revenue, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "The page opens the 大田原藩 (Ōtawara, Shimotsuke) entry of fascicle two of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, and the three columns to the right of the ○大田原藩 marker close out the preceding domain's block (temples 49 with 77 monks; an outcaste population of 33, 18 male and 15 female; and a force of three platoons totalling 110 men). Ōtawara's own figures give a nominal assessment (草高) of 16,021.4939 koku against an actual grain revenue (現石) of 2,482.8631 koku, itemised as 2,163.1646 koku of rice, 96.21098 koku of soybeans and 220.01924 koku of oil-perilla — components that fall 3.46828 koku short of the stated total. The domain returns 2,397 households and 12,535 people, of which 122 shizoku households and 60 sotsu households, followed by a population of 724 whose printed male and female figures (358 and 399) in fact sum to 757. The bottom margin carries the printed page number 144."
  },
  {
   "id": "otawara_lower_p161_right",
   "sequence": 241,
   "domain_canonical": "大田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōtawara",
   "image": "images/lower_p161_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 161,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大田原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Ōtawara (大田原藩): officials roster",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-8 domain-officials roster (governor and councillors) — the data belongs to Ōtawara domain (大田原藩), NOT Wakayama despite the batch label",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a Fascicle 8 page of the survey, listing the appointed administrative officers of a single domain. The running header names Ōtawara (大田原藩), a small fudai domain of about 11,400 koku in Shimotsuke Province, and the governor (知事) is its hereditary lord Ōtawara Ichigaku (大田原一學). The roster records one governor, one senior councillor (大参事), one acting senior councillor (権大参事), five junior councillors (少参事), and three acting junior councillors (権少参事), each named individually. A small interlinear note beside the fifth junior councillor records a variant reading of his name."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshimi_upper_p115_left",
   "sequence": 242,
   "domain_canonical": "吉見藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉見藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshimi",
   "image": "images/upper_p115_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 115,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（吉見）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Yoshimi)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yoita's household, population and troop returns; Yoshimi's assessed yield",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 205 of fascicle 3 carries the tail of the Yoita (與板) return and the opening of the Yoshimi (吉見) return, divided by the ○吉見藩 marker. Everything to the right of that marker is Yoita's: 253 shizoku and 71 sotsu households, 5 eta households, a population of 21,032 (10,287 male, 10,745 female), 60 people in shrine households (12 hafuri priests, 17 men, 31 women), 235 in temple households (106 monks, 32 men, 97 women), 1,203 domain samurai and foot-soldiers with their households (584 male, 619 female), 29 eta persons (16 male, 13 female), and 178 troops. The village-count heading and the sub-heading 兵隊士卒 are printed with no figures entered. To the left of the marker Yoshimi's return opens with an assessed yield of 12,000 koku, to which the survey adds 2,391.80724 koku of komidaka and 117.686 koku of new-field yield."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshimi_upper_p116_right",
   "sequence": 243,
   "domain_canonical": "吉見藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉見藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshimi",
   "image": "images/upper_p116_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 116,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（吉見）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 3 (Yoshimi)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yoshimi domain: assessed yield, five-year average land and miscellaneous tax, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 206 of fascicle 3 continues the entry for Yoshimi domain (Musashi province); no maru-marker appears on the leaf, and the running header names Yoshimi. The domain's combined assessed yield (合高) is 14,509.49324 koku. Under the heading \"five-year average,\" the regular land tax (正租) is reported as 4,750.728856 koku of rice together with 2,544 ryō 1 bu 2 shu in gold and 377 kan 74.859 mon in ei-cash, and the miscellaneous tax (雜稅) as 205.2688 koku of rice, 12 ryō 1 shu in gold, and 62 kan 531.38 mon in ei-cash. The household section prints its heading (戸數) with no total, then lists 13 shrines and 11 temples — each qualified as covering only the tax-exempt-land holdings, the remainder being unknown — 73 shizoku households and 58 sotsu households, with a note that a further four households are counted within those two figures; the categories eta and hinin are printed as bare headings with no figures."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshimi_lower_p176_right",
   "sequence": 244,
   "domain_canonical": "吉見藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉見藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshimi",
   "image": "images/lower_p176_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 176,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八 (吉見)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Yoshimi (吉見藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military (職員兵隊) — Yoshii officials/troops overflowing right of the Yoshimi marker, plus the opening of the Yoshimi entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a Fascicle 8 leaf recording domain officials and military strength, sitting on the boundary between two domains. The ○ (domain-boundary marker) printed here reads ○吉見藩, so Yoshimi (吉見藩) is the page's own domain: its entry opens with the governor (知事, unnamed on this half) and one senior councillor (大参事), continuing onto the facing half. Everything to the right of the marker is the overflow of the preceding domain, Yoshii (吉井藩): its lower-rank tallies — three junior councillors (少参事), two acting senior councillors (権大参事), and three acting junior councillors (権少参事) — a military strength of 178 men (兵員), and a roster of nine named officials. Two small collation notes record variant readings from another copy of the source."
  },
  {
