   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Survey Table, Fascicle Four (Nobeoka)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka deductions and the regular land tax (正租高)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the continuation of Nobeoka domain's land-assessment entry in fascicle four of the Hansei ichiran; there is no maru-marker on the page and every figure belongs to 延岡藩. Two deductions open the page: 1,315.24897 koku of hikidaka, glossed as yield newly assessed after Enkyō 4 (1747, a rabbit year), and 8,942.45138 koku deducted for waste ground, itemized as long-untaxed land, samurai residence lots, row-house plots and road allowances, ditch beds, embankment beds, thickets, river washouts, and gravel- and sand-covered fields; the remainder (殘) stands at 72,872.6217 koku, which with the two deductions restores a 草高 of 83,130.32205 koku. The regular land tax (正租高) is then entered as 28,010.0626 koku of actual rice at a five-year average rate of 0.3497, broken down into 22,948.17407 koku of true rice, 2,125.405 koku commuted into 2,550.486 koku of red rice at exactly 1.2 to 1, 2,135.505 koku commuted into 3,416.808 koku of soybeans at exactly 1.6 to 1, and a further 456.00666 koku whose commutation runs over onto the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "nobeoka_upper_p180_left",
   "sequence": 246,
   "domain_canonical": "延岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "延岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Nobeoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p180_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 180,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（延岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (Nobeoka)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nobeoka tax-rice conversions, miscellaneous tax, and total rice",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the fascicle-4 revenue block of Nobeoka Domain (延岡藩) begun on the facing page; it carries no maru-marker, so every column on it belongs to Nobeoka. The right half records grain and cash conversions of tax items — 1,094.416 koku of barley, a bare 158.6205 koku, 317.241 koku of wheat, 186.35137 koku of rice, and a cash equivalent of 1,490 ryō 811 mon — after which a closing 〆 mark ends that list. The left half opens the heading 雜稅高 (miscellaneous tax), totalling 896.29525 koku of rice, broken into 305.836 koku and 590.45925 koku, which sum exactly to that total; the second portion is converted to 4,723 ryō 674 mon. The block closes with 合米 28,906.35785 koku, the domain's combined tax rice, and both cash conversions run at exactly eight ryō per koku, which independently confirms the digit readings."
  },
  {
   "id": "nobeoka_upper_p181_right",
   "sequence": 247,
   "domain_canonical": "延岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "延岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Nobeoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p181_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 181,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（延岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 4 (Nobeoka)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nobeoka products, tax, households and status population",
   "page_summary_en": "This sheet continues the fascicle-4 return for Nobeoka domain in Hyūga province. It lists the domain's products — charcoal, Taihei ink, timber (pine, katsura, hemlock, zelkova and miscellaneous wood), long cedar stock, tea, shiitake, hemp and ramie, and silkworm mounting frames — on which the tax is 1,700-odd ryō, and it adds copper, assorted papers, wax and seaweed, which the Accounting Bureau buys in and which therefore bear no tax. The domain returns 23,960 households and 124,966 people. Of these the sheet itemises six status groups: 490 shizoku households (2,120 people), 944 sotsu households (4,022), 203 Shinto priestly households (1,082), 156 temple households (413), 81 mountain-ascetic households (411) and 8 blind-monk households (40 people, comprising 14 blind monks, 16 women and 10 lay men)."
  },
  {
   "id": "nobeoka_upper_p181_left",
   "sequence": 248,
   "domain_canonical": "延岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "延岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Nobeoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p181_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 181,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（野村）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table (fascicle) Four — Nomura",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nobeoka households, population and status counts; opening of the Nomura kokudaka entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the fourth-fascicle return for Nobeoka Domain (Hyūga) and opens the return for Nomura Domain. Nobeoka reports 21,965 commoner households and a total population of 116,189 (60,495 male, 55,694 female), together with one kazoku household of four persons (the former daimyo-governor), 38 eta households, 69 hinin households, and six households in the two outlying wards of Ehira-machi and Keiga-machi; its territory is given as 5 districts, 165 villages and 1,507 shrines, with Buddhist halls left uncounted. The marker ○野村藩 then opens Nomura Domain (Iyo), whose assessed kokudaka is 13,089.007 koku, of which 2,721.363 koku is newly opened paddy (shinden) and 34.466 koku is komidaka. The eta figures do not reconcile: the printed total of 350 persons exceeds the sum of the male and female sub-counts (188 + 62 = 250)."
  },
  {
   "id": "nobeoka_lower_p199_right",
   "sequence": 249,
   "domain_canonical": "延岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "延岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Nobeoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p199_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 199,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九 （延岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Nobeoka (延岡藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "officials_and_military",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the officials-and-military page for Nobeoka (延岡藩) in Hyūga Province, governed by Naitō Masanori (内藤政學), from Fascicle 9 of the survey. Read right-to-left, the ○ (domain-boundary marker) ○延岡藩 opens Nobeoka's entry: a governor (知事), two senior councillors (大参事), one acting senior councillor (権大参事), and five junior councillors (少参事), together with a separately reported list of officials. Nobeoka's military (兵隊) totals 878 men — 345 samurai troops and 503 foot-soldier troops (upper and lower), plus six cannon (大砲) with thirty gunners. The three fields to the right of the marker — undetailed officials, 159 foot soldiers, and 175 rural levies — are overflow belonging to the previous domain in this fascicle, not to Nobeoka."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamaga_upper_p200_left",
   "sequence": 250,
   "domain_canonical": "山家藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山家藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamaga",
   "image": "images/upper_p200_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 200,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（山家）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 5 — (Yamaga)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yamaga domain: land assessment, tax receipts, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 375 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle 5, carries the fiscal and household return for Yamaga domain in Tanba. The assessed gross yield (草高) is 10,082.83 koku, and the tax rice actually taken is 4,370.52641 koku, stated as one year's share of a five-year average; of that, 3,460.52641 koku was delivered in rice and 910 koku was commuted to a silver payment, while the miscellaneous tax came to 15.475 koku in rice and soybeans plus 3,202.82 monme of silver. A 〆 line totals the grain at 4,386.00141 koku, which is exactly 4,370.52641 + 15.475. The household block records 76 shizoku houses, 38 sotsu houses and 25 temple houses, with a note that the commoner household count was not reported; the population heading (人員) opens at the left edge and its figures print on the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamaga_lower_p207_right",
   "sequence": 251,
   "domain_canonical": "山家藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山家藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamaga",
   "image": "images/lower_p207_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 207,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（山上、山家）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Yamagami (山上藩) and Yamaga (山家藩): officials and military",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (chiji through gon-shōsanji, with appointee names and a kōginin) and military strength for Yamagami-han and Yamaga-han",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf comes from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表), the fascicle that records each domain's officials roster and military strength, and its running head names the two domains it covers: Yamagami (山上藩) and Yamaga (山家藩). The ○ domain-boundary marker on this leaf opens Yamaga (○山家藩), which lists one 知事 (governor), two 大参事 (senior councillors), two 権大参事 (junior senior councillors), and four 少参事 (junior councillors), with named appointees. The officials and 兵隊 (troops) block printed to the right of the ○山家藩 marker belong to the previous domain sharing this leaf, Yamagami — whose roster runs from governor down through junior councillors and whose military is given as 36 士族 (samurai-class troops) and 61 卒 (foot-soldier-class troops), for 97 in all."
  },
  {
   "id": "yatabe_upper_p201_right",
   "sequence": 252,
   "domain_canonical": "谷田部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "谷田部藩",
   "domain_en": "Yatabe",
   "image": "images/upper_p201_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 201,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（谷田部）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 5 — (Yatabe)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Close of Yamaga's population returns; opening of Yatabe's kokudaka and land tax",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand columns finish the returns for 山家藩 (Yamaga, Tanba): 343 shizoku (163 male, 180 female), 131 sotsu, 47 temple personnel (45 male, 2 female), one shrine attendant, one shrine building, and a governor's household of seven (three male, four female). The maru-marker ○谷田部藩 then opens 谷田部藩 (Yatabe, Hitachi), whose gross assessed kokudaka is 27,924.5998 koku, itemised in small type as 11,659.6998 koku across three Hitachi districts and 16,264.9 koku in one Shimotsuke district — the two components summing exactly to the printed total. Yatabe's regular land tax (正租) is rendered in three media: 3,724.7687 koku of hulled rice, 1,501 ryō in gold, and 156.25 mon in eiraku cash; miscellaneous taxes (雜税) add 63.9439 koku of rice. The sotsu breakdown is the one figure that will not reconcile: 63 male plus 69 female is 132 against a printed total of 131, and single-character zooms confirm all three numerals as set, so the discrepancy is the source's own."
  },
  {
   "id": "yatabe_upper_p201_left",
   "sequence": 253,
   "domain_canonical": "谷田部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "谷田部藩",
   "domain_en": "Yatabe",
   "image": "images/upper_p201_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 201,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（谷田部）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Tables, Fascicle Five (Yatabe)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yatabe domain households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-five return for Yatabe domain, whose maru-marker ○谷田部藩 stands on the facing right-hand page. It closes the miscellaneous-tax entry with 37 ryō in gold and 1 kan 357 mon 5 bu 7 rin 5 mō in eisen cash, then gives the domain's household count of 2,605, of which 107 belong to the shizoku, 147 to the sotsu, 105 are temples, 22 are cloister quarters, 11 are shrine-priest houses, 12 are Shugendō houses and 1 is a hermitage. The population stands at 13,425 persons, split 6,955 male and 6,470 female, with 448 shizoku (219 male, 229 female), 232 sotsu (150 male, 82 female), 64 shrine-priest household members (27 male, 37 female) and 40 Shugendō practitioners (20 male, 20 female). Each male-female pair sums exactly to its printed total, and the outer margin carries the running header and the printed page number 377."
  },
  {
   "id": "yatabe_lower_p207_left",
   "sequence": 254,
   "domain_canonical": "谷田部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "谷田部藩",
   "domain_en": "Yatabe",
   "image": "images/lower_p207_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 207,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — Yatabe (谷田部藩), with Yachi (谷地藩) and Matsue (松江藩)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (governor and councillors) with appointee names, plus military notation, for Yatabe, Yachi, and Matsue",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf comes from Fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran (藩制一覧表), the fascicle recording each domain's officials roster and military strength, and is read right to left. Its principal domain is Yatabe (○谷田部藩), whose full slate of officials is printed: one 知事 (governor), one 大参事 (senior councillor), three 権大参事 (junior senior councillors), and four 少参事 (junior councillors), together with eight named appointees; Yatabe's troop strength is left unspecified (兵隊未詳, troops not detailed). This leaf also carries the opening of two neighbouring domains — Yachi (○谷地藩), whose officials and troops are both marked undetailed (職員兵數不詳), and Matsue (○松江藩), which shows one 知事 (governor) with its remaining figures continuing onto the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "koriyama_lower_p012_left",
   "sequence": 255,
   "domain_canonical": "郡山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "郡山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kōriyama (Yamato-Kōriyama)",
   "image": "images/lower_p012_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 12,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō (Survey of Domain Administration), Fascicle 6",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kōriyama domain — land assessment and tax (kokudaka, land tax, miscellaneous tax, cash)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the fascicle-6 (藩制一覧表第六) economic entry for Kōriyama Domain (郡山藩, Yamato province; Yanagisawa clan). It records a gross assessed yield (草高) of 152,912.29987 koku and states the land tax as three rice figures — regular land-tax rice (正租米) 34,931.513 koku, a rice item of 902.9454 koku, and an unlabeled component of 18,417.38 koku — which sum exactly to the 合 total of 54,251.8384 koku (arithmetic verified). Miscellaneous-tax rice (雜稅米) is 101.3114 koku, and the entry lists two cash figures (39 ryō + 永36.7 mon; 2 ryō 1 bu 2 shu + 永16.8 mon) plus a further rice figure of 3,824.4078 koku. The block is a single domain: the ○郡山藩 marker sits at upper right, all data columns lie to its left, and a rectangular library-collection seal overlaps the running header at the top right."
  },
  {
   "id": "koriyama_lower_p013_right",
   "sequence": 256,
   "domain_canonical": "郡山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "郡山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kōriyama (Yamato-Kōriyama)",
   "image": "images/lower_p013_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 13,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（郡山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Kōriyama)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kōriyama domain: households, population, and rice/cash figures",
   "page_summary_en": "This second folio of the 郡山藩 (Yamato-Kōriyama, Yanagisawa) entry in fascicle 6 records the domain's household and population statistics alongside rice and cash figures. Households total 22,557 (戸數), of which the itemized special statuses are 士族 1,114, 卒族 754, 社人 49, 陰陽師 7, 座頭 2, 非人番 70, 煙亡 116, and 穢多 575. The population is 102,426 (男 50,917; 女 51,509), of which the 士族 population is 4,468 (男 2,018; 女 2,450). The sheet also gives rice sums of 1,303.1926 koku (米) and a combined 5,228.9118 koku (合米), and two cash amounts headed 金 (≈15 ryō and ≈56 ryō)."
  },
  {
   "id": "koriyama_lower_p013_left",
   "sequence": 257,
   "domain_canonical": "郡山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "郡山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kōriyama (Yamato-Kōriyama)",
   "image": "images/lower_p013_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 13,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（郡山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Kōriyama)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Special-status population counts and religious institutions (Kōriyama)",
   "page_summary_en": "This interior leaf of the Kōriyama (Yamato) domain block in fascicle 6 tabulates special-status population counts and religious institutions. It records the sub-samurai (卒族) class at 1,781 (872 male / 909 female) and religious and outcaste groups including 897 Buddhist monks, 25 nuns, 169 shrine attendants, 26 onmyōji diviners, 2 zatō, 228 hinin watchmen, 225 onbō, and 2,003 eta (990 male / 1,013 female), with male/female breakdowns that all sum correctly. It counts 406 Shinto shrines and 683 Buddhist temples, and identifies the principal shrine, Sasaki-jinja at Jōrakuji village in Gamō district, Ōmi province, with an assessed endowment (受領高) of 100 koku and regular land-tax rice (正租米) of 63.9375 koku. A bracketed \"of which\" male/female note beside the monk and nun entries reads 308 male / 745 female — a total (1,053) that exceeds the 922 monks-plus-nuns, an apparent source inconsistency noted but transcribed as printed."
  },
  {
   "id": "koriyama_lower_p217_left",
   "sequence": 258,
   "domain_canonical": "郡山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "郡山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kōriyama (Yamato-Kōriyama)",
   "image": "images/lower_p217_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 217,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九　（郡山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 9 (Kōriyama)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso folio of fascicle 9 closes the entry for Fukiage domain and opens that for Kōriyama. The three columns to the right of the maru-marker complete Fukiage's roster of six 權少參事 (junior councillors) — Horiuchi Tametarō, Horie Ikuzaemon, Katayama Shinzaburō, Mikami Kakunoshin, Hayakawa Mouemon and Okayama Hanzaemon — and record its force as two platoons, 129 men. Left of the ○郡山藩 marker, Kōriyama's senior officers are listed by grade: governor Yanagisawa; senior councillor Nitta Saburō (Yoshio); acting senior councillors Yasumoto Hikosuke (Shinao) and Motegi Kyōzaemon (Michikazu); junior councillor Hiraoka Uemon, against whose name the compilers print a bracketed note that the resident-officer's return gave Uchida Nariyuki instead and carried no Hiraoka; and acting junior councillors Noguchi Saori and Aoki Masuyoshi. Kōriyama's troops are reported in two status classes, 889 shizoku and 472 sotsu, 1,361 men in all."
  },
  {
   "id": "koga_lower_p015_right",
   "sequence": 259,
   "domain_canonical": "古河藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "古河藩",
   "domain_en": "Koga",
   "image": "images/lower_p015_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 15,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（古河）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Table of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 6 (Koga)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Koga domain: land assessment, land/misc tax with cash-commutation, and households",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the opening page of the 古河藩 (Koga Domain) entry in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran. It records Koga's base assessment 本高 80,000 koku and gross assessment 草高 101,257.932593 koku (of which 1,096.764 koku is 従前無地高, formerly no-land / newly-assessed yield); a regular land tax 正租米 24,108.736514 koku with a commuted-cash component 永 12,431.170142 kan-mon equal to 1,553.89628 koku of rice (at the noted rate of 8 ryō per koku); a small miscellaneous tax 雜税米 3.8323 koku with its own cash component 永 318.285347 kan-mon = 39.785669 koku; a grand total 合米 25,706.250763 koku; and 16,747 households. The two columns to the right of the ○古河藩 marker (正税 2.28 koku and the note 右制物有之分) are overflow belonging to the PRECEDING entry — the 佐々木神社 shrine estate in Ōmi (江州蒲生郡常樂寺村, 受領高 100 koku) — not to Koga."
  },
  {
   "id": "koga_lower_p015_left",
   "sequence": 260,
   "domain_canonical": "古河藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "古河",
   "domain_en": "Koga",
   "image": "images/lower_p015_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 15,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（古河）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Koga)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Koga domain population and status register (fascicle 6, demographic)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is a continuation of the fascicle-6 (demographic) return for Koga Domain (古河藩), a Shimōsa domain held by the Doi house. It records a total population of 74,777 (37,707 male / 37,070 female), broken out by status: 1,349 shizoku persons in 287 households, and 2,682 sotsu (lower-retainer/foot-soldier class) in 665 households. Clerical and outcaste groups follow: 448 Buddhist clergy (monks+nuns), 412 shrine attendants and 122 shrine households, plus 3,679 eta in 735 households, 77 hinin in 20 households, and 16 onbō (crematory/grave attendants) in 4 households. The page closes with 313 temples and 337 koku of shrine-and-temple land. Nearly every population total is followed by a male/female split that sums exactly to the total; the one exception is the Buddhist-clergy line, whose printed total (448) exceeds its own 345+95 breakdown by eight."
  },
  {
   "id": "komoro_lower_p016_right",
   "sequence": 261,
   "domain_canonical": "小諸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小諸藩",
   "domain_en": "Komoro",
   "image": "images/lower_p016_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 16,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（小諸）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration Survey, Fascicle 6 (Komoro)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Komoro domain kokudaka, land tax & tax-in-kind; Koga military tail",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf of Fascicle 6 opens (top right) with the military tail of the PREVIOUS domain, Koga (古河藩) — 12 platoons totalling 576 troops plus a 4-unit, 28-man artillery corps — printed to the right of the ○小諸藩 marker. The rest of the page is Komoro Domain (小諸藩, Shinano): a gross assessed yield (草高) of 28,772.689 koku, broken by the 内 sub-lines into 15,804.4211 koku established paddy (本田) and 12,968.268 koku new paddy (新田). Regular land tax in rice (正租米) is 9,665.695 koku and miscellaneous tax in rice (雜税米) 245.654 koku. Two tax-in-kind commodities close the page — buckwheat 5.1 koku and soybean 0.462 koku — each carrying a cash-conversion warichu (代金 17 ryo; 代永 2 kan 310 mon) and a 此米 rice-equivalent (2.125 and 0.289 koku); all conversions reconcile at 1.25 to of rice per ryo."
  },
  {
   "id": "komoro_lower_p016_left",
   "sequence": 262,
   "domain_canonical": "小諸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小諸",
   "domain_en": "Komoro",
   "image": "images/lower_p016_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 16,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（小諸）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Institutions at a Glance (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 6 (Komoro)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Komoro domain — population by status, households, koku yield, and cash tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left (continuation) page of the Komoro (小諸) domain entry in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran (1870). It records a total population of 31,910 (16,357 male; 15,553 female) in 6,743 households, with status counts for samurai (士族: 681 persons / 127 households), foot-soldiers (卒族: 926 / 152), shrine personnel (社人: 60 / 13), mountain ascetics (修驗: 37 households), and the outcaste groups eta (穢多: 122 households) and hinin (非人: 8 households). Fiscal figures give a total current yield (現石) of 10,016.23 koku, a derived rice figure (此米) of 102.467 koku, and a cash sum (金) of 550 ryō 2 bu plus eisen 269 kan 233 mon 4 rin, with an editorial note that the miscellaneous tax revenue is folded into the main kokudaka figure."
  },
  {
   "id": "komoro_lower_p017_right",
   "sequence": 263,
   "domain_canonical": "小諸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小諸藩",
   "domain_en": "Komoro",
   "image": "images/lower_p017_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 17,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（擧母）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (Hansei Ichiran), fascicle 6, Koromo section",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Komoro civil/religious/military tail; Koromo kokudaka opening",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf concludes the Komoro (小諸藩) entry in fascicle 6 and opens the Koromo (擧母藩) entry. Komoro's tail fields, printed to the right of the ○擧母藩 marker, record 64 villages, 136 shrines, 54 temples, 108 Buddhist clergy (僧), 143 Shugendō ascetics (修驗), and outcaste populations of 573 eta and 42 hinin, together with a two-platoon infantry of 120 men plus 42 officers and a 26-man artillery corps. Left of the marker, Koromo's block begins: a nominal assessment of 20,000 koku (高貳萬石), a detailed figure of 18,262.848 koku inclusive of new-field development (內新田込高共), and shrine-temple land of 58.14 koku. The running header names （擧母）; the printed page number is 十 (10)."
  },
  {
   "id": "koromo_lower_p017_left",
   "sequence": 264,
   "domain_canonical": "挙母藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "挙母",
   "domain_en": "Koromo",
   "image": "images/lower_p017_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 17,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（挙母）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Koromo)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Koromo domain kokudaka, genmai (net tax-rice) breakdown, and cash tax revenues (fascicle 6)",
   "page_summary_en": "This interior page of Fascicle 6 records the fiscal accounts of Koromo domain (挙母藩, a Naitō holding in Mikawa Province). The assessed kokudaka is 2,125.385 koku, with a further provisional ~4,300 koku of substitute land (代地) in Katsukita-gun, Mimasaka, still under transfer and to be surveyed later. The five-year-average genmai (net tax rice) is 5,231.1958 koku, itemized into 正租 5,051.8072, 口米 147.9556, 雑租 24.722, and 雑税 6.711 koku, which sum exactly to the total. Cash levies under the 諸産物及諸税數 heading total 502 ryō 3 bu 1 shu in gold (雑税 204, 諸運上 119, and 普請役夫金 179 ryō), plus a 永 (eisen) figure of 28.2 mon."
  },
  {
   "id": "koromo_lower_p018_right",
   "sequence": 265,
   "domain_canonical": "挙母藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "擧母藩",
   "domain_en": "Koromo",
   "image": "images/lower_p018_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 18,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（擧母）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 6 (Koromo)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Koromo domain — kokudaka, five-year-average tax, households",
   "page_summary_en": "This page is the complete Hansei Ichiran entry for Koromo domain (挙母藩), a 20,000-koku Mikawa-province holding of the Naitō house. Its nominal kokudaka is 20,000 koku, while the total assessed high including reclaimed land is 22,634.907 koku, of which 2,634.907 koku is new field (so old fields = 20,000). The five-year-average land tax is rendered as 16,127.307 bales of rice (four-to bales, including the miscellaneous taxes of both Mikawa and Mimasaka) plus two cash sums: 203 ryō 3 bu 2 shu in miscellaneous-tax money and 298 ryō 2 bu in various imposts and construction-corvée. The domain counts 4,778 total households, of which 23 are shrine-family households, 39 temples, 30 halls, 20 yamabushi households, and 36 households of town-detached watchmen and outcastes."
  },
  {
   "id": "koromo_lower_p219_right",
   "sequence": 266,
   "domain_canonical": "挙母藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "擧母藩",
   "domain_en": "Koromo",
   "image": "images/lower_p219_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 219,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（擧母、小泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Nine (Koromo, Koizumi)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop line, fascicle 9",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-nine (officials) half-leaf. The ○擧母藩 marker opens Koromo Domain, which prints five posts — 知事 1, 大參事 2, 權大參事 1, 少參事 3, and 權少參事 whose count is not printed — followed by ten officials named in two registers: Kawanishi Bunpachi, Kawanishi Rokuzō, Tanaka Jishō, Mori Osamu, Kimura Shizumaro, Yamada Yoichirō, Nakagawa Sashichirō, Matsushita Hyōsuke, Ebina Sanpei and Shibata Junpei. The 知事 column carries its count but no name. Koromo's military line, printed after its officials and standing to the right of the next domain's marker, records 兵隊 未詳 — troop numbers not reported. The ○小泉藩 marker then opens Koizumi Domain with 知事 1, 大參事 1 and 權大參事 2; no Koizumi officials are named on this leaf. The printed page number in the bottom margin is 414."
  },
  {
   "id": "koizumi_lower_p018_left",
   "sequence": 267,
   "domain_canonical": "小泉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小泉藩",
   "domain_en": "Koizumi",
   "image": "images/lower_p018_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 18,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（小泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō (Overview of Domain Administration), Fascicle 6 (Koizumi)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Koromo demographic tail & Koizumi kokudaka/tax head",
   "page_summary_en": "This page straddles two domains, divided by the single ○小泉藩 marker. To its right stands the demographic tail of Koromo Domain's (挙母藩) entry: total population 18,746 (9,489 male / 9,257 female), with parenthetical counts of clergy and outcastes; 100 samurai households (461 persons: 230 M / 231 F), 200 sotsu households (446 persons: 211 M / 235 F), and 79 villages. To its left, Koizumi Domain's (小泉藩) entry opens with an assessed yield (kokudaka) of 11,202.617 koku, net tax rice (現米) 5,330.2326 koku, a regular-rice component (正米) 189.7224 koku, and total tax rice (合米) 5,519.955 koku (= 現米 + 正米), followed by 2,109 total households, with a note that the governor's single household is subtracted. The running header and marker both name Koizumi (fascicle 6, printed page 13); a red-ink editorial note dates the survey to the twelfth month of Meiji 2 (1869)."
  },
  {
   "id": "koizumi_lower_p019_right",
   "sequence": 268,
   "domain_canonical": "小泉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小泉藩",
   "domain_en": "Koizumi",
   "image": "images/lower_p019_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 19,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（小泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 6 — Koizumi",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Koizumi domain population and household census by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This page is the population/household census of Koizumi domain (小泉藩, a small Katagiri fudai domain in Yamato) in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei ichiran. The total population is 9,223 persons (4,564 male, 4,659 female). The status breakdown gives shizoku 165 households / 680 persons, sotsu 91 households / 288 persons, and commoners (平民) 1,483 households / 6,841 persons, together with small religious and outcaste groups: 57 temples with 66 monks, 3 convents with 11 nuns, 1 shugen (mountain-ascetic) household of 1 person, 293 eta households / 1,273 persons, and 11 hinin households / 43 persons. A marginal note records that the governor (知事) and his four family members — 5 persons in all — are accounted for separately from the tabulated totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "komono_lower_p019_left",
   "sequence": 269,
   "domain_canonical": "菰野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "菰野藩",
   "domain_en": "Komono",
   "image": "images/lower_p019_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 19,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（菰野）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Komono)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Komono kokudaka/tax head + Koizumi demographic tail",
   "page_summary_en": "The left (marked) block opens the entry for Komono domain (○菰野藩, Ise; Fascicle 6): base assessed yield 11,000.94 koku plus 1,385.447 koku of newly-opened paddy, for a combined total (合高) of 12,386.391 koku. Its five-year-average regular land tax is recorded in rice — a main assessment (本高) of 12,468.171 bales and 847.105 bales from miscellaneous new fields — which, the two combined and converted to koku, equal 5,326.276 koku. The right block is the demographic tail of the preceding domain, Koizumi (小泉藩): 21 villages, 22 shrines, 2 shrine-attendant (社家) households with a population of 4 (male 3, miko 1), and 4 onbō (煙亡) households with a population of 20 (male 8, female 12). Both male/female splits reconcile to their totals; the kokudaka components fall 0.004 koku short of the printed combined total, a minor source inconsistency."
  },
  {
   "id": "komono_lower_p020_right",
   "sequence": 270,
   "domain_canonical": "菰野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "菰野",
   "domain_en": "Komono",
   "image": "images/lower_p020_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 20,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（菰野）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle 6 (Komono)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Miscellaneous taxes, tax totals, households and population by status (Komono han)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a continuation data page for Komono han (菰野藩), Ise province, in the sixth fascicle of the Hansei ichiran, identified only by the running header 藩制一覧表第六（菰野）; no maru domain-marker appears on the leaf, so the whole page belongs to Komono. It records the domain's miscellaneous taxes — 396.677 koku of rice (annotated as mountain-land and labor levies) and 118.810 kan-mon in cash (annotated as tea and bamboo taxes) — then the totals of 5,822.953 koku of tax rice (合米) and the same 118.810 kan-mon of total cash (合錢). Population and household figures follow: 1,981 total households and a total population of 10,064 (the male/female split left blank in the source, marked マゝ), itemized as 90 samurai (shizoku) households / 480 persons (236 male, 244 female), 17 foot-soldier (sotsu) households / 91 persons (51 male, 40 female), and 1,839 commoner (farmer-artisan-merchant) households. NOTE: the printed 總戸數 reads 千九百八拾壹戸 = 1,981, not 1,980 as recorded in MASTER (which dropped the 壹); the scan is unambiguous."
  },
  {
   "id": "komono_lower_p219_left",
   "sequence": 271,
   "domain_canonical": "菰野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "菰野藩",
   "domain_en": "Komono",
   "image": "images/lower_p219_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 219,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九　（菰野）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 9 (Komono) — outer-margin running header",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the verso of printed page 415 in fascicle 9 of the Hansei Ichiran, the fascicle that records domain officials and troop strength. Its two rightmost columns finish the return for Kōizumi domain — three junior councillors, and a force of two platoons totalling 101 men — after which the maru-marker ○菰野藩 opens the block for Komono domain (Ise province, the Hijikata house). Komono's own return gives one governor, two senior councillors, three acting senior councillors, four junior councillors, and acting junior councillors entered without a figure, followed by eleven named office-holders laid out in two registers of six and five columns. Komono's troops are two platoons of forty-eight men each, ninety-six in all, with eight officers additional."
  },
  {
   "id": "komatsu_lower_p020_left",
   "sequence": 272,
   "domain_canonical": "小松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小松藩",
   "domain_en": "Komatsu (Iyo-Komatsu)",
   "image": "images/lower_p020_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 20,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（小松）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Komatsu)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Komatsu domain kokudaka (with tail of Komono demographics)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 6 is filed under Komatsu (小松藩) and carries the complete kokudaka block for that domain: a base assessment of 10,000 koku plus three supplementary yields — 132.468 koku of new paddy (新田高), 1,416.643 koku of progressively surveyed new paddy (追々改出新田), and 1,761.876 koku of new and mountain dry fields combined (新畑山畑共) — summing to a total (合高) of 13,310.987 koku. The columns to the right of the ○小松藩 marker are the demographic tail of the preceding domain, Komono (菰野藩): a commoner population of 9,335 (4,595 male / 4,740 female), 6 shrine-priest households with a population of 35, 29 temples with 123 resident clergy, 125 shrines, and no eta/hinin. The printed page number is 17."
  },
  {
   "id": "komatsu_lower_p021_right",
   "sequence": 273,
   "domain_canonical": "小松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小松",
   "domain_en": "Komatsu (Iyo-Komatsu)",
   "image": "images/lower_p021_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 21,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（小松）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Komatsu) — running header (provenance)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Komatsu land tax, miscellaneous taxes, and household/facility counts (5-yr avg)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-6 civil/economic entry for Komatsu (Iyo-Komatsu) Domain. It records the 1864–1868 five-year-average official land tax (正租米) as 4,666.078 koku of net rice plus 277.740 kan-mon of cash, then a miscellaneous products-and-taxes block (諸産物及諸税): 83.444 koku of fixed-rate rice levied on upland/paddy/pond land — of which 81.444 koku was the amount actually delivered — together with 187.004 kan-mon of cash (including the tea-monopoly fee) and 610 ryō of gold (including the mulberry-paper monopoly fee). The domain reported 3,029 total households, and among its facilities 20 temples, 21 hermitages, one storehouse, and one town storehouse. Two figures correct the project dataset: the 5-yr-avg net rice is 4,666.078 koku (not the recorded 4,660.718), and a \"delivered amount\" row of 81.444 koku is present on the page but absent from the dataset."
  },
  {
   "id": "komatsu_lower_p021_left",
   "sequence": 274,
   "domain_canonical": "小松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小松藩",
   "domain_en": "Komatsu (Iyo-Komatsu)",
   "image": "images/lower_p021_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 21,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（天童）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Tendō) — running header / provenance",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Komatsu domain demographics; opening of Tendō domain kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf (Fascicle 6, printed page 19) carries the demographic tail of Komatsu domain (小松藩), then the opening of Tendō domain (天童藩), the two separated by the ○天童藩 maru-marker. Komatsu's register records a total population of 14,018 (male 7,325, female 6,693), itemized as 83 shizoku households / 423 persons, 40 sotsu households / 316 persons, and 100 eta (outcaste) households / 408 persons, alongside 19 villages, 16 shrines, 16 halls, 8 shrine-priest households, and one row-house (長屋) and one mint site (錢場所). The male and female totals each carry a warichu note subtracting clergy — shrine attendants, monks/nuns, and mountain ascetics — to give lay remainders of 7,261 and 6,668. Left of the marker, Tendō opens with a nominal kusadaka of 21,156.4976 koku and an assessed 18,000 koku; the running header names 天童 even though the bulk of the page's data is Komatsu's."
  },
  {
   "id": "komatsu_lower_p220_right",
   "sequence": 275,
   "domain_canonical": "小松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "天童藩",
   "domain_en": "Komatsu (Iyo-Komatsu)",
   "image": "images/lower_p220_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 220,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（小松、天童）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey, Fascicle 9 (Komatsu, Tendō)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle 9 officials rosters — Komatsu and Tendō",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page carries the fascicle-9 officials rosters of two small domains, Komatsu (Iyo) and Tendō (Dewa), under the running header 藩制一覽表第九（小松、天童）on printed page 416. Komatsu records one governor (知事), one senior councillor (大參事) Kitagawa Tetsutarō, two acting senior councillors (權大參事) of whom only Hitotsuyanagi Kennosuke is named — the modern editor's sic mark （マヽ）stands beside that count of two — and one junior councillor (少參事) Kuroda Sanosuke; its military line reads 兵隊　未詳, strength not recorded. Tendō records one governor, two senior councillors of whom only Tsuda Nagamasa is named (the note 外一人不詳, \"the other one person unknown\", follows), one acting senior councillor Matsubara Arata, two junior councillors Aikawa Rizaemon and Yoshida Tonan, and two acting junior councillors Yoshida Samon and Takazawa Hiroto under a 權少參事 heading that carries no printed count; its military line likewise reads 兵隊　未詳. Neither governor is named: both 知事 columns print only 一人, giving 5 posts for Komatsu and 8 for Tendō against 3 and 6 personal names respectively."
  },
  {
   "id": "tendo_lower_p022_right",
   "sequence": 276,
   "domain_canonical": "天童藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "天童（藩制一覧表第六（天童））",
   "domain_en": "Tendō",
   "image": "images/lower_p022_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 22,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（天童）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Domain-System Survey Table), Fascicle 6 (Tendō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Tendō domain — regular land tax, miscellaneous tax, households and status counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Tendō-han (天童藩) entry in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran, recording the domain's tax and household figures (a five-year average, 五ヶ年平均). The regular land tax (正租) is 5,863.72355 koku of rice plus 5,168 ryō 2 bu in cash; expressed wholly in rice (此米) it totals 7,592.58825 koku, of which 1,728.8647 koku was commuted to cash payment (金納) and 5,863.72355 koku paid in kind, with an additional assessed yield (込高) of 3,156.49749 koku. Miscellaneous tax (雜税) comes to 35.69853 koku of rice and 70 kan 536.54 mon in cash. The domain had 2,551 households in total, including 127 shizoku and 189 sotsu households. (Scan-based corrections to the master dataset: 此米 = 7,592.58825 not 7,592.4825; the commuted-rice figure = 1,728.8647 not 1,728.0647; and the miscellaneous-tax cash line 永七拾貫五百三拾六文五分四厘 is an additional field not previously captured.)"
  },
  {
   "id": "tendo_lower_p022_left",
   "sequence": 277,
   "domain_canonical": "天童藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "天童藩",
   "domain_en": "Tendō",
   "image": "images/lower_p022_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 22,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（天童）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Tendō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Population and household census (Tendō)",
   "page_summary_en": "The left leaf of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 6, continuing the demographic entry for Tendō domain (天童藩, a small ~20,000-koku holding in Dewa). It records a total population (人員) of 13,393 — 6,762 male and 6,631 female — broken down by status: 642 shizoku, 535 sotsu, 12,046 commoners, 47 shrine-attendants (社家), 54 Buddhist monks plus a further 53 Ikkō-sect clergy (僧 一向宗), and 16 eta (outcastes). Household and facility counts follow: 2,220 commoner households, 12 shrine-attendant and 3 eta households, 12 Shinto shrines, and 23 Buddhist temples. The status sub-counts and every male/female split reconcile exactly to the 13,393 total, and small warichu notes flag manservants/maidservants (下男/下女) inside the clergy figures."
  },
  {
   "id": "akita_lower_p023_right",
   "sequence": 278,
   "domain_canonical": "秋田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋田藩",
   "domain_en": "Akita",
   "image": "images/lower_p023_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 23,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（秋田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 6 (Akita)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akita domain: kokudaka, land and miscellaneous taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf opens the Akita-han (秋田藩) entry in Fascicle 6 of the Han Administration Overview. It records a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 332,038.779 koku, a regular tax (正税) of about 90,983 ryō rendered in money, and miscellaneous taxes (雜税) of 13,038 koku of rice plus two money accounts — 175,069.22 ryō of product taxes (諸産物税) and 12,868 ryō of other duties on mountains, rivers, fields, livestock, forest and sake-brewing — which sum to the 貳口合 total of 187,937.22 ryō (a five-year average). Demographically it reports 77,456 total households and 435,267 total inhabitants, of which the shizoku (samurai) class numbered 3,219 households and 15,514 persons (7,506 male, 8,008 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "akita_lower_p023_left",
   "sequence": 279,
   "domain_canonical": "秋田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋田藩",
   "domain_en": "Akita",
   "image": "images/lower_p023_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 23,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（秋田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, fascicle 6 (Akita)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akita status-group & institutional demographics (households and population)",
   "page_summary_en": "Left half of a demographic spread for Akita domain (秋田藩), fascicle 6 of the 藩制一覧表. Reading right to left, it tabulates households (戸數) and population (人口, each split 男/女) for a run of status and institutional categories: sotsu-class lower samurai 卒族 (1,977 households / 8,059 persons), samurai-household servants 士族下部 (1,131 / 12,535), Shinto shrine-priest families 社家 (278 / 844), Buddhist temple population 寺院 (881 households / 4,786 persons, flagged as an April count 但四月調), a mining population 鑛山 (1,386 / 12,030), and the eta outcaste class 穢多 (89 / 386); a final column records 529 temples (寺院 五百二十九ヶ寺). Every male+female split reconciles exactly to its stated total. No maru-marker (domain boundary) appears, so the entire page belongs to Akita — a continuation of the demographic block begun on the facing right page."
  },
  {
   "id": "akita_lower_p024_right",
   "sequence": 280,
   "domain_canonical": "秋田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋田藩",
   "domain_en": "Akita",
   "image": "images/lower_p024_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 24,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（秋田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Akita)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akita domain population & status breakdown (Meiji 3/1870 census)",
   "page_summary_en": "A single-domain continuation page for 秋田藩 (Akita) in fascicle 6 of the 藩制一覧表, giving the domain's 庚午 (Meiji 3 / 1870, 9th month) demographic census. It records a total 76,755 households (惣戸數) and 413,493 people (同人口), broken down \"of which\" (内) into shizoku 21,202, sotsu 6,929, shrine-office personnel 3,219, Buddhist clergy 1,911, and eta/ban/hinin outcaste classes 944, plus 7 kazoku nobles (男3/女4), 3,460 shrines (本社 3,055 + 末社 405), and 18 Shugendō households. These 庚午 totals are lower than the undated counts on the preceding page (435,267 people / 77,456 households on p23R), indicating population decline; every gender sub-count reconciles to its status total. A top-of-column restatement \"同人口 1,911\" (plain numerals, red-ink editorial insertion) duplicates the domain's clergy (僧) figure."
  },
  {
   "id": "akita_lower_p220_left",
   "sequence": 281,
   "domain_canonical": "秋田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋田藩",
   "domain_en": "Akita",
   "image": "images/lower_p220_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 220,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（秋田）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Nine (Akita)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Akita domain officials and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle-nine entry for Akita domain, marked by the single maru-marker ○秋田藩 in the rightmost column; no ink stands to its right, so the whole page belongs to Akita. The officials block records one governor (知事一人), senior councillors printed as 一人 but editorially corrected to （二）, five acting senior councillors (權大參事五人), and junior councillors printed as 二人 but corrected to （六人）; thirteen names then follow in a two-register column layout, which matches the corrected totals of 2 + 5 + 6 exactly. The military block records six battalions plus one company of shizoku infantry, with a company set at 58 men and eight companies at one battalion, three battalions plus one company raised from sotsu, and ten artillery units of eight guns and 103 men each, again drawn from shizoku. The running header prints 藩制一覽表第九（秋田） and the leaf carries the printed page number 四百十七 (417)."
  },
  {
   "id": "akashi_lower_p024_left",
   "sequence": 282,
   "domain_canonical": "明石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "明石藩",
   "domain_en": "Akashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p024_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 24,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（明石）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 — (Akashi)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akashi domain — civil register (population, households, kokudaka, land tax)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the opening page of the Akashi (明石藩) block in Fascicle 6 (civil register) of the Han-sei Ichiran, in the bound lower volume (Vol.2 下). It records an official kokudaka (表高/高) of 80,000 koku against an assessed gross (草高) of 90,304.109 koku — the 10,304.109-koku gap attributed to new-field (新田) development — plus 805.8+ koku of vermilion- and black-seal shrine-and-temple land. Fiscally it reports a five-year-average (1864–1868) land tax of 43,235.01754 koku of rice and 1,848 ryō of miscellaneous cash tax (231.11012 koku rice-equivalent), for a combined 現米 total of 43,466.12766 koku. Demographically the domain had 16,896 households and 76,004 people (38,890 male / 37,114 female), of whom the samurai class held 481 households and 1,805 persons. The lone column to the right of the ○明石藩 marker — a 66-person ditto-population count surveyed 1870/10 — is the tail of the preceding Kubota (Akita) domain."
  },
  {
   "id": "akashi_lower_p025_right",
   "sequence": 283,
   "domain_canonical": "明石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "明石藩",
   "domain_en": "Akashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p025_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 25,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（秋月）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 6 (Akizuki section)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akashi clergy/sotsu demographic tail; Akizuki kokudaka opening",
   "page_summary_en": "A two-domain boundary page in Fascicle 6 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. The right two-thirds carry the tail of Akashi domain's (明石藩) demographic register — its lower-samurai (sotsu) and religious-community counts: 905 sotsu households (population 3,226 = 1,654 male / 1,572 female), 442 Shinto shrines, 292 Buddhist halls (堂), 2 hermitages (庵), 175 temples, and household/population figures for shrine-priest (社家: 33 hh, 134 persons), miko (神子: 6 hh, 12 persons), temple clergy (寺院人口: 377 persons), and Shugendō ascetic (修驗: 17 hh, 76 persons) communities. At the ○秋月藩 marker the page turns to Akizuki domain (秋月藩), whose kokudaka opens here: base assessment (草高) 50,000 koku plus new-field land (新田高) 1,783.62539 koku, giving a total (合高) of 51,783.62539 koku. An isolated maru-marker at the far left introduces Akizuki's 現石 (actual-assessed-koku) tax section, whose text continues on the facing page. The running header names Akizuki, though most of the page's data belongs to Akashi."
  },
  {
   "id": "akashi_lower_p221_right",
   "sequence": 284,
   "domain_canonical": "明石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "明石藩",
   "domain_en": "Akashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p221_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 221,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（明石、秋月）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Akashi, Akizuki)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of Fascicle 9 gives Akashi Domain's officer corps and its troop strength. The domain reports one governor (chiji), two senior councillors, two acting senior councillors and four junior councillors, of whom five are named: Oda Tamotsu and Mamiya Sankyū as senior councillors, Hashimoto Naka and Saitō Morie as acting senior councillors, and Kawamura Kurazō as a junior councillor. The military entry records eight small companies totalling 400 men drilled on the British pattern, a further 532 men for whom rifle companies were being raised at the time of the survey, and an artillery section with its attached personnel of 304 men. Two items on the page belong to neighbouring domains: two artillery companies raised from the sotsu class, printed to the right of the Akashi marker, carry over from Akita Domain on the preceding leaf, and Akizuki Domain's entry opens at the left edge with its governor's post (no figure printed) and one senior councillor, Toki Masunobu."
  },
  {
   "id": "akizuki_lower_p025_left",
   "sequence": 285,
   "domain_canonical": "秋月藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋月藩",
   "domain_en": "Akizuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p025_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 25,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（秋月）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Akizuki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akizuki domain finances: land tax, miscellaneous tax, current koku, and products",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-6 economic survey of Akizuki (秋月藩), a Chikuzen sub-domain of Fukuoka. As a five-year average it records the regular land tax (正租) — 17,490.129 koku of rice plus 2,050.904 koku of soybeans — and the miscellaneous tax (雜税) — 1,246.266 koku of rice, 153.068 koku of soybeans, and roughly 32.27 kanme of silver, the silver re-expressed as 67.229 koku or 203.239 bales at the stated market rate of eight ryō per koku. The domain's current assessed yield (現石) is given as 20,803.741 koku, and its listed products (産物) are 1,759 kin of raw wax (cast in balls of 80 kin each) and 800 boxes of kudzu (8 shō per box). An editorial note dated 1870/12/18 flags that the domain's submitted report and the compiled main text do not agree."
  },
  {
   "id": "akizuki_lower_p026_right",
   "sequence": 286,
   "domain_canonical": "秋月藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋月",
   "domain_en": "Akizuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p026_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 26,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（秋月）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, fascicle 6 (Akizuki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akizuki products and population / household status breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "A single-domain page for 秋月藩 (Akizuki, a ~50,000-koku sub-domain of Fukuoka in Chikuzen), from fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran. It opens with two products — laver (壽海苔) 6,000 sheets and coal (焚石) 2,000,000 kin — then gives the grand totals of 6,014 households (戸數) and 33,084 persons (人員), followed by an \"of which\" (内) status breakdown. The itemised statuses are shizoku 205 houses / 1,212 persons, sotsu 701 / 3,232, Shinto priests 16 / 91, temples 35 / 188 clergy, townsfolk 448 / 2,318, and Yasu-district peasants 2,317 houses / 13,394 persons across 40 villages (two of them shared-tenure villages under Fukuoka domain). Each population figure carries a male/female split; the itemised households and persons sum to about 62% of the recorded totals, so the register enumerates a coherent subset rather than the full population."
  },
  {
   "id": "akizuki_lower_p026_left",
   "sequence": 287,
   "domain_canonical": "秋月藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋月藩",
   "domain_en": "Akizuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p026_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 26,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（朝日山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, fascicle 6 (Asahiyama)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akizuki domain demographics — district households/population, outcaste and religious counts, villages and shrines",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the demographic block of Akizuki domain (秋月藩) in Hansei Ichiran fascicle 6, covering two of its districts. Geza district (下座郡) held 679 households and 3,916 people (2,036 male, 1,880 female) across 17 villages; Kama district (嘉麻郡) held 1,613 households and 8,733 people (4,515 male, 4,218 female) across 25 villages. Recorded separately are 170 eta (outcaste) households with 965 persons (526 male, 439 female) and 33 hinin (18 male, 15 female, in 18 households counted within the peasant household total), while shugenja are folded into the temple counts; domain-wide totals given here are 82 villages (3 shared with Fukuoka domain) and 75 shrines. The ○朝日山藩 marker in the far-left margin opens the following Asahiyama-han section, and the printed page number is 29."
  },
  {
   "id": "akizuki_lower_p221_left",
   "sequence": 288,
   "domain_canonical": "秋月藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "秋月藩",
   "domain_en": "Akizuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p221_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 221,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（朝日山）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Nine (Asahiyama)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillor roster and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 (officials) leaf of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, printed book page 419. Most of the page completes the councillor roster of Akizuki Domain: three acting senior councillors (權大參事 三員 — Tozawa Seiei, Yoshida Teihachi, Etō Ryōichi), the junior councillors (少參事), whose printed figure 五員 is corrected in a parenthesis to 九員 and is confirmed by the nine names that follow, one acting junior councillor (權少參事 Yamada Masanaga), and a troop strength of 兵隊 六百五十六員 — 656 men. To the left of the maru-marker ○朝日山藩 the entry for Asahiyama Domain begins, with 知事 (no name printed), 大參事 (Iwasaki Katsutomo and Chiga Hisashi) and 權大參事 (Tomomatsu Nobuyoshi); the rest of the Asahiyama block runs on to the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "asahiyama_lower_p027_right",
   "sequence": 289,
   "domain_canonical": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_en": "Asahiyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p027_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 27,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（朝日山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 6 (Asahiyama)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Domain land assessment and land tax (kokudaka, komidaka, tax rice, cash, misc. tax)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-6 fiscal entry for Asahiyama Domain (朝日山藩) in the 1870 Hansei Ichiran land-administration survey. The domain's nominal assessed yield (kusadaka) is 50,000 koku, held across 29 towns and 21 villages in Murayama District of Uzen Province and 19 villages in Sakata and Asai Districts of Ōmi Province; adding a supplementary komidaka of 580.88 koku gives a total assessed yield (gōdaka) of 50,580.88 koku, of which 5,331.66 koku is mujidaka (assessment carrying no cultivated land). On the tax side the page records land-tax rice (konomono narumai) of 13,120.38 koku, miscellaneous tax rice (zassei) of 3,047.53 koku, and cash levies in eiraku and gold; the five-year-average regular land tax (seiso, in current koku) is 16,172.32 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "asahiyama_lower_p027_left",
   "sequence": 290,
   "domain_canonical": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_en": "Asahiyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p027_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 27,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（朝日山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (Hansei Ichiran), fascicle 6, Asahiyama section",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Asahiyama domain — tax subtotals, population and household counts (fascicle 6 civil tail)",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of printed page 31 completes the fascicle-6 civil return for 朝日山藩 (Asahiyama, a small Echigo domain). It closes the fiscal section — miscellaneous tax of 50 ryo 2 bu 1 shu in gold; a large eisen figure of 479 kan 230 mon 3 bu 2 rin 7 mo; a combined \"gold-and-eisen\" subtotal (529 ryo 3 bu / 42.8 mon) with its rice equivalent (282 bales); and a two-portion rice total (二口合) of 43,488 bales — then gives the demographics: 6,797 households and 35,874 people (17,940 male, 17,934 female). Of these it itemizes the warrior class (士族, 272 households / 1,398 persons) and foot-soldiers (卒, 401 households / 1,794 persons), each with an internally consistent male/female split. No maru-marker appears, so the entire page is 朝日山 data."
  },
  {
   "id": "asahiyama_lower_p028_right",
   "sequence": 291,
   "domain_canonical": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_en": "Asahiyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p028_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 28,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（朝日山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Table of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 6 (Asahiyama)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Households & population by social class; shrines and temples (Asahiyama)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the household-and-population return for Asahiyama Domain (朝日山藩) in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran; the running header names 朝日山, and MASTER confirms the whole page is this single domain. A subtotal at the top (合) records 673 households and 3,192 persons (1,511 male, 1,681 female) — most plausibly the warrior/administrative classes (士族・卒) whose class-by-class breakdown ran on the preceding page. The commoner (平民) entry gives 5,347 households and 28,401 persons (14,182 male, 14,219 female), spread across Murayama district in Uzen and the Sakata and Asai districts in Ōmi, plus one outcast (非人) household of a single person counted separately. The shrine-and-temple (社寺) section, sited within Murayama district of Uzen, lists 7 Shinto shrines and 137 Buddhist temples totalling 748 households and 4,775 persons, itemised as 175 shrine, 569 temple, and 4 Nishinomiya grand-kagura-master households."
  },
  {
   "id": "asahiyama_lower_p029_right",
   "sequence": 292,
   "domain_canonical": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "朝日山藩",
   "domain_en": "Asahiyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p029_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 29,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六 （尼崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 6 — filed under the Amagasaki (尼崎) section, though most of the page completes the preceding Asahiyama (朝日山藩) entry: shrine/temple lands and clergy, village and town counts.",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Asahiyama shrine/temple lands & clergy, village/town counts; opening of the Amagasaki entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of fascicle 6 mostly completes the entry for Asahiyama (朝日山藩): it records the domain's religious establishment — 11 shrines, 3,051 koku of shrine land (社領) and 3,559 koku of temple land (寺領) — together with the attached clergy (2 Shinto priests and 41 Buddhist monks, plus their women and servants), and geographic counts of 40 villages and 29 towns. A double-column note explains that the 40 villages are scattered across Murayama district in Uzen (Dewa) and the Sakata and Asai districts of Ōmi, and a closing line states that Asahiyama's household and population totals were given on the preceding page. At the lower left the ○尼崎藩 marker opens the Amagasaki entry, giving its assessed yield of 40,000 koku (草高) and a territory of 84 villages across five districts of Settsu. The running margin header files the page under the Amagasaki (尼崎) section."
  },
  {
   "id": "amagasaki_lower_p029_left",
   "sequence": 293,
   "domain_canonical": "尼崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "尼崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Amagasaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p029_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 29,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（尼崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, fascicle 6 (Amagasaki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Amagasaki kokudaka breakdown, land & miscellaneous taxes, households and population (fasc. 6)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the Amagasaki (尼崎藩) civil/economic register in fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran; the ○尼崎藩 boundary marker and the 草高 total stand on the facing right page (lower_p029_right), so every column here belongs to Amagasaki. The domain's assessed land is split between Settsu-province holdings (5 districts, 84 villages = 38,301.47939 koku) and Harima-province holdings (3 districts, 50 villages = 13,180.593 koku), which together with 1.0 koku of newly-reclaimed field yield the combined total of 51,483.07239 koku. The five-year-average tax take is a regular land tax of 25,722.98685 koku of rice plus 1,104.36862 kan-mon in cash, and miscellaneous taxes of 1,871.12069 koku of rice plus 162.447212 kan-mon in cash. The page closes with 10,613 households and a population of 49,403, followed by an 内 (\"of which\") marker that opens the status breakdown continuing on the next spread."
  },
  {
   "id": "amagasaki_lower_p030_right",
   "sequence": 294,
   "domain_canonical": "尼崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "尼崎",
   "domain_en": "Amagasaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p030_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 30,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（尼崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle 6 (Amagasaki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Amagasaki domain population by legal status (households and persons)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-6 demographic table for Amagasaki domain (尼崎藩), recording households (戸數) and persons (人員) by legal status. The noble house (華族) numbers 4 (1 male, 3 female); the samurai class (士族) 360 households / 1,742 persons, and the lower-samurai (卒) 287 households / 1,376 persons. Commoners (平民) dominate at 9,767 households and 45,759 persons, alongside 24 Shinto-priest (社家) households (89 persons), 175 Buddhist-temple (寺院) households (437 persons), and the Edo-period outcaste groups eta (穢多, 602 households / 2,715 persons) and hinin (非人, 71 households). Every population total is split into male (男) and female (女) counts that sum exactly to the printed total."
  },
  {
   "id": "amagasaki_lower_p222_left",
   "sequence": 295,
   "domain_canonical": "尼崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "尼崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Amagasaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p222_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 222,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（尼崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabular Survey of Domain Institutions (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 9 — Amagasaki",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "fascicle 9 officials roster and military establishment — close of Asahiyama, opening of Amagasaki",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the fascicle-9 entry for Asahiyama domain and opens that for Amagasaki. Asahiyama's last four named officials (Sekiguchi Kinshi, Sugihara Zen'emon, Utsugi Setsutei, Okura Gen'emon) are followed by its military establishment: one battalion of six companies at forty-four men each, that is 264 men, together with half a gun-battery of four pieces. The ○尼崎藩 marker then opens Amagasaki, whose office headings 知事, 大參事 and 權大參事 stand in the upper heading band and 少參事 and 權少參事 in the lower; eleven officials are named on this page and the roll continues onto the facing leaf. Amagasaki's own force is entered as half a battalion of four companies with no headcount given, and the domain also reports four junior councillors and one acting junior councillor — a count that does not reconcile with the eight acting-junior-councillor names actually printed here and on page 422."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashimori_lower_p030_left",
   "sequence": 296,
   "domain_canonical": "足守藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足守藩",
   "domain_en": "Ashimori",
   "image": "images/lower_p030_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 30,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（足守）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey (Hansei Ichiran), Table/Fascicle 6 (Ashimori)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Ashimori kokudaka block; tail of Amagasaki villages/shrines/personnel",
   "page_summary_en": "This page from Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran opens the entry for Ashimori Domain (足守藩) in Bitchū province, signalled by the circle-marker ○足守藩. Ashimori's nominal assessment is 25,000 koku; adding 5,898.689 koku of reassessed new fields (改高新田) gives a stated total (合) of 30,898.689 koku (25,000 + 5,898.689 = 30,898.689). Of that holding, 13,855.1035 koku is recorded as 29 villages in Kayō district, Bitchū, with a further 5,894.33 koku of reclaimed new field (改出新田) in the same district. The columns to the right of the marker complete the preceding Amagasaki Domain (尼崎藩) entry: 134 villages, 324 shrines plus 237 branch shrines, and 207 personnel (114 male, 93 female; 114 + 93 = 207)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashimori_lower_p031_right",
   "sequence": 297,
   "domain_canonical": "足守藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足守",
   "domain_en": "Ashimori",
   "image": "images/lower_p031_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 31,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（足守）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Table No. 6 (Ashimori)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-6 land tax and kokudaka return — Ashimori domain, including its Iwashiro/Shinobu exclave",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the fascicle-6 (land-tax / kokudaka) return for Ashimori domain (足守藩). The right-hand block gives a grand-total kokudaka of 19,749.4335 koku (○合), a five-year-average land tax (正租) of 8,182.1998 koku in genmai, miscellaneous tax (雜税) of 1.69775 koku, gold (金) 173 ryō, and Eiraku cash (永) 84 mon. The left-hand block itemizes the domain's exclave in Shinobu district of Iwashiro province: 11 villages assessed at 11,144.8965 koku (高) plus 4.359 koku of newly-opened paddy (外高), subtotalling 11,149.2555 koku (○合), with its own five-year-average land tax of 1,880.1284 koku. The internal check reconciles exactly (11,144.8965 + 4.359 = 11,149.2555). Both ○ symbols mark subtotals, not domain boundaries; no maru+藩 domain marker appears, so the whole page belongs to Ashimori."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashimori_lower_p031_left",
   "sequence": 298,
   "domain_canonical": "足守藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足守藩",
   "domain_en": "Ashimori",
   "image": "images/lower_p031_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 31,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（足守）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabular Survey of Domain Institutions, fascicle 6 — (Ashimori)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Two-province combined kokudaka and five-year-average tax totals",
   "page_summary_en": "The closing summary of Ashimori domain's fascicle-6 fiscal entry, drawing together its home lands in Bitchu with the eleven villages in Shinobu district, Iwashiro province, that appear on the facing leaf. The first two columns finish the Iwashiro block — land tax 461.2855 kanmon in cash, miscellaneous tax 67.4746 kanmon — after which a bulleted line gives the two provinces' combined assessed yield as 47,937.9155 koku. Under the heading \"both provinces combined, five-year average\" the survey then restates the whole tax take: land tax 10,062.3282 koku of rice plus 461.2855 kanmon, miscellaneous tax 1.69775 koku plus 173 ryo, 84 mon and 67.4749 kanmon. The grand total in rice, 10,064.02595 koku, is printed at the left; the matching cash grand total is labelled here but its figure runs over onto the next leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashimori_lower_p032_right",
   "sequence": 299,
   "domain_canonical": "足守藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足守藩",
   "domain_en": "Ashimori",
   "image": "images/lower_p032_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 32,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（足守）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (Hansei Ichiran), fascicle 6, Ashimori (足守) section — running margin header (provenance)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Products, miscellaneous-goods taxes, grand total, and household count (産物・雑品税・戸数)",
   "page_summary_en": "The tail of Ashimori domain's (足守藩, a ~25,000-koku Bitchū domain of the Kinoshita house) fascicle-6 civil entry. It lists the domain's products — raw cotton, cotton cloth, lamp oil, cast-metal pots/kettles, and charcoal/firewood for the home territory, plus oil-pressing, fishing, and water-wheels for a detached holding at Iwashiro-Senoue (岩代瀬上) — and the miscellaneous-goods taxes on them: 1.69775 koku of rice and 173 ryō / 84 mon in cash for the home territory, and 67 kan 474 mon 6 bu of Eiraku cash for the exclave (noted as already included in the total). The grand total (惣計) tax is 701 ryō 3 bu 1 shu plus 31 mon 6 bu, and the household count is 4,324. No maru-marker appears on the page: the entire sheet belongs to Ashimori, and the running header reads 藩制一覽表第六（足守）."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashimori_lower_p032_left",
   "sequence": 300,
   "domain_canonical": "足守藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足守",
   "domain_en": "Ashimori",
   "image": "images/lower_p032_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 32,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（足守）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, fascicle 6 (Ashimori)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Population & household register (足守藩)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page from fascicle 6 (人員/demographics) of the Hansei Ichiran records the household-and-population return of 足守藩 (Ashimori, a ~25,000-koku domain of the Kinoshita house in Bicchū). Total registered population (人員) = 17,453. Of this, the samurai orders are 士族 (153 households / 633 persons: M 301, F 332) and 卒 (151 households / 347 persons: M 215, F 132), giving a samurai subtotal of 304 households / 980 persons (M 516, F 464 — fully internally consistent). The commoner (平民) population is reported for two districts: the home district 備中國賀陽郡 (3,111 households / 12,139 persons: M 6,327, F 5,812) and a detached holding — a post-Boshin administrative assignment — in 岩代國信夫郡 (823 houses / 4,254 persons printed), combined into a commoner-household total of 3,934 (= 3,111 + 823). The 岩代 enclave block is internally inconsistent: its printed male 2,188 + female 2,606 = 4,794, its own printed district total reads 4,254, and the grand-total arithmetic (17,453 − 980 − 12,139) implies 4,334 — three irreconcilable figures, a source-level error flagged here."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashimori_lower_p033_right",
   "sequence": 301,
   "domain_canonical": "足守藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足守",
   "domain_en": "Ashimori",
   "image": "images/lower_p033_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 33,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（足守）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-System Overview, Fascicle 6 (Ashimori)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Ashimori religious institutions, households, population, outcastes, and governor's family",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation page of the Ashimori (足守藩) entry in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei ichiran, covering religious institutions and demographic totals for the domain's holdings across two provinces (printed in abbreviation as 備 and 岩). It records a populace (人口) of 16,393 (8,515 male / 7,878 female), 30 shrines, and 85 temples (11 of them unoccupied), with clergy comprising 73 monks, 16 shugendō practitioners (10 male / 6 female), 2 nuns, and 61 shrine attendants across 21 households (33 male / 28 female); a marginal note flags that one temple is Jōdo Shinshū. The two-province combined section (兩國合) gives 4,324 households and a total personnel count (人員) of 17,453, plus 290 outcastes (穢多; 154 male / 136 female) with a note of 2 more besides, and a governor's family of 4 (2 male / 2 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashimori_lower_p223_right",
   "sequence": 302,
   "domain_canonical": "足守藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足守藩",
   "domain_en": "Ashimori",
   "image": "images/lower_p223_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 223,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（足守）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 9 — (Ashimori)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-9 officials roster and troop strength for Ashimori domain",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 9 (officials and troops) of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran, printed book page 422. The leaf opens Ashimori domain's entry with the maru-marker ○足守藩 and records four posts: a governor (知事) printed with neither a headcount nor an incumbent's name, two senior councillors (大參事 二員), four acting senior councillors (權大參事 四員), and two junior councillors (少參事 二員). Eight officials are then named, and that number matches the 2+4+2 establishment exactly. Ashimori's military line closes the block as 三小隊　但一隊五十五人, three platoons of fifty-five men each, or 165 troops, with no artillery recorded. To the right of the marker the leaf still carries the tail of the preceding entry, Amagasaki domain: its artillery line 大砲 二門 (two cannon) and six further officials' names, running from 遠藤二右衞門 to 百瀨貞右衞門."
  },
  {
   "id": "ako_lower_p033_left",
   "sequence": 303,
   "domain_canonical": "赤穂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "赤穗藩",
   "domain_en": "Akō",
   "image": "images/lower_p033_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 33,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（赤穗）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Akō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Land tax and rice revenue (fiscal)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fiscal (land-tax and revenue) block for Akō Domain (赤穂藩), a 20,000-koku domain in Harima province, from Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran-hyō. Against a nominal assessment (草高) of 20,000 koku, the five-year-average regular land tax (正租) is 8,404.9306 koku of rice, with a further 914.53306 koku of supplementary income (外ニ) drawn from inspection-assessed fields, floodplain fields, and salt-flats covering 341 chō 3 tan 9 se 3 bu. Additional rice levies are the kuchimai surtax (口米, 197.3704 koku, same average), corvée-labor rice (夫米, 497.5452 koku), and a small fishing-net levy (網役米, 0.596 koku). All revenue figures are stated as five-year averages in rice equivalent (現米)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ako_lower_p034_right",
   "sequence": 304,
   "domain_canonical": "赤穂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "赤穗",
   "domain_en": "Akō",
   "image": "images/lower_p034_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 34,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（赤穗）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Akō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akō domain — fascicle 6 miscellaneous rice & cash revenues (salt levies, product taxes, grand totals)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Fascicle 6 (economic) entry for Akō domain (赤穂藩), listing its miscellaneous rice and cash revenues. Rice levies comprise a grass-land levy (草米, 16.366 koku), boatmen's rice (水主米, 154.8 koku), and an upland levy (山手番, 23.055 koku); the salt-flat levy (鹽濱運上) yielded 813 ryō 2 bu plus 110 mon, with a marginal note that this levy was abolished and replaced by a new 3,000-ryō salt tax (鹽稅金). A combined cash levy on four commercial items — rice brokerage (米仲買), sardine nets (鰯網), sake brewing (酒造), and a pine-branch license (松枝冥加) — totaled 14 ryō 3 bu 3 shu plus 205 mon, and the domain held 11 forest sites (山林) and 4 groves (籔). The grand totals are 10,209.19626 koku of rice (惣合米) and 828 ryō 1 bu 3 shu plus 315 mon in cash (惣合金); the salt-flat levy plus the four-item levy reconcile exactly to the cash grand total."
  },
  {
   "id": "ako_lower_p034_left",
   "sequence": 305,
   "domain_canonical": "赤穂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "赤穂藩",
   "domain_en": "Akō",
   "image": "images/lower_p034_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 34,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（赤穂）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 6 (Akō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Akō domain: cultivated area, households/population by status, temple & shrine land, salt product",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a continuation page of the Akō (赤穂) domain entry in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran survey (printed page 45); it carries no domain marker, and the running header 藩制一覧表第六（赤穂） confirms the whole leaf belongs to Akō. It records the domain's total cultivated area (反別 ≈ 11.77 chō), a household-and-population block broken down by status — shizoku 580 persons / 132 households, sotsu 433 / 129, lower sotsu (下卒) 649 / 214, with printed totals of 1,657 persons and 475 households — and tax-exempt land grants: temple land (寺領) 81.846 koku and shrine land (社領) 59.4246 koku, each with its own cultivated-area sub-note, totalling (惣計) 211.5768 koku. The domain's notable product (産物) is salt (鹽), for which Akō was historically renowned. The household sub-counts reconcile exactly to 475, but the status populations sum to 1,662 against the stated total of 1,657 — a five-person discrepancy internal to the source."
  },
  {
   "id": "ako_lower_p035_right",
   "sequence": 306,
   "domain_canonical": "赤穂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "赤穂藩",
   "domain_en": "Akō",
   "image": "images/lower_p035_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 35,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（赤穂）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Akō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Commoner & religious demographics, households, livestock (Akō)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page completes the fascicle-6 civil-demographic register for Akō (赤穂藩), read right to left. It tallies commoners (平民: 7,266 households, 32,211 persons), outcastes (穢多: 104 households, 486 persons), livestock (1,492 cattle, 28 horses), 45 Shinto shrines, shrine-priest families (社家: 8 households, 35 persons), Shugendō practitioners (修驗: 2 households, 11 persons), 48 Buddhist temples with 324 clergy, and the governor's own household (知事初家族: 13 persons). The closing grand totals record 7,896 households (the 48 temples included) and 33,067 persons; the latter excludes the governor's household per the note 但知事ハ除ク. Every male/female split and the population grand total reconcile exactly (32,211+486+35+11+324 = 33,067)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ako_lower_p223_left",
   "sequence": 307,
   "domain_canonical": "赤穂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "赤穗藩",
   "domain_en": "Akō",
   "image": "images/lower_p223_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 223,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（赤穗、綾部）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Akō, Ayabe)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fascicle-9 officials register for Akō Domain and the opening of the register for Ayabe Domain. Akō lists a governor's post with no incumbent named, then four councillor grades with printed counts — two senior councillors (大參事), three acting senior councillors (權大參事), three junior councillors (少參事) and four acting junior councillors (權少參事) — and exactly twelve names stand under them, so the counts and the roster agree. The third acting senior councillor, Kanki Jūzō, carries a small-type rider 公議人 marking him as the domain's delegate to the Kōgisho. Akō's military line, printed to the right of the Ayabe marker and therefore still Akō's, gives three companies at fifty men each, or 150 troops. The Ayabe block opens with a governor's post and a senior councillor's post, both without printed counts, and one name, Kuki Hannojō; the rest of the Ayabe roster runs onto the following leaves."
  },
  {
   "id": "ayabe_lower_p035_left",
   "sequence": 308,
   "domain_canonical": "綾部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "綾部藩",
   "domain_en": "Ayabe",
   "image": "images/lower_p035_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 35,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（綾部）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran Table, Fascicle 6 (Ayabe)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Ayabe domain — kokudaka and land-tax survey",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the complete kokudaka-and-tax entry for Ayabe domain (綾部藩, Tanba province, Kuki house). The nominal assessed base (草高) is 19,500 koku; two supplements — Shimada-allotment rice (島田分米込高, 1,506.742 koku) and new-field additional yield (新田改出高, 55.43896 koku) — bring the grand total (合) to 21,062.18096 koku, of which 1,724.462 koku is untaxed-land koku (無地高). Petty imposts (小物成高) amount to 298.99 koku, equal to about 2 kan 989.9 monme in silver (10 monme/koku). The five-year-average tax figures are regular land tax 4,530.7782 koku (genmai), silver-paid regular tax 1,075.304 koku, soybeans 512.7 koku, and miscellaneous taxes 1,412.4468 koku, with a note that silver payments were consolidated at a rate of 8 ryō per koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "ayabe_lower_p036_right",
   "sequence": 309,
   "domain_canonical": "綾部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "綾部藩",
   "domain_en": "Ayabe",
   "image": "images/lower_p036_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 36,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（綾部）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Ayabe)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Ayabe domain — tax rice, silver, products, shrines/temples, households and population (fascicle 6)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fascicle-6 fiscal, product and demographic record for Ayabe (綾部) domain, a small Tanba han. Its total net tax rice (合現米) is 7,160.959 koku and its silver revenue 2,989.9 monme; the three listed products — tea, silk thread and cotton — are entered only as qualitative notes recording that output is limited and that no fixed quota can readily be set. The domain contains 4,284 households and 18,373 people, of whom the shizoku number 762 (367 male, 395 female) living in 153 households. Religious establishments comprise 72 shrines and 39 temples (one of them Ikkō-shū), endowed with 36 koku of shrine-and-temple land."
  },
  {
   "id": "ayabe_lower_p036_left",
   "sequence": 310,
   "domain_canonical": "綾部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "綾部藩",
   "domain_en": "Ayabe",
   "image": "images/lower_p036_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 36,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（綾部）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Han Administration at a Glance, Fascicle 6 (Ayabe)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sotsu and commoner (heimin) population, households and religious institutions by district — Ayabe domain",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation page of the Ayabe (綾部) demographic section, fascicle 6; it carries NO maru-marker, so all fifteen data columns belong to Ayabe. It opens with the sotsu (卒) status class: 323 persons (156 male, 167 female) in 67 households. The commoner (平民) block is then broken out by the two Tanba districts of the domain. Ikaruga-gun (何鹿郡, 9 villages): 8,914 commoners (4,404 male / 4,510 female) in 2,156 households, with 47 shrines (15 attendants: 7 m / 8 f), 24 temples (of which 1 Ikkō-shū), 56 monks and 9 nuns. Amata-gun (天田郡, 18 villages, marked 同上 \"ditto\"): 7,311 commoners (3,649 male / 3,662 female) in 1,674 households, with 24 shrines (16 attendants: 7 m / 9 f). Every male+female split reconciles exactly to its stated total."
  },
  {
   "id": "ayabe_lower_p037_right",
   "sequence": 311,
   "domain_canonical": "綾部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "綾部藩",
   "domain_en": "Ayabe",
   "image": "images/lower_p037_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 37,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（安中）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 6 — (Annaka)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Ayabe demographics tail and Annaka kokudaka opening (fascicle 6)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes Ayabe's fascicle-6 population block and opens Annaka's entry. Reading right to left, it finishes Ayabe's Amata-district holdings (10 temples, 23 monks, 6 nuns), then records the detached Funai-district holding: 4 villages with 469 people (235 male, 234 female), 101 houses, 1 shrine with 5 shrine personnel (2 male, 3 female), and 5 temples with 8 monks. Domain-wide outcaste entries follow — 450 eta (204 male, 246 female; 102 households) and 144 hinin (79 male, 65 female; 31 households) — plus the governor's family of 10 (4 males, one of them the governor himself, and 6 females). After the ○安中藩 marker, Annaka's block begins with a kusadaka of 30,000 koku (17,000 koku castle-attached, 13,000 koku in Shimōsa) and a supplementary output assessment (komidaka, new fields, and re-survey increases) of 3,125.7415 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "annaka_lower_p037_left",
   "sequence": 312,
   "domain_canonical": "安中藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "安中藩",
   "domain_en": "Annaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p037_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 37,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（安中）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table No. 6 (Annaka)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Annaka Domain taxes, products, and exempt land (Table 6 continuation)",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of Annaka Domain's entry in Table 6 of the Hansei Ichiran (1870 domain survey). The page completes the land-register figures — 970 chō 4 tan 8 bu of assessed acreage for the supplementary parcel and a combined total (合高) of 33,125.7415 koku — then reports the five-year-average regular tax: 7,311.683 koku in actual rice plus 2,611 kan 360 mon in cash, each followed by a red-ink deduction line (3,948.161 koku and 383 kan 7 mon of assorted deductions). Miscellaneous taxes add 328 kan 450 mon in ei cash and 284 kan 674 mon in copper coin. The products section lists raw silk and silkworm-egg cards (untaxed, per the printed note), and tax-exempt lands are located within Usui and Gunma districts of Kōzuke Province."
  },
  {
   "id": "annaka_lower_p038_right",
   "sequence": 313,
   "domain_canonical": "安中藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "安中藩",
   "domain_en": "Annaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p038_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 38,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（安中）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey Table No. 6 (Annaka)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Shrine-temple exempt land, temple and shrine-personnel counts, household and population totals",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Annaka domain entry in fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran (1870 Dajōkan domain survey). The page records shrine-temple exempt land: 38 chō 6 tan 9 se 23 bu in the main holdings plus 8 chō 4 tan 7 [bu] in the domain's detached districts of Sōsa, Katori, and Kaijō (printed as Shimotsuke Province, evidently a misprint for Shimōsa), combining to a printed total of 47 chō 1 bu (the components sum to exactly 47 chō 1 tan). It further lists 42 Buddhist temples (of which 4 Shugendō practitioners), one additional temple, 10 and 13 shrine personnel, temples in 73 villages with one temple on exempt land under another authority's administration, and the domain totals of 6,035 households and 27,034 persons; an editorial note marks three of the temple-shrine lines as red marginal writing in the original manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "annaka_lower_p038_left",
   "sequence": 314,
   "domain_canonical": "安中藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "安中藩",
   "domain_en": "Annaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p038_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 38,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（安中）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Governance Survey, Table 6 (Annaka)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Annaka domain demographics: households and population by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Annaka domain entry in fascicle 6 (households and population) of the Hansei Ichiran. The page records 158 shizoku households (709 persons: 333 male, 376 female) and 76 sotsu households (252 persons: 130 male, 122 female), totalled in the source as 234 households and 961 persons (463 male, 498 female); all sums are internally consistent. Commoners number 5,499 houses with 25,103 persons (12,941 male, 12,162 female); shrine personnel 112 persons (58 male, 54 female) in 35 households. The religious establishment comprises 110 Buddhist temples (32 holding vermillion-seal grants, 47 without resident priest) and 18 yamabushi households (1 with a vermillion seal), with a temple-and-yamabushi population printed as 123 (55 monks, 16 males, 17 yamabushi, 34 females — components sum to 122, one short of the printed total). Printed book page 53."
  },
  {
   "id": "annaka_lower_p224_left",
   "sequence": 315,
   "domain_canonical": "安中藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "安中藩",
   "domain_en": "Annaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p224_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 224,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（安中）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Systems, fascicle 9 (Annaka)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a fascicle-9 page, printed book page 425, whose running head names Annaka Domain. Its right-hand columns finish the preceding domain, Ayabe: five officer names in the lower register, then Ayabe's military return of 兵員 百人 — 100 men, broken down as 12 officers (司官十貳人), 14 artillerymen (砲兵十四人) and 74 infantry (步兵七十四人), which sum exactly to the printed total. Left of the ○安中藩 marker the page opens Annaka's own return: 知事 (governor) printed as a bare office heading with neither a member count nor a name, 大參事 一員 (one senior councillor, Yokoi Gen'emon), and 權大參事 五員 (five acting senior councillors — Yokoi Sennosuke, Eba Kamagorō, Iida Itsunosuke, Wada Mon'emon and Hoshino Takesaburō), whose five names are set in a two-row block beneath the heading and match the stated count. No fiscal or demographic fields appear on this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "asada_lower_p039_right",
   "sequence": 316,
   "domain_canonical": "麻田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "麻田藩",
   "domain_en": "Asada",
   "image": "images/lower_p039_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 39,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（麻田）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Table 6 (Asada)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "End of Annaka's civil block (outcastes, shrines, villages, governor's family) and start of Asada's kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-6 page closes Annaka Domain's civil-survey block and opens Asada Domain's. For Annaka it records 157 outcaste (eta/hinin) households totalling 735 persons (375 male, 360 female), 97 shrines (79 in Kōzuke Province, 18 in Shimōsa), and 65 villages (42 in Kōzuke, 23 in Shimōsa) besides the post town of Annaka-juku, ending with the governor's family of five (the governor, his heir, his wife, and two daughters). Left of the ○麻田藩 marker, Asada Domain's block begins with a kusadaka of 10,807.519 koku plus 415.849 koku of newly developed field assessment, for a combined total of 11,223.368 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "asada_lower_p039_left",
   "sequence": 317,
   "domain_canonical": "麻田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "麻田藩",
   "domain_en": "Asada",
   "image": "images/lower_p039_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 39,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（麻田）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Table 6 (Asada)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Asada domain five-year-average tax receipts, households, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Asada domain (麻田藩, a small Settsu-province domain) entry in fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran. The page records five-year-average annual receipts: a regular land tax of 5,208.592 koku of rice — of which 5,145.604 koku fell under fixed (jōmen) assessment — plus miscellaneous taxes of 6.1274 koku in rice, 5 ryō 2 bu 2 shu in gold, and 113 kan 248 mon in copper cash, the money items being explained as license (unjō) and myōga fees on ponds and rivers, sake brewing, and water mills, all noted as fixed annual payments. It then opens the demographic block: 2,228 households and a population of 10,341 persons, split 5,272 male and 5,069 female, with the status-class breakdown continuing on the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "asada_lower_p040_right",
   "sequence": 318,
   "domain_canonical": "麻田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "麻田藩",
   "domain_en": "Asada",
   "image": "images/lower_p040_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 40,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（麻生）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran Table, Fascicle 6 (Asō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Population by status group (Asada Domain)",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of Asada Domain's (麻田藩, Settsu Province, ~10,000 koku) fascicle-6 status census. The page enumerates households and persons by legal status: shizoku 77 households / 313 persons, sotsu 60 / 148, shrine priests 5 / 20, Buddhist temples 51 with 85 clergy (54 monks, 17 women, 3 laymen, 11 nuns), Shugendō practitioners 1 household / 2 persons, commoners 2,034 households / 9,773 persons, and — recorded separately with the prefix 外ニ — eta outcastes 89 households / 415 persons, for roughly 10,756 persons in all. The domain's army is a single platoon of 72 men (12 of them officers), noted as already counted within the shizoku and sotsu rows, and 29 Shinto shrines are listed excluding branch shrines. The ○麻生藩 marker at the far left opens Asō Domain (Hitachi Province), whose data begins on the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "asada_lower_p225_right",
   "sequence": 319,
   "domain_canonical": "麻田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "麻田藩",
   "domain_en": "Asada",
   "image": "images/lower_p225_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 225,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（麻田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Systems, fascicle 9 (Asada)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 leaf (printed page 426) that closes out Annaka Domain's return and opens Asada Domain's. The three columns to the right of the ○麻田藩 marker still belong to Annaka: two 少參事 (junior councillors), whose names the return declines to give, four 權少參事 (acting junior councillors), and a force of three platoons. Asada's own block follows: a 知事 heading with no name attached, one 大參事 (Seki Kingo), two 權大參事 (Fukui Daizō and Muraoka Shirō), four 少參事 (Toda Tetsuya, Aoki Kuhachirō, Morimoto Rokuzō and Iwata Keizō), and a single platoon of sixty men. Two notes record changes carried by a later return of the 12th month of the snake year (Meiji 2/12): a bracketed insert puts Toda Tetsuya at 權少參事, and a parenthesised note under Fukui Daizō says that return gives Tamura Haruma in his place and no Fukui at all."
  },
  {
   "id": "aso_lower_p040_left",
   "sequence": 320,
   "domain_canonical": "麻生藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "麻生藩",
   "domain_en": "Asō",
   "image": "images/lower_p040_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 40,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（麻生）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey Table, Fascicle 6 (Asō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Asō domain kokudaka, land-tax and household/population totals",
   "page_summary_en": "Opening data page of the Asō domain block (a small Hitachi-province domain) in fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran. Its assessed yield (kusadaka) is 14,582.2585 koku including komi-daka and new fields; after deductions for wasteland, the jin'ya compound and kuwashita exemptions the taxable remainder is 11,769.0162 koku. The combined take (toriai) is 4,618.796 koku of rice plus 30.6486 kan-mon in ei cash (converted at 2.5 koku per kan-mon), of which the regular land tax is 3,945.1066 koku — exactly 11,271.733 bales at 3 to 5 shō per bale — plus 32.28294 kan-mon, with miscellaneous taxes of 22 ryō 3 bu 1 shu in gold, 34.0276 kan-mon in ei, and 12.36 kan-mon in copper cash. The page closes with 1,723 households and a population of 9,092, beside which the 1928 editors note the original manuscript carried 9,249 in red ink."
  },
  {
   "id": "aso_lower_p041_right",
   "sequence": 321,
   "domain_canonical": "麻生藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "麻生藩",
   "domain_en": "Asō",
   "image": "images/lower_p041_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 41,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（麻生）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran Table, Fascicle 6 (Asō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Asō Domain population status breakdown, shrines, temples, and infantry",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of the Asō Domain (Hitachi Province) entry in fascicle 6, giving the status breakdown of the domain population of 9,092 reported at the end of the previous page. The listed statuses are shizoku 405 (234 male, 171 female), sotsu 195 (142 male, 53 female), shrine functionaries 36, Buddhist clergy 29, shugen ascetics 3, blind 1, eta 15 (in 4 households), and hinin 19 (in 2 households); the domain also counts 12 shrines and 68 temples. According to the 1928 editor's marginal note, the parenthesized entries reproduce passages written in red ink in the original 1870 manuscript, among them the note that the figures were revised on the basis of the survey of the ninth month of Kōgo (Meiji 3, autumn 1870). The military line records a single infantry platoon of 60 men with 10 officers."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashikaga_lower_p041_left",
   "sequence": 322,
   "domain_canonical": "足利藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足利藩",
   "domain_en": "Ashikaga",
   "image": "images/lower_p041_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 41,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（足利）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table 6 (Ashikaga)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Ashikaga domain tax rice, taxes, households, and status populations",
   "page_summary_en": "The Hansei Ichiran fascicle-6 block for Ashikaga domain (Shimotsuke). It records tax rice on a five-year-average basis across the domain's four districts — 15,112.73728 koku in total, an annual mean of 3,022.54746 koku, equivalent to 8,635.32295 bales — plus miscellaneous taxes of 7 kan 178.18 mon in permanent cash, 4,058 households, and a population of 17,878 (printed male/female split 8,765/9,014, which sums only to 17,779 — an inconsistency in the source print). Separately noted \"besides\" the main counts are 53 eta households with 262 persons (printed split 148/122) and 419 shizoku (211 male, 208 female). An artillery squad of 36 men belonging to the preceding Asō domain's block overflows onto the head of the page."
  },
  {
   "id": "ashikaga_lower_p042_right",
   "sequence": 323,
   "domain_canonical": "足利藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "足利",
   "domain_en": "Ashikaga",
   "image": "images/lower_p042_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 42,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（足利）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Institutions Survey (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 6 (Ashikaga)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Ashikaga population by status; religious institutions and special-status households",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-6 continuation page for Ashikaga Domain (Shimotsuke Province) records a demographic and religious-institution breakdown. It lists 114 shizoku (samurai) households and 37 sotsu households comprising 108 persons (60 male, 48 female). The religious/special-status section gives 18 Shinto-priest households (70 persons: 34 male, 36 female), 81 Buddhist temples with 79 monks, 3 hermitages (庵), 5 dormitory-halls (寮), 1 nenbutsu hall, and 267 shrines (small shrines included); plus special-status households of 4 ferrymen (船越), 13 bell-ringers (鉦打), 5 monkey-trainers (猿引), and 1 shrine-attendant. Marginal notes state that Shinto priests and the categories below are counted within the domain totals, and flag the following twelve lines as vermilion writing in the original."
  },
  {
   "id": "anji_lower_p042_left",
   "sequence": 324,
   "domain_canonical": "安志藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "安志藩",
   "domain_en": "Anshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p042_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 42,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（安志）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 6 — Anji (安志藩)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka and school/temple land holdings with five-year average revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "Left half of a fascicle-6 fiscal-survey spread carrying the seam between two domains. The right-hand columns close out the Ashikaga Domain (足利藩) block: a 100-koku school-land holding in Ashikaga district yielding 14.09175 koku of rice plus 12 ryō 2 bu 2 shu in gold and 543 mon in cash, temple-held land (寺院受領高) of 232.836 koku, and five-year-average totals of 74.24451 koku of rice, 6.25 ryō in gold, 10,530.463 mon in ei accounting cash, and 71,753 mon in zeni. Left of the ○安志藩 marker the Anji Domain block opens: a grass yield (草高) of 10,000 koku lying within three districts of Harima Province, an additional 9.69465 koku of new-field yield (新田高), and a combined assessment (合高) of 10,009.69465 koku — the components sum exactly. Anji's own five-year-average section is headed at the far left and its figures continue on the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "anshi_lower_p043_right",
   "sequence": 325,
   "domain_canonical": "安志藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "安志",
   "domain_en": "Anshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p043_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 43,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（安志）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Anshi)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Anshi domain land tax, miscellaneous taxes, and products",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fiscal survey of Anshi (安志) domain, a small 10,000-koku fudai holding in Harima province. Its regular land tax (正租) is reported as 4,967.493 koku of actual rice (a fixed-rate assessment that varies with disaster years and is paid entirely in kind), and its miscellaneous tax (雜稅) as 6.231 koku of rice plus 163.9375 ryō in cash (163兩3分3朱 with a 2.972-monme silver remainder), the cash converting to 20.4959 koku at an 8-ryō-per-koku rate. Summing these components yields the printed present-koku total (現石合) of 4,994.2199 koku, an internal check that reconciles exactly. The domain's products — sedge-thread (菅絲), tea, tobacco, and soy sauce — are all untaxed, with a note that paper-money borrowing the previous year prompted efforts to market these goods and build up commerce."
  },
  {
   "id": "anshi_lower_p043_left",
   "sequence": 326,
   "domain_canonical": "安志藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "安志",
   "domain_en": "Anshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p043_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 43,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（安志）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-System Survey Table, Fascicle 6 (Anshi)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Anshi Domain population and household census",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the demographic return for Anshi Domain (安志藩, Harima Province; Hansei Ichiran fascicle 6), a small ~10,000-koku Ogasawara holding. It records 2,596 total households and a population of 10,037. The breakdown gives shizoku 67 households / 274 persons, sotsu 74 / 252, sub-sotsu retainers (卒以下) 44 / 102 — together 185 households and 635 persons (the latter figure including the 7 monks of the domain's 3 prayer-temples) — plus commoners (平民) 2,367 households / 9,254 persons and 43 shrine-attendants (社人). Marginal notes state that shrine/temple stipendiaries are combined into the household total and that shrine-attendants, monks, and eta are counted within the population, which accounts for the 44-household and ~105-person shortfall between the itemised classes and the grand totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "sakura_lower_p047_right",
   "sequence": 327,
   "domain_canonical": "佐倉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐倉藩",
   "domain_en": "Sakura",
   "image": "images/lower_p047_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 47,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（佐倉）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 6 (Sakura)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sakura domain taxes, households, religious institutions, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This continuation page of fascicle 6 (第六) records the fiscal and demographic returns of Sakura domain (佐倉藩). Regular tax (正稅) was 47,265.618 koku of rice plus 2,343.757 kan of eiraku cash; miscellaneous tax (雜稅) comprised 2,442.308 koku of rice, 604.626 kan of eiraku cash, 49.125 ryō of gold, 1,213.235 kan of copper cash, and 16.995 koku of salt. The domain held 19,791 households and a population of 111,265 persons. Under an \"of which\" (内) marker the page lists religious institutions: 21 Shinto priests (神主), 16 shrine officials (神職), 9 shrine families (社家), 501 temples, 40 mountain ascetics (修驗), and 1 onmyōji."
  },
  {
   "id": "sakura_lower_p047_left",
   "sequence": 328,
   "domain_canonical": "佐倉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐倉藩",
   "domain_en": "Sakura",
   "image": "images/lower_p047_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 47,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐倉）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 6 (Sakura) — outer running header / provenance",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sakura domain: population male/female split, clergy & special-status head-counts, and shizoku/sotsu household and population totals",
   "page_summary_en": "A single-domain continuation page for Sakura (佐倉藩), fascicle 6 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran survey. It opens with the 内 breakdown of the domain's total population — 55,724 men and 54,976 women (110,700 total; the grand total itself sits on the preceding right-hand page) — then enumerates religious and special-status groups in two stacked registers: 24 kannushi, 16 shinshoku, 19 shrine attendants, 362 Buddhist monks, 39 Shugendō ascetics, 53 physicians, 1 onmyōji, 11 dancer-priests, 20 zatō, 9 blind persons, 10 dōshin, and 1 nun. It closes with the warrior tallies — 521 shizoku households (3,021 persons: 1,502 M / 1,519 F) and 1,110 sotsu households (4,469 persons: 2,763 M / 1,706 F) — plus one monkey-trainer household (10 persons) and one leprosy-afflicted household (7 persons). Every 内 male/female warichu sum-checks against its parent total."
  },
  {
   "id": "sakura_lower_p227_left",
   "sequence": 329,
   "domain_canonical": "佐倉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐倉藩",
   "domain_en": "Sakura",
   "image": "images/lower_p227_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 227,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（佐倉）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 9 (Sakura)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Sakura domain officials roster and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of the spread continues the fascicle-9 entry for Sakura domain (佐倉藩), whose maru-marker ○佐倉藩 stands on the facing page (printed 430). It names the domain's councillors: two senior councillors (大參事), Hirano Nuidono and Nishimura Kanae; one acting senior councillor (權大參事), Yoda Uemonjirō; one junior councillor (少參事), Saji Taijirō; and six acting junior councillors (權少參事), Kōsokabe Hayato, Ikeura Naoe, Onda Gengobē, Saitō Yaichizaemon, Irie Hikozaemon and Tanaka San. Two military columns follow: nine platoons of rifle troops at 60 men each (540 riflemen) and two artillery companies at 48 men each (96 gunners), a combined 636 men under arms. The roster closes with 外役々, which signals that the remaining offices are not itemised; the printed page number is 431."
  },
  {
   "id": "shinoyama_lower_p048_right",
   "sequence": 330,
   "domain_canonical": "篠山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "篠山藩",
   "domain_en": "Sasayama",
   "image": "images/lower_p048_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 48,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（篠山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 6 (Shinoyama)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Shinoyama kokudaka, land tax and products; tail of Sakura demographic fields",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand (earlier-read) columns complete the tail of Sakura domain (佐倉藩): 19 districts, 738 shrines (a figure originally in vermilion, plus 53 shrine-places held in common), 21 eta households totalling 156 persons (73 male, 83 female), and 14 hinin households totalling 81 persons (42 male, 39 female). The circular marker ○篠山藩 then opens Shinoyama domain, whose scattered holdings lay in Tanba, Settsu and Tajima provinces. Shinoyama's assessed kokudaka is 60,000 koku plus 8,222.17626 koku of newly-reclaimed land, totalling 68,222.17626 koku (合高); regular land tax in rice (正租) is 30,898.79233 koku and miscellaneous rice taxes (雜稅) 5,390.16026 koku, with cash dues (永) of 204 kan 860 mon 9 bu, charcoal 372 bales, and firewood 7,757.3 loads. A marginal note dates the Shinoyama figures to the Kōgo (1870) 10th-month survey."
  },
  {
   "id": "sasayama_lower_p048_left",
   "sequence": 331,
   "domain_canonical": "篠山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "篠山藩",
   "domain_en": "Sasayama",
   "image": "images/lower_p048_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 48,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（篠山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle (Table) 6 (Sasayama)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sasayama domain: notable (untaxed) products and household census by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the Sasayama-domain (篠山藩) return in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran. The upper-right column heads a list of the domain's notable products, all flagged as untaxed (右無税): tea 13,500 kanme, raw silk 410 kanme, ceramics 7,500 packloads (駄), tobacco 34,400 kin, and cocoons 1,779.5 kanme. The remainder is a household census totalling 13,616 households (戸數), broken down (内) by status: 413 shizoku, 495 sotsu, 11,840 commoners (農工商), 269 temples, plus small counts of shrine families (19), yamabushi (3), onmyōji (4), crematory/grave keepers (23), outcaste watchmen (41) and 509 eta. The ten status components sum exactly to the printed 13,616 total."
  },
  {
   "id": "sasayama_lower_p228_right",
   "sequence": 332,
   "domain_canonical": "篠山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "篠山藩",
   "domain_en": "Sasayama",
   "image": "images/lower_p228_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 228,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（篠山、佐土原）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Systems, Fascicle 9 (Sasayama, Sadowara)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 9 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran, covering domain officialdom and military strength, opens Sasayama Domain's entry at the right of the page and Sadowara Domain's at the left. Sasayama's establishment is printed as a governor (知事, no count and no name given), 2 senior councillors, 6 acting senior councillors, 5 junior councillors and 3 acting junior councillors — 17 posts in all — followed by eleven individual names, and it closes with a troop strength of 552 men. The counts for the senior councillors, junior councillors and acting junior councillors are each matched exactly by the names printed beneath them; the acting senior councillors are not, since only one name (Akami Tamēmon) stands against a printed count of six. Sadowara's entry records its officials simply as \"not ascertained\" (審ナラス) and gives its force as four infantry platoons, each of 61 men including 40 riflemen, i.e. 244 infantry."
  },
  {
   "id": "sadowara_lower_p049_right",
   "sequence": 333,
   "domain_canonical": "佐土原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐土原藩",
   "domain_en": "Sadowara",
   "image": "images/lower_p049_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 49,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐土原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Sadowara)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sasayama population/status breakdown and Sadowara kokudaka/land-tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf of Fascicle 6 straddles two domains, divided by the single ○佐土原藩 domain-marker. To the RIGHT of the marker lies the tail of Sasayama-han's (篠山藩) demographic block: a total population of 58,723 persons, broken down by status into commoners (農工商 52,281), shizoku (2,158), sotsu (1,466), eta (2,204), Buddhist clergy (267), non-persons/guards (208), cremators (61), yin-yang diviners (19), shrine households (53) and mountain ascetics (9), together with 166 Shinto shrines. To the LEFT of the marker begins Sadowara-han's (佐土原藩) fiscal block: an assessed yield (高) of 27,070.713 koku carrying a 183.466-koku revised deduction (改減高引) and 6,375.5462 koku of additional yield (外二高), with land tax (正租) of 17,055.35265 koku paid in rice. The printed status sub-counts sum to 58,726, three above the stated 58,723 total — a minor source-level non-footing. Printed page number 74."
  },
  {
   "id": "sadowara_lower_p049_left",
   "sequence": 334,
   "domain_canonical": "佐土原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐土原",
   "domain_en": "Sadowara",
   "image": "images/lower_p049_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 49,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐土原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 6 (Sadowara)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Products, miscellaneous taxes, samurai households, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-6 (economic) survey for Sadowara Domain (佐土原藩), a small Hyūga-province domain. The right-hand columns close out the domain's tribute/tax figures — soybeans 3,605.79135 koku, salt 50.29606 koku, and a cash levy of 9,108.924 kan-mon — after which the section header 諸産物及諸税 (\"various products and taxes\") introduces paper (800 rolls, at 6,000 sheets per roll), half-cut paper (500 rolls, at 11,000 sheets per roll), and raw wax (3,000 jin), all recorded as five-year averages, plus a five-year-average miscellaneous forest/river/marsh tax of 5,329.124 kan-mon. It closes with 854 samurai (shizoku) households and a total population of 3,778 (male 1,893; female 1,881 — the printed total exceeds the male+female sum by four)."
  },
  {
   "id": "sadowara_lower_p050_right",
   "sequence": 335,
   "domain_canonical": "佐土原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐土原藩",
   "domain_en": "Sadowara",
   "image": "images/lower_p050_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 50,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（西條）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, fascicle 6 (Saijō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sadowara household/population demographics by status; Saijō kokudaka opening",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of fascicle 6 closes the civil register of Sadowara Domain (佐土原藩, a Shimazu cadet branch in Hyūga) and opens that of Saijō Domain (西條藩, a Kishū-Tokugawa branch in Iyo). The Sadowara block, read right-to-left, tabulates households and population by status: 883 sotsu (lower-samurai) households totalling 3,133 persons (1,715 m / 1,418 f), 5,171 commoner households totalling 18,666 persons (9,583 m / 9,083 f), 209 shrine (Shintō) households totalling 806 persons (437 m / 369 f), and 8 temples with 37 persons (33 m / 4 f); every male-plus-female pair sums exactly to its stated total. Left of the ○西條藩 boundary marker, Saijō's entry begins with an assessed yield (高) of 40,801.8 koku, of which 30,000 koku is the anciently-granted amount (前々拝領高) and 3,149.99 koku the honden-included figure (本田込高), the remaining breakdown carrying onto the facing page. A vermilion editorial note records that the figures derive from the tenth-month survey of the Snake year (Meiji 2 / 1869)."
  },
  {
   "id": "saijo_lower_p050_left",
   "sequence": 336,
   "domain_canonical": "西條藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西條藩",
   "domain_en": "Saijō",
   "image": "images/lower_p050_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 50,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（西條）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Survey Table, Fascicle 6 (Saijō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Saijō domain — land tax, miscellaneous taxes, and samurai/soldier household and population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand sheet continues the Saijō (西條) domain entry in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei ichiran. It records the domain's regular land tax (正租) of 16,913.966 koku of rice, together with a new-paddy/reassessed-output increment of 7,651.81 koku and roughly 209 chō of village land left unassessed because its yield was not fixed. Miscellaneous cash taxes are itemized as 923.32 ryō (fixed minor imposts), 192.01 ryō (variable imposts), and 635.03 ryō (mountain-district dues), plus an occasional-tax item of 32.10 koku of rice. Household and population figures are given for the samurai class (shizoku: 292 houses, 1,501 people — 709 male, 792 female) and the soldier classes (heisotsu: 153 houses, 725 people — 361 male, 364 female; keisotsu: 295 houses). The printed folio number is 77."
  },
  {
   "id": "saijo_lower_p051_right",
   "sequence": 337,
   "domain_canonical": "西條藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西條藩",
   "domain_en": "Saijō",
   "image": "images/lower_p051_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 51,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（西條）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Saijō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Saijō domain: population, status-tier personnel breakdown, and religious households",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation page of the fascicle-6 demographic entry for Saijō Domain (西條藩). It opens with a samurai-class personnel total (士族人員) of 1,252 — 615 male, 637 female — followed by a nine-line breakdown that was originally written in red ink in the manuscript and here parenthesized as marginal entries. The breakdown gives civil officials (文官), troops (兵隊), and unassigned/no-post men (無役) across three status tiers: shizoku (104 / 85 / 183), heisotsu foot-soldiers (79 / 46 / 72), and keisotsu light-troops (111 / 106 / 147); the 兵隊 counts also note platoon strengths (2, 1, and 2 small platoons). The page closes with religious households: 28 Shinto-priest houses (社家) holding 137 people (63 male, 74 female) and 39 Shugendō/yamabushi houses (修驗). No maru-marker appears, so the entire page belongs to Saijō, as confirmed by the running header 藩制一覽表第六（西條）and page number 七十八 (78)."
  },
  {
   "id": "saijo_lower_p051_left",
   "sequence": 338,
   "domain_canonical": "西條藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西條藩",
   "domain_en": "Saijō",
   "image": "images/lower_p051_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 51,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "七十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（西條）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Saijō)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Saijō demographics (town/temple/shugen) and land-tax revenue (正税・雜税)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left page continues the 西條藩 (Iyo Saijō, fascicle 6) entry with commoner demographic and fiscal data compiled from the 1870 (庚午) survey; there is no maru-marker on the page, so every column belongs to Saijō. It records a town/rural (在町) population of 54,400 in 11,281 households (27,215 male / 27,185 female), 89 temple buildings (寺院堂庵) with 192 clergy (172 male / 20 female), and 181 persons (88 male / 93 female) attached to the 39 shugen lodges (修驗) whose category-head stands on the preceding page. The regular tax (正税) is entered as 18,187.584 koku of rice plus a further 11.30469 koku and a cash sum of 90 ryō 1 bu 3 shu, and the miscellaneous tax (雜税) as 814.148 and 140.86088 koku of rice; a warichu note flags these tax lines as originally red-ink marginalia drawn from a single register."
  },
  {
   "id": "saijo_lower_p228_left",
   "sequence": 339,
   "domain_canonical": "西條藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西條藩",
   "domain_en": "Saijō",
   "image": "images/lower_p228_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 228,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百三十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（西條、佐伯）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Saijō, Saeki)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 433 of fascicle 9 of the Hansei ichiran, the Dajōkan's 1869-70 survey of the domains, carrying the officials-and-troops entries for three domains in succession. The leaf opens with the tail of Sadowara domain's military return — one artillery company, four field guns and four mortars — then the maru-marker for Saijō domain (Iyo), whose full slate is printed here: a governor, one senior councillor, three acting senior councillors, one junior councillor and two acting junior councillors, with troops of five platoons totalling 237 men. That troop figure reconciles exactly with the fascicle-6 breakdown recorded elsewhere in the survey for the same domain (2 platoons/85 men + 1 platoon/46 men + 2 platoons/106 men). The Saeki domain (Bungo) marker follows, and its entry begins with a governor, one senior councillor (Sakuma Gi'emon) and two acting senior councillorships filled by a single named man, Hazama Shichirōemon, the shortfall recorded in a small interlinear gloss reading 一人."
  },
  {
   "id": "saeki_lower_p052_right",
   "sequence": 340,
   "domain_canonical": "佐伯藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐伯藩",
   "domain_en": "Saeki",
   "image": "images/lower_p052_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 52,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐伯）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 6 (Saeki) — running header",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Land-tax / fiscal record of Saeki domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-6 (land-tax and fiscal) record for Saeki domain (佐伯藩), a 20,000-koku Mōri domain in Bungo province. Its base kokudaka (高) of 20,000 koku plus 1,952.21043 koku of newly-reclaimed field (新田改出高) gives a total assessed kokudaka (合) of 21,952.21043 koku; the tax rice actually collected (此取米) is 9,858.895 koku, itemized (内譯) into 7,626.37 koku paid in kind (現石納高) and 2,232.525 koku paid by substitution (代納高). The substitute payment is valued at 12,884.46816 kan of eizeni (此永); the total money assessment (此金) is 1,126 ryō 3 bu 2 shu (at 8 ryō/koku), total rice (合米) is 19,153.89357 koku, miscellaneous taxes (雑税高) total 18,926.08383 kan, and the domain reports 191 shizoku households (士族戸數). The entire leaf is Saeki; although the project index also tags 三田藩 here, no Sanda marker or data is physically present (Sanda's record begins on the next leaf, p53)."
  },
  {
   "id": "saeki_lower_p052_left",
   "sequence": 341,
   "domain_canonical": "佐伯藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐伯藩",
   "domain_en": "Saeki",
   "image": "images/lower_p052_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 52,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐伯）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Saeki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Status-group population & household census (Saeki)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page completes the Saeki (佐伯藩) entry in fascicle 6 of the Hansei Ichiran, a status-group population and household census. The domain's total population is 65,366 (male 33,724, female 31,642) living in 12,173 households across 26 villages, with 22 Shinto shrines and 32 Buddhist temples. Itemised status groups include 937 samurai (shizoku, M436/F501), 1,247 sotsu (foot-soldier class, M613/F634) in 252 households, 28 shrine-priest (shake) households (165 persons), 10 Shugendo households (46 persons), a temple population of 326 (289 monks + 37 women, plus 1 nun), and small outcaste groups (eta: 2 households/8 persons; hinin: 22 households/127 persons). A vermilion editorial note records the domain's military as two infantry platoons, one drawn from the samurai class and one from the sotsu class."
  },
  {
   "id": "sanda_lower_p053_right",
   "sequence": 342,
   "domain_canonical": "三田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三田藩",
   "domain_en": "Sanda",
   "image": "images/lower_p053_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 53,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（三田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 6 (Sanda)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka and land-tax accounts of Sanda domain (Settsu / Tanba)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page records the fiscal accounts of Sanda domain (三田藩), whose lands lay in Settsu and Tanba provinces. Its assessed kokudaka was 36,000 koku, with an additional 1,717.337 koku of newly reclaimed paddy (新田高), giving a combined total (合高) of 37,717.337 koku. Regular land tax (正稅) in rice came to 12,220.655 koku from the Settsu holdings and 2,289.828 koku from Tanba, and miscellaneous tax (雜稅) added 558.997 koku of rice plus 127 kan 632 mon in cash in Settsu and 197.833 koku of rice in Tanba, together with soybean (大豆) levies of 20 and 1.6 koku. A red-ink editorial note attributes the kokudaka figure to the Meiji 2 survey."
  },
  {
   "id": "mita_lower_p053_left",
   "sequence": 343,
   "domain_canonical": "三田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三田藩",
   "domain_en": "Sanda",
   "image": "images/lower_p053_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 53,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（三田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, fascicle 6 (Mita)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Mita domain civil/fiscal survey — households, population, status, temples/shrines, land tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page carries the fascicle-6 (civil) survey for Mita domain (三田藩), in Settsu. It records 4,438 households and a total population of 20,332 (10,376 male, 9,956 female), including 667 samurai/shizoku (226 male, 441 female) and a 16-household hinin-ban watch of 80 persons (42 male, 38 female); religious institutions number 69 temples (with 95 monks and 18 nuns) and 60 shrines. Fiscal figures are a regular land tax (正税) of 14,530.483 koku of rice and miscellaneous taxes (雑税) of 758.43 koku of rice plus 127.632 kanmon in cash, with marginal red-ink notes recording 240 foot-soldiers and that the sotsu class is counted within the rural population. The ○鯖江藩 marker at the far left opens the next domain, Sabae, whose data begins on the following page — everything to its right on this page belongs to Mita."
  },
  {
   "id": "sanda_lower_p229_right",
   "sequence": 344,
   "domain_canonical": "三田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三田藩",
   "domain_en": "Sanda",
   "image": "images/lower_p229_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 229,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百三十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（三田、鯖江）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Sanda, Sabae)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 434 of the fascicle-9 officials-and-military survey, carrying the whole of 三田藩 (Sanda, Settsu; Kuki house) together with the tail of the preceding entry and the opening of the next. Sanda reports two senior councillors (大參事 Sawano Kichizaemon and Shirasu Taizō), two acting senior councillors (權大參事 Mutō Shūjirō and Murayama, given name printed 沉雄), one junior councillor (少參事 Amaoka Hanzaemon), one acting junior councillor (權少參事 Kuki Iori), and 240 troops (兵隊 貳百四十員); the 知事 heading prints with no governor's name under it. To the right of the ○三田藩 marker the previous entry, 佐伯藩 (Saiki, Bungo), finishes with three junior councillors (少參事 三員, one name given, Nishina Hyōemon), two acting junior councillors (權少參事 二人, Kuniya Tōemon and Yamaguchi Tōzaemon), and a military line reading 步兵二小隊 人員記セス — two infantry platoons, personnel not recorded. At the far left the ○鯖江藩 marker and a bare 知事 heading open the Sabae entry, whose counts and its 282 troops continue on page 435."
  },
  {
   "id": "sabae_lower_p054_right",
   "sequence": 345,
   "domain_canonical": "鯖江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鯖江",
   "domain_en": "Sabae",
   "image": "images/lower_p054_right.jpg",
