   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（鯖江）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 6 (Sabae)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sabae domain: kokudaka, land/product tax, products, shizoku &amp; sotsu households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the fascicle-6 entry for Sabae domain (鯖江藩, Echizen), assessed at 40,000 koku plus 66.951 koku of newly reclaimed paddy (改出シ新田) for a total assessed yield of 40,066.951 koku. Its regular tax in actual rice (正税現米) was 12,404.4216 koku, and a product tax (産物税) of 5 kan 761.8 mon in ei-cash was levied on four taxed products — hōsho paper, lime, whetstone, and ajiro woven hats — while eight further products (raw silk, paper-mulberry bark, birch, ramie cloth, lacquer bowls, moxa, straw matting, and rapeseed) were listed as untaxed. The domain counted 311 shizoku households with a population of 1,377 (621 male, 756 female) and 303 sotsu households with a population of 1,289 (667 male, 622 female). No maru-marker is present; the domain is identified only by the running header, and the page carries printed page number 84."
  },
  {
   "id": "sayama_lower_p054_left",
   "sequence": 346,
   "domain_canonical": "狹山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "狹山藩",
   "domain_en": "Sayama",
   "image": "images/lower_p054_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 54,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（狹山、吉井）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Sayama, Yoshii)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Civil register (Sabae overflow) plus kokudaka and revenue (Sayama)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of Fascicle 6 carries three domains. Its bulk is the tail of the 鯖江 (Sabae) civil register, printed to the right of the ○狹山藩 marker and therefore belonging to the preceding domain: 5,718 households and 27,151 people (13,793 male / 13,358 female), 8 shrines, 8 shrine-attendant houses (39 people), 78 temples (294 temple residents = 152 monks, 11 nuns, 8 lay men, 123 lay women), 4 yamabushi houses (17 people) and 3 outcaste (穢多) houses (13 people). To the marker's left the 狹山 (Sayama) entry opens with an assessed kokudaka of 11,615.7026 koku and collected revenue of 5,467.72984 koku of rice, its regular and miscellaneous taxes recorded as entirely undetailed (正雜稅其他一切不詳). The ○吉井藩 (Yoshii) marker then opens at the far left, its figures continuing on the next page."
  },
  {
   "id": "sano_lower_p055_right",
   "sequence": 347,
   "domain_canonical": "佐野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐野藩",
   "domain_en": "Sano",
   "image": "images/lower_p055_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 55,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐野）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Survey, Fascicle 6 (Sano)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka, land tax and household figures for Sano (plus the tail of Yoshii)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of Fascicle 6 mainly records Sano Domain (佐野藩), a 16,000-koku domain whose lands lay in Shimotsuke (1 district), Kōzuke (4 districts) and Ōmi (1 district). Its combined assessed kokudaka is 17,162.56328 koku — a 16,000-koku base plus 1,162.56328 koku of additional land (外高, annotated 込高, \"included in the total\"). Regular land tax (正租) was 5,108.36512 koku of rice plus 501 kan 39 mon 8 rin in cash (永), and miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) 232.35608 koku plus 430 kan 870 mon in cash; the domain had 2,518 households, of which the page lists 64 shrines and 5 Shinto-priest households before the breakdown continues on the facing page. The three rightmost data columns are the tail of the preceding Yoshii Domain (吉井藩, a 10,000-koku domain): its regular and miscellaneous taxes are noted as \"entirely undetailed,\" though its collected rice (此收納) was 2,155.89537 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "sano_lower_p055_left",
   "sequence": 348,
   "domain_canonical": "佐野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐野",
   "domain_en": "Sano",
   "image": "images/lower_p055_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 55,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐野）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Sano)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sano domain population and clergy/status demographics",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation page of the Sano (佐野) domain return in Fascicle 6 of the Hansei ichiran, recording population and religious/status demographics. The total population (人員) is 11,893 (6,075 male, 5,818 female). The samurai orders comprise 111 shizoku households (473 persons: 213 male, 260 female) and 119 sotsu households (628 persons: 329 male, 299 female); the governor's own family numbers 2 (1 male, 1 female). Religious tallies include 56 Buddhist temples, 1 training hall, 4 hermitages, 3 practitioner households, 63 monks, 15 shrine-family men, 14 shrine women and 24 temple women."
  },
  {
   "id": "sano_lower_p229_left",
   "sequence": 349,
   "domain_canonical": "佐野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐野藩",
   "domain_en": "Sano",
   "image": "images/lower_p229_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 229,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（狹山、佐野）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Fascicle 9 (Sayama, Sano)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 page carrying the officials-and-military returns of three domains. It opens with the tail of Sabae's entry — two senior councillors (dai-sanji), two acting senior councillors, two junior councillors, and 282 troops — then the maru-marker of Sayama, whose entire return is the single note 審ナラス, \"not ascertained\". Sano's marker follows: its total troop strength is likewise unascertained, but the units are itemised as four rifle platoons of 32 men each (128 riflemen), one artillery company of 20 men, and three cannon. Sano's councillors are then named — three dai-sanji (Sudō Hidenosuke, Tominaga, Kōsaka) and one gon-dai-sanji, Imai Kinpei, who is glossed in small type as the domain's kōgi-nin, its delegate to the deliberative assembly."
  },
  {
   "id": "sanuki_lower_p056_right",
   "sequence": 350,
   "domain_canonical": "佐貫藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐貫藩",
   "domain_en": "Sanuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p056_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 56,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐貫）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 6 — (Sanuki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sanuki kokudaka and averaged land/miscellaneous taxes (plus Sano's outcaste-status and village tail)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf of Fascicle 6 opens the entry for Sanuki Domain (佐貫藩, Kazusa; Abe house), whose ○-marker sits mid-page: everything to its right is the closing tail of the preceding Sano Domain (佐野藩), everything to its left is Sanuki. Sanuki is assessed at a 16,000-koku base plus 199.92195 koku of additional land (外高) — annotated by a warichu as komidaka together with previously-opened new paddy — for a combined 16,199.92195 koku, a sum the page states exactly. Under a 平均 (\"average\") heading it records regular land tax (正租) of 4,000.82626 koku of rice plus 1,838 kan 957 mon in ei-cash, and miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) of 8.971 koku plus 412 kan 595 mon — an effective land-tax incidence of about 24.7 percent of the combined assessment, against 29.8 percent for neighbouring Sano. Sano's four closing columns give 3 eta households (10 persons: 6 male, 4 female), 1 hinin male, and 36 villages; the leaf carries printed page number 88."
  },
  {
   "id": "sanuki_lower_p056_left",
   "sequence": 351,
   "domain_canonical": "佐貫藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐貫藩",
   "domain_en": "Sanuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p056_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 56,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第六（佐貫）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 6 (Sanuki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Product tax and status-group household and population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of printed page 89 in Hansei ichiran fascicle 6, continuing the entry for Sanuki domain (Kazusa province, base kokudaka 16,000 koku), whose ○佐貫藩 marker stands on the facing right-hand leaf. It opens with a product tax of 200 ryō in gold, then walks the domain's population by status group: 16 kazoku (7 male, 9 female); 91 shizoku households holding 401 persons (204 male, 197 female); 29 sotsu households holding 110 persons; 53 shrines served by 19 Shinto-priest households (80 persons); 47 temples with 78 clergy; and 3,314 commoner households totalling 16,908 persons (8,447 male, 8,461 female) — some 96 percent of the enumerated population. Every male-plus-female split on the page reconciles exactly against its printed total. Two vermilion editorial notes (原朱) qualify the figures: one dates the household and population counts to the Kōgo (1870) survey, the other preserves a Mi-year (1869) count of 180 shrines and 48 temples that departs sharply from the 53 shrines and 47 temples printed in the table itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "sanuki_lower_p230_right",
   "sequence": 352,
   "domain_canonical": "佐貫藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "佐貫藩",
   "domain_en": "Sanuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p230_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 230,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（佐貫）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Sanuki)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 436 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle 9 (domain officials and troops), given over almost entirely to Sanuki domain (佐貫藩, Kazusa Province, Abe house). The single column standing to the right of the ○佐貫藩 marker still belongs to Sano domain (佐野藩): one junior councillor, 永野又藏, carried over from book page 435. Sanuki's own entry prints the governorship (知事) as a heading with no name filled in, two senior councillors (木邨又右衛門, 石田鐵右衛門), four junior councillors (玉井平助, 栗飯原八百之進, 岩堀舍, 東條糺), and a force of 80 men (兵 八拾員). A revised roster below, headed 庚午ノ調左ノ如シ留守官届 — the Kōgo-year (1870) return filed by the domain's Tokyo caretaker office — names nine officials: two senior councillors, three acting senior councillors, one kōginin delegate, and three junior councillors."
  },
  {
   "id": "sakurai_lower_p057_right",
   "sequence": 353,
   "domain_canonical": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_en": "Sakurai",
   "image": "images/lower_p057_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 57,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（櫻井）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 6 (Sakurai)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sakurai kokudaka and tax opening; Sanuki's outcaste and village tail",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 90 of fascicle 6 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran-hyō. The five columns right of the maru-marker close out Sanuki domain's (佐貫藩) record: 14 eta households totalling 97 persons (52 male, 45 female), 9 hinin households totalling 26 persons (14 male, 12 female), and 48 villages. The ○櫻井藩 marker then opens Sakurai domain, whose entry gives a kokudaka (高) of 10,179.11318 koku, regular land tax (正租) of 2,882.93654 koku in delivered rice plus 437.98321 kan in cash (永), miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 290.67734 koku plus 89.23593 kan, and status counts of 5 kazoku (2 male, 3 female) and 85 shizoku households — a land-tax take of about 28 percent of assessed yield. A brace above the tax columns is labelled 附箋 (fusen, \"attached slip\"), the reprint's editors recording that those figures stood on a paper slip attached to the original manuscript rather than in its main text."
  },
  {
   "id": "sakurai_lower_p057_left",
   "sequence": 354,
   "domain_canonical": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_en": "Sakurai",
   "image": "images/lower_p057_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 57,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（櫻井）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey (Hansei ichiran-hyō), Fascicle 6 — Sakurai",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Sakurai population by status group, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 91, the continuation of the 櫻井藩 (Sakurai) entry in fascicle 6; the block was opened by the ○櫻井藩 marker on the facing recto (p. 90), and since no marker appears on this leaf every column belongs to Sakurai. Fourteen columns give the domain's population broken out by status group, each count followed by its own 人員 total and a 内 male/female split: the 85 shizoku households returned on the facing page hold 321 people (149 male, 172 female); 25 sotsu households hold 54 (30/24); 2,623 commoner households hold 12,866 (6,422/6,444); 5 shrine-priest (社家) households hold 24 (15/9); and 5 households of peasants on shrine land hold 26 (13/13). The page closes with 59 shrines, 42 temples whose resident population is 57 (54 male, 3 female), and a single watchman's hut. All six male+female splits reconcile exactly with their printed totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "sakurai_lower_p058_right",
   "sequence": 355,
   "domain_canonical": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_en": "Sakurai",
   "image": "images/lower_p058_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 58,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（岸和田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 6 (Kishiwada)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Appendix kokudaka and five-year-average taxes (Sakurai); Kishiwada entry opens",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of this page completes Sakurai domain's fascicle-6 entry, which began on printed page 九十 and continues from 九十一. It gives 27 villages; a registered headcount of 39 persons (20 male, 19 female) belonging to the watchman's-hut category carried over from the preceding page; and, under a brace headed 符箋 (\"attached slip\") with the qualifier 別冊 (\"separate appendix\"), an alternative kokudaka of 10,162.19517 koku plus five-year-average tax figures: paddy main tax 3,158.58065 koku of hulled rice, upland main tax 276.88845 koku with 533.654104 kan in cash, and miscellaneous tax 47.15785 koku with 82.020827 kan in cash. Left of the ○岸和田藩 marker, Kishiwada domain's entry opens with a base kokudaka of 53,000 koku plus 6,028.3232 koku of newly reclaimed field, totalling 59,028.3232 koku — an arithmetic identity that confirms the reading. The running head names Kishiwada even though most of the page's data is Sakurai's, so it must be treated as section provenance rather than a column label."
  },
  {
   "id": "sakurai_lower_p230_left",
   "sequence": 356,
   "domain_canonical": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "櫻井藩",
   "domain_en": "Sakurai",
   "image": "images/lower_p230_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 230,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（櫻井、岸和田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Nine (Sakurai, Kishiwada)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-nine page carries the officials returns for two domains plus the tail of a third. Sakurai (櫻井藩) heads its column run with the office 知事 (governor) printed with no name beneath it, then two senior councillors (大参事 金子正路 and 近藤門造), two junior councillors (少参事 中島周平治 and 倉橋貢), and a troop strength of 五十七員 — 57 men. Kishiwada (岸和田藩) opens at the left with a different reporting format that gives head-counts as well as names: 大参事 一人 (Furuya Sōbee) and 権大参事 一人 (Hori Gokujin), one man in each grade. The lower right of the leaf, printed to the right of the ○櫻井藩 marker, holds three 権少参事 (石井孫八郎, 館野彌一右衛門, 萩原篤右衛門) that finish Sanuki domain's second (Kōgo-year) officials list begun on the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "kishiwada_lower_p058_left",
   "sequence": 357,
   "domain_canonical": "岸和田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岸和田藩",
   "domain_en": "Kishiwada",
   "image": "images/lower_p058_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 58,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（岸和田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview Table, Fascicle 6 (Kishiwada)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kishiwada domain: averaged rice tax, status-group households and population, villages, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "The verso of PDF leaf 58, printed book page 93, carrying the second half of Kishiwada domain's entry in fascicle 6 of the 1869–70 Dajōkan 藩制一覽表 survey. It records an averaged annual regular rice tax of 29,099.633 koku (正稅) plus 3,686.4111 koku of miscellaneous tax (雜稅) — jointly 32,786.0441 koku, or roughly 49% of the 59,028.3232-koku 合高 printed on the facing recto (p. 92) — alongside 93 villages, 274 shrines and 190 temples. The status-group counts are 華族 8 persons, 士族 552 households / 2,212 persons, 卒 851 households / 2,393 persons, and 平民 12,459 households / 58,748 persons, giving 13,862 households and 63,361 people in all; every 男＋女 split on the page sums exactly to its printed parent total. A five-column note in small type at the head of the page, flagged （原朱） as written in vermilion in the manuscript original, adds 17 Shinto shrine-priest (社家) households, 50 persons, of whom 35 male."
  },
  {
   "id": "kikuma_lower_p059_right",
   "sequence": 358,
   "domain_canonical": "菊間藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "菊間藩",
   "domain_en": "Kikuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p059_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 59,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（菊間）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 6 (Kikuma)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kikuma's opening kokudaka and tax block; Kishiwada's outcaste counts carried over",
   "page_summary_en": "The ○菊間藩 marker opens the Kikuma entry mid-page, with a warichu naming the four provinces its holdings lay in (Kazusa, Echigo, Mikawa, Izu). Kikuma's block runs leftward from there: kokudaka 54,653.55489 koku; regular tax (正租) of 15,623.46883 koku of rice plus 653.54918 kan in ei-sen and 2.776 kan in copper cash; miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 2,162.40931 koku, 2,156.704105 kan, 19.018 momme of silver and 3.007 kan of cash; and a further 653.26 koku of shrine-and-temple land. The two columns to the right of the marker close the PREVIOUS domain, 岸和田藩 (Kishiwada), whose entry ends on the facing page lower_p058_left (printed 93): eta 2,108 persons (1,076 male / 1,032 female) and hinin 241 (89 / 152). The top-margin head-note is Kishiwada's too — 「女子十五人」 completes the red-ink 社家 note begun on p058_left (35 males + 15 females = the 50 persons stated there), and 「外ニ非人二十一人 男九人 女十二人」 adds 21 more hinin."
  },
  {
   "id": "kikuma_lower_p059_left",
   "sequence": 359,
   "domain_canonical": "菊間藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "菊間藩",
   "domain_en": "Kikuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p059_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 59,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（菊間）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran (Domain Administration Survey), Fascicle 6 — (Kikuma). Running header / provenance, printed in the outer (low-x) margin.",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Shrine-temple land taxes and exempt-land breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 95 closes Kikuma domain's fiscal register in fascicle 6, running on from page 94 with no new ○marker, so every column is Kikuma's. It carries two sub-accounts that sit below the domain-level totals recorded on the facing page. First, the shrine-and-temple land account opened there by 外 社寺領高 653.26 koku: a komidaka supplement of 20.87533 koku, of which 35 koku is precinct-exempt and yields no revenue, taxed at 367.59901 koku of rice, 152.3557 kan of ei, 18.985 kan of copper cash and 1.12198 koku of soybeans in regular tax (正租), plus 13.736 koku of rice, 1.3631 kan of ei and 983.228 kan of copper cash in miscellaneous tax (雜稅). Second, the exempt-land account: 除地高 110.323 koku, itemised as 100 + 6.913 + 3.41 koku — a breakdown that sums exactly to the printed total. The 100-koku parcel is the exempt land of Hikozaemon, a peasant of Sanbongi village in Echigo, whose revenue the domain says it will report only after investigation; 6.913 koku is precinct-exempt with no revenue; and the 3.41 koku that does yield revenue bears 0.57288 koku of rice in regular tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "kikuma_lower_p060_right",
   "sequence": 360,
   "domain_canonical": "菊間藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "菊間藩",
   "domain_en": "Kikuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p060_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 60,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（菊間）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Kikuma)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Status households, populations, and religious establishments",
   "page_summary_en": "The tail of Kikuma Domain's fascicle-6 civil register, given over entirely to status households, their populations, and religious establishments. Read right to left, it records shizoku 131 households / 551 persons, quasi-shizoku 191 / 842, sotsu 329 / 1,403, commoners 14,314 / 70,190, and shrine-priest (shake) houses 45 / 239 — every one of the five given with an 内 male/female split that sums exactly to its stated total. The privileged tiers together account for 651 of 15,010 households (4.3%) and 2,796 of 73,225 persons (3.8%), so the commoner block carries roughly 96% of the domain's recorded population. The religious counts close the entry: 202 shrines, 214 Buddhist temples, and 98 Buddhist halls (堂) — note the 45 shake households against 202 shrines, implying most shrines had no resident priestly house."
  },
  {
   "id": "kikuma_lower_p231_right",
   "sequence": 361,
   "domain_canonical": "菊間藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "菊間藩",
   "domain_en": "Kikuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p231_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 231,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（菊間）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Nine (Kikuma)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-nine page carrying the end of the Kishiwada Domain return and the opening of the Kikuma Domain return, divided by the ○菊間藩 marker. To the right of the marker Kishiwada reports one 少參事 and two 權少參事 (Yasui Shitomi, Inui Shinsaku, Hirao Kazuma) and a troop return of 584 men, broken into 126 soldiers in three platoons, an 80-man samurai reserve corps, and 378 rank-and-file in nine platoons, with platoons of 42 men throughout. To the left, Kikuma lists twelve officials across four grades — one 大參事, three 權大參事, four 少參事 and four 權少參事 — with the names printed in an upper and a lower register, and reports 380 riflemen in eight platoons, noting a platoon of 40 men and a company of 80. Three of the six office entries print a second, smaller figure beside or below the first, and in each case that smaller figure, not the larger, equals the number of names actually listed."
  },
  {
   "id": "kitsuki_lower_p061_right",
   "sequence": 362,
   "domain_canonical": "杵築藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "杵築藩",
   "domain_en": "Kitsuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p061_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 61,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（杵築）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 6 (Kitsuki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Residual rice, miscellaneous taxes, households by status",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 98 of fascicle 6 continues the civil register of Kitsuki (杵築藩), a 32,000-koku fudai domain in Bungo province; no ○ marker is printed here — the ○杵築藩 boundary stands on the preceding, unscanned book page 97 — so every column on the leaf belongs to Kitsuki. The page records residual rice of 19,885.6211 koku and miscellaneous taxes of 258.7243 koku of rice plus 1,690 ryō 3 bu 2 shu in cash (with 58 mon 9 bu 7 rin reckoned in ei), then a total of 12,251 households broken out ten ways: 392 hanshi, 300 hansotsu, 5 \"baisotsu\" (which the compiler flags マヽ/sic, apparently for 陪卒), 115 shrine households, 118 celibate-clergy temples, 23 Ikkō-shū temples, 25 Shugendō ascetics, 15 blind priests, 10,771 farmers and 487 merchants — a set that sums exactly to the printed total. The population of 51,535 then opens its own status breakdown, of which only the hanshi line (990 male, 990 female) fits before the register runs on to the next page; that 1,980 matches the shizoku count independently attested for Kitsuki in the Meiji Shiyō."
  },
  {
   "id": "kiyosue_lower_p062_right",
   "sequence": 363,
   "domain_canonical": "清末藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "清末藩",
   "domain_en": "Kiyosue",
   "image": "images/lower_p062_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 62,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（清末）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 6 — (Kiyosue)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kiyosue kokudaka, land tax, and status-group households",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half of PDF spread 62 (printed book page 100) opens the fascicle-6 civil entry for Kiyosue (清末藩), a 10,000-koku Mōri branch house in Nagato province. Kiyosue reports a base kokudaka of 10,000 koku plus 13,091 koku odd of yield newly brought out from new fields (新田打出高), for a total 合高 of 23,091 koku odd; regular land tax (正租) runs 6,888 koku of rice plus 767 kan of cash, with a further 873 kan in miscellaneous taxes (雜稅). Its status counts are 9 kazoku (3 male, 6 female), 195 shizoku households totalling 848 persons (429 male, 419 female), and 165 sotsu households totalling 677 persons (370 male, 307 female) — every male/female pair sums exactly to its printed total. The single column standing to the right of the ○清末藩 marker (華族 6 persons: 3 male, 3 female) is the page-spilled closing field of the preceding domain, Kitsuki (杵築藩), whose block runs back through book pages 97–99."
  },
  {
   "id": "kiyosue_lower_p232_right",
   "sequence": 364,
   "domain_canonical": "清末藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "清末藩",
   "domain_en": "Kiyosue",
   "image": "images/lower_p232_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 232,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（清末）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, ninth fascicle (Kiyosue)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Folio 440 of the ninth fascicle carries the close of Kitsuki Domain's military return and the opening of Kiyosue Domain's entry. The six columns to the right of the ○清末藩 marker are Kitsuki's troop strength: three shizoku platoons at forty men each (120), five sotsu platoons at the same rate (200), an artillery company of 40 and a further 60 officers, under a printed grand total of 426 — six more than its own components sum to. Left of the marker, Kiyosue enters with eight officials in three ranks: one senior councillor (Naitō Chūtarō), two provisional senior councillors (Iki Yosazaemon and Hiroi Shōkichi), and five junior councillors (Hirai Ihachirō, Takano Takumaro, Katami Kojirō, Sakamoto Kenzō and Emoto Kurōkichi). Kiyosue's own military begins in the last column with four infantry platoons of forty men each plus twenty staff, and runs on to the facing leaf, where two artillery sections of ten men each and two more staff complete the return."
  },
  {
   "id": "kiyosaki_lower_p063_right",
   "sequence": 365,
   "domain_canonical": "清崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "清崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Kiyosaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p063_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 63,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（清崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 6 (Kiyosaki section) — running header (provenance)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Five-year average main-tax receipts, itemised",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 102 continues Kiyosaki (Kiyozaki — i.e. Itoigawa in Echigo; 10,000 koku, Matsudaira) domain's fascicle-6 civil register, itemising the five-year average 正租納高 (main land-tax receipts) whose heading stands at the foot of the preceding page-side. Seven 一-marked items run right to left: rice 3,722.2298 koku, being the two-thirds of the collected torimai paid in kind plus the sashimai surcharge; gold 7,238 ryō with 3.678 monme silver, the commuted one-third, equal to 1,682.889 koku of rice; gold 291 ryō with 10.892 monme, the soybean levy commuted to cash, equal to 33.282 koku of soybeans; ei 84 kan 571 mon 1 bu of komononari from Uonuma district (restated as 84 ryō 2 bu + 4.27 monme); silver 11.96785 kanme of komononari from Kubiki district (restated as 199 ryō 1 bu + 12.85 monme); gold 461 ryō 1 bu from the various unjō licence levies; and 54 kan 527 mon of copper cash, likewise unjō. Both cash restatements close exactly at the standard 60-monme-per-ryō rate. The leaf ends with the 1928 editors' note that the next ten lines are red-ink marginalia, and with the red-ink heading 又　庚午調 (\"again — the 1870 survey\"), which opens a second, Kanoe-uma restatement carried onto the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "kiyosaki_lower_p064_right",
   "sequence": 366,
   "domain_canonical": "清崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "清崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Kiyosaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p064_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 64,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（清崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Table of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 6 (Kiyosaki)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Tax revenue and status/household population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues 清崎藩 (Kiyosaki, a small post-Boshin Echigo domain) from its ○-marker two printed pages earlier; no marker appears here, so the whole page is Kiyosaki's. Reading right to left it gives the domain's two tax lines — regular land tax of 5,397.0203 koku in hulled rice (正租現米) and miscellaneous tax of 975.0131 kan in eiraku cash (雜稅永) — then walks down the status register: 5 kazoku (2 male, 3 female), 72 shizoku households holding 359 people (186 male, 173 female), and 46 sotsu households holding 138 people. Below these come 4,046 households, plus 10 shrine-priest houses, 42 temples and 13 Gyōnin-ha ascetic houses marked 外 (\"in addition\"), and a closing population of 21,392 (10,515 male, 10,670 female) — about 5.2 persons across the 4,111 listed houses. Two of the four male/female splits fail to reconcile with their own printed totals (the sotsu 76+65=141 against a printed 138, and the closing 10,515+10,670=21,185 against a printed 21,392), and the editors' vermilion warichu notes at the top flag variant manuscript readings of 11 for the 10 shrine-priest houses and 55 for the 42 temples — signs of a domain return transmitted with unresolved internal disagreement."
  },
  {
   "id": "kiyosaki_lower_p232_left",
   "sequence": 367,
   "domain_canonical": "清崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "清崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Kiyosaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p232_left.jpg",
