   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Kitsuregawa assessed yield with its paddy/upland split, and the average annual land tax in rice, cash and upland grains",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Kitsuregawa (喜連川藩) entry in Fascicle 6: the ○喜連川藩 marker stands at the far right, so the whole page is Kitsuregawa. The domain's assessed yield (高) is 10,209.5195 koku, broken down by the 内 (\"of which\") marker into 5,694.4276 koku of paddy (田方) and 4,515.0919 koku of upland (畑方) — the two components sum to the printed total exactly. Under the 平均 (\"average\") heading the survey itemizes the average annual land-tax take: 1,788.40984 koku of rice (31.4% of the paddy assessment), 102 kan 926.8623 mon in eiraku cash (永) and 1,051 kan 282 mon in copper cash (錢), plus five upland crops rendered in kind — soybeans 102.8964 koku, barnyard millet 82.49035 koku, perilla 1.248 koku, and sesame and adzuki beans at 0.192 koku each. The running header names Kitsuregawa, matching the data, and the bottom margin carries printed book page 107."
  },
  {
   "id": "kitsuregawa_lower_p066_right",
   "sequence": 369,
   "domain_canonical": "喜連川藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "喜連川藩",
   "domain_en": "Kitsuregawa",
   "image": "images/lower_p066_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 66,
