   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第六（喜連川）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 6 (Kitsuregawa)",
   "table_number": 6,
   "page_topic": "Villages, households, population and status-group counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 108 of the Hansei Ichiran, fascicle 6, continuing the return for Kitsuregawa domain (喜連川藩, Shimotsuke) that opened on the preceding leaf (page 107) with its assessed kokudaka of 10,209.5195 koku. The page records 17 villages, 683 households and a population of 3,549 — split 1,752 male and 1,797 female, two figures that sum exactly to the stated total — together with 171 shizoku and 433 shizoku family members. The remaining columns enumerate religious and status groups: 9 Shinto shrine households (38 persons), 4 Shugendō households (16 persons), 11 temples (92 persons), 25 ban-hinin and 28 eta. A head-note in the top margin, （原朱）卒族不詳, states that the sotsu (lower-samurai) figure was left unrecorded in the original manuscript — the single gap in the domain's status return, and the reason no sotsu column is printed between 士族 and 同家族."
  },
  {
