   "pdf_page": 66,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（結城）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Table of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 7 (Yūki)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Yūki opening: territory, kokudaka, land tax + red-ink variant addendum",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf (printed page 百九 = 109) opens fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran-hyō and with it the entry for Yūki domain (結城藩, Shimōsa) — the facing leaf, page 108, is still fascicle 6 (Kitsuregawa). A two-part warichu under the ○結城藩 marker lists Yūki's holdings across four provinces and six districts: Yūki honchō plus 55 villages — 12 in Yūki district (Shimōsa), 10 in Haga and 3 in Tsuga (Shimotsuke), 12 in Makabe and 1 in Ibaraki (Hitachi), 15 in Musha and 2 in Yamabe (Kazusa). The body gives an assessed yield (高) of 26,369.32159 koku and a regular land tax (正租) of 11,370 four-to bales of rice (= 4,548 koku) plus 1,686.112 kan of ei-cash, dated by a vermilion top-margin note to the fourth month of 1870. Four further columns, flagged 以下十行欄外朱書 as a ten-line red-ink marginal addendum quoting \"one [variant] copy,\" report a 支配地總高 of 17,000 koku and restate the same rice and cash figures — exactly — as five-year averages."
  },
  {
   "id": "yuki_lower_p067_right",
   "sequence": 371,
   "domain_canonical": "結城藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "結城藩",
   "domain_en": "Yūki",
   "image": "images/lower_p067_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 67,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（結城）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview Table, Fascicle 7 (Yūki)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Product-tax ledger, shrines and temples, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "The middle leaf (printed page 110) of Yūki domain's fascicle-7 return, carrying no maru-marker: the ○結城藩 marker stands on page 109 and the block runs on to page 111. The right half reproduces Yūki's own Product-Tax Investigation Ledger (産物稅取調帳): 35 ryō from the Yūki-town pongee-and-cotton wholesalers Tahei and Chōemon, 3 bu from the Kubota-village brokers Gonbei, Hanjūrō and Kyūzaburō, totalled with a 〆 mark at 35 ryō 3 bu and repeated in the 雜稅 field — a trivial 35.75 ryō of commercial revenue against a 17,000-koku domain — followed by the declaration that silkworm eggs, white cotton and everything else went untaxed. The left half gives the establishment and demographic counts: 206 shrines, 36 halls, 116 temples, 3,452 households and 17,192 persons. The population resolves in an unusual way: the 内 split of 8,682 males and 8,337 females covers only the lay population, and the 173-person remainder is made up exactly by the separately enumerated religious and professional categories (13 Shinto priests and 3 shrine attendants here; 128 monks, 10 physicians, 6 mountain ascetics, 4 blind performers, 8 lay devotees and 1 shugendō practitioner on the facing leaf)."
  },
  {
   "id": "yuki_lower_p067_left",
   "sequence": 372,
   "domain_canonical": "結城藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "結城藩",
   "domain_en": "Yūki",
   "image": "images/lower_p067_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 67,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（結城）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Yūki)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Status & household registers (shizoku, eta, clergy)",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of PDF page 67 (printed book-page 111) completes Yūki Domain's household-and-population register in fascicle 7, continuing the 内 (\"of which\") breakdown of the commoner population begun on the facing right page. Six occupational/religious categories are itemised — 僧 128, 醫師 10, 道心 8, 山伏 6, 座頭 4, 修驗 1 — after which the 外 marker opens the registers counted outside the commoner totals: 穢多 60 households / 278 persons (男 146 + 女 132 = 278 ✓) and 鉦打 4 households / 6 persons (男 4 + 女 2 = 6 ✓). The samurai register follows: 士卒戸數 231 households, itemised under 内 as 133 shizoku + 74 sotsu + 24 households under kinshin (house-arrest), summing exactly to 231; their population is 950 persons, of whom 士族妻子 (shizoku wives and children) number 289 male + 324 female = 613. The remaining status lines (卒族同斷 256, 謹愼同斷 82) print on p068R to the right of the ○湯長谷藩 marker and therefore still belong to Yūki; those three lines sum to 951 against the printed total of 950 — a one-person inconsistency in the source."
  },
