   "sequence": 373,
   "domain_canonical": "結城藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "結城藩",
   "domain_en": "Yūki",
   "image": "images/lower_p233_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 233,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（喜連川、結城、湯長谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Kitsuregawa, Yūki, Yunagaya)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 leaf carrying the officials and military returns of three small eastern domains. Kitsuregawa's entry consists of the single note 審ナラス — nothing about its offices or its troops was ascertained. Yūki's entry, which fills most of the leaf, records one senior councillor (大參事), a provisional senior councillorship with an establishment of two of which one was filled at the time, a junior councillorship with an establishment of four, and a provisional junior councillorship, followed by an eleven-man roster of named officeholders set in two lower registers, and then the domain's forces: one infantry company of sixty men with sixty rifles. Yunagaya's entry opens on the far left with 大參事　欠員 — its senior councillorship stood vacant. The printed page number is 四百四十二 (442)."
  },
  {
   "id": "yunagaya_lower_p068_right",
   "sequence": 374,
   "domain_canonical": "湯長谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "湯長谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Yunagaya",
   "image": "images/lower_p068_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 68,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（湯長谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 — (Yunagaya)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Yunagaya kokudaka and five-year-average land tax; tail of Yūki's dependant counts and standing troops",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 百十二 (112) of fascicle 7 opens the entry for 湯長谷藩 (Yunagaya, Iwaki) at an ○湯長谷藩 marker roughly mid-leaf. Yunagaya's assessed yield is 壹萬四千石 (14,000 koku), drawn from 31 villages in Iwaki Province (Iwasaki and Kikuta districts) and 3 villages in Tanba Province (Hikami and Ikaruga districts), plus a further 1,223.019 koku of reclaimed and resurvey-added land; its five-year-average land tax is 2,927.7373 koku of rice, 194.064 koku of soybeans, 570 kan 885 mon 1 bu in ei, 1,037 ryō 3 shu in gold, and 426 mon in copper cash — a vermilion note in the top margin cautions that these are the two provinces' combined figures. Everything to the right of the marker is the tail of 結城藩 (Yūki), carried over from printed page 111: the male and female dependants of the sotsu (144 and 112) and of those under kinshin confinement (40 and 41), whose totals (256 and 81) close exactly against Yūki's 人員九百五十人 with the 613 shizoku dependants on the facing page. Yūki's entry ends with its standing force — one infantry platoon of 60 men and 60 rifles — flagged by an editorial note that the two lines following were written in vermilion in the original."
  },
  {
   "id": "yunagaya_lower_p068_left",
   "sequence": 375,
   "domain_canonical": "湯長谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "湯長谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Yunagaya",
   "image": "images/lower_p068_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 68,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（湯長谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 7 — Yunagaya section (running header; provenance, not data)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Yunagaya han — unjō/miscellaneous tax receipts and status-group household & population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page is the interior of the 湯長谷藩 (Yunagaya, Iwaki, 14,000 koku) block in fascicle 7 of the 藩制一覧表. Its right half records non-land tax receipts: 65 ryō of komononari miscellaneous tax, then 220.5 ryō in gold plus 4.671 kan in ei and 1,329.406 kan in copper cash, with split-column notes assigning the gold to unjō on coal and sundries (石炭諸運上) and the cash to unjō on assorted goods (品々運上) — coal dues being the signature revenue of a domain sitting on the Jōban coalfield. Its left half is the status census: 85 shizoku households holding 359 persons (男160 + 女199), 25 sotsu households holding 80 persons (男41 + 女39), 38 komono menials, and 1,905 commoner households, of which 16 are shrine-priest (社家) and 4 are shugendō (修驗) households. Both male/female splits reconcile exactly to their printed totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "miharu_lower_p070_left",
   "sequence": 376,
   "domain_canonical": "三春藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三春藩",
   "domain_en": "Miharu",
   "image": "images/lower_p070_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 70,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（三春）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Miharu (三春藩): kokudaka and land taxes",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Miharu's kokudaka (草高 = 本田 + 新田) and its 正租 / 雜 land-tax block, opening at the ○三春藩 marker",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-leaf (book page 117) of the seventh fascicle opens Miharu domain's (三春藩) civil entry: the ○三春藩 marker stands mid-page, and everything to its left is Miharu's. The headline kokudaka (草高) is 61,740.8208 koku, resolving exactly into 50,002.692 koku of established fields (本田 — effectively the domain's nominal 50,000-koku rating) and 11,738.1288 koku of newly opened fields (新田). The tax block records regular land tax (正租) of 10,749.12044 koku rendered in rice (米納) plus 13,805.17978 koku assessed for cash commutation (金納) — together 39.8 percent of 草高, close to the conventional four-tenths rate — the cash itself given as 4,026.3879 ryō (此金) and restated as 503.29849 koku of rice (此米) at the eight-ryō-per-koku rate declared in the 但石八兩立 note; a miscellaneous levy (雜) of 602.31763 koku of rice closes the leaf, and these lines sum exactly to the 12,581.34-koku 合米 total printed on the next leaf. The four columns to the right of the marker are not Miharu's but the tail of Mito domain's (水戸藩) entry: shrine land (社領) of 1,003 koku with a current assessment of 1,071.712, and temple land (寺領) of 1,152.6 koku with a current assessment of 1,501.127."
  },
  {
   "id": "miharu_lower_p071_right",
   "sequence": 377,
   "domain_canonical": "三春藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三春藩",
   "domain_en": "Miharu",
   "image": "images/lower_p071_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 71,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（三春）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Miharu) — running header",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Miharu domain: cash tax, total tax-rice, households, population and status-group counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 118 of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 7 — the second and final civil-economy page of the Miharu (三春) block, which opens with the ○三春藩 marker on the facing page 117 and gives way to ○宮津藩 on the next page 119. The page closes the domain's tax accounts (miscellaneous cash levy 5,812.8275 ryō; its rice equivalent 726.60344 koku at the printed rate of 8 ryō per koku; grand total 合米 12,581.34 koku) and then reports demography: 7,253 commoner households and 38,619 people, 904 shizoku-and-sotsu households and 2,724 people counted separately (外ニ), plus small status groups — 79 shrine-priest households (458 people), 109 temples (130 clergy), 6 Shugendō households (32 people), 3 Hiruko households, and 12 outcaste households (63 people). The rice arithmetic closes exactly: the four printed 米 figures across pages 117–118 (10,749.12044 + 503.29849 + 602.31763 + 726.60344) sum to the 合米 total of 12,581.34, which also confirms the cash figure as 5,812.8275 ryō. The headline 人口 does not close: the printed male (17,034) and female (16,156) split sums to 33,190, some 5,429 short of the printed 38,619, and two small printed ink marks sit against the very digits (八 and 九) that the shortfall implicates."
  },
  {
   "id": "miyazu_lower_p071_left",
   "sequence": 378,
   "domain_canonical": "宮津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宮津藩",
   "domain_en": "Miyazu",
   "image": "images/lower_p071_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 71,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（宮津）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table (fascicle) 7 — (Miyazu)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Miharu's samurai-class demographics and military tail; opening of Miyazu's kokudaka block",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 119 of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 7 (藩制一覽表第七) records the junction of two domain entries. The five columns right of the ○宮津藩 marker close out 三春藩 (Miharu, Mutsu): five infantry platoons at 60 men each (300 troops), one and a half artillery sections, 445 shizoku households / 1,587 persons (783 male, 804 female), 459 sotsu households / 1,137 persons (630 male, 507 female), and a 20-koku 受領高 — household and population figures that sum exactly to the 904 households and 2,724 persons p071R reports as Miharu's aggregate samurai class, confirming the attribution. Left of the marker, 宮津藩 (Miyazu, Tango) opens with 草高 70,718.194 koku, resolved as 高 70,000 plus 718.194 koku of 新田改出高, against which 内 itemises deductions of 5,402.784 koku (永荒地・鍬下引, five-year average) and 127.073 koku (社寺寄附地), totalling 合 5,529.857 — the subtraction that yields the 殘 65,188.337 koku printed as Miyazu's first field on p072R. A run of three isolated glyphs (州・傳・寺) prints low in the 受領高 column; it is genuine ink but belongs to no field."
  },
  {
   "id": "miyazu_lower_p072_right",
   "sequence": 379,
   "domain_canonical": "宮津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宮津藩",
   "domain_en": "Miyazu",
   "image": "images/lower_p072_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 72,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（宮津）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Miyazu section) — running header (provenance)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Miyazu land-tax totals and household/population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 120 lies wholly inside the Miyazu (宮津藩) block of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 7: the ○宮津藩 marker stands on printed page 119 and the next marker, ○水口藩, on page 121, so no domain boundary falls on this leaf and every column is Miyazu's. The tax half carries the remainder figure 殘 65,188.337 koku forward from the preceding page and then itemises the levy — regular land tax 25,295.164 koku, miscellaneous tax rice 1,843.366 koku, and miscellaneous tax cash 1,284.736 kan, the last converted at almost exactly 50 kan per koku into the 但現米 note of 25.695 koku; the three rice figures sum precisely to the 都合米 total of 27,164.225 koku, or 41.7 per cent of the 殘 base. The demographic half records 520 shizoku households (2,298 persons) and 311 sotsu households (1,048 persons) ahead of a general count of 14,579 households and 65,696 people, whose printed male/female split of 32,976 and 32,720 reconciles to the total exactly. A closing entry places 200 households of Kūyadō-school mendicant-bowl practitioners (hachitataki) outside the ordinary household roll."
  },
  {
   "id": "minakuchi_lower_p072_left",
   "sequence": 380,
   "domain_canonical": "水口藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "水口藩",
   "domain_en": "Minakuchi",
   "image": "images/lower_p072_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 72,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（水口）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 — Minakuchi section (running header, provenance)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Miyazu status-group demography and troops; opening of the Minakuchi kokudaka/tax block",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 121 of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 7 straddles two domains, divided by the ○水口藩 maru-marker at mid-page. Right of the marker the page completes 宮津藩 (Miyazu)'s status-group demography: the 1,021 persons (M 529 / F 492) of the 200 Kūya-dō alms-practitioner households carried over from p.120, then 非人 58 households / 275 persons (M 137 / F 138), 穢多 162 households / 949 persons (M 482 / F 467), 社人 51 households / 188 persons (M 98 / F 90), 227 temples housing 442 people (377 monks, 7 nuns, 58 women), and a standing force of 239 troops. Left of the marker the 水口藩 (Minakuchi, Ōmi) block opens with 表高 25,000 koku, a 込高新田 new-field increment of 1,491.88614 koku, 正租 land tax of 11,333.161 koku of rice, and 雜稅 miscellaneous tax of 363.418 koku — a regular tax take of about 42.8% of the implied 26,491.886-koku gross. Every male/female and status split on the leaf sums exactly to its printed total, and that arithmetic net is what exposed two MASTER transcription errors (非人 male, 穢多 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "minakuchi_lower_p073_right",
   "sequence": 381,
   "domain_canonical": "水口藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "水口藩",
   "domain_en": "Minakuchi",
   "image": "images/lower_p073_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 73,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（水口）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table Seven (Minakuchi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Minakuchi households, population and status/clergy breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the demographic block of 水口藩 (Minakuchi, Omi province) in Table 7 of the Hansei Ichiran, opening with a currency remainder (金一分 = 0.25 ryo plus eisen 10 kan 532.333 mon, and 錢一貫文) carried over from the preceding leaf. Minakuchi returns 4,704 households and a population printed as 20,356, against male 10,154 and female 10,196 which sum to 20,350 — a six-person discrepancy the compilers marked with a 〔ママ〕 (\"sic\") glyph. The 内 breakdown gives 356 shizoku households holding 1,391 people (718 male, 673 female) and 88 sotsu households holding 150 people (96 male, 54 female), both of which reconcile exactly. Religious and outcast counts close the page: 5 shake, 5 onmyoji and 9 yamabushi households against a combined 94 persons (a second 〔ママ〕 — the 39/59 split sums to 98), 98 temples with 76 monks of whom 51 are Shinshu plus 44 women, and 63 hinin (32 male, 31 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "mibu_lower_p073_left",
   "sequence": 382,
   "domain_canonical": "壬生藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "壬生藩",
   "domain_en": "Mibu",
   "image": "images/lower_p073_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 73,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（壬生）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 7 — Mibu (壬生藩): opening of the Mibu block (assessed yield, households, population); the columns right of the marker close out Minakuchi.",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mibu kokudaka, households and population; Minakuchi's closing outcaste, shrine and military columns",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Mibu (壬生藩) entry in Fascicle 7 of the 1870 domain survey: the ○壬生藩 marker sits at mid-page and everything to its left is Mibu's. Mibu reports an assessed yield (草高) of 49,061.9401 koku — its formal 30,000-koku kokudaka plus 19,061.9401 koku of yield disclosed by cadastral survey and new-field revision (檢地出高・新田改出込高), which sum exactly to the total — together with 3,288 households spread across the two provinces of Shimotsuke and Shimōsa (野總二州) and a population of 18,213 (9,300 men, 8,913 women). The columns to the right of the marker close out the preceding Minakuchi (水口藩) entry, running on from p.122: 410 outcaste (穢多) persons (208 men, 202 women), 86 shrines (神社), two 50-man infantry platoons plus 28 men from the commander down, a 24-man artillery unit (砲隊) and 20 drum-and-fife players (鼓笛手). Minakuchi's block then ends with a small appended holding of 29.3 koku attributed to the temple Daitoku-ji (大德寺), whose five-year average regular tax (正税五ヶ年平均) is 6.8416 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "mibu_lower_p074_right",
   "sequence": 383,
   "domain_canonical": "壬生藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "壬生藩",
   "domain_en": "Mibu",
   "image": "images/lower_p074_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 74,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（壬生）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Table of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 7 (Mibu)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mibu domain demographic return: households, population, status and outcaste sub-counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 124 of fascicle 7 continues the household-and-population return for Mibu Domain (壬生藩, Shimotsuke); the ○壬生藩 marker stands on the facing page 123 and the next marker (○三日月藩) does not appear until page 125, so every column here belongs to Mibu. Reading right to left, the page first closes out the Shimotsuke–Shimōsa (野總二州) holding carried over from page 123 with its outcaste supplements — eta, 169 persons in 34 households (95 male, 75 female), and hinin, 25 persons — and then records a village count of 91, which the 1928 editors gloss as 欄外朱書 (added in red in the margin of the manuscript). A second territorial block follows for the Yamato–Harima (和播二州) exclaves: 1,119 households and 5,353 persons (3,718 male, 2,635 female), plus onbō 28 persons in 5 households and hinin 13 households / 16 persons. The page closes with the domain-wide status groups — shizoku 207 households and 827 persons, sotsu 230 households and 866 persons, and shrine personnel 23 households and 121 persons — and carries two editorial （ママ） \"sic\" marks where the printed totals fail to match their own male/female splits (169 against 170, and 5,353 against 6,353)."
  },
  {
   "id": "mibu_lower_p074_left",
   "sequence": 384,
   "domain_canonical": "壬生藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "壬生藩 / ○三日月藩",
   "domain_en": "Mibu",
   "image": "images/lower_p074_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 74,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（三日月）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覽表), Fascicle 7 — the printed header names 三日月 (Mikazuki), the domain that only OPENS on this leaf; most of the page is the tail of Mibu (壬生藩). Provenance, not an attribution of the data.",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Close of Mibu's religious-personnel register plus its red-ink army note, then the opening kokudaka and land-tax columns of ○三日月藩 (Mikazuki)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left leaf of PDF spread 74 (printed page 百二十五 = 125, fascicle 7) spans a domain boundary at its single ○三日月藩 marker. Everything to the RIGHT of the marker closes Mibu's (壬生藩) civil register: 117 temples (寺) and 78 shrines (社); 84 Buddhist clergy (僧), broken out as 75 male and 9 female; 4 nuns (尼); 6 shugen/yamabushi households (修驗) totalling 25 people (11 male, 14 female); and 6 gong-beater households (鉦打) totalling 10 people (7 male, 3 female). A bracketed editorial note, （以下二行欄外朱書）, flags that the next two lines stood in red ink in the manuscript margin: 12 infantry companies at 30 men each (兵隊十二小隊〔一隊三十人〕), totalling 合三百六十人 = 360 troops — the arithmetic closes exactly. To the LEFT of the marker, Mikazuki (三日月藩), a small Mori house in Harima, opens its entry with an official kokudaka of 15,000 koku (高 壹萬五千石), a further 560.487 koku of newly opened land (外ニ … 新開地), and a main land tax (正租) of 7,498.10954 koku of rice plus 1,397.8906 koku of soybeans."
  },
  {
   "id": "mikazuki_lower_p075_right",
   "sequence": 385,
   "domain_canonical": "三日月藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三日月藩 / ○峯山藩",
   "domain_en": "Mikazuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p075_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 75,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（峯山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覽表), Fascicle 7 — the printed header names 峯山 (Mineyama), the domain that only OPENS on this leaf at its ○ marker; ten of the page's thirteen substantive columns are the tail of Mikazuki (三日月藩). Provenance, not an attribution of the data.",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mikazuki's household, population and status register, then the opening kokudaka of ○峯山藩 (Mineyama)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 126 of fascicle 7 closes the civil register of Mikazuki Domain (三日月藩, a 15,000-koku Mori house in Harima) and then opens the entry for Mineyama (峯山藩) at the page's single ○ marker. Everything right of that marker is Mikazuki's: a miscellaneous cash tax (雜稅) of 484 kan 641 mon; shizoku, 156 households and 679 persons (344 male, 335 female); sotsu, 155 households and 664 persons (340 male, 324 female); a domain total of 4,823 households and 17,945 persons (9,459 male, 8,486 female); 12 shrine-personnel households holding 55 people (27 male, 28 female); 54 temples, hermitages and shugendō establishments housing 112 religious (64 monks, 21 nuns, 27 women); and an army of three platoons. Left of the marker Mineyama opens with an assessed kokudaka of 11,144.441 koku plus a further 155 koku of newly opened paddy and dry field. Every male/female pair on the page sums exactly to its printed total and the temple breakdown closes on 112, while Mineyama's two figures reconcile precisely with the 合高 of 11,537.331 koku on the facing leaf (page 127) once its 237.89 koku of 込高 is added — a cross-page check that also shows the facing leaf's fiscal columns belong to Mineyama, not to Mikazuki."
  },
  {
   "id": "mikazuki_lower_p235_left",
   "sequence": 386,
   "domain_canonical": "三日月藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三日月藩",
   "domain_en": "Mikazuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p235_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 235,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（三日月、峰山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, ninth fascicle (Mikazuki, Mineyama)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-9 officials roster and troop return",
   "page_summary_en": "Folio 447 of the ninth Hansei Ichiran fascicle, the register of domain officials and troops. The leaf opens at the right with a 73-man staff supplement (外ニ役員七十三人) that closes Mibu domain's return from the facing recto, then the ○三日月藩 marker starts Mikazuki (Mori house, Harima, 15,000 koku). Mikazuki's roster runs through four councillor grades — 大參事 二人, 權大參事 一人, 少參事 二人 and 權少參事 with no figure printed — and names nine men, from Imamura Matauemon down to Kishi Heisuke; its troop return is 兵隊三小隊 with a half-size double-column note fixing a platoon at roughly twenty-five men apart from officers, so about 75 men in all. Two compiler's marks sit in the margins: a reduced-type 三人 beside 權大參事 一人, which matches the three men actually named there, and a parenthesised マ (sic) beside 少參事 二人, where only one man is named. The ○峰山藩 marker then starts Mineyama (Kyōgoku house, Tango), whose 大參事 一人 and 權大參事 二人（五人）head four named appointees before the roster carries over to folio 448."
  },
  {
   "id": "mineyama_lower_p075_left",
   "sequence": 387,
   "domain_canonical": "峯山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "峯山藩",
   "domain_en": "Mineyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p075_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 75,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（峯山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Mineyama)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mineyama domain assessed yield and land-tax revenue (fascicle 7)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page is the tax half of 峯山藩's (Mineyama, Tango province) entry in fascicle 7 of the 藩制一覧表, printed book page 127. It closes the domain's assessment — a 込高 supplement of 237.89 koku lifting the 合高 to 11,537.331 koku — then sets out revenue in three blocks: 正租 (regular land tax) at 5,955.63293 koku of rice, 47.5 ryō gold, 730.1 mon ei and 481 mon copper cash; 雜稅 (miscellaneous taxes) at 67.124 koku, 1 ryō, 6,323.02 mon ei and 1,426 mon cash; and the 正雜合 combined total at 6,022.75693 koku, 48.5 ryō and 7,053.12 mon ei, each carrying a conversion note (此米, 此金). Every component sums exactly to its printed total, and the 合高 reconciles with the 高 (11,144.441 koku) and 新田畑 (155 koku) printed on the facing right-hand page. The block overruns the foot of this page and finishes on lower_p076_right, which carries the combined group's copper-cash total and the closing 合米."
  },
  {
   "id": "mineyama_lower_p076_right",
   "sequence": 388,
   "domain_canonical": "峯山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "峯山藩",
   "domain_en": "Mineyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p076_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 76,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（峯山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey, Fascicle 7 (Mineyama)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Tax conversion tail and household/population register",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 128 of the Hansei Ichiran, fascicle 7, carrying the closing revenue lines and the complete household/population register of Mineyama Domain (峯山藩). The revenue tail restates a copper-cash levy of 1 kan 911 mon as 3 shu 35 mon in gold and 0.02413 koku in rice, adds a further 0.88164 koku carried over from the preceding leaf, and closes with a combined rice total (合米) of 6,029.72502 koku. The register reports 1,754 households and 9,337 people (4,556 male, 4,781 female), including 65 shizoku households with 250 people and 127 sotsu households with 383 people; the shizoku figure carries an editorial （ママ）\"sic\" because its own male/female split sums to 251. Four status groups are listed separately: 9 shrine-attendant (社人) households with 33 people, 26 temples with 52 people, 17 hachiuchi (鉢打) households with 82 people, and 1 chasen (茶筅) household with 8 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "mineyama_lower_p236_right",
   "sequence": 389,
   "domain_canonical": "峯山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "峯山藩",
   "domain_en": "Mineyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p236_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 236,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百四十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（三上）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 9 — running head names Mikami (三上藩); the leaf carries the tail of Mineyama's (峯山藩) officials roster and the opening of Mikami's",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Officials roster and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-9 half-leaf, printed page 448, carries the tail of Mineyama Domain's (峯山藩) officials roster and the opening of Mikami Domain's (三上藩), the two separated by the ○三上藩 marker at x973-1063. Twelve Mineyama names stand to the right of that marker: Shibasaki Shichirobē, the fifth acting senior councillor (權大參事) of a group whose heading and first four names print on the preceding leaf; seven junior councillors (少參事) under a heading that prints 二人 with the 1928 editor's マヽ \"sic\" marks beside the figure; and four acting junior councillors (權少參事) under a heading with no count printed. Mineyama's military line closes its entry with 兵隊　二小隊 — two companies, no headcount given — the one element of this page already held in MASTER. Left of the marker, Mikami's entry opens with one senior councillor (粥川小十郎), two acting senior councillors (神山雪江 and 塚本九一郎), one junior councillor (水谷榮三郎) and one acting junior councillor (餌取傳), none of the four headings carrying a printed person-count."
  },
  {
   "id": "mikkaichi_lower_p076_left",
   "sequence": 390,
   "domain_canonical": "三日市藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三日市藩",
   "domain_en": "Mikkaichi",
   "image": "images/lower_p076_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 76,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（三日市）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Mikkaichi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka build-up, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of spread 76 (printed book page 129, fascicle 7) opens the entry for 三日市藩 (Mikkaichi), a 10,000-koku Yanagisawa domain in Echigo. The three columns standing to the right of the ○三日市藩 marker still belong to the preceding domain, 峯山藩 (Mineyama, whose block occupies the facing right half at book page 128): 穢多 60 households / 255 people, 非人番 11 households / 55 people, and a 兵隊 of two platoons. Mikkaichi's own block builds its assessment from a base 高 of 10,000 koku plus 込高 101.3967 and 改出新田 1,213.101, printed as a 合高 of 11,314.4077 koku, from which 273.7095 koku is deducted for landslide, river-washout and sand-inundation losses (山崩川欠砂入引), leaving a 殘 of 11,040.6982 koku. The domain records 1,505 households and a population of 8,224 (4,164 male, 4,060 female), of whom 107 are shizoku."
  },
  {
   "id": "miyagawa_lower_p077_right",
   "sequence": 391,
   "domain_canonical": "宮川藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宮川藩",
   "domain_en": "Miyagawa",
   "image": "images/lower_p077_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 77,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（宮川）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Table of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 7 — (Miyagawa). Provenance only; on this leaf it agrees with the main data, since Miyagawa's entry opens here at the ○宮川藩 marker.",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Close of the Mikkaichi civil block, then Miyagawa's opening kokudaka, land tax, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 130 of fascicle 7 spans a domain boundary at its single ○宮川藩 marker. The five columns to the RIGHT of the marker close out the Mikkaichi (三日市藩, Echigo) block that opens on the facing page: 48 villages, 10 Buddhist temples, an eta (outcaste) return of 1 household and 13 persons, 38 sotsu-rank retainers, and an army of two platoons totalling 80 men. To the LEFT of the marker, Miyagawa (宮川藩, Ōmi Province) opens its civil register with a base assessment of 13,000 koku plus 198.3078 koku of re-surveyed newly reclaimed land, against which it returns a regular land tax of 4,139.69206 koku of rice — a nominal take of 31.8 percent of the base kokudaka — and miscellaneous taxes of just 25.7813 koku. The domain records 1,586 households and 6,735 people, or about 4.25 persons per household; the half-size male/female split below the total gives 3,307 men and 3,428 women, which sums exactly to the printed figure."
  },
  {
   "id": "miyagawa_lower_p077_left",
   "sequence": 392,
   "domain_canonical": "宮川藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宮川藩",
   "domain_en": "Miyagawa",
   "image": "images/lower_p077_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 77,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（峯岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 7 (Mineoka)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Status-group population, shrines and temples; kokudaka, land tax and demography",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes Miyagawa domain's fascicle-7 entry and opens Mineoka's. Miyagawa's tail, occupying the two-thirds of the page right of the ○峯岡藩 marker, registers 60 temples (74 monks, 50 women, 2 nuns) and 46 shrines, then its samurai-class establishment: shizoku 145 men and 167 women, sotsu 70 men and 12 women, and 40 fusotsu (porter-attendants), which the following column totals as 右戸數 — 95 households, 434 persons — a sum that reconciles exactly (312 + 82 + 40 = 434). Two outcaste groups close the block: 41 eta (23 male, 18 female) and 6 hinin (2 male, 4 female). Left of the marker, Mineoka enters at 15,071.145 koku assessed yield against 4,393.9743 koku of land-tax rice (29.2 per cent), with 1,976 households and a printed population of 11,040 — a figure that sits 60 above its own male/female split of 5,385 and 5,595, an inconsistency in the source itself rather than a transcription error."
  },
  {
   "id": "miyagawa_lower_p237_right",
   "sequence": 393,
   "domain_canonical": "宮川藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宮川藩",
   "domain_en": "Miyagawa",
   "image": "images/lower_p237_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 237,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百五十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（峯岡、三草）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 9 (Mineoka, Mikusa)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of Fascicle 9 closes one domain's entry and opens two more. The columns standing to the right of the ○峯岡藩 marker finish Miyagawa Domain's roster of councillors and then give its forces: one rifle platoon of 71 men, 11 of them officers, and one artillery section of 14. Miyagawa's acting senior councillorship is printed as 一人 but carries a small-type 三人 beside it and lists three men, while the junior councillorship is printed as 五人 with the editor's sic mark （マヽ）against only three names. Mineoka Domain receives a marker and nothing else — the editorial note reads 峯岡藩原書記載ナシ, \"no entry for Mineoka in the original manuscript\" — and Mikusa Domain follows with six named officials across three grades and no headcounts printed at all, three of the six surnamed Niwa."
  },
  {
   "id": "mineoka_lower_p078_right",
   "sequence": 394,
   "domain_canonical": "峯岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三草藩",
   "domain_en": "Mineoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p078_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 78,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（三草）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 — (Mikusa)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mineoka's status/population tail and the opening of Mikusa's kokudaka and land-tax block",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 133 of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 7 carries two domains. To the right of the ○三草藩 marker the survey finishes 峯岡藩 (Mineoka, Awa; entry opened on the preceding leaf): 66 shizoku households totalling 334 people, 62 sotsu households totalling 325, one shrine-priest household of 3, 15 temples housing 127 (49 monks plus 42 men and 36 women), 6 eta households of 48, 68 shrines, and a military establishment of just 58 men. To the left of the marker 三草藩 (Mikusa, Harima) opens with a sōdaka of 10,379.05068 koku, which the page itself decomposes exactly into a base 高 of 10,000 koku plus 379.05068 koku of komidaka new fields — the arithmetic signature of a minimum-threshold 10,000-koku domain — against a regular land tax (正租) of 4,678.56896 koku of rice and a miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 158.7226 koku. One figure does not reconcile: Mineoka's sotsu male 159 and female 66 sum to 225 against a printed population of 325, a hundred-koku-style dropped-digit error in the source itself (325 − 159 = 166), recorded here verbatim rather than silently corrected."
  },
  {
   "id": "mikusa_lower_p078_left",
   "sequence": 395,
   "domain_canonical": "三草藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三草藩",
   "domain_en": "Mikusa",
   "image": "images/lower_p078_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 78,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（三池）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 7 — (Miike)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Mikusa domain's population/status/temple/military tail, then the opening of Miike domain's kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 133 of fascicle 7 carries the tail of Mikusa domain's return (Harima; kusadaka 10,379.05068 koku per the facing page) and then opens Miike's. Mikusa is recorded with 1,976 households against a printed population of 8,961; its retainer body was 79 shizoku households (309 persons) and 75 sotsu households (188 persons), alongside 9 temples with 10 cloisters and 15 monks, 3 shrine-attendant households, 5 Gyōnin-ha households and 4 eta households (23 persons); its force was three platoons totalling 126 men, and the block closes with 10 koku of former vermilion-seal land held by Okuyama-dera. The ○三池藩 maru-marker then opens Miike's block with a kusadaka of 11,997.38574 koku. Two readings depart from the project's MASTER file — the female population is 女四千三百十四人 (4,314, not 4,344) and Miike's kusadaka is 千九百九十七 (11,997.38574, not 11,977.38574) — and the printed population total falls 129 short of its own male/female split."
  },
  {
   "id": "miike_lower_p079_right",
   "sequence": 396,
   "domain_canonical": "三池藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三池藩",
   "domain_en": "Miike",
   "image": "images/lower_p079_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 79,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（三池）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Miike section)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Land tax + coal tax, Chikugo & Iwashiro holdings",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues Miike's fascicle-7 civil entry: it carries NO maru-marker of its own (the ○三池藩 marker sits on the preceding page, lower_p078_left), so every column on it belongs to Miike. It splits the domain's assessed land into its two scattered holdings — 5,071.80144 koku across five villages in Chikugo Province and 6,925.5843 koku across six villages in Date District, Iwashiro Province — and for each prints the regular land tax (Chikugo: 860.95657 koku rice, 605.10844 koku ōgome, 278.70642 koku soybeans; Iwashiro: 1,727.9909 koku rice plus 246.8558 kan in Eiraku cash) and the miscellaneous taxes. The page closes with the tax on the Miike coal mines: 2,526.8458 ryō in gold, converted at the printed rate of 8 ryō per koku into 315.85573 koku of hulled rice. Two independent arithmetic nets confirm the readings — the two territory kokudaka sum to exactly the 草高 of 11,997.38574 koku printed on lower_p078_left, and the coal-tax gold divided by 8 reproduces the printed 此現米 to the 才 place."
  },
  {
   "id": "miike_lower_p079_left",
   "sequence": 397,
   "domain_canonical": "三池藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "三池藩",
   "domain_en": "Miike",
   "image": "images/lower_p079_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 79,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（三池）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Miike)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Miike domain households, population and status breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf of the 三池藩 (Miike) entry in fascicle 7, carrying the domain's demographic return with no maru-marker of its own. Miike reports 1,757 households and a population of 8,961 (4,508 male, 4,453 female); the 内 (\"of which\") breakdown that follows lists 123 shizoku households with 503 persons (251 male, 252 female), 63 sotsu households with 183 persons (97 male, 86 female), and 16 eta households with 78 persons (35 male, 43 female) — a selective subset rather than an exhaustive partition. The religious fields record 24 shrines, while the 寺 (temples) field prints its label with no figure at all. The page closes with two lines the editors flag as vermilion in the original (以下二行原朱書), enclosed in a single bracket spanning both columns: 68 heishi and 38 heisotsu, 106 men under arms."
  },
  {
   "id": "shizuoka_lower_p080_right",
   "sequence": 398,
   "domain_canonical": "静岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "靜岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Shizuoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p080_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 80,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（靜岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 7 (Shizuoka)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka and land-tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Hansei Ichiran fascicle-7 (fiscal) entry for Shizuoka Domain — the 700,000-koku holding granted to the Tokugawa house under Tokugawa Iesato after the Restoration — and records a total assessed yield (高) of 699,182.24817 koku across Suruga (7 districts), Mikawa (7 districts) and Tōtōmi (11 districts). A further 538.81 koku is entered as 外 (\"outside\" the assessment), with an interlinear note explaining that this land had not yet been transferred from Toyohashi Domain and that an inquiry over its receipt was still pending. Regular land tax (正稅) is returned as 185,738.02411 koku of rice plus 2.265 koku of soybeans and three cash lines — 1,239.775387 kan in eiraku reckoning, 9,336.357 kan in bita (debased copper), and 123.04 kan in coin; miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) add 22,668.50006 koku of rice, 469.03184 koku of barley, 422.56086 koku of soybeans and 0.24 koku of adzuki beans, with the schedule continuing on the facing page. Rice alone thus amounts to roughly 29.8% of the assessed yield. An editorial note in red ink dates the return to the tenth month of the kanoe-uma year (Meiji 3 / 1870)."
  },
  {
   "id": "shizuoka_lower_p080_left",
   "sequence": 399,
   "domain_canonical": "静岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "靜岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Shizuoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p080_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 80,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（靜岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Shizuoka)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shizuoka domain: remaining tax dues in kind and cash, timber levies, and the opening of the products list",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left-hand continuation of the 静岡藩 return in fascicle 7 of the 藩制一覧表; the ○静岡藩 marker itself stands on the facing right-hand page, so the whole page belongs to Shizuoka and carries no domain boundary. The columns record the tail of the domain's dues — buckwheat 0.24 koku, salt 73.373 koku, 18 hoe handles, silver 68.95 monme — followed by three separate cash reckonings: ei 3,554.353233 kan, bita (debased copper) 1,106.776 kan, and copper cash 2,685.316 kan. An 外 (\"besides\") sub-heading then introduces a timber group of roughly 14,600 round logs, 200 pieces of squared timber, and about 100 flat-stock finished goods, closed by the note 右十分一運上 — a one-tenth unjō duty taken on the foregoing. The page ends by opening the 産物 (products) section with the domain's signature commodity, tea, at over 123,909 kanme (roughly 465 tonnes); the products list runs on to the next page."
  },
  {
   "id": "shizuoka_lower_p081_right",
   "sequence": 400,
   "domain_canonical": "静岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "靜岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Shizuoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p081_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 81,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（靜岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Shizuoka section) — running header, provenance",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shizuoka products and household/population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf inside the 静岡藩 (Shizuoka) block of fascicle 7 — no maru-marker prints here, and the running header 藩制一覽表第七（靜岡） confirms every column belongs to Shizuoka. Ten product columns run right to left: paper (半紙・半切紙, 51,500 kan), sugar (白・黑砂糖, 115,100 kanme), dried bonito (鰹節, 7,260 kanme), shiitake (2,187 koku), indigo (8,064 kanme), bupleurum root (柴胡, 1,300 kanme), Ryukyu tatami facing (508,000 sheets), cotton wool (54,730 kanme), cotton cloth (20,000 tan) and roof boards (9,900 pieces); two of these — the paper and the sugar — are pairs of commodities set in a two-line warichu that share a single figure. The three leftmost columns carry the population data: 藩士戸數 10,093 samurai households with 人員 48,064 persons, and a domain total 戸數 of 157,297 households, whose matching 人口 of 777,011 prints on the facing leaf. A red-ink warichu adds a 水附名籍 register of 597 households and 2,795 persons, and a headnote cautions that shizoku and sotsu, and male and female, are not broken out and that the samurai households are presumably subsumed within the 157,297 total."
  },
  {
   "id": "shizuoka_lower_p237_left",
   "sequence": 401,
   "domain_canonical": "静岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "靜岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Shizuoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p237_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 237,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（三池、靜岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 9 (Miike, Shizuoka) — the officials-and-military fascicle of the 1869-70 Dajōkan domain survey. The header names the domains whose entries open on this leaf, not every domain printed on it: Mikusa's tail also runs across the right-hand edge.",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-9 domain officials: Miike's whole councillor roster and the opening of Shizuoka's",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 451 of fascicle 9, an officials leaf with no military section. It opens on the right with the tail of Mikusa domain — one 權少參事 column carrying Ishiwata Mori'e and Ozaki Yaichirō — after which the ○三池藩 marker introduces Miike's complete councillor establishment: a summary line 大小參事 七人 (senior and junior councillors, 7 persons) followed by one senior councillor, two acting senior councillors, two junior councillors and two acting junior councillors, seven named men that reconcile exactly with the printed figure; a small-type （一二八人）, 128 persons, stands in the gutter beside it and cannot be a correction to that count. The ○靜岡藩 marker then opens the Tokugawa house's Shizuoka domain with thirteen men in three grades: one senior councillor (Hiraoka Tanji), nine acting senior councillors including Ōkubo Ichiō, Yamaoka Tetsutarō (Tesshū) and the kōgi-nin Tsumaki Tsutomu, and three junior councillors including Tsuda Shin'ichirō, the later jurist Tsuda Mamichi. Shizuoka's entry prints no troop line and runs on to the next leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "shibata_lower_p081_left",
   "sequence": 402,
   "domain_canonical": "新發田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新發田藩",
   "domain_en": "Shibata",
   "image": "images/lower_p081_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 81,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（新發田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Shibata)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shizuoka population tail; Shibata kokudaka and taxes",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the boundary between two fascicle-7 domain entries. Its five right-hand columns close 靜岡藩 (Shizuoka)'s civil register: a domain population of 777,011 (men 391,788 + women 385,223, reconciling exactly), which pairs with the 157,297 households printed as the last column of the preceding page, plus two small status categories — 轉士 (8 households / 36 persons) and 穢多非人 (1,651 households / 7,709 persons). The ○新發田藩 marker then opens Shibata's entry, giving a total kokudaka of 139,102.18735 koku held within Kanbara district of Echigo and Shinobu district of Iwashiro, of which 此譯 (\"the breakdown thereof\") itemises the Echigo portion at 132,399.04313 koku. Shibata's Echigo taxes follow: land tax (正租) of 64,170.0563 koku of rice, and miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 5,035.4176 koku of rice, 26 ryō 1 bu in gold, and 308.677985 kan in eiraku cash. A red-ink note dates the return to the second month of the kanoe-uma year (Meiji 3 / 1870)."
  },
  {
   "id": "shibata_lower_p082_right",
   "sequence": 403,
   "domain_canonical": "新發田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新發田藩",
   "domain_en": "Shibata",
   "image": "images/lower_p082_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 82,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（新發田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 7 — (Shibata)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shibata domain land tax and levies (fascicle 7), continued",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the 新發田藩 (Shibata, Echigo) entry in fascicle 7 of the Hansei ichiran; the domain's maru-marker ○新發田藩 stands on the preceding page in reading order (lower_p081_left, printed p.139), so every column here belongs to Shibata and no domain boundary falls on the leaf. The right-hand columns close out the miscellaneous levies (雜稅) on Shibata's Echigo–Kanbara parcel — silver 75.55364 kan, copper cash 5,106.61 kan, perilla seed 0.694 and 253.3462 koku, soybeans 3,073.0258 koku and barnyard millet 178.0974 koku — with marginal notes separating a fixed in-kind levy (但定納ニ付代米不相渡, \"no rice-equivalent is paid\") from levies commuted to rice (但代米渡正納之事). The middle columns open the domain's second, detached parcel, 6,702.24422 koku 「岩代國信夫郡ノ内」 (Shinobu district, Iwashiro), with its own regular tax of 1,366.6696 koku of rice and miscellaneous levies of 37.9781 koku of rice plus 122.49166 kan of ei. The three leftmost columns are domain-wide totals — rice 70,610.1216 koku, gold 26.25 ryō, ei 431.169645 kan — each of which reconciles exactly against the components printed here and on p.139, and the totals block runs on to p.141 with silver and copper cash."
  },
  {
   "id": "shibata_lower_p082_left",
   "sequence": 404,
   "domain_canonical": "新發田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新發田藩",
   "domain_en": "Shibata",
   "image": "images/lower_p082_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 82,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（新發田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Shibata)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shibata specie holdings, tax-exempt temple land, and samurai households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf from the Shibata (新發田) entry in fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran; the running header names the domain and no maru-marker appears, so the whole page belongs to Shibata. The right-hand columns record the domain's specie: 75 kan 556 monme 6 fun 4 rin of silver and 5,106 kanmon 610 mon of copper cash. The centre carries an eight-line block — flagged by an editorial note as having been written in vermilion in the original manuscript — listing tax-exempt land (除地) in Shinobu district, Iwashiro Province, granted in six parcels to five temples (東安寺, 法輪寺, 長福寺, 東源寺, 勝念寺) and to the ascetic Sankai (行人山海), under a printed total of 7.34 koku of rice that exceeds the sum of its own six parcels (7.21 koku) by 0.13. The left-hand columns give the samurai establishment: 870 shizoku households with a population of 4,783 (2,336 male, 2,447 female), followed by 1,017 sotsu households whose population count carries over to the next leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "shibata_lower_p083_right",
   "sequence": 405,
   "domain_canonical": "新發田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新發田藩",
   "domain_en": "Shibata",
   "image": "images/lower_p083_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 83,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（新發田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle 7 (Shibata)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Households, population, shrines, temples and eta households",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-7 return for 新發田藩 (Shibata, Echigo). No maru-marker appears anywhere on the page, so every column belongs to Shibata; the domain is identified only by the running header 藩制一覽表第七（新發田）. The page opens with a population of 5,685 (3,091 male, 2,594 female) carried over from the household entry that ended on the preceding leaf, then gives 33,282 households and a population of 178,986 (91,202 male, 87,784 female). Religious establishments are broken out by province: within Echigo (越後國ノ内), 856 shrines with 763 attached persons and 178 temples with 1,975; within Iwaki (岩城國ノ内), 2 shrine-priest households with 17 persons and 7 temples with 4 men. It closes with 12 eta (穢多) households totalling 132 persons, evenly split 66 male and 66 female."
  },
  {
   "id": "shibata_lower_p083_left",
   "sequence": 406,
   "domain_canonical": "新發田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新發田藩",
   "domain_en": "Shibata",
   "image": "images/lower_p083_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 83,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（島原）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 7 — running header keyed to Shimabara",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shibata's outcast/ferryman households, kazoku and army; opening of Shimabara's kokudaka and land tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page closes 新發田藩 (Shibata, Echigo) fascicle-7 block and opens 島原藩 (Shimabara, Hizen). For Shibata it records 13 hinin households holding 97 people (51 male, 46 female), 17 ferryman (渡守) households holding 149 people (80 male, 69 female), and a kazoku house of 10 (4 male, 6 female), followed by a 兵員 military block: 3 infantry battalions — glossed in a warichu as 60 men to a platoon and 8 platoons to a battalion, i.e. 1,440 foot — plus 200 gunners, 24 cannon, and 2,000 small arms. The ○島原藩 marker then opens Shimabara, whose lands are given as 肥前高來郡 together with 豐後宇佐郡 and 豐後國東郡 across the strait, at a kokudaka (高) of 74,872.3111 koku, explicitly noted as base high plus new-paddy and dry-field reclamation increases. Its regular tax (正税) is stated in 現米 (rice actually delivered) at 36,945.7416 koku, roughly 49 percent of the assessed high."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimabara_lower_p084_right",
   "sequence": 407,
   "domain_canonical": "島原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "島原藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimabara",
   "image": "images/lower_p084_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 84,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（島原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 — (Shimabara)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shimabara taxes, national products, and 華族/士族/卒 status counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 144, the tax-products-and-status leaf of the Shimabara (島原藩, Hizen) civil entry in Fascicle 7. There is no domain marker on this side: the ○島原藩 marker, the assessed 高 of 74,872.31111 koku and the opening of the 正稅 account (現米 36,945.74116 koku) all stand on the preceding page 143 (lower_p083_left), so the whole page is Shimabara. It closes the 正稅 account with 8,280 koku of miscellaneous grain and 2,571 ryō (plus 134.7 ei-mon) in cash, then records 雜稅 of 2,919.6896 koku in current rice (inclusive of kuchimai, fumai and komonomari) and 3,361 ryō in cash (inclusive of kuchikin, fukin, sundry unjō and komonomari). Under 國産 it lists 990 head of farm cattle and horses — 240 oxen and 750 horses — yielding 15 ryō 500 mon in licence duty, and 3,500,000 kin of camphor seed returning 3,000 ryō in profit; the status register then opens with 3 kazoku (1 male, 2 female), 369 shizoku households totalling 2,220 persons (1,070 m + 1,150 f), and 888 sotsu households totalling 4,322 persons (2,062 m + 2,260 f), with the commoner and domain-wide totals continuing on page 145 (lower_p084_left)."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimabara_lower_p084_left",
   "sequence": 408,
   "domain_canonical": "島原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "島原藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimabara",
   "image": "images/lower_p084_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 84,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（島原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覽表), Fascicle 7 — Shimabara (島原藩): household and population register by status and religious category",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "household and population counts by status/religious category, with domain totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left leaf of Shimabara's fascicle-7 household-and-population return, continuing the register that begins on the facing right leaf; no ○ domain marker appears, so the whole page is 島原藩. Reading right to left it records the town-and-village households (市鄉 34,839) and their population (165,615 = 83,239 male + 82,376 female), then the religious and outcaste categories — 神社 (shrines: no figure printed, marked 不詳 in a head-note above the column), 社家 138 houses / 678 persons, 修驗 5 / 22, 山伏 2 / 9, 寺院 113 temples / 772 persons (539 monks + 233 women), 尼庵 2 / 4, 穢多 225 / 1,353, 非人 8 / 53. It closes with the domain totals 合戸數 36,590 households and 合人員 175,051 persons (87,961 male + 87,090 female). The totals close exactly across the spread: 36,590 − 35,332 (this leaf's components) = 1,258, precisely the facing leaf's 1 kazoku + 369 shizoku + 888 sotsu households."
  },
  {
   "id": "shinjo_lower_p085_right",
   "sequence": 409,
   "domain_canonical": "新庄藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新庄藩",
   "domain_en": "Shinjō",
   "image": "images/lower_p085_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 85,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（新庄）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Shinjō)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shimabara army units; Shinjō kokudaka, taxes and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand half of the fascicle-7 spread straddles a domain boundary. The six army columns to the right of the ○新庄藩 marker close Shimabara's (島原藩) military return: a 1st and a 2nd battalion of six 40-man companies each (240 apiece), a 遊擊 flying battalion of three 30-man gun companies (90), four standing platoons at 60 men (240), seven reserve platoons on the same establishment (420), and three artillery companies of 20 (60) — with a small editorial note, （以下三行附筆）, warning that the last three of those columns were appended to the original return. Left of the marker, Shinjō's entry opens: an assessed 高 of 103,434.7983 koku across 59 villages in Mogami district, Uzen; regular land tax of 25,280.77101 koku of rice; miscellaneous taxes of 186 ryō 13.585 monme in specie plus 770 kan 948 mon in copper cash; 630 koku of shrine-and-temple land; and a force of seven 60-man infantry platoons (420) with a single 36-man artillery section. A vermilion note in the top margin above the 高 column records that the 藩制 return itself carried no base kokudaka and that the figure was taken instead from the tax register (租稅錄)."
  },
  {
   "id": "shinjo_lower_p085_left",
   "sequence": 410,
   "domain_canonical": "新庄藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新庄藩",
   "domain_en": "Shinjō",
   "image": "images/lower_p085_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 85,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（新庄）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 — (Shinjō)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Status-group households &amp; population",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 147 continues Shinjō domain's fascicle-7 civil register with its status-group household and population table; the block opened on the facing right-hand page (book page 146), where the ○新庄藩 marker stands, so this side carries no boundary marker and is entirely Shinjō's. Reading right to left, the page records 200 reserve troops, then households and people by status: 521 shizoku households (1,255 persons plus 1,446 women), 761 sotsu households (1,005 persons plus 436 women), 2 Shinto-priest households (8 male, 8 female), 96 temples (207 male, 74 female) with 4 of them priestless, 91 shugen households (202 male, 61 female), and 7,944 commoner households totalling 47,405 people (25,023 male, 22,382 female). It closes with the two outcaste categories, 2 eta households (8 male, 6 female) and 10 hinin households (29 male, 23 female). The commoner split validates exactly against its printed total (25,023 + 22,382 = 47,405), and across all status groups the page yields 9,427 households and 52,173 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "shigehara_lower_p086_right",
   "sequence": 411,
   "domain_canonical": "重原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "重原藩",
   "domain_en": "Shigehara",
   "image": "images/lower_p086_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 86,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（重原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Survey (Hansei Ichiran-hyō), Fascicle 7 — (Shigehara)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka, land deductions and land-tax",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 7, printed page 148, carries the entire fiscal opening of Shigehara domain (重原藩), a small jin'ya-holding house with 88 villages spread across the Aomi, Kamo, Shitara and Hazu districts of Mikawa. Its gross assessment (草高) is 28,352.28558 koku \"including komidaka\"; five 內 deductions totalling 2,842.45158 koku — dominated by 2,521.90385 koku of permanently ruined ground (river washout, sea encroachment, landslide and ponded land) against just 24.06714 koku for the domain's own jin'ya and village-granary plots — leave a printed 殘高 of 25,509.804 koku. An editorial note, （以下二行原朱書）, flags the next two lines as written in vermilion in the original: the five-year-average tax rice (此取米) of 9,877.06762 koku, less 1,569.2116 koku remitted for crop failure on paddy and dry fields, which resolves into 正租 8,168.9281 koku and 雜稅 138.92846 koku. Both internal arithmetic nets close to within 0.03 and 0.00054 koku respectively — small slips in the source, and a strong independent check on the transcription."
  },
  {
   "id": "shigehara_lower_p086_left",
   "sequence": 412,
   "domain_canonical": "重原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "重原藩",
   "domain_en": "Shigehara",
   "image": "images/lower_p086_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 86,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（重原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Table, Fascicle 7 (Shigehara)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Households, population by status, and religious establishments",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the civil and religious returns of Shigehara Domain (重原藩, Mikawa) from fascicle 7 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran; it bears no maru-marker and continues the domain's block from the facing right-hand page. The domain reports 8,100 households and a population of 34,789 (17,623 male, 17,166 female), within which the non-commoner statuses are 235 shizoku households (949 persons) and 107 sotsu households (258 persons), alongside 10 shrine-priest and 3 shugendō households. Its religious establishment comprises 582 Shinto shrines and 73 Buddhist temples, staffed by 63 shrine personnel (31 male, 32 female), 388 Buddhist clergy (275 male, 113 female), and 6 shugendō practitioners. Shrine and temple lands held tax-exempt under vermilion-seal grant total 303.09 koku together with 9,986 tsubo."
  },
  {
   "id": "shigehara_lower_p087_right",
   "sequence": 413,
   "domain_canonical": "重原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "重原藩",
   "domain_en": "Shigehara",
   "image": "images/lower_p087_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 87,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百五十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（新宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Table Seven (Shingū)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka and tax closing block (fascicle 7)",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 150 carries the closing block of 重原藩 (Shigehara)'s fascicle-7 entry, not 新宮藩's: the ○新宮藩 maru-marker is the page's leftmost column, so every substantive column stands to its right and belongs to the preceding domain. A compiler's note records that the governor's family, the eta and warships are not entered, with warships glossed 不所持 (\"none held\"). Six lines flagged as red-ink marginalia give the 1865–1869 (乙丑–己巳) five-year averages — 正租 8,351.64362 koku plus 雜稅 1,663.9262 koku, footing exactly to the printed 合〆 10,015.56982 koku — bracketed as the 辛未 (1871) survey. The main columns then restate, on the authority of the five-year-average register, 草高 28,352.28554 koku, 正租 7,737.79882 koku and 雜稅 1,148.2914 koku with cash converted to rice; that 草高 matches 重原藩's 28,352.28558 koku printed under its own marker on lower_p086_right, whereas 新宮藩's own 草高 opens the next page at 35,743.104 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "shingu_lower_p087_left",
   "sequence": 414,
   "domain_canonical": "新宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Shingū",
   "image": "images/lower_p087_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 87,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（新宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 (Shingū)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shingū domain kokudaka, five-year-average tax yields, and household/population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "The whole of this page is the civil/economic register of Shingū Domain (新宮藩, Kii province), continuing from the facing right-hand half of the spread where the ○新宮藩 marker opens the entry. It records a kusadaka of 35,743.104 koku plus a further 6,569.6662 koku of 改出新田 (new fields added by re-survey), and — as a five-year average — a main land tax of 15,190.6316 koku of rice, 797.44791 koku of miscellaneous tax rice, 9,678.6875 ryō in gold, and 19.592 kan of copper cash. The demographic block gives 9,592 total households and 54,377 people (27,512 male, 26,865 female), of whom the shizoku account for 502 households and 1,892 people (874 male, 1,018 female) and the sotsuzoku for 350 households and 1,265 people (637 male, 628 female). Every male+female pair sums exactly to its printed total, a check that corrects three MASTER readings and recovers the 卒族 population row MASTER omits."
  },
  {
   "id": "shingu_lower_p088_right",
   "sequence": 415,
   "domain_canonical": "新宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Shingū",
   "image": "images/lower_p088_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 88,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百五十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（新宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō (Table of Domain Administration), Fascicle 7 — Shingū",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Non-commoner household and population counts (chūgen, temples, yamabushi) with a seven-line red-ink marginal breakdown of the temple population",
   "page_summary_en": "The tail of Shingū domain's fascicle-7 block (the ○新宮藩 marker stands on p. 87 recto; no marker is printed on this leaf), covering the non-commoner household and population categories: 91 chūgen households holding 235 people (161 male / 74 female), 176 temples with 178 residents (161 male / 17 female), and 24 yamabushi households with 118 people (61 male / 57 female). A bracketed editorial note, 「（以下七行欄外朱書）」, flags the next seven columns as red-ink marginalia, and the count is exact — the 1928 editors open a bracket at 「（寺人口」 and close it seven columns later, after 「人口三十一人…女十五人）」. Those seven lines itemise the temple population as 145 monks and 2 nuns, then — separated by the collation formulae 「右一二云」 and 「又一二云」 — a Monto-sect (Jōdo Shinshū) component of 5 temples with 31 residents (16 male / 15 female). The marginalia reconcile exactly with the main text (145+16=161 male, 2+15=17 female, 147+31=178), so the red block is a complete partition of the temple population rather than a competing count, and the contrast between the 145:2 and 16:15 sex ratios is precisely the difference between celibate clergy and Shinshū's married priestly families."
  },
  {
   "id": "shingu_lower_p239_left",
   "sequence": 416,
   "domain_canonical": "新宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Shingū",
   "image": "images/lower_p239_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 239,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（新宮、下館）",
   "page_header_en": "Conspectus of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Shingū, Shimodate)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 455 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle 9, the fascicle that records domain officials and armed force. The right-hand third of the page closes out the preceding domain — Shigehara in the project dataset — with a five-man complement of acting junior councillors, named below as Ogasawara Tōgo, Gotō Jūrō, Ōtei Genkurō, Shimizu Seigo and Takahashi Hidezō, and with a force of 150 infantry plus a 16-man artillery corps. The ○新宮藩 marker then opens Shingū's own entry, which lists nine named officeholders across the two registers (one senior councillor, two acting senior councillors, four junior councillors, two acting junior councillors) and a force of twelve platoons at 58 men each, that is 696 men. A second marker, ○下館藩, stands at the left edge with no data beside it: Shimodate's block begins on the facing page, and the running header names only Shingū and Shimodate, saying nothing about the preceding domain whose tail occupies the right of the leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimodate_lower_p088_left",
   "sequence": 417,
   "domain_canonical": "下館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "下館藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimodate",
   "image": "images/lower_p088_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 88,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（下館）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Survey of Domain Administration), Fascicle 7 (Shimodate)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shimodate's kokudaka and tax receipts (block opening), after the close of Shingū's population return",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 153 opens the fascicle-7 entry for Shimodate (下館藩, a 20,000-koku Ishikawa house in Hitachi) at the ○下館藩 marker. Left of the marker Shimodate returns a base kokudaka of 20,000 koku plus a further 2,116.186 koku of reclaimed new paddy (外…込高新田), assessed on a five-year average fixed rate (五ヶ年平均定免) that yields 6,027.4448 koku of land tax in rice, 33.281 koku of miscellaneous rice tax, 10,646.8125 ryō in gold and 644.417416 kan in eiraku cash — a land-tax take of about 30 percent of the base kokudaka. The five columns to the right of the marker are not Shimodate's: they close the preceding domain Shingū's (新宮藩) return with 180 eta households totalling 759 persons (1 monk, 391 male, 367 female — summing exactly to the printed total), 254 shrine sites but no Shinto priests, a six-person governor's household, and no transport vessels. The running header names only 下館, so on this page the header is provenance for the block that opens here rather than a label for everything printed on the leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimodate_lower_p089_right",
   "sequence": 418,
   "domain_canonical": "下館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "下館藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimodate",
   "image": "images/lower_p089_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 89,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百五十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（下館）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview Table, Fascicle 7 (Shimodate) — the printed parenthetical agrees with the data; every column on this leaf is Shimodate's. Provenance, not a value.",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shimodate's miscellaneous-tax cash, the red-ink product tax, vermilion-seal shrine/temple land, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "The middle leaf (printed page 百五十四 = 154) of Shimodate domain's (下館藩) fascicle-7 return, carrying no maru-marker: the ○下館藩 marker stands on printed page 153 (pdf 88-left) and the block runs on to page 155 (pdf 89-left), where ○芝邨藩 opens. Reading right to left it completes the domain's miscellaneous-tax (雜稅) receipts in cash — 139 ryō 1 bu 2 shu in gold, 138 kan 297.044 mon in eisen, and 62 kan 451 mon in copper — continuing the 雜稅米 of 33.281 koku that closes the previous leaf; against a 20,000-koku domain these are trivial sums. A bracketed group of four lines, flagged by the editorial note （以下四行欄外朱書） as having stood in red ink in the manuscript margin, records a product tax (產物税) of 200 ryō on freeze-dried tofu (氷豆腐) from the domain's administered district in Kawachi Province, and 137.7 koku of vermilion-seal land (朱印地) is booked under the category label 社寺領 (shrine-and-temple lands). The leaf closes with the demographic counts: 2,827 total households and 15,182 people (7,768 male, 7,414 female), of whom 255 households and 1,156 people (590 male, 566 female) were shizoku — a samurai share of 7.6% of the population and 9.0% of households."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimodate_lower_p089_left",
   "sequence": 419,
   "domain_canonical": "下館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "下館藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimodate",
   "image": "images/lower_p089_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 89,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（芝邨）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Shibamura)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shimodate status-group households and population; Shibamura's entry opens",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes Shimodate domain's fascicle-7 entry and opens Shibamura's. Everything printed to the right of the ○芝邨藩 marker is Shimodate's status-group tail: 64 sotsu households (148 people, 94 M / 54 F), 15 shrine households (50 people), 104 temples with 62 resident clergy, 26 eta households (195 people), 19 hinin households (68 people), 126 shrines, a governor's household of 3 (2 M / 1 F), three districts (Makabe in Hitachi, Ishikawa and Furuichi in Kawachi), 52 villages, and no transport vessels. Left of the marker Shibamura's entry begins with a warichu note giving its own three districts (Shikijō, Yamanobe, Shimoshimo) and 25 villages, then its kusadaka of 10,021.959 koku, qualified as including revised newly-reclaimed-field yield. The running head reads 藩制一覽表第七（芝邨）, naming Shibamura even though the bulk of the page's data belongs to Shimodate — a provenance label, not an ownership label."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimodate_lower_p240_right",
   "sequence": 420,
   "domain_canonical": "下館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "下館藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimodate",
   "image": "images/lower_p240_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 240,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（芝村）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Nine (Shibamura)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 456 of fascicle nine gives the councillor roster and troop strength of Shimodate domain (下館藩, Hitachi province), whose entry opened at the foot of the preceding page. Two parallel rosters are printed: the survey's own list — two senior councillors (大參事 Suzuki Kihachirō and Itō Naoki), one acting senior councillor (權大參事 Kawamata Yūma) and four junior councillors (少參事 Muraoka Sanemasa, Kinugasa Bunji, Okamura Kanma, Arita 睃喜) — and, to the left of the note （留守官午四月届左ノ如シ）, a revised list submitted by the domain's caretaker office in the fourth month of the horse year, naming one senior councillor (Okuyama Kongō), two acting senior councillors (Suzuki Kitarō and Kawamata Yūma, the latter glossed 公議人, delegate to the public assembly), four junior councillors (Itō Naoki, Kinugasa Bunji, Okamura Kanma, Muraoka Saneo) and one acting junior councillor (Yamazaki Tsukumo). Shimodate's force is recorded as 兵隊 百三十五人, 135 troops. The page closes with the ○芝村藩 maru-marker and the first column of Shibamura domain's own entry, 大參事 一人 恒岡直史, which continues on the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "shibamura_lower_p090_right",
   "sequence": 421,
   "domain_canonical": "芝邨藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "芝邨藩",
   "domain_en": "Shibamura",
   "image": "images/lower_p090_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 90,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（芝邨）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 7 (Shibamura)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shibamura Domain — taxes and demographics (1869 main survey + 1871 marginal update)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the entire fascicle-7 entry for Shibamura Domain (芝邨藩, a small ~10,000-koku Oda house in Yamato province), identified only by the running header — there is no maru-marker, so every column belongs to Shibamura. The right block is the 1869 (己巳, 10th month) main survey, reporting five-year-average regular land-tax rice of 4,818.81731 koku and miscellaneous-tax rice of 60.88241 koku. A two-column editorial note flags that the following five lines are red-ink marginal additions and dates the main survey to 1869/10; the left block is a supplementary survey of the 2nd month of 1871 (辛未) giving regular tax 5,079.66734 koku, miscellaneous tax 132.4245 koku, 1,625 total households, and a population of 7,338 (male 3,662 / female 3,676), of which 117 shizoku households and 474 shizoku persons plus 77 sotsu households. Male + female sub-counts reconcile exactly to both population totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "shibamura_lower_p090_left",
   "sequence": 422,
   "domain_canonical": "芝邨藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "芝邨",
   "domain_en": "Shibamura",
   "image": "images/lower_p090_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 90,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（芝邨）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 — Shibamura",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Temple / shrine / outcaste establishment counts and populations (Shibamura, fascicle 7)",
   "page_summary_en": "The left leaf of Shibamura domain's (芝邨藩) fascicle-7 return, continuing a religious-and-status demographic block. There is no maru-marker anywhere on the page, and the running header names 芝邨, so the entire page belongs to Shibamura (the block opens mid-way, carried over from the preceding right leaf). It records establishment counts — 18 temples (寺院拾八戸), 10 Buddha halls (佛堂十字), a separate 寺 count of 17 (寺十七字), 39 shrines (神社三十九座), 7 shrine-family households (社家戸數七戸) and 49 outcaste households (穢多戸數四十九戸) — paired with populations: a temple population of 75 (30 monks, 6 nuns, 13 lay men, 26 lay women), a shrine-family population of 39 (13 M / 26 F) and an outcaste population of 242 (114 M / 128 F), plus three further bare 人口 figures of 138 (96 M / 42 F), 43 (15 M / 28 F) and 38 (28 M / 10 F). A mid-page editorial note, （以下五行欄外朱書）（一二云）, flags five of the columns as figures that originally stood as red-ink marginalia in the source. Printed page number 157."
  },
  {
   "id": "shiiya_lower_p091_right",
   "sequence": 423,
   "domain_canonical": "椎谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "椎谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Shiiya",
   "image": "images/lower_p091_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 91,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百五十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（椎谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 — Shiiya",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shiiya Domain: land yield, taxes, households, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page of the Hansei Ichiran (fascicle 7) records Shiiya Domain (椎谷藩), a small Echigo domain. Its nominal assessed yield (草高) is 10,000 koku, supplemented by 746.11776 koku of new-field yield (外/新田), for a combined total (合) of 10,746.11776 koku. Regular land-tax rice (正租米) averaged 4,337.69926 koku over the five years from Kōshi (1864) to Boshin (1868), and miscellaneous-tax rice (雜稅米) was 67.67749 koku. The domain comprised 2,303 households and a population of 10,918. Editorial notes record that the governor's family (知事家族) and transport vessels (運輪舶) were not entered."
  },
  {
   "id": "shiiya_lower_p091_left",
   "sequence": 424,
   "domain_canonical": "椎谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "椎谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Shiiya",
   "image": "images/lower_p091_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 91,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（椎谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Shiiya)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Domain demographics — households and population by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This left page continues the Shiiya (椎谷藩, Echigo) entry of the Hansei Ichiran domain survey, fascicle 7, printed page 159. It records the domain's total population by sex (male 5,329; female 5,589 = 10,918) and by status group: 66 samurai (shizoku) households / 218 persons; 47 sotsu (foot-soldier) households / 167 persons; 1 shrine-family (shake) household / 4 persons; 36 temples and 18 halls housing 171 persons; and 18 outcaste (eta) households / 117 persons. The governor's family numbers 3 (1 male, 2 female), and an editorial note records that shrine [populations] were not registered. No maru-marker appears on the page, so all figures belong to Shiiya."
  },
  {
   "id": "shiiya_lower_p240_left",
   "sequence": 425,
   "domain_canonical": "椎谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "椎谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Shiiya",
   "image": "images/lower_p240_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 240,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百五十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（椎谷、芝山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 9 (Shiiya, Shibayama)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 officials page carrying the tail of Shibamura domain's roster, the whole of Shiiya domain's roster, and the opening of Shibayama domain's. Shibamura closes with one acting senior councillor (Niwa Hōhō), one Kōgisho delegate (Wada Yoshitaka), a junior councillor (Uwaji Tadakage, printed without a count), one acting junior councillor (Mori Masayuki), and a troop return of 25 heishi plus 50 heisotsu, 75 men in all. Shiiya prints a symmetrical roster of two men in each of the four councillor grades — Iida Teizō and Hayashi Heinojō as senior councillors, Hara Kabunosuke and Mikumo Shūzō as acting senior, Ōtani Bunzaemon and Kumagai Tomiya as junior, Shibata Sajūrō and Teraishi Sekitarō as acting junior — followed by 84 troops in three squads. Shibayama's block opens with three senior councillors and no count printed: Kōga Hidetaka, Fukushima Jūichi and Kunihi Seiichi."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimotsuma_lower_p092_right",
   "sequence": 426,
   "domain_canonical": "下妻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "下妻藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimotsuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p092_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 92,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（下妻）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle 7 (Shimotsuma)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shimotsuma domain kokudaka, land tax, and household/status counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the economic and household block for Shimotsuma domain (下妻藩), a 10,000-koku base holding (本高一萬石) whose gross assessed yield (草高) reaches 12,232.245 koku including komidaka and newly-opened fields. Its land tax (正租) is 1,992.626 koku of rice plus 1,035.522 kan of cash; miscellaneous tax (雜税) is 2.353 koku of rice plus 36.666 kan of cash; exempt shrine/temple land within the domain (管轄内社寺領除地) totals 394.481 koku, with a note that the red-and-black-seal parcels cannot be distinguished. The domain has 1,786 households, of which 64 are shizoku (one of them an ichimon collateral house), 19 sotsu, 27 associate-shizoku, and 25 associate-sotsu; its holdings span parts of Hitachi, Musashi, and Shimotsuke across 33 villages. The three census-tail columns at the top right (郡三郡 / 村三十二ヶ邨 / 軍艦船ナシ) overflow from the preceding domain, Shiiya (椎谷藩)."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimotsuma_lower_p092_left",
   "sequence": 427,
   "domain_canonical": "下妻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "下妻藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimotsuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p092_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 92,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（下妻）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 — (Shimotsuma)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shimotsuma population, status classes, and religious/outcaste household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of printed page 161 continues the Shimotsuma (下妻藩) return in Fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran. It records a total population of 8,805 (male 4,485 / female 4,320) and breaks out the privileged and religious classes: 士族 249, 准士族 104, 卒族 40, 准卒族 59, plus 社人 (shrine attendants) 29, 寺侶 (Buddhist clergy) 95, and 山伏 (mountain ascetics) 11 persons. Margin counts on the right give 社家 15 shrine households, 寺院 61 temples, 山伏 3 dwellings, 穢多番非人 41 outcaste households, and a combined shrine-temple tally of 79 buildings (alternatively reckoned as 64 temples). No maru-marker appears on the leaf, so every column belongs to Shimotsuma."
  },
  {
   "id": "shimotsuma_lower_p241_right",
   "sequence": 428,
   "domain_canonical": "下妻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "下妻藩",
   "domain_en": "Shimotsuma",
   "image": "images/lower_p241_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 241,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百五十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（下妻、志筑）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Fascicle 9 (Shimotsuma, Shizuku)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop formation",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 officials page carrying the end of Shibayama domain's roster, the whole of Shimotsuma domain's entry, and the opening of Shizuku domain's. Shibayama's councillors are given by name with no counts: six provisional senior councillors (Satomi Shōbee, Hamano Hirota, Aoki Shōzō, Akagishi Hyōzō, Aoki Genee, Kawazoe Shōki), six junior councillors (Yamagishi Sazō, Hisamatsu Koyata, Tsuchiya Sō, Satake Yoshiee, Kawazoe Shinhito, Shinomiya Naoyoshi), and two provisional junior councillors (Yamazumi Kayoshi, Kondō Takuma). Shimotsuma reports the opposite way — counts with no names: one senior councillor, two provisional senior councillors, two junior councillors, three provisional junior councillors, eight in all, plus a military entry of one platoon with no headcount printed. Shizuku's entry begins with two senior councillors, written 貳員."
  },
  {
   "id": "shizuku_lower_p093_right",
   "sequence": 429,
   "domain_canonical": "志筑藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "志筑藩",
   "domain_en": "Shizuku",
   "image": "images/lower_p093_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 93,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（志筑）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Table 7 (Shizuku)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "domain statistics: outcaste/servant population, shrines, governor's family, ships, kokudaka and land tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This page from fascicle 7 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran carries the end of Shimotsuma domain's (下妻藩) entry and the opening of Shizuku domain's (志筑藩), divided by the ○志筑藩 section marker. The Shimotsuma columns record 255 eta/hinin (130 male, 125 female), 12 temple-front and tenant households, a further population of 80 (57 male, 23 female), 30 unregistered bond-servants (29 male, 1 female), 58 shrines, a governor's family of 10, and a note that warships are not recorded. Shizuku's block reports an assessed yield (草高) of 10,110 koku including new-field development, a principal land tax (正租) of 1,837.849 koku of rice plus a cash levy (永) of 325.26074 kan, a rice-equivalent (此米) of 40.658 koku, and miscellaneous tax (雜税) of 90.79915 koku in perilla and beans. The printed page number is 163."
  },
  {
   "id": "shizuku_lower_p093_left",
   "sequence": 430,
   "domain_canonical": "志筑藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "志筑藩",
   "domain_en": "Shizuku",
   "image": "images/lower_p093_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 93,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（志筑）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 — (Shizuku)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Population, households, and tax-in-kind conversions (Shizuku domain, Fascicle 7)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf continues the Shizuku (志筑) domain block in Fascicle 7 of the Han-sei Ichiran — a Hitachi-province domain of roughly 10,000 koku held by the Honda house. At the head it records tax-in-kind conversions: a rice figure of 45.3996 koku (reckoned at 1 koku = 4 ryō) and an ei-cash sum of 184.49608 kanmon whose rice equivalent, 23.062 koku (reckoned at 1 koku = 8 ryō; 184.49608 ÷ 8 = 23.062, arithmetic checks), follows. It then gives the domain's demography: total population 5,568 across 888 households — including 73 shizoku and 38 sotsu households, a governor's family of 9, 56 shrine-lay persons, 19 temple clergy, 10 shrine-priest households, 9 temples and 10 shrines. Note that the printed male/female split of the total population (男 2,694 + 女 2,674 = 5,368) falls 200 short of the printed total 5,568, a source-level inconsistency; the scan prints 女二千六百七十四人 (六百), whereas MASTER records 女2874."
  },
  {
   "id": "shishido_lower_p094_right",
   "sequence": 431,
   "domain_canonical": "宍戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宍戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Shishido",
   "image": "images/lower_p094_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 94,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（宍戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 7 (Shishido)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shishido domain fiscal & demographic return (kokudaka, land tax, households, population)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the fascicle-7 (civil and fiscal) return for Shishido Domain (宍戸藩), a 10,000-koku fief of twenty-seven villages in Ibaraki district, Hitachi Province. Its gross assessed yield (草高) is 10,499.666 koku; the main land tax (正租) is 1,531.6374 koku of rice plus 115.883 koku of soybeans and 602 kan 449 mon in cash (永), and a miscellaneous tax (雜稅) adds 4.427 koku of rice and 69 kan 427 mon 4 bu in cash. The domain reports 978 households (with shizoku households explicitly not tallied) and a population of 6,309 (3,201 male, 3,108 female), plus 5 shrine-attendant and 7 shugen households and 40 temples. The two notes at the upper right — 船艦不記 (no warships recorded) and 穢多非人支配地ニ無御坐候 (no eta/hinin in the controlled land) — belong to the preceding domain, Shizuku (志筑藩), overflowing to the right of Shishido's marker."
  },
  {
   "id": "shichinohe_lower_p094_left",
   "sequence": 432,
   "domain_canonical": "七戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "七戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Shichinohe",
   "image": "images/lower_p094_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 94,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（七戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview (Hansei Ichiran), fascicle 7 (Shichinohe)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Tail of Shishido population/status counts + opening of Shichinohe land-and-tax figures",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-7 (財政/民政) page straddles two domains. To the right of the sole maru-marker sit the last seven columns of Shishido-han (宍戸藩) social-status counts: shizoku 190 (男98/女92, plus 28 servants), sotsu 59 (男23/女36), shrine-people (社人) 29 (男16/女13), Buddhist clergy (寺侶) 55 (男46/女9), and Shugen ascetics (修驗) 31 (男13/女18), together with two \"not recorded\" notations for the governor's family (知事家族不記) and the outcaste population (穢多等不記). The marker ○七戸藩 then opens Shichinohe-han: assessed yield (草高) 10,384.647 koku, land-tax rice (正租) 1,150.0209 koku, gold tax 174 ryō (plus 永40.1 mon), copper cash 3,695.838 kan, and miscellaneous tax (雜稅) 232.25 ryō. The running header and page number (165) belong to the Shichinohe entry."
  },
  {
   "id": "shichinohe_lower_p095_right",
   "sequence": 433,
   "domain_canonical": "七戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "七戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Shichinohe",
   "image": "images/lower_p095_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 95,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（七戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 — (Shichinohe)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Shichinohe domain — population, households by status, and cash/tax revenues",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of Fascicle 7 records the Shichinohe domain (七戸藩) of northern Mutsu. Total population is 15,527 (male 8,406, female 7,121) across 2,994 households; the status breakdown gives 240 shizoku and 50 sotsu households, 12 shrine-family and 2 outcaste households, and 18 temples, with population by status of 1,680 shizoku, 350 sotsu, 84 shrine personnel, and 54 clergy. Four fiscal lines list cash revenues of 300 ryō (kelp / dried-abalone / sea-cucumber tax), 60 kan (sardine pressed-lees tax, ~10,100 me), roughly 1,800 ryō together with ~850 horses and ~50 cattle in annual miscellaneous taxes, and 2,665.422 kan. No domain marker appears; the entire page is Shichinohe."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirado_lower_p103_right",
   "sequence": 434,
   "domain_canonical": "平戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "平戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirado",
   "image": "images/lower_p103_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 103,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（平戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Overview of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 7 (Hirado)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hirado domain kokudaka and tax revenue (fascicle 7)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page continues the Hirado (平戸) domain entry in Fascicle 7 of the Hansei ichiran, recording assessed landholding and tax revenue. The combined kokudaka (合高) is 120,912.301 koku; on the same page a component 高 of 49,212.301 koku and a separate 10,000-koku cadet (branch) holding are given, the latter tied to a junior branch of the Matsuura house (末家 松浦, Junior Fifth Rank). Regular land tax is stated as 50,422.2531 koku (己/1869 survey vintage) and as 51,121.6155 koku of rice (正租米), while miscellaneous cash taxes total 11,149.125 ryō, split into gold (此金 7,654.5 ryō; 諸税金 3,175.6875 ryō) and copper-cash (錢 76,540.769 kan, plus 312 mon). Editorial notes state the figures rest on the public-storehouse expense ledger (公廛入費帳) and are five-year averages for the 辛未 (1871) survey."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirado_lower_p103_left",
   "sequence": 435,
   "domain_canonical": "平戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "平戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirado",
   "image": "images/lower_p103_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 103,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（平戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 — (Hirado)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hirado demographic summary + start of Hirado-Shinden sub-domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This left page (printed p.183) closes the Hirado (平戸藩) entry of Fascicle 7 with its household/population block: 31,991 total households and a population of 148,507 (male 76,610 + female 71,897). A red-ink marginal addition, flagged by the editor's bracketed note (「但シ…（以下七行欄外朱書）本文ノ士族卒ノ内ナルヘシト考ヘル」, \"the following seven lines are red-ink marginalia; treat them as [belonging] within the main text's shizoku and sotsu\"), breaks the samurai classes out: shizoku = 572 households / 2,838 people, sotsu = 3,031 households / 12,521 people. A maru-marker (arc over 平戸新田) then opens the small sub-domain Hirado-Shinden (平戸新田藩): shizoku 128 households / 495 people, sotsu 112 households / 177 people as printed — though the sotsu male (258) + female (219) sum to 477, so the printed hundreds digit (百) is very likely a source error for 四百."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirado_lower_p104_right",
   "sequence": 436,
   "domain_canonical": "平戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "平戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirado",
   "image": "images/lower_p104_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 104,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（平戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, fascicle 7 (Hirado)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hirado — minor status-group household counts and populations (temples, shrines, ascetics, blind guild, diviners, sub-vassals)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page continues Hirado domain's (平戸藩) demographic survey in 藩制一覧表 fascicle 7, tabulating its minor status groups as paired household-and-population columns read right to left. It records sub-vassals and their servants (陪卒脇間又者: 9,009 households; population 46,839 = 24,608 male + 22,231 female), shrine-attendant families (社人: 130 households; 605 persons), mountain ascetics (山伏: 132 households; 614 persons), the blind guild (座頭: 50 households; 243 persons), yin-yang diviners (陰陽師: 31 households; 114 persons), Buddhist temples (寺: 214, with a resident population of 499), and Shinto shrines (神社: 1,813, of which 25 are Engishiki-registered Shikinai shrines). Every male+female split reconciles exactly to its stated total."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitoyoshi_lower_p104_left",
   "sequence": 437,
   "domain_canonical": "人吉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "人吉藩",
   "domain_en": "Hitoyoshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p104_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 104,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（人吉）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Hitoyoshi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka and land-tax assessment (Hitoyoshi)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the fascicle-7 (藩制一覧表第七) land-assessment block for Hitoyoshi han (人吉藩), a small Higo domain. Its base assessed yield (草高) is 22,100 koku; three supplementary increments (外) — komidaka/shinden 35,446.9083 koku, the field-tax soybean and cash-payment portion 3,363.05815 koku, and retainer/shrine-temple land reclassified as increase-yield 2,509.36841 koku — bring the total assessed yield (合高) to 63,419.33486 koku, and the three 外 plus 草高 sum exactly to that total. The ten-year-average regular land tax is 23,995.57356 koku of rice (正租米) together with 1,179.62751 koku of soybeans (大豆). A bracketed editorial note records that village count, the governor's family, and transport vessels were \"not recorded\" (記セス) for this domain."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitoyoshi_lower_p105_right",
   "sequence": 438,
   "domain_canonical": "人吉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "人吉藩",
   "domain_en": "Hitoyoshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p105_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 105,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（人吉）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle 7 (Hitoyoshi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hitoyoshi domain fiscal record: land tax, cash equivalents, and households",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fiscal survey (fascicle 7) for Hitoyoshi domain (Higo province, Sagara clan). It records a regular land-tax assessment (正租高) of 23,995.57 koku; of this, a soybean portion of 1,179.63 koku is valued at 4,718.5 ryō (five-year average, 4 ryō per koku) and re-expressed as 589.81 koku of rice, yielding an actual-rice figure (現石米) of 24,585.39 koku (23,995.57 + 589.81). It also reports two cash-tax figures — 1,134.19 ryō (金) and 2,904.5 ryō in miscellaneous-tax cash (雜稅金) — and a household total of 11,299 (總戸數). A marginal note states that the following nine lines are red-ink annotations entered per the survey of 1870/8/3 and that miscellaneous taxes are otherwise not itemized."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitoyoshi_lower_p105_left",
   "sequence": 439,
   "domain_canonical": "人吉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "人吉",
   "domain_en": "Hitoyoshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p105_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 105,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（人吉）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle 7 (Hitoyoshi)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hitoyoshi population and household counts by legal status",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the Hitoyoshi (人吉藩) return in Fascicle 7 (藩制一覧表第七) of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, tabulating population and household counts by legal status. The total registered population is 53,577 (27,265 male, 26,312 female). It divides into samurai (士族: 3,368 people in 721 households), lower-rank retainers (卒族: 14,930 in 3,417 households), Shinto shrine personnel (社人: 547 in 127 households), Shugendō mountain ascetics (修驗: 142 in 38 households), Buddhist temple clergy (寺院: 94 in 48 households), and blind persons (盲人: 65 in 18 households). Several status blocks carry a three-way split (a status specialist plus male and female members); the shrine-personnel total of 547 is marked by the 1928 editor because its stated parts (社人 211 + female 271 + male 62) sum to 544."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitoyoshi_lower_p106_right",
   "sequence": 440,
   "domain_canonical": "人吉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "人吉藩",
   "domain_en": "Hitoyoshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p106_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 106,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（久居）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle 7 (Hisai)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hitoyoshi minority-status demographics; Hisai kokudaka opening",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes the Hitoyoshi (人吉藩) entry and opens the Hisai (久居藩) entry. For Hitoyoshi it records the tail demographic fields: 2 goze (blind female performer) households totaling 21 persons, 30 eta (outcaste) households totaling 194 persons (94 male, 100 female), and 273 shrines; the village count and the governor's family are both marked \"not recorded\" (記セス) and warships as \"none\" (ナシ). The ○久居藩 marker then begins Hisai, whose nominal yield (草高) is 43,000 koku, followed by an \"of which\" (内) breakdown of deducted lands amounting to 121.519 koku and 30.842 koku (main-village samurai/temple residence lots and other miscellaneous deductions). The running header files the spread under Fascicle 7 (久居), and the printed book-page number is 188."
  },
  {
   "id": "hitoyoshi_lower_p244_right",
   "sequence": 441,
   "domain_canonical": "人吉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "人吉藩",
   "domain_en": "Hitoyoshi",
   "image": "images/lower_p244_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 244,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（人吉、久居）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, fascicle 9 (Hitoyoshi, Hisai)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Military establishment and domain officials",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 464 of fascicle 9, whose running head names Hitoyoshi and Hisai. The five columns standing to the right of the ○人吉藩 marker close the preceding domain's military return: three battalions (one of mixed shizoku and quasi-shizoku at four fifty-man platoons, two of artillery sotsu at six fifty-man platoons each, 800 men in all), eight heavy guns attached to each battalion, four platoons of forty-eight artillery sotsu (192 men), and two thirty-man platoons that still keep the old archery drill (60 men). Hitoyoshi's own entry then gives its councillor establishment — 2 senior councillors, 4 acting senior councillors with 2 posts vacant, 6 junior councillors of whom 4 are in post and 2 unrecorded, and 6 acting junior councillors with 2 posts vacant — followed by ten names in the lower register, one of them, Shingū Chikuma, also marked as the domain's delegate to the Kōgisho. Hitoyoshi's forces close the entry at four cannon with twenty-eight gunners and four rifle platoons of sixty men each (240), and the ○久居藩 marker in the leftmost column opens Hisai, whose data begins on the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "hisai_lower_p106_left",
   "sequence": 442,
   "domain_canonical": "久居藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久居",
   "domain_en": "Hisai",
   "image": "images/lower_p106_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 106,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（久居）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Hisai)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hisai domain — kokudaka assessment and tax yields (continuation)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the Hisai (久居藩) entry in fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran; it carries no domain marker, since the ○久居藩 heading falls on the preceding page, and the running header (久居) confirms the ownership. It records the domain's land assessment — an assessed high (高) of 42,878.481 koku and a new-field high (新田高) of 5,415.896 koku, against a deduction (引去) of 90.677 koku at Heki (戸木) village — together with its tax yields: a regular land tax (正租) of 19,170.4306 koku and a miscellaneous rice tax (雜稅米) of 585.739 koku, each given as a five-year average, plus cash levies of 314 ryō and 932 mon. Editorial notes flag these figures as vermillion marginalia in the original manuscript and record the averaging years (the boar-through-dragon cycle, omitting the tiger year, for the land tax; the consecutive rat-through-dragon cycle for the miscellaneous tax). Note: the assessed high reads 七十八 (…878), correcting the project dataset's 七十九 (…879)."
  },
  {
   "id": "hisai_lower_p107_right",
   "sequence": 443,
   "domain_canonical": "久居藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久居",
   "domain_en": "Hisai",
   "image": "images/lower_p107_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 107,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（久居）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview Table, Fascicle 7 (Hisai)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hisai domain: land yield, tax, households, and population (with red-ink variant figures)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the entry for Hisai domain (久居藩) in Fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran. It records a total assessed yield (惣高) of 58,686.165 koku — of which 81.134 koku is extension land (延高) — a current/actual yield (現石) of 24,539.1216 koku, miscellaneous tax cash (雜稅金) of 319 ryō plus 5 kan 962 mon of copper cash, 8,285 total households (總戸數), and a population of 38,310 (male 19,281, female 19,298). A red-ink marginal note (\"one edition states\") supplies a variant population of 37,878 (male 19,018, female 18,860). Samurai (士族) households number 297 with a samurai population of 1,399 (male 708, female 691)."
  },
  {
   "id": "hisai_lower_p107_left",
   "sequence": 444,
   "domain_canonical": "久居藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久居",
   "domain_en": "Hisai",
   "image": "images/lower_p107_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 107,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（久居）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran Table, Fascicle 7 (Hisai) — outer-margin running header",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Status demographics — households and population by class",
   "page_summary_en": "This left page continues the demographic block of 久居藩 (Hisai, a 15,000-koku Tōdō sub-domain of Tsu in Ise) in Fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran. In ruled columns it records, by status, both households and population: sotsu-class 155 households / 875 people (male 422, female 453), shrine-attendant households 17 / 98, temples 247 with 434 clergy, eta 271 households / 1,374, and hinin 25 households / 101. Six lines of red-ink marginalia (欄外朱書) — flagged by an editorial note that their date is not recorded — add a shizoku count of 1,402 (male 703, female 699) and restate the sotsu class as 1,487 (male 876, female 611), the latter conflicting with the ruled table's sotsu population of 875. Every male-plus-female split reconciles to its stated total except the temple line, whose printed components (275+178) exceed the printed total of 434."
  },
  {
   "id": "hisai_lower_p244_left",
   "sequence": 445,
   "domain_canonical": "久居藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久居藩",
   "domain_en": "Hisai",
   "image": "images/lower_p244_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 244,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（廣瀬）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Nine (Hirose)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop return",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle nine of the 1870 domain survey, printed book-page 465. Almost the whole leaf belongs to Hisai Domain in Ise, whose entry opened with the ○久居藩 marker at the end of the facing page: twelve councillors are named — one senior councillor, Tōdō Naokado of the domain's own ruling house; one acting senior councillor, Okamoto Tei; six junior councillors; and four acting junior councillors — and one of them, Agawa Rokurō, carries the interlinear note 留守官届ニナシ, that he does not appear in the caretaker official's return. Hisai's troop return follows: 60 officers, 64 soldiers, 15 bandsmen, 540 rank-and-file (of whom ten platoons of riflemen at 48 men to the platoon, or 480), 48 gunners and 12 drummers, 739 men in all, with no grand total printed. The single maru-marker on the page, ○廣瀬藩, stands about two-thirds of the way across; to its left Hirose Domain in Izumo begins with two senior councillors, Iwasaki Shin'ichirō and Kōyama Kanzaemon."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirose_lower_p108_right",
   "sequence": 446,
   "domain_canonical": "廣瀬藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "廣瀬藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirose",
   "image": "images/lower_p108_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 108,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（廣瀬）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 (Hirose)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hirose kokudaka accounting; Hisai religious/administrative demographics",
   "page_summary_en": "The page is split by the ○廣瀬藩 domain-marker near center. Everything to the right of it (read first) is the tail of the previous domain, 久居藩 (Hisai): shrine attendants 134 (M81/F53), Buddhist monks 375 (M213/F162), nuns 6, shrines 132 (of which 21 are Engishiki 式内), governor's-family 5 (M2/F3), 93 villages, and a declaration of no warships/steamers. Everything to its left is 廣瀬藩 (Hirose, an Izumo branch domain of 元高 30,000 koku): assessed gross (草高) 33,128.09 koku, a 萬引 deduction of 13,376.991 koku, a five-year average crop-loss (毛損) of 4,514.032 koku (Kōshi 1864–Boshin 1868), a remaining assessment (殘高) of 19,751.099 koku (including 480.224 koku of new field, 新田), and an actual tax yield (物成) of 9,994.491 koku at a rate of roughly 免六ツ六厘. The kokudaka arithmetic checks: 草高 33,128.090 − 萬引 13,376.991 = 殘高 19,751.099."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirose_lower_p108_left",
   "sequence": 447,
   "domain_canonical": "廣瀬藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "廣瀬藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirose",
   "image": "images/lower_p108_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 108,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（廣瀬）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Hirose)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hirose domain — population, households, land tax and levies",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the fascicle-7 (civil and economic) return for Hirose domain (廣瀬藩), a sub-domain of Matsue in Izumo Province. It records a population of 26,350 (14,089 male, 12,261 female) living in 5,873 households — among them 152 shizoku and 210 sotsu households, 30 shrine-family houses, 71 temples with 17 subsidiary hermitages, and 102 outcaste (鉢屋・穢多・隱亡) houses — with a marginal variant giving the total population as 26,396. Fiscal figures include a regular land tax (正租) of 12,338.072 koku; three surtaxes (口米 199.89, corvée rice 夫米 1,194.794, and 948.897 koku of assessed rice); a miscellaneous tax (雜税) of 1,250 bales of rice; and cash levies (錢) of 15,522.985 kan."
  },
  {
   "id": "hirose_lower_p109_right",
   "sequence": 448,
   "domain_canonical": "廣瀬藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "廣瀬藩",
   "domain_en": "Hirose",
   "image": "images/lower_p109_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 109,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（日出）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 7 (Hiji)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Hirose population-by-status and shrine/temple land; opening of the Hiji fiscal block",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the tail of the Hirose (廣瀬藩) fascicle-7 entry and the opening of the Hiji (日出藩) entry, divided by the ○日出藩 maru-marker. Hirose's block records population by status — 士族 748 (M357/F391) and 卒族 761 (M396/F365) — plus religious personnel 社人 162, 寺侶 247, 鉢屋穢多隱亡 382, 修驗 8, the governor's family (知事家族) 5, and 167 shrines, followed by shrine/temple land 社寺領 122.276 koku (社領 78.558 + 寺領 43.718). Left of its marker, Hiji opens with a nominal 元高 of 25,000 koku and an assessed 草高 of 27,500.2203 koku (new fields included). The running header names Hiji and the printed leaf number is 194."
  },
  {
   "id": "mori_lower_p114_left",
   "sequence": 449,
   "domain_canonical": "母里藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "母里藩",
   "domain_en": "Mori",
   "image": "images/lower_p114_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 114,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（母里）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 7 (Mori)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Land-tax accounts (fascicle 7): fief assessment, deductions, and rice/tax totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This page-half records the fascicle-7 (land-tax) accounts of Mori Domain (母里藩), a 10,000-koku sub-domain of Matsue in Izumo province. The nominal fief (受領高) is 10,000 koku, while the surveyed total of administered land (支配地總高) is 9,560.931 koku; deducting an assessed 2,118.992 koku (removed by the man-biki proportional-reduction method) yields the net assessed yield (殘高) of 7,441.939 koku — an internally consistent figure (9,560.931 − 2,118.992 = 7,441.939). Tax entries include principal land-tax rice (正租米) 3,943.993 koku (also given as 365.17176 bales), miscellaneous-tax rice (雜稅米) 863.341 koku, and a remainder (殘) of 4,792.36224 koku, several qualified as five-year averages inclusive of crop loss (毛損). A single maru-marker (○母里藩) at the top-right opens the domain, so all data on this page-half belong to Mori."
  },
  {
   "id": "mori_lower_p115_right",
   "sequence": 450,
   "domain_canonical": "母里藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "母里藩",
   "domain_en": "Mori",
   "image": "images/lower_p115_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 115,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（母里）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-System Survey Table, Fascicle 7 (Mori)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "母里藩 cash receipts, population, and household counts (fascicle 7)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-7 (藩制一覧表第七) entry for Mori Domain (母里藩), a 10,000-koku branch house of Matsue in Izumo. It records cash receipts of 102.5 ryō from sundry transit dues (諸運上, stated as equal to 100 koku) plus 50 ryō from raw-wax sale proceeds (生蠟代出目金), summing to a combined 152.5 ryō (合金), along with an additional 2,500 tawara of rice that a marginal note says was received annually from the main house as storehouse rice. Demographic totals give a population of 8,222 (4,269 male, 3,953 female) in 1,908 total households, of which 66 are shizoku households (241 persons: 120 male, 121 female), 88 sotsu households (295 persons: 152 male, 143 female), and 2 foot-soldier households. A double-column note beside the shizoku household count flags that the main text (本書) gives the figure as 211 persons, but that the itemized breakdown is followed here."
  },
  {
   "id": "mori_lower_p115_left",
   "sequence": 451,
   "domain_canonical": "母里藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "母里藩",
   "domain_en": "Mori",
   "image": "images/lower_p115_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 115,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（母里）",
   "page_header_en": "Overview of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 7 (Mori)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Population by status group, temple/shrine counts, governor's family (Mori domain, fascicle 7 demographics)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-7 demographic return for Mori domain (母里藩), a small 10,000-koku branch domain of Matsue in Izumo province. It records population by status group: foot-soldiers (步卒) 75 persons, all male, continued from the preceding page; shrine-service (社務) 13 households with 72 persons (32 male / 40 female); Buddhist temples (寺院) 19, with a temple population of 59 (39 male / 20 female); the hachiya-eta outcaste group (鉢屋穢多) 43 households with 248 persons (124 male / 124 female); and non-persons (非人) with no households but 2 persons (male). The governor's family (知事家族) numbered 3 (2 male / 1 female). Village count and shrine count are both entered as \"not recorded\" (記セス), and the domain reports no transport vessels (運輸舶ナシ). All male/female splits reconcile with their status totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "mori_lower_p246_left",
   "sequence": 452,
   "domain_canonical": "母里藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "母里藩",
   "domain_en": "Mori",
   "image": "images/lower_p246_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 246,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（母里）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Mori, Izumo)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 469 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle 9, closes the officials return of 森藩 (Bungo) and then opens the entry for 母里藩 (Izumo) at the maru-marker. The 森藩 remnant lists four 少參事 (水野古後, 村上久, 加藤量平 and 大島丹下, the last annotated ナシ) together with one 權少參事 (村上半下), and it ends with the dating note 「右巳十二月廿七日屆」, that is, reported on the 27th day of the 12th month of the snake year (Meiji 2, 1869). For 母里藩 the sheet records 2 cannon with 12 gunners (2 of them overseers, plus 4 labourers), a standing force of one platoon of 50 men and a reserve force of one platoon of 50 men with 8 further men attached, summarised as 2 guns and 2 rifle platoons, so 100 men in the two platoons. Its official roster names eight men: two 大參事, three 權大參事, one 少參事 and two 權少參事."
  },
  {
   "id": "sendai_lower_p116_right",
   "sequence": 453,
   "domain_canonical": "仙臺藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "仙臺藩",
   "domain_en": "Sendai",
   "image": "images/lower_p116_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 116,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（仙臺）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Sendai)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Sendai population, households, and status/clerical counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-7 demographic return for 仙臺藩 (Sendai); the domain's kokudaka is expressly left unrecorded (\"草高等不詳細\"). Sendai reports 38,962 households and a total population of 238,893 (123,143 male, 115,750 female). Status and clerical sub-counts include a samurai (兵士) population of 29,408 living in 4,262 dwellings, a foot-soldier (兵卒) population of 13,091 in 3,050 dwellings, 683 shrine-family (社家) members in 124 households, 998 mountain-ascetics (修驗) attached to 236 halls, 43 yin-yang diviners (陰陽師) in 17 households, 694 Buddhist temples, and 141 eta/outcast-hut households. Every male/female split reconciles exactly to its parent total."
  },
  {
   "id": "zeze_lower_p116_left",
   "sequence": 454,
   "domain_canonical": "膳所藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "膳所藩",
   "domain_en": "Zeze",
   "image": "images/lower_p116_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 116,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（膳所）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Zeze)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Zeze domain kokudaka and tax revenue; tail demographic fields of Sendai",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page (printed page 209) straddles two domains. To the right of the ○膳所藩 maru-marker are the closing fields of the previous domain, 仙臺藩 (Sendai): Buddhist clergy 2,331 persons (2,219 male / 112 female), the outcaste-class population 1,138 (669 male / 469 female), 990 Shinto shrines, a governor's household of 7 (6 male / 1 female), and a note that no warships are held. Left of the marker begins 膳所藩 (Zeze), located in Ōmi and Kawachi provinces (146 villages across 9 districts) with an original assessed kokudaka of 60,000 koku. Its recorded figures are a nominal (kusadaka) kokudaka of 65,811.7681 koku, regular land tax of 24,251.5668 koku of rice, miscellaneous tax of 970.0702 koku of rice plus cash of 535 ryō 3 bu in gold and 834 kan 66 mon in copper cash, with the cash figures given as a five-year average."
  },
  {
   "id": "zeze_lower_p117_right",
   "sequence": 455,
   "domain_canonical": "膳所藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "膳所藩",
   "domain_en": "Zeze",
   "image": "images/lower_p117_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 117,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（膳所）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Zeze)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Zeze domain — population, status households, temples, and land-tax (fascicle 7)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page continues the Fascicle 7 entry for Zeze domain (膳所藩) in Ōmi province; there is no maru-marker, so every column belongs to Zeze. It records a total population of 45,723 (22,756 male + 22,967 female, which sum exactly) living in 10,185 households, of which 451 are samurai (shizoku) and 527 are foot-soldier (sotsu) households, alongside 74 shrine-family households, 273 eta and 80 hinin outcaste households, and 293 temples with 6 nunneries. A separate leftmost column gives the samurai population as 1,858 persons (871 male + 987 female). The land-tax figures — a regular-plus-miscellaneous grand total of 25,299.10 koku, regular tax of 27,872.01 koku, and miscellaneous rice tax of 1,194.83 koku — are five-year averages (years of the Rooster, Dog, Boar, Ox, and Rabbit) that appeared in the margin of the original manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "sekiyado_lower_p117_left",
   "sequence": 456,
   "domain_canonical": "關宿藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "關宿藩",
   "domain_en": "Sekiyado",
   "image": "images/lower_p117_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 117,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（關宿）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 7 (Sekiyado)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Zeze status-group demographic tail meeting the start of the Sekiyado kokudaka/land-tax block",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page straddles a domain boundary in Fascicle 7. To the right of the ○關宿藩 marker sit the closing demographic columns of the previous domain, Zeze (膳所藩): status-group headcounts for lower retainers (卒族 1,787), shrine servants (社人 340), Buddhist clergy (寺侶 695), nuns (尼 17), outcaste groups (穢多 1,244; 非人 342), 110 shrines, the governor's family (3), and a \"no warships held\" (船艦不所持) notation, each split into male/female sub-counts that reconcile to their totals. To the left, Sekiyado's own block opens with a base kokudaka of 43,000 koku (本高) drawn from 3 districts of Shimōsa, 2 of Shimotsuke and 2 of Hitachi (131 villages, new fields included), an assessed gross yield (草高) of 52,386.28213 koku, and a regular land tax of 5,960.4342 koku of rice plus 6,775.76354 kan in eiraku cash (rice-equivalent 8,469.70443 koku). The printed page number is 211."
  },
  {
   "id": "sekiyado_lower_p118_right",
   "sequence": 457,
   "domain_canonical": "關宿藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "關宿藩",
   "domain_en": "Sekiyado",
   "image": "images/lower_p118_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 118,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（關宿）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 7 (Sekiyado)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Sekiyado domain miscellaneous tax (雜税) receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-7 revenue return for Sekiyado domain (關宿藩) and is given over entirely to miscellaneous taxes (雜税). It opens with an \"of which\" breakdown carried over from the preceding page — 2,679.266 koku of rice and 283.822 kan in eiraku cash — annotated that only the fixed-assessment portion is stable and the remainder varies from year to year. A first 雜税 heading then governs four lines that the compilers flag as having been written in red ink in the original: 29.25 ryō plus 490,706 mon in petty imposts (小物成), 143.125 ryō plus 36,721 mon from timber sales (材木代), 441.125 ryō from domestic tea manufacture (國産製茶), and 212.375 ryō from licence fees (運上類). A second block, headed \"the Horse-year return states\" and marked as having stood in the margin of the original manuscript, gives the same category as 853.608 koku of rice, 746.625 ryō in gold, 1,341.832 kan in eiraku, and 584.508 kan in copper cash; the closing 合計 label prints here but its total carries over to the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "sekiyado_lower_p118_left",
   "sequence": 458,
   "domain_canonical": "關宿藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "關宿藩",
   "domain_en": "Sekiyado",
   "image": "images/lower_p118_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 118,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第七（關宿）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table (Fascicle) 7 — (Sekiyado)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Sekiyado domain — households, status populations, temples/shrines, and tax totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a continuation leaf for Sekiyado domain (關宿藩) in fascicle 7 of the Hansei Ichiran (1870 domain survey). It records 9,605 total households; the shizoku (230 households / 1,185 persons), sotsu (324 households / 1,016 persons) and shrine-attendant (272 persons) sub-populations with male/female splits; 191 town-watchman and outcaste (eta) dwellings; and 292 temple-and-shrine buildings (38 of them prayer-halls and yamabushi residences) holding 642.3 koku of temple-shrine land. A combined regular-plus-miscellaneous tax total of 15,552.11009 koku is annotated as actual-rice tax (朱黒印 grant lands not separately distinguished), and a monetary figure of 2,146 ryō (plus ei-cash) carries over from the preceding page. The 人口 grand total (27,805 with its male/female breakdown) is NOT printed on this leaf — only the section header and the status sub-counts appear here."
  },
  {
   "id": "sekiyado_lower_p247_left",
   "sequence": 459,
   "domain_canonical": "關宿藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "關宿藩",
   "domain_en": "Sekiyado",
   "image": "images/lower_p247_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 247,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（關宿）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Sekiyado)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "The page closes the fascicle-9 entry for Zeze Domain and opens that for Sekiyado. Zeze's remaining officials are three 少參事 (junior councillors) — Kawai Jirō, Shigene Yagara and Yūki Inao — and three 權少參事 (acting junior councillors) — Shibata Aiemon, Igari Emori and Tomioka Kenjirō; its military line records one battalion of 337 men, and a top-margin note breaks that figure into 164 shizoku and 173 sotsu (164 + 173 = 337). Sekiyado's entry opens with five named officials (Kamei, Kondō, Tomita, Hafuto and Kinoshita) and a troop line of 168 soldiers and 50 rank-and-file, 218 men in all. A small-type source note, 留守官屆 (\"report of the resident officer\"), then heads a second, tabulated roster of nine Sekiyado officials whose office assignments do not fully agree with the first list."
  },
  {
   "id": "susaka_lower_p119_right",
   "sequence": 460,
   "domain_canonical": "須坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "須坂藩",
   "domain_en": "Suzaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p119_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 119,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（須坂）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 7 (Susaka)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "End of Sekiyado's population tally; opening of Susaka's kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes the fascicle-7 population return for Sekiyado Domain and opens the corresponding return for Susaka Domain. For Sekiyado it records the residual status categories — 330 Buddhist clergy (295 male, 35 female), 114 mountain ascetics (62 male, 52 female), 6 shrine mediums, 8 nuns, and 853 town-outcaste watchmen and eta (433 male, 420 female) — and closes with a total population of 49,058, against male and female components of 25,055 and 24,002 that sum to 49,057; a bracketed editorial mark printed beside the disputed digit flags the discrepancy. Three absence notations follow: no record of the governor's household, no shrine count, and no warships. To the left of the ○須坂藩 marker, Susaka opens with 13 villages and a gross assessed yield (草高) of 12,153.3708 koku, partitioned into 12,138.3708 koku of domain-administered land and 15 koku held as Kōkoku-ji temple land; a nested entry notes that 2,080.5208 koku of that total is newly reclaimed paddy added by resurvey."
  },
  {
   "id": "suzaka_lower_p119_left",
   "sequence": 461,
   "domain_canonical": "須坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "須坂藩",
   "domain_en": "Suzaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p119_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 119,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（須坂）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Seven (Suzaka)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Suzaka tax revenue (five-year average), households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of Fascicle 7 records Suzaka Domain's fiscal and demographic returns, all revenue figures given as a five-year average (五ヶ年平均). Land tax in rice (正租米) is 4,217.8779 koku and miscellaneous tax rice (諸税米) 6.5636 koku, summing exactly to the printed total (合) of 4,224.4415 koku; 12.6 koku of assessed land is recorded as tax-exempt (除地). On the cash side, surcharges (諸掛物永) of 70.783 kan, miscellaneous tax cash of 734.394 kan and sundry income (雜入永) of 3 kan sum exactly to the stated total of 808.177 kan, which the entry then converts to 101.0221 koku of rice (此米) at a rate of precisely 8 kan-mon per koku. The domain reports 1,518 households and a population of 11,315, of whom 5,489 are male and 5,826 female."
  },
  {
   "id": "suzaka_lower_p120_right",
   "sequence": 462,
   "domain_canonical": "須坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "須坂",
   "domain_en": "Suzaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p120_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 120,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（須坂）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 7 (Suzaka)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Suzaka domain status-group households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-7 civil register for Suzaka domain (Shinano), giving household counts and paired male/female populations for each status group. Shizoku number 98 households and 431 people (213 male, 218 female); sotsuzoku 128 households and 403 people (214 male, 189 female). The religious establishment is small: 2 Shinto-priest households with 12 people, 21 Buddhist temples with 150 clergy (94 male, 56 female), and 2 Shugendō households with 4 people. The outcaste registers close the page with 43 eta households totalling 239 people (114 male, 125 female) and 7 hinin households."
  },
  {
   "id": "suzaka_lower_p120_left",
   "sequence": 463,
   "domain_canonical": "須坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "須坂藩",
   "domain_en": "Suzaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p120_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 120,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第七（須坂）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 7 (Suzaka)",
   "table_number": 7,
   "page_topic": "Suzaka: outcaste headcount, shrines, governor's household, no vessels",
   "page_summary_en": "This sparse left-hand leaf closes the 須坂藩 (Suzaka) entry in fascicle 7 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran-hyō; it carries no maru-marker, so every column belongs to the domain already running from the preceding leaf, as the running header 藩制一覽表第七（須坂）confirms. Read right to left, it records a status sub-population of 44 persons (25 male, 19 female — the two components sum exactly to the printed total), 29 Shinto shrines, and a governor's household of 9 persons (2 male, 7 female, again summing to the total). The final column is the absence notation 舶ナシ, declaring that Suzaka held no vessels. The 44-person figure is far too small to be Suzaka's whole population and corresponds to the outcaste (非人) category whose heading falls on the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "suzaka_lower_p248_right",
   "sequence": 464,
   "domain_canonical": "須坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "須坂藩",
   "domain_en": "Suzaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p248_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 248,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百七十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（須坂）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 9 (Suzaka)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "The leaf carries the tail of Sekiyado Domain's Fascicle 9 officials roster and then, at the ○須坂藩 marker, the opening of Suzaka Domain's entry. Sekiyado contributes five further names: Uetake Eiichi, who closes the junior-councillor list begun on the facing leaf, and Ambo Seisuke, Inoue Yagara, Aoki Tsunenosuke and Murai Monjirō under the acting junior councillorship. Suzaka records 2 senior councillors, 2 acting senior councillors, 1 junior councillor and 2 acting junior councillors, seven men in all, and every printed count is matched by the names set beneath it. Its force is 32 heishi and 74 heisotsu, 106 men in total, organised as 2 rifle companies with 2 cannon."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwakuni_upper_p023_right",
   "sequence": 465,
   "domain_canonical": "岩國藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩國藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwakuni",
   "image": "images/upper_p023_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 23,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（岩國）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran (Overview of Domain Administration), Fascicle 1 — Iwakuni",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Household and population counts by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page closes the Izuhara (Tsushima) entry and then opens the entry for Iwakuni at the maru-marker ○岩國藩. The Izuhara columns give a carried-over status group of 679 people (460 male, 219 female), 110 outcaste (eta) households entered as an addition with a population of 496 (260 male, 236 female), a military establishment of 470 men organised as six infantry platoons and two artillery sections, and a closing territorial note recording 3,142 households and 14,639 people (7,536 male, 7,103 female) in Tsushima province. The Iwakuni entry begins with the headings 草高 and 高 printed without any figures, then lists the domain's status groups: 874 samurai (shizoku) households with 3,533 people, 587 sotsu households with 2,715 people, 456 rear-vassal (baisotsu) households with 1,764 people, and 48 rural-samurai (gōshi) households with 185 people. Every male-plus-female split on the page reconciles exactly with its printed total."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwakuni_lower_p122_right",
   "sequence": 466,
   "domain_canonical": "岩國藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩國藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwakuni",
   "image": "images/lower_p122_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 122,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（岩國）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Iwakuni)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Iwakuni domain officials: office head-counts and roster",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the fascicle-8 (domain officials) entry for Iwakuni Domain (岩國藩), marked by the circle-marker ○岩國藩 at the head of the block. The upper register prints four office lines: 知事 (governor) with no figure recorded, 大參事 (senior councillor) at 2 posts annotated 當時欠員 \"at present vacant,\" 權大參事 (acting senior councillor) at 4, and 少參事 (junior councillor) at 7. The lower register prints eleven personal names in a single run — 宮莊將美, 香川景逸, 目加田喜助, 鹽谷鼎, 都野新左衞門, 今田彦馬, 藤田浪江, 三須文郎, 中村彦兵衞, 安田源三 and 大草終吉 — a count that reconciles exactly with the 4 acting senior councillors plus 7 junior councillors, the two vacant senior councillor seats supplying no names. Only one domain appears on the leaf; nothing prints to the right of the marker except the running header and the folio number 二百二十 (page 220)."
  },
  {
   "id": "imabari_upper_p023_left",
   "sequence": 467,
   "domain_canonical": "今治藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "今治藩",
   "domain_en": "Imabari",
   "image": "images/upper_p023_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 23,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（今治）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Survey of Domain Administration), Fascicle 1 (Imabari)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Imabari kokudaka and population, after the tail of Iwakuni's religious households and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "The right half of the leaf closes out Iwakuni domain's fascicle-1 return: 51 shrine-priest households (277 persons), 41 mountain-ascetic households (155 persons), 65 blind-monk households (106 persons), 28 shrines, two rifle battalions of 800 men (a platoon reckoned at 50, plus 70 officers and staff), and one artillery battery of 36 men with 11 officers. The maru-marker ○今治藩, annotated （屆日限未詳）\"date of return not recorded\", then opens Imabari domain. Imabari's assessed yield is given as 43,234.814 koku, resolving into a base 35,000 koku, 1,808.057 koku of included yield (込高), and 6,426.757 koku of newly surveyed reclaimed land — the three components sum exactly to the total. Its population is 15,681 households and 74,994 persons, split 38,247 male and 36,747 female, which likewise sums exactly."
  },
  {
   "id": "imabari_lower_p122_left",
   "sequence": 468,
   "domain_canonical": "今治藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "今治藩",
   "domain_en": "Imabari",
   "image": "images/lower_p122_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 122,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（今治）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran, Fascicle 8 (Imabari)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military units (Iwakuni tail, Imabari opening)",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso carries the end of the 岩國藩 (Iwakuni) entry and the opening of the 今治藩 (Imabari) entry in Fascicle 8 of the Hansei ichiran, printed book-page 221. Right of the ○今治藩 marker, Iwakuni's roster closes with three acting junior councillors (權少參事) — Kasai Jirōemon, Hara Shichiemon and Moriwaki Taizō — preceded by two further named officials, Katsura Kanzaemon and Katsura Kurōbee, whose office heading falls on the facing recto. Iwakuni's forces are recorded as two rifle battalions (銃兵二大隊) at 800 men per battalion and 50 men per company, i.e. 1,600 men, with 7 additional officers, plus one artillery battery (砲隊一砲隊) of 36 men with 11 additional officers. Left of the marker, Imabari's entry begins with its governor Hisamatsu of Junior Fifth Rank (知事 久松從五位), senior councillor Hisamatsu Osamu (大參事 久松修) and acting senior councillor Kidokoro Chikara (權大參事 城所力)."
  },
  {
   "id": "iiyama_upper_p024_left",
   "sequence": 469,
   "domain_canonical": "飯山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯山藩",
   "domain_en": "Iiyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p024_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 24,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（飯山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 1 (Iiyama)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Iiyama domain: reclaimed-land assessment, land and miscellaneous taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf continues the entry for Iiyama Domain (Shinano, Honda house) in fascicle 1 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran-hyō; the ○飯山藩 marker and the 草高 column stand on the facing right-hand half, so every column here belongs to Iiyama. Reading right to left, the domain reports 15,192.297 koku of newly reclaimed paddy above its 20,000-koku nominal assessment, a regular rice tax of 11,513.433 koku struck as a five-year average from Genji 1 (1864) to Meiji 1 (1868), and miscellaneous taxes of 63.814 koku of rice, 1 ryō 2 bu in gold, 20 kan 123 monme 5 fun 4 rin in silver, and 19,548 mon in copper cash. The population section gives 6,739 households and 30,365 people, split 14,785 male and 15,580 female, with 30 Shinto priests, 180 Buddhist monks and 18 yamabushi among the men and 5 nuns and 2 miko among the women. Printed notes state that samurai and sotsu, and the hinin and eta, are all excluded from those totals; the outcaste groups are then listed apart as 3 hinin households, 27 hinin persons (12 male, 15 female), and 56 eta households."
  },
  {
   "id": "iiyama_lower_p123_right",
   "sequence": 470,
   "domain_canonical": "飯山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯山藩",
   "domain_en": "Iiyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p123_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 123,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（飯山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyo, Fascicle 8 (Iiyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 222 of the Hansei Ichiran fascicle 8 (officials and troops), carrying the tail of the Imabari Domain entry and the opening of the Iiyama Domain entry. The right-hand columns, which precede the ○飯山藩 marker, complete Imabari's roster with three shōsanji (Ogawa Toshima, Taga Otoya, Ikeuchi Shigeka) and record Imabari's forces: 15 platoons of 50 men each (750 troops), of which 5 platoons are shizoku and the remainder sotsu, plus one platoon of gunners (shizoku) and one drum-and-bugle platoon (sotsu). Left of the marker, Iiyama Domain lists its governorship (chiji) as blank and staffs one daisanji, three gon-daisanji and one shōsanji — five posts matched by exactly five names, from Asano Heima through Kashiwabara Gengoemon. Iiyama's own military figures do not appear here; they continue on the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "inuyama_upper_p025_left",
   "sequence": 471,
   "domain_canonical": "犬山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "犬山藩",
   "domain_en": "Inuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p025_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 25,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（犬山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 1 (Inuyama)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Inuyama domain: rice-tax receipts and household/population returns",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Inuyama (犬山藩) entry in fascicle 1 of the Hansei Ichiran and carries no domain marker of its own; the running header identifies the block. The rice-tax group records a main land tax (正租米) of 12,519.81964 koku, averaged over the five years 1864-1868, plus miscellaneous taxes (雜税米) of 324.66971 koku reckoned at eight ryō the koku, for combined receipts (合現米) of 12,844.48935 koku — the three figures reconcile exactly. The demographic group returns 11,782 households and 53,302 people (26,408 male, 26,894 female), with outcaste populations tallied separately and outside the totals: 47 hinin households and 123 hinin persons, 22 eta houses and 91 eta persons. The remaining columns count 190 shrines (with 27 shrine-priest households, 143 persons), 108 temples (with 15 shugendō, 18 chapel-keeper and 1 onmyōji establishments and a religious population of 457), 62 villages, and a warrior-status (士族) population of 1,364 in 312 households."
  },
  {
   "id": "inuyama_lower_p123_left",
   "sequence": 472,
   "domain_canonical": "犬山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "犬山藩",
   "domain_en": "Inuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p123_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 123,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（犬山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 8 (Inuyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of fascicle 8 carries the close of Iiyama Domain's entry and the opening of Inuyama Domain's. To the right of the ○犬山藩 marker, Iiyama's official roster ends with two acting junior councillors (權少參事 二人), named below as Honda Kozaemon and Ishihara Misao, followed by an editorial note that the names above are not recorded, and then Iiyama's military establishment: a rifle corps of six platoons, two cannon, and 165 troops including officers. Left of the marker, Inuyama's entry begins: the governorship is recorded with the name lacking (名欠), with one senior councillor (Takada Tsutomu) and four acting senior councillors, of whom Chiba Takeshi and Koike Masato are named, plus two Kōgisho delegates, Honda Hikosaburō and Yoshida Shū. Inuyama's junior councillors and its own military (six platoons, 324 troops) continue on the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "inuyama_lower_p124_right",
   "sequence": 473,
   "domain_canonical": "犬山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "犬山藩",
   "domain_en": "Inuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p124_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 124,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（出石）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Izushi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 224 of the lower volume closes out the fascicle-8 entry for Inuyama Domain (犬山藩) and then opens the entry for Izushi Domain (出石藩). Inuyama's official roster is completed here with 少参事 4 persons — a figure the 1928 editors flag 〔sic〕 because five names stand beneath it (神谷辛歲, 小林守男, 横井恰, 山田莊平, 八木銀次郎) — and 権少参事 5 persons (水野鎬, 平尾義造, 高田大次郎, 小川渉, 水谷眞須美); two of the shōsanji, Yokoi and Yamada, carry the small side-annotation 公用人兼, \"concurrently kōyōnin.\" Inuyama's military follows in the fascicle-8 pattern of printing troops after officials: six platoons with a stated strength of 324 men at 48 men per platoon, so the six platoon complements account for 288 and the remaining 36 are officers and staff. The leftmost column carries only the maru-marker ○出石藩; Izushi's own figures begin on the facing page 225."
  },
  {
   "id": "izushi_upper_p026_left",
   "sequence": 474,
   "domain_canonical": "出石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "出石藩",
   "domain_en": "Izushi",
   "image": "images/upper_p026_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 26,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（出石）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 1 (Izushi)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Inuyama's revised 1870 household and population returns; opening of the Izushi entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf (printed folio 27) closes Inuyama domain's fascicle-1 entry and opens Izushi's. The whole right-hand two-thirds of the page belongs to Inuyama and consists of corrected returns: religious personnel totalling 442 persons (306 male, 136 female) by the intercalary-tenth-month survey against a cross-check figure of 457 (308 male, 149 female), a combined religious-personnel head-count of 383 male and 224 female, and bracketed revisions of the household count to 11,800 and of the population to 53,309, each flagged 改正 and 改正閏十月. Four notes below a printed rule reconcile these against the originals on folio 25 (11,782 households; 53,302 persons): +18 households, +22 shrine personnel, −15 persons, and a net +7 persons of which 5 male and 2 female. Left of the ○出石藩 marker, Izushi's entry begins with 高 30,000 koku and 草高 32,818.64045 koku, joined by a two-column printed bracket."
  },
  {
   "id": "izushi_upper_p027_right",
   "sequence": 475,
   "domain_canonical": "出石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "出石",
   "domain_en": "Izushi",
   "image": "images/upper_p027_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 27,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（出石）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle One (Izushi)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Izushi domain: yield, land tax, miscellaneous taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the fascicle-one entry for Izushi domain (出石藩) in Tajima, printed on book page 28. It records an included yield (込高) of 2,818.64045 koku from new fields and reassessment; a regular land tax (正租) averaged over the five years Ansei 6 (1859) to Bunkyū 3 (1863) of 12,911.65508 koku of rice and 1,687.5012 koku of soybeans, whose printed total 14,599.15628 koku reconciles exactly; and miscellaneous taxes (雜税) of 467.11564 koku of rice, 10.5235 koku of soybeans, and 54 kan 592 monme 7 fun 7 rin of silver, reckoned at the rate of 100 monme of silver to one ryō of gold. The demographic block gives 7,076 households and 32,201 people (16,286 male, 15,915 female) for town and countryside together, and then counts two occupational groups separately: 42 watchman (番人) households with 197 people, and 42 tea-whisk-maker (茶筅) households with 192 people. Rules across the head of the page date the tax columns to a tenth-month return and the household and population columns to an eleventh-month return."
  },
  {
   "id": "izushi_upper_p027_left",
   "sequence": 476,
   "domain_canonical": "出石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "出石藩",
   "domain_en": "Izushi",
   "image": "images/upper_p027_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 27,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（出石）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 1 (Izushi)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Izushi outcast, shrine and temple counts, shizoku/sotsu households and population, plus a supplementary Tajima return",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes the fascicle-1 return for Izushi domain (printed page 29) and then opens a dated supplement to it. The main entry records 78 eta households with 444 persons (218 male, 226 female), 307 shrines staffed by 10 shrine attendants, 6 shrine maidens and 10 mountain ascetics, and 90 temples housing 197 monks, 25 nuns and 29 women together with 8 hermitages; the 村數 (village count) field is printed but left without a figure. Two separately-counted status groups follow, each flagged 外ニ (counted apart from the domain totals given earlier in the entry): 288 shizoku households with 1,501 persons (706 male, 795 female) and 333 sotsu households with 1,284 persons (673 male, 611 female), of whom 197 serve as 兵士 and 110 as 兵卒, including 104 sons and younger brothers. The ○追補（出石藩） marker then introduces a return dated to the second month, 但馬國支配地之内社人醫師戸數人員取調書, reporting 22 shrine-family households with 79 persons, itemised as 36 in shrine-attendant families (17 male, 19 female) and 31 in mountain-ascetic families (19 male, 12 female) — 12 persons short of the stated total, the physicians named in the title never being broken out on this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "izushi_lower_p124_left",
   "sequence": 477,
   "domain_canonical": "出石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "出石藩",
   "domain_en": "Izushi",
   "image": "images/lower_p124_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 124,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（出石）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Izushi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Izushi domain officials and samurai corps",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 officials-and-military page for Izushi Domain (出石藩, Tajima, Sengoku house). Read right to left, it gives the governor Sengoku Masakata (Junior Fifth Rank, Fujiwara) and the councillor establishment: one Senior Councillor, four Provisional Senior Councillors, six Junior Councillors with one post vacant, and one Provisional Junior Councillor. A lower register prints the eleven incumbents by name — Araki Hitoshi; Kanazawa Makoto, Asami Yoshinaga, Hotta Tomochika, Sakurai Kumaichi; Ogawa Etsutarō, Nagaoka Shizumu, Shimamura Kōhei, Nishiyama Midori, Nishikawa Tomijirō; and Tanino Tō — a count that reconciles exactly with 1 + 4 + (6 − 1) + 1. The leftmost data column records the domain's samurai corps at three platoons of forty men, i.e. 120 troops."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwamura_lower_p125_right",
   "sequence": 478,
   "domain_canonical": "岩邨藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩邨藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwamura",
   "image": "images/lower_p125_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 125,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（岩邨、一關）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Iwamura, Ichinoseki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran, printed page 226, records the post-restoration official establishment and troop strength of Iwamura Domain (Mino) and the opening of Ichinoseki Domain (Mutsu). Iwamura reports 1 governor (chiji), 1 senior councillor (daisanji), 3 acting senior councillors, 4 junior councillors and 13 acting junior councillors, with a standing force of 3 platoons totalling 180 men; the governor's name is marked \"name omitted\" (名欠) and each subsequent post dittos that absence. Ichinoseki, whose marker opens at the left of the sheet, reports 1 governor (name not recorded), 2 senior councillors, 1 acting senior councillor with an editorial variant note that one account gives three, and 3 junior councillors. A trailing entry at the far right, \"sotsutai, 2 platoons,\" stands to the right of the Iwamura marker and therefore carries over from the preceding domain's military return rather than belonging to Iwamura."
  },
  {
   "id": "ichinoseki_upper_p028_left",
   "sequence": 479,
   "domain_canonical": "一關藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一關藩",
   "domain_en": "Ichinoseki",
   "image": "images/upper_p028_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 28,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（一關）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 1 (Ichinoseki section) — running header (provenance)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "End of Izushi's civil register with its Mino-Toki supplement, and the opening of Ichinoseki's entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf (printed page 31) closes Izushi Domain's fascicle-1 civil register and then opens Ichinoseki's. Right of the ○一關藩 marker, Izushi's returns end with the outcast line (13 households, 102 persons: 47 male, 55 female), counts of 296 shrines and 65 temples with the village count left unprinted, a supplementary household register headed 美濃國土岐郡戸籍追加 for Toki district in Mino province (5,278.862 koku; 1,354 households; 5,788 persons, of whom 2,889 male and 2,801 female; 24 Buddhist clergy, 27 Shinto officiants and 20 hinin-ban, each with its own sex split; 6 shrines, 15 temples, 7 villages), and the domain's military totals of 24 officers and 180 soldiers and sotsu troops. Left of the marker, Ichinoseki's entry begins with a gross assessed yield (草高) of 30,347.37 koku and an official assessed kokudaka (高) of 27,000 koku. Two of the printed sums do not close: the Toki population total of 5,788 exceeds its male and female components by 98, and the Buddhist-clergy total of 24 falls 6 short of its own 16 male plus 14 female."
  },
  {
   "id": "ichinoseki_upper_p029_right",
   "sequence": 480,
   "domain_canonical": "一關藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一關藩",
   "domain_en": "Ichinoseki",
   "image": "images/upper_p029_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 29,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（一關）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Survey of Domain Administration), Fascicle 1 — (Ichinoseki)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Ichinoseki: land tax in rice and cash, miscellaneous tax, households, population by status, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the second and final page of Ichinoseki domain's fascicle-1 return, continuing from the ○一關藩 marker on the facing page (printed 31) and running up to the ○岩崎藩 marker that opens page 33. Above the base assessment of 27,000 koku recorded on the previous page, this page adds incorporated and newly reclaimed field yield of 13,347.37 koku, and reports the principal land tax as 10,635.08 koku of rice plus 1,170 ryō 3 bu in cash (with 1,400.2 koku of beans), miscellaneous taxes of 580 ryō 3 bu, and 4,595 households holding 26,123 people (13,551 male, 12,572 female). The status breakdown gives 333 shizoku households with 1,658 people and 285 sotsu households with 1,149 people, alongside 24 shrines, 36 temples housing 56 monks, and 24 shrine-attendant households. Two warichu notes qualify the money figures: the rice tax is a five-year average for 1860-1864, and cash is converted at ten kan of copper to one ryō of gold."
  },
  {
   "id": "ichinoseki_lower_p125_left",
   "sequence": 481,
   "domain_canonical": "一關藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一關藩",
   "domain_en": "Ichinoseki",
   "image": "images/lower_p125_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 125,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（一關）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Ichinoseki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Ichinoseki military officer ranks (fascicle 8, continued)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Ichinoseki Domain's fascicle-8 military return, listing twelve officer posts with their establishment strengths and opening with the entry for troop numbers (兵隊數), which is marked 記セス — not recorded. The posts run from the overall commander (總兵長, 1) through the gunners' chief, artillery, transport, ordnance and inspectorate (銃士長 1, 砲隊長 1, 輜重長 1, 兵器長 1, 軍監 2) to the rifle-infantry and sapper line (銃卒長 2, 銃士次長 1, 坑兵長 1, 銃卒次長 2, 銃士小長 4) and the reserve command (豫備長 1), eighteen men in all on this page. An editorial parenthesis opened above 總兵長 carries the note （以下三十八行原朱書）, recording that the following thirty-eight lines were written in vermilion in the original manuscript; only twelve of those lines fall on this leaf, so the roster and the vermilion span both continue overleaf. The printed page number in the bottom margin is 二百二十七 (227)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ichinoseki_lower_p126_right",
   "sequence": 482,
   "domain_canonical": "一關藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一關藩",
   "domain_en": "Ichinoseki",
   "image": "images/lower_p126_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 126,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（一關）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Ichinoseki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Ichinoseki military establishment: corps and specialist headcounts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-8 military establishment of Ichinoseki Domain, listing thirteen offices and corps with their authorized complements in 員 (persons). The largest body is the riflemen (銃士) at 60, commanded by eight junior rifle-corps officers (銃卒小長) and two reserve rifle-corps commanders (豫備銃卒長); the artillery (砲士) numbers 6 and the scouts (斥候士) 6, with three baggage-train officers (輜重長校) and three ordnance officers (兵器管事). Support and specialist posts are small — one bandmaster (樂手長), two band physicians (樂手醫師), two clerks (筆生), and two junior army inspectors (小軍監). The two garrison categories are exceptional: the reserve-grade residence-and-fort guards (散級館砦衞士) are explicitly recorded as 無定員, having no fixed complement, while the active-grade guards (勤級館砦衞士) are printed with no number at all."
  },
  {
   "id": "ichinoseki_lower_p126_left",
   "sequence": 483,
   "domain_canonical": "一關藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一關藩",
   "domain_en": "Ichinoseki",
   "image": "images/lower_p126_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 126,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（一關）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table (Fascicle) Eight — Ichinoseki",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Ichinoseki military establishment — troop and officer headcounts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Ichinoseki (一關藩) military return in fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran; there is no domain marker on the page, so all thirteen entries belong to Ichinoseki, the domain named in the running header. Read right to left, the page lists establishment strengths for baggage-train sub-officers (2), sapper deputy commanders (2), patrolmen (6, provisionally established), samurai-company standard-bearers (2, provisionally established), artillery-company standard-bearers (2), sotsu-company standard-bearers (4), riflemen (120), sappers (32), bandsmen together with baggage-train junior officers (2 shared under one brace), ordnance junior officers (4), sapper junior officers (2), and one orderly. Reserve troops (豫備卒) are recorded as 無定員 — no fixed establishment. The riflemen and sappers dominate the page: the twelve defined categories total 179 men, of which 120 are riflemen. The printed page number is 二百二十九 (229)."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwasaki_upper_p029_left",
   "sequence": 484,
   "domain_canonical": "岩崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwasaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p029_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 29,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（岩崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 1 (Iwasaki)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Iwasaki domain fascicle-1 return: land tax, miscellaneous taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the whole of the fascicle-1 return for Iwasaki domain, opened by the maru-marker ○岩崎藩 in the rightmost column, with no other domain present. The 草高 (nominal assessed yield) label is printed but its figure is missing, so the fiscal picture begins with the main land tax in rice, 10,419.2 koku, given as a five-year average running to Boshin (1868); miscellaneous taxes add 630 koku of rice plus two cash items, 6,640 ryō of koyakugin and a further 253.3 ryō, converted on the page at 8 ryō to the koku into 830.5 and 31.6625 koku of rice. The demographic block records 3,180 households and a population of 17,397 (9,591 male, 7,806 female), of which the samurai estate holds 171 houses and 547 people and the sotsu estate 98 houses and 243 people. All three male-female splits sum exactly to their totals, and the second cash conversion is exact; the first is not, since 6,640 ryō at the stated rate yields 830.0 rather than the printed 830.5 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwasaki_lower_p127_right",
   "sequence": 485,
   "domain_canonical": "岩崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwasaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p127_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 127,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（岩崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Eight (Iwasaki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and armed strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the fascicle-8 entry for Iwasaki Domain (岩崎藩), a small Satake cadet holding in Dewa, and covers the domain's administrative roster and its armed strength. The governor is recorded only as Satake, Junior Fifth Rank (佐竹從五位); the given names of the senior administrators are explicitly not recorded (名記セス, with 同 \"ditto\" carried down the remaining posts). Below the governor sit one senior councillor (大參事), two acting senior councillors (權大參事) and three junior councillors (少參事) — seven senior administrators in all. Military strength is given as 48 soldiers (兵士四十八人) and 40 riflemen (銃卒四十人), while the organisation of the troops into units is noted as unrecorded (兵隊記セス). Two functional offices are printed as raised headings without counts of their own: the drill office (練兵方), staffed by a head instructor and one instructor and one associate instructor each, and the guard office (衛兵方), with a single watch-company commander."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwatsuki_upper_p030_right",
   "sequence": 486,
   "domain_canonical": "岩槻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩槻藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwatsuki",
   "image": "images/upper_p030_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 30,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（岩槻）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabular Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle One (Iwatsuki)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Iwatsuki assessed yield and five-year-average tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed book page 34 opens the Iwatsuki (岩槻) entry in fascicle 1 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran: the maru-marker gives a former assessed yield of 23,000 koku, and the surveyed 草高 is 33,020.48923 koku. The revenue block, averaged over the five years from Kōshi (1864) to Boshin (1868), records regular land tax of 8,233.574 koku of rice plus 2,916 ryō 3 bu and 238.77 ei-mon in cash, and miscellaneous taxes of 13.798 koku plus 2,114 ryō 1 bu and 221.9 ei-mon; the totals are 8,247.372 koku and 5,031 ryō 1 bu 210.67 ei-mon, with a warichu converting the cash total to 628.933 koku of rice at eight ryō per koku. The four columns to the right of the marker close the preceding Iwasaki (岩崎) entry: 4 shrines with 26 attendants (15 male, 11 female) and 53 temples with 256 monks (233 male, 23 female). A prose note there states that Iwasaki has no eta, hinin, or ferrymen, but that persons calling themselves bashu are recorded as belonging to a class akin to eta, their number unstated."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwatsuki_upper_p030_left",
   "sequence": 487,
   "domain_canonical": "岩槻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩槻",
   "domain_en": "Iwatsuki",
   "image": "images/upper_p030_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 30,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（岩槻）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 1 (Iwatsuki)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "households, population and status/religious sub-counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-1 civil return for Iwatsuki Domain, giving 6,862 households and a population of 38,404 (19,054 male, 19,350 female), together with 146 villages. A collator-supplied bracketed 「（内）」 marks everything that follows as a subdivision of those totals: 4 hinin households with 70 persons, 37 eta households with 244 persons, 46 Shinto priestly households with 168 persons (46 shrine priests, 48 other males, 74 females), 211 temples plus 8 hermitages with 226 residents (195 monks, 30 laymen, 1 woman), and 379 shizoku-and-sotsu households with 1,683 persons (960 male, 723 female). Three further columns, which the collator's head-note identifies as red-ink annotations in the original manuscript, break the retainer body into 203 shizoku households with 994 persons, 176 sotsu households with 739 persons, and 3 Shugendō households with 4 males; the household figures sum exactly to 379 but the person figures exceed the 1,683 total by 50. Bracketed editorial remarks record that the number of Shinto shrines and the number of warships were not entered, and that the governor's household numbered 12 (10 male, 2 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwatsuki_lower_p127_left",
   "sequence": 488,
   "domain_canonical": "岩槻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩槻藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwatsuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p127_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 127,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（岩槻）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Iwatsuki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials: posts, establishment counts, and named officeholders",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle-8 officials entry for Iwatsuki Domain (Musashi), marked by the circle-marker ○岩槻藩 with the note that the return was compiled in the Snake year (Meiji 2 / 1869). The three columns printed to the right of that marker are not Iwatsuki's: they are the tail of the preceding domain's military roster — 銃卒隊長 2, 番組司令 2, 銃卒五長 3 — overflowing past the next domain's marker, and MASTER assigns them to Iwasaki Domain. Iwatsuki's own establishment is given as governor (知事) 1, senior counsellor (大参事) 1, acting senior counsellor (権大参事) 2, junior counsellor (小参事) 2, and acting junior counsellor (権少参事) 4, for ten posts in all. The lower register names the holders: governor Ōoka Tadatsura, Junior Fifth Rank, followed by Fujisaki Yutaka, Aoki Ataeru, Nakakuki Yanagi, Kodama Sōgo, Murase Tamaki, Tomita Yoshi, Takagi Tōichi and Yamazaki Hachirōji — nine of the ten, the fourth acting junior counsellor continuing on the next page. Printed book page 231."
  },
  {
   "id": "iino_upper_p031_right",
   "sequence": 489,
   "domain_canonical": "飯野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯野藩",
   "domain_en": "Iino",
   "image": "images/upper_p031_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 31,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（飯野）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — Iino (飯野藩): assessed yield, five-year average tax receipts in rice, soybeans, cash and silver, households and population",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Iino domain assessed yield, tax receipts converted to rice, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This right half-page is the complete Fascicle 1 entry for Iino domain (飯野藩), a 20,000-koku domain in Kazusa whose nominal assessment is printed as a gloss on the domain name (本高二萬石). The surveyed yield (草高) is 21,062.894 koku including newly opened fields, and the tax figures are given as a five-year average running from the kōshi year to the boshin year, 1864 to 1868 (甲子ヨリ戊辰マテ五ヶ年平均): regular tax of 7,126.04821 koku of rice, 34.34 koku of soybeans (17.17 koku of rice), and 177 kan 458.834 mon in cash (22.1823 koku), then miscellaneous taxes of 323.798057 koku of rice, 22 kan 207.23 mon in cash (2.7758 koku) and 2 kan 31.2 monme of silver (4.2317 koku). A small two-line gloss under the first conversion prints the rate used throughout, eight ryō to the koku, and the total rice actually received (合現米) is 7,496.20658 koku, about half a shaku more than the six components add to. The register closes with 4,375 households and a population of 21,433, split into 10,734 men and 10,553 women — a breakdown that falls 146 short of the stated total."
  },
  {
   "id": "iino_lower_p128_right",
   "sequence": 490,
   "domain_canonical": "飯野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯野藩",
   "domain_en": "Iino",
   "image": "images/lower_p128_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 128,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（飯野）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Table Eight (Iino)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 leaf (printed page 232) whose single maru-marker, ○飯野藩, sits well to the left, so most of the sheet still belongs to the preceding domain, Iwatsuki. The right-hand two-thirds carry Iwatsuki's second, Sheep-year (未ノ年, Meiji 4/1871) return: governor \"same as before\", 2 senior councillors (大參事) and 1 junior councillor (小參事), named as Nakakuki Nobuchō, Takagi Kiyoatsu and Takahashi Shigemasa, with a tenth official from the domain's earlier Snake-year roster (上都準) overflowing from page 231. Iwatsuki's military follows: overall troop numbers are \"not recorded\" (兵隊 記セス), but companies 1-3 muster 120 men and companies 4-6, the rifle-conscript companies, another 120, with a further 28 from company commander down to the squad commanders — 268 men in all. Left of the marker, Iino Domain's own entry opens with a governor (no member count printed) and 2 senior councillors, continuing onto page 233."
  },
  {
   "id": "iida_upper_p031_left",
   "sequence": 491,
   "domain_canonical": "飯田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯田藩",
   "domain_en": "Iida",
   "image": "images/upper_p031_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 31,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（飯田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 1 (Iida)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Iino status-group households and population; Iida kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 37 of fascicle 1, headed for Iida domain but mostly occupied by the close of the preceding domain's return, Iino. Right of the ○飯田藩 marker Iino reports 188 shizoku households with 638 people (317 male, 321 female), 82 sotsu households with 203 people (107 male, 96 female), 296 eta households with 737 people (363 male, 372 female, plus the 2 monks of two eta temples), 110 temples housing 213 people of whom 142 are clergy (129 monks, 13 nuns), and 4 shrine-attendant households with 9 people, 4 of them head priests; the village count prints シレス (not recorded) and a bracketed note reports the governor's family, warships, and shrine count all unrecorded. An editor's note above flags the two 士族/卒族 lines that repeat those figures in 口 units as a red-ink header note in the manuscript original. Left of the marker the Iida entry opens with a former assessment of 17,000 koku and a kusadaka of 20,092.91977 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "iida_upper_p032_right",
   "sequence": 492,
   "domain_canonical": "飯田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯田藩",
   "domain_en": "Iida",
   "image": "images/upper_p032_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 32,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（飯田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Part One (Iida)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Iida domain tax rice, households, population, religious houses, and warrior-class households",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-1 return for Iida domain in Shinano, with no domain marker on the page: every figure belongs to Iida. The right-hand block gives the five-year average tax rice for 1864 through 1868 — regular land tax 9,191.7371 koku, miscellaneous land rent 123.14144 koku, and miscellaneous imposts 723.62848 koku, summing exactly to the printed total of 10,038.50702 koku of actual rice. The demographic block records 5,770 households and 26,580 people in the horse-year (1870) count, split 13,383 men and 13,197 women, with a marginal note giving the snake-year (1869) figures of 5,722 households and 26,418 people. The religious and status counts follow: 49 shrines with 11 attendant households (23 men, 19 women), 8 yamabushi households (11 men, 16 women), 52 temples broken down as 36 temples, 12 sub-temples and 4 nunneries with 167 residents (136 men, 31 women including 5 nuns), 208 shizoku houses holding 1,075 people, and 130 sotsu houses holding 504."
  },
  {
   "id": "iida_lower_p128_left",
   "sequence": 493,
   "domain_canonical": "飯田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯田藩",
   "domain_en": "Iida",
   "image": "images/lower_p128_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 128,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（飯田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Iida)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed leaf 233 of fascicle 8 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō, carrying the tail of Iino Domain's entry and the opening of Iida Domain's. The right-hand columns, printed before the ○飯田藩 marker, complete Iino's officer roster — 3 gon-daisanji, 1 shōsanji, 5 gon-shōsanji — and record its only military figure, two platoons of Dutch-style riflemen at 46 men per platoon (92 men) as of the fifth month of 1870, with a supplementary note giving a unit strength of 66 men; the entry closes 右庚午四月ノ調, \"the foregoing is the survey of the fourth month of 1870.\" Left of the marker, Iida Domain's entry opens with the governorship recorded but unnamed, 3 daisanji and 3 gon-daisanji, and a lower name register listing Ishizawa Kingo, Okazawa Hitoshi, Yasutomi Minsō and Nakayama Shitomi. Iida's remaining officers (4 shōsanji and the gon-shōsanji) continue on the following leaf, page 234."
  },
  {
   "id": "iida_lower_p129_right",
   "sequence": 494,
   "domain_canonical": "飯田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飯田藩",
   "domain_en": "Iida",
   "image": "images/lower_p129_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 129,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（飯田）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 8 (Iida section) — running header (provenance)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Iida domain officials — shōsanji and gonshōsanji rosters",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Fascicle 8 (officials) entry for Iida domain in Shinano. It is laid out in two registers: office titles set at the top of their columns, and the corresponding rosters set bottom-flush in the same and successive columns to the left. Two rank headings appear — 小參事, given as 四員 (four officers), and 權少參事, for which no numerical count is printed. Thirteen personal names are recorded in all: the two rightmost columns (羽生孫九郎, 小林直) complete the roster of the senior rank headed on the preceding page; the next four (田總九郎兵衞, 齋藤愼吾, 松岡七郎, 杉本傳) exactly fill the four 小參事 posts; and the remaining seven (杉本愿藏, 一色英馬, 鍋木堅藏, 渡邊八郎, 石田平右衞門, 西尾爲右衞門, 中山安太郎) are the 權少參事. No domain-boundary marker occurs on the sheet, so the whole page belongs to Iida; the printed book-page number is 234."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwakidaira_upper_p032_left",
   "sequence": 495,
   "domain_canonical": "磐城平藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "磐城平藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwakitaira",
   "image": "images/upper_p032_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 32,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（磐城平）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview (Hansei ichiran-hyō), Fascicle 1 (Iwakidaira) — running provenance header in the outer margin",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Iwakidaira opening block: kokudaka, land and miscellaneous tax, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 39 of Fascicle 1 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō. The right-hand third of the leaf closes the preceding Iida-han entry: 26 villages, an eta/hinin register of 109 households and 222 persons (109 male, 113 female), and a parenthetical recording a six-person governor's household (2 male, 4 female) and that no warships were entered. The ○磐城平藩 marker then opens the Iwakidaira entry, which returns a kusadaka of 29,939.894 koku against a round assessed rating of 30,000 koku; regular land tax of 7,344.925 koku of rice plus 1,883 kan 320 mon 5 bu 8 rin in ei-cash, averaged over the four years from Genji 1 (1864); miscellaneous tax of only 1.632 koku of rice but 422 kan 23 mon 6 rin in cash; and totals of 3,216 households and 16,339 persons from the kōgo (Meiji 3 / 1870) survey. The Iwakidaira block continues on the following leaf, where its temple and shrine counts appear."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwakitaira_lower_p129_left",
   "sequence": 496,
   "domain_canonical": "磐城平藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "磐城平藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwakitaira",
   "image": "images/lower_p129_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 129,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（磐城平）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Iwakitaira)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster (Iwakitaira), with Iida troop total overflowing at right",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran records domain office-holders. The ○磐城平藩 marker opens Iwakitaira Domain's roster, which lists nine posts in a two-register layout: Governor (知事) Andō, holder of Junior Fifth Rank; Senior Councillors (大參事) Yashiro Makoto and Murakami Hajime; Provisional Senior Councillors (權大參事) Kamoshita Nakaji and a second Murakami Hajime; Muro Naoshi, annotated as the domain's representative to the Kōgisho (公議人); and three Junior Councillors (少參事), Ajioka Seiichi, Murakami Hisashi and Matsuura Kyūnai. Three columns printed to the right of the marker — the names Ichinose Kanbee and Takahara Shichibee, and a troop strength of 兵隊 貳百八十三員 (283 men) — belong to the preceding domain, Iida, whose roster began on the facing page. The printed page number is 235."
  },
  {
   "id": "ikusaka_upper_p033_right",
   "sequence": 497,
   "domain_canonical": "生坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "生坂藩",
   "domain_en": "Ikusaka",
   "image": "images/upper_p033_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 33,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（生坂）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 (Ikusaka) — outer-margin running head",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "population by status group, shrines and temples (fascicle 1)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-1 boundary leaf. The eleven data columns to the right of the ○生坂藩 marker close out Iwakitaira domain (磐城平藩): its population by status group, comprising 302 samurai households with 1,481 people, 195 sotsu households with 705, 2,524 commoner households with 13,699, 57 shrine-priest households with 269, 119 clerical households with 56, 16 eta households with 81, and 2 hinin households with 38, each total further split into male and female counts. The same block records 48 shrines and 51 temples, plus a supplementary 381.1 koku described as the combined assessed yield of seventeen temples that formerly held vermilion-seal land grants. Ikusaka domain's own entry opens at the marker with its assessed yield, 草高 15,000 koku. All seven male/female pairs sum exactly to their printed totals, and the leaf carries the printed book page 40."
  },
  {
   "id": "ikusaka_upper_p033_left",
   "sequence": 498,
   "domain_canonical": "生坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "生坂藩",
   "domain_en": "Ikusaka",
   "image": "images/upper_p033_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 33,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（石岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 1 (Ishioka)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Land-tax rice, households and status population (Ikusaka)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf completes the fascicle-1 entry for 生坂藩 (Ikusaka), a 15,000-koku Ikeda branch house whose block opens on the facing right-hand leaf. It records land-tax rice of 5,680.3348 koku as a five-year average for 1864-68, 1,772 households and a population of 9,097, and then breaks the domain down by status: 86 shizoku households with 322 persons, 62 sotsu households with 174 persons, 6 light-sotsu households with 7 persons, 50 eta households with 938 persons, 16 shrine-attendant households with 67 persons and 15 onbō households with 90 persons, alongside 22 shrines and 5 temples housing 9 monks. Every status sub-total reconciles with its male and female components, but the domain-wide split does not: the printed 男 4,854 and 女 4,167 sum to 9,021, seventy-six short of the printed total of 9,097. The ○石岡藩 marker at the left edge closes the Ikusaka block and opens the next domain, whose own figures begin on the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "ikusaka_lower_p130_right",
   "sequence": 499,
   "domain_canonical": "生坂藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "生坂藩",
   "domain_en": "Ikusaka",
   "image": "images/lower_p130_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 130,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（生坂）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Ikusaka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 boundary leaf: the right two-thirds close out Iwakitaira domain (磐城平藩) and the left third opens Ikusaka domain (生坂藩) at the maru-marker ○生坂藩. For Iwakitaira the page lists five acting junior councillors of the first and second grades (一二權少參事) — Nonoyama Noboru, Murakami Hisashi, Urushibara Ugenta, Matsuura Kyūnai, and Nakamura Mohei — followed by the domain's troop strength: 20 standing samurai-rank soldiers and 20 standing rank-and-file, plus 18 reserve soldiers and 12 reserve rank-and-file, 70 men in all. Ikusaka's entry begins with its three senior officers: Governor Ikeda Masanori (知事 池田政禮), Senior Councillor Miyake Kei (大參事 三宅敬), and Acting Senior Councillor Takao Takenobu (權大參事 高尾武信). The leaf carries the printed book page 236."
  },
  {
   "id": "ishioka_upper_p034_right",
   "sequence": 500,
   "domain_canonical": "石岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "石岡",
   "domain_en": "Ishioka",
   "image": "images/upper_p034_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 34,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（石岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran, Fascicle 1 (Ishioka)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Ishioka kokudaka, land tax, miscellaneous taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the whole fascicle-1 civil return for Ishioka domain in Hitachi province. Its assessed yield is 29,069.6831 koku, made up of a 20,000-koku base enfeoffment plus 9,069.6831 koku of newly opened fields brought onto the register; the regular land tax runs 5,253.995 koku of rice on a stated five-year average, together with a cash portion of 1,244 kan 237.92 mon. Miscellaneous taxes are reported in three currencies at once: 676.75 ryo in gold, 29,874.2 mon in ei-cash and 183,502.6 mon in copper cash. The commoner return is 2,774 households and 16,913 people (8,591 male, 8,322 female), with a separately counted samurai population of 198 households and 901 people (418 male, 483 female), so the samurai class is about 5.3 percent of the domain's recorded population."
  },
  {
   "id": "ishioka_upper_p034_left",
   "sequence": 501,
   "domain_canonical": "石岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "石岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Ishioka",
   "image": "images/upper_p034_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 34,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（今尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran (Domain Survey), Fascicle 1 — running header names Imao (今尾), the domain whose entry opens at the far left of this half-page; the twelve data columns on the page belong to the preceding domain, Ishioka (石岡藩)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Ishioka domain, close of the fascicle-1 register: lower-retainer and outcast households and populations, shrines, temples, villages, shrine-priest and Shugendō households, and the domain's two military units",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page closes the Fascicle 1 entry for Ishioka domain (石岡藩) and then opens the entry for Imao (今尾藩) with the maru-marker ○今尾藩 at the far left, so every data column on the page belongs to Ishioka while the running header 藩制一覽表第一（今尾）names Imao. Under the supplementary rubric 外二 it records 109 sotsu-rank households with 182 people (the internal split, 男 126 and 女 62, sums to 188, six more than the printed total), 14 outcast (穢多・非人) households with 100 people (男 52 / 女 48), 70 shrines, 98 temples housing 48 residents (男 45 / 女 3), 70 shrine-priest (社家) households with 123 people, and 8 Shugendō (修驗) households with 27 people; a separate column gives 37 villages. Under the heading 兵隊數 the domain reports two rifle platoons — a marginal note gives each platoon as 68 men including 8 officers — and two heavy cannon served by 12 gunners and 2 officers. The printed leaf number in the outer margin is 四十三 (43)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ishioka_lower_p130_left",
   "sequence": 502,
   "domain_canonical": "石岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "石岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Ishioka",
   "image": "images/lower_p130_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 130,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（石岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Ishioka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 (officials and military) of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, printed book page 237. The right-hand columns close out the preceding domain, Ikusaka (生坂藩), with two named officials — Kisabe Takanobu, holding the same post as the entry carried over from the facing page, and Junior Councillor (少參事) Habara Takamasa — followed by its military return, which records the troop total as 不詳 (\"not ascertained\") and enumerates only officer posts: one inspector-of-troops (監軍), one platoon commander (小隊長), and one half-platoon commander (半隊長). The maru-marker ○石岡藩 then opens the block for Ishioka Domain (Hitachi, ~20,000 koku), whose administrative establishment is given by headcount: three Senior Councillors (大參事), four Acting Senior Councillors (權大參事), three Junior Councillors (小參事), two Acting Junior Councillors (權小參事), and two clerks (役司). Its forces comprise two rifle platoons of 68 men each (136 riflemen) plus twelve artillerymen (礮手), with a small variant note, 一ニ曰ク (\"one account states\"), giving an alternative return of four platoons totalling 200 men at 52 per platoon."
  },
  {
   "id": "imao_upper_p035_right",
   "sequence": 503,
   "domain_canonical": "今尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "今尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Imao",
   "image": "images/upper_p035_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 35,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（今尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran, Fascicle 1 (Imao)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Imao domain fiscal and demographic record (fascicle 1)",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 44 carries the fascicle-1 record of Imao (今尾藩), a small Mino holding whose Takenokoshi lords had served as hereditary chief retainers of Owari. The surveyed yield (草高) is 17,906.913 koku against a nominal assessment (高) of 30,000 koku, from which a marginal note records that 10,000 koku had been returned to Nagoya domain, leaving 20,000. Regular land tax in rice is given as 5,444.337 koku, a five-year average on the 20,000-koku figure, with a further 47.011 koku from mitori fields and newly broken moor and thicket dry fields, 201.441 koku of kuchimai surcharge rice, and cash levies of 32 ryo 1 bu plus 5 monme 6 fun 5 rin in silver. The demographic side records 5,732 households and 26,411 people (13,314 male, 13,097 female), 9 shrines and 71 temples with their resident clergy, and separately 1,337 shizoku (661 male, 676 female) for whom the source states that no household count exists."
  },
  {
   "id": "imao_lower_p131_right",
   "sequence": 504,
   "domain_canonical": "今尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "今尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Imao",
   "image": "images/lower_p131_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 131,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（今尾、伊勢崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Imao, Isesaki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military units (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-8 (officials and military) opening page for Imao domain (今尾藩), a small Owari cadet house in Mino. A dating note at the head of the block records that the earlier returns were surveyed on 1870/6/19 (kanoe-uma, 6th month, 19th day) while the later returns carry no stated year or month. Imao's councillor block prints five standing rank headings — 知事, 大参事, 権大参事, 小参事, 権少参事 — of which only 大参事 and 権大参事 carry names: 奧田忠 and 高野瀨和人 under 大参事, 小串右門 and 奧田又十郎 under 権大参事. The domain also reports 66 men in outside-duty offices (外役司) and six musketeer platoons (銃兵 六小隊) at a stated 50 men per platoon, i.e. 300 men. The Isesaki (伊勢崎藩) marker opens at the left edge of the page with only its 知事 heading; Isesaki's own councillors and troops continue on the facing left page (printed p. 239)."
  },
  {
   "id": "isesaki_upper_p035_left",
   "sequence": 505,
   "domain_canonical": "伊勢崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "伊勢崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Isesaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p035_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 35,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（伊勢崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle One (Isesaki)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Close of Imao's fascicle-1 return; opening of Isesaki",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 45 of fascicle one carries the tail of Imao domain's return and then opens Isesaki's. Right of the ○伊勢崎藩 marker, Imao reports 353 sotsu (176 male, 177 female) with no separate household count, 29 villages, no eta or hinin, and a military establishment of six rifle platoons at fifty men each plus 66 officers — 366 troops in all, exactly the figure given in the small note that excludes them from the civil counts. Eight Shugendō halls holding 34 people (18 male, 16 female) and two hermitage cells holding two women are counted within the total households. A collator's note flags the last three lines as red-ink additions: a received holding assessed at 52 koku, the lands of Shin-Hasedera temple in Yoshida village, Muge district, Mino province, yielding a five-year average of 19.5 koku of rice."
  },
  {
   "id": "isesaki_upper_p036_right",
   "sequence": 506,
   "domain_canonical": "伊勢崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "伊勢崎",
   "domain_en": "Isesaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p036_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 36,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（伊勢崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 1 (Isesaki)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Isesaki domain: land assessment, tax revenue, households and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf, printed page 46, carries the continuation of the Isesaki-han entry in Fascicle 1 of the Hansei ichiran; the domain's opening maru-marker stands on the preceding leaf, so the whole page belongs to Isesaki. The domain returns a nominal assessment (草高) of 25,492.363 koku, of which 5,492.363 koku is newly opened land (改出新田高), leaving exactly the 20,000 koku of the domain's formal rating. Tax revenue, averaged over the five years from the year of the rat to the year of the dragon, is 12,830.276 hyō of rice in regular land tax, 1,832 ryō 2 bu in gold plus 28 monme 6 fun of silver on dry fields, and 106 ryō 2 shu plus 5 monme 9 fun in miscellaneous imposts. Population is 3,978 households and 20,056 people (10,167 male, 9,889 female), itemised as 191 shizoku households with 815 people, 25 sotsu households with 115, 123 eta households with 584, 10 hinin households with 34, and 61 shrines served by 21 priestly households with 70 people; a further 163 men are recorded as soldiers and 39 as sotsu-equivalent."
  },
  {
   "id": "isesaki_lower_p131_left",
   "sequence": 507,
   "domain_canonical": "伊勢崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "伊勢崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Isesaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p131_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 131,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（伊勢崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Isesaki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Isesaki domain officials roster and military strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 239 continues the fascicle-8 entry for Isesaki domain, whose ○伊勢崎藩 marker and blank 知事 line stand at the end of the facing page 238. The leaf records two overlapping registers of domain officials: a first listing 大參事 Ishihara Masumi and Nagao Okujirō with three 小參事 (Tomioka Hajime, Nagaya Yasujirō, Igarashi Rai), and a second listing a 一二大參事 Nakamura Jinbee, 權大參事 Ishihara Masumi and Suzuki Nobori, and 少參事 Kawada Tōzō and Hōnoki Jihei — the duplication of Ishihara and the alternation of 小參事/少參事 reflecting the two-submission note printed at the head of the section. Military strength is given as 兵士隊 two platoons at forty men each (80 samurai troops), 卒隊 one platoon on the same establishment (40 foot troops), and 大砲 two cannon, for roughly 120 men under arms. The page carries no maru-marker of its own; the running header names Isesaki as provenance."
  },
  {
   "id": "ichinomiya_upper_p036_left",
   "sequence": 508,
   "domain_canonical": "一宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Ichinomiya",
   "image": "images/upper_p036_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 36,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（一宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 1 (Ichinomiya)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Ichinomiya domain: land assessment, rice revenue, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Hansei Ichiran entry for Ichinomiya domain (Kazusa province) in fascicle 1 of the 1869-70 Dajōkan survey. Ichinomiya's assessed yield is given as a base 高 of 13,000 koku plus a 込高 of 3,106.40636 koku, summing exactly to the 草高 of 16,106.40636 koku, of which 537.76 koku is newly reclaimed field; five-year average rice revenue is 5,465.80373 koku. The domain reports 2,884 households and a population of 14,204, with a samurai (士族) segment of 73 households and 319 people including 33 bearing arms, and 45 卒族 households whose population count runs over onto the next leaf. The four columns to the right of the ○一宮藩 marker are trailing fields of the preceding domain, Isesaki: 50 temples with 74 monks, three infantry platoons of 40 men each under 3 platoon commanders and 22 staff, and 2 cannon."
  },
  {
   "id": "ichinomiya_lower_p132_right",
   "sequence": 509,
   "domain_canonical": "一宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "一宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Ichinomiya",
   "image": "images/lower_p132_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 132,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（一宮、泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Ichinomiya, Izumi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop complements (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of fascicle 8 records the administrative establishment and troop strength of Ichinomiya domain (Kazusa) and opens the entry for Izumi domain (Iwaki). Ichinomiya's authorized complements are two senior councillors (daisanji), four acting senior councillors (gon-daisanji), seven junior councillors (shōsanji) and nine acting junior councillors (gon-shōsanji); the warichu notes attached to the two senior grades explain that the domain's kōgi-nin (public-assembly delegate) is drawn from those ranks, raising the effective totals to three and five respectively. Its forces number 33 heishi (samurai-rank soldiers) and 47 heisotsu (rank-and-file), the latter annotated as the Seiyū-tai. No governor's name is printed for Ichinomiya, whereas Izumi's governor is given as Honda no Fujiwara Tadanobu. Three acting junior councillors of the preceding domain, Isesaki — Tomioka Shinpachi, Nagaya Yasujirō and Igarashi Kitaru — overflow into the right margin of this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwamurada_upper_p037_left",
   "sequence": 510,
   "domain_canonical": "岩村田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩村田藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwamurada",
   "image": "images/upper_p037_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 37,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（岩村田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 1 (Iwamurada)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-1 fiscal and religious-establishment data: end of Izumi's entry, opening of Iwamurada's",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of the spread (printed book page 49) carries the tail of Izumi Domain's fascicle-1 entry and the opening of Iwamurada Domain's, divided by the single maru-marker ○岩村田藩. The Izumi columns to the right of the marker record 39 shrines staffed by 16 shrine attendants and 2 negi priests, 72 temples with 27 monks, 3 halls and 5 hermitages, and 24 eta households holding 98 people (54 male, 44 female); the 村數 (village count) label prints with no figure beside it. To the left of the marker Iwamurada's entry opens with a kusadaka of 15,125.04949 koku against a nominal assessment (高) of 15,000 koku, a land tax in rice (正租米) of 3,653.5623 koku noted as a five-year average of actual collections, and a rate on the assessment of 2分4厘3毛 and over — which is exactly 3,653.5623 ÷ 15,000. Miscellaneous mountain and forest dues follow in three media: 50 kan 901.5 mon in ei-cash, 10.1803 koku of rice, and 34 kan 563 mon in copper cash."
  },
  {
   "id": "iwamurata_lower_p132_left",
   "sequence": 511,
   "domain_canonical": "岩村田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岩村田藩",
   "domain_en": "Iwamurada",
   "image": "images/lower_p132_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 132,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（岩村田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle 8 (Iwamurata)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials rosters and standing/reserve troop counts",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 leaf carrying the tail of Izumi Domain's entry and the opening of Iwamurata Domain's. Right of the ○岩村田藩 marker, Izumi's officials are listed under three office headings — 大参事 (Kuwabara Fujiwara Shigenobu and Hirano Fujiwara Rensuke), 権大参事 (Kitagō Taira Yasusada), and 小参事 (Kameda Tachibana Akira, Takigawa Ōtomo Kazumasa, and Yamauchi Fujiwara Yamahiko) — followed by Izumi's military strength: 30 standing troops (常備兵) and 30 reserve troops (豫備兵), 60 men in all. Left of the marker, Iwamurata's roster begins: the 知事 (governor) heading is printed with no incumbent name beneath it, then 大参事 Takahashi Tōta Norimichi, 権大参事 Uehara Sakunoshin Satotsugu, and 少参事 Inoue Ryōzō Yasuchika. Iwamurata's own troop figures do not appear on this leaf. The printed page number in the bottom margin is 241."
  },
  {
   "id": "hasunoike_upper_p038_left",
   "sequence": 512,
   "domain_canonical": "蓮池藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "蓮池藩",
   "domain_en": "Hasunoike",
   "image": "images/upper_p038_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 38,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（蓮池）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey Table, Fascicle 1 (Hasunoike)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka assessment, rent, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-1 entry for Hasunoike, a branch domain of Saga in Hizen. The survey reports a gross assessed yield (草高) of 59,659.784875 koku, against a register base (本高) of 52,625 koku plus 3,225.32275 koku of re-surveyed and newly opened land. Rent (租額) comes to 23,863.91395 koku, exactly forty percent of the gross assessment, made up of 21,050 koku on the base holding together with 1,523.77235 koku of karimai and kuchimai surcharge rice, and 1,290.1416 koku on the new land; miscellaneous taxes add 74.2 koku, the rice equivalent of 371 ryō in cash. Actual collection averaged 23,335.2601 koku over five years, and the domain counted 6,232 households and 31,349 people (15,801 male, 15,548 female), of whom 354 shizoku houses held 1,770 people (865 male, 905 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "hasunoike_lower_p133_right",
   "sequence": 513,
   "domain_canonical": "蓮池藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "蓮池藩",
   "domain_en": "Hasunoike",
   "image": "images/lower_p133_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 133,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（蓮池）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Hasunoike)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle 8 officials roster — Hasunoike domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the opening page of Hasunoike domain's Fascicle 8 entry, the survey's roster of domain officers. It names the governor Nabeshima Naonori (Junior Sixth Rank), one senior councillor pair (Naritomi Seiki and Ishii Kyūma), one provisional-senior pair (Naritomi Shin and Ōno Kanae), and a junior-councillor group of six — Tsuruta Seizō, Nagata Yūsuke (flagged 公議人, the domain's delegate to the public assembly), Shibayama Daizō, Tsuruta Bungo, Kagiama Shōgo and Kawazoe Ikuta / Nagasaki Shūzō. Two editorial notes survive in small type: one records that a variant copy writes Shibayama's name as 代之進, the other that Nagasaki Shūzō does not appear in the caretaker-office register (留守官書ニナシ). The right-hand quarter of the page still belongs to the preceding domain, Iwamurata: its four provisional junior councillors and its military line, 兵隊 二小隊 = 43 shizoku plus 51 sotsu, 94 men in two platoons."
  },
  {
   "id": "hanabusa_upper_p039_right",
   "sequence": 514,
   "domain_canonical": "花房藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "花房藩",
   "domain_en": "Hanabusa",
   "image": "images/upper_p039_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 39,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（花房）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Fascicle 1 (Hanabusa)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tail of Hasunoike's population, shrine, temple and outcaste counts, then Hanabusa's assessed yield, actual rice income and miscellaneous taxes",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand third of this sheet closes out the preceding domain's fascicle-1 return: 679 sotsu-class houses holding 3,562 people (1,810 male, 1,752 female), 293 shrines with 17 shrine-attendant households (38 male, 52 female), 54 temples with 151 male and 68 female residents, and 11 outcaste households holding 84 people (40 male, 44 female). The maru-marker ○花房藩 then opens Hanabusa Domain, whose block runs to the left margin. Hanabusa reports an assessed yield (kusadaka) of 43,743.39766 koku and an actual rice income (genmai) of 14,571.554 koku averaged over the five years from 1864 to 1868, plus a supplementary 226.57666 koku drawn from surveyed-yield levies, boat duty, forest and embankment licences, grass-field rice, sailor corvée, upland land tax and mountain grass licences; the two rice figures sum exactly to the printed total of 14,798.13066 koku. Miscellaneous taxes are recorded in three currencies: 875.5 ei-mon, 8 ryo 3 bu in gold, and 659,492 mon in copper cash."
  },
  {
   "id": "hanabusa_upper_p039_left",
   "sequence": 515,
   "domain_canonical": "花房藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "花房藩",
   "domain_en": "Hanabusa",
   "image": "images/upper_p039_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 39,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（八戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle 1 (Hachinohe)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Households, population and religious establishments (Hanabusa)",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 53 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle 1. Every data column on this leaf belongs to Hanabusa domain, whose entry opened on the facing page 52; the one maru-marker here, ○八戸藩, stands at the far left and merely opens Hachinohe domain, whose own figures begin on the next page. Hanabusa is recorded with 12,063 households and a population of 61,410, against a male/female split of 32,426 and 32,078 that the printed note （改正男女減數未詳）marks as not reconciled with the revised total. Status counts are 1,288 shizoku in 312 households, 700 sotsu in 177 households, 137 eta in 19 households and 111 hinin in 20 households; the religious establishments are 564 shrines with 68 shrine-officer households (334 persons), 281 temples and 9 halls with 319 residents, plus 5 shugendō and 16 onmyōji households, while the rightmost column carries the tail of the miscellaneous-tax list from page 52 — 85 kan 245 mon 6 bu of cash as the salt-flat annual tax."
  },
  {
   "id": "hanabusa_lower_p133_left",
   "sequence": 516,
   "domain_canonical": "花房藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "花房藩",
   "domain_en": "Hanabusa",
   "image": "images/lower_p133_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 133,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（花房）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Hanabusa)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillor posts and rifle units",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of fascicle 8 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran carries the tail of the 蓮池藩 (Hasunoike, a Saga sub-domain) entry and the opening of the ○花房藩 (Hanabusa, Kazusa) entry. Right of the marker, Hasunoike's provisional junior councillors (權少參事) are named — 副島哲藏, 栗山英二, 尾形榮二郎, 鵜田禮作 — followed by its rifle forces: 銃士 one platoon and 銃卒 four platoons, with a printed note that a platoon is a unit of forty men, giving 160 rifle foot-soldiers. Left of the marker, Hanabusa lists 知事 (governor, heading only), 大參事 at one post with a small-type note that regular and provisional councillors together put three men on duty per day, and 權大參事 at five posts. Four councillor names print for Hanabusa: 西尾鐵之助, 佐藤武彦, 清水源次郎, 柴田源三. The running header names 花房 and the leaf is printed page 243."
  },
  {
   "id": "hanabusa_lower_p134_right",
   "sequence": 517,
   "domain_canonical": "花房藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "花房",
   "domain_en": "Hanabusa",
   "image": "images/lower_p134_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 134,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（花房）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 8 (Hanabusa)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster (權大參事 / 少參事 / 權少參事)",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page continues the official roster of Hanabusa domain (花房藩). At right, two names (青山儀一郎, 永富織衞) complete the five-position Provisional Senior Councillor (權大參事) establishment carried over from the preceding half. The center-right heads the Junior Councillor office (少參事), with an establishment of six positions and an interlinear note recording that four serve per day, three at present, and that provisional appointees are not listed; its six holders are named. At left the Provisional Junior Councillor office (權少參事) is headed with an establishment of eight positions, of which four holders are named on this half. The printed page number is 244."
  },
  {
   "id": "hachinohe_upper_p040_right",
   "sequence": 518,
   "domain_canonical": "八戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "八戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Hachinohe",
   "image": "images/upper_p040_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 40,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（八戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey, Fascicle 1 (Hachinohe)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Land assessment, land and miscellaneous tax revenue, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the opening economic and demographic run of the Hachinohe entry in fascicle 1 of the 1870 Han Administration Survey. It records a gross assessed yield of 40,074 koku, made up of a base assessment of 20,000 koku plus 20,074 koku of added yield, against which the regular land tax runs to 6,031.277 koku of rice and 91,642 kan 388 mon of copper cash, both stated as a five-year average covering 1864 through 1868. Miscellaneous taxes come in two forms, 12,660 ryō 2 bu 1 shu in gold and 33,261 kan 181 mon in copper cash, each followed by its rice equivalent (1,582.82031 koku and 415.765 koku) computed at the rates printed in the inline note, ten kanmon to one ryō and eight ryō to one koku of rice. The sheet closes with 13,386 households and a population of 67,647, split into 35,352 men and 32,295 women."
  },
  {
   "id": "hachinohe_lower_p134_left",
   "sequence": 519,
   "domain_canonical": "八戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "八戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Hachinohe",
   "image": "images/lower_p134_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 134,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（八戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle Eight (Hachinohe)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain conciliar officials and troop companies",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of Fascicle 8 closes the Hanabusa domain entry and opens Hachinohe. Hanabusa's material, all standing to the right of the maru-marker, consists of four carried-over acting-junior-councillor names (Yamada Hyakuzō, Tsuchiya Matahachi, Aoyama Kanji, Hiratomi Tanomo) followed by its military return: two platoons of samurai troops and one platoon of sotsu troops, with a single note fixing company strength at sixty men — 120 and 60 men respectively. Left of the ○八戸藩 marker, Hachinohe reports a twelve-man conciliar establishment: one senior councillor, two acting senior councillors, three junior councillors and six acting junior councillors. Hachinohe's roster is given by surname alone, the column under 大參事 carrying the interlinear disclaimer 名欠 以下同 (\"given name lacking; the same below\"), and the acting-junior-councillor list reconciles as four surnames plus 二員缺, two vacant posts, against the printed establishment of six."
  },
  {
   "id": "hakuta_upper_p040_left",
   "sequence": 520,
   "domain_canonical": "伯太藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "伯太藩",
   "domain_en": "Hakata",
   "image": "images/upper_p040_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 40,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（伯太）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Table, Fascicle One (Hakuta)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Close of the Hachinohe entry (status populations, shrines, temples, villages, troops) and opening of the Hakuta entry (yields and tax rice)",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-leaf, printed book page 55 of fascicle one, carries two domains. The right-hand eight columns close Hachinohe's entry: 370 samurai households with 2,927 people (1,395 male, 1,532 female), 200 sotsu households with 1,041 people (533 male, 508 female), an outcaste (eta) population of 54 split evenly 27 and 27, 130 shrines, 53 temples plus 3 lodging temples and 19 hermitages, 83 villages, and a military establishment of one battalion of 462 men with an artillery corps of 85. The maru-marker ○伯太藩 then opens Hakuta domain (Izumi Province), whose surveyed yield is 14,273.0341 koku against a base yield of 13,520 koku, with regular tax rice of 5,995.3023 koku and miscellaneous tax rice of 72.5531 koku, both figures headed \"five-year average.\" The new-field increment row 込高新田 is printed but left blank, so the 753.0341-koku difference between the surveyed and base yields is nowhere stated on the page."
  },
  {
   "id": "hakata_upper_p041_right",
   "sequence": 521,
   "domain_canonical": "伯太藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "伯太藩",
   "domain_en": "Hakata",
   "image": "images/upper_p041_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 41,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（林田）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覽表), Fascicle 1 — running head printed for Hayashida (林田). The head names the domain whose block opens on this leaf; the data on the leaf is almost entirely Hakata's (伯太藩).",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Civil register: cash tax and rice equivalents, households, population, and non-commoner status groups",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the fascicle-1 civil register of Hakata domain (伯太藩), a 13,500-koku Watanabe holding in Izumi province whose block opened on the facing earlier page. It records a miscellaneous tax in gold of 43 ryō 1 bu 3 shu plus 53.18 mon in ei-cash, its rice equivalent of 5.4363 koku, and a combined current-rice total (合現石) of 6,073.2917 koku, against 2,109 households and a population of 10,439. Below the commoner figures the page breaks out the non-commoner groups: 149 samurai and sotsu households (86 shizoku, 63 sotsu) holding 615 people, an outcast (穢多) group of 71 households and 294 people split evenly at 147 men and 147 women, 82 shrines with 8 shrine-attendant households and 22 people, 76 temples with 131 people, and 75 villages. The last column belongs to the next domain: the ○林田藩 marker opens Hayashida's block with an assessed yield (草高) of 14,889.6719 koku. Two totals do not close as printed — the male-plus-female split of the population falls 294 short of the printed 10,439 (exactly the outcast count), and the status breakdown of the 615 samurai-class people sums to 574."
  },
  {
   "id": "hakata_lower_p135_right",
   "sequence": 522,
   "domain_canonical": "伯太藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "伯太藩",
   "domain_en": "Hakata",
   "image": "images/lower_p135_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 135,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（伯太）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administrative Survey, Fascicle 8 (Hakata)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Official roster (Hakata) with preceding domain's military tail",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page of the Han Administrative Survey (藩制一覧表) primarily records the civil-official roster of Hakata Domain (伯太藩, Izumi Province, Watanabe clan). To the right of the ○伯太藩 marker it carries the overflow military tail of the preceding domain, Hachinohe (八戸藩): a rifle corps of one battalion totalling 462 men (each 48-man platoon organized into 8 platoons), an 85-man artillery corps, and transport/equipment-manufacture/construction sections totalling 30 men. Hakata's officials comprise Governor Watanabe Akitsuna (Junior Fifth Rank), two senior councillors (大参事: Nonomura Takashi and Satake Yūzaburō), three acting senior councillors (権大参事: Sugiura Yoshimi, Shiratori Seigo, Ishii Arata), one junior councillor (少参事: Kajiwara Tan), and one acting junior councillor (権少参事: Yamada Giheita); the domain block continues onto the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "hayashida_lower_p135_left",
   "sequence": 523,
   "domain_canonical": "林田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "八戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Hayashida",
   "image": "images/lower_p135_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 135,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八、（林田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey, Fascicle 8 (Hayashida) — running header",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Hachinohe officials roster + troop strength (1870 red-ink revision); start of Hayashida entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 (officials/military) page carries the tail of the Hachinohe (八戸藩) entry followed by the opening of the Hayashida (林田藩) entry. The Hachinohe portion is an 1870 (庚午) revision, which the editor flags at top right as \"(the following eight lines were originally in red ink)\": two daisanji (Satake Yūzaburō, Nonomura Takashi), two gon-daisanji (Shiratori Seigo, Sugiura Yoshimi), two shōsanji (Ishii Arata, Kajiwara Tan) and one gon-shōsanji (Yamada Giheita), plus a troop strength of 84 men and a separate 9-man military band. At the ○林田藩 marker the Hayashida entry begins with the governor (知事, printed without a name here) and a daisanji surnamed Tatebe (建部). The outer-margin running header files the page under Hayashida; the printed page number is 247."
  },
  {
   "id": "hanbara_upper_p042_right",
   "sequence": 524,
   "domain_canonical": "半原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "半原藩",
   "domain_en": "Hanbara",
   "image": "images/upper_p042_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 42,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "五十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（半原）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle One — (Hanbara)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Hanbara domain: assessed yield, tax, population, shrines, temples, villages",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the fascicle-1 entry for Hanbara domain (Mikawa province, Andō house), marked by the ○半原藩 device in the fifth substantive column from the right. The domain is assessed at 22,228.137 koku of kusadaka, plus 837.23 koku of komidaka and 1,138.807 koku of new-field yield; it renders 5,829.38233 koku in regular rice tax and 892,306.075 mon of eiraku cash in miscellaneous taxes. The commoner register gives 3,029 households and 13,824 people (7,000 male, 6,824 female) in 53 villages, alongside 44 shrines staffed by 101 people and 73 temples with 122 clergy; counted separately under the heading （外ニ）are 657 samurai (343 male, 314 female) in 162 households. The four columns to the right of the marker close out the preceding entry, Hayashida domain, recording 3 shrine-office households with 12 residents and 13 temples with 68 residents."
  },
  {
   "id": "hanbara_upper_p042_left",
   "sequence": 525,
   "domain_canonical": "半原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "半原藩",
   "domain_en": "Hanbara",
   "image": "images/upper_p042_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 42,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "五十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（西尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 1 — running head names Nishio (西尾), the domain whose block opens on this leaf; the right-hand columns still belong to Hanbara.",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Close of Hanbara's status-group and population totals, then the opening of Nishio's land and revenue columns",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-1 leaf straddles two domains. It closes Hanbara (半原藩) with the bottom of its status register — 168 sotsu in 62 households (of whom 74 servants and 55 sotsu women), 242 eta in 41 households (116 men, 126 women), 6 hinin in a single household — and then a bracketed grand total for the whole domain of 3,410 households and 15,122 people, followed by Hanbara's military establishment of one regiment (a platoon being 47 men), 16 gunners, and 4 drummers and buglers. The ○西尾藩 marker then opens Nishio (西尾藩) with its assessed yield, 草高 63,205.63154 koku, and six revenue columns: regular land tax of 20,093.0826 koku of rice plus 321 kan 709 mon in cash, and miscellaneous taxes of 3,575.4648 koku of rice, 105 ryō in gold with 772.411 monme of silver, 247 kan 281 mon in eiraku cash, and 1,270 kan 259 mon in copper cash, all under a marginal note that the figures are five-year averages. The printed folio number is 59."
  },
  {
   "id": "hanbara_lower_p136_right",
