   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military (fascicle 8): tail of Hanbara (7 officials + troops), start of Nishio (officials)",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page of the 1870 Han Administration Overview (藩制一覧表) straddles the boundary between Hanbara (半原藩) and Nishio (西尾藩). It closes Hanbara's entry with seven named officials (吉野六郎左衞門, 井上八十八, 鈴木市之進, 猪野新右衞門, 石川淸兵衞, 春名三太夫, 望月太兵衞) and Hanbara's military establishment: one regiment (兵隊 一聯隊, with a note that one platoon numbers 47 men), 16 artillerymen (砲兵 拾六人), and 4 drummers-and-buglers (皷手吹角手 四人). The ○西尾藩 marker then opens Nishio's entry, whose officials begin with a missing line (一行欠) followed by two senior councillors (大參事), 今井弘 and 川住敦. The printed folio number is 249."
  },
  {
   "id": "niimi_upper_p045_right",
   "sequence": 528,
   "domain_canonical": "新見藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新見藩",
   "domain_en": "Niimi",
   "image": "images/upper_p045_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 45,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第一（新見）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle One (Niimi)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Niimi domain kokudaka, land and miscellaneous taxes, samurai and sotsu households",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf (printed page 64) opens the fascicle-one entry for Niimi Domain in Bitchū Province, marked by the circle-marker ○新見藩 in the middle of the leaf. Niimi's assessed kokudaka (草高) is 18,196.1402 koku, of which 196.1402 koku is recorded separately as an added increment from newly reclaimed fields (込高新田), averaged over five years — leaving the domain's nominal 18,000-koku assessment exactly. The regular land tax came in at 5,731.4909 koku of rice plus 2,204 ryō 2 bu 1 shu and 32.5 mon in cash, the cash portion being valued at a further 440.919 koku of rice at the stated rate of 5 ryō per koku; miscellaneous taxes added 296.7454 koku of rice, 291 ryō 1 bu 3 shu and 19.4 mon, and a further 58 ryō from ironworks, blacksmiths and livestock markets that the entry notes varies from year to year. The domain counted 124 shizoku households (592 people: 312 male, 280 female) and 217 sotsu households (612 people: 330 male, 282 female). The two columns to the right of the marker — 59 temples with 62 monks plus 5 yamabushi households, and a force of two companies at 60 men each — are the tail of the preceding domain's entry and belong to Niwase Domain."
  },
  {
   "id": "niimi_lower_p138_left",
   "sequence": 529,
   "domain_canonical": "新見藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新見藩",
   "domain_en": "Niimi",
   "image": "images/lower_p138_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 138,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（新見）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 8 (Niimi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "A Fascicle 8 (officials and military) page that ends Niwase Domain's (庭瀬藩) roster on the right and opens Niimi Domain's (新見藩) on the left, split by the ○新見藩 marker. On the Niwase side the page records a junior-councilor (少参事) quota of 2 members, a senior councilor (大参事) — 森岡喜多右衞門 — who filed a resignation request on account of illness in the 3rd month, an assistant-junior-councilor (権少参事) post, and a military strength of 2 companies at 60 men each (120 troops), together with eight named officials including the liaison officer (公用人) 近藤彌. On the Niimi side the entry opens with one senior councilor (大参事) and three assistant senior councilors (権大参事), named 大橋求馬, 大橋靱負, and 蜂屋恕平. The printed book-page number is 253."
  },
  {
   "id": "niimi_lower_p139_right",
   "sequence": 530,
   "domain_canonical": "新見藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新見藩",
   "domain_en": "Niimi",
   "image": "images/lower_p139_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 139,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（西大路）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle Eight (Nishiōji)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster and military establishment (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the tail of the Niimi (新見) domain entry in fascicle 8 (domain officials and military establishment). It records the councillor establishment — five junior councillors (少參事) and three acting junior councillors (權少參事) — together with a roster of eight named officials (蜂屋新, 八木代右衞門, 今村績, 中村和三郎, 平田有無, 内藤範, 宮地源三郎, 佐々木勇夫) and a 一名欠 note marking one vacant post. The military establishment is a 75-man standing corps (常備兵隊 七十五人), 60 reserve infantry (豫備歩兵 六十人), and 19 reserve artillery (豫備砲兵 十九人). The maru-marker ○西大路藩 at the far left opens the next domain, Nishiōji, whose data continues on the following leaf; the running header names 西大路 as provenance while all data here belongs to Niimi."
  },
  {
   "id": "niiya_upper_p046_right",
   "sequence": 531,
   "domain_canonical": "新谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Niiya",
   "image": "images/upper_p046_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 46,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（新谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 1 (Niiya)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Kokudaka, rice and soybean taxes, population, temples, shrines and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-leaf, printed book page 66 of Hansei ichiran fascicle 1, closes the entry for 西大路藩 (Nishi-ōji, Ōmi) and opens the entry for 新谷藩 (Niiya, Iyo). For Nishi-ōji it records a retainer population of 768 (379 male, 389 female), split into 352 shizoku and 416 sotsu; 40 outcaste (eta) households holding 171 persons; 56 shrines served by 10 households and 41 persons; 50 temples with 86 monks and 27 women; 29 villages; and two platoons totalling 80 men including officers. The maru-marker ○新谷藩 then opens Niiya, which returns a gross assessed yield (草高) of 9,692.67578 koku against a rated kokudaka (高) of 10,000 koku, a rice tax (正税米) of 3,824.2028 koku, and — under a 諸雜税 heading annotated as a five-year average from the Meiji 2 kishi-year survey — 1,295.40188 koku of soybeans, converted to rice at 80 percent as 1,036.3215 koku. Two figures need flagging: the eta counts sum to 172 against a printed total of 171, an inconsistency in the source itself, and the 草高 printed here carries a 五合七勺 that the project's MASTER row omits."
  },
  {
   "id": "niiya_lower_p139_left",
   "sequence": 532,
   "domain_canonical": "新谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "新谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Niiya",
   "image": "images/lower_p139_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 139,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（新谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain System Overview, Fascicle 8 (Niiya)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Niiya domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This page is the fascicle-8 (officials and military) entry for 新谷藩 (Niiya), a small Iyo-province sub-domain, printed as book page 255. It records the domain's administrative establishment: 1 governor (知事, Katō Yasunori 加藤泰令), and councillors at their current strength — 1 senior councillor (大参事), 2 acting senior councillors (権大参事), 3 junior councillors (少参事), and 3 acting junior councillors (権少参事) — with nine named officers listed, whose count (1+2+3+3) exactly matches the nine names. Military strength is given as two platoons totaling 80 persons including officers (二小隊役員共八十人). The ○新谷藩 marker sits at the block's left (tail) edge; the facing right page (254) carries the separate 西大路藩 entry."
  },
  {
   "id": "nishibata_upper_p047_right",
   "sequence": 533,
   "domain_canonical": "西端藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西端藩",
   "domain_en": "Nishibata",
   "image": "images/upper_p047_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 47,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（西端）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 1 (Nishibata)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Nishibata domain land assessment, tax yield, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 68 of fascicle 1 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō, given over entirely to Nishibata domain in Mikawa province; the single maru-marker ○西端藩 opens the block and no other domain appears on the leaf. The survey records a gross assessed yield (草高) of 14,008.75433 koku against an official kokudaka (高) of 10,500 koku, with newly opened and re-surveyed land (込高・新田・改出高) accounting for 3,508.9994 koku. Regular land tax, given as a five-year average, came to 2,912.06805 koku of rice plus 1,385 kan 524.283 mon in cash, and miscellaneous taxes to 273.70508 koku of rice, 160 kan 737.119 mon, 2,842 mon in bita coin and 5,690 mon in zeni. The domain counted 2,599 households and 12,442 people (6,356 male, 6,086 female), of whom 5 households and 23 people (11 male, 12 female) were registered as hinin."
  },
  {
   "id": "nishibata_upper_p047_left",
   "sequence": 534,
   "domain_canonical": "西端藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "西端藩",
   "domain_en": "Nishibata",
   "image": "images/upper_p047_left.jpg",
