   "pdf_page": 47,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（西大平）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 1 — running head names Nishiōdaira (西大平藩), the entry that opens on this leaf; the bulk of the leaf is the tail of the preceding Nishibata (西端藩) entry",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Nishibata clergy, shrine/temple/village counts and samurai population; opening of the Nishiōdaira entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-1 leaf (book page 69) closes the survey entry for Nishibata (西端藩) and opens the entry for Nishiōdaira (西大平藩). For Nishibata it records 133 samurai-and-sotsu households (83 shizoku, 50 sotsu) and 362 people in that class (275 shizoku, 87 sotsu; 187 male and 175 female), alongside 41 villages, 202 Shinto shrines and 96 Buddhist temples, 101 Shinto priests in 20 households, 111 monks and nuns, and 2 Shugendō practitioners in 2 households. It then itemises four temple stipend grants in Tama district of Musashi province — Kisshōin at Yokozawa village and Kōgonji at Tokura village at 20 koku each, Myōdaiji at Ajiro village at 5 koku, and Saifukuji at Ōkuno village at 5.3 koku — bracketed under a stated total of 50.3 koku, which the four items reproduce exactly. Left of the maru-marker, Nishiōdaira's entry begins with an assessed yield (草高) of 10,416.1454 koku followed by a bare 高 sub-heading for which no figure is printed on this leaf; the entry resumes on the next leaf with a new-paddy yield of 414.5239 koku."
  },
  {
