   "book_page": "七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（本庄）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 1 (Honjō)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Nishi-Ōhira's closing civil return and Honjō's opening kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-leaf closes the fascicle-1 civil return for Nishi-Ōhira domain (Mikawa) and opens that for Honjō domain (Dewa). For Nishi-Ōhira it records 28 shrines and 51 temples; 61 shizoku households (with 2 more noted apart) holding 237 people (117 male, 120 female); 10 sotsu households holding 40 people (18 male, 22 female); 28 villages; no eta; 21 shrine officiants (13 male, 8 female) and 246 Buddhist clergy (111 male, 135 female). Two temple endowments follow: Myōgon-ji with a grant of 45 koku yielding 3.09917 koku of land-tax rice and 21 ryō 2 bu 3 shu plus 50.417 ei-mon in cash, and Sanmyō-ji with a grant of 20 koku yielding 7.324 koku. Left of the maru-marker ○本庄藩 the page gives Honjō's kusadaka as 27,223.061 koku, of which 7,164.255 koku is entered as newly opened field and paddy, together with a note that the figures continuing overleaf are five-year averages running from Kōshi (1864) to Boshin (1868)."
  },
  {
   "id": "honjo_lower_p141_right",
