   "domain_canonical": "本荘藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "本莊藩",
   "domain_en": "Honjō",
   "image": "images/lower_p141_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 141,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（本莊）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Honjō)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials & military roster (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 (officials & military) of the 1870 Han-sei ichiran-hyō. The page opens with the tail of Horie domain's entry, printed to the right of the ○本莊藩 marker: its five junior assistant councillors (gon-shōsanji — Ōhashi Kumatarō, Inoue Hayashi, Kose Hisashi, Ochiai Senzō, Yoshino Heigo) and a troop strength of 20 line soldiers plus a corps commander, 8 officers and a 5-man band (about 33 military personnel in all). Honjō domain's own entry then begins at the marker: governor (chiji) Rokugō Masaaki, senior councillor Moriya, two junior senior councillors (Minagawa and Shiraiwa Kagemori), and assistant councillor Ishii. Honjō's own junior councillors and military continue on the following page. Printed book-page 258."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyama_upper_p054_left",
   "sequence": 539,
