   "pdf_page": 55,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（富山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 2 (Toyama)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyama domain revenue and population breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-2 return for Toyama Domain and carries no maru-marker, so all of it belongs to Toyama. Its upper half closes one revenue group with a cash line of 12,503 kan 920 mon and then gives a second group of 64,616.25 koku of net rice, 15,711 ryō 2 bu in gold, and 32,998 kan 892 mon in cash. Its lower half reports 30,966 households and a population of 133,415 (67,821 male, 65,317 female), followed by a status breakdown under the heading 內譯: 3,521 warrior and foot-soldier households holding 16,772 people, split into 1,259 shizoku households with 7,257 people and 2,262 sotsu households with 9,515 people. The shizoku and sotsu figures reconcile exactly against their parent totals, but the printed sex splits for the domain-wide population and for the shizoku fall short of their own totals by 277 and 500 respectively."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyama_lower_p143_left",
   "sequence": 541,
   "domain_canonical": "富山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "富山藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p143_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 143,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（富山、豐浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 8 (Toyama, Toyoura)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment (Fascicle 8): Toyama and Toyoura",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf from Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran records the officials and military of Toyama Domain (富山藩) and the opening of Toyoura/Chōfu Domain (豐浦藩). Toyama lists two senior councillors (大参事), one acting senior councillor (権大参事), two junior councillors (少参事) and two acting junior councillors (権少参事), leaves the governorship (知事) blank, and reports its forces only as doctrine — one English-style battalion (一大隊 英式) and one French-style artillery unit (一砲隊 佛式), strength \"per the standard English/French complement\" (但英佛定員通り) — giving no explicit head count. The two rightmost military columns — naval-and-land forces of 231 persons (海陸軍兵備 貳百三十一人), of which 171 heavy-cannon gunners (内大砲手 百七拾壹人) — sit to the right of Toyama's marker and belong to the preceding domain, Kawara (香春藩), whose military overflows onto this leaf, exactly as Tottori's overflow appears to the right of Kawara's marker on the facing page (p.262). Toyoura begins with a blank governorship and one senior councillor (大参事 一員). The printed page number is 263."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyohashi_upper_p057_right",
   "sequence": 542,
   "domain_canonical": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyohashi",
   "image": "images/upper_p057_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 57,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle Two (Toyohashi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyohashi domain assessed yield and tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Toyohashi (豐橋藩) entry in fascicle two of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran and reports the domain's assessed yield and its tax receipts. The nominal assessment (草高) is 89,978.87909 koku, and the four vermilion-ink lines that follow give normal-year averages: land-tax rice 25,303.04753 koku, miscellaneous-tax rice 3 bales (1.2 koku), wheat 5.859 koku (1.95104 koku in rice), and cash 1,378 ryō 3 bu 2 shu plus 640 mon (220.63026 koku in rice). A large inset note supplies a competing five-year average covering 1864 through 1868, flagging the 1868 dragon year as a crop failure, and itemises rice 22,838.781 koku, miscellaneous-tax rice 3,143.103 koku, gold, copper cash, lime and wheat, all converted to rice at roughly 8 ryō and 80 kan per koku, for a stated total of 26,198.543 koku. The components of that inset sum exactly to the printed total, which confirms the reading of every figure in it."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyohashi_upper_p057_left",
   "sequence": 543,
   "domain_canonical": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyohashi",
   "image": "images/upper_p057_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 57,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview Table, Fascicle 2 (Toyohashi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyohashi domain: closing product entry, net rice revenue, households and population with warrior breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf, printed page 89 of fascicle 2 of the Hansei ichiran, completes the entry for Toyohashi domain (豐橋藩) in Mikawa. It closes the domain's product list with lime, 19.2 koku, valued at 1.92 koku of rice, and then records the domain's aggregate net rice revenue (合現米) of 25,528.74883 koku alongside 995.3 koku of shrine and temple seal land. The population survey follows: 17,517 households and 76,228 people, of whom the page prints 38,431 male and 37,697 female. A 内譯 breakdown then isolates the warrior population at 1,061 shizoku and sotsu households and 3,242 people, split into 595 shizoku households with 2,120 people and 466 sotsu households with 1,122 people; every subtotal in that warrior chain sums correctly, while the domain-wide male and female counts fall 100 short of the printed grand total."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyohashi_lower_p144_right",
   "sequence": 544,
   "domain_canonical": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyohashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p144_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 144,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（豐橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Toyohashi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillor establishment (with names) and the previous domain's military units",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 (administrative-personnel) page of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. Its right portion carries the tail of the previous domain, Toyoura (豐浦藩): acting senior councillors (權大參事 2), junior councillors (少參事 5), and the military — a three-battalion rifle corps totalling 960 troops (one platoon = 40) and a two-platoon artillery corps of 42 troops (one platoon = 21). The ○豐橋藩 marker then opens Toyohashi (豐橋藩), whose councillor establishment follows: governor (知事, no count printed), senior councillor (大參事 1, parenthetical 2), acting senior councillors (權大參事 2, parenthetical 4), and junior councillors (少參事 4, parenthetical 2). The seven named officers appear in the lower register: 西村爲周 (大參事); 和田元亨・深井資生 (權大參事); 倉垣長峽・北原弘光・松井奧讓・遊佐昉重 (少參事). Printed page 264."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyohashi_lower_p144_left",
   "sequence": 545,
   "domain_canonical": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyohashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p144_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 144,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（德山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 8 (Tokuyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Toyohashi-han officials and military (fascicle 8); opening of the Tokuyama-han entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 (officials and military) page concludes the entry for Toyohashi-han (豐橋藩) and opens that of Tokuyama-han (德山藩). Toyohashi's record here comprises an acting-junior-councillor office of seven members (權少參事 七員), a lower-register block of eight named officials (宮脇正成 … 石川景祥), and three military units: an infantry corps of 180 (30 officers + 150 riflemen, \"2½ small companies\"), an artillery platoon of 26 (9 officers + 17 gunners), and a 20-man band (3 officers + 17 buglers). To the left of the ○德山藩 maru-marker, Tokuyama's entry begins with only its 知事 (governor) heading; its councillors and troops continue on the next leaf (p145R, headed 鳥羽). The running header reads 藩制一覽表第八（德山） and the printed page number is 265."
  },
  {
   "id": "toba_upper_p059_right",
   "sequence": 546,
   "domain_canonical": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Toba",
   "image": "images/upper_p059_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 59,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（鳥羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 2 (Toba)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Close of Tokuyama's population and religious counts; opening of Toba's yield and tax entry",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand page of leaf 92 closes Tokuyama Domain's fascicle-2 entry and opens Toba's. Right of the maru-marker stand Tokuyama's remaining counts: 529 sotsu households holding 2,147 people (1,139 male, 1,008 female), 31 shrine-priest households holding 150 (72 male, 78 female), 92 temple establishments holding 338 residents (261 male, 77 female), and 675 shrines, followed by bracketed notes that no warships and no record of the governor's family survive. A small-type editorial note reports that the original manuscript gave 346 for the temple population and that the printed 338 instead follows the male/female breakdown. Left of the marker, Toba Domain opens on a base assessment of 30,000 koku, a gross assessed yield of 31,813.709 koku including newly opened and re-surveyed fields, a regular rice tax of 10,992.318 koku, cash of 10,341 ryo 1 bu together with 232 mon in ei-sen, and a miscellaneous rice tax of 1,997.307 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "toba_upper_p059_left",
   "sequence": 547,
   "domain_canonical": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Toba",
   "image": "images/upper_p059_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 59,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（鳥羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table Two (Toba)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toba domain revenue totals, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-two entry for Toba domain (Shima province) with no maru-marker of its own, so every figure on it belongs to Toba. The right-hand columns close out the itemised revenue list: 4,218 ryo 3 bu in gold, 191 ei-mon, 40 kan 41 mon in copper cash, and a further 662 ryo 1 bu plus 123 ei-mon in licence dues on the salmon and mullet fisheries and sundry other undertakings, with a note that the fishery figure differs from year to year. The 合 totals follow at 12,989.625 koku of rice, 15,032 ryo 3 bu in gold, 46 ei-mon and 40 kan 41 mon in copper cash. The demographic block records 10,161 households plus 150 tenement hearths and a population of 53,521 (26,216 male, 27,305 female), of which the shizoku breakdown accounts for 249 households and 1,191 people (602 male, 589 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "toba_upper_p060_right",
   "sequence": 548,
   "domain_canonical": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Toba",
   "image": "images/upper_p060_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 60,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（鳥羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Table 2 (Toba)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toba Domain status-group demographics, villages, shrines, temples, and vessels",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of Toba Domain's fascicle-2 civil entry. The page records household and population counts by status group: sotsu (foot-soldier) families occupying 150 row-house hearths with 542 persons (310 male, 232 female); 43 shrine-priest households with 285 persons (140 male, 145 female); 155 temples with a population of 228, of whom the 206 males are all monks; 50 eta households with 289 persons (156 male, 133 female); and 10 hinin households with 94 persons (53 male, 41 female). It closes with 73 villages (a note states the town of Toba is included) across 5 districts, 253 shrines served by the priesthood, and one Western-style sail-rigged working vessel of 200 koku capacity."
  },
  {
   "id": "toba_lower_p145_right",
   "sequence": 549,
   "domain_canonical": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Toba",
   "image": "images/lower_p145_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 145,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（鳥羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Table 8 (Toba)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This page from Table 8 (officials and military) of the Hansei Ichiran carries the overflow tail of 德山藩 (Tokuyama) on the right and opens the entry for 鳥羽藩 (Toba) at the ○鳥羽藩 marker. Right of the marker, Tokuyama records 2 senior councillors (大参事) and 3 acting senior councillors (権大参事), rifle troops of 6 companies (2 platoons = 1 company, 4 companies = 1 battalion; 40 men per platoon = 480 total), and artillery of 1 battery (36 gunners + 11 support = 47). Toba's block shows no incumbent governor (知事 blank), a vacant senior councillor post (大参事 欠), and 4 acting senior councillors (権大参事 四員) named 稲垣保, 門野豊右衛門, 稲垣夫右衛門, and 鈴木仲右衛門. The printed page number is 266."
  },
  {
   "id": "toba_lower_p145_left",
   "sequence": 550,
   "domain_canonical": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鳥羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Toba",
   "image": "images/lower_p145_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 145,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（鳥羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain-System Overview Table, Fascicle 8 (Toba)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Toba domain councilors and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation of Toba domain's Fascicle 8 (officials and military) entry, printed page 267. The officials register lists 3 少参事 (junior councilors: Inagaki Mitsue, Chiba Gondayū, Asahina Hanbee) and 6 権少参事 (provisional junior councilors: Arai Gonbee, Tsuji Jin'emon, Kadono Tadami, Nakane Bunpei, Yamamoto Mizuo, Akimoto Isato), whose names are set out in a lower register beneath their office headings — 3 + 6 = 9 names, matching the printed member counts. The military establishment records 60 standing soldiers (常備兵士) plus a further 60-man foot-soldier corps (同卒隊), i.e. 120 troops, together with uncounted categories of unit commanders, officers, guides, shrine priests, and drum-and-fife players. A marginal editorial note states that the following six lines were entered in red ink in the margin of the source manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyooka_upper_p060_left",
   "sequence": 551,
   "domain_canonical": "豐岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyooka",
   "image": "images/upper_p060_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 60,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table Two (Toyooka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyooka assessed yield and five-year average tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the opening page of the Toyooka domain block in fascicle 2 of the Hansei Ichiran, printed as folio 95. The domain's nominal assessed yield (honkoku) is 15,000 koku and its surveyed gross yield (kusadaka) 15,806.30385 koku, the 806.30385 koku difference being new-field and re-survey increments folded in, as the small note below the figure states. Under the heading \"five-year average\" the survey reports land tax rice of 5,785.64165 koku, miscellaneous tax rice of 220.067 koku, and miscellaneous tax cash of 2,063 kan 927 mon. A bracketed editorial note then flags seven lines that stood in vermilion in the manuscript, giving a second, lower set — 5,135.8162 koku, 219.98711 koku, 2,061 kan 219 mon, and that cash converted to 25.76523 koku of rice — and explains the gap: the red-ink set is the straight 1864-68 average, while the main-text set drops the catastrophic 1866 harvest and averages 1863-68 instead. The prose explanation breaks off mid-sentence and runs on to the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyooka_upper_p061_right",
   "sequence": 552,
   "domain_canonical": "豐岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyooka",
   "image": "images/upper_p061_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 61,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain System Survey, Table 2 (Toyooka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "Continuation page of the Toyooka domain entry in fascicle 2, giving the domain's demographics per the Snake-year (Meiji 2, 1869) survey: 3,809 households and a population of 18,725 (9,415 male, 9,310 female), with an interlinear note recording the Horse-year (Meiji 3, 1870) survey totals of 3,873 households and 19,033 persons. A breakdown follows by status group: shizoku 83 households with 431 persons, sotsu 62 households with 362 persons, shrine families (households not recorded) with 50 persons, and 42 temples with 129 persons plus a note of 8 nuns besides. All male/female splits sum exactly to their printed totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyooka_lower_p146_right",
   "sequence": 553,
   "domain_canonical": "豐岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyooka",
   "image": "images/lower_p146_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 146,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（豐岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Toyooka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Toyooka officials roster and margin military figure, with Toba military overflow",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page belongs mainly to Toyooka Domain (豐岡藩), whose ○marker opens its officials roster: the governorship (知事) is left unfilled, under it a Senior Councillor Inoko Kiyoshi (大参事 猪子清), an Acting Senior Councillor Tabe Gennoshin (権大参事 田邨源之進), and two Junior Councillors (少参事) sharing one printed rank-title, Iwasaki Yutaka (岩崎豐) and Funaki Katsumi (舟木克己). Toyooka's own military is entered in red in the left margin as 140 troops (兵隊 百四拾員) taken from the 1869 (己巳) survey, flagged by a note that the following seven lines are marginal red-ink, in contrast to the marker's 1871 (辛未) survey date. To the right of the marker, overflow belonging to the preceding Toba Domain (鳥羽藩) records five companies totalling 260 troops (兵員 貳百六十人; 52 men per company), of which one company is the artillery unit and 25 are bugle/saddle-fife men. The printed book-page number in the lower margin is 268."
  },
  {
   "id": "tonami_lower_p146_left",
   "sequence": 554,
   "domain_canonical": "斗南藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "斗南藩",
   "domain_en": "Tonami",
   "image": "images/lower_p146_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 146,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（斗南）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Tonami)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 (officials) page carries the roster of Tonami Domain (斗南藩), flagged as compiled from the Kanoe-uma (1870) survey (右庚午ノ調). Tonami reports 3 senior councillors (権大参事三員) and 2 junior councillors (権少参事二員), with the daisanji and shosanji posts vacant (大少参事欠); the governor (知事) and public-assembly representative (公議人) are printed without named holders, and troops are not recorded (兵隊記セス), the military system to be settled later. Printed to the right of the Tonami marker is the overflow officials roster of the preceding Toyooka Domain (豐岡藩): its grand councillor Inoko Kiyoshi (猪子淸) and five senior councillors (西山久左衞門・岩崎豐・田邨源之進・勝田佐・舟木克己). The printed page number is 269."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyotsu_upper_p053_right",
   "sequence": 555,
   "domain_canonical": "豐津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐津藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyotsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p053_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 53,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐津）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyo, fascicle 2 (Toyotsu)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyotsu domain kokudaka breakdown, preceded by the tail of the Tottori entry",
   "page_summary_en": "The right third of the page closes the Tottori (鳥取藩) entry of fascicle 2: an 外ニ insert for 大山領, Tottori's Daisen holding in Hoki, giving 475 households and 1,425 people (725 male plus 700 female, which sums correctly), followed by Tottori's own tail fields — warships not recorded, governor's family not recorded, ten battalions totalling 3,734 men, and an artillery corps of 240. The marker ○豐津藩 then opens the Toyotsu block, whose kokudaka is itemised as 支配地高 118,018.803 koku, 企救郡代御藏米 31,981.2 koku and 御賞典米 5,000 koku, subtotalled at 〆155,000.003 koku; adding 改出新田高 57,598.549 koku yields the 合高 of 212,598.552 koku, and both sums reconcile to the koku. Of that total, 10,000 koku is administered by the branch domain of Chizuka (千束藩) and entered in a separate register, while 36,981.2 koku is carried as 御藏米. A compiler's note in the top-left margin records that the main-text 御藏米 figure and the figure derived by subtraction differ by 5,000 koku — precisely the 御賞典米 award. The printed book page is 80."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyotsu_upper_p053_left",
   "sequence": 556,
   "domain_canonical": "豐津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐津",
   "domain_en": "Toyotsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p053_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 53,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐津）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, fascicle 2 (Toyotsu)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyotsu domain land tax, miscellaneous tax and 1871 re-survey of rice revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "A single-domain fiscal page from fascicle 2 of the Hansei ichiran, carrying the revenue block of Toyotsu domain (Buzen, the former Kokura han). The 1869-70 return runs: a remainder of 165,617.352 koku; regular land tax of 73,030.6081 koku on a five-year average; an unlabelled 11,193.42 koku taken at three and a half tenths on a granary assessment of 31,981.2 koku; miscellaneous rice taxes of 6,317.8804 koku with a cash component of 15,613 kan 706 mon; and a combined receipt of 90,541.9085 koku, which is the exact sum of the three rice heads. Six further lines, flagged by the reprint's editors as red-ink insertions, give a re-survey dated Meiji 4/10/24 (6 December 1871): current rice of 89,420.4474 koku, of which 1,250 koku is the imperial reward grant reckoned at two and a half tenths of a 5,000-koku base, leaving 76,977.0274 koku of regular and miscellaneous tax. A head-note in the top margin records the 1928 editors' suspicion that the 5,000-koku reward base should read 1,000."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyotsu_upper_p054_right",
   "sequence": 557,
   "domain_canonical": "豐津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐津藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyotsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p054_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 54,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐津）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Domain Survey Tables, Fascicle Two (Toyotsu)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status group, Toyotsu Domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the whole of Toyotsu Domain's fascicle-two return of households and population; the domain's entry opened on the preceding leaf, and no maru-marker appears anywhere on this page, so every column belongs to Toyotsu. The two right-hand columns close out the fiscal matter carried over from the previous leaf: an annual rice levy of 11,193 koku 4 to 4 sho for Kisuki District, drawn from a kokudaka of 31,981 koku 2 to at a rate of three and a half tenths (0.35), and 31,981.2 x 0.35 = 11,193.42 confirms the pair. The domain returns 22,081 households and 117,835 people (58,863 male, 58,972 female). The shizoku-and-sotsu block records 16,233 people (shizoku 6,253; sotsu 9,980) but states outright that no household count exists for them because they lodge in farmers' houses; the remaining status groups are 152 shrine households with 733 people, 312 temple households with 1,042 people, 1,341 eta households with 6,356 people, and 20 hinin households with 82 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyotsu_lower_p147_right",
   "sequence": 558,
   "domain_canonical": "豐津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐津藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyotsu",
   "image": "images/lower_p147_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 147,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（豐津・千束）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Toyotsu; Chizuka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (councillors) — Toyotsu and Chizuka",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 (domain officials) of the Hansei ichiran, opening the entries for two small Buzen-province Ogasawara domains, Toyotsu (豐津藩) and Chizuka (千束藩). Toyotsu's roster lists one Senior Councillor (大参事: Hirai Junro), three Provisional Senior Councillors (権大参事: Shimizu Sen, Irie Tan, Yasumi Yagara), and three Junior Councillors (少参事: Shizuno Setsuzō, Fukuoku Heizō, Miyake Gozō). Chizuka's entry prints no name under the Governor (知事) line, marks the Senior Councillor post vacant (大参事欠), and lists two Provisional Senior Councillors, Baba Isao (馬場功) and Niki Shin (二木新). No troop figures appear for either domain — this half-page carries officers only. Printed book page 270."
  },
  {
   "id": "ryugasaki_upper_p062_left",
   "sequence": 559,
   "domain_canonical": "龍崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龍崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Ryūgasaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p062_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 62,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（龍崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Table 2 (Ryūgasaki)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Fiscal and demographic summary of Ryūgasaki Domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Table 2 block for Ryūgasaki Domain (龍崎藩), a small eastern domain assessed at a grass yield of 12,425.53838 koku. Its regular land tax brought in 2,686.07228 koku of rice plus 587 ryō 3 shu and 359 mon in cash, and miscellaneous taxes added 545.7648 koku and 181 ryō 2 bu 2 shu with 110 mon; the printed totals of 3,231.83708 koku and 768 ryō 3 bu 1 shu with 469 mon reconcile exactly with these components. The domain counted 1,669 commoner households with 9,167 residents (4,688 male, 4,479 female), and in addition 61 shizoku households with 237 persons (114 male, 123 female). A single overflow column at the far right — one infantry platoon of 60 men — belongs to the preceding domain, Chizuka (千束藩)."
  },
  {
   "id": "oami_lower_p147_left",
   "sequence": 560,
   "domain_canonical": "龍崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大網藩",
   "domain_en": "Ryūgasaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p147_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 147,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大網、沼田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle Eight (Ōami, Numata)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials rosters and military strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 leaf recording domain administrative establishments and troop strength. The main block is Ōami domain (大網藩): the governor's post (知事) is printed with no incumbent, alongside one senior councillor (大參事一員), two acting senior councillors (權大參事貳員), three junior councillors (少參事三員), two acting junior councillors (權少參事二員), and a military corps of forty-eight men (兵隊四十八員). To the right of the Ōami marker, overflow from the preceding domain Senzoku (千束藩) carries its junior councillors Yamaguchi Noboru and Ōno Minoru (少參事), its acting junior councillors Matsuzaki Kiyoshi and Morikawa Haya (權少參事), and an infantry platoon of sixty men (步兵一少隊、兵員六十名). The following domain, Numata (沼田藩), is opened by its maru-marker at the left edge, with its data continuing on the next leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "ogi_upper_p075_right",
   "sequence": 561,
   "domain_canonical": "小城藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小城藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogi",
   "image": "images/upper_p075_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 75,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小城）",
   "page_header_en": "Comparative Table of Domain Institutions, fascicle 2 (Ogi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ogi domain: assessed yield, tax receipts, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page opens the fascicle-2 entry for Ogi domain (小城藩), a 73,252-koku cadet domain of Saga in Hizen province. The three columns above the ○小城藩 marker finish the previous domain's entry — 25,626 total households, a population of 120,539 (60,626 male and 59,913 female, which sums exactly to the printed total), and 35 temples. Ogi's own figures then run leftward: a gross assessed yield of 82,126.32 koku, of which 8,873.82 koku is newly opened and re-surveyed land, leaving 73,252.50 koku — Ogi's nominal kokudaka; regular land tax of 26,213.22544 koku of rice plus 19,435.4 monme of silver in miscellaneous taxes converted at sixty sen to the ryō, worth 40.49041 koku, for a combined 26,253.71585 koku. The household counts close the page: 6,977 households, and besides those, 334 shizoku and 261 auxiliary-retainer households."
  },
  {
   "id": "ogi_upper_p075_left",
   "sequence": 562,
   "domain_canonical": "小城藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小城藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogi",
   "image": "images/upper_p075_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 75,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小城）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Survey, Fascicle 2 (Ogi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "household and population counts by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-2 household-and-population entry for Ogi domain that opens on the facing right-hand page under the marker ○小城藩; no maru-marker appears here, so every column belongs to Ogi. The household breakdown closes with 1,004 sotsu households, 28 shrine-family households, 164 temples, 7 Shugendo yamabushi households, 2 hinin households and 19 eta households. A population figure of 33,332 persons (men 17,556, women 15,076) then heads a status list introduced by the small marker 外, \"besides\": 1,632 shizoku, 1,409 auxiliary samurai (fukushi), 4,488 sotsu, 126 shrine-family, 173 temple, 23 Shugendo, 97 eta and 5 hinin, each with its own male and female run. Seven of the nine male/female pairs sum exactly to their printed totals; the 33,332 figure (components sum to 32,632) and the temple figure of 173 (components sum to 73) do not, each falling short by a round number of hundreds."
  },
  {
   "id": "ogi_lower_p153_left",
   "sequence": 563,
   "domain_canonical": "小城藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小城藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogi",
   "image": "images/lower_p153_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 153,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百八十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Ogi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle 8 officials and military: tail of Ōmura, opening of Ogi",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 (officials and military) page carries the end of Ōmura domain's (大邨=大村) entry followed by the opening of Ogi domain's (小城). Right of the ○小城藩 marker, Ōmura's administration is given as office head-counts — Senior Councillors (大參事) 2, Provisional Senior Councillors (權大參事) 2, Junior Councillors (少參事) 7, Provisional Junior Councillors (權少參事) 7, the governor (知事) left unnumbered — followed by its forces: a four-battalion rifle corps of 1,000 troops (小銃隊) and a one-battalion artillery unit of 212 men (大砲). Left of the marker, Ogi (a Nabeshima branch house in Hizen held under Saga) opens with its governor and councillors — 大參事 2, 權大參事 2 — and a lower band names four of its officers, headed by the governor Nabeshima Yukie. The running head files the page under Ogi; the printed leaf number is 283."
  },
  {
   "id": "obi_upper_p076_right",
   "sequence": 564,
   "domain_canonical": "飫肥藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飫肥藩",
   "domain_en": "Obi",
   "image": "images/upper_p076_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 76,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（飫肥）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 2 (Obi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Obi domain kokudaka, tax rice and cash revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "The page opens 飫肥藩 (Obi, Hyūga province) with the maru-marker ○飫肥藩 and then gives its land and revenue figures: an assessed 草高 of 60,595.4065 koku, of which 9,509.0065 koku is newly opened paddy and dry field added by resurvey, and an actual tax rice (現米, regular land tax) of 24,238.1626 koku. The 内 breakdown itemises 11,931.7327 koku of white rice, 7,453.094 koku converted from 8,198.4034 koku of red rice, and 727.2966 koku converted from 960.0316 koku of barley, with two printed conversion rules — red rice discounted one tenth against rice, barley discounted two tenths against red rice — that both reconcile exactly, though the three components fall 4,126.0393 koku short of the stated 現米 total. Cash revenue is 18,887 ryō 3 bu 2 shu plus 76 mon in ei. The four columns to the right of the marker close the preceding domain, 小城藩 (Ogi, Hizen): shrines not ascertained, one sail-rigged transport vessel, eight infantry platoons of sixty men each with sixty-nine officers and staff, and one artillery battery of twenty-eight men."
  },
  {
   "id": "obi_upper_p076_left",
   "sequence": 565,
   "domain_canonical": "飫肥藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飫肥藩",
   "domain_en": "Obi",
   "image": "images/upper_p076_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 76,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（飫肥）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Table (fascicle) 2 — Obi",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Miscellaneous tax, household counts and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a continuation leaf of the Obi domain (飫肥藩) entry in fascicle 2 of the Hansei ichiran, printed book page 127; no maru-marker appears, so the whole leaf belongs to Obi. It records the domain's miscellaneous tax — 484.7631 koku of hulled rice plus 6,970 ryō in cash, levied per the 但 note on pine, cedar, camphorwood, oak, shiitake, camphor, sugar, dried bonito and paper — together with 9,904 households and a population of 48,285 (24,957 male, 23,328 female, which sum exactly). Within those totals the leaf itemises 1,019 shizoku households, 1,339 sotsu households, 3,114 households of 浮世人 (glossed in an interlinear note as stipendless former retainers of the Itō house), 77 shrine-servant and 139 yamabushi households, 81 temples, and 61 outcaste households, with the matching populations of 5,882 shizoku, 6,716 sotsu, 12,892 浮世人 and 451 shrine servants. Every male/female pair reconciles with its total except the shizoku population, where the printed 2,895 men and 2,989 women sum to 5,884 against a printed total of 5,882 — a two-person inconsistency in the source itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "obi_lower_p154_right",
   "sequence": 566,
   "domain_canonical": "飫肥藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "飫肥藩",
   "domain_en": "Obi",
   "image": "images/lower_p154_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 154,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（飫肥）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Institutions Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 8 (Obi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military strength (Obi domain; overflow tail of Ogi domain)",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page of the Hansei Ichiran records domain officials and military strength. Most of it belongs to Obi Domain (飫肥藩, Hyūga province): to the left of its ○飫肥藩 marker are a vacant 知事 (governor), 大参事 2, 権大参事 2, 少参事 3 (one seat currently vacant, 當分一員欠), and 権少参事, with the seven office-holders' names listed below (including the noted Confucian scholar 平部嶠南). To the right of the marker the tail of the preceding Ogi Domain (小城藩, a Saga/Hizen sub-domain) overflows onto the page: 少参事 1, plus its military — 銃兵 of 8 platoons at 60 men each (480 riflemen) and 大砲兵 of 1 company (28 gunners) — with its junior councillor 持永迺 named below. The running header reads 藩制一覧表第八（飫肥） and the printed book page number is 284."
  },
  {
   "id": "odawara_upper_p077_right",
   "sequence": 567,
   "domain_canonical": "小田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Odawara",
   "image": "images/upper_p077_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 77,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二 (小田原)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 2 — Odawara (小田原藩): land assessment, following the close of the Obi (飫肥藩) entry",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "close of Obi's status head-counts and troop strength, then Odawara's land assessment",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the tail of the Obi (飫肥藩) return and the opening of the Odawara (小田原藩) return in fascicle 2 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. Right of the ○小田原藩 marker, Obi closes with head-counts for three status groups — 651 yamabushi (335 male, 316 female), 273 temple clergy (201 male, 72 female) and 274 outcaste residents recorded under the domain-specific heading 穢多鴟居來 (137 male, 137 female) — followed by its troop strength: one infantry battalion of 240 men at 40 men to the platoon, 36 artillerymen, and a combined 347 men made up of 46 officers and 301 rank and file. Left of the marker, Odawara's land assessment begins with a five-year average 草高 of 75,532.40314 koku set against a nominal 高 of 75,000 koku. Of that nominal figure the survey enters 9,509.579 koku as an amount the yield register shows was never handed over, leaving a net 差引殘高 of 65,490.421 koku, and the three figures reconcile exactly."
  },
  {
   "id": "odawara_upper_p077_left",
   "sequence": 568,
   "domain_canonical": "小田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Odawara",
   "image": "images/upper_p077_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 77,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小田原）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabulated Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle 2 (Odawara)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Odawara: supplementary yield, miscellaneous taxes, households, population, clergy and religious houses",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-2 return for Odawara Domain; no maru-marker appears on it, and the running header names 小田原 as the block it belongs to. It records a supplementary assessed yield (込高) of 10,041.98214 koku, miscellaneous taxes of 1,614.06 bales of rice together with 3,779 ryō in cash, 17,396 households, and a population of 84,257 (43,311 male and 40,946 female, which sum exactly to the printed total). Counted in addition to those figures are 754 shizoku households with 2,891 people as printed and 469 sotsu households with 1,507 people, for a combined 1,223 households and 5,398 people; the shizoku total is internally inconsistent, since its own male and female sub-counts (1,912 and 1,979) come to 3,891 and only that value reconciles with the combined 5,398. The page closes with 432 Buddhist temples and 1,721 monks and nuns (stated to be included within the population count), while the number of Shinto shrines is given as 不詳, not known."
  },
  {
   "id": "odawara_upper_p078_right",
   "sequence": 569,
   "domain_canonical": "小田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Odawara",
   "image": "images/upper_p078_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 78,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（岡崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 2 (Okazaki)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Odawara status-group households and armed forces; opening of Okazaki's kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page closes Odawara's fascicle-2 entry and opens Okazaki's. Odawara's side records 235 villages and the households and headcounts of five status groups — kawasaku leather-workers (160 households, 908 people: 498 male, 410 female), hinin (43 households, 143 people), Shugendō ascetics (37 households, 23 people), onmyōji diviners (8 households, 7 people), and maidayū performers (27 households, 22 people) — together with one infantry battalion plus two skirmisher companies (381 men in the battalion, 94 in the companies) and two cannon served by 25 gunners. Left of the ○岡崎藩 marker, Okazaki's entry begins with a gross assessment (草高) of 60,521.917 koku, deductions of 4,986.0137 koku, a remainder of 55,535.9033 koku, and a five-year average genmai yield of 21,327.5676 koku; the subtraction reconciles exactly. One discrepancy stands in the source itself: Odawara's hinin sex split (83 male + 61 female = 144) exceeds the printed hinin total of 143 by one person."
  },
  {
   "id": "odawara_lower_p154_left",
   "sequence": 570,
   "domain_canonical": "小田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Odawara",
   "image": "images/lower_p154_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 154,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百八十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（小田原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle Eight (Odawara)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Odawara domain official roster; Obi domain military tail (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 (officials and military), printed book-page 285. The ○小田原藩 maru-marker opens the Odawara domain block; everything to its right is the military tail of the preceding domain, Obi (飫肥藩), carried over from the previous leaf: one infantry battalion (一大隊, glossed as 40 men x 6 platoons = 240), 36 artillerymen (礮兵三拾六員), and a combined strength of 347 (合三百四十七人), broken down in a warichu note as 46 officers (士官四十六人) and 301 rank-and-file (兵士三百一人). Left of the marker is Odawara's official roster: the governorship (知事) left vacant, senior councillors (大参事) Katō Tōru and Ōkubo Tsunazō, five acting senior councillors (権大参事) — Yamamoto, Yokoi Sakujūrō, Mukai Azuma, Masaki Arata, Horie Isamu — and junior councillor (少参事) Sanpei Gen. Note: MASTER records only Katō Tōru for 大参事 (it drops the printed second daisanji Ōkubo Tsunazō) and its 合 breakdown (41+346) does not reconcile; the scan reads 46+301=347."
  },
  {
   "id": "odawara_lower_p155_right",
   "sequence": 571,
   "domain_canonical": "小田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Odawara",
   "image": "images/lower_p155_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 155,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（岡崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Okazaki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster and military establishment (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle-8 leaf of the Hansei Ichiran completes the 小田原藩 (Odawara) entry and opens that of 岡崎藩 (Okazaki). For Odawara it records the Provisional Junior Councilors (權少參事): a standing complement of four (山本九三, 大久保一養, 孕石孫六, 石原渡) plus five more appointed in the 5th month of 1870 (中垣齋, 石原五郎左衛門, 近藤綵, 永原章俊, 栗田信圭), and the domain's military establishment — one battalion of 8 companies totalling 381 troops, 2 skirmisher companies of 92 troops, and 2 cannon with a crew of 25. Okazaki's block begins with its ○marker, the governorship (知事, unnamed here), and a Senior Councilor office (大參事) of five members of whom 都築勉 is named. The running header reads 藩制一覧表第八（岡崎）and the printed leaf number is 286."
  },
  {
   "id": "okazaki_upper_p078_left",
   "sequence": 572,
   "domain_canonical": "岡崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Okazaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p078_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 78,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（岡崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Okazaki)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Okazaki: tax breakdown, households, and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "The verso continues Okazaki domain's fascicle-2 entry. It opens with 此内譯 (\"the breakdown of the foregoing\"), whose single item here is 19,883.5796 koku carried under a marginal note giving the tax rate (免) as three tsu five bu eight rin and a fraction, roughly 0.358; miscellaneous taxes (雜税) then follow at 1,443.988 koku plus 191 ryo 3 bu 1 shu and 49 ei-mon in cash. The domain returns 13,282 households and a population of 52,814, broken into 8 kazoku (7 male, 1 female), 1,546 shizoku, 1,595 sotsu, 48,352 commoners, 198 shrine functionaries, 878 Buddhist clergy and 3 nuns. Two internal checks fail: the clergy's male and female sub-counts total 873 against the printed 878, and the status categories together fall 234 short of the stated population, so part of the count must stand on the facing recto or the return itself is inconsistent."
  },
  {
   "id": "okazaki_lower_p155_left",
   "sequence": 573,
   "domain_canonical": "岡崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Okazaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p155_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 155,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百八十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（岡崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Overview, Fascicle 8 (Okazaki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Okazaki domain officials — office counts (gon-daisanji, shōsanji) and a 13-name roster",
   "page_summary_en": "This left leaf (printed p.287) continues the fascicle-8 officials listing for Okazaki Domain (岡崎藩); the ○岡崎藩 marker, the governor (知事) and 大参事 appear on the facing right page (p.286). The upper register carries two office-count entries: gon-daisanji (權大參事), established at 3 posts with 2 in office, and shōsanji (少參事), established at 7 posts with 4 in office. The lower register lists thirteen named officials read right-to-left, from Ōtani Samon (大谷左門) to Tamon Denjūrō (多門傳十郎). No numeric domain statistics (population, kokudaka, troops) appear here — the page is purely a personnel roster."
  },
  {
   "id": "ono_upper_p079_right",
   "sequence": 574,
   "domain_canonical": "大野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大野藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōno",
   "image": "images/upper_p079_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 79,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大野）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Ōno)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Close of Okazaki's entry (outcaste counts, shrine and temple lands) and the opening of Ōno's assessment",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand two-thirds of this leaf close the entry for Okazaki domain, whose maru-marker stands on an earlier page: 97 eta (44 male, 53 female) and 142 hinin (77 male, 65 female), 12 Shinto shrines, shrine land assessed at 1,281.0097 koku with 502.07639 koku of actual rice and 0.56 koku of tax rice, and temple land at 2,672.38912 koku with 947.03211 koku of actual rice and 7.2166 koku of tax rice, followed by a cash item of 4 kan 250 mon. The maru-marker ○大野藩 then opens the entry for Ōno domain in Echizen, of which only the first two figures print on this leaf: a kusadaka of 40,000 koku and, in addition, newly reclaimed land of 1,244.7184 koku. The running header reads 藩制一覽表第二（大野） and the printed page number is 132. Of the sixteen printed items the project's extracted dataset carries only six, and its parse of the newly reclaimed land figure (1244.71834) does not match the printed sub-unit chain 七斗壹升八合四勺."
  },
  {
   "id": "ono_upper_p079_left",
   "sequence": 575,
   "domain_canonical": "大野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大野藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōno",
   "image": "images/upper_p079_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 79,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大野）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 2 (Ōno)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōno domain: residual yield, five-year average taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fascicle-2 fiscal and demographic return for Ōno domain in Echizen, continuing a block that began on the facing right-hand page; no maru-marker opens a new domain here. It records a residual assessed yield (殘高) of 39,320.577 koku and, under the heading \"five-year average,\" a regular land tax of 30,075.0429 hyō of rice, a miscellaneous tax of 31,556.3096 hyō, and a cash remittance of 109 ryō 1 bu plus 238 mon. The household return is 6,476 in total, itemised as 275 shizoku, 398 sotsu, and 5,803 remaining households, the last including 7 shrine-family households and 67 temples. Population stands at 31,031, of whom 1,343 are shizoku (657 male, 686 female) and 487 sotsu (242 male, 245 female), with 52 persons in shrine households and 290 in temples."
  },
  {
   "id": "ono_lower_p156_right",
   "sequence": 576,
   "domain_canonical": "大野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大野藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōno",
   "image": "images/lower_p156_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 156,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（大野）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 8 (Ōno) — running header / provenance",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-8 personnel/organization: Okazaki's officials-tail + military overflow, then the opening of Ōno's roster",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 (personnel and organization) page, printed book page 288, records the tail of Okazaki domain's roster followed by the opening of Ōno domain's block. On the Okazaki side — read first, to the right of the ○大野藩 marker — it lists the two vice junior councillors (権少参事) Sano Hanji and Ishibashi Zehachi (noted as reported to the caretaker office/Rusukan on Meiji 3, 4th month, 23rd day), the official Ishihara Hachijūrō with a textual-variant note, and Okazaki's military: an infantry half-battalion of 300 men, 29 gunners (砲), and a 189-man garrison unit (留守隊). The ○大野藩 marker then opens Ōno, whose upper register names the offices 知事 (governor; no holder entered here), 大参事, and 権大参事 (3 officials), with the four office-holders Nakamura Masanoshin, Okada Kyūma, Totsuka Josui and Uchiyama Sukesuke listed in the lower name register. The running header names Ōno; Ōno's own military and remaining officials continue on the facing page (printed 289)."
  },
  {
   "id": "ono_lower_p156_left",
   "sequence": 577,
   "domain_canonical": "大野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大野藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōno",
   "image": "images/lower_p156_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 156,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百八十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（大多喜）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 8 (Ōtaki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Ōno Domain officials and military establishment; Ōtaki Domain section-marker",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 (officials and military) page whose data belongs to Ōno Domain (大野藩), continued from the preceding leaf. The civil roster lists Junior Councillors (少参事, 2 members) and a Vice Junior Councillor (権少参事, 1 member); an editorial warichu note states that the following four lines were in vermilion in the original manuscript and records a manuscript variant. Three lower offices follow — Senior Councillor (大参事), Vice Senior Councillor (権大参事) and Junior Councillor (少参事) — with seven named office-holders (鈴木準治, 中村束, 吉田拙藏, 中村雅之進, 戸塚如水, 小野茅, 大熊潜). The military establishment records 192 total personnel (兵員), 48 company- and half-company-commanders and below, 142 soldiers (兵士), 50 rank-and-file troops (兵卒) and 48 peasant militia (農兵). At the left the maru-marker ○大多喜藩 opens the next domain, Ōtaki, whose figures continue overleaf; the running header names 大多喜 as provenance and the printed page number is 289."
  },
  {
   "id": "otaki_upper_p080_right",
   "sequence": 578,
   "domain_canonical": "大多喜藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大多喜藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōtaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p080_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 80,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大多喜）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 2 — (Ōtaki)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōtaki: assessed yield, land and miscellaneous taxes, samurai population and households",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of fascicle 2 opens the entry for Ōtaki (大多喜藩) in Kazusa, and the four military lines standing to the right of the ○大多喜藩 marker close the preceding entry for Ōno (大野藩): 48 men from company and half-company commander down, 50 rank-and-file (兵卒), 142 soldiers (兵士) and 48 farmer-soldiers (農兵), 288 in all. Ōtaki's assessed yield (草高) is 27,281.93669 koku; against it the regular land tax runs to 7,580.119085 koku of rice plus 2,023 kan 363 mon in ei-denominated cash and 9 kan 969 mon in copper cash, and the miscellaneous tax to 5.771 koku of rice plus 17 kan 240 mon. The domain returns 698 shizoku (printed as 320 male and 371 female, two sub-counts that total 691 and fall seven short of the printed total), 113 sotsu marked as entered in the commoner register (民籍ニ編入), and 4,204 households, with a further sixteen households whose 56 people (32 male, 24 female) are recorded separately. A small-type note 五年平均 at the foot of the 草高 column marks the returns as five-year averages."
  },
  {
   "id": "otaki_lower_p157_right",
   "sequence": 579,
   "domain_canonical": "大多喜藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大多喜藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōtaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p157_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 157,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大溝）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, eighth fascicle (Ōmizo) — running page-header / provenance",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster and military strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This recto (folio 290) from the eighth fascicle of the Hansei ichiran (domain officials and military) closes Ōtaki domain's entry and opens Ōmizo's, the two separated by the ○大溝藩 maru-marker. Ōtaki records a vacant governorship (知事), three gon-daisanji (Ōno Han, Inoue Noboru, Amano Hanzaburō) and four shōsanji (Okamoto Kingo, Kubota Hyakuroku, Iwakami Makita, Mori Hankichi), plus a military force of one platoon of 48 men drilled on the French model (佛式). Ōmizo, opened by its marker, shows a vacant governorship, a daisanji establishment of one member (Miyake Jirō) and a gon-daisanji establishment of three members (one named here, Nagano Kishichi). The running header names Ōmizo, although most of the page's data belongs to the preceding domain, Ōtaki."
  },
  {
   "id": "okada_upper_p081_right",
   "sequence": 580,
   "domain_canonical": "岡田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡田藩",
   "domain_en": "Okada",
   "image": "images/upper_p081_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 81,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（岡田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 2 (Okada)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōmizo's demographic tail and the opening of Okada's fascicle-2 entry",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-2 leaf carrying two domains. The seven columns to the right of the ○岡田藩 marker close out Ōmizo Domain: 2,526 households and 11,433 people (5,663 male, 5,770 female), 143 hinin and 57 eta, four shrine staff, 34 villages, and 195 Buddhist clergy plus 7 nuns. The five columns to the left open Okada Domain's entry with an assessed yield (草高) of 16,983.95003 koku, a rice land tax (正租米) of 7,699.76473 koku, miscellaneous cash taxes of 415 ryō 2 bu 1 shu plus 254 mon 9 rin 9 mō, and a warrior establishment of 143 shizoku and 159 sotsu households. Okada's shizoku-and-sotsu population is printed as 1,123, though its own components (513 men, 499 women, 130 children) total 1,142."
  },
  {
   "id": "okada_upper_p081_left",
   "sequence": 581,
   "domain_canonical": "岡田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡田藩",
   "domain_en": "Okada",
   "image": "images/upper_p081_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 81,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小野）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Survey, Fascicle 2 (Ono)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Okada demographic and religious tail; Ono opening land and tax figures",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of this leaf close out Okada Domain's fascicle-2 entry, which begins on the facing page (book p. 136). It records 3,084 households and a population of 16,231, a parenthetical breakdown of the samurai-household population into 470 shizoku and 653 sotsu, an outcaste population of 1,151 eta in 83 households and 173 onbo in 27 households, 21 shrines with 21 shrine-service households (28 men, 38 women), and 56 temples plus 9 hermitages staffed by 48 monks and 7 nuns. The maru-marker ○小野藩 then opens Ono Domain, whose four opening entries follow to its left: an assessed yield (kusadaka) of 11,099.313 koku, of which 1,099.313 koku is newly surveyed reclaimed land; regular land tax of 5,281.03858 koku; and miscellaneous tax of 1 ryō 2 bu in cash. The running header names Ono even though most of the page's data is Okada's."
  },
  {
   "id": "okada_lower_p157_left",
   "sequence": 582,
   "domain_canonical": "岡田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "岡田藩",
   "domain_en": "Okada",
   "image": "images/lower_p157_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 157,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（岡田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Okada)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military (fascicle 8): Ōmizo tail and Okada",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page tabulates domain officials and military establishment for two neighboring domains. The right side continues the roster of Ōmizo (大溝藩): a Senior Councillor line (retainer Maeda Tokuzō plus one vacant post, 一員欠), three Junior Councillors (少參事三員), two Acting Senior Councillors (權大參事貳員), and a military strength of two platoons totaling 100 troops (貳小隊兵員百人). To the left of the ○岡田藩 marker begins Okada (岡田藩), whose entries list a Governor (知事, no incumbent name printed), one Senior Councillor (大參事一員, Uraike), and two Acting Senior Councillors (權大參事二員, Tatekawa Kyū and Katō Jihei). The printed page number is 291."
  },
  {
   "id": "ono_upper_p082_right",
   "sequence": 583,
   "domain_canonical": "小野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小野藩",
   "domain_en": "Ono",
   "image": "images/upper_p082_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 82,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小幡）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabular Conspectus of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Obata)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "End of Ono domain's civil and military return; opening of Obata domain's assessed yield",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes Ono domain's fascicle-2 return and opens Obata's. For Ono the survey records 1,646 households and a population of 7,395 (3,700 male, 3,695 female); 153 samurai and sotsu households comprising 691 people (79 shizoku households with 386 people, 74 sotsu households with 305); 30 villages; 20 shrines with 5 priest households totalling 28 people; and 17 temples with 27 monks and 5 nuns, plus a supplementary 4 monks and 1 woman. Ono's forces are two companies, the Ichiwa-tai and the Ryujo-tai, each with 6 officers and 36 soldiers, together with 14 gunners and 4 drum-and-fife men. To the left of the ○小幡藩 marker Obata's entry begins with a nominal yield of 23,070.141 koku, printed as a 20,000-koku base plus 3,070.145 koku folded in from newly opened and reassessed fields."
  },
  {
   "id": "ono_lower_p158_right",
   "sequence": 584,
   "domain_canonical": "小野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小野藩",
   "domain_en": "Ono",
   "image": "images/lower_p158_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 158,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（小野）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey Table, Fascicle 8 (Ono)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials roster + military (fascicle 8): Okada tail and Ono",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 leaf carries the officials rosters of two small Bitchū-province domains. To the right of the ○小野藩 marker stand the closing entries of Okada domain (岡田藩): a junior councillor (少参事, 1 member — Inamura Shin) and a provisional junior councillor (権少参事, 1 member — Sano Tsuna), then its military — the regular troops (兵隊), whose strength the domain reports as not yet fixed (a note dated 己巳/1869, tenth month), and 100 foot-soldiers (兵卒). Left of the marker begins Ono domain (小野藩), whose governor is 一柳越智宿禰末德 (Hitotsuyanagi Suenori, Junior Fifth Rank): the roster gives one senior councillor (河合藤原政溫忠), two provisional senior councillors (神山源正滿保・黒石平長之涯), two assembly representatives (公議人: 葛山藤原正貫半・福鳥大江智信漠) and two junior councillors (原田越智敦明又兵衛・寺本藤原惟常); the 権少参事 heading is printed but left unfilled here. Printed folio number 292."
  },
  {
   "id": "obata_upper_p082_left",
   "sequence": 585,
   "domain_canonical": "小幡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小幡藩",
   "domain_en": "Obata",
   "image": "images/upper_p082_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 82,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小幡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Obata)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Obata domain land tax, households, population, temples and shrines",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the second part of Obata domain's fascicle-2 return, running from the tax figures on the right through the household and population counts in the middle to the religious establishments on the left. The domain reports an actual rice yield of 3,631.3348 koku, a dry-field tax of 3,234.1846 kan and miscellaneous taxes of 1,070.8955 kan in eiraku cash, which the small-type notes convert to 404.273 and 133.861 koku, and a parenthetical line totals the three at 4,169.4697 koku. On the demographic side Obata records 2,979 households and 13,257 people, 212 samurai households and 65 sotsu households holding 639 people between them. The religious entries give 62 temples with 57 monks and 19 servants, 3 Shugendo households, and 8 shrines whose 11 shrine-family households hold 39 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "obata_lower_p158_left",
   "sequence": 586,
   "domain_canonical": "小幡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小幡藩",
   "domain_en": "Obata",
   "image": "images/lower_p158_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 158,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（小幡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle 8 (Obata)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military units (Obata head / Ono tail)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page from Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran spans two domains, divided by the ○小幡藩 marker. To the right of the marker is the tail of Ono Domain (小野藩): its Acting Junior Councillor (権少参事 Inoue Sugawara-no-Korei), followed by four military units — the Ichiwa infantry unit (36 soldiers plus 6 officers), the Ryūjō unit (ditto, 36 plus 6 officers), the artillery unit (14 gunners), and the drum-and-fife corps (4). Left of the marker begins Obata Domain (小幡藩), whose officials are a vacant governorship (知事), 2 Senior Councillors (大参事), 2 Acting Senior Councillors (権大参事), and 4 Junior Councillors (少参事); six of their names are printed in the lower register (Ogura Mataichi, Naoi Tetsuya, Saitō Watando, Ishihara Shichirō, Kikuta Yonegorō, Honda Kyūma). The printed book-page number is 293."
  },
  {
   "id": "obata_lower_p159_right",
   "sequence": 587,
   "domain_canonical": "小幡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小幡藩",
   "domain_en": "Obata",
   "image": "images/lower_p159_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 159,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（荻野山中）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Ogino-yamanaka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster and military establishment (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This Fascicle-8 leaf (officials and military), printed leaf number 294, completes the 小幡藩 (Obata) entry and opens that of 荻野山中藩 (Ogino-yamanaka). For Obata, right of the marker, it records a three-member Provisional Junior Councilor office (權少參事 三員) with five named officials (平子子平, 濱田藤治, 山本榮, 矢野記内, 松浦數馬) and an editorial note 一二松浦ナシ, plus the military establishment: no separate troop-unit figure is given (兵隊 記セス) but total strength is 100 men (兵員 百人), glossed in a warichu note as 3 platoons of 32 men each plus 4 gunners (3×32 + 4 = 100). The ○荻野山中藩 marker then opens Ogino-yamanaka, whose roster begins with an unfilled governorship (知事), Senior Councilor 井上正行 (大參事), and two Provisional Senior Councilors 横山政達 and 岡山隆德 (權大參事). The running header names 荻野山中 as provenance."
  },
  {
   "id": "kokubo_upper_p083_left",
   "sequence": 588,
   "domain_canonical": "小久保藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小久保藩",
   "domain_en": "Kokubo",
   "image": "images/upper_p083_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 83,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（小久保）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 2 (Kokubo)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "closing population, temple and shrine columns for one domain and the opening yield-and-tax columns for the next",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page closes the fascicle-2 entry for Ogino-Yamanaka Domain and opens that for Kokubo Domain, the boundary marked by the ○小久保藩 circle two-thirds of the way across. Ogino-Yamanaka's trailing columns give 25 villages; a retainer-class population of 345 persons (179 male, 161 female) divided into 285 shizoku and 57 sotsu, with 25 further sotsu counted separately; 72 shizoku and 33 sotsu households; 2 shugen households of 4 persons; 46 temples with 42 monks; 49 shrines with 10 attendant households and 52 persons; and 48 eta households totalling 299 persons. Left of the marker, Kokubo's entry begins with a gross assessed yield (kusadaka) of 11,265.1497 koku, regular land tax of 3,329.96779 koku, miscellaneous taxes of 79.74773 koku, and a 17.3092-koku reduction arising from a village exchange. Two of the printed sub-totals do not reconcile with their own male-female splits: the retainer population is set at 345 against components summing to 340, and the shizoku total at 285 against 142 plus 141."
  },
  {
   "id": "kokubo_upper_p084_right",
   "sequence": 589,
   "domain_canonical": "小久保藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小久保藩",
   "domain_en": "Kokubo",
   "image": "images/upper_p084_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 84,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（生實）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Oyumi)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Kokubo civil and religious returns; Oyumi kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "The right five-sixths of the leaf completes the fascicle-2 return for Kokubo Domain in Kazusa: 2,262 households and a printed population of 9,750 (4,880 male and 4,837 female, which sum to 9,717 and leave a 33-person gap in the source), of which 120 shizoku households hold 361 people (197 male, 164 female) plus 31 menial attendants. It also records 47 shrines with 7 attendant households and 39 attendant persons, 47 temples with 49 monks, 1 nun and 9 lay religious, 29 villages, and a force of 43 troops. A closing note adds 55 koku of former vermilion-seal land held outside the main assessment: 40 koku for Saishofukuji in Shinmido village, Sue district, Kazusa province, and 15 koku for Kenryakuji in Hamafuru village of the same district. Left of the maru-marker the entry for Oyumi Domain opens with a kusadaka of 10,627.70566 koku, of which 598.19886 koku is newly reclaimed land counted into the total."
  },
  {
   "id": "kokubo_lower_p159_left",
   "sequence": 590,
   "domain_canonical": "小久保藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "小久保藩",
   "domain_en": "Kokubo",
   "image": "images/lower_p159_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 159,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（小久保）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Kokubo)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-8 officials roster and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a fascicle-8 (officials and military) page whose ○ marker begins 小久保藩 (Kokubo, a Kazusa domain of the Hayashi house). For Kokubo the page prints the councillor establishment — 大参事 （四員）二員 and 少参事 （五員）一員 — while the governor (知事) seat carries only a 庚午ノ調 (1870 Kōgo survey) note with no count, and six retainer names appear in the councillor registers (鈴木晉平, 篠原眞, 龜山政喜, 鈴木庵, 都筑貫一, 林小逸郎). To the right of the marker the tail of the preceding domain 荻野山中藩 overflows: its 少参事 (安西胤繼, 石橋信奎, 松下藏人), 権少参事 (堀田又兵衞), and a military strength of 兵隊 八拾人 (80 troops). The printed leaf number is 二百九十五 (295)."
  },
  {
   "id": "oyumi_upper_p084_left",
   "sequence": 591,
   "domain_canonical": "生實藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "生實藩",
   "domain_en": "Oyumi",
   "image": "images/upper_p084_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 84,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百四十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（生實）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Table (fascicle) Two — Oyumi",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Land tax, cash revenue, households, population, samurai households, villages and shrines",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the tax, household and population block of the fascicle-2 return for Oyumi domain (生實藩, Kazusa Province, present-day Chiba City), a small Morikawa house. Revenue is given as regular land tax in rice of 3,827.250544 koku plus miscellaneous taxes of 183.155347 koku plus a cash item of 176 ryō 2 shu and 11 mon, which the survey converts to 22.015762 koku at the stated rate of eight ryō to the koku, for a printed total of 4,032.42166 koku. The domain returns 1,774 households and 8,785 people across 29 villages, of which the samurai population is 203 households (87 shizoku, 116 sotsu) and 540 people. Seventy-six Shinto shrines are recorded, staffed by 15 men and 10 women."
  },
  {
   "id": "oyumi_lower_p160_right",
   "sequence": 592,
   "domain_canonical": "生實藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "生實藩",
   "domain_en": "Oyumi",
   "image": "images/lower_p160_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 160,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（生實）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Oyumi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (fascicle 8): councillor head-counts and named office-holders",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 officials page straddles the boundary between two small Kazusa/Shimōsa domains, marked by the single ○生實藩 (Oyumi) marker. To the RIGHT of the marker it carries the tail of Okubo (小久保) domain's administration: 53 troops (兵隊, with an editorial parenthetical reading 四十三人 that does not match the total), 3 acting senior councillors (權大參事), and 3 acting junior councillors (權少參事), together with a roster of nine named office-holders (堀部積, 井上賢, 中桐友衞, 各務貫, 中村民治, 阿部貞, 中村定, 堀策郎, 島田實). To the LEFT, Oyumi (生實) domain's block begins: the governorship (知事) is listed without a name, and the single senior councillor (大參事, 一名) is named 氏家平馬. The running header files the page under 生實 (fascicle 8); the printed page number is 296."
  },
  {
   "id": "oyumi_lower_p160_left",
   "sequence": 593,
   "domain_canonical": "生實藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "生實藩",
   "domain_en": "Oyumi",
   "image": "images/lower_p160_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 160,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（大田原）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Overview, Fascicle 8 (Ōtawara)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials and military roster (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the tail of the fascicle-8 (officials and military) entry for Oyumi Domain (生實藩); all of its data prints to the right of the ○大田原藩 maru-marker that opens the next domain. Oyumi's senior staff comprise 2 gon-daisanji (權大參事), 3 shō-sanji (少參事, against an establishment of 5), and gon-shōsanji (權少參事), with eleven named officers in all — among them the public-affairs officer (公用方) Nakagawa Sajiuemon. The domain's rifle corps of three platoons (銃手三小隊) numbers 144 men, with a variant figure of 218 noted in parentheses. The running header and marker at left begin Ōtawara Domain (大田原藩), whose own data starts on the following leaf; the printed book-page number is 297."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamauchi_lower_p164_left",
   "sequence": 594,
   "domain_canonical": "山内藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山内藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamauchi",
   "image": "images/lower_p164_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 164,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（山内、龜岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle 8 (Yamauchi, Kameoka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left page of the fascicle-8 (officials and military) spread for the Yamauchi and Kameoka domains. Its right portion continues the previous domain, Kochi (Tosa): the total naval-and-land forces of 9,000 men (海陸兵員 九千人, equal to Tosa's 6,600 standing plus 2,400 reserve troops) and seven of its senior officials, including Iwasaki Yataro (岩崎彌太郎), the future founder of Mitsubishi. The Yamauchi Domain block, opened by the ○山内藩 marker, records the governor (知事) and senior-councillor (大参事) office headers and a standing force of 89 men (常備兵 八十九人). The ○龜岡藩 marker at the left margin opens the small Kameoka Domain, whose figures continue on the following page. The printed page number is 305."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameoka_upper_p091_right",
   "sequence": 595,
   "domain_canonical": "龜岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p091_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 91,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（龜岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Table, Fascicle 2 (Kameoka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Kameoka: closing kind-to-cash conversions, total kokudaka, households, population and shrines",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-2 return for Kameoka Domain (龜岡藩) with no maru-marker of its own, so every figure on it belongs to the block opened on the preceding leaf. It closes out the revenue schedule — a straw-rope, matting and bran levy worth 193 kan 570 mon 2 bu 6 rin in ei-currency, equal to 193 ryō 2 bu 1 shu in gold and to 24.1962 koku of rice at the stated rate of eight ryō the koku — and then prints the grand total, 28,381.1367 koku. The demographic block follows: 10,843 households and a population of 45,253 (23,343 male, 21,910 female), of which 533 shizoku households holding 682 domain retainers and 2,034 people (652 male, 1,382 female), and 525 sotsu households with 724 people (383 male, 341 female). The leaf ends with 25 Shinto shrines staffed by 69 shrine officers (36 male, 33 female). The printed page number in the bottom margin is 156."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameoka_lower_p165_right",
   "sequence": 596,
   "domain_canonical": "龜岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p165_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 165,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（龜岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Kameoka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Kameoka domain councillor offices, appointee roster, and armed-retainer totals (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a fascicle-8 (職員, officials-and-armed-retainers) page for Kameoka domain (龜岡藩). It lists the councillor offices with their current strength and regular establishment: 大參事 1 (one appointee, with a 欠 vacancy noted), 權大參事 2 against an establishment of 3 (三員), 少參事 3 against 5 (五名), and 權少參事 4; the 知事 (domain governor) office is named but its value is left blank. Ten named appointees are rostered in the lower band, each anchored under its office (大參事: 奥村愛竹; 權大參事: 酒井惺齋, 加藤增人; 少參事: 太田一道, 坂部螻堂, 柳島彦作; 權少參事: 坂部恒, 松島潜, 內藤盤溪, 伴牛). Two aggregate figures close the block at the far left: 銃士卒 (musketeer foot-soldiers) 154 and 役員 (staff) 43. No maru-marker is printed on the page; the domain is identified only by the running header, and the printed book-page number is 三百六 (306)."
  },
  {
   "id": "karatsu_upper_p091_left",
   "sequence": 597,
   "domain_canonical": "唐津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "唐津藩",
   "domain_en": "Karatsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p091_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 91,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百五十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（唐津）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabular Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Karatsu)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Karatsu's land assessment and yields, after the tail of Kameoka's civil returns",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes Kameoka Domain's civil returns and opens Karatsu Domain's at the ○唐津藩 marker. Kameoka's tail records 290 temples (231 monks, 41 women, 13 nuns), 131 villages, 156 soldiers, 43 officials and 79 reserve sotsu. Karatsu's block then gives a gross assessment (草高) of 64,735.863 koku against a nominal enfeoffment of 60,000 koku, with 3,727.519 koku of newly opened field and 1,263.344 koku of komidaka inside it. The paddy and dry-field figures — 48,393.438 koku taxed at an average rate of 0.4057723 and 16,342.425 koku at 0.3853866 — add up exactly to the gross assessment, and the two rates reproduce the printed yields of 19,636.721 koku from the paddy and 25,934.873 koku in all, the latter noted as a five-year average running from the Rat year to the Dragon year (1864-1868)."
  },
  {
   "id": "karatsu_lower_p165_left",
   "sequence": 598,
   "domain_canonical": "唐津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "唐津藩",
   "domain_en": "Karatsu",
   "image": "images/lower_p165_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 165,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（唐津）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 8 (Karatsu)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Karatsu domain officials roster (fascicle 8, 職員)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-8 (officials, 職員) page for Karatsu Domain (唐津藩), printed page 307. Reading right to left, the entry opens with the ○唐津藩 marker and lists the domain's Meiji-4 administrative roster: one governor (知事, Ogasawara Nagakuni), two senior councillors (大参事: Nakazawa Izumi, Fukuda Tokinaka), three acting senior councillors (権大参事), three junior councillors (少参事), and four acting-junior-councillor posts (権少参事), of which three names are legibly printed. The single column to the right of the marker, 豫備卒 七十九人 (79 reserve conscripts), is overflow belonging to the preceding domain, Kameoka (龜岡藩), whose full entry occupies the facing page (page 306); Kameoka's military tail there ends with 154 gunner-conscripts and 43 staff, with the reserve count spilling onto this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameda_upper_p098_right",
   "sequence": 599,
   "domain_canonical": "龜田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜田藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameda",
   "image": "images/upper_p098_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 98,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（龜田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Kameda)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kameda domain assessed yield and five-year-average tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Kameda domain (龜田藩, Dewa) entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, the fiscal fascicle. Kameda's nominal assessed yield (草高) is 19,904.555 koku, from which a five-year average deduction of 2,296.411 koku for landslides, river washouts, distant or abandoned fields, and crop-failure abatement leaves 17,608.144 koku. The five-year average tax take is 8,781.1814 koku of regular land tax in actual rice, 3,161.3069 koku of miscellaneous tax in rice, and 2,052 ryō 3 shu in cash converted at 8 ryō per koku to 256.5234 koku, giving a grand total of 12,199.0117 koku, stated equivalently as 48,796 bales at 0.25 koku of base rice each (0.29 koku including the nobekuchi handling surcharge). The parenthesised military figures in the far-right column — 15 troop officers, one upper-grade platoon, two lower-grade platoons, and 16 artillerymen — stand to the right of the ○龜田藩 marker and therefore close out the preceding domain, Kanō."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameda_upper_p098_left",
   "sequence": 600,
   "domain_canonical": "龜田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜田藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameda",
   "image": "images/upper_p098_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 98,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（龜田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Kameda)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kameda produce prices and household/population returns",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-3 return for Kameda (Dewa province, Iwaki house) with no domain marker on the page, so the whole leaf belongs to Kameda as named in the running header. The upper block closes the 產物 (produce) list with five commodities and their official prices: soybeans at 420 mon per bale, with a note that the tax on them has been collected in cash since the kanoe-uma year (Meiji 3 / 1870) and that the same applies to the entries below; red beans and wheat at the same unit and the same price; millet seed at the same price per straw bag; and bracken starch at 840 mon per straw bag. The lower block gives the household and population returns under the paired headings 戸數 and 人員: 230 shizoku households with 1,208 people (603 male, 605 female), 301 sotsu households with 1,507 people (717 male, 790 female), and 3,437 commoner (hyakushō) households with 19,113 people (10,045 male, 9,068 female). Every male-plus-female split sums exactly to its printed total, and the three household counts match the project's extracted dataset, which however records none of the nine population figures and none of the produce prices."
  },
  {
   "id": "kameda_upper_p099_right",
   "sequence": 601,
   "domain_canonical": "龜田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜田藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameda",
   "image": "images/upper_p099_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 99,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（龜田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Kameda)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kameda domain household and population table (fascicle 3)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the tail of the fascicle-3 household-and-population table for Kameda domain. It closes the commoner status list with townspeople — 298 houses holding 1,430 people (712 male, 718 female) — then states the domain's ordinary households at 4,266 and the people in them at 23,258 (12,077 male, 11,181 female). Under the small heading 外ニ (\"in addition\") four supplementary categories follow: shrine-attendant families (14 households, 79 people), Shugendō ascetics (26, 182), temples (42 establishments, 314 as printed), and eta outcaste households (8, 45), subtotalled at 90 households and 636 people. The grand total is 4,356 households and 23,894 people; twenty shrines are counted; four kazoku (2 male, 2 female) are recorded separately outside the total; and the district-and-village count is entered as 未詳, \"not ascertained.\""
  },
  {
   "id": "kameda_lower_p168_left",
   "sequence": 602,
   "domain_canonical": "龜田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龜田藩",
   "domain_en": "Kameda",
   "image": "images/lower_p168_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 168,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（龜田、上ノ山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 8 (Kameda, Kaminoyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials roster & military strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 (officials & military) leaf carrying the administrative roster of 龜田藩 (Kameda, Dewa) and the opening of 上ノ山藩 (Kaminoyama). Kameda lists a 知事 (governor — the rank heading is printed but no appointee name appears on this leaf), a 大參事 (Iwaki Takatomo, 岩城隆知), two 權大參事 (Yoshida Tomoyuki 吉田俱之 and Unuma Kunimō 鵜沼國蒙), and two 少參事 (Saso Toyokata 佐曾豐賢 and Yoshikawa Nobutoshi 吉川信敏), followed by its military strength of 277 personnel (兵員貳百七拾七人). Kaminoyama's block begins with governor 從五位松平源信安 (Jugoi Matsudaira [Minamoto] Nobuyasu) and 大參事 藤井八百太郎 (Fujii Yaohatarō); its remaining ranks and troops continue on the next leaf. The two rightmost name columns (安達蘇平, 吉田古今吾) are the roster tail of the preceding domain, 笠間藩. Printed book page 313 (三百十三)."
  },
  {
   "id": "kashima_upper_p101_left",
   "sequence": 603,
   "domain_canonical": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_en": "Kashima (Hizen)",
   "image": "images/upper_p101_left.jpg",
