   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（鹿島）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Kashima)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kashima domain land area, land-rice and tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the whole of the Kashima domain entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran; a single maru-marker (○鹿島藩) opens it and no other domain appears. Kashima's assessed kokudaka is 20,000 koku, made up of 1,939 chō 8 tan 6 se of arable yielding 13,711.1444 koku of land-rice and 1,515 chō 1 se of hill and moor yielding 6,288.8556 koku, the two figures summing exactly to the 20,000 koku the page then restates. On a five-year average the domain collected 10,047.2682 koku in regular land tax and 28 kan 159 monme 9 rin of silver in miscellaneous imposts, the silver reckoned at eight ryō to the koku and so equal to 58.6648 koku of hulled rice, for a combined actual rice revenue of 10,105.933 koku. The closing note 右十分之一 marks the one-tenth share of that revenue, but the amount itself is not printed on this page; the printed book-page number is 177."
  },
  {
   "id": "kashima_upper_p102_right",
   "sequence": 604,
   "domain_canonical": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_en": "Kashima (Hizen)",
   "image": "images/upper_p102_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 102,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（鹿島）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, fascicle three (Kashima)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kashima land-rice deductions and the governor's stipend",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 178 of fascicle three carries the close of Kashima domain's Meiji 3 (1870) return and the whole of its earlier Meiji 2 (1869) return. The 1870 block ends with a governor's household stipend of 1,010.5933 koku of rice, exactly one tenth of the 10,105.933 koku of actual rice recorded on the preceding page, followed by the note that the return was submitted in the twelfth month of the kanoe-uma year. After a separator circle the 1869 return restates the nominal land rice of 20,000 koku and subtracts three items: 315.2594 koku for the domain's residences, shrines and temples and other building plots; 3,348.6166 koku written off for crop failure from flood, tidal inundation and drought, taken as a five-year average; and 6,288.8556 koku assessed on mountain and moorland that yields no rice. Those three sum exactly to the printed total of 9,952.7316 koku, leaving 10,047.2684 koku as the annual land-tax receipt in actual rice, of which the page directs that one tenth be taken."
  },
  {
   "id": "kashima_upper_p102_left",
   "sequence": 605,
   "domain_canonical": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_en": "Kashima (Hizen)",
   "image": "images/upper_p102_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 102,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（鹿島）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table Three (Kashima)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kashima domain: governor's stipend, products and their silver taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page completes the fascicle-three return of Kashima domain (Hizen, 20,000 koku, a branch house of Saga), whose entry opened after the bare circle on the facing page 178. It closes the land-and-rice section with the governor's household stipend of 1,000 koku — one tenth of the 10,047.2684 koku of annual net rice revenue reported on the facing page — and with the note dating the return to the tenth month of 1869. It then lists the domain's products: 20,000-odd kin of processed tea and 50,000 kin of haze wax, each taxed 10 kanme of silver; 3,000 koku of sake taxed 3 kanme; bamboo, timber and firewood taxed 5 kanme 170 monme 4 bu; and eight untaxed goods (pottery, charcoal, paper, roof tiles, tobacco, dried shrimp, jellyfish and shochu). The four taxes sum exactly to the stated total of 28 kanme 170 monme 4 bu, of which one tenth, 2 kanme 817 monme, went to the governor. The demographic section records 3,135 households and 13,721 people, of whom the shizoku accounted for 294 households and 1,644 people (778 male, 866 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "kashima_upper_p103_right",
   "sequence": 606,
   "domain_canonical": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_en": "Kashima (Hizen)",
   "image": "images/upper_p103_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 103,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（鹿島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle 3 (Kashima)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kashima domain population by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the household-and-population return for Kashima domain in Hizen, a sub-domain of Saga, under fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran survey. Reading right to left it lists 卒 463 households / 1,823 persons, 社家 11 / 47, 寺院 41 / 148 (its male run headed 僧, monks: 111), 山伏 9 / 47, 百姓 1,804 / 8,126, 町人 508 / 1,863, and two bodies of retainers from neighbouring domains living in Kashima — 佐賀藩卒 4 / 19 and 蓮池藩卒 1 / 6. Two 外ニ (\"besides\") groups are then counted apart from that list: the outcaste categories 穢多 6 / 37 and 非人 8 / 32, whose printed 合 subtotal of 14 households and 69 persons matches them exactly; and the single 華族 household of 5 persons, its one male annotated 知事, the domain governor. The page closes with 社 十社, ten shrines. Every status entry carries a male/female breakdown that sums correctly to its total, and the categories together give 2,856 households and 12,153 persons."
  },
  {
   "id": "kashima_lower_p169_right",
   "sequence": 607,
   "domain_canonical": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鹿島藩",
   "domain_en": "Kashima (Hizen)",
   "image": "images/lower_p169_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 169,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（鹿島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle 8 (Kashima)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-8 domain officials rosters and troop counts",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 (officials and military) leaf. The right portion finishes Kaminoyama Domain (上ノ山藩, Dewa): its provisional senior councillors (権大参事) Matsudaira Narinoshin and Ono Sohei, its junior councillors (少参事) Tachibana Hirotaka, Sensui Hiroshi and Koike Harukage, and its forces — infantry of one company (noted at 60 men per platoon) and artillery of one section (15 men including officers). The ○鹿島藩 marker then opens Kashima Domain (鹿島藩, Hizen): the governor (知事) line is left blank, followed by senior councillor (大参事) Hara Yoichi and provisional senior councillors (権大参事) Nagano Kakuichi, Shimizu Kyoichi and Ureshino Issai. The running header reads 藩制一覧表第八（鹿島） and the printed page number is 314."
  },
  {
   "id": "kamogata_upper_p103_left",
   "sequence": 608,
   "domain_canonical": "鴨方藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鴨方藩",
   "domain_en": "Kamogata",
   "image": "images/upper_p103_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 103,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三 （鴨方）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Governance Survey (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 3 — Kamogata",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kamogata assessed yield and land tax",
   "page_summary_en": "The leaf closes Kashima domain's entry and opens Kamogata's. To the right of the ○鴨方藩 marker stand Kashima's settlement count — one district (the eastern part of Fujitsu), two rural townships (Kashima and Nokomi), 35 villages, 5 towns, 2 post-stations, 5 harbours — and a parenthetical troop note recording twelve companies formed into two battalions, 400 men in all. Left of the marker the survey states Kamogata's fiscal base: a nominal assessment of 25,000 koku, a further 839.77 koku of newly reclaimed paddy brought onto the register, and a combined assessment of 25,839.77 koku. The regular land tax, given as a five-year average in net hulled rice, is 9,216.9846 koku — about 35.7 percent of the combined assessment — alongside a cash item of 5 ryō plus 489.5 mon in eiraku reckoning, and salt is listed as the domain's product, untaxed."
  },
  {
   "id": "kamogata_upper_p104_right",
   "sequence": 609,
   "domain_canonical": "鴨方藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鴨方藩",
   "domain_en": "Kamogata",
   "image": "images/upper_p104_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 104,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（鴨方）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Kamogata)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf from Kamogata Domain's entry in Fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran, giving the domain's household and population counts broken out by status. Kamogata reports 4,425 households and a population of 27,793. The household breakdown is 138 shizoku, 109 sotsu, 168 keisotsu, 3,973 commoners (of whom 15 are eta households), 23 Shinto priestly households and 14 yamabushi households, which sums exactly to the 4,425 total; a note records that the domain's seven temple buildings are excluded from that count. On the population side the leaf records 494 shizoku (251 male, 243 female), 291 sotsu, 312 keisotsu and 26,455 commoners (13,549 male, 12,701 female), with 205 eta (113 male, 92 female) counted inside the commoner total."
  },
  {
   "id": "kamogata_lower_p169_left",
   "sequence": 610,
   "domain_canonical": "鴨方藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鴨方藩",
   "domain_en": "Kamogata",
   "image": "images/lower_p169_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 169,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（鴨方）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Kamogata)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials roster (junior councillors) and military of Kashima; opening of Kamogata",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 leaf carries the tail of Kashima domain's (Hizen, a Saga/Nabeshima branch) officials-and-military entry alongside the opening of Kamogata domain (Bicchū, an Okayama/Ikeda branch). Kashima's junior councillors (shō-sanji) and provisional junior councillors (gon-shō-sanji) are listed by name across seven columns — including two men written Watanabe Kanji, one flagged by a marginal note recording the caretaker-official's report of his appointment as shō-sanji — followed by Kashima's forces: 288 troops and 4 cannon. Left of the ○鴨方藩 maru-marker, Kamogata's own entry begins with its governor (chiji, unnamed on this leaf) and its senior councillor (dai-sanji) Yamaba Takesada. The running head files the leaf under Kamogata; the printed leaf number is 315."
  },
  {
   "id": "kaibara_upper_p104_left",
   "sequence": 611,
   "domain_canonical": "柏原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柏原藩",
   "domain_en": "Kaibara",
   "image": "images/upper_p104_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 104,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（柏原）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Kaibara)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kaibara's assessed yield and tax, after the tail of Kamogata's returns",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand two-thirds of the leaf closes out the preceding domain's fascicle-3 return: 132 shrine-priest household members (69 male, 63 female), 5 Buddhist clergy, 104 yamabushi (49 male, 55 female), a total population of 27,793, seven shrine buildings, one kazoku household of three persons (two male, one of them the domain governor; one female), and a bracketed military note recording a rifle platoon with eight officers and an artillery corps of fourteen men forming one squad. The maru-marker for 柏原藩 at mid-leaf opens Kaibara's own block. Kaibara returns a base assessment of 20,000 koku plus 133.6976 koku of newly opened field, giving a kusadaka of 20,133.6976 koku; against that it renders 7,007.05098 koku in rice as the main land tax and a further 2,003.41328 koku paid in cash and stated here in rice equivalent. The running header and the printed page number 183 place the leaf in fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran under Kaibara."
  },
  {
   "id": "kaibara_upper_p105_right",
   "sequence": 612,
   "domain_canonical": "柏原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柏原藩",
   "domain_en": "Kaibara",
   "image": "images/upper_p105_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 105,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（柏原）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Kaibara)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kaibara domain: miscellaneous taxes and household/population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Kaibara (Tanba) return in fascicle 3 of the Hansei Ichiran, and carries the domain's miscellaneous taxes together with its household and population counts. The miscellaneous taxes were rendered in three media: 173.1103 koku of rice, 20 ryō in gold, and 179.1 mon in eiraku cash. Kaibara reported 4,024 households and a population of 17,569 (8,900 male, 8,669 female); counted separately from that total were 139 shizoku households with 633 people and 70 sotsu households with 273 people. Religious personnel are broken out as 20 shrine-priest households with 61 people, 66 temples with 149 people, and 8 Shugendō households with 24 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "kashiwara_lower_p170_right",
   "sequence": 613,
   "domain_canonical": "柏原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柏原藩",
   "domain_en": "Kaibara",
   "image": "images/lower_p170_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 170,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（柏原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Table, Fascicle 8 (Kashiwara) — running header",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-8 officials rosters and military strength: Kamogata tail + Kashiwara opening",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page carries the tail of Kamogata-han's (鴨方藩) officials-and-military roster followed by the opening of Kashiwara-han (柏原藩), the domain named in the running header and marked by the ○柏原藩 boundary marker. Right of the marker, Kamogata lists four Acting Senior Councillors (権大参事: Uchida Tadaatsu, Uragami Munehisa, Yabuki Atsushi, Yabuki Tōru), a vacant Junior Councillor post (少参事 欠), and two Acting Junior Councillors (権少参事: Nishigōri Kunitami and Makihara), together with an artillery corps of 14 men (大砲隊 十四人) and a rifle corps of 10 platoons whose headcount is unrecorded (銃隊 十小隊 人員記セス; a variant note renders it as 20 platoons / 362 men). Left of the marker, Kashiwara opens with a Governor (知事, no appointee named), one Senior Councillor (大参事 一員: Tsuda Kaname) and two Acting Senior Councillors (権大参事 貳員, of whom only Tanabe is named). The bottom margin prints book page 316."
  },
  {
   "id": "karasuyama_upper_p105_left",
   "sequence": 614,
   "domain_canonical": "烏山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "烏山藩",
   "domain_en": "Karasuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p105_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 105,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（烏山）",
   "page_header_en": "Tables of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Karasuyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Karasuyama land assessment, tax receipts and household count",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fascicle-3 economic entry for Karasuyama Domain in Shimotsuke, opened by the ○烏山藩 marker in the upper right. Its nominal assessment (草高) and base holding (高) are both 30,000 koku; adding supplementary registered yield of 7,688.7668 koku and newly reclaimed land of 3,072.81924 koku gives a printed total (高合) of 40,761.58532 koku, which falls 0.00072 koku short of the sum of its own components. Regular land tax came to 6,136.2055 koku of rice plus 2,122 kan 177 mon 4 bu in cash, and miscellaneous taxes to 906.9427 koku of rice plus 789 kan 304 mon 9 bu 5 rin in cash; the domain counted 5,583 households, with a half-size inset noting 417. The four columns to the right of the marker still belong to the preceding domain: 11 nunnery households with 22 nuns, and a parenthesised military line of 50 heishi and 56 heisotsu."
  },
  {
   "id": "karasuyama_upper_p106_right",
   "sequence": 615,
   "domain_canonical": "烏山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "烏山藩",
   "domain_en": "Karasuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p106_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 106,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（烏山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Karasuyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Karasuyama population, status groups, temples and shrines, villages, militia",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 186 continues the Karasuyama (烏山藩) entry in fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran; the ○烏山藩 marker and the domain's land and tax figures stand on the facing page 185, so no marker appears here and the whole leaf belongs to Karasuyama. The population is printed as 27,209, divided 13,721 male and 13,193 female, and a smaller figure set beside the total gives 26,912 instead. Counted inside that population are 37 Shinto-priest households (137 people) and 121 temples (122 residents, of whom 101 are monks), with 60 temples recorded as having no resident priest. Listed separately under 外ニ are 209 samurai households (755 people), 46 sotsu households (76 people) together with 328 hired sotsu, and 28 eta households (128 people); the domain held 85 villages, and the page closes with a parenthesised militia return of three platoons of 52 men and an artillery company of 44, totalled at 203."
  },
  {
   "id": "karasuyama_lower_p170_left",
   "sequence": 616,
   "domain_canonical": "烏山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "烏山藩",
   "domain_en": "Karasuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p170_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 170,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（烏山）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration Systems, Fascicle 8 (Karasuyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left page from Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran records domain officials and military strength across a domain boundary. The right portion completes the entry for Kaibara Domain (柏原藩): 5 junior councillors (少参事), 1 acting junior councillor (権少参事), a garrison of 106 troops (兵員), and seven named officials. The circular marker ○烏山藩 then opens the entry for Karasuyama Domain (烏山藩), listing a governor post (知事, with no member count printed here), 2 senior councillors (大参事), and 3 acting senior councillors (権大参事), with three named officials shown (Ōtsuka Magohachirō, Ōkubo Kingo, Nakamura Tanomo) before the roster continues on the next page. The printed page number in the lower margin is 317."
  },
  {
   "id": "karasuyama_lower_p171_right",
   "sequence": 617,
   "domain_canonical": "烏山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "烏山藩",
   "domain_en": "Karasuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p171_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 171,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（刈谷）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 8 — running header: (Kariya)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Karasuyama fascicle-8 officials & military (overflow); Kariya opening marker",
   "page_summary_en": "This page (printed 318) carries the tail of the Fascicle 8 (officials and military) entry for Karasuyama domain (烏山藩, Shimotsuke). It records two lower-secretary offices — 少參事 with 3 members (a small, anomalous \"四\"/4 is also printed) and 権少參事 with 4 members — together with a roster of ten named officials (菅谷半藏, 吉田平藏, 平野有隣, 多賀有, 志村義敬, 清水周邦, 瀧田東作, 五味淵廉, 江口晉六, 堀江良藏). The domain's military follows: two platoons totalling 80 troops (兵員八拾人, with a detached-duty note 外役々) and six cannon (大砲六門) served by 42 gunners (砲手四拾貳人). At the far left the maru-marker ○刈谷藩 opens the next domain, Kariya (刈谷藩, Mikawa), whose own institutions continue on the following page; the running header has already advanced to （刈谷）."
  },
  {
   "id": "kariya_lower_p171_left",
   "sequence": 618,
   "domain_canonical": "刈谷藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "刈谷藩",
   "domain_en": "Kariya",
   "image": "images/lower_p171_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 171,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（勝山）",
   "page_header_en": "Register of Domain Administration (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 8 — (Katsuyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-8 officials roster and military strength (tail of Kariya; Katsuyama section marker)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page (printed p. 319) concludes the fascicle-8 (officials and military) entry for Kariya Domain (刈谷藩) and opens the section for Katsuyama Domain (勝山藩). Kariya's administration is recorded as a governor (知事, with no personnel count printed), one senior councillor (大参事 一員), three acting senior councillors (権大参事 三員), three junior councillors (少参事 三員), and three acting junior councillors (権少参事 三員); the ten named incumbents are listed in the lower register. Kariya's military is given as four platoons (兵隊 四小隊), with the note that one platoon comprises 48 men (但一小隊四十八員), i.e. 192 troops. The ○勝山藩 maru-marker at the page's left edge begins Katsuyama's entry, whose data carries onto the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "katsuyama_upper_p107_right",
   "sequence": 619,
   "domain_canonical": "勝山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "勝山藩",
   "domain_en": "Katsuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p107_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 107,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百八十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（勝山）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Katsuyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "End of Kariya's population and military tallies; opening of Katsuyama's kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 188 of fascicle 3, where two domain blocks meet. The nine columns to the right of the maru-marker close out 刈屋藩 (Kariya, Mikawa): 6 shugen households; 13 hinin households holding 49 people (24 male, 25 female); 18 eta households holding 88 people (47 male, 41 female); 232 shizoku households with 289 domain samurai and 612 family members (173 male, 439 female); 103 sotsu households with 129 sotsu and 184 family members (46 male, 138 female); 32 villages; and a bracketed military line giving four platoons at 48 men each plus 12 artillerymen. The marker ○勝山藩 then opens the Katsuyama block, which records 本高 22,777 koku and 新田高 683.172 koku for a 合高 of 23,460.172 koku, the two components summing exactly to the total. Katsuyama's block continues on the facing page 189 with the 引方 deduction and the tax figures."
  },
  {
   "id": "katsuyama_upper_p107_left",
   "sequence": 620,
   "domain_canonical": "勝山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "勝山藩",
   "domain_en": "Katsuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p107_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 107,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（勝山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Tables, Fascicle Three (Katsuyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tax totals and taxed products",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf completes the fiscal entry for Katsuyama Domain in fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran. It records a deduction of 2,402.77 koku against the gross assessment, leaving an actual yield (此實高) of 21,057.402 koku, and it gives five-year averages for the regular land tax (6,783.9209 koku of hulled rice) and for miscellaneous taxes (404.0647 koku plus 301 ryo 1 bu and 100 mon in cash). The braced grand total of 7,187.9856 koku reconciles exactly with the two rice figures, but the cash grand total prints as 301 ryo 3 bu against the 301 ryo 1 bu of the miscellaneous line, a two-bu inconsistency in the source itself. A closing survey of taxed products lists 500,000 kin of shredded tobacco (tax 62 kan 500 mon), 350 kanme of raw silk (13 kan 125 mon), and 10,000 straw bags of coal (13 kan 125 mon)."
  },
  {
   "id": "katsuyama_upper_p108_right",
   "sequence": 621,
   "domain_canonical": "勝山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "勝山藩",
   "domain_en": "Katsuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p108_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 108,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（勝山）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Katsuyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Katsuyama domain: products, households, population, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 190 continues the Katsuyama domain entry (Echizen; Ogasawara house, 22,777 koku assessed) that opens on page 188. The lower register closes the domain's product list — rapeseed at about 3,000 straw bales, lacquer at about 50 loads (the only taxed item, at 2 kan 500 mon), ramie cloth at about 20,000, kihada bark at about 5,000 kanme, cedar boards at about 20,000 ken, and charcoal at about 20,000 kanme — and the upper register records a grand total of 91 kan 250 mon in ei-currency. The civil counts give 3,381 households and a population of 17,169, split 8,550 male and 8,619 female, together with 5 Shinto-priest households holding 18 people, 141 people resident in temples, 32 temples, and 160 samurai households holding 765 people. The shrine count is entered as 記シテ無シ, \"not recorded,\" and every male-female split on the page sums exactly to its parent total."
  },
  {
   "id": "katsuyama_lower_p172_right",
   "sequence": 622,
   "domain_canonical": "勝山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "勝山藩",
   "domain_en": "Katsuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p172_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 172,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（勝山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Statistical Compendium, Fascicle 8 (Katsuyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment (Katsuyama, Awa)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page records the officials and military establishment of Katsuyama domain in Awa province (安房勝山藩), fascicle 8 of the Han Statistical Compendium. The council roster gives one senior councillor (大参事), four provisional senior councillors (権大参事), seven junior councillors (少参事, amended in vermilion to nine), and two provisional junior councillors (権少参事, amended to four); the governorship (知事) is held by Sakai Isao. The military entry lists one infantry company (a platoon numbering 60 men), two cannon, and one artillery squad whose personnel count is not recorded. Nine named officials are listed in the lower register, and the printed leaf number is 320."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanbe_upper_p108_left",
   "sequence": 623,
   "domain_canonical": "神戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "神戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanbe",
   "image": "images/upper_p108_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 108,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（神戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Kanbe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kanbe's assessed yield, following the tail of the previous domain's troop and sotsu-household returns",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf spans a domain boundary in fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran. Right of the ○神戸藩 marker the preceding domain closes its return: 91 sotsu households, a sotsu population printed as 519 persons split into 311 male and 308 female, 99 heishi and 72 heisotsu for a stated total of 171 troops formed into four platoons of 40 men each, and an express note that the number of villages was not recorded. The male and female figures sum to 619, exactly 100 above the printed total, so the total's 五百 stands where 六百 is required. Left of the marker the Kanbe entry opens with a main assessment of 15,000 koku plus two supplementary komidaka items: 1,563.937 koku of newly opened paddy, and 372.0355 koku of land transferred under earlier regulation together with reverted and newly opened land. The running header reads 藩制一覽表第三（神戸）and the printed page number is 191."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanbe_upper_p109_right",
   "sequence": 624,
   "domain_canonical": "神戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "神戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanbe",
   "image": "images/upper_p109_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 109,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百九十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（神戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Kanbe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kanbe domain kokudaka, five-year land-tax rice, cash miscellaneous tax, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the fiscal and demographic block for Kanbe domain (神戸藩) in Ise Province, continuing an entry that began on the preceding page. Its total assessed yield is 16,970.6555 koku, and the regular land tax struck as a five-year average yields 5,224.2296 koku of actual rice from Ise and 2,180.8284 koku from Kawachi, summing to the printed subtotal of 7,405.058 koku; a further 21.3352 koku of fixed rice from Ise brings the grand total to the printed 7,426.3932 koku, alongside 4 ryō and 915.8 mon of miscellaneous cash tax from the two provinces. A warichu note records that the Tiger and Dragon years within the five-year span were exceptionally bad harvests and were replaced by the earlier Dog and Boar years in the averaging. The domain counts 2,224 households and 9,683 people (4,803 male, 4,880 female), plus five Shinto priestly households holding 23 people (9 male, 14 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanbe_upper_p109_left",
   "sequence": 625,
   "domain_canonical": "神戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "神戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanbe",
   "image": "images/upper_p109_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 109,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百九十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（神戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 3 — (Kanbe). Provenance only; the fascicle number is a pointer to the source survey, not a data field.",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kanbe: samurai and outcaste households and population, shrines and temples, troops, temple land",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the Kanbe (神戸) entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 domain survey, continuing from the general totals given on the facing page. It records 155 samurai-and-soldier households and 755 persons (418 male, 337 female), broken down into 91 shizoku households / 427 persons, 44 sotsu households / 171 persons, 20 light-soldier households / 116 persons, and 41 shichō servants (all male, \"女無之\"). Two outcaste groups are entered separately with the prefix 外ニ — 41 hinin-ban and 27 hinin — and for both the survey records \"戸數無之\", no households. The leaf also gives 115 shrines and 89 temples with a temple population of 119 (75 monks, 5 men, 39 women), a troop strength of 75 men, and a temple landholding for Ryūkōji of 20.3+ koku assessed with 8.76 koku of regular tax rice."
  },
  {
   "id": "kanbe_lower_p172_left",
   "sequence": 626,
   "domain_canonical": "神戸藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "神戸藩",
   "domain_en": "Kanbe",
   "image": "images/lower_p172_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 172,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（神戸）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Survey (Hansei ichiran-hyō), Fascicle 8 (Kanbe)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials roster (fascicle 8: officials & military)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left page of pdf leaf 172 (lower volume, fascicle 8: officials & military) opens the entry for 神戸藩 (Kanbe, Ise province) and carries the tail of the preceding 勝山藩 (Katsuyama) entry. Kanbe's block records the report date (Meiji 2 / snake year, 11th month, 8th day = 1869-11-08), a vacant governorship (知事), and one senior councilor (大参事), 神谷直與. To the right of the ○神戸藩 marker stand nine officials of 勝山藩 — seven junior councilors (少参事: 關鎌鉢, 福非武太郎, 前田唯一, 蓁晉, 黑柳彌六, 小木柳也, 鈴木定七) and two acting junior councilors (權少参事: 木原佗作, 島田清右衞門) — a group the editors note was originally written in vermilion (以下九行原朱書). The printed book-page number is 321."
  },
  {
   "id": "yodo_upper_p113_left",
   "sequence": 627,
   "domain_canonical": "淀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "淀藩",
   "domain_en": "Yodo",
   "image": "images/upper_p113_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 113,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（淀）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Yodo)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yonezawa garrison troops; Yodo assessed yield and tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of leaf 113 (printed page 201) carries the tail of the Yonezawa (米澤藩) entry and the opening of the Yodo (淀藩) entry in Fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran. Everything to the right of the ○淀藩 marker belongs to Yonezawa: a Raigeki (Thunderstrike) Corps of two platoons at fifty men to the platoon, seven staff officers for the units listed above, and garrison-farmer soldiers stationed one platoon apiece in Oguni district and the villages of Ayukai, Arato, Nakayama and Nukanome, with the note that unit strengths are not uniform. To the left of the marker Yodo's fiscal block begins with a 草高 heading that carries no figure, an actual assessed yield (現石高) of 43,784.76092 koku, and, as a five-year average running from 1864 to 1868, a regular land tax of 39,589.31002 koku of rice together with 1,037 kan 520 mon 3 bu 6 rin 5 mō in cash. Miscellaneous taxes add 4,030.2912 koku of rice and 2 bu in gold, which the page itself converts to 0.0625 koku at the stated rate of eight ryō per koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "yodo_lower_p174_right",
   "sequence": 628,
   "domain_canonical": "淀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "淀藩",
   "domain_en": "Yodo",
   "image": "images/lower_p174_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 174,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（淀）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, fascicle 8 (Yodo)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials roster and military organization (fascicle 8): Yodo opening; Yonezawa military overflow",
   "page_summary_en": "This fascicle-8 page opens the entry for Yodo domain (淀藩, Inaba clan of Yamashiro) at the ○淀藩 marker. Yodo's officials are recorded as a vacant governorship (知事), one Senior Councillor (大參事 = 田邊又太郎), and three Provisional Senior Councillors (權大參事 = 川俣右門, 坂口省吾, 淺尾貞); the junior ranks continue on the following page. Everything to the right of the marker belongs to the preceding domain, Yonezawa (米澤藩): its French-organized army (佛式) comprising a 15-company main line (雲從隊, 60 infantry per company ≈ 900 men), 4.5 artillery sections (砲兵, ≈9 guns), and 8 reserve companies (豫備兵, personnel not recorded), plus two Provisional Junior Councillors (權少參事) and the councillors 森三郎, 堀尾重與, 片山仁一郎. The fold column carries the printed book-page number 324."
  },
  {
   "id": "yodo_lower_p174_left",
   "sequence": 629,
   "domain_canonical": "淀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "淀藩",
   "domain_en": "Yodo",
   "image": "images/lower_p174_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 174,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（淀）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Yodo)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Yodo domain officials roster (junior councillors and named office-holders)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf continues the fascicle-8 (職員 officials) listing for Yodo Domain (淀藩), a Yamashiro domain adjoining Kyoto. The upper register prints two office headings — 少參事 (junior councillor), staffed by three posts (三員), and 權少參事 (provisional junior councillor), whose post-count is not printed on this leaf — while the lower register lists thirteen named officials in single columns read right to left, from 廣瀬桐江 through 加瀬春人. The running header reads 藩制一覽表第八（淀）and the printed book-page number is 325 (三百二十五). No entry-marker (○…藩) appears, confirming a continuation page; MASTER's Yonezawa (米澤藩) rows for this spread — military companies and French drill doctrine — belong to the facing right-hand page, not this leaf, whose only MASTER-matching cell is 少参事 三員."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshida_upper_p114_right",
   "sequence": 630,
   "domain_canonical": "吉田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉田藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshida",
   "image": "images/upper_p114_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 114,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（吉田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Yoshida)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yoshida domain assessed yield, land tax and households",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 202 of the third fascicle of the Hansei ichiran opens the return for Yoshida domain (Iyo-Yoshida, a 30,000-koku house). Yoshida reports a gross assessed yield (草高) of 30,007.68854 koku, noted as including the komidaka, and a tax yield (此物成高) of 16,764.63206 koku made up of 14,108.5637 koku of rice and 2,656.06836 koku of soybeans, the two components summing exactly to the stated total. Its regular land tax, marked as a five-year average taken from a direct survey, runs to 13,667.71315 koku of rice and 2,501.35322 koku of soybeans; miscellaneous taxes come to 288 ryō 3 bu 2 shu in gold, and the domain counts 9,569 households. Three columns printed to the right of the ○吉田藩 marker close out the preceding domain, Yodo: 永 211 kan 994 mon 8 bu 5 rin 1 mō, 錢 712 kan 622 mon, and a troop line Yodo returned as 不分明, not ascertained."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshida_upper_p114_left",
   "sequence": 631,
   "domain_canonical": "吉田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉田藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshida",
   "image": "images/upper_p114_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 114,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（吉田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Survey Tables, Fascicle 3 (Yoshida)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Household, clerical and status-group population counts for Yoshida domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-3 (population and status) entry for Yoshida domain; no maru-marker appears anywhere on it and the running head prints 藩制一覧表第三（吉田）, so every column belongs to Yoshida. The upper register records institutional and household counts — 205 samurai (士族) households, 530 sub-samurai (卒族) households, 868 shrines, 72 temples, 50 shugendō households, 101 eta households and 4 hinin households — followed by a total population of 53,481 (27,658 male, 25,823 female). The 内 breakdown filling the rest of the page distributes that population by status: shizoku 1,171, sotsu 1,718, shrine servants 279, clergy 98 (95 monks and 3 nuns), shugendō practitioners 348, eta 649, hinin 23, farmers 47,916 living in 8,298 households, and merchants 1,711 in 440 households. Each of those nine figures splits into male and female counts that add up exactly, yet the nine together come to 53,913 — 432 more than the total the page itself prints. The page closes with the military line: six platoons of roughly fifty men each, which the domain notes rises and falls from time to time."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoshida_lower_p175_right",
   "sequence": 632,
   "domain_canonical": "吉田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吉田藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoshida",
   "image": "images/lower_p175_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 175,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（吉田）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Fascicle 8 (Yoshida)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (Yoshida) with the preceding domain's (Yodo) military note",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of fascicle 8 records the administrative officials of Yoshida (Iyo) Domain. Under the governor line (知事, no number printed), it lists 2 senior councillors (大參事), 3 acting senior councillors (權大參事 — with a small editorial \"四\"=4 inserted, though the true figure is 3), and 4 junior councillors (少參事): nine named officials in all, whose names print in the lower register (荻野矢治馬, 飯淵眞徹, 郷六豐香, 大森貞彦, 今村和多留, 横田與一郎, 荻野彦六郎, 五島愼一郎, 家藤三平), and 2+3+4=9 confirms the 3-person reading. At the top right, overflowing from the previous domain (Yodo), a military note (兵記 記セス) states that no troop numbers were recorded and only unit-commander titles survive. The printed page number is 326."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoita_upper_p115_right",
   "sequence": 633,
   "domain_canonical": "與板藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "與板藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoita",
   "image": "images/upper_p115_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 115,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（與板）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Table Three (Yoita)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Yoita domain land assessment, five-year average tax revenue, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 204 of the Hansei Ichiran, fascicle three, carrying the land-and-revenue return for Yoita domain in Echigo. The assessed base yield (kusadaka) is 20,000 koku; adding 587.1076 koku of new-field land and 1,087.46219 koku of folded-in tax increment gives the stated combined total of 21,674.56979 koku, and the three components sum to that figure exactly. Tax is reported as a one-year figure averaged over the five years from Genji 1 (1864) to Meiji 1 (1868): regular land tax of 6,802.02956 koku in current rice plus miscellaneous taxes of 391.76526 koku, together 7,193.79482 koku — again an exact sum. The domain returns 4,693 households, 12 shrine-priest households, 44 temples, and 132.6423 koku of shrine-and-temple land. To the right of the Yoita marker, two military columns overflow from the preceding domain, Yoshida: about 150 soldiers, some ten of whom receive no stipend, and about 238 foot soldiers."
  },
  {
   "id": "yoita_lower_p175_left",
   "sequence": 634,
   "domain_canonical": "與板藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "與板藩",
   "domain_en": "Yoita",
   "image": "images/lower_p175_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 175,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（與板）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran, Fascicle 8 (Yoita)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle 8 domain officials & military: Yoshida roster tail and Yoita entry opening",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page from Fascicle 8 (officials and military) of the Hansei Ichiran is headed for Yoita Domain (與板藩), but most of the printed matter is the tail of the preceding domain, Yoshida (吉田藩), whose entry overflows to the right of the ○與板藩 marker. Yoshida's portion records acting junior councillors (権少参事: 7 members), a military strength of 6 battalions (with a note that one platoon = 50 men), and nine named officials. Yoita's own entry begins at the marker with a senior-councillor count of 2 (大参事 二, filled by Matsushita Sada and Nagai Gentarō) and a governor (知事) line left without a name. The printed book-page number is 327."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatsuki_upper_p128_left",
   "sequence": 635,
   "domain_canonical": "高槻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高槻藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatsuki",
   "image": "images/upper_p128_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 128,
