   "book_page": "二百三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高槻）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 3 (Takatsuki)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Close of Takanabe's population and military entry; opening of Takatsuki's yield and land-tax entry",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of the sheet finishes the entry for Takanabe Domain: 32,510 commoners (16,734 male, 15,776 female), 244 persons in the eta/hinin registers (133 male, 111 female), and a military section listing one steamship, the Senshu-maru (14 ken long, 2.5 ken in beam, fourteen aboard), five rifle platoons of 64 men each drawn from shizoku and sotsu with eight officers, and one artillery company with six guns, thirteen support staff and fifty-four gunners. The maru-marker ○高槻藩 then opens the entry for Takatsuki Domain, whose first columns give a nominal yield (kusadaka) of 36,000 koku plus additional yield of 2,575.6299 koku (including zodaka and komidaka) and 185.252 koku from newly reclaimed fields, summing exactly to the recorded combined yield of 38,760.8819 koku. Takatsuki's regular land tax, averaged over five years, is 18,714.2652 koku of hulled rice at a rate of 5.106 tenths, of which the tenth share reserved to the lord is 1,871.4265 koku; miscellaneous taxes add 1,347.707 koku of rice. The running header and printed page number identify the sheet as Fascicle 3, page 231."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatsuki_upper_p129_right",
   "sequence": 636,
   "domain_canonical": "高槻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高槻",
   "domain_en": "Takatsuki",
   "image": "images/upper_p129_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 129,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高槻）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Takatsuki)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takatsuki: minor dues, households, population, status counts and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf inside the Takatsuki (高槻藩) entry of fascicle 3, printed book page 232, carrying no domain marker of its own. It closes the domain's minor-dues list — cash of 3,729 kan 688 mon under the head \"assorted minor dues\" (品々小物成), 272 bundles of small bamboo, and 30 oak logs — and then gives the household and population returns: 4,622 households and 21,558 people (10,730 male, 10,828 female), with a separate town-quarter count of 463 houses and 1,659 people (764 male, 895 female). Status and force figures follow: 395 samurai households and 192 sotsu households; a garrison of 180 men in three platoons (two platoons of 120 samurai, one platoon of 60 sotsu); and 2,328 samurai and sotsu persons, of whom 1,445 are samurai (715 male, 730 female) and 883 sotsu (437 male, 446 female). The leaf ends with 69 shrines, 168 Buddhist halls, 678 eta and hinin, and 79 villages. Every component group on the page sums exactly to its stated total."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatsuki_lower_p180_right",
   "sequence": 637,
   "domain_canonical": "高槻藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高槻藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatsuki",
   "image": "images/lower_p180_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 180,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（高槻）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Takatsuki)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Takatsuki domain officials roster and troop count (caretaker-officials name report)",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 (officials and military) entry for Takatsuki domain (高槻藩). It records the domain's senior administrators — 3 gon-daisanji (權大參事) and 4 shō-sanji (少參事) — together with a standing force of 264 rank-and-file soldiers (兵卒 二百六十四人). A parenthetical note frames the section as the caretaker-officials' name report (留守官姓名届書); the caretakers named at left are daisanji Mishima Shikito and gon-daisanji Kataoka, Takashina Mintarō and Toyoda Josetsu, while the foot of the page lists the full gon-daisanji and shō-sanji rosters (Kataoka, Sunaga, Fukuyama; Namiki, Komano, Seki, Takamatsu). The printed book-page number is 336."
  },
  {
   "id": "tatsuno_upper_p129_left",
   "sequence": 638,
   "domain_canonical": "龍野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龍野藩",
   "domain_en": "Tatsuno",
   "image": "images/upper_p129_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 129,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（龍野）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Tatsuno)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tatsuno domain assessed land, tax, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle-3 entry for Tatsuno domain (龍野藩) in Harima, printed book page 233. Its assessed land is broken into four components — 48,962.023 koku in Harima, 869.123 koku of new fields, 2,127.26 koku in Mimasaka province, and 333.116 koku of komidaka — which sum exactly to the combined total of 52,291.522 koku. Regular land tax stands at 25,449.697 koku, of which 735.072 koku was rendered in soybeans and 299.525 koku in cash, alongside 2,296.447 koku of miscellaneous rice tax and 107 ryō 2 bu in gold. The domain returns 10,833 households and 47,248 people (24,151 male, 23,097 female), with 366 shrines and 84 temple halls. A bracketed supplement at the right edge of the leaf, belonging to the preceding domain (Takatsuki), records a further 56 households and 234 people (108 male, 126 female) of onbō, an outcaste occupational group."
  },
  {
   "id": "tatsuno_lower_p180_left",
   "sequence": 639,
   "domain_canonical": "龍野藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龍野藩",
   "domain_en": "Tatsuno",
   "image": "images/lower_p180_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 180,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（龍野）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Tatsuno)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials (councillor establishment) and samurai troop count",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the fascicle-8 (officials and military) entry for Tatsuno domain (龍野藩), printed page 337. Tatsuno's councillor establishment is given as counts only: 2 senior councillors (大参事, one post vacant), 4 provisional senior councillors (權大参事, one post vacant), 2 junior councillors (少参事), and 5 provisional junior councillors (權少参事), together with a samurai militia (士族兵隊) of 270 men. A double-column warichu note records that the names of the regular and provisional junior councillors were still vacant and under investigation, an inquiry having been submitted, to be reported in the third month (Meiji 3, 1870). The lower and right band of the page carries the overflow of the preceding Takatsuki domain's roster (高槻藩, page 336): nine of its junior/provisional-junior councillors by name — 館野忠左衛門, 並木晴宇, 駒野知彦, 和氣雄平, 關機一郎, 進藤直衛, 加藤琢磨, 水谷歳助, 加集寛."
  },
  {
   "id": "tanabe_upper_p130_right",
   "sequence": 640,
   "domain_canonical": "田邊藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田邊藩",
   "domain_en": "Tanabe",
   "image": "images/upper_p130_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 130,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（田邊）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Tanabe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tatsuno status counts; Tanabe land assessment and taxes",
   "page_summary_en": "The right half of the leaf closes out Tatsuno domain's status returns: 2,796 shizoku in 494 households (1,293 male, 1,503 female), 540 sotsu in 212 households (342 male, 198 female), the labels eta and hinin printed with no figure beside them, and a bracketed military entry of 278 shizoku troops, 219 sotsu troops and 172 peasant troops. The maru-marker ○田邊藩 then opens Tanabe domain, and the columns left of it give Tanabe's land and revenue. Tanabe's registered assessment is 37,065.996 koku, to which a marginal note adds 2,300.44584 koku of new fields, producing the combined assessment of 39,366.44184 koku printed in the next column. Tanabe's land tax is 15,310.3278 koku of rice, its miscellaneous tax 15.8424 koku, its product tax 5,535 ryō 2 shu, and its silver levy 333 kan 260 monme 9 rin."
  },
  {
   "id": "tanabe_upper_p130_left",
   "sequence": 641,
   "domain_canonical": "田邊藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田邊藩",
   "domain_en": "Tanabe",
   "image": "images/upper_p130_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 130,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三　（田邊）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 3 (Tanabe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf gives the household and population returns of Tanabe domain from fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. The domain reports 12,541 households and 55,076 people, of whom 28,126 are recorded as male and 26,950 as female. Households divide into 811 retainer and foot-soldier houses (372 samurai, 346 foot-soldier, 93 servant), 14 shrine-priest houses, 112 temples, 11,011 farmer, artisan and merchant houses, and 593 outcaste houses; the corresponding person counts are 3,013, 58, 302, 48,830 and 2,873, each broken into male and female. The domain also returns 188 shrines. Every subtotal reconciles to its printed total, though the summary male/female split differs from the sum of the component splits by 17 persons in each direction."
  },
  {
   "id": "tanabe_lower_p181_right",
   "sequence": 642,
   "domain_canonical": "田邊藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田邊藩",
   "domain_en": "Tanabe",
   "image": "images/lower_p181_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 181,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（田邊）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 8 (Tanabe)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military returns (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page from Fascicle 8 of the Hansei Ichiran records the administrative officials of Tanabe Domain (田邊藩, most likely Tango/Maizuru Tanabe) together with the tail end of neighbouring Tatsuno Domain's (龍野藩) military returns. Tatsuno's figures — 219 sotsu-class troops (卒族兵隊) and 172 peasant soldiers (農兵) — overflow to the right of Tanabe's domain marker, following the fascicle-8 convention of printing military counts after a domain's officials. Tanabe itself is credited with 1 senior councillor (大参事), 3 acting senior councillors (権大参事), and 4 junior councillors (少参事); an acting-junior-councillor heading (権少参事) is printed with no count. Ten named officials are listed in the lower band, aligning one, three, four, and two men respectively beneath the four councillor ranks; the entry for Yokoyama Kinjūrō (横山謹十郎) carries the editorial warichu note （一ニナシ）, 'absent in manuscript one'."
  },
  {
   "id": "takashima_upper_p131_right",
   "sequence": 643,
   "domain_canonical": "高島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高島藩",
   "domain_en": "Takashima",
   "image": "images/upper_p131_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 131,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高島）",
   "page_header_en": "Overview Tables of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Takashima)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takashima domain kokudaka, land tax and products",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the tail of Tanabe domain's return and the opening of Takashima domain's return in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran. Tanabe closes with a population of 55,076 (28,126 male and 26,950 female, which sum exactly to the printed total) and a parenthetical military note recording five platoons totalling 250 men plus a further 150 men then in training. Takashima's entry opens after the maru-marker with a base assessment of 30,087.59 koku, newly reclaimed fields of 15,834.6701 koku, and a combined yield of 45,922.261 koku. Under a five-year-average heading it reports a regular land tax of 15,082.38022 koku of rice and miscellaneous taxes of 1,377.20938 koku of rice plus 169.74072 koku of soybeans, and its product list begins with raw silk and lake fish, both entered without quantities."
  },
  {
   "id": "takashima_upper_p131_left",
   "sequence": 644,
   "domain_canonical": "高島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高島",
   "domain_en": "Takashima",
   "image": "images/upper_p131_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 131,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Table 3 (Takashima)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takashima population, households, status counts, religious institutions and military strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the whole of Takashima Domain's fascicle-3 return: 2,157 ryō in miscellaneous taxes, 84 villages, 12,405 households and 59,926 people (printed as 31,612 male and 28,888 female, a split that exceeds the stated total by 574). Status counts follow — 336 shizoku households with 1,933 people, 876 sotsu households (counted through the koshamono servants) with 3,070 people, and 36 eta-hinin households with 212 people — each with a male/female breakdown that sums correctly to its own total. The domain reports 158 shrines and 71 temples. The military lines, which the 1928 editors mark as written in vermilion in the original, give 222 heishi and 240 heisotsu for a combined 462, of whom 220 were on active duty, organised in 8 rifle platoons with 4 cannon, followed by a caveat that the establishment was not fixed and would rise or fall with circumstances."
  },
  {
   "id": "takashima_lower_p181_left",
   "sequence": 645,
   "domain_canonical": "高島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高島藩",
   "domain_en": "Takashima",
   "image": "images/lower_p181_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 181,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（高島）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table 8 (Takashima)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Takashima domain councillor roster (with Tanabe military/official tail)",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of Hansei Ichiran fascicle 8 (printed page 339) is mainly the officials roster of Takashima (Suwa) Domain, opened by its ○高島藩 section marker and an editorial note 實名不分 (\"real personal names not distinguished\"). It lists nine domain councillors — Senior Councillors (大參事) Chino (Magokurō) and Ushiyama (Sukenojō); acting Senior Councillors (權大參事) Yajima (Denzaemon) and Maeda; and Junior Councillors (少參事) Matsui (Kozaemon), Suganuma (Onemon), Chino Masayoshi (Shinzaemon), Chino Fusataka, and Suwa — most identified only by their common names in parentheses. To the right of the marker, the tail of the preceding Tanabe Domain entry prints its military strength (five platoons, 205 men, with a further 150 currently in training) and a single named official, Watanabe Tesshin, whose formal name is recorded as \"none.\" The provenance header 藩制一覧表第八（高島） and the page number run down the left margin."
  },
  {
   "id": "takashima_lower_p182_right",
   "sequence": 646,
   "domain_canonical": "高島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高島藩",
   "domain_en": "Takashima",
   "image": "images/lower_p182_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 182,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（高島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 8 (Takashima)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Takashima domain military strength and its revised second-month officer roster",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-leaf (printed page 340) continues the fascicle-8 entry for Takashima domain (Suwa, Shinano), whose maru-marker ○高島藩 stands on the preceding half-leaf at page 339; no marker appears here, so the whole page is Takashima. The military return gives 222 heishi and 240 heisotsu for a stated total of 462 men — the components reconcile exactly — organised as a rifle corps of eight platoons inclusive of its corps officers, with four cannon. Below the military figures the page prints a second, parenthetically dated roster, （午二月届）, listing eight named officers: one daisanji (Chino Magokurō), two gon-daisanji (Ushiyama Sukenojō, Yajima Denzaemon), two shōsanji (Matsui Kozaemon, Suganuma On'emon), and three gon-shōsanji (Chino Shinzaemon, Yamanaka Chūji, Kanai Jun'pachi). A small vermilion editorial note at the head of the page instructs that the second-month report is the one to be followed, resolving it against the conflicting Takashima roster printed on page 339, where Ushiyama and Chino Shinzaemon hold higher ranks and three other men appear."
  },
  {
   "id": "takato_upper_p132_right",
   "sequence": 647,
   "domain_canonical": "高遠藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高遠藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatō",
   "image": "images/upper_p132_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 132,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高遠）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey, Fascicle 3 (Takatō)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takatō assessed yield and land-tax return",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Takatō domain entry in Fascicle 3 of the 1870 Han System Survey (printed page 238). Takatō's assessed gross yield (kusadaka) is 34,999.4491 koku, of which two increments are itemised: a folded-in increment (komidaka) of 89.13 koku and a re-surveyed new-field yield (shinden kaide-daka) of 1,820.3191 koku; the two together leave a remainder of exactly 33,090 koku against the domain's nominal 33,000-koku assessment. The five-year average return is given as 15,224.2295 koku of rice plus 7.4675 kan in cash, and the regular land tax (seiso) repeats those same two figures; miscellaneous taxes (zatsuzei) add 63.04 koku of rice. The two columns at the right edge — 93 persons exempt from service, and the note that the aged and young, officials, troops and all others are assigned to reserve and temporary auxiliary duty — stand to the right of the ○高遠藩 marker and close out the preceding Takashima domain entry."
  },
  {
   "id": "takato_upper_p132_left",
   "sequence": 648,
   "domain_canonical": "高遠藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高遠藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatō",
   "image": "images/upper_p132_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 132,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百三十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高遠）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 3 (Takatō)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takatō domain: miscellaneous and product taxes, population by status, shrines and temples, troops",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso, printed page 239, continues the Takatō 高遠 entry in fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō. No maru-marker stands on the leaf; the marker ○高遠藩 prints on the facing recto, so all thirty-three elements here belong to Takatō. The two rightmost columns finish the miscellaneous-tax (雜税) entry begun opposite, at 738 ryō 1 bu in gold and 1,093 kan 537 mon in copper cash, and are followed by taxes on products at 875 ryō 2 bu in gold and 6.011 monme in silver. The population block gives five status groups, each with households, a total and a male/female split: commoners 8,892 households and 45,096 people (23,889 male, 21,207 female), shizoku 259 households and 1,250 people, sotsu 245 households and 1,249 people, eta 23 households and 244 people, and hinin 13 households and 44 people, every split summing exactly to its printed total. The leaf closes with 550 shrines, 96 temples, and a military line the editor marks as red-inked in the original: 778 troops in eight platoons, with a warichu breakdown that does not add up to 778 and an editorial note, ○一本如此, recording that another copy reads differently."
  },
  {
   "id": "takato_lower_p182_left",
   "sequence": 649,
   "domain_canonical": "高遠藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高遠藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatō",
   "image": "images/lower_p182_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 182,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百四十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（高遠）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Takatō)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Takatō domain officials roster and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 341 of fascicle 8 carries the whole of the Takatō (Shinano) entry; the ○高遠藩 marker is the rightmost element on the leaf and nothing prints to its right, so no preceding domain's material appears here. The roster gives twelve men: two daisanji (Asai Sumi, Okano Koheiji), two gon-daisanji (Kōno Etsu, Naitō Shin), seven shōsanji (Okamura Gon and Naitō Yo with the office printed inline, then Misawa I, Kanba Sō, Kawachi Tetsugorō, Ono Shigeki and Okamura Magozō under a 少參事 heading), and one gon-shōsanji (Kōno Taiji). The military establishment is eight platoons at forty men per platoon, i.e. 320 troops, with an interlinear note splitting the eight into four platoons of soldiers plus four platoons of soldiers. A five-line editorial note above the officials records that the Rusukan (Regency Office) return entered Kōno as daisanji and judges this an error, since a small domain may not appoint three daisanji; two further warichu flag Okamura and Naitō as gon-daisanji in a variant text."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuruta_upper_p133_right",
   "sequence": 650,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鶴田藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuruta",
   "image": "images/upper_p133_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 133,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（鶴田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Tsuruta)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tsuruta domain land assessment, tax receipts, households, population, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the whole fascicle-3 entry for Tsuruta domain and no other domain. The land figures are a gross assessment (草高) of 36,189.707 koku and a further 24,810.923 koku delivered from the domain storehouse, against a combined total printed as a round 61,000 koku; a small editorial parenthesis notes that one manuscript copy of the survey lacks both the storehouse figure and the combined total. Tax receipts are 10,777.38216 koku of regular land tax, 1,191.1134 koku of rice in miscellaneous levies, and 79.10514 kan in cash. The domain returns 6,021 households and 28,201 people (14,927 male, 13,274 female, which sums exactly to the printed total), plus 546 samurai houses with 2,569 persons and 375 sotsu houses with 1,401 persons; households and population for eta and hinin are expressly not recorded. The entry closes with 46 shrines and 25 temples."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuruta_lower_p183_right",
   "sequence": 651,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "鶴田藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsuruta",
   "image": "images/lower_p183_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 183,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（鶴田）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 8 (Tsuruta)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials: councillor establishment (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 342 of the Hansei Ichiran officials-and-military register (fascicle 8) opens the entry for Tsuruta domain. Its upper register carries the ○鶴田藩 boundary marker and the first three councillor grades — 大參事 2 men, 權大參事 2 men, 少參事 3 men — with the establishment continuing onto the facing page 343, which prints 權少參事 4 men and Tsuruta's troop figures (兵隊 375, 士族 185, plus 82 instructors and above). The entire lower register of the page, nine name columns running from 逸見牧太 on the right to 星野蔀 on the left, still belongs to Takatō domain: it continues the 權少參事 roster whose heading and first appointee, 河野泰司, close page 341. Because the page reads right to left, only the ○鶴田藩 marker and the three columns to its left are Tsuruta's; the nine names to the marker's right are Takatō's overflow, and they are absent from the project's existing MASTER extraction."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatori_upper_p133_left",
   "sequence": 652,
   "domain_canonical": "高取藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高取藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatori",
   "image": "images/upper_p133_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 133,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三　（高取）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Takatori)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takatori kokudaka and rice-tax breakdown, with the tail of the Tsuruta entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Takatori domain (高取藩) entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran and, in its five right-hand columns, closes the entry for Tsuruta domain (鶴田藩) that began on the facing page. The Tsuruta tail records 5 districts and 113 villages, and a bracketed military note of 8 infantry platoons at 56 men each (448 men), 15 artillerymen in one section, and 82 men of instructor rank or above. Takatori's own block gives a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 25,228.90296 koku and a rice take (此取米) of 8,384.802 koku, itemised as 3,704.479 koku commuted to cash at one third and 4,680.323 koku delivered as grain — the two components sum exactly to the stated total. Two supplementary entries follow under 外: 9.625 koku assessed on newly opened paddy and dry fields and drained pond beds, and 40.69 koku held free of service obligation."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatori_upper_p134_right",
   "sequence": 653,
   "domain_canonical": "高取藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高取藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatori",
   "image": "images/upper_p134_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 134,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高取）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration (Hansei ichiran-hyō), Fascicle 3 — (Takatori)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takatori: sundry tax rice, households and population by status, shrines and temples, villages, troops",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf of the Takatori domain entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran-hyō; there is no maru-marker on the page, so all of it belongs to Takatori. The right-hand columns close out the tax account: mountain tribute rice 338.56 koku, bamboo-grove tribute rice 43.27 koku, the kuchimai surcharge 251.544 koku (levied, a marginal note says, at 3 shō per koku), a total rice figure of 9,068.491 koku, and within that 683.689 koku of sundry taxes. The left-hand columns give the population by status: 4,111 commoner households and 18,420 commoners (9,064 male, 9,356 female), 142 shizoku households and 576 persons, 311 sotsu households and 1,355 persons, 247 eta households and 1,645 persons, and 9 onbō households and 51 persons — 4,820 households and 22,047 people in all. The leaf closes with 117 shrines, 150 temples, 80 villages in 5 districts, and a force of four platoons totalling 152 men (28 officers, 4 gunners, 120 rank and file)."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatori_lower_p183_left",
   "sequence": 654,
   "domain_canonical": "高取藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高取藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatori",
   "image": "images/lower_p183_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 183,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百四十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（高取）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table Eight (Takatori)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso (printed page 343) of fascicle 8 closes the entry for Tsuruta Domain and opens Takatori Domain. Tsuruta's surviving official line here is 權少參事, with four holders; its forces are recorded by status as 375 shizoku and 185 sotsu (560 in all, no total printed), organised as eight infantry platoons of 56 men each plus one artillery section of 15, with a further 82 persons of instructor grade and above counted separately. The ○高取藩 marker then opens Takatori, which names five councillors in the two-register office/name layout: 大參事 Murata Jōshirō and Seo Tadashirō, 少參事 Yokokōji Yamon and Hamada Nakaba, and 權少參事 Tarao Tsuka. Takatori's force is given as four platoons comprising 28 officers, 120 troops and 4 drummers, 152 men in all."
  },
  {
   "id": "tanagura_upper_p134_left",
   "sequence": 655,
   "domain_canonical": "棚倉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "棚倉藩",
   "domain_en": "Tanagura",
   "image": "images/upper_p134_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 134,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（棚倉）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Tanagura)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tanagura Domain land assessment and tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 243 of fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. The rightmost column closes the preceding entry for Takatori Domain with its artillery — two cannon, fourteen men counted including officers and standard-bearers — after which the maru-marker ○棚倉藩 opens the fiscal block for Tanagura Domain in Mutsu. Tanagura's assessed yield (草高) is 60,000 koku; its regular land tax (正租) is 7,421.23779 koku of rice together with 1,958.18179 kan in ei cash, and its miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) are 1,166.9638 koku of rice with a further 343.26561 kan. The entry also records 27 ryō 3 bu in gold, 2.575 monme of silver, 1,123.844 kan of copper cash, 510 koku of shrine and temple lands, and, under the heading 外, two supplementary rice receipts: 542.7322 koku of measurement-surplus rice and 516.315 koku of bale-packing rice."
  },
  {
   "id": "tanagura_upper_p135_right",
   "sequence": 656,
   "domain_canonical": "棚倉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "棚倉藩",
   "domain_en": "Tanagura",
   "image": "images/upper_p135_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 135,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高梁）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Takahashi)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tanagura households, status population and troops; opening of Takahashi's assessed yield",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the tail of Tanagura Domain's fascicle-3 return and the first three lines of Takahashi Domain's. For Tanagura it records a myoga rice levy of 191.9462 koku, 19 kazoku (7 male, 12 female), 5,243 households of which 361 shrines and 186 temples, and a population of 26,756 (13,771 male, 12,931 female) — a total the source itself flags with the note 此數不合, \"these figures do not agree,\" since the male and female counts sum to 26,702. Below that come 689 shizoku households with 3,145 people, 233 sotsu households with 686 people, 17 eta households with 107 people and 6 hinin households with 29 people, and a military establishment of one battalion of 373 men plus one artillery company of 73, with a further 502 men on assorted duties. The maru-marker ○高梁藩 then opens Takahashi Domain with a kusadaka of 20,000 koku, against which two waste-land deductions are entered: 854.6257 koku of permanent waste on paddy and dry fields including newly opened land, and 871.2269 koku of waste carried over year to year."
  },
  {
   "id": "tanagura_lower_p184_right",
   "sequence": 657,
   "domain_canonical": "棚倉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "棚倉藩",
   "domain_en": "Tanagura",
   "image": "images/lower_p184_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 184,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（棚倉、高梁）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Tanagura, Takahashi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-8 (officials and military) opening for Tanagura Domain, whose entry begins at the ○棚倉藩 marker in the middle of the page. Tanagura reports twelve senior officials — 2 daisanji, 3 gon-daisanji, 3 shōsanji, 3 gon-shōsanji, and 1 kōginin (the last filled by the regular and acting senior councillors, per a small-type note) — together with a single battalion of 500 men. To the right of the marker stands the tail of the preceding domain's return, Takatori Domain's artillery: 2 cannon and a combined officer-and-gun-crew strength of 14 men. Takahashi Domain's entry opens at the left with 1 daisanji and 2 gon-daisanji, whose names print at the foot of the page as Ōishi Joun, Inoue Masahiko, and Saigō Sōichi."
  },
  {
   "id": "tadotsu_upper_p136_left",
   "sequence": 658,
   "domain_canonical": "多度津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多度津藩",
   "domain_en": "Tadotsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p136_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 136,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（多度津）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Tadotsu)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tadotsu land assessment, deductions and tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the 多度津藩 (Tadotsu, Sanuki province) entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran and gives the domain's assessed yield and its tax take. Tadotsu's nominal assessment (草高) is 10,000 koku; a further 4,018.676 koku of extended assessment, newly reclaimed fields and re-survey additions brings the combined assessment (合高) to 14,018.676 koku, against which 1,167.3846 koku is written off as permanent and fixed-term remissions, leaving a printed balance of 13,851.2914 koku. Land tax (正租), averaged over five years, is 6,898.4116 koku of rice, stated on the page both as 17,246 four-to bales plus a small remainder and as its koku equivalent; miscellaneous taxes come to 1,589 ryō 1 bu in cash. The two columns at the upper right belong to the preceding domain, 高梁藩, closing its entry with 2 cannon (16 gunners and attached officials) and 23 officials."
  },
  {
   "id": "tadotsu_upper_p137_right",
   "sequence": 659,
   "domain_canonical": "多度津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多度津藩",
   "domain_en": "Tadotsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p137_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 137,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（多度津）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 3 (Tadotsu)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Households, population, religious institutions, status-group counts, and military strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 248 of the Hansei Ichiran, fascicle 3, continuing the return for Tadotsu domain in Sanuki. It records 4,912 households and 21,687 residents, 357 shrines, 28 temples and 65 hermitages, together with the copper-cash tail of a monetary entry carried over from the preceding page (18 kan 849 mon). Status groups follow: 379 shizoku (174 male, 205 female), 884 sotsu (491 male, 393 female), 49 eta households holding 121 people, 6 shake households holding 40 people, 12 yamabushi households holding 30 people, and 5 hinin hearths holding 59 people. The leaf closes with the domain's military strength — 65 men in the shizoku corps and 240 in the corps drawn from sotsu and below, a stated total of 305, of whom 55 are officers."
  },
  {
   "id": "tadotsu_lower_p184_left",
   "sequence": 660,
   "domain_canonical": "多度津藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多度津藩",
   "domain_en": "Tadotsu",
   "image": "images/lower_p184_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 184,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百四十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（多度津）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Tadotsu)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf of fascicle 8 closes the entry for Takahashi Domain and opens that for Tadotsu Domain. Takahashi reports one Junior Councillor (Itakura Jun'ichirō) and one Acting Junior Councillor (Tanamura Saheiji), plus an infantry force of two platoons at sixty-five men each, 130 men in all. Tadotsu returns no headcounts for its posts at all, noting only \"Senior Councillor and below: not broken out,\" and reports its troops as 65 shizoku and 240 sotsu and below-rank, 305 men in total. Its seven named officers follow in the lower register: two Senior Councillors (Hayashi Ju, Hata Heigaku), two Acting Senior Councillors (Okada Shinji, Kawaguchi Jun) and three Acting Junior Councillors (Ishikawa Junzō, Ōoka Kōhei, Matsumoto Yūhei)."
  },
  {
   "id": "takasu_upper_p137_left",
   "sequence": 661,
   "domain_canonical": "高須藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高須藩",
   "domain_en": "Takasu",
   "image": "images/upper_p137_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 137,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高須）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Three (Takasu)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takasu domain kokudaka and five-year-average tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle-three record for Takasu domain (高須藩, Mino province), assessed at a nominal 30,000 koku. Newly surveyed paddy (改出新田高) adds 154.503 koku, giving a total holding (總高) of 30,154.503 koku. Under the heading \"five-year average\" the page reports land tax (正租) of 5,797.352 koku of hulled rice plus a 405.744-koku handling surcharge (口米), and miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) of 275.593 koku plus a 19.292-koku surcharge; the four figures sum exactly to the printed total receipts (合現米) of 6,497.981 koku. Tax-exempt religious land is listed separately at 59 koku of vermilion-seal land and 52 koku of other exempt land, and a parenthetical peerage count of five persons at the right edge closes the preceding Tadotsu domain entry."
  },
  {
   "id": "takasu_upper_p138_right",
   "sequence": 662,
   "domain_canonical": "高須藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高須藩",
   "domain_en": "Takasu",
   "image": "images/upper_p138_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 138,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高須）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Takasu)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takasu population, clergy, status groups, villages, cash tax and troops",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Takasu domain return in the third fascicle of the Hansei ichiran and carries no domain marker, so every column belongs to Takasu. It records 4,480 commoner households holding 23,353 people (11,829 male, 11,524 female), 32 shrine-attendant households, 71 temples with 217 residents, and 770 shrines whose 26 priestly households hold 159 people. The domain's own status groups follow: 1,231 shizoku in 282 households and 1,221 sotsu in 290 households, alongside 13 eta households (104 people) and 14 hinin households (105 people). The administrative and fiscal columns close the page with 3 districts and 69 villages, a cash tax of 253 ryo 3 bu 1 shu plus 35 mon 6 bun in ei levied on river fish, raw silk and silk floss, and a force of 148 troops including duty officers together with 62 sotsu troops."
  },
  {
   "id": "takasu_lower_p185_right",
   "sequence": 663,
   "domain_canonical": "高須藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高須藩",
   "domain_en": "Takasu",
   "image": "images/lower_p185_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 185,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（高須）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabular Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Takasu)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Takasu domain officials: councillor post counts and named incumbents",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the fascicle-8 (officials) entry for Takasu Domain in Mino province, marked by the ○高須藩 maru-marker at the head of the block. The upper register records four councillor grades with their establishment strengths - 大參事 one man, 權大參事 four, 少參事 three, 權少參事 three - for eleven posts in all. The lower register then prints those eleven incumbents by name, right to left: Gomi Orie as dai-sanji; Iio Sukeemon, Arakawa Kanzō, Ōtsuka Gihei and Oyamada Teizō as gon-dai-sanji; Aoyama Teiki, Hasegawa Matabei and Harada Kyūma as shō-sanji; and Yagi Tōzō, Morii Naoe and Tanaka Shūzō as gon-shō-sanji. At the right edge, before the marker, a single trailing column gives the kōyōnin (liaison officer) Akao Ki of the preceding domain, Tadotsu; the printed book-page number is 346."
  },
  {
   "id": "tahara_upper_p138_left",
   "sequence": 664,
   "domain_canonical": "田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tahara",
   "image": "images/upper_p138_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 138,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（田原）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Tahara)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tahara domain: land yield, tax receipts, households, population, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the whole of the Tahara (田原) entry from fascicle 3 of the Hansei Ichiran, and no other domain appears on it. Tahara's assessed yield (草高) is 12,072.43 koku, with a further 2,878.251 koku entered as re-surveyed increase (改出高) and 5,228.264 koku as newly opened field (新田高). Regular land tax came to 5,605.48263 koku of hulled rice, miscellaneous imposts to 1,042.77296 kan in ei-cash, and produce and sundry taxes to 1,178 ryō 2 bu 2 shu plus 1 kan 142 mon in copper. The domain counted 4,317 commoner households and 185 households in the domain establishment, a commoner population of 21,752 (10,838 men, 10,914 women) against 894 in the establishment (598 shizoku and 296 sotsu), plus 20 eta households of 80 people, and it held 248 shrines and 69 Buddhist temples housing 176 monks and 36 women."
  },
  {
   "id": "tahara_lower_p185_left",
   "sequence": 665,
   "domain_canonical": "田原藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田原藩",
   "domain_en": "Tahara",
   "image": "images/lower_p185_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 185,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（田原）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview (Hansei ichiran), Table 8 (Tahara)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Tahara domain officials roster and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 (officials and military) page for Tahara Domain, printed book page 347. The upper register gives Tahara's post-1869 domain executive: 1 daisanji (senior councillor), 3 gon-daisanji, 1 shosanji (junior councillor) and 5 gon-shosanji, ten posts in all, together with a military establishment of 3 platoons — 2 platoons of shizoku-and-sotsu troops plus 1 platoon of farmer-sotsu troops. The lower register names each officeholder in the same right-to-left order (Murakami; Watanabe, Hirayama, Suzuki; Yagi; Ikuta, Sato, Murakami, Wada, Ueda), and the ten names reconcile exactly with the four printed counts. To the right of the Tahara maru-marker the page carries the tail of the preceding domain's entry: Takasu Domain's troop strength of 177 shizoku and 125 sotsu, 302 men in all."
  },
  {
   "id": "tannan_upper_p139_right",
   "sequence": 666,
   "domain_canonical": "丹南藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丹南藩",
   "domain_en": "Tannan",
   "image": "images/upper_p139_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 139,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（丹南）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Tannan)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tannan's assessed yield and land tax; Tahara's outcaste, village, priest, troop and noble counts",
   "page_summary_en": "The five columns at the right of the leaf close out Tahara domain (Mikawa), whose block begins on the facing page: 8 hinin outcaste households holding 32 people (15 male, 17 female), 24 villages, 6 Shinto-priest households holding 27 people (14 male, 13 female), a force of two samurai-and-sotsu companies plus one peasant-sotsu company at 50 men each for 150 in all, and a noble (kazoku) house of 12 people (5 male, 7 female). The maru-marker ○丹南藩 then opens Tannan domain, held by the Takagi house, and a warichu records that its land lay in Kawachi and Shimotsuke provinces; a heading confirms that the figures which follow combine the two. For Tannan the survey gives an assessed yield (kusadaka) of 11,007.59437 koku, a land tax of 6,041.964 koku of rice together with 142.80056 kan in ei cash, cotton cloth \"included in the land tax and varying in quantity from year to year\", and 36,661 bolts of woven cloth for the past Dragon year (1868). The running head names Tannan and the printed page number is 252."
  },
  {
   "id": "tannan_upper_p139_left",
   "sequence": 667,
   "domain_canonical": "丹南藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丹南藩",
   "domain_en": "Tannan",
   "image": "images/upper_p139_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 139,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（丹南）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Tannan)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Taxes, households, population, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-3 return for Tannan Domain, whose maru-marker stands on the facing right-hand page; no marker appears here, so every column belongs to Tannan. It records miscellaneous taxes of 87.745 koku of rice and 22.041 kan of cash, 10 koku of shrine land, 1,709 households and a population of 7,878 (3,845 male and 3,967 female, a breakdown that falls 66 short of the printed total in the source itself). The religious establishment comprises 41 shrines, 48 temple buildings with 59 monks and 4 manservants, 6 shrine-priest houses holding 26 people, and 3 hermitages. A compiler's note marks the last five columns — 129 shizoku, 134 sotsu with 581 family members, the shrine-priest houses, the hermitages, and 16 further persons — as written in red ink in the original manuscript, and a second note flags the combined shizoku-and-sotsu figure of 190 households as reproduced from that original."
  },
  {
   "id": "tannan_lower_p186_right",
   "sequence": 668,
   "domain_canonical": "丹南藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丹南藩",
   "domain_en": "Tannan",
   "image": "images/lower_p186_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 186,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（丹南、龍岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Eight (Tannan, Tatsuoka)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillor posts and troop counts (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-8 officials-and-military leaf carrying the tail of one domain's entry and the openings of two more. Overflowing from the preceding domain (Tahara) at the right edge is a two-column military note — each platoon fifty men, 150 men in all — together with an editorial gloss that its senior and junior councillors are recorded by surname only. The Tannan Domain block that follows gives its councillor establishment purely as counts: 1 senior councillor (daisanji), 2 provisional senior councillors, 2 junior councillors and 3 provisional junior councillors, plus 119 rank-and-file soldiers. The Tatsuoka Domain block then opens and, unlike Tannan, supplies names: Ide Fukami as senior councillor, and Kinugawa Bai and Owaki Dan as the two provisional senior councillors. Printed book-page 348."
  },
  {
   "id": "tako_upper_p141_left",
   "sequence": 669,
   "domain_canonical": "多古藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多古藩",
   "domain_en": "Tako",
   "image": "images/upper_p141_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 141,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（多古）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Tako)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tako Domain land tax (正租): five-year average, rice and cash portions",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Tako Domain's fascicle-3 return from the facing page, under the heading 五ヶ年平均 (five-year average) that ends book page 256. The regular land tax (正租) is given as 2,242.52727 koku of rice paid in kind (米納), followed by four further lines: 238.55994 koku commuted to 609.093 kanmon, 221.6439 koku commuted to 322.15683 kanmon, a cash levy of 138.9255 kanmon whose stated rice equivalent is 347.31375 koku (exactly 2.5 koku per ryō), and a residual cash item of 434.16 mon labelled 永方. A 内 (\"of which\") marker then splits the account by mode of payment: 2,906.0742 koku paid in rice, and 549.359 koku remitted in ei-cash, the latter stated twice — once at the fixed conversion price (定石靑束石代), worth 101.7708 kanmon, and once at the market rate of 3 koku 7 shō 2 gō per ryō, whose cash figure runs on to the next page."
  },
  {
   "id": "tako_upper_p142_left",
   "sequence": 670,
   "domain_canonical": "多古藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多古藩",
   "domain_en": "Tako",
   "image": "images/upper_p142_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 142,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（多古）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 3 (Tako)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tako domain: tax figures from a variant manuscript copy, then villages, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf (printed page 259) continues the fascicle-3 entry for Tako domain in Shimōsa; it carries no maru-marker, because ○多古藩 stands two pages earlier. The rightmost column, 此代永四貫四百九十文二分 (4.4902 kan-mon), completes an item begun on the preceding page. Two editor's notes in small type follow: 「（以下九行原朱書）」, which says the next nine lines stood in vermilion in the original manuscript, and 「（一本」, which opens a large parenthesis — closed at the foot of the soybean column — enclosing exactly those nine lines as the reading of another manuscript copy. Inside the bracket the regular land tax (正租) is given as 高米 2,702.72806 koku plus 576.26966 kan-mon in cash, and the miscellaneous taxes (雜税) as 366.5948 koku of rice, 130.703318 kan-mon, 4.4902 kan-mon, and 1.832 koku of soybeans valued at 0.408 koku per ryō; that rate reproduces the 4.4902 kan-mon figure exactly. The three columns outside the bracket are the domain's own running totals: 18 villages, 1,468 households, and 7,241 people, split 3,765 male and 3,476 female."
  },
  {
   "id": "tako_upper_p143_right",
   "sequence": 671,
   "domain_canonical": "多古藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多古藩",
   "domain_en": "Tako",
   "image": "images/upper_p143_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 143,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三 (田原本)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 3 — running header for the Tawaramoto (田原本) section; provenance only, since most of the page completes the preceding Tako (多古藩) entry",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tako's shrines, temples, status population and militia; Tawaramoto's opening land assessment and tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This page falls on the join between two fascicle-3 entries, with the maru-marker ○田原本藩 dividing them. To the right of the marker the survey return for 多古藩 (Tako, Shimōsa) closes: 42 shrines with 10 shrine-priest households, 48 temples with 10 Shugendō households, 15 koku of former shogunal vermilion-seal land, and a combined samurai-and-sotsu population of 501 (268 male, 233 female). The same block records 5 kazoku (3 male, 2 female), outcaste household counts returned as \"not ascertained\" for both 穢多 (5 persons) and 非人 (10 persons), a standing force — the Heishō Corps — of one and a half platoons with 12 officers, and one cannon served by 3 officers and 7 gunners. Left of the marker the entry for 田原本藩 (Tawaramoto, Yamato) opens with an assessed yield (草高) of 10,001.838174 koku and, as five-year averages, a land tax (正租) of 3,053.38333 koku together with 6 kan 500 mon in cash."
  },
  {
   "id": "tako_lower_p186_left",
   "sequence": 672,
   "domain_canonical": "多古藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多古藩",
   "domain_en": "Tako",
   "image": "images/lower_p186_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 186,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百四十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（多古）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 8 (Tako)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain troops and named domain officials (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 349 of fascicle 8 straddles two domains. Its right-hand half closes out Tatsuoka Domain (龍岡藩, Shinano), whose block opened on the facing page 348: the named-officials list continues with a third 權大參事 (Suzuki Kakuemon), two 少參事 (Kawamura Azuma, Umemura Shūji) and two 權少參事 (Tahara Kaname, Satō Tasuku), and its forces are entered as one small company of 兵士 at 43 men, one small company of 兵卒 at 40 men, and a half company of 夫卒 (baggage labourers) at 22 men — 105 men in all. The ○多古藩 marker then opens Tako Domain (Shimōsa), whose return is far thinner: the administrative structure is recorded as 不詳 (\"not known\"), a corps named the Heishō-tai musters one and a half small companies with 12 officers, and a single cannon is manned by a crew of 3. No officials are named for Tako on this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "tako_lower_p187_right",
   "sequence": 673,
   "domain_canonical": "多古藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "多古藩",
   "domain_en": "Tako",
   "image": "images/lower_p187_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 187,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八 （多古）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 8 — Tako (多古藩): councillor roster and a residual military headcount",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "domain officials roster — sanji ranks and their named appointees",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the continuation leaf of the fascicle-8 (officials and military) entry for Tako Domain (多古藩), a 12,000-koku holding in Shimōsa whose ○多古藩 boundary marker stands on the preceding page; no marker appears here, so the whole leaf is Tako's. The upper register closes out Tako's military establishment with a demolition detail (破手) of 7 men, following the 43-man infantry platoon, 40-man rank-and-file platoon, 22-man half-platoon of porters and single field gun recorded on the preceding leaf. The lower register gives the domain's post-1869 councillor roster under four ranks: 大参事 with 2 men (Hara Sajima, Nomura Hayata), 権大参事 with 4 (Ogura Hajime, Tsuji Yoya, Hattori Raisuke, Terai Jitarō), 少参事 with 3 (Hirano Keisuke, Takahashi Kan, Ōki Tadami) and 権少参事 with 3 (Sekiya Kiemon, Namiki Kichibē, Terai Keiji) — twelve councillors in all, each printed as its own name column beneath its rank heading. The printed book-page number in the outer margin is 三百五十 (350)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tawaramoto_lower_p187_left",
   "sequence": 674,
   "domain_canonical": "田原本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田原本藩",
   "domain_en": "Tawaramoto",
   "image": "images/lower_p187_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 187,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第八（田原本、館山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table Eight (Tawaramoto, Tateyama)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, covering domain officials and military establishment, printed here for two 10,000-koku domains. Tawaramoto (Yamato province) occupies the right two-thirds of the leaf and is given twice: a first roster of one acting senior councillor (權大參事 Saitō Fusaho) and two junior councillors (少參事 Nishitani Zenjutsu and Ogawa Masaakira), and then a second roster headed （二） listing a senior councillor (Himeshima Kazuo), an acting senior councillor (Saitō Toshirō), a junior councillor (Shimotsuma Kitōta) and an acting junior councillor (Nishitani Naomaru), with the source of that second roster noted as the caretaker official's register （留守官留書）. Between the two rosters Tawaramoto's entire military establishment is recorded as a single platoon of 70 men. Tateyama (Awa province) begins at its own maru-marker on the left and lists three men: senior councillor Sasaki Yoshiya, and acting senior councillors Shimamura Izō and Matsushita Naoe, the last also serving as a kōgisho representative (公議人)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tateyama_upper_p143_left",
   "sequence": 675,
   "domain_canonical": "館山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "館山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tateyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p143_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 143,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（館山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Tateyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tawaramoto population and status counts; Tateyama's opening yield figures",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed book page 261 of the 藩制一覽表 fascicle 3 closes out Tawaramoto Domain's return and opens Tateyama Domain's. Ten columns to the right of the maru-marker record Tawaramoto's miscellaneous tax of 119 ryō 2 bu, 1,027 households, a population of 3,942 (1,914 male, 2,028 female), one Shinto shrine and 22 Buddhist temples, 263 shizoku in 65 households, 158 sotsu, 10 eta households (40 persons), 7 hinin households (36 persons), and a single platoon of 70 troops. Left of the marker ○館山藩 the page gives Tateyama's yield figures: a nominal 草高 of 10,000 koku, an additional 2,319.1447 koku of komidaka and newly reclaimed paddy, and a 合高 of 12,319.1447 koku. Every male/female pair on the page sums exactly to its printed total, and the two Tateyama increments sum exactly to the printed total yield."
  },
  {
   "id": "tateyama_upper_p144_right",
   "sequence": 676,
   "domain_canonical": "館山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "館山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tateyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p144_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 144,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（館山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Three (Tateyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tateyama domain: religious lands, land and cash taxes, villages, households, population, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf continues the Tateyama (館山) entry in fascicle three of the 1870 Hansei ichiran. No maru-marker appears anywhere on the page, so all fifteen printed columns belong to Tateyama. The survey records shrine lands of 73.22 koku, temple lands of 300.249 koku and, in addition, 60 ken square of vacant land; the regular land tax stands at 3,298.55032 koku of rice and the cash levy at 1,033.55463 kan, which an interlinear note converts into 200.40624 koku of rice at the five-year average price of one ryo to 0.19390 koku. Miscellaneous taxes carry no figure: the page prints 雜稅不詳. The domain held 50 villages and 3,526 households with a population of 23,202 persons (11,492 male and 11,710 female), together with 9 shrines staffed by 70 people (40 male, 30 female) and 96 temples housing 80 monks, of which 41 buildings had no resident priest."
  },
  {
   "id": "tateyama_lower_p188_right",
   "sequence": 677,
   "domain_canonical": "館山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "館山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tateyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p188_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 188,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（高富）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 8 (Takatomi)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and infantry platoons (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page finishes the fascicle-8 officials and military entry for Tateyama Domain and then opens the entry for Takatomi. Tateyama is credited with three junior councillors (shōsanji Iinuma, Yamada Emori, Itō Daijirō), three acting junior councillors (Takahashi Bunpei, Okuda Hidesaburō, Otsuhata Seiichirō), one kōyōnin agent (Matsushita Kenji), and two infantry platoons of 45 men each: the first breaks down as 20 shizoku plus 25 sotsu (=45), but the second is printed as 50 shizoku plus 25 sotsu (=75), which the 1928 collator marks with the note 校訂者云計數合ハス, \"the collator says the counts do not tally.\" A second collator note glosses the given-name-less Iinuma as appearing elsewhere as Katsura Inosuke. Left of the ○高富藩 marker, Takatomi's officials are recorded only as head-counts — 2 daisanji, 1 gon-daisanji, 1 shōsanji, 1 gon-shōsanji — and the printed page number 三百五十二 (352) sits in the right margin."
  },
  {
   "id": "takase_lower_p188_left",
   "sequence": 678,
   "domain_canonical": "高瀬藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高瀨藩",
   "domain_en": "Takase",
   "image": "images/lower_p188_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 188,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八　（高瀨）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Takase) — outer-margin running header giving the survey title, the fascicle number, and the header-designated domain.",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Takase domain officials roster (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 8 (officials register) page opening the entry for 高瀨藩 (Takase), a branch domain of Kumamoto. The single column to the right of the ○高瀨藩 marker — 兵隊　不詳, \"troops: not detailed\" — closes the preceding 高富藩 (Takatomi) entry, whose own 大參事/權大參事/少參事/權少參事 counts end on the facing recto at folio 352. Takase's roster names eleven men under three headings: 執政 3 (米野覺右衞門, 黑澤丹下, 三友市郎右衞門), 參政 7 (大野束, 戸川忠右衞門, 原三右衞門, 大槻彌左衞門, 柴田津司馬, 平野岩之丞, 西市太郎), and 公議人 1 (笠間英之進). No kokudaka, population, or troop figures are printed for Takase here; the folio number in the bottom margin is 三百五十三 (353)."
  },
  {
   "id": "sonobe_upper_p147_left",
   "sequence": 679,
   "domain_canonical": "園部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "園部藩",
   "domain_en": "Sonobe",
   "image": "images/upper_p147_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 147,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（園部）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 3 (Sonobe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Sonobe domain assessed kokudaka and five-year-average land tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Sonobe domain's fascicle-3 return with no domain marker of its own, so all fifteen printed elements belong to 園部藩. The land base closes here: 11,632.0513 koku of newly reclaimed and re-surveyed paddy is added, giving a total assessment of 38,343.2173 koku, from which 2,424.6397 koku of permanently waste and landless holdings is struck, leaving a true standing assessment of 35,918.5776 koku. Under the heading \"five-year average\" the tax follows: regular land tax of 8,191.48039 koku in rice plus a further 3,967.6982 koku commuted to money at 29,356 ryō 1 bu and 43.3 ei-mon, totalling 12,159.17819 koku; miscellaneous taxes run to 2,749.64231 koku of rice, commuted at 19,164 ryō 1 bu and 53.2 ei-mon. Subtracting the reclamation figure from the total leaves 26,711.166 koku, matching Sonobe's nominal kokudaka of 26,711 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "sonobe_upper_p148_right",
   "sequence": 680,
   "domain_canonical": "園部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "園部藩",
   "domain_en": "Sonobe",
   "image": "images/upper_p148_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 148,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百七十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（園部）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Three (Sonobe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Sonobe domain: total tax rice and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the closing part of the 園部藩 (Sonobe) entry in fascicle three of the 1870 Hansei ichiran; the running head reads 藩制一覽表第三（園部）and the printed folio number is 270. A bracketed note announces that the next five lines stand in red in the original: tax-exempt shrine and temple land of 1.19 and 1.6727 koku, and an assessed yield of 28.46186 koku described as the share dropped from within the miscellaneous taxes. The domain's combined rice total is 14,908.8209 koku, qualified at the foot of the column as 正物成, the regular levy taken in kind. The population block then gives 7,511 households and 34,183 people (17,431 male, 16,752 female), 217 shrine and temple buildings with 35 shrine attendants, 193 monks and nuns, 217 shizoku households holding 829 people, 408 sotsu households holding 1,655 people, and eta and hinin returned as 不詳, not known."
  },
  {
   "id": "sonobe_lower_p189_left",
   "sequence": 681,
   "domain_canonical": "園部藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "園部藩",
   "domain_en": "Sonobe",
   "image": "images/lower_p189_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 189,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（園部、曾我部）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 9 (Sonobe, Sogabe)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle 9 officials roster: councillor ranks and named appointees for two small domains",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries fascicle 9 (domain officials) for two small domains, opened by the ○園部藩 and ○曾我部藩 maru-markers. Sonobe (Tanba, 26,711 koku by its fascicle-3 草高) reports four councillor ranks — 大參事, 權大參事, 少參事 and 權少參事 — each with two stacked headcount figures (2/1, 1/3, 2/4, and a lone 2 for gon-shōsanji) followed by ten named officeholders; the lower figure of each pair matches the names printed, and the four lower figures sum exactly to those ten men, while the five upper figures read as the authorised establishment. Sonobe's military line is the single note 兵制不詳, \"military system not ascertained\" — no troop, gun or ship figures at all. Sogabe (printed 曾我野藩 elsewhere in HI, a 10,000-koku house) reports only three ranks with two names each and no headcounts whatever. The outer margin repeats the running head 藩制一覽表第九（園部、曾我部）above the printed folio number 355."
  },
  {
   "id": "tayasu_upper_p146_left",
   "sequence": 682,
   "domain_canonical": "田安藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田安藩",
   "domain_en": "Tayasu",
   "image": "images/upper_p146_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 146,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（田安）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Tayasu)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tayasu Domain kokudaka and tax revenue, following the close of Takatomi Domain's status-household and troop returns",
   "page_summary_en": "The six right-hand columns close out Takatomi Domain's fascicle-3 return: 46 temple-and-hermitage households holding 69 people, 8 Shugendō households holding 26, 2 goze households holding 2, 5 cloister households holding 18, and 25 eta and hinin households holding 87, followed by a bracketed military line of three platoons plus two artillery gun-carriages, 199 men in all. The maru-marker ○田安藩 then opens Tayasu Domain, and a small-type gloss places its holdings in Settsu, Izumi, Harima, Kai and Shimōsa. Tayasu returns a total assessed yield of 101,799.25055 koku, with a further 1,920.8638 koku of newly opened land recorded outside that total; its regular land tax is 39,970.80366 koku in actual rice plus 706 kan 669.5 mon in ei cash, and its miscellaneous taxes are 2,427.5103 koku of rice plus 663 kan 998.18 mon in ei cash. The printed book page is 267."
  },
  {
   "id": "tayasu_upper_p147_right",
   "sequence": 683,
   "domain_canonical": "田安藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田安藩",
   "domain_en": "Tayasu",
   "image": "images/upper_p147_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 147,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（園部）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Three (Sonobe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tayasu retainer households, population, temples, shrines, villages and troops; Sonobe's assessed yield opens",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes the fascicle-three entry for Tayasu domain and opens that of Sonobe. Tayasu reports 1,025 shizoku households (5,045 persons), 318 sotsu households (1,199 persons) and 20 seasonally indentured households (194 persons), for a retainer subtotal of 1,363 households and 6,438 persons, set against a domain-wide 17,802 households and 84,743 persons spread over 240 villages. It also records 310 shrines with 364 attached persons, 458 temples with 1,130 attached persons, and a standing force of 721 men counting bushi and foot soldiers together. Left of the maru-marker the Sonobe entry begins with an assessed yield (kusadaka) of 26,711.166 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "tayasu_lower_p189_right",
   "sequence": 684,
   "domain_canonical": "田安藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "田安藩",
   "domain_en": "Tayasu",
   "image": "images/lower_p189_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 189,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第八（田安）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 8 (Tayasu)",
   "table_number": 8,
   "page_topic": "Officials line and troop strength (fascicle 8)",
   "page_summary_en": "Folio 354 of fascicle 8 of the 1869-70 Dajōkan domain survey, carrying the tail of the Takase entry and the opening of the Tayasu entry. To the right of the ○田安藩 maru-marker, Takase's military closes out: three platoons of infantry (兵隊 三小隊) and two artillery carriages (砲兵 貳車), summed by the page as 合百九十九人, 199 men. To the left of the marker, Tayasu's own return begins: its officials are declared 不詳, no figure returned, and its forces are given as 兵士 500 men, 兵卒 150 men, and a separately organized body of 別段組立兵士 200 men, of whom 100 form a sharpshooter unit (内百人狙擊隊). Tayasu's three troop figures total 850 men, but the page prints no Tayasu total, so that entry continues onto the facing verso."
  },
  {
   "id": "nariwa_upper_p164_right",
   "sequence": 685,
   "domain_canonical": "成羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "成羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Nariwa",
   "image": "images/upper_p164_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 164,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（成羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Table Four (Nariwa)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nariwa domain rice revenue, products, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf (printed page 302) carries a single domain's fascicle-4 return for 成羽藩 (Nariwa, in Bitchū province); no maru-marker appears on the page, so the entry began on the preceding leaf. It records two rice figures — 3,893.246 koku of genmai from the land tax and a further 127.705 koku standing for the miscellaneous taxes together with unjō and myōga levies — followed by a product list of charcoal, soybeans, adzuki beans, coal, tobacco, seed cotton and rafted timber. The domain returns 3,514 households and 16,619 people across 26 villages, broken down by status into 3,393 commoner households (16,158 people), 81 shizoku households (389), 69 sotsu households (373), 23 shrine households (129), 27 temples (32 residents) and 62 outcaste households (293); a parenthetical line at the far left gives a military strength of 78 men. Every male/female pair sums exactly to its own subtotal, but the status groups together exceed the headline household and population totals by 141 households and 755 people, a discrepancy internal to the source."
  },
  {
   "id": "nariwa_lower_p195_right",
   "sequence": 686,
   "domain_canonical": "成羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "成羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Nariwa",
   "image": "images/lower_p195_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 195,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（成羽、苗木）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 9 (Nariwa, Naegi)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 officials-and-military leaf carrying the end of one domain's return and the whole of another's. To the right of the ○成羽藩 maru-marker stand the four councillor ranks of the preceding domain, 長島藩 — 大參事 (福原藏右衞門, 吉見頼母), 權大參事 (山田新右衞門, 伴勘九郎), 少參事 (久我兵右衞門, 宮田彥兵衞) and 權少參事 (中島夷則, 石川央), eight men in all, with no headcount printed against any rank — followed by its military line 兵隊 二百十五人, 215 troops. To the left of the marker, 成羽藩 returns three ranks whose printed counts each read 一人 but which the 1928 editors correct in small parentheses: 大參事 一人（三人）, 權大參事 一人, 少參事 一人（四）. The corrected figures reconcile exactly with the eight names printed below (田邊確彦, 清水入衞, 小川勇雄; 田邊農夫也; 岡周齋, 村瀬節造, 井上篤次, 信原德太郎), and 成羽藩 returns no troop figure at all, printing 兵隊 不詳. The ○苗木藩 marker at the far left opens Naegi's entry, whose data begins on the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "murakami_upper_p165_left",
   "sequence": 687,
   "domain_canonical": "村上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "村上藩",
   "domain_en": "Murakami",
   "image": "images/upper_p165_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 165,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四 （村上）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Murakami)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "tax remittance totals, households, population, religious houses and villages",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 305 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle four. The right-hand two thirds of the leaf complete the entry for 七日市藩 (Nanokaichi, Kōzuke): 132.03053 koku of regular and miscellaneous tax remitted in rice, a further 81 ryō 3 bu 2 shu in cash paid in lieu, and a combined total (合) of 2,604.67987 koku, followed by 1,640 households, a population of 6,472 (3,457 male, 3,015 female), 25 shrines with 5 shrine-priest households and 5 priests, 20 temples with 19 monks, one hall, three hermitages with two mountain ascetics, 18 villages, and 174 troops. The ○村上藩 marker then opens 村上藩 (Murakami, Echigo), whose 草高 is 77,653.022 koku, of which 50,090.88 koku is 本高; the 27,562.142 koku remainder appears on the next leaf. The population total is printed 六千四軒七拾二人, with 軒 set in error where 百 is required — the male and female sub-counts sum to 6,472 and settle the reading."
  },
  {
   "id": "murakami_upper_p166_right",
   "sequence": 688,
   "domain_canonical": "村上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "村上",
   "domain_en": "Murakami",
   "image": "images/upper_p166_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 166,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（村上）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyo, fascicle 4 (Murakami)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Murakami tax yield, miscellaneous taxes and products (fascicle 4)",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf of the Murakami domain entry in fascicle 4 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, printed page 306. It reports a yield of 27,562.142 koku (the field label stands on the preceding leaf; a marginal note states that new-field yield is included, and a warichu states that a five-year average from Ansei 6 (1859) to Bunkyu 3 (1863) is used by granted petition), actual rice of 28,963.079 koku, and miscellaneous taxes on the same basis of 1,679.49 koku, which total 30,642.569 koku. From that total 672.791 koku is deducted for soybeans, straw matting and other goods taken in lieu of rice, leaving a remainder of 29,969.778 koku; the miscellaneous taxes reckoned in gold come to 11,534 ryo and 186.85 ei-mon. Under products, a five-year average of 750.085 koku of sake is recorded with a cash value of 60,006 kan 800 mon, with a proviso that 32.172 koku of sake-brewing duty rice is carried inside the miscellaneous taxes."
  },
  {
   "id": "murakami_upper_p166_left",
   "sequence": 689,
   "domain_canonical": "村上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "村上藩",
   "domain_en": "Murakami",
   "image": "images/upper_p166_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 166,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（村上）",
   "page_header_en": "Conspectus of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Murakami)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Murakami products and the Meiji 2 household and population survey",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Murakami Domain entry in fascicle four of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran, closing the product list and then giving the domain's household and population survey. Two commodities are priced: 20,800 salted salmon worth 60,560 kanmon, and, under the heading \"amounts surveyed in the snake year, Meiji 2 (1869)\", 272,660 kin of tea worth 121,873 kan 932 mon; a warichu note on each records that 4,000 ryo of transit dues and 3,000 kanmon of service dues respectively were folded into the miscellaneous tax. The survey returns 14,615 households and 80,034 people, itemized as 373 samurai households (1,838 people: 852 male, 986 female), 365 sotsu households (1,770 people: 844 male, 926 female), 19 Shinto households (98 people: 45 male, 53 female), 132 temples (565 people: 362 monks, 5 male, 198 female), and 13,542 peasant households. The itemized households total 14,431, or 184 fewer than the printed grand total of 14,615, a discrepancy present in the print itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "murakami_upper_p167_right",
   "sequence": 690,
   "domain_canonical": "村上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "村上藩",
   "domain_en": "Murakami",
   "image": "images/upper_p167_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 167,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（村松）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Four (Muramatsu)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Murakami population, religious and outcaste households, districts and troops; Muramatsu land assessment",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page closes the Murakami-domain entry in fascicle four and opens the Muramatsu entry at the ○村松藩 marker. For Murakami it records a population of 74,769 (36,894 male, 37,875 female), five dōjō housing 26 people (12 monks, 2 men, 12 women), 30 shugendō houses with 126 people, 149 eta, ferry-keeper and hinin houses with 842 people, 527 shrines, three districts (Iwafune, Kanbara, Mishima), 191 villages, and two platoons of sixty men each with three further platoons not yet organized. Left of the marker the Muramatsu land figures begin: a kusadaka of 30,002.91 koku plus a further 9,112.041 koku of included and newly surveyed yield, totalling 39,114.951 koku. Against that assessment the five-year-average genmai stands at 20,125.65227 koku, about 51 percent of the combined koku figure."
  },
  {
   "id": "murakami_lower_p196_right",
   "sequence": 691,
   "domain_canonical": "村上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "村上藩",
   "domain_en": "Murakami",
   "image": "images/lower_p196_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 196,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（村上）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration (Hansei ichiran-hyō), Fascicle 9 (Murakami)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillors and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 368 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 9, the fascicle that records each domain's councillor posts and its armed force. The right-hand quarter of the leaf closes the block of the preceding domain (Nanukaichi, per MASTER's fascicle-9 military sweep): a 權少參事 heading followed by five acting junior councillors — Yokoo Katsuma, Furudate Sakae, Saitō Jun, Hosaka Chibumi and Hata Ikkaku — and a 兵隊 entry of 43 domain samurai plus 81 foot soldiers, 124 men in all. The ○村上藩 marker then opens Murakami Domain, which returns two 大參事 (Esaka Emori, Hisanaga Sōemon), two 權大參事 (Natsume Kichibee, Wada Masayoshi), one 公議人, two 少參事 and one 權少參事, and a force of two platoons of sixty men each together with 32 staff officers and 8 buglers, or 160 men. A small editorial note printed in the upper margin, marked as vermilion in the original manuscript, records that the names of Murakami's 公議人 and of its full and acting junior councillors were not supplied, which is why those three columns carry a headcount but no roster."
  },
  {
   "id": "mutsuura_upper_p170_right",
   "sequence": 692,
   "domain_canonical": "六浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "六浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Mutsuura",
   "image": "images/upper_p170_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 170,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（六浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (Mutsuura)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Land assessment and annual tax yield of Mutsuura Domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the fascicle-4 entry for Mutsuura Domain (六浦藩), the 12,000-koku Yonekura holding on Musashi Bay. Its base assessment (草高) is 11,999.9996 koku; a further 4,584.69888 koku of new-field and resurveyed land (外高, glossed in the marginal note as 込高＝新田高・打出高) brings the combined assessment (合高) to 16,584.6984 koku. Under a five-year average the domain collected 2,365.7329 koku of rice plus 1,575,845.1 mon in cash as regular land tax (正租), and 15.344 koku plus 988,473.8 mon in miscellaneous imposts (雜稅), for a total assessed yield (物成高) of 2,701.61675 koku — the cash converting at a flat 8 kanmon to the koku. The four columns to the right of the marker close out the preceding entry, Muraoka Domain: 6.0879 koku of temple land, one district (Shitomi in Tajima) and 73 villages, and two companies of troops numbering 40 and 60 men."
  },
  {
   "id": "mutsuura_upper_p170_left",
   "sequence": 693,
   "domain_canonical": "六浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "六浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Mutsuura",
   "image": "images/upper_p170_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 170,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（六浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Mutsuura)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Household and population counts by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the household and population return for Mutsuura domain (Musashi province, Yonekura house) in the 1869-70 Dajōkan survey: 2,362 households and 12,848 people. The household total is broken into 79 samurai (士族), 8 sotsu, 2,135 commoners, 22 shrine households, 43 temples, 7 shugendō households, 66 eta and 2 hinin households, which sum exactly to 2,362. The persons total is then broken down with male and female subtotals for each status: 324 samurai (145 male, 179 female), 46 sotsu (40/6), 11,899 commoners (6,012/5,887), 105 shrine people (55/50), 65 monks (62/3) and 43 shugendō practitioners (23/20). The eta and hinin person counts do not print on this leaf and continue on the next page, which is why the six status figures shown here sum to 12,482 rather than the printed 12,848. A 但 note carried over from the facing page records that the portion of dues paid in cash (永納) was converted to actual rice at a rate of eight ryō per koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "mutsuura_lower_p197_right",
   "sequence": 694,
   "domain_canonical": "六浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "六浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Mutsuura",
   "image": "images/lower_p197_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 197,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（六浦、宇和島）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 9 (Mutsuura, Uwajima)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain councillor posts and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page of fascicle 9 carries the complete administrative-and-military entries for two domains. Mutsuura, opened by the maru-marker in the second column from the right, reports one senior councillor (daisanji), two acting senior councillors (gon-daisanji), two junior councillors (shōsanji), and 52 rank-and-file soldiers, with no officeholders named. Uwajima, opened by the second maru-marker, reports two senior councillors, three acting senior councillors, three junior councillors, an acting junior councillorship printed without any count, and 924 military personnel. Nine officeholders are named in the lower register — Ueda Sadaichi, Sudō Tan, Tsugemori Shūzō, Nakatomi Jirō, Narita Seki, Ōnishi Noboru, Kasahara Jodō, Suzuki Tameo and Miura Shizuma — and since the three printed counts account for only eight of them, the ninth name fills the uncounted acting junior councillorship."
  },
  {
   "id": "ushiku_upper_p178_left",
   "sequence": 695,
   "domain_canonical": "牛久藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "牛久藩",
   "domain_en": "Ushiku",
   "image": "images/upper_p178_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 178,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（牛久）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle Four (Ushiku)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Ushiku kokudaka and five-year-average tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 331 of the fourth fascicle of the Hansei Ichiran. The four columns to the right of the maru-marker close out Utsunomiya domain in Shimotsuke: one komusō temple, thirty assembly-hall lodges, ten bōshiki lodges, four districts holding 172 villages and 38 towns, and a bracketed military note recording eight infantry platoons (40 men, 6 officers), 32 drummers, and one artillery company (31 men, 10 officers). The ○牛久藩 marker then opens Ushiku, whose assessed kusadaka of 10,017.024 koku plus a further 1,884.3209 koku gives the printed total of 11,901.3449 koku. Under the heading \"five-year average\" the page records regular land tax of 3,585.5446 koku of rice, 885 ryō in gold and 497.332 mon in eiraku cash, with miscellaneous taxes of 10,092.57 mon."
  },
  {
   "id": "ushiku_upper_p179_right",
   "sequence": 696,
   "domain_canonical": "牛久藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "牛久藩",
   "domain_en": "Ushiku",
   "image": "images/upper_p179_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 179,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百三十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（牛久）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle Four (Ushiku)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Ushiku domain households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues Ushiku domain's fascicle-four return at printed book page 332, the block having been opened by the ○牛久藩 marker on the preceding half-page. It begins with the rice equivalent of the domain's miscellaneous tax — 1.26157 koku, reckoned at eight ryō to the koku — and then gives 1,646 households and 8,604 people, divided among 130 warrior households (434 people), 1,416 commoner households (8,072 people), 12 shrine-priest households (34 people), 47 temples (44 people) and 41 hermitages (20 people); those five components sum exactly to both printed totals. Two groups are entered outside the totals under the note 外ニ: 4 eta households with 28 people and 9 hinin households with 42 people. The page closes with a kazoku family of one man and three women, 166 shrines, and a territory of 6 districts and 31 villages."
  },
  {
   "id": "ushiku_lower_p198_left",
   "sequence": 697,
   "domain_canonical": "牛久藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "牛久藩",
   "domain_en": "Ushiku",
   "image": "images/lower_p198_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 198,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（牛久、宇土）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Fascicle Nine (Ushiku, Udo)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop establishment (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page carries the whole fascicle-9 entry for 牛久藩 (Ushiku, Hitachi province, Yamaguchi house). Its officials are recorded twice over: under the pre-reform titles, bracketed together as a group — 執政 (山口旬, 山口誠, 會美四郎), 參政 (野尻傳八, 青木又, 小川傳右衞門) and 公議人 (廣澤鉉一郎) — and again under the 1869 titles, where 山口旬 becomes the single 大參事, the other three become the three 權大參事 (the count 三 is printed in small type beside that title), the three 參政 carry over unchanged as 少參事, and three further men (山口三郎, 愛智元, 川角純藏) appear as 權少參事. The domain's force is slight: one rifle regiment of 85 men and a single cannon with 17 crew. Two columns to the right of the ○牛久藩 marker still belong to 六浦藩 — an artillery company of 10 officers and 31 gunners, and 32 drummers — while the ○宇土藩 marker at the far left opens the next domain, whose figures run on to the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "kurume_upper_p186_right",
   "sequence": 698,
   "domain_canonical": "久留米藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久留米藩",
   "domain_en": "Kurume",
   "image": "images/upper_p186_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 186,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（久留米）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Survey, Fascicle Five (Kurume)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kurume population by status group and shrine count",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Kurume domain's fascicle-five (demographic) return with no maru-marker of its own, so every figure on it belongs to 久留米藩. The domain reports a total population of 264,577 persons, alongside a second figure of 242,086 persons that the collator notes stood in the margin of the original manuscript; the difference is exactly the six status groups printed below, namely 5,030 shizoku, 11,641 sotsu, 1,416 shrine personnel, 1,912 temple personnel, 2,223 eta and 269 hinin, each broken into male and female counts that sum to their own totals. The domain also returns 598 shrines. Two editorial caveats head the page, warning that the survey does not make clear whether shrine households, eta and hinin were excluded, and that the categories written out below are to be treated as excluded from the figure at right."
  },
  {
   "id": "kurume_lower_p201_right",
   "sequence": 699,
   "domain_canonical": "久留米藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久留米藩",
   "domain_en": "Kurume",
   "image": "images/lower_p201_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 201,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九、（桑名）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview (Hansei Ichiran), Fascicle 9 — (Kuwana)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the tail of Kurume domain's fascicle-9 return and the opening of Kuwana's. Right of the single maru-marker, Kurume lists two gon-daisanji, seven shōsanji and seven gon-shōsanji by name, followed by its military strength: the seventh battalion at 3,310 men and the eighth at 3,802, for a printed total of 7,112 — the two components sum exactly to the total. Left of the ○桑名藩 marker, Kuwana's entry opens with one chiji (no name printed on this leaf) and a daisanji establishment given as one person, though two names follow, 酒井孫八郎 and 服部半十郎; the 1928 edition marks the discrepancy with an editorial （マヽ）. Only six of Kurume's seven shōsanji are named here, the seventh evidently falling on the preceding leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "gujo_upper_p187_left",
   "sequence": 700,
   "domain_canonical": "郡上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "郡上藩",
   "domain_en": "Gujō",
   "image": "images/upper_p187_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 187,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百四十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（郡上）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran (Survey of Domain Administration), Fascicle 5 (Gujō)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Gujō domain revenue and household registers",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Gujō domain (郡上藩) entry in fascicle 5, marked by the circle marker ○郡上藩 with a former assessment (元高) of 48,000 koku. The domain's recorded revenue is a land tax (正税) of 15,566.38006 koku of rice and a miscellaneous tax (雜税) of 3,227.2614 ryō in cash; the 現穀 column restates the two together and an editorial bracket sums them at 15,969.83036 koku, a conversion of the cash at roughly eight ryō per koku. Households number 9,398, of which 164 are samurai (士族), 236 sotsu (卒族), 196 shrine households (社家) and 132 temples and hermitages (寺庵), while the 草高 field is printed as a bare label with no figure beneath it. The two columns to the right of the marker — three districts (三郡) and a governor's household of four persons, one male and three female — close the preceding entry for Kuwana domain (桑名藩), whose data fills the facing page 三百四十八."
  },
  {
   "id": "gujo_upper_p188_right",
   "sequence": 701,
   "domain_canonical": "郡上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "郡上藩",
   "domain_en": "Gujō",
   "image": "images/upper_p188_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 188,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（久留里）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Kururi)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Gujō population by status; Kururi's kokudaka opening",
   "page_summary_en": "The page carries the closing columns of Gujō Domain's fascicle-5 return and then opens Kururi Domain's. Gujō reports a population of 55,668, of which 26,728 male and 24,774 female commoners, plus 977 shizoku, 1,265 sotsu, 1,088 shrine people, 807 temple people (including 161 monks and 2 shugendō practitioners) and 29 persons exempt from all corvée duties; those seven figures sum exactly to the printed total. Six eta and seventy-two hinin are bracketed off as counted separately, with an editorial note that the original manuscript gives no household counts for them. Gujō also reports 84 shrines and a governor's household of four, one of them the governor and three his sisters. The maru-marker ○久留里藩 then opens Kururi, rated at an original 30,000 koku, with a kusadaka of 33,081.48628 koku and a five-year average genmai of 10,855.544 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "gujo_lower_p201_left",
   "sequence": 702,
   "domain_canonical": "郡上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "郡上藩",
   "domain_en": "Gujō",
   "image": "images/lower_p201_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 201,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第九（郡上）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Gujō)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials rosters and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of fascicle 9 closes the officials roster of Kuwana Domain and opens that of Gujō Domain, the two separated by the ○郡上藩 marker at x≈1651–1754. Right of the marker Kuwana records two acting senior councillors (Yamawaki Jūrō, Machida Busuke), one junior councillor (Baba Jinhachirō) and three acting junior councillors (Matsuura Sakubē, Ebihara Gengo, Fukumoto Iori), together with its forces: two infantry battalions, reckoned at eight platoons of forty men each, and four artillery batteries of twenty-seven men each — 640 infantry and 108 gunners. Left of the marker Gujō's entry opens with governor Aoyama Yukiyoshi, two senior councillors (Sasaki Giichi, Suzuki Shigeken), one acting senior councillor (Ayabe Seiichi) and four junior councillors, of whom only Kuki Shigenade is named before the entry runs onto the following leaf. A note in the governor's column records that the eleven small-type lines that follow, printed in red in the original, come from the caretaker official's report of the fourth month of the horse year."
  },
  {
   "id": "kururi_upper_p188_left",
   "sequence": 703,
   "domain_canonical": "久留里藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久留里藩",
   "domain_en": "Kururi",
   "image": "images/upper_p188_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 188,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 (久留里)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Kururi (久留里藩): tax total, stipends, shrine and temple lands, population by status",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "eiraku-cash tax total, stipend heads, shrine/temple lands, population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the second half of the fascicle-5 entry for Kururi domain (久留里藩) in Kazusa; no maru-marker appears on it, so all of it belongs to the domain opened on the preceding leaf. The tax side closes with an eiraku-cash total of 2,617 kan 17 mon, averaged over five years and glossed by a printed note that the eiraku total is the sum of all the various taxes, converted to 278.877 koku of current rice at eight ryō to the koku. Two stipend heads combined come to 11,126.421 koku, and one tenth of that, 1,112.6421 koku, is the house stipend; two shrines hold 26.8 koku of land and nine temples 125.3 koku, with a warichu noting that the original manuscript does not record whether these were vermilion-seal or black-seal grants. The population runs 1,189 shizoku (595 male, 594 female), 143 sotsu (114 and 29), 20,766 commoners (10,478 and 10,288), 92 shrine-household people (50 and 40) and 298 temple people (141 clergy plus 81 men and 76 women), with the shizoku males further divided into 128 officeholders, 333 old or young, and 130 soldiers."
  },
  {
   "id": "kururi_upper_p189_right",
   "sequence": 704,
   "domain_canonical": "久留里藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久留里藩",
   "domain_en": "Kururi",
   "image": "images/upper_p189_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 189,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（黑石）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 5 (Kuroishi)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kururi household, population, shrine and village counts; opening of the Kuroishi block",
   "page_summary_en": "The page closes out the fascicle-5 return for Kururi domain (Kazusa) and opens that of Kuroishi (Mutsu). For Kururi it gives the tail of the population return — 77 eta (30 male, 47 female) and 115 hinin (66 male, 49 female) — followed by a total population of 22,580, then the full household return: 253 samurai, 74 sotsu, 21 shrine-keeper, 73 temple, 4,465 commoner, 13 eta and 23 hinin households, totalling 4,922, a figure the components confirm exactly. Kururi is further credited with 520 shrines (with a note that none of them is listed in the Engishiki), 89 villages, and a governor's household of three: the governor, the retired lord and the wife. The maru-marker ○黑石藩 then opens Kuroishi's block with an assessed yield of 13,251.885 koku, qualified by a note that shrine and temple allowances are excluded. The printed population total is internally inconsistent — the male and female sub-counts sum to 22,680 — and the 1928 reprint marks it （マヽ）, \"thus in the original\"."
  },
  {
   "id": "kururi_lower_p202_right",
   "sequence": 705,
   "domain_canonical": "久留里藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "久留里藩",
   "domain_en": "Kururi",
   "image": "images/lower_p202_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 202,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（久留里）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Administration Overview, Fascicle 9 (Kururi)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Officials and military strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "The page straddles two domains. To the right of the ○久留里藩 marker it completes 郡上藩 (Gujo, Mino province): three more junior councillors of the main list (Takagi Shigetoshi, Otobe Tsugiyoshi, Hayashi Taneyasu), four acting junior councillors from the small-type list the caretaker-official reported (Otobe Kichijuro, Ayabe Seiichiro, Shimotsu Kyuma, Hayashi Yasutane), and the domain's whole military return — four infantry platoons with 6 staff and 3 bandsmen each and 60 rank-and-file, and 10 cannon itemised as 2 six-pounders, 4 boat guns, 1 rifled gun and 3 mortars, a breakdown that sums exactly to the stated total. To the left of the marker 久留里藩 (Kururi, Kazusa province) begins: a 知事 heading with no name printed against it, 大參事 三人 filled by Mizunuma Gun'emon, Chiba Keizo and Mori Kakuzaemon, and 權大參事 六人 of whom only Tsurumi Ichigaku and Tamaru Kamazo appear here, the other four running onto the facing page. The running header names Kururi even though most of the page's content is Gujo's, a reminder that the header is a provenance tag rather than a content label."
  },
  {
   "id": "kurobane_upper_p190_left",
   "sequence": 706,
   "domain_canonical": "黒羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "黑羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Kurobane",
   "image": "images/upper_p190_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 190,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（黑羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, fascicle 5 (Kurobane)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kurobane domain kokudaka, tax revenue, districts, villages and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Kurobane (黑羽) block in fascicle 5 of the Hansei ichiran. The domain's original assessment is 18,000 koku, while the surveyed gross yield (草高) is 29,443.6468 koku, which the warichu note says already includes the added assessment (込高) and the newly opened fields (新田). Regular tax (正税) is printed as 13,443.6468 koku; of the revenue actually taken, 5,014.0543 koku came in rice and 1,374 ryō 628 mon in cash (equal to 171.8285 koku at eight ryō per koku), and miscellaneous tax of 1,200 ryō converts to 150 koku of current rice, giving the printed total of 5,335.8828 koku. Kurobane held 2 districts, 70 villages and 3,666 households, among them 223 shizoku and 415 sotsu households."
  },
  {
   "id": "kurobane_upper_p191_right",
   "sequence": 707,
   "domain_canonical": "黒羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "黒羽藩",
   "domain_en": "Kurobane",
   "image": "images/upper_p191_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 191,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（櫛羅）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle Five — (Kujira)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kurobane population, shrines and temples; opening of the Kujira entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page closes Kurobane domain's fascicle-five entry and opens Kujira's. Kurobane is credited with a population of 19,493, of whom 837 were shizoku (393 male, 444 female) and 1,100 sotsu (764 male, 336 female); it held 153 Shinto shrines served by 88 shrine personnel from 22 priest households, and 34 Buddhist temples with 37 temple personnel (34 monks and 3 women), while the governor's family is entered as \"not recorded in the original document.\" Left of the ○櫛羅藩 marker, Kujira begins at a kusadaka of 10,000 koku, with a regular land tax — averaged over the five years from Genji 1 (1864) to Meiji 1 (1868) — of 3,440.675 koku of rice, 4,471 ryō 1 bu 1 shu in gold, and 8.69 mon in ei-cash. The marker's interlinear note places Kujira's 26 villages in four Yamato districts."
  },
  {
   "id": "kurobane_lower_p203_right",
   "sequence": 708,
   "domain_canonical": "黒羽藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "黒羽",
   "domain_en": "Kurobane",
   "image": "images/lower_p203_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 203,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（黒羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, ninth fascicle (Kurobane)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Kurobane domain officials roster and troop return",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf of Kurobane domain's ninth-fascicle entry, printed folio 382, carrying the domain's council roster and then its troop return. Seven appointees are named under four Meiji ranks: one 大參事 (Jōbōji Tanomo), one 權大參事 (Ōnuma Wataru), three 少參事 (Yanase Tarōbei, Ōtsuka Nizaemon, Andō Saburōzaemon) and two 權少參事 (Andō Kotarō, Kuno Jūbei); a closing line dates the return to the third month of the horse year, Meiji 3 (1870), and an editorial note records that the last three columns stand in vermilion in the manuscript. The military section reports eight rifle platoons of 60 men each, 480 in all, plus 32 reserve riflemen and 36 gunners, the gunners being organised with six mountain rifled guns into a single artillery company that with 7 officers and 2 signalmen comes to 45 men. The three components as printed total 557; no grand total is printed on this leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "yanagawa_upper_p194_left",
   "sequence": 709,
   "domain_canonical": "柳河藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳河藩",
   "domain_en": "Yanagawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p194_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 194,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百六十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（柳河）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Five (Yanagawa)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yanagawa domain assessed yield and tax receipts in kind",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Yanagawa (柳河藩) entry of fascicle five, printed page 363. Yanagawa's assessed yield (草高) is 155,394.06 koku, qualified by a warichu noting that the new-field yield has been revised and the surplus yield is included, and the domain administers five districts. Its regular tax (正税) is returned in three commodities — 63,270.27 koku of rice, 4,723.238 koku of soybeans and 604.118 koku of wheat — while the miscellaneous tax (雜稅) adds 8,697.118 koku of rice, 864.235 koku of soybeans, 5,277.447 koku of rapeseed, and a further 3,260.524 koku of rice earmarked by an explicit note for coastal-embankment repair. The four columns to the right of the Yanagawa marker still belong to Yamaguchi (Chōshū): three vessels — the Otchū-maru, Heiin-maru and Kayō-maru, with their foreign names, rigs and hull materials — and a note that the former governor's family members were not recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "yanagawa_upper_p195_right",
   "sequence": 710,
   "domain_canonical": "柳河藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳河藩",
   "domain_en": "Yanagawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p195_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 195,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（柳河）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Yanagawa)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Tax receipts in kind and their cash equivalents",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Yanagawa domain's fascicle-5 return and carries no domain marker, so every figure on it belongs to 柳河藩. The right-hand columns give the domain's tax take in kind and coin: miscellaneous taxes of 40,340 kan 540 mon in cash, combined rice of 75,727.912 koku, soybeans 5,587.473 koku, wheat 604.118 koku, and rapeseed 5,277.447 koku. The left-hand columns convert the three non-rice crops into silver at rates printed beneath each entry — soybeans at 4.605 ryo per koku for 25,729.116 ryo, wheat at 2.115 for 1,277.71 ryo, and rapeseed at 4.758 for 25,110.093 ryo — and close with a total of 52,114.7645 koku reckoned at 8 ryo per koku, actual rice of 82,242.6765 koku, and 26,461 households. A note in the editor's hand runs down the middle of the page: the following six lines were supplied on a separate sheet."
  },
  {
   "id": "yanagawa_upper_p195_left",
   "sequence": 711,
   "domain_canonical": "柳河藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳河藩",
   "domain_en": "Yanagawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p195_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 195,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（柳河）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 5 (Yanagawa)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yanagawa domain population and households by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Yanagawa (柳河藩) entry in fascicle 5 of the Hansei ichiran, printing status-group counts of households on the right and of individual people on the left. The household side records 818 shizoku, 34 kachi, 347 rōshi, 90 shrine attendants and 1,396 light foot-soldier households, together with 288 Buddhist temples, 186 eta and 29 hinin households. The population total is 127,323 people, split 64,853 male and 62,470 female; the status groups printed below it — 4,979 shizoku, 179 kachi, 1,942 rōshi, 530 shrine people, 1,481 clergy, 7,615 light foot soldiers, 169 hinin and 937 eta — come to 17,832, so the commoner majority is not itemised on this leaf. Every male/female pair sums to its printed total except the rōshi, where 951 and 985 give 1,936 against a printed 1,942."
  },
  {
   "id": "yanagawa_lower_p205_right",
   "sequence": 712,
   "domain_canonical": "柳河藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳河藩",
   "domain_en": "Yanagawa",
   "image": "images/lower_p205_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 205,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（柳河）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Nine (Yanagawa)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Yanagawa officials roster and troop establishment (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle nine of the 藩制一覽表 for 柳河藩 (Yanagawa, Chikugo province). The domain reports one 知事 (governor, name not printed), two 大參事 (senior councillors: Ono Takamoto and Tachibana Chikanori), three 權大參事 (acting senior councillors: Totoki Koreyuki, Sugimori Norimasa and Totoki Ichirō), and 少參事 (junior councillors) whose number the printer omitted although four men are named — Hori Akira, Totoki Nobuto, Ōmura Tsutomu and Yoshida Magoichirō. Under the heading 兵隊 the domain records a shizoku battalion of 400 men, one battalion of light foot-soldiers with no headcount given, and a shizoku artillery arm of two batteries at fifty men each, that is 100 gunners. The two right-hand columns, 丙寅丸 and 花陽丸, stand to the right of the ○柳河藩 marker and therefore close out the warship list of 山口藩 (Chōshū) that begins on the preceding page."
  },
  {
   "id": "yanagimoto_upper_p196_right",
   "sequence": 713,
   "domain_canonical": "柳本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳本藩",
   "domain_en": "Yanagimoto",
   "image": "images/upper_p196_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 196,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（柳本）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Yanagimoto)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yanagimoto domain: assessed yield, land tax and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Yanagimoto (柳本) domain entry in fascicle 5 of the Hansei Ichiran, after four closing columns belonging to the preceding domain. Yanagimoto is recorded at 10,000 koku both as motodaka (元高) and as kusadaka (草高), with an explicit note that there is no komidaka or newly opened field acreage; its holdings lay in Shikijō, Yamanobe and Uda districts of Yamato Province. Regular tax (正税) is 6,531.30928 koku of rice and miscellaneous tax (雜税) 65.93838 koku, and the printed total (合) of 6,597.24766 koku reconciles exactly with the sum of the two. Households number 1,454, of which 99 are shizoku and 60 sotsuzoku, and a warichu note records that about 66.1478 koku is deducted from the assessment for the upkeep of Emperor Sujin's imperial tomb, which stands at Yanagimoto. The four columns to the right of the marker close the previous domain's entry: 1,213 shrines, no warships, a governor's household of 17 (6 male, 11 female), and one Shugendō house with 4 residents (2 male, 2 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "yanagimoto_upper_p196_left",
   "sequence": 714,
   "domain_canonical": "柳本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳本藩",
   "domain_en": "Yanagimoto",
   "image": "images/upper_p196_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 196,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百六十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（柳本）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview Table, Fascicle 5 (Yanagimoto)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yanagimoto population by status, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-5 return for Yanagimoto Domain, giving the religious establishments and the status breakdown of the population. It records 2 shrines and 9 temples and hermitages, 41 eta and hinin households, and a total population of 6,814; the printed male and female sub-totals of 3,063 and 3,138 sum to only 6,201, and the 1928 editors set attention dots beside the 八 and the 四 of that total. The status components are shizoku 396 (200 male, 196 female), sotsu 197 (103 and 94), shrine staff 5 (1 and 4), temple clergy 18 (14 monks and 4 nuns), 2 female shrine mediums, eta 137 (66 and 71) and hinin 108 (59 and 49), each of which reconciles internally. Two editorial parentheses appear: one states that the eta-hinin household figure was taken from the discrepancy between the earlier and later returns, the other records a variant copy reading 17 monks and 1 nun; the leaf closes with the governor's household of 4 persons and a note that the domain had no warships."
  },
  {
   "id": "yanagimoto_lower_p205_left",
   "sequence": 715,
   "domain_canonical": "柳本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳本藩",
   "domain_en": "Yanagimoto",
   "image": "images/lower_p205_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 205,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（柳本、山崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey Table, Fascicle 9 (Yanagimoto, Yamazaki)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-9 official rosters and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle-9 entries for two 10,000-koku Yamato/Harima domains. Yanagimoto (柳本藩) is given a governor (知事), one senior councillor (大參事), four provisional senior councillors (權大參事), one junior councillor (少參事) and a provisional junior councillorship, with six officials named — Ajioka Saburōbei, Sakuma Yoemon, Ajioka Yaichizaemon, Harunaga Sōsuke, Mizoguchi Isamu (whose appointment carries the small-type note 留守官屆, \"reported through the caretaker official\") and Katsuta Uheita. Yanagimoto's military follows its roster and, as fascicle 9 always prints it, overflows to the right of the next domain's marker: one platoon, 50 men. The ○山崎藩 marker then opens Yamazaki with a governor, one senior councillor (Takema Motegi) and two provisional senior councillors (Tachibana and Baba); Yamazaki's own troop figures print on the following leaf. In both domains the governorship is listed with a headcount but no name."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamasaki_upper_p197_right",
   "sequence": 716,
   "domain_canonical": "山崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamasaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p197_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 197,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（山崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Yamasaki)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yamasaki domain yield and tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 368 carries the whole fascicle-5 fiscal entry for Yamasaki, a 10,000-koku domain in Harima holding thirty-nine villages. Its surveyed yield (kusadaka), newly reclaimed fields included, was 11,032.2817 koku against a nominal assessment (motodaka) of 10,000 koku. Regular tax took 5,397.4547 koku of rice and 1,029.3694 koku of soybeans (reckoned as 757.92153 koku of rice); miscellaneous tax took 454.8421 koku of rice, 82.3496 koku of soybeans, 21.42486 ryo in cash, and 5,133.17 monme of silk floss. Converting cash and kind at the five-year average price of eight ryo per koku of rice, the printed combined total of 6,680.115 koku reconciles exactly with the six components, and a warichu warns that the red-ink corrections printed beside the regular-tax figure are doubtful and were not added into that total."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamasaki_upper_p197_left",
   "sequence": 717,
   "domain_canonical": "山崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamasaki",
   "image": "images/upper_p197_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 197,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百六十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（山崎）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 5 (Yamasaki)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Households and population of Yamasaki domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the fascicle-5 household and population return for Yamasaki domain in Harima province: 2,421 households and a population of 10,232, split 5,284 male and 4,948 female. The 内 breakdown itemises 93 shizoku and 110 sotsu households together with 3 shrine households, 3 shugendo households, 14 temples and 4 hermitages; by persons it gives 420 shizoku (209 male, 211 female), 470 sotsu (240 male, 230 female), 27 shrine personnel, 71 temple and hermitage residents (56 monks and 15 women) and 10 shugendo practitioners. A 但 subtext records that the fifteen women are those of six Ikko-sect temples. A closing 右總計 restates the same 2,421 households and 10,232 persons, and a bracketed entry gives 19 shrines."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamasaki_lower_p206_right",
   "sequence": 718,
   "domain_canonical": "山崎藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山崎藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamasaki",
   "image": "images/lower_p206_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 206,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（山崎、柳生）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Table, Fascicle Nine (Yamasaki, Yagyu)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "domain officials and infantry companies",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 388 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle nine, the fascicle that records domain officeholders and military establishment. The right two-thirds of the leaf completes the Yamasaki (Harima) entry begun on page 387: eight personal names under the junior-councillor and acting-junior-councillor headings, then the domain's three infantry companies — the Jasei company at 64 men raised from shizoku, the Sekisui company at 72 men raised from sotsu, and the Enseki company at 62 men on the same basis, 198 men in all. The maru-marker for Yagyu (Yamato) then opens that domain's entry, which lists one governor with no name printed, one senior councillor (Oyamada Kazushige), two acting senior councillors (Matsuda Kagetake and Makita Yoshiyasu), and two junior councillors (Oyamada Kazuyoshi and Okamura Yoshitatsu). Every Yagyu personal name carries its holder's common name in a small-type gloss."
  },
  {
   "id": "yashima_upper_p198_left",
   "sequence": 719,
   "domain_canonical": "矢嶋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "矢島藩",
   "domain_en": "Yajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p198_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 198,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百七十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（矢島）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 5 (Yashima)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yashima assessed yield, land tax and miscellaneous tax",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 5 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō, printed page 371, showing the fiscal entry for Yashima Domain (Dewa) together with the tail of the preceding domain's block. Yashima's assessed yield (草高) is 16,133.88 koku across 47 villages; its regular land tax (正税) is 6,197.349 koku and its miscellaneous tax (雑税) 244 ryō 2 bu in gold plus 246 mon in eiraku cash, converted at 8 ryō per koku to 30.593 koku, giving a combined 6,227.942 koku. An editor's note flags the next five lines as marginal additions to the manuscript; three of them appear here, giving a base rice tax (本途米) of 4,443.491 koku and a subtotal (此計) of 5,865.408 koku. To the right of the ○矢島藩 marker the previous domain's block closes with 188 sotsu-rank retainers (116 male, 72 female), 21 temple residents (all monks), no shrine personnel, and a governor's household of two."
  },
  {
   "id": "yajima_upper_p199_right",
   "sequence": 720,
   "domain_canonical": "矢嶋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "矢島藩",
   "domain_en": "Yajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p199_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 199,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（矢島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Survey, Fascicle 5 (Yajima)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Households, population and status counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 372 continues the fascicle-5 return for Yajima domain in Dewa; the ○矢島藩 marker itself stands on the facing page 371, so every column here belongs to Yajima. Two rice-tax lines close the revenue list carried over from that page: surcharge, corvée and horse-service rice (口米・夫米・馬役米) at 251.47018 koku, and a bracketed subtotal 此計 of 331.941 koku. The household return gives 3,031 households in all, itemizing 109 shizoku, 117 sotsu, 45 shrine-family and 16 temple-and-hermitage households plus one jail-warden house and one eta household, with 415 shrines listed 算外, outside the count. Population is 15,280 (8,123 male, 7,157 female), of whom 447 are shizoku, 324 sotsu, 248 shrine personnel and 40 temple residents (36 monks and 4 women)."
  },
  {
   "id": "yajima_lower_p206_left",
   "sequence": 721,
   "domain_canonical": "矢嶋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "矢島藩",
   "domain_en": "Yajima",
   "image": "images/lower_p206_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 206,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（矢島、山上）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 9 (Yajima, Yamagami) — outer-margin running header / provenance",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Yajima domain's senior officials, with the troop line left unrecorded",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 389 of Fascicle 9, the officials fascicle of the 1870 Hansei ichiran. The rightmost column, 兵隊未詳 (\"troops not ascertained\"), stands to the right of the ○矢島藩 marker and therefore closes the previous domain's entry, that of Yagyū (柳生藩), whose officials run on the facing leaf, printed page 388. Yajima domain (Ugo province, Ikoma house) then lists a governorship (知事) with neither a number nor an incumbent recorded, one 大参事, three 権大参事, five 少参事 (printed 一人 with a small-type correction 五人 beside it, and five names follow), and four 権少参事 for which no number was printed at all, thirteen named officials in total, closing with 兵隊未詳 for its own military strength. The ○山上藩 marker at the far left opens Yamagami domain, whose figures begin on the next leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsushiro_upper_p204_left",
   "sequence": 722,
   "domain_canonical": "松代藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松代藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsushiro",
   "image": "images/upper_p204_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 204,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松代）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Matsushiro)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsushiro assessed yield and tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the entry for 松代藩 (Matsushiro, Shinano) with the maru-marker ○松代藩 and records the domain's assessed and actual yields. The nominal assessment (草高) is 123,570.02 koku; regular land tax in rice is 37,123.0457 koku and miscellaneous taxes 7,493.105 koku, of which 5,895.9823 koku is the rice equivalent of 47,167.8584 kanmon in cash — the gloss 石八兩立 sets the conversion at eight ryō the koku, and 47,167.8584 ÷ 8 reproduces the rice figure exactly. Those three figures sum precisely to the bracketed total actual rice (現米合) of 50,512.133 koku. Under 外 (\"besides\") the page adds 688.3269 koku for the shrines of Hachiman, Togakushi and Iizuna together with Zenkōji and twenty-eight other temples, and a further 533.82494 koku of petty-corvée and sundry tax money, equal to 4,270.5995 kanmon at the same eight-to-one rate; the closing combined figure for actual, deducted and shrine-temple yield is 55,030.10827 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsushiro_upper_p205_right",
   "sequence": 723,
   "domain_canonical": "松代藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松代藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsushiro",
   "image": "images/upper_p205_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 205,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（松代）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Table 5 (Matsushiro)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the household and population returns of Matsushiro Domain from fascicle 5 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, with no maru-marker anywhere on the page: it is the interior of a block already running. The domain reports 31,381 households in all, and the 内 breakdown that follows itemises only the specially classified ones — 436 samurai, 268 quasi-samurai and 1,679 sotsu households; 271 temples, 769 temple halls, 157 shugendo practitioners, 96 Shinto priestly houses, 2 miko, and 769 households of Buddhist hall-keepers, nuns and dōshin; 41 masterless samurai, 36 doctors, 307 outcaste households, and 227 commoner households renting row-house dwellings inside the domain. The population is 148,669, split 74,249 male and 74,420 female, of whom 2,145 are samurai and 1,320 quasi-samurai. Both the total population and the quasi-samurai figure reconcile exactly with their male and female components; the samurai male figure, printed 千十八 (1,018), falls 100 short of what the printed total of 2,145 and the female figure of 1,027 require, and appears to have lost a 百 in the source."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsushiro_upper_p205_left",
   "sequence": 724,
   "domain_canonical": "松代藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松代藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsushiro",
   "image": "images/upper_p205_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 205,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（松代）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran Table, Fascicle 5 (Matsushiro)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsushiro status-group and religious population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Matsushiro Domain's fascicle-5 return and records its non-peasant status groups, each given as a total with a male/female breakdown under the 内 marker. The largest entry is the sotsu retainer class at 6,778 (3,473 men, 3,305 women); the outcaste categories follow at 1,853 eta (953 men, 900 women) and 129 hinin (60 men, 69 women), with 43 persons recorded as leprous. Religious and professional groups are smaller: 827 Shugendo practitioners, 762 persons attached to temples, 535 in Shinto priestly households, 446 masterless samurai, 187 physicians, 179 Buddhist clergy (92 dōshin, 87 nuns), 797 commoners renting row-house lodgings inside the domain, and 2 shrine maidens. The leaf closes with 4 districts and the note that shrines were not ascertained; a bracketed editorial note records that the eta, hinin and leprosy lines were written outside the ruled frame of the original manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsushiro_upper_p206_right",
   "sequence": 725,
   "domain_canonical": "松代藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松代藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsushiro",
   "image": "images/upper_p206_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 206,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松代）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran Table, Fascicle 5 (Matsushiro)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsushiro villages and towns, governor's household, and the domain's entrusted-land (御預り地) tax and population account",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes Matsushiro Domain's own fascicle-5 entry — 251 villages, 8 towns (with a note that 41 kumi lie outside the towns), and a governor's household of 6 (2 male, 4 female) — and then opens, at the maru-marker ○松代藩御預り地, a separate account for the lands held by Matsushiro in trust. Those entrusted lands are assessed at a 草高 of 20,645.6548 koku, yielding 4,941.709 koku of regular land tax in hulled rice, 51.288 koku of miscellaneous rice dues, and 93 kan 84 mon 1 bun of eiraku cash, both cash and rice dues itemised as mitori, komonari, takagakarimono and sundry levies. The entrusted territory holds 4,114 households and 17,895 people (8,867 male, 9,028 female), with a partial occupational breakdown of 5 Shinto priestly houses, 14 physicians, 75 temples, 73 eta households, 18 Shugendo practitioners and 48 Buddhist chapels. Male and female counts sum exactly to the printed population total, and the governor's-household split likewise reconciles."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsushiro_lower_p209_right",
   "sequence": 726,
   "domain_canonical": "松代藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松代藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsushiro",
   "image": "images/lower_p209_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 209,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（松代）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 9 (Matsushiro)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 9 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, covering domain officials and armed forces. The page opens with the tail of the preceding domain, Iyo-Matsuyama, whose 權少參事 (acting junior councillors) are named here — Inoue Shōzaemon, Yamamoto Shinzaemon and Tsuchiya Yashichirō — printed to the right of the next domain's marker. The ○松代藩 marker then begins Matsushiro, which reports one governor (chiji, unnamed), one senior councillor (Sanada Ōzan), five acting senior councillors (Kambara Yōsui, Akazawa Rankei, Kawahara Hitoshi, Ōkuma Tadashi, Iwasaki Bō) and three junior councillors (Tamagawa Chōfu, Kanai Reisui, Suzuki Yō). Its army is 13 infantry companies — 2 of shizoku and 11 of sotsu — mustering 120 and 660 men respectively, plus 130 officers and staff, for the 910 total that the survey completes on the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "maebashi_upper_p206_left",
   "sequence": 727,
   "domain_canonical": "前橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "前橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Maebashi",
   "image": "images/upper_p206_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 206,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（前橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 5 (Maebashi)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Maebashi opening: assessed yield and rice tax",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of the p.206 opening (printed page 387) finishes the block for 松代藩御預り地, the entrusted lands held in custody by Matsushiro domain, whose marker and totals print on the facing right-hand page, and then opens the block for 前橋藩 (Maebashi). Right of the ○前橋藩 marker the sheet completes the entrusted lands' population breakdown under a stranded 内: Shinto priests 23 (12 male, 11 female), yamabushi 64 (34/30), physicians 72 (36/36), temple clergy 226 (151/75), Buddhist religious 23 (14 dōshin, 9 nuns) and eta 468 (239/229), with the shrine count entered as 不詳 (not known), 2 districts and 52 villages. Left of the marker Maebashi's own entry begins with a 草高 of 217,709.03384 koku, annotated \"including komidaka\" with a komidaka of 44,124.71136 koku lying within Maebashi, Hitachi, Matsuyama and Ōmi. The collator flags the next six lines as a marginal insertion: the main text is the first-month 1870 survey, but the tenth-month survey of the same year gives a 物成 (rice tax actually taken) of 51,884.54411 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "maebashi_upper_p207_right",
   "sequence": 728,
   "domain_canonical": "前橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "前橋",
   "domain_en": "Maebashi",
   "image": "images/upper_p207_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 207,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百八十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（前橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Maebashi)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Maebashi land tax, miscellaneous taxes, and shrine/temple lands",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation page of the fascicle-five entry for Maebashi Domain in Kōzuke, carrying no domain marker of its own; the running header names Maebashi and every column belongs to it. The regular land tax is recorded as 44,847.72403 koku of rice together with 20,525,937.985 mon of ei-cash, with a marginal note putting the average rate on assessed yield at roughly 32.38 percent. Miscellaneous taxes come to 417 ryō 1 bu in gold and 80,800 mon in copper cash, drawn from holdings in Kōzuke and Musashi, and a note warns that these amounts differ from year to year. Vermilion-seal shrine and temple lands total 1,440.1 koku, held by 10 shrines and 110 temple buildings across Kōzuke, Shimotsuke, Hitachi, Ōmi and Musashi, and split internally into 141 koku of shrine land and 1,299.1 koku of temple land; the domain counted 652 Shinto shrines in all."
  },
  {
   "id": "maebashi_upper_p207_left",
   "sequence": 729,
   "domain_canonical": "前橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "前橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Maebashi",
   "image": "images/upper_p207_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 207,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（前橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Table Five (Maebashi)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status, Maebashi domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Maebashi (前橋藩) entry in fascicle five of the 1870 Hansei ichiran; it carries no maru-marker, so all twenty-nine printed elements belong to Maebashi, whose marker stands on the preceding leaf. The household block gives 33,840 households, with a marginal note that shizoku and sotsu households are excluded, plus 652 shrines; under \"of which\" it lists 223 shrine-priest and shugendō households, 696 temples and 2 eta households, states that no shizoku household figure exists, and prints the sotsu heading with no figure beside it. The population block gives 174,239 persons (88,043 male, 86,196 female), subdivided into shizoku 4,656 (2,315 M / 2,341 F), sotsu 5,506 (2,774 / 2,732), shrine-priest and shugendō 808 (453 / 355), temple residents 711 (654 / 57), and eta 10 (6 / 4). Every male-plus-female pair sums exactly to its stated total, and the printed book page is 389."
  },
  {
   "id": "maebashi_lower_p209_left",
   "sequence": 730,
   "domain_canonical": "前橋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "前橋藩",
   "domain_en": "Maebashi",
   "image": "images/lower_p209_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 209,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（前橋）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey, Fascicle 9 (Maebashi) — outer-margin running header / provenance",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the fascicle-9 entry for Matsushiro (松代藩) and opens the entry for Maebashi (前橋藩). To the right of the ○前橋藩 marker, Matsushiro's military tally ends with a grand total of 910 men, a note that artillery troops are at present lacking (砲兵今闕), and 53 cannon; the lower band carries the rank heading 權少參事 followed by seven acting junior councillors — Takano Hiroma, Ichiba Genshichirō, Kishi Zenpachi, Kitazawa Kangaku, Kusama Ichiro, Okano Keiichirō and Satō Miyokichi. Left of the marker, Maebashi reports one governor, one senior councillor, one acting senior councillor and one junior councillor, then opens its military block with 1,378 troops and 208 officers and staff. The printed page number is 395."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsumoto_upper_p208_right",
   "sequence": 731,
   "domain_canonical": "松本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松本藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsumoto",
   "image": "images/upper_p208_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 208,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松本）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle Five (Matsumoto)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsumoto domain: land assessment and tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the fascicle-5 block for Matsumoto domain (松本藩) in Shinano province, which held 249 villages — 70 in Chikuma district and 179 in Azumi. Against a nominal motodaka of 60,000 koku the survey records an assessed gross yield (草高) of 97,522.6591 koku, a figure the printed note says already folds in komidaka and new-field yield. Regular land tax took 35,112.4499 koku of rice, about 36 percent of that gross, with a further 1,547.9771 koku of rice, 1,674 ryō 1 bu 3 shu in gold and 358.55 mon in ei-cash entered as miscellaneous tax, plus 19,036.6 bundles of straw and 906.28 bales of rice bran collected in kind. The largest cash item is the tax on miscellaneous goods at 6,456 ryō 3 bu 1 rin, recorded beside a combined 861.86 mon of ei-cash gathered from the villages of the two districts."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsumoto_upper_p208_left",
   "sequence": 732,
   "domain_canonical": "松本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松本藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsumoto",
   "image": "images/upper_p208_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 208,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松本）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey, Fascicle 5 (Matsumoto)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsumoto domain: product tax, shrine-temple land, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Matsumoto domain return begun on the facing page (book page 390), where the ○松本藩 marker and its 元高 of 60,000 koku print. It closes the miscellaneous product-tax group with a copper-cash item of 446 kan 74 mon (446,074 mon), then gives the product tax proper as a bracketed total of 773 ryō 3 bu 3 shu in gold together with 8 kan 970 mon 5 bu in ei-sen, noted as collected from the villages of Chikuma and Azumi districts. Shrine and temple land in those districts is entered at 362.5693 koku, and the return counts 163 temples and 62 shrine-priest households, with a marginal line that the 1928 collators reproduce in parentheses adding 236 shrines. Of 25,080 households it itemises 313 shizoku, 707 sotsuzoku, 62 shrine-priest, 163 temple, 27 eta and 10 hinin dwellings, and it puts the population at 122,472, of whom 63,259 are male and 59,213 female."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsumoto_lower_p210_right",
   "sequence": 733,
   "domain_canonical": "松本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松本藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsumoto",
   "image": "images/lower_p210_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 210,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（松本）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Matsumoto)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Matsumoto domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens Matsumoto domain's fascicle-9 entry with the maru-marker ○松本藩 and runs its administrative and military returns. The council is given as one governor (知事), one senior councillor (大參事, Inamura Ataka), two acting senior councillors (權大參事) against which three names are printed (Nonoyama Shirō, Tomonari Tanomo, Hayashi Kuramon), two junior councillors (少參事, one named: Nonoyama Yokurō), and an acting junior councillorship (權少參事) whose head-count is not printed although two names follow it (Maki Shigeru, Ayukai Mitsuru). Under the 兵隊 heading four troop lines are recorded: four companies of upper-grade infantry, 268 men, of whom 16 drummers and buglers; a garrison company, 75 men; one company of upper lower-grade infantry, 58 men, of whom 4 drummers and buglers; and seven companies of middle lower-grade infantry, 282 men, of whom 28 drummers and buglers — 683 men in all, with 48 drummers and buglers among them. The single column to the right of the marker, 喇叭手四拾五人 (45 buglers), is the tail of the preceding domain's military return, Maebashi, carried over from the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "marugame_upper_p209_right",
   "sequence": 734,
   "domain_canonical": "丸亀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丸龜藩",
   "domain_en": "Marugame",
   "image": "images/upper_p209_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 209,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（丸龜）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 5 (Marugame) — running provenance header in the outer margin",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsumoto's status-group population tail and the opening land and tax entries of Marugame",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes Matsumoto domain's status-group population return and opens Marugame domain's block in Fascicle 5 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. Matsumoto's seven counts, all printed to the right of the ○丸龜藩 marker, are 2,309 shizoku, 3,449 sotsu, 491 light foot-soldiers (輕卒), 359 shrine-household persons, 413 temple-and-hermitage residents, 140 eta and 412 hinin; the male/female breakdowns reconcile exactly for the first five, while the eta figures fall one person short of their total and the hinin breakdown (21 + 21) falls far short of the printed 412. Marugame's entries begin with a governor's household of ten persons and a base assessment (草高) of 51,512.5 koku, to which 30,641.383 koku of extended, newly reclaimed and re-surveyed land is added to give a combined assessment (合高) of 82,153.883 koku. The regular land tax is 32,145.7124 koku of rice, and the single miscellaneous tax recorded is 259.8 koku of salt."
  },
  {
   "id": "marugame_upper_p209_left",
   "sequence": 735,
   "domain_canonical": "丸亀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丸龜藩",
   "domain_en": "Marugame",
   "image": "images/upper_p209_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 209,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（丸龜）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Table (fascicle) 5 — Marugame",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Marugame households, population and miscellaneous taxes",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the fifth-fascicle return for Marugame domain in Sanuki province. It records 32,333 households in all, itemising 534 samurai (shizoku), 1,099 sotsu, 75 shrine-priest, 206 temple and 596 outcaste (eta) households, and a population of 135,101 persons split 70,510 male and 64,591 female, with the status groups standing at 1,517 samurai, 5,719 sotsu and 103 shrine-priest persons. Temple and shrine vermilion-seal and donated land is assessed at 541.9591 koku, of which 45 koku is vermilion-seal land proper. The miscellaneous-tax lines, whose heading stands on the facing page, close the entry at 43.4178 koku of rice and 6,666 ryo 3 bu 3 shu in gold plus 51 mon in copper cash."
  },
  {
   "id": "marugame_lower_p210_left",
   "sequence": 736,
   "domain_canonical": "丸亀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丸龜藩",
   "domain_en": "Marugame",
   "image": "images/lower_p210_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 210,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（丸龜）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 9 (Marugame)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Marugame officials and troop establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 9, printed page 397: the officials-and-troops return. The three columns to the right of the ○丸龜藩 marker close out Matsumoto's military return carried over from the facing leaf — a lower-grade garrison company of 193 men, two lower-grade lower companies of 96 men (8 of them drummers and buglers), and the grand total 總計九百八拾九人, 989 men. Marugame's own entry then opens with a governor (1), senior councillors (2), acting senior councillors (3), junior councillors (2) and an acting junior councillorship printed with no head-count, and names eight councillors: 本庄央 and 大塚夢鶴齋; 加藤修造, 大塚樸也 and 土肥大作; 大河内寬藏 and 新居彌學; 小野二郎. Marugame's 兵隊 section then begins with three rifle battalions (four companies to a battalion, 52 men and 12 officers and staff to a company) and three artillery batteries of 3 guns, 29 men and 5 staff each, nine guns in all; the remainder of the Marugame return runs onto the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "maizuru_upper_p210_right",
   "sequence": 737,
   "domain_canonical": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_en": "Maizuru",
   "image": "images/upper_p210_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 210,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Maizuru)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Marugame's closing survey fields and Maizuru's opening kokudaka block",
   "page_summary_en": "This page straddles two domains. To the right of the ○舞鶴藩 marker the survey finishes 丸亀藩 (Marugame, Sanuki): 718 temple personnel (568 monks plus 150 temple-household members, with the male/female split recorded as unknown), 2,697 eta (1,373 male, 1,324 female), holdings in three provinces (Sanuki, Harima and part of Ōmi) across 8 districts and 126 villages, 178 shrines, a governor's household of 3, and a nil return for warships. Left of the marker 舞鶴藩 (Maizuru, Tango) begins: an assessed 草高 of 35,000 koku plus 911.1377 koku of newly opened paddy and upland, giving a combined 合高 of 35,911.1377 koku. Its 正租 rice tax is 21,132.13098 koku, 58.8 percent of the combined assessment. Every component group printed on the page reconciles with its printed total."
  },
  {
   "id": "maizuru_upper_p210_left",
   "sequence": 738,
   "domain_canonical": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴",
   "domain_en": "Maizuru",
   "image": "images/upper_p210_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 210,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Table Five (Maizuru)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Maizuru domain: miscellaneous taxes, households, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the closing part of Maizuru domain's fascicle-five return in the Hansei ichiran; the domain's maru-marker stands on an earlier page, and the fold-margin header prints 藩制一覽表第五（舞鶴）above the book-page number 395. The revenue entries end the tax section with miscellaneous taxes of 214.9091 koku of rice and 882,070 mon in cash, followed by a parenthetical rice total of 21,347.04008 koku. The demographic entries record 10,245 households in all, of which 298 shizoku, 171 sotsu, 129 temple and yamabushi establishments, 2 shrine-family houses, and 150 outcast households, and 49,111 people, comprising 24,656 males and 24,455 females. Within that population the page itemizes 1,710 shizoku (814 male, 896 female), 670 sotsu (384 male, 286 female), 10 shrine-family members (4 male, 6 female), and 380 persons in temple and yamabushi households (241 monks plus 139 family members and servants)."
  },
  {
   "id": "maizuru_lower_p211_right",
   "sequence": 739,
   "domain_canonical": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_en": "Maizuru",
   "image": "images/lower_p211_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 211,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Maizuru)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Maizuru domain officials and troop strength, with Marugame's military overflow",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 398 of fascicle 9 opens the Maizuru (Tango) entry at the ○舞鶴藩 marker. The three columns standing to the right of that marker are still Marugame's, its military listing having run over from the previous page: 150 troop-attached staff (50 to each of its three rifle battalions), a garrison battalion (留守隊一大隊) built from six 52-man platoons, and that battalion's 72 unit officers. Maizuru itself records one governor, 2 senior councillors, 3 acting senior councillors and 6 junior councillors, with eleven appointees named below; the junior-councillor column prints 七人 in full-size type with a smaller 六人 inserted beside it, and the six names listed show the smaller figure to be the operative one, while no name at all is printed for the governor. Its army is entered as 藩兵三百二十人, divided 士分二百三人 and 卒百拾七人 (203 + 117 = 320)."
  },
  {
   "id": "maruoka_upper_p211_right",
   "sequence": 740,
   "domain_canonical": "丸岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丸岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Maruoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p211_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 211,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（丸岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Table Five (Maruoka)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Maruoka domain's opening entry — yield and taxes — after the tail of Maizuru's returns",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of Hansei ichiran fascicle 5 closes out Maizuru domain and opens the block for Maruoka domain in Echizen. Right of the maru-marker, Maizuru reports 123 villages, 511 shrines, no warships, no record of the governor's household, an outcaste population of 852 (434 male, 418 female), and a bracketed supplementary entry for Ashida Yoemon, a holder of newly reclaimed land ranked with domain samurai, whose household numbered 80 (39 male, 41 female). The marker ○丸岡藩 assigns Maruoka an original assessment of 50,000 koku over 77 villages (74 in Sakai district, 1 in Yoshida, 2 in Nanjō), against a surveyed yield of 50,253.4209 koku, regular land tax of 17,006.14583 koku of rice measured in Kyoto masu, and miscellaneous taxes of 639.2173 koku plus 1,147 ryō and 2,981 mon. The printed totals of 17,645.36313 koku and the same cash sum reconcile exactly with those components."
  },
  {
   "id": "marugaoka_upper_p211_left",
   "sequence": 741,
   "domain_canonical": "丸岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丸岡",
   "domain_en": "Maruoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p211_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 211,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（丸岡",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, Fascicle 5 — Marugaoka section (running header, provenance)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Marugaoka households, status breakdown, population, and a marginal kokudaka correction",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the tail of the Marugaoka (丸岡藩) return in Fascicle 5 of the 1869-70 Dajōkan domain survey. A five-line note that the 1928 editor flags as written in the manuscript's margin corrects the domain's assessment: 816.3122 koku had been lost to river washout and permanent ruin, 81.3272 koku of that has since been brought back into cultivation and is deducted, leaving a remaining assessed kokudaka (殘正高) of 49,518.4359 koku — which implies a gross 草高 of 50,253.4209 koku, close to Marugaoka's nominal 50,000. The domain returns 5,305 households in total, of which it itemises 249 shizoku, 447 sotsu, 7 Shinto-priest, 64 temple (including 7 sub-temples), 3 eta, 22 hinin and 3 Shugendō households, leaving commoner households unenumerated. Population is 22,900, split 11,342 male and 11,558 female. The printed book-page number is 397."
  },
  {
   "id": "maruoka_upper_p212_right",
   "sequence": 742,
   "domain_canonical": "丸岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丸岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Maruoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p212_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 212,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Systems, Fascicle Five (Matsuo)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Maruoka status-group population; Matsuo assessed yield",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand leaf closes the fascicle-5 entry for Maruoka Domain (Echizen) and opens the entry for Matsuo Domain (Kazusa) at the ○松尾藩 marker. Maruoka's status-group counts are 962 shizoku (459 male, 503 female), 1,454 sotsuzoku (707 male, 747 female), 21 Shinto priests, 241 temple residents (145 monks and 96 women, 16 of the women nuns), 8 Shugendo practitioners, 18 eta and 83 hinin, together with 104 shrines and a governor's household of 8; the domain declares that it holds no warships. Left of the marker, Matsuo's nominal assessed yield (kusadaka) is entered as 53,427.56063 koku. A note appended below states that this is the figure as formally handed over and that the previous survey had recorded 53,428.90073 koku, a difference of 1.3401 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "maruoka_lower_p211_left",
   "sequence": 743,
   "domain_canonical": "丸岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "丸岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Maruoka",
   "image": "images/lower_p211_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 211,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（丸岡、松尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey, Fascicle 9 (Maruoka, Matsuo) — outer-margin running header, provenance only",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Maruoka domain officials roster and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 page carrying the domain officials roster and the military-strength block. To the right of the ○丸岡藩 marker the previous domain's list runs on: Maizuru's 權少參事 heading with three appointees (安川久米五郎, 內海雄右衞門, 恒川竹香), the count itself not printed. Maruoka's own block gives 知事 一人 (the count printed but no name), 大參事 一人 (有馬由己), 權大參事 二人 (有馬峻太郎, 新名與太郎), 少參事 二人 (有馬天然, 皆吉安宅), and 權少參事 with no printed count but four names (近藤浪江, 有馬將作, 草野正記, 馬場松彥) — nine councillors in all. Its forces are six infantry companies of 32 men and 10 officers each and two artillery sections of 12 men and 3 officers each, that is 192 and 24 rank-and-file, or 252 and 30 counting officers. The page closes at the left with the ○松尾藩 marker, glossed 改柴山 because Matsuo is the renamed Shibayama domain, and the printed page number 三百九十九 (399) in the outer margin."
  },
  {
   "id": "mashima_upper_p213_left",
   "sequence": 744,
   "domain_canonical": "眞島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "眞島藩",
   "domain_en": "Mashima",
   "image": "images/upper_p213_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 213,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（眞島）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 5 (Mashima)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Mashima Domain kokudaka and tax revenue; tail of Matsuo Domain's population and shrine counts",
   "page_summary_en": "The leaf closes Matsuo Domain's demographic entries and opens the Mashima Domain block, the maru-marker ○眞島藩 falling about two-thirds of the way across. Matsuo's remaining figures are 77 shrines, 10 shugendō practitioners (5 male, 5 female), 12 eta (5 male, 7 female), 201 banhinin (110 male, 91 female), and a note that the governor's family is not recorded. Mashima's territory is 96 villages in Mashima District and 1 village in Ōba District of Mimasaka Province, 97 villages across 2 districts; its nominal assessment (kusadaka) is 30,809.103 koku, within which komidaka accounts for 7,741.649 koku and newly reclaimed paddy 67.454 koku. Regular land tax is 10,547.866 koku and miscellaneous tax 1,384.74148 koku (1,334.24904 koku in rice plus 252 ryō 462 mon 2 bu 5 mō in cash, worth 50.49244 koku), together the 11,932.60748 koku total rice of the 1869 survey, while a parallel 1871 return gives the same combined total as 11,932.6-odd koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "mashima_upper_p214_right",
   "sequence": 745,
   "domain_canonical": "眞島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "眞島藩",
   "domain_en": "Mashima",
   "image": "images/upper_p214_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 214,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（眞島）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Mashima)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "households, population and religious establishments",
   "page_summary_en": "This page-half carries the fascicle-5 return for Mashima domain: household and population totals with their privileged-status and religious sub-counts. The domain reports 5,795 households and 26,240 people, split 13,808 male and 12,432 female. Within those totals it enumerates 200 shizoku and quasi-shizoku households (791 people), 189 sotsu households (478 people), 38 Shinto-priest households (190 people), 37 temples (75 people) and 10 Shugendo households (22 people), and it counts 633 shrines. The governor's own family is entered as 不記, not recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "mashima_lower_p212_right",
   "sequence": 746,
   "domain_canonical": "眞島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "眞島藩",
   "domain_en": "Mashima",
   "image": "images/lower_p212_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 212,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（眞島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview Table, Fascicle 9 (Mashima)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the fascicle-9 page on which Mashima domain (Mimasaka) opens, marked by the circle-marker ○眞島藩 two-thirds of the way across the sheet. The six columns to the right of that marker still belong to Matsuo domain, the entry that precedes it: one governor, three senior councillors, six acting senior councillors, six junior councillors, and troops of 313 men, with a smaller-type note stating that the figure covers the unit commander and every rank below him down to the common soldiers. Mashima's own establishment follows to the left of the marker — one governor, two senior councillors, one acting senior councillor, and five junior councillors — and ten officials are named in two right-to-left lines in the lower half of the page. The printed count of acting senior councillors is corrected in the gutter by a smaller-type 二人, and the ten names bear that correction out: five names in the first line answer to the governor, the senior councillors and the acting senior councillors, and five in the second line to the junior councillors. The printed page number in the margin is 四百 (400)."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsumine_upper_p214_left",
   "sequence": 747,
   "domain_canonical": "松嶺藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松嶺藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsumine",
   "image": "images/upper_p214_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 214,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松嶺）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Table (fascicle) 5 — (Matsumine)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsumine domain: assessed yield, land and miscellaneous taxes, retainer households, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 403 of fascicle 5 of the Hansei ichiran gives the fiscal and household return of Matsumine domain (松嶺藩) in Dewa. Its base assessment (本高) is 22,500 koku and its gross assessed yield (草高) 26,800.15744 koku, drawn from Akumi district in Ugo province, Tagawa and Murayama districts in Uzen, and Seta district in Kōzuke, with the newly-reclaimed-field addition folded in. Regular land tax delivered 9,297.60741 koku of rice and 683.68918 koku of soybeans, while miscellaneous taxes came to 969.18538 koku together with 819 ryō 3 bu 2 shu in gold, 5.249 monme of silver, 3.12 monme of placer gold and 33.21 monme of raw silk. The domain returned 118 shizoku and 336 sotsu households, seven shrines and nine temples; the single parenthesised column at the far right, （船艦不所持）, closes the preceding Mashima (眞島藩) entry rather than opening Matsumine's."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsumine_lower_p212_left",
   "sequence": 748,
   "domain_canonical": "松嶺藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松嶺藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsumine",
   "image": "images/lower_p212_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 212,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（松嶺）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei Ichiran-hyo (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 9 — outer-margin running header keyed to Matsumine",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Matsumine domain office roster and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of fascicle 9 (printed book page 401) opens with the trailing military line of the preceding domain block: 兵隊 百八拾七人, 187 troops, which belongs to Mashima Domain because it is printed to the right of the ○松嶺藩 maru-marker. Everything left of that marker is Matsumine Domain in Dewa, the 22,500-koku Sakai branch house of Shonai: a governorship (知事) with one holder, a senior councillorship (大參事) with no figure returned, three acting senior councillors (權大參事 三人), six junior councillors (少參事 六人), and an acting junior councillorship (權少參事) likewise without a printed count. Eleven officeholders are named in the two lower registers and the printed counts tally exactly with them — three under 權大參事 (Orita Seiemon, Abe Magosaburo, Kobanawa Taroto) and six under 少參事 (Hayashi Shingoemon, Ota Genshichi, Taguchi Genpachiro, Suzuki Shiroemon, Kitago Koemon, Suzuki Enemon) — while the two men entered under 權少參事 (Tsukada Kan, Togano Hachiemon) stand without a figure and the 知事 and 大參事 columns carry no name at all. The page closes with Matsumine's own military line, 兵隊 百五十四人, 154 troops."
  },
  {
   "id": "moriyama_upper_p215_right",
   "sequence": 749,
   "domain_canonical": "守山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "守山藩",
   "domain_en": "Moriyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p215_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 215,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（守山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table (藩制一覽表), Fascicle 5 — Moriyama (守山) section; running header, printed provenance for the page",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "close of Matsumine's population return and the opening land and tax figures for Moriyama",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand third of this fascicle-5 page closes the entry for Matsumine domain (松嶺藩): 339 shizoku and 735 sotsu, both returned without a male/female split, no aggregate population figure, no count of administered commoner households (\"not in the original manuscript\"), no foreign personnel, no warships, and no record of the governor's family. The maru-marker ○守山藩 then opens Moriyama domain, noting that it has been renamed Matsukawa (松川ト改) and that its 26 villages lie at Moriyama in Iwaki and Natsumi in Hitachi. Moriyama's assessed nominal yield (草高) is 29,322.31933 koku, stated to include komidaka and the revised new-field assessment, against which the regular tax is 5,673.2372 koku of rice plus 1,622 ryō 3 bu 1 shu in cash. The kusadaka and cash-tax readings both differ from the project's MASTER extraction, which records 29,320.21933 koku and 1,620 ryō; the printed page reads 貳拾貳 in each case."
  },
  {
   "id": "moriyama_upper_p215_left",
   "sequence": 750,
   "domain_canonical": "守山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "守山藩",
   "domain_en": "Moriyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p215_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 215,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（守山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Table 5 (Moriyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Moriyama domain: closing tax entries, shrine and temple land, households, shrines, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso (printed page 405) completes the fascicle-5 return for Moriyama domain, a Mito cadet house holding land in Mutsu and Hitachi whose entry opens with the ○守山藩 marker on the facing recto. It closes the regular land tax with an eisen line of 843.72 mon, then records the miscellaneous levies — 195.691 koku of rice and 814 ryō 2 shu in gold plus 576 mon in copper — and 424.27486 koku of shrine and temple land, glossed in a warichu as including newly opened paddy re-registered to the Moriyama Shrine holding. The household return totals 3,289 houses, of which 276 are samurai, 190 sotsu, 29 shrine servants, 81 temples, 8 shugendō practitioners and 6 banhinin, the unlisted balance of 2,699 being commoner houses; 137 shrines are counted separately. The population is 17,673 (9,147 male, 8,526 female), of whom 809 are samurai (444 male, 365 female); both splits sum exactly to their printed totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "moriyama_upper_p216_right",
   "sequence": 751,
   "domain_canonical": "守山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "守山藩",
   "domain_en": "Moriyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p216_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 216,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（敦賀）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Regulations Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — running head \"Tsuruga\" (敦賀); the page actually carries the tail of Moriyama's (守山藩) status-group population returns and the opening of Tsuruga's (敦賀藩) land assessment.",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "status-group population tail of one domain, then the next domain's opening land assessment",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of this page close out Moriyama domain's (守山藩) fascicle-5 population return: 373 lower retainers (sotsu; 258 male, 115 female), 133 shrine personnel (80 male, 53 female), 42 temple residents (sexes explicitly \"not separated\"), 36 Shugendō ascetics (12 male, 24 female), and 60 ban-hinin guard-outcastes (37 male, 23 female). Two bracketed absence notes follow: the governor's family is \"not recorded\" and the domain has no warships. The ○敦賀藩 marker then opens Tsuruga domain, annotated \"changed to Mariyama\" and \"originally 10,000 koku\", with territory in Tsuruga and Nanjō districts of Echizen and part of Takashima district in Ōmi. Tsuruga's assessed yield (草高) is 11,275.26442 koku, stated to include the supplementary assessment and new fields; the collator notes that the eight lines that follow — original assessment 10,000 koku, supplementary assessment (込高) 1,105.45592 koku, 1,326.5053 koku of land exchanged for a former Awa-Province holding, and a note that the Echizen portion is omitted as unsurveyed — were originally written in vermilion in the margin."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsukawa_lower_p213_right",
   "sequence": 752,
   "domain_canonical": "守山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松川藩",
   "domain_en": "Moriyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p213_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 213,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（松川、鞠山）",
   "page_header_en": "Tabular Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Matsukawa, Mariyama)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officeholders and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "Folio 402 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, fascicle 9, the fascicle that records each domain's officeholders and its armed strength. The leaf opens Matsukawa Domain (Mutsu; the Tachibana house then seated there after its transfer from Miike) with a governor, one senior councillor, five provisional senior councillors and two junior councillors — nine officers in all — followed by a 兵隊 heading whose value column gives 133 heishi in the upper register and 136 heisotsu in the lower register of the same column, 269 men together. The ○鞠山藩 marker then opens Mariyama Domain, the 10,000-koku Sakai branch of Obama in Wakasa, with a governor, one senior councillor, two provisional senior councillors and three junior councillors; its own 兵隊 heading is the last printed column on the leaf and its troop figures run over onto folio 403, where 17 heishi and a 48-man heisotsu platoon appear. No appointee names print on this leaf, and no totals or internal splits appear that would require a sum check."
  },
  {
   "id": "moriyama_lower_p246_right",
   "sequence": 753,
   "domain_canonical": "守山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "守山藩",
   "domain_en": "Moriyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p246_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 246,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百六十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（守山、森）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 9 (Moriyama, Mori)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials, with Mori's military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 468 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle 9, opens the officials rosters of Moriyama (Mutsu) and Mori (Bungo). Moriyama returns twelve named officers: one daisanji (Sakaba Hikosuke), five gon-daisanji (Noguchi Katsuzo, Komuro Kan, Miura Taira, Okada Shinro, Kataoka Shichiroji), two shosanji (Shirato Seiji, Kataoka Hi), and four gon-shosanji (Kurabe Kuwasaku, Hanawa Jugoro, Seimiya Sohei, Mashiko Kongozaburo); two of the four office columns overflow leftward into unheaded continuation columns. Mori prints its senior post 正權大參事 with no incumbent at all, lists three shosanji (Murakami Hisashi, Kato Ryohei, Oshima Tange), and then gives its forces as three infantry platoons of forty rank-and-file plus one supervising officer each, together with one artillery company at the same complement, which comes to 164 men. A second, later return follows the military entry with a daisanji (Miyano Magoichi) and a gon-daisanji (Sakuma Sunao), and it runs on to the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "funai_upper_p222_left",
   "sequence": 754,
   "domain_canonical": "府内藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "府内",
   "domain_en": "Funai",
   "image": "images/upper_p222_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 222,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（府内）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Five (Funai)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Funai domain assessed yield, land-tax receipts and household count",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the entry for Funai domain (Bungo province, present-day Ōita) in fascicle five of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, and Funai is the only domain on the page. It records a gross assessed yield (kusadaka) of 26,422.3301 koku with newly opened paddy already counted in and no shrine or temple allowance, then four tax receipts: 12,720.895 koku of the regular land tax paid in rice, 51.623 koku commuted to 412,985.9 mon in ei-currency, 1,144.547 koku delivered as 2,173.053 koku of soybeans, and miscellaneous taxes of 1,940,993.15 mon worth 242.624 koku of rice. Those four sum exactly to the printed total rice figure of 14,159.689 koku, and both cash conversions run at 8,000 mon per koku. A bracketed block of five lines, which the 1928 editors note was written in vermilion in the original manuscript, deducts a permanent tenth-portion of 1,286.3961 koku and a current tenth-portion of 1,612.7813 koku from the gross yield to leave a remainder of exactly 23,523.1527 koku; the domain reports 7,370 households."
  },
  {
   "id": "funai_upper_p223_right",
   "sequence": 755,
   "domain_canonical": "府内藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "府内藩",
   "domain_en": "Funai",
   "image": "images/upper_p223_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 223,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（府内）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 5 (Funai)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status group",
   "page_summary_en": "A continuation leaf from the Funai domain entry in fascicle 5 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, carrying no domain marker of its own; the running header identifies the block as Funai. The right-hand half completes the household (戸) breakdown: 238 samurai households, 233 sotsu, 69 Shinto-priest, 125 temple-and-hermitage, 13 shugendo, 62 eta and 10 hinin households, 750 in all on this leaf. The left-hand half opens the population count at 33,323 persons, split 17,043 male and 16,280 female, then begins the status breakdown with 1,265 samurai, 1,068 sotsu, 312 Shinto-priest, 328 temple, 35 shugendo and 317 eta persons, each carrying its own male/female pair. Every sex split on the page sums exactly to its printed parent total, and the commoner and hinin population lines run on to the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "funai_upper_p223_left",
   "sequence": 756,
   "domain_canonical": "府内藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "府内藩",
   "domain_en": "Funai",
   "image": "images/upper_p223_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 223,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（府内）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 5 (Funai)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Funai domain: villages, shrines, governor's household, outcaste population, and the pasted land-tax slip",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the closing half of the Funai domain (Bungo province) entry in fascicle 5 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō. The right-hand columns give the domain's administrative and demographic tail: 1 district, 97 villages, 114 shrines, no record of vessels, a governor's household of 3 persons (2 male, 1 female), and an outcaste (hinin) population of 72 persons (39 male, 33 female). The left two-thirds of the page is a 付箋 — a paper slip pasted onto the manuscript, its extent marked by a hooked rule — carrying the tax figures: regular land tax (正租) of 12,726.7667 koku of rice and 2,111.962 koku of soybeans, and miscellaneous taxes (雜税) of 126 ryō 43.8 mon plus 445.479 koku of rice and 100.991 koku of soybeans under the fixed levy (小物成定納), with a further 455 ryō 959.7 mon under the non-fixed levy (小物成不定納). A note on the slip records that the month and year of the accounting period are not distinguished."
  },
  {
   "id": "funai_lower_p216_right",
   "sequence": 757,
   "domain_canonical": "府内藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福知山藩",
   "domain_en": "Funai",
   "image": "images/lower_p216_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 216,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（福知山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey Table, ninth fascicle (Fukuchiyama)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials rosters and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "This recto is the join between two fascicle-9 entries. Reading right to left, the first columns close 府内藩 (Funai, Bungo): the headings 少參事 (three persons) and 權少參事 over seven named appointees, then the 兵隊 block recording 士族兵隊 二百二十壹人 (221 troops raised from the shizoku) and 卒族兵隊 百四十五人 (145 from the sotsu), 366 men in all. The ○福知山藩 marker then opens 福知山藩 (Fukuchiyama, Tanba), whose officials fill the rest of the sheet: 知事 一人 with no name printed beneath it, and 大參事, 權大參事, 少參事 and 權少參事 whose strengths are given only as 人員未詳 (\"number of personnel not known\") and 同上 (\"the same\"), with eight officers named below. The running header 藩制一覽表第九（福知山）and the folio number 四百八 (408) stand in the outer margin."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukue_upper_p225_right",
   "sequence": 758,
   "domain_canonical": "福江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福江藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukue",
   "image": "images/upper_p225_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 225,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福江）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Fukue)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukue domain: assessed yield, land and miscellaneous tax, household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the entry for Fukue domain (Gotō, Matsuura district, Hizen) in fascicle five of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, and prints its assessment and tax block. The assessed yield (kusadaka) stands at 22,360.426372 koku with the revision increase included; a bracketed figure to its right, flagged by the editor as coming from a slip of paper attached to the manuscript at this point, gives 19,375.956666 koku before that increase. Regular land tax is 8,485.197077 koku of rice plus 80 ryō 3 shu and 100 mon in cash, miscellaneous tax is 13,574 ryō 3 bu 2 shu plus 1,486 mon, and the combined total of 10,192.099714 koku reconciles with those components at the stated conversion of about eight yen to the koku. Households number 11,892, of which the page itemises 316 shizoku, 285 sotsu, 190 shrine houses, 45 temples, 2 shugen and 4 eta. The parenthetical governor's-household figure at the far right of the sheet stands to the right of the Fukue marker and belongs to the preceding domain, Fukuchiyama."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukue_upper_p225_left",
   "sequence": 759,
   "domain_canonical": "福江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福江藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukue",
   "image": "images/upper_p225_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 225,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福江）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Systems, Fascicle 5 (Fukue)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukue population by status, shrines, and attached-slip land and tax totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso continues the Fukue domain entry from the facing recto and carries no maru-marker, so every figure on it belongs to 福江藩. It gives a population of 62,294 (32,311 male, 29,983 female), broken down into 1,718 samurai (shizoku), 1,279 sotsu, 1,187 shrine personnel, 99 temple persons (\"all monks; no women\"), 23 eta, and 15 shugendō practitioners, followed by 40 shrines and a governor's household of 7 (4 male, 3 female). The three left-hand columns are bracketed under the label 符箋 (\"attached slip\") and give an assessed yield of 23,972.082431 koku, a rice land tax of 8,042.690762 koku, and miscellaneous taxes of 6,778 ryō 3 bu 2 shu in gold plus 1,768 mon in copper cash. The note beneath explains that these slip figures are the combined totals including the former fief of Gotō Jūnojō, which was afterwards handed over to Nagasaki Prefecture, the remainder standing as printed in the main text."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukue_lower_p216_left",
   "sequence": 760,
   "domain_canonical": "福江藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福江藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukue",
   "image": "images/lower_p216_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 216,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（福江、福本）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 9 (Fukue, Fukumoto)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and military strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 409 of Hansei ichiran fascicle 9 carries the tail of Fukuchiyama domain's return, the whole of Fukue domain's entry, and the opening of Fukumoto domain's entry. Fukuchiyama closes with one more official name, Sahara Kazen, and its military line of 94 heishi and 134 heisotsu (228 men). Fukue reports one governor, one senior councillor, three acting senior councillors and two junior councillors, and a force of 640 men; a double-column interlinear note breaks that force into 151 standing troops — two platoons built on forty-man squads, plus platoon officers, physicians, ordnance officers and artillery attachments — and 493 men of the assembled corps drawn from the coastal batteries and shore villages, figures that sum to 644 and so exceed the printed total by four. Fukumoto's block opens with one governor and one senior councillor, the latter named as Kanbe Yutaka."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukiage_upper_p227_right",
   "sequence": 761,
   "domain_canonical": "吹上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吹上藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukiage",
   "image": "images/upper_p227_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 227,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（吹上）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 5 (Fukiage)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukiage annual revenue totals and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the fascicle-5 (revenue) entry for Fukiage Domain, carrying the last itemised tax heads, the grand totals, and the household counts. The itemised heads printed here are soybeans 4 koku, gold 6 ryō 1 bu with silver 14 monme 4 fun 4 rin, eiraku cash 321 kan 379 mon 4 fun 4 rin, and copper cash 6 kan 174 mon, the last carried with a marginal note fixing the exchange at 10 kan of copper cash to 1 ryō of gold. The totals then run 3,422.07655 koku of rice (合米), an eiraku subtotal of 818 kan 777 monme 7 fun converted to 818 ryō 3 bu plus 10 monme 6 fun 6 rin of silver, a further 4 ryō with 6 monme 5 fun of silver, and a grand total of 825 ryō 3 bu with 8 monme 1 fun 6 rin of silver, alongside the 4 koku of soybeans restated. The population section records 1,473 households in all, of which 106 were shizoku and 70 sotsu."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukiage_upper_p227_left",
   "sequence": 762,
   "domain_canonical": "吹上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吹上",
   "domain_en": "Fukiage",
   "image": "images/upper_p227_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 227,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（吹上）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Fukiage)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukiage population by status group, with temples, shrines and the governor's household",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-five return for Fukiage Domain and gives its 1870 population accounts. The domain reports 6,826 people in all (3,436 male, 3,390 female), of whom 383 are samurai (士族), 166 are lower retainers (卒族), 50 belong to shrine-priest households, 73 live at temples and practice halls (including 20 monks), 186 are eta and 9 are hinin watchmen; every status figure reconciles exactly with its male-female breakdown. The household and institution counts are 8 shrine-priest dwellings, 43 temples and practice halls (3 of them practice halls, 20 temples without holdings), 56 eta houses, 2 hinin houses and 49 shrines, and the governor's own family numbers 4 (2 male, 2 female). A bracketed editorial slip (付箋) at the right margin records that the later survey supplied no itemised breakdown, so these figures follow the earlier survey."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukiage_lower_p217_right",
   "sequence": 763,
   "domain_canonical": "吹上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "吹上藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukiage",
   "image": "images/lower_p217_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 217,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（吹上）",
   "page_header_en": "Comparative Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Fukiage)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "A fascicle-9 page recording domain office-holders and military strength. Its right-hand third closes the entry for Fukumoto Domain, begun on the facing page: two acting senior councillors named Iwamoto Noriharu and Morioka Hayata, one junior councillor, and a force totalling 117 men, made up of the Soyo company (35), the Koyo company (67), and 15 gunners and bandsmen together. The maru-marker for Fukiage Domain then opens that domain's entry, which fills the rest of the sheet with its establishment alone: one governor, one senior councillor (Yasuda Yaemon), four acting senior councillors (Makino Shungo, Sasaki Tetsuemon, Tomioka Sareiji, Hirose Chojiro), and four junior councillors (Nakamura Chuzaemon, Miyake Shichiemon, Anzai Tomotaro, Hirata Bunzaemon) — nine of the ten declared posts named, the governor's seat left unnamed. No troop figures for Fukiage appear on this page."
  },
  {
   "id": "izumi_upper_p037_right",
   "sequence": 764,
   "domain_canonical": "泉藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "泉藩",
   "domain_en": "Izumi",
   "image": "images/upper_p037_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 37,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（泉）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 1 (Izumi)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Izumi domain opens: kokudaka, rice tax and household register (fascicle 1)",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 48 of fascicle 1 of the Hansei ichiran-hyō, the Dajōkan's 1869–70 domain survey. The right-hand third of the page closes out the previous domain, Ichinomiya (43 villages, 7 shrines, 55 temples, 2 hermitages and 1 hall; 13 outcaste households totalling 60 people; 47 soldiers), after which the maru-marker ○泉藩 opens the Izumi entry. Izumi reports a nominal kokudaka of 18,000 koku against an inclusive figure of 19,543.51775 koku with new-field re-surveys added, a rice tax of 4,550.24558 koku averaged over 1864–68 and 3,966.88085 koku averaged over the five years from Keiō 1 to Meiji 2, and miscellaneous cash taxes of 1,391 ryō 1 bu 1 shu plus 612 mon. The domain returns 2,049 households and a population of 9,603, with 209 shizoku and 51 sotsu; the household count for shizoku and sotsu is entered as 不詳, \"not known\", and the printed male and female figures (4,834 and 4,620) fall 149 short of the stated population total."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyoura_upper_p055_left",
   "sequence": 765,
   "domain_canonical": "豐浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyoura (Chōfu, Nagato province)",
   "image": "images/upper_p055_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 55,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（豐浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran Table, Fascicle 2 (Toyoura)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyama religious, outcaste and village counts; Toyoura kokudaka and land-tax rice",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of the leaf closes out Toyama Domain's fascicle-2 return: 26 shrine-priest households holding 181 people (127 men, 54 women, of whom 5 manservants and 18 maidservants); 409 temples (289 head temples and 121 sub-temples) housing 1,665 people (1,055 men and 610 women, including 1,015 monks and 76 nuns); 301 outcaste (穢多) households holding 1,434 people (698 men, 736 women); 1,070 shrines; and 487 villages. Two absence notes follow — the domain has no warships, and the governor's family is not recorded. Left of the maru-marker the Toyoura (Chōfu) entry opens with an assessed base of 50,000 koku, a surveyed 草高 of 124,063 koku and more including new-field increments, 23,901 koku of that allotted out of Toyoura district to Kiyosue, and a remainder of 100,972 koku; the regular land-tax rice, averaged over the five years 1864-1868, is 31,542 koku and more. The printed subtraction does not close (124,063 − 23,901 = 100,162, not 100,972), and the temple breakdown overshoots its own total by one, so both figures are recorded as printed rather than reconciled."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyoura_upper_p056_right",
   "sequence": 766,
   "domain_canonical": "豐浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐浦",
   "domain_en": "Toyoura (Chōfu, Nagato province)",
   "image": "images/upper_p056_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 56,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "八十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 2 (Toyoura)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Toyoura tax totals and household/population breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 86 of fascicle 2 continues the return for Toyoura (Chōfu) domain in Nagato; the leaf carries no maru-marker, so the whole page belongs to the domain named in the running header. It closes the revenue block with 9,875 kanmon of cash carried over from a field begun on the preceding leaf, 7,285 koku of miscellaneous tax rice paired with 81,830 kanmon of cash, and a combined current-rice figure of 39,972 koku, which the reprint's editorial note says was arrived at by converting the cash into rice. The demographic block then reports 17,126 households and 76,096 people (38,617 male and 37,478 female, one short of the printed total), of whom 1,931 households and 8,665 people were shizoku and sotsu. Two named sub-groups follow inside that figure: 426 shizoku households with 2,121 people, and 301 quasi-samurai (准士) households with 1,456 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "toyoura_upper_p056_left",
   "sequence": 767,
   "domain_canonical": "豐浦藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "豐浦藩",
   "domain_en": "Toyoura (Chōfu, Nagato province)",
   "image": "images/upper_p056_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 56,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "八十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（豐浦）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran (Survey of Domain Institutions), Fascicle 2 — (Toyoura)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Status-group household and population counts, shrine and village counts, transport vessel, governor's family",
   "page_summary_en": "The left-hand leaf of printed page 87 continues the fascicle-2 entry for Toyoura Domain (豐浦藩, the renamed Chofu branch of the Mori house in Nagato). No ○-marker appears anywhere on the leaf, so every column belongs to Toyoura, whose marker stands earlier in the entry on the facing leaf. The page completes the status-group census: 779 sotsu households holding 3,601 people (1,816 male, 1,785 female); 425 rear-vassal households whose population is printed as 4,487, although the male and female sub-counts of 750 and 737 add to only 1,487; 106 shrine-servant households with 464 people (233 male, 231 female); 373 temples with a clergy population of 804 (700 monks, 104 nuns), followed by a bracketed warichu giving 164 temple establishments and a resident population of 1,037 (680 monks, 253 women, 104 nuns) under an unlabelled leading figure 一二八; 98 eta households with 509 people (252 male, 257 female); and 91 hinin households with 461 people (218 male, 243 female). It closes with 373 shrines — the same figure the page prints for temples — a village count the source records only as シレス (unknown), one transport vessel of English build, and a governor's household of three (one male, two female). Every male-plus-female split on the leaf reconciles exactly except the rear-vassal population."
  },
  {
   "id": "tokuyama_upper_p058_right",
   "sequence": 768,
   "domain_canonical": "德山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "德山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tokuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p058_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 58,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（德山）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覽表), Fascicle 2 — Tokuyama (德山藩); the right of the leaf completes the entry for Toyohashi (豐橋藩)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "close of Toyohashi's religious, outcaste and village counts; the Tokuyama marker and kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the right-hand leaf of printed page 90 in fascicle 2 of the 1870 domain survey, and it holds the end of one domain's entry and the start of another. The right two-thirds still belongs to Toyohashi (豐橋藩), whose entry opened two leaves earlier: it closes out the religious and outcaste sections with 110 shrine-priest households holding 512 people (250 male, 262 female), 380 temples, 22 shugendō establishments, 6 hall-keeper posts and 2 onmyōji households accounting for 904 people between them (790 male, 114 female), and 270 eta and banta households holding 1,129 people (611 male, 518 female), then 260 villages, a shrine count recorded only as \"not known\" (シレス), a governor's household of 4, and warships \"not recorded.\" An editorial note in the middle of the leaf flags that the original manuscript put the clerical population at 884, and that the compilers printed 904 instead because that is what the male and female sub-totals add to. The ○德山藩 marker then opens Tokuyama Domain toward the left edge, giving a base assessment (本高) of 40,010 koku and an assessed yield (草高) of 69,054 koku plus a fraction, the latter stated to include newly opened fields — a difference of 29,044 koku — with a further note that the tax figures continuing on the facing leaf are five-year averages for 1864 through 1868."
  },
  {
   "id": "tokuyama_upper_p058_left",
   "sequence": 769,
   "domain_canonical": "德山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "德山藩",
   "domain_en": "Tokuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p058_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 58,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（德山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 2 (Tokuyama)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Tokuyama tax receipts, products, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Tokuyama entry in fascicle 2 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran; no maru-marker appears on it, so every column belongs to Tokuyama. The domain reports regular land tax (正租) of 17,870 koku of rice and 129.8 kanme of silver, plus miscellaneous taxes (諸税) of 2,805 koku of rice, 509 ryō 3 bu 3 shu in gold, and a second silver figure of 194.2 kanme that the project's extracted dataset omits. Two products are recorded under a single brace annotated 年々不同, \"differs from year to year\": 1,000 bundles of hanshi paper and about 2,500 kin of dried sea cucumber. The demographic block gives 12,337 households and 54,471 people (28,173 male, 26,298 female), of which the shizoku-and-sotsu classes account for 975 households and 4,150 people, and the shizoku alone for 446 households and 2,003 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "chizuka_upper_p061_left",
   "sequence": 770,
   "domain_canonical": "千束藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "千束藩",
   "domain_en": "Chizuka",
   "image": "images/upper_p061_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 61,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "九十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（斗南）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Overview, Table 2 (Tonami)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-2 kokudaka and land-tax register (Chizuka block; Tonami unrecorded; Toyooka civil-register tail)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes Toyooka's fascicle-2 civil register and opens the entries for Tonami and Chizuka. Toyooka's tail records outcaste (eta) households as \"not known\" with a population of 214 (96 male, 118 female), hinin households likewise unknown with a printed population of 145 — though the printed split of 61 male and 81 female sums to only 142 — plus 68 villages, 236 shrines, and a governor's family of 3. Tonami, the relocated Aizu domain, prints only 未記 (\"not recorded\"). Chizuka's block gives a base assessment (高) of 10,000 koku, new-land taka of 172.2126 koku, total kusadaka of 10,172.2126 koku (exactly the sum), and a tax yield (物成) of 5,413.076 koku at a fixed rate computed as the five-year average from Genji 1 (1864) through the boshin year (1868)."
  },
  {
   "id": "chizuka_upper_p062_right",
   "sequence": 771,
   "domain_canonical": "千束藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "千束藩",
   "domain_en": "Chizuka",
   "image": "images/upper_p062_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 62,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "九十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（千束）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table 2 (Chizuka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Chizuka Domain taxes, households, population, shrines and temples (block continuation)",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the Table 2 entry for Chizuka Domain (千束藩), a small Buzen-province holding of the Okudaira house, begun on the preceding page. It records a ditto tax figure of 4,431.8241 koku carried over from the previous page's category, miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) of 4,800.39321 koku plus 13 ryō and 48.13 mon in Ei cash, 1,380 commoner households, and a population of 5,787 (2,838 male, 2,949 female). The status breakdown gives roughly 317 samurai-and-soldier households, 446 shizoku (213 male, 233 female) and 483 sotsu (244 male, 239 female), alongside 3 huts, 12 outcasts, 27 shrines with 2 shrine-keeper households (5 male, 4 female), and 5 temples housing 13 males and 17 females. The village-count label (村數) stands at the page edge with its value printed on the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "omura_upper_p074_right",
   "sequence": 772,
   "domain_canonical": "大村藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大村藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōmura",
   "image": "images/upper_p074_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 74,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大村）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Ōmura)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōmura domain assessed yield, land tax and product values",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the whole of Ōmura domain's fascicle-2 entry: assessed yield, land tax, and the cash value of its taxed products. The gross assessment (草高) is 50,454.61356 koku, and the page breaks it into three parts that reconcile to the last decimal place — a base yield of 27,973.877 koku, 5,360.68506 koku added from newly reclaimed fields, and 17,120.0515 koku revised out a second time, which a note attributes to land taken back from the shizoku in 1870. The regular land tax is given as a five-year average of 21,392.63 koku of rice plus 157.044 kanmon in cash. Six products follow, valued in kanmon: tea 2,000, shikimi seed 1,212.183, coal 1,000, dried sea cucumber 438.802, charcoal 400, and pottery 100. Three unlabelled figures in small type are printed beside the yield and tax columns; one of them completes the sub-koku places of the reclaimed-field figure, and the other two (8,970.99494 and 8,516.38738 koku) the page leaves unexplained."
  },
  {
   "id": "omura_upper_p074_left",
   "sequence": 773,
   "domain_canonical": "大村藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大村藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōmura",
   "image": "images/upper_p074_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 74,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大村）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 2 (Ōmura)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Status-group households and population; salt and camellia entries",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Ōmura domain block in fascicle 2 of the Hansei Ichiran and carries no domain marker of its own; the running header in the outer margin identifies the block as Ōmura. Reading right to left, it opens with the tail of a product list — salt at 479 kan 40 mon and camellia at 171 kan 150 mon — and then runs through six status groups, each given as a household or population count with a male/female breakdown printed as a two-column warichu beneath it. Ōmura reports 1,821 shizoku households holding 9,371 people (4,535 male, 4,836 female), 222 heisotsu households holding 1,005 people, 676 sotsuzoku households holding 2,937 people, 64 shrine-personnel households holding 289 people, 192 Buddhist clergy, and 75 eta households holding 495 people — 2,858 households and 14,289 people across the groups printed on this page. Every male-plus-female sum matches its printed total exactly."
  },
  {
   "id": "omizo_upper_p080_left",
   "sequence": 774,
   "domain_canonical": "大溝藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大溝藩",
   "domain_en": "Ōmizo",
   "image": "images/upper_p080_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 80,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百三十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第二（大溝）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 2 (Ōmizo)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Ōtaki population, religious houses and villages; opening of the Ōmizo land-and-tax block",
   "page_summary_en": "The left half of printed page 135 in fascicle 2 carries the tail of the Ōtaki (大多喜藩, Kazusa) entry and then the opening of the Ōmizo (大溝藩, Ōmi) entry, which begins at the ○大溝藩 marker. Ōtaki is credited with a commoner population of 21,481 (10,610 male, 10,871 female) spread over 64 villages, together with 178 temples housing 276 people, 18 shrines with 19 shrine-service households and 87 residents, 86 hinin and 37 eta. Left of the marker, Ōmizo opens with an assessed gross (草高) of 20,097.67058 koku plus a new-field increment of 96.47058 koku, land tax in rice of 5,823.10305 koku and miscellaneous imposts of 905.95237 koku; those two sum exactly to the printed combined rice figure of 6,729.05542 koku. Ōmizo's warrior households are given as 537 shizoku (257 male, 280 female) and 349 sotsu (181 male, 168 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "oginoyamanaka_upper_p083_right",
   "sequence": 775,
   "domain_canonical": "荻野山中藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "荻野山中藩",
   "domain_en": "Ogino-Yamanaka",
   "image": "images/upper_p083_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 83,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百四十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第二（荻野山中）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 2 (Ogino-Yamanaka)",
   "table_number": 2,
   "page_topic": "Fascicle-2 fiscal and demographic returns: opening of the Ogino-Yamanaka block, with the tail of the Obata block",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 140 of Hansei ichiran fascicle 2 carries the closing columns of the Obata (小幡) domain return and then, from the maru-marker ○荻野山中藩 leftward, the opening columns of Ogino-Yamanaka (荻野山中), a 13,000-koku Ōkubo house in Sagami. Obata's tail records 40 villages, 35 eta households with 145 people (88 male, 57 female), 17 hinin (10 male, 7 female), and a force of 100 men organised as three platoons of 32 plus four drummers. Ogino-Yamanaka's block opens with an assessed gross yield (草高) of 13,684.19767 koku, which reconciles exactly against the domain's nominal 13,000 koku once the two increment columns are added — 込高 683.84567 koku and 改出高 0.352 koku — followed by main rice tax 3,213.48405 koku, cash dues 1,224貫745文 and a fraction, 2,226 households, 12,255 people, and 11 hinin households with 61 people. The one internal failure on the page is the main population split: the printed male and female sub-totals (6,331 and 5,910) come to 12,241, fourteen short of the printed total of 12,255."
  },
  {
   "id": "kaminoyama_upper_p099_left",
   "sequence": 776,
   "domain_canonical": "上ノ山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "上山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kaminoyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p099_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 99,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三　（上山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 3 (Kaminoyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kaminoyama land assessment and five- and four-year tax averages",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page opens the fascicle-3 entry for Kaminoyama (上山藩) in Dewa. It gives a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 27,000 koku, a supplementary yield (込高) of 1,409.4579 koku, a printed combined total (合高) of 28,409.4577 koku, and a cultivated area of 109 chō 9 tan 4 se 25 bu 2 rin, which is then restated after the total with the note 見取, marking land taxed by field inspection rather than by survey. Tax receipts appear for two averaging periods: a five-year average of 4,551.75 koku in regular land tax (正租) together with 530.7003 kan of miscellaneous tax (雜稅) in ei-denominated cash, and a four-year average of 5,834.896 koku with 273.4639 kan. The single column to the right of the ○上山藩 marker, （兵員　百五十四人）, closes the preceding Kameda (龜田藩) entry with a troop strength of 154 men."
  },
  {
   "id": "kaminoyama_upper_p100_right",
   "sequence": 777,
   "domain_canonical": "上ノ山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "上山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kaminoyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p100_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 100,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（上山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Kaminoyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Land tax, products, and household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-leaf continues the Kaminoyama Domain entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran; it carries no maru-marker, so every column belongs to the domain whose marker stands on the preceding leaf. The regular land tax (正租), stated as a five-year average, is 10,487.166 koku of rice reckoned in actual koku, with a note that 804 kan 64 mon 2 bu of miscellaneous cash taxes were converted at eight ryō per koku and folded into that figure — and a compiler's parenthetical warning that regular and miscellaneous tax are mixed and the number is printed as it stands. Four products follow: ōbōshi and washi paper joined by a brace (about 2,000 ryō made per year), raw silk (about 1,200 kanme by thread weight, varying with the year), ramie (about 500 ryō), and lacquer (about 600 ryō), with the tax rules on all four deferred for later inquiry. The leaf closes with 5,570 households, of which 122 are shizoku and 147 sotsu."
  },
  {
   "id": "kaminoyama_upper_p100_left",
   "sequence": 778,
   "domain_canonical": "上ノ山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "上ノ山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kaminoyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p100_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 100,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百七十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（上山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Fascicle 3 (Kaminoyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "household counts by status and the population total",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf continues the Kaminoyama domain block in fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran, carrying the tail of the household schedule and the head of the population schedule; it bears no maru-marker, so every figure on it belongs to Kaminoyama. Households are reported separately for the home territory (commoners 1,915; eta and ban-hinin 3; shrine-priest, temple and Shugendo households 38 under one brace) and for the domain's Echigo holdings (commoners 3,293; eta together with ferry-keepers 22; shrine-priest, temple and Shugendo households 30). Those six figures, plus the 122 shizoku and 147 sotsu households recorded elsewhere in the block, sum to exactly 5,570, the domain's total household count. The page then gives the population as 33,399 persons, of which 625 are shizoku, split 328 male and 297 female; the remaining status groups run on to the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "kaminoyama_upper_p101_right",
   "sequence": 779,
   "domain_canonical": "上ノ山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "上山藩",
   "domain_en": "Kaminoyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p101_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 101,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "百七十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三　（上山）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Table Three (Kaminoyama)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Population by status, the Echigo detached lands, and the two standing units",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Kaminoyama (上ノ山藩) entry in fascicle 3 and carries the domain's population broken out by status. The home (Dewa) lands give 753 sotsu (349 male, 404 female), a clergy group of 47 shrine personnel, 6 yamabushi, 68 women, 3 nuns and 43 monks, and 11,507 commoners (5,868 male, 5,639 female). A heading 越後地 then opens a parallel clergy group for the domain's detached holdings in Echigo province — 15 shrine personnel, 8 yamabushi, 42 women, 7 nuns, 48 monks — followed by 18,069 Echigo commoners (9,038 male, 9,031 female) and 146 eta and ferry-keepers, whose male and female sub-counts (80 and 62) fall four short of the printed total. The compilers add that the counts of shrines, temples and villages are not known in detail, and close with the domain's forces in parentheses: one infantry company (a platoon reckoned at 60 men, with 12 officers) and one artillery section (15 officers)."
  },
  {
   "id": "kariya_upper_p106_left",
   "sequence": 780,
   "domain_canonical": "刈屋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "刈屋藩",
   "domain_en": "Kariya",
   "image": "images/upper_p106_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 106,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "百八十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（刈屋）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Kariya)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Kariya domain: land assessment, tax revenue, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the whole fascicle-3 return for Kariya domain (刈屋藩, modern 刈谷藩) in Mikawa province, opened by the maru-marker ○刈屋藩 at the right edge; no other domain appears on the page. The land block reports an assessed gross yield (草高) of 27,734.68338 koku, made up of the official 23,000-koku assessment (高) plus a new-field increment (込高改出新田高) of 4,734.68338 koku, against which the domain collected 6,974.38751 koku in land-tax rice together with 219 ryō 2 bu 1 shu in gold, 28.342 monme of silver, 269 kan 341 mon of copper cash and 689 kan 887 mon 3 bu 1 mō in eiraku currency. The demographic block records 5,957 households and 26,257 people (13,079 male, 13,178 female, which sum exactly to the printed total), with 10 shrine attendants and 171 Buddhist clergy counted separately, alongside 22 shrines and 140 temples. A bracketed 付箋 slip added by the compilers notes that temples, Shugendō practitioners and shrines were surveyed and returned village by village; the printed book-page number in the bottom margin is 187."
  },
  {
   "id": "daishoji_upper_p123_right",
   "sequence": 781,
   "domain_canonical": "大聖寺藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大聖寺藩",
   "domain_en": "Daishōji",
   "image": "images/upper_p123_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 123,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（大聖寺）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Daishōji)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Daishōji domain: assessed yield, land tax and product taxes",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Daishōji (大聖寺) entry in fascicle 3 of the Hansei ichiran with the domain's land and revenue figures: a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 80,000 koku, new-field yield (新田高) of 3,738.303 koku, and a further 33.73 koku of 籠高. The land tax (正租), stated as a five-year average, is 26,045.50578 koku of rice together with 32,354 kan 824 mon in cash, and products and miscellaneous taxes bring in another 14,715 kan 560 mon; the domain's named products are Yamanaka woodware, tea, thread, silk, Kutani ceramics and oil. The four columns standing to the right of the ○大聖寺藩 marker are the tail of the preceding Tatebayashi (館林) entry: 6 cannon with 46 men attached, 814 troops in all, 213 samurai in office and 264 without office, and in addition 74 officials, 18 standard-bearers and 44 buglers, 4 of the buglers being officials. A parenthetical note there warns that \"in office\" and \"without office\" describe ordinary samurai (平士) and not soldiers."
  },
  {
   "id": "daishoji_upper_p123_left",
   "sequence": 782,
   "domain_canonical": "大聖寺藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大聖寺藩",
   "domain_en": "Daishōji",
   "image": "images/upper_p123_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 123,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（大聖寺）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Daishōji)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "household and population counts by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page continues the fascicle-3 return for Daishōji domain (Kaga province, 80,000 koku 草高) that begins on the facing right-hand page; it carries no maru-marker, so all thirty-one printed elements belong to 大聖寺藩. The household block totals 55,915 dwellings and its nine components sum to that figure exactly: 54,911 commoner houses (48,050 rural, 6,856 urban, 5 leather-workers'), 469 shizoku, 265 sotsu, 194 shrines, 49 temples, 10 shrine-priest, 8 shrine-keeper, 4 yamabushi and 5 eta. The population block gives 48,736 persons (24,027 male, 24,709 female), of which 2,037 are shizoku, 2,184 sotsu, and 76 shrine priests and shrine keepers taken together; the remaining status counts print on the following page (44,059 commoners, 316 temple, 19 yamabushi, 45 eta), and those seven components likewise sum to 48,736 exactly. The two blocks rest on surveys of four different months of the horse year (Meiji 3 / 1870) — the third, fourth, sixth and eleventh — and they contradict each other: the dwelling total exceeds the population total, which cannot be literally true of houses and people."
  },
  {
   "id": "daishoji_upper_p124_right",
   "sequence": 783,
   "domain_canonical": "大聖寺藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "大聖寺藩",
   "domain_en": "Daishōji",
   "image": "images/upper_p124_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 124,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（大聖寺）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Three (Daishōji)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Status-group population tail and military establishment",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes Daishōji Domain's status-group population count and then reports its armed forces. Four population lines are given with male/female splits and the date of the survey each rests on: temple clergy 316 (205 male, 111 female, surveyed 4/4 of the horse year 1870), commoners 44,059 (21,286 male, 22,773 female, surveyed in the 11th month), mountain ascetics 19 (13 male, 6 female, surveyed 4/3), and eta outcastes 45 (18 male, 27 female, surveyed 3/12). The military entry records 668 troops formed into two battalions, broken down into 480 riflemen and 188 men from company commanders down to drummers, plus a separate artillery company of 98 (64 gunners and 34 from commanders down to drummers and the like). Three notes state the organisational rules and the domain's shortfall: a platoon is twenty-five men or more and six platoons make a battalion, eight guns make an artillery company, and although there is a surplus amounting to one further battalion of both rifle and artillery units, it is not yet fully equipped and will be organised in stages — a sentence that breaks off at the foot of the page."
  },
  {
   "id": "tate_upper_p124_left",
   "sequence": 784,
   "domain_canonical": "館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "館藩",
   "domain_en": "Tate",
   "image": "images/upper_p124_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 124,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（館）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey Tables, Fascicle 3 (Tate)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tate domain: land assessment and tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "The opening page of the entry for Tate domain (館藩, the former Matsumae domain of Oshima province in Ezo) in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran. Its nominal assessment is 30,000 koku, to which an 外高 of 10,382.0164 koku is added to give a subtotal of 40,382.0164 koku; the internal breakdown assigns 9,719.456 koku to seven villages in Date district, Iwashiro, and 30,662.5604 koku to forty-one villages in Murayama district, Uzen, and the two components sum exactly to the subtotal. Regular tax (正租) is recorded as 91,751 yen collected through the port office at Fukuyama in Oshima, together with 1,952.89495 koku of rice from Yanagawa in Iwashiro, a cash payment of 278 ryō 905 mon 1 bu commuted at seven koku to the ryō, that same sum restated as 1,952.89495 koku of rice, and 6,807.7829 koku from Higashine in Uzen. The page also records a quarterly government grant of 17,300 ryō and miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) of 1,840 ryō from town and village petty imposts."
  },
  {
   "id": "tate_upper_p125_right",
   "sequence": 785,
   "domain_canonical": "館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "館藩",
   "domain_en": "Tate",
   "image": "images/upper_p125_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 125,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（館）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Tate)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Exclave minor dues, domain tax totals, and Oshima district products",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-3 tax return for Tate domain (館藩), the Matsumae house after its 1869 renaming and reseating in Oshima. It records the minor dues (小物成) owed from the domain's two Honshu exclaves: Yanagawa in Iwashiro province yields 103.477 koku of rice and 285,415 mon of ei-cash, while Higashine in Uzen province yields 469.0555 koku of rice, 218,210.5 mon of ei-cash, and 16.342 koku of perilla seed reckoned at 8.171 koku of rice, exactly half, a clean 2:1 conversion. Two aggregate lines follow, 9,341.38135 koku of rice and a 〆 total of 111,681 ryo in gold together with 610.6 mon in ei-cash, both of which sum items carried over from earlier leaves. The page then opens the register of products and tax figures, listing herring, sardine meal, kelp, fish oil, dried squid, miscellaneous fish and timber from the four Oshima districts of Fukushima, Tsugaru, Hiyama and Nishi, and closes with 1,848 ryo of miscellaneous taxes from those same districts."
  },
  {
   "id": "tate_upper_p125_left",
   "sequence": 786,
   "domain_canonical": "館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "館藩",
   "domain_en": "Tate",
   "image": "images/upper_p125_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 125,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（館）",
   "page_header_en": "Tables of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Three (Tate)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Miscellaneous-tax note and the products and dues of the domain's two mainland enclave districts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-three return of 館藩 (Tate, the former Matsumae house). It opens with the closing sentence of a submission note covering four districts: the licence dues on river fishing and on shore set-net fishing, together with the taxes on artisans, merchants, pawnbrokers, malt-houses, sake brewers and soy-sauce brewers, are given only as an approximate aggregate, because the disorder during the rebels' occupation made a prompt audit impossible and the itemised ledger would follow later. Two enclave districts are then reported. The seven villages of Date district in Iwashiro yield silkworm egg-cards, silk thread, floss silk and light-weight silk cloth, and their miscellaneous taxes come to 285 kan 415 mon in ei-cash (breakdown omitted) plus 103.477 koku of rice, made up of 97.645 koku of kuchimai surcharge and 5.832 koku of fumai corvée-commutation rice. The forty-one villages of Murayama district in Uzen yield tobacco, paper mulberry, mountain mulberry, foxtail millet, barley, soybeans, adzuki beans, buckwheat, wheat, silkworms and raw silk. The printed book-page number is 225."
  },
  {
   "id": "tate_upper_p126_left",
   "sequence": 787,
   "domain_canonical": "館藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "館藩",
   "domain_en": "Tate",
   "image": "images/upper_p126_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 126,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三 （館）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 3 (Tate)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the household-and-population return of Tate Domain (館藩, the Matsumae house's domain in Ezo), dated the fifth month of the kanoe-uma year (Meiji 3 / 1870). It records 16,268 households in total, broken down as 9 shrines, 111 temples, 808 shizoku households, 848 sotsu households, 20 shrine-family households, 61 shugen households and 14,411 commoner households; those components sum exactly to the printed total. Population is given as 79,792 persons — 40,223 male and 39,569 female — with the same status breakdown: 5,703 shizoku, 3,559 sotsu, 122 shrine-family members, 459 monks and shugen practitioners, and 69,949 commoners, each with its own male/female split, and every sub-count reconciles to both the status total and the sex total. A double-column interlinear note attached to the shrine figure explains that the return was not compiled shrine by shrine but from the shrine-family stipend allotments, and that counting instead by shrine-family households would yield twenty."
  },
  {
   "id": "takanabe_upper_p127_right",
   "sequence": 788,
   "domain_canonical": "高鍋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高鍋藩",
   "domain_en": "Takanabe",
   "image": "images/upper_p127_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 127,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高鍋）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Takanabe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "End of Tate domain's troop return; opening of Takanabe domain's land assessment",
   "page_summary_en": "The right-hand two-thirds of this leaf closes the entry for Tate (the 1869 renaming of Matsumae) in Ezo with its military return, which a note dates to the survey of the sixth month of 1870. Fukuyama supplied 372 standing infantry, 447 reserve infantry, 61 standing artillerymen and 78 men on coastal heavy-gun duty; Esashi supplied 148 infantry and 20 artillerymen; ordnance, manufacturing and construction sections added 30, 30 and 28 men; and a battalion staff of 35 (one commander, two inspectors, two chief guides, a left-wing guide, a drum major and a 28-man baggage train) brings the printed total to 1,249 men, which the components reproduce exactly. The maru-marker ○高鍋藩 then opens the entry for Takanabe in Hyūga, recording a nominal assessment (草高) of 27,000 koku against an actual yield (此實高) of 59,992.793 koku, with the 内 breakdown running on to the facing leaf. The running head reads 藩制一覧表第三（高鍋）and the printed page number is 228."
  },
  {
   "id": "takanabe_upper_p127_left",
   "sequence": 789,
   "domain_canonical": "高鍋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高鍋藩",
   "domain_en": "Takanabe",
   "image": "images/upper_p127_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 127,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高鍋）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Takanabe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Land assessment, regular and miscellaneous taxes, and taxed products",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf is the fascicle-3 fiscal return for Takanabe domain (Hyūga province, Akizuki house), printed book page 229. It opens with three assessment figures — 成高 27,000 koku, 改出高 23,155.216 koku and 新高 9,837.577 koku — which together come to 59,992.793 koku, within eight koku of a round 60,000. The regular land tax (正租) is returned as 13,956.5283 koku of rice, 1,609.471 koku of soybeans and 4,911 kan 461 mon in cash; the miscellaneous taxes (雜税) as 605.8684 koku of rice, 105.2955 koku of soybeans, 401.415 koku of barley, 76 ryō 1 bu 2 shu in gold and 16,685 kan 335 mon in cash. Under the heading 諸産物税金 the domain then lists nine taxed products — raw wax, shiitake, paper, cattle and horse hides, charcoal, salt, thatch matting, timber and mullet — with no quantities printed against them."
  },
  {
   "id": "takanabe_upper_p128_right",
   "sequence": 790,
   "domain_canonical": "高鍋藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高鍋藩",
   "domain_en": "Takanabe",
   "image": "images/upper_p128_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 128,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百三十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高鍋）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 3 (Takanabe)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "households, status composition and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the household-and-population page of the fascicle-3 return for Takanabe domain (高鍋藩, Hyūga province). The domain reports 9,499 households, broken down as 382 shrines, 78 Buddhist halls, 438 samurai (士族) households, 1,708 sub-samurai (卒族) households, 140 shrine-attendant buildings, 66 Shugendō mountain-ascetic households, 6,630 commoner households and 57 eta-hinin households — figures that sum exactly to the printed total. Total population is 43,344 (22,287 male, 21,057 female), and the page then gives population by status: samurai 2,097, sub-samurai 7,420, shrine attendants 698, Buddhist clergy 139 and mountain ascetics 236, each with its own male/female split; the commoner and eta-hinin counts continue on the facing page. At the head of the page a tax figure of 138 ryō carries over from the item whose label prints on the preceding page."
  },
  {
   "id": "takahashi_upper_p135_left",
   "sequence": 791,
   "domain_canonical": "高梁藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高梁藩",
   "domain_en": "Takahashi",
   "image": "images/upper_p135_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 135,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百四十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高梁）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle Three (Takahashi)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka deductions, land-tax totals and domain products",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left-hand page of the 高梁藩 (Takahashi, Bitchū) entry in fascicle three of the Hansei ichiran, printed book-page 245, and it carries no maru-marker: the whole page belongs to Takahashi. It closes the domain's kokudaka reckoning with a final exempted item of 2,431.098 koku remitted for crop failure, a subtotal of exemptions of 4,156.9506 koku, and a remaining assessed yield of 15,843.0494 koku; the last two sum to exactly 20,000 koku, the domain's nominal assessment, and the tax rice taken on the remainder is 7,232.7814 koku. A pair of marginal notes divides the page: everything to the right is the Kanoe-uma (1870) return, while everything to the left comes from a Kanoto-hitsuji (1871) re-survey, which reports a five-year average regular land tax of 8,519.0927 koku (863.0333 of it left out of the 1870 return) and miscellaneous taxes of 60.8521 koku reckoned at eight ryō the koku (24.6363 of it newly added by the re-survey). The page ends with the domain's products: danshi paper with no quantity recorded, 120 horse-loads of rice-threshing implements, 14,700 bundles of firewood, 1,939 bales of leaf tobacco and 8,550 bales of stripped tobacco."
  },
  {
   "id": "takahashi_upper_p136_right",
   "sequence": 792,
   "domain_canonical": "高梁藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高梁",
   "domain_en": "Takahashi",
   "image": "images/upper_p136_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 136,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百四十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高梁）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Three (Takahashi)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takahashi taxes, households and population by status, shrines and temples, infantry",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-three return for Takahashi domain in Bitchū; no maru-marker appears, so every column belongs to Takahashi. It opens by closing the products list carried over from the preceding page with the note that the five items above were untaxed, then records miscellaneous taxes of 195 ryō 1 bu 1 shu in gold together with 6 mon 4 bun in ei-currency. The bulk of the page is the household and population return by status: 5,080 commoner households holding 22,003 people (11,293 male, 10,710 female); 369 shizoku households with 1,726 people and 372 sotsu households with 1,231 people, the two bracketed together under a 士卒 heading whose own aggregate was left blank and flagged with an attached slip; and 215 eta households with 866 people. The page also returns 737 shrines and 98 Buddhist temples, and ends with two infantry platoons at sixty men apiece, 120 men in all, while the 非人 line is printed with no figure at all."
  },
  {
   "id": "tatsuoka_upper_p140_right",
   "sequence": 793,
   "domain_canonical": "龍岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龍岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Tatsuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p140_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 140,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（龍岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration (Hansei ichiran), Fascicle 3 — running head naming Tatsuoka",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Assessed yield and land tax on Tatsuoka's Shinano and Mikawa holdings",
   "page_summary_en": "Page 254 of Fascicle 3 opens the entry for Tatsuoka domain (龍岡藩), a Matsudaira holding whose lands lay in Shinano and Mikawa provinces, as the warichu beside the maru-marker states. The domain's assessment is reported province by province: the Shinano administered lands carry an assessed yield of 12,093.612 koku, against which the five-year average land tax runs 3,710.613 koku of rice plus 18 ryō 1 bu 2 shu in gold and 106.1 ei-mon in cash, with a 小物成 (miscellaneous petty levies) heading printed below and its figures carried to the facing page; the Mikawa administered lands are assessed at 4,185.608 koku, and their average tax likewise continues overleaf. The two assessments sum to 16,279.220 koku, which matches Tatsuoka's nominal 16,000-koku standing. The four columns printed to the right of the marker close out the preceding domain's entry (Tannan, 丹南藩): 26 villages, three kazoku (all male), an eta population of 30 persons in 6 households (18 male, 12 female), and officer counts of six for the samurai corps and seven for the sotsu corps, with the survey noting that the rank-and-file strengths of both units were not recorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "tatsuoka_upper_p140_left",
   "sequence": 794,
   "domain_canonical": "龍岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龍岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Tatsuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p140_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 140,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百五十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三　（龍岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 3 — Tatsuoka (龍岡藩): tax receipts, temple land, and retainer households",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "tax receipts, totals, and retainer households",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf continues the fascicle-3 return for Tatsuoka domain (龍岡藩) in Shinano; the ○龍岡藩 marker and the opening figures stand on the facing right-hand page, so every column here belongs to Tatsuoka. It finishes the Mikawa-province side of the tax account — 1,423.8354 koku of rice on the five-year average, plus a miscellaneous tax of 0.593 koku of rice and 4 kan 400 mon in copper cash — and then gives the combined totals for both provinces: 5,135.4014 koku of rice, 18 ryō 1 bu 2 shu in gold together with 106.1 mon in ei-currency, and 4 kan 400 mon in cash. A bracketed note records temple land of 35.774 koku beside two further amounts of 26.36 and 20 koku for which the survey prints no label. The retainer body is small: 112 shizoku households holding 468 people (222 male, 246 female), 65 sotsu households holding 189 people (96 male, 93 female), and 72 corvée attendants."
  },
  {
   "id": "tatsuoka_upper_p141_right",
   "sequence": 795,
   "domain_canonical": "龍岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "龍岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Tatsuoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p141_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 141,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百五十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（多古）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Fascicle 3 (Tako)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tail of Tatsuoka's fascicle-3 entry and the opening of Tako's",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf, printed page 256 of Fascicle 3, closes the survey entry for Tatsuoka Domain (Shinano) and opens that for Tako Domain (Shimosa) at the maru-marker ○多古藩 in mid-page. Tatsuoka reports 2,978 commoner households and 12,559 people across 63 villages, with 13 shrines, 49 temples staffed by 77 monks, 14 women, 11 chapel wardens and 4 manservants, and 8 Shugendo halls staffed by 26; its untaxed products are raw silk thread, silkworm-egg cards and ginseng, and it fields one platoon of 43 soldiers plus 22 farmer-soldiers. The population split prints as 6,454 men and 6,096 women, which sums to 12,550 against the printed total of 12,559 — a nine-person discrepancy in the source itself, confirmed by single-character re-inspection of every digit. Tako's entry then begins with a granted assessment of 12,000 koku plus 2,173.12636 koku of absorbed and newly reclaimed land, after which the five-year-average heading carries the entry onto the facing leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "takaoka_upper_p144_left",
   "sequence": 796,
   "domain_canonical": "高岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Takaoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p144_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 144,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Han-sei ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 3 (Takaoka) — running header in the outer margin, provenance only",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Tateyama religious, warrior and militia counts, then Takaoka's two land-tax figures",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the left half of leaf 263 in Fascicle 3 of the Han-sei ichiran-hyō. The single maru-marker ○高岡藩 stands in the middle of the leaf, so the eleven columns to its right still belong to 館山藩 (Tateyama, Awa province), whose block carries over from the facing half-leaf, and only the two columns to its left belong to 高岡藩 (Takaoka, Shimōsa). The Tateyama columns count religious and status households: 5 Shugendō houses (34 people), 2 yin-yang diviner houses (11 people), 1 house licensed under the Nishinomiya Ebisu-dayū (7 people), 66 Buddhist halls of which 54 had no resident priest (13 clergy), 140 warrior households (79 shizoku, 61 sotsu) holding 433 people, two 45-man platoons of 20 shizoku and 25 sotsu each, and 3 kazoku; the eta and hinin counts are entered 不詳, not ascertained. For Takaoka the page prints only the two tax lines — an assessed gross yield (草高) of 12,016.5427 koku, expressly including new fields, against a regular land tax (正租) of 3,084.51039 koku of rice, about 25.7 percent of the gross."
  },
  {
   "id": "takaoka_upper_p145_right",
   "sequence": 797,
   "domain_canonical": "高岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Takaoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p145_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 145,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三（高岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Administration Survey, Fascicle 3 (Takaoka)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takaoka domain: tax remainder, households, population, retainer counts, shrines, temples, villages, kazoku",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the second leaf of the 高岡藩 (Takaoka, Shimōsa) entry in fascicle 3 of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran, printed book page 264. It opens with the cash remainder of the land tax carried over from page 263 — 320 kan 68.412 mon in ei-currency, followed by a note that 9 koku 6 to of soybeans were levied in one lot as petty imposts (小物成) — and then gives the miscellaneous tax at 7 kan 250 mon. The domain counted 1,558 households and 7,935 people (3,927 male, 4,008 female), of whom the retainer corps held 84 houses (68 shizoku, 16 sotsu) and 306 people (263 shizoku, 43 sotsu), with a further 70 troops recorded as miscellaneous foot registered on the farmers' rolls. The leaf closes with 56 shrines, 31 temples, 33 villages, an editorial note that the next twelve lines were written in vermilion in the original, a statement that the eta and hinin population was not ascertained, and 5 kazoku (3 male, 2 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatomi_upper_p145_left",
   "sequence": 798,
   "domain_canonical": "高富藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高富藩",
   "domain_en": "Takatomi",
   "image": "images/upper_p145_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 145,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第三　（高富）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle Three (Takatomi)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takatomi domain kokudaka and tax revenue, with an attached slip for Takaoka",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens the Hansei Ichiran entry for Takatomi domain (Mino Province), printed book page 265 of fascicle three. Takatomi's granted assessment is 10,000 koku, with a further 380.4892 koku entered as 外高 and marked 込高; its regular land tax is 2,898.20264 koku of rice plus 318.45968 kan in ei-cash, and its miscellaneous tax 2.72 koku of rice plus 14.374 kan. To the right of the ○高富藩 marker, inside the editors' bracket, sits an 附箋 (a slip pasted to the original) that belongs to the preceding domain, Takaoka: it reports a variant copy's figures of 10,329.28977 koku over 29 villages in three districts of Shimosa and 1,687.2523 koku over 4 villages in two districts of Kazusa, together with five-year average yields of 2,509.27977 koku of rice, 283.169375 kan of ei-cash and 9.6 koku of soybeans for the first holding, and 856.2188 koku of rice and 45.50718 kan for the second. Those two figures sum to 12,016.54207 koku, which differs by 47.97072 koku from the 12,064.51279 koku recorded as Takaoka's 草高 in the main text on the previous page."
  },
  {
   "id": "takatomi_upper_p146_right",
   "sequence": 799,
   "domain_canonical": "高富藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "高富",
   "domain_en": "Takatomi",
   "image": "images/upper_p146_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 146,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百六十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第三（高富）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Three (Takatomi)",
   "table_number": 3,
   "page_topic": "Takatomi assessed yield, land tax, miscellaneous tax and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 266 continues the Takatomi (高富) entry in fascicle three of the Hansei ichiran; the block opens on the preceding leaf-face with the marker ○高富藩, so every column here belongs to Takatomi. The return carries its own date note, the eighth month of the sheep year, Meiji 4 (1871). Assessed yield is 10,000 koku plus a supplementary 380.4892 koku of newly surveyed land, giving a total of 10,380.4892 koku; against that the regular land tax is 3,081.3991 koku of hulled rice and 292 kan 740.36 mon in cash, with miscellaneous taxes of a further 102.316 koku and 75 kan 93.33 mon. The population columns record 70 samurai households (306 people, 146 male and 160 female), 40 sotsu households (55 people, 46 male and 9 female), 1,352 commoner households (6,100 people, 3,063 male and 3,037 female) and 8 shrine households (45 people, 18 male and 27 female)."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumai_upper_p153_right",
   "sequence": 800,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴舞藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumai",
   "image": "images/upper_p153_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 153,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Survey, Fascicle Four (Maizuru)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Close of Tsuchiura's household and troop returns; opening of Tsurumai's land-yield and tax block",
   "page_summary_en": "The right side of the page closes out Tsuchiura domain's fascicle-four return: 441 households, 201 outcaste (eta and hinin) households with a population of 1,180, and 178 villages, followed by a troop roster of two battalions — seven samurai platoons and five sotsu platoons — totalling 586 men, plus 34 drummers, 46 engineers and 44 in the ordnance and medical sections, which sum exactly to the printed total of 710. Three platoons of farmer-militia and 34 roving troops garrisoned at the Izumi and Mimasaka jin'ya are counted separately as extras. The maru-marker ○舞鶴藩 then opens the next domain, which the project keys as Tsurumai (the print reverses the two characters of the name), with an assessed yield of 69,624.69366 koku including new fields and a regular land tax of 23,626.49238 koku in rice, averaged over 1864 to 1868 and taken for the snake year. Four lines that the reprint marks as vermilion in the manuscript record an original assessed yield of 69,724.84995 koku and note that at the transfer of the ninth month of 1868 the exchange yield fell 515.53246 koku short."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumai_upper_p153_left",
   "sequence": 801,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴舞藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumai",
   "image": "images/upper_p153_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 153,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百八十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (printed \"Maizuru\"; the entry is Tsurumai domain)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "1869 main-tax and miscellaneous-tax cash, salt, and the conversion-shortfall note",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso completes the fascicle-4 tax entry for Tsurumai domain in Kazusa, which the Hansei ichiran prints under the name 舞鶴藩. It opens with the end of a note carried over from the facing recto: 415.37617 koku was received in the seventh month of 1869 and 100.15629 koku remained short, the two together making the 515.53246 koku deficit printed opposite. A double-column gloss then records the 1870 assessed rice at 23,468.84638 koku and states that salt went unrecorded that year while the cash entries repeated their 1869 values. The page prints salt at 149.713 koku and two parallel cash blocks, main tax of 0.75 ryo, 3,007,340.834 mon in eiraku, 133,279 mon in copper and 12.54 monme of silver, then miscellaneous tax of 294.9596 koku of rice, 32 ryo, 145,396.44 mon in eiraku, 64,770 mon in copper and 1,139.18 monme of silver; each pair sums exactly to the combined figures on page 154 recto."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumai_upper_p154_right",
   "sequence": 802,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴舞藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumai",
   "image": "images/upper_p154_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 154,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 4 (Maizuru — the form in which HI prints the name of Tsurumai domain)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Closing revenue totals and the shrine-and-temple land account with its five-year averages",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 282 of the Hansei ichiran, fascicle 4, continues without a maru-marker the entry that opened on page 280 for the domain HI prints as 舞鶴藩 and the project records as Tsurumai (鶴舞藩), a 60,000-koku Kazusa domain. The right-hand columns close the domain's revenue account: combined actual rice (合現米) of 23,921.45198 koku — the 23,626.49238 koku of regular land tax and the 294.9596 koku of miscellaneous rice tax recorded on the two preceding pages — together with 149.713 koku of salt, 32.75 ryō in gold, 3,152,737.274 mon in nagasen, 198,049 mon in copper cash and 1,151.72 monme of silver. The left-hand columns open a separate account for the 509.22 koku held by five shrines and twenty-five temples (受領高), whose five-year average yield is 224.02948 koku of regular rice tax and 0.30325 koku of miscellaneous rice tax, with 3.375 ryō of gold, 23,562.969 mon of nagasen and 73,886 mon of cash. A small note set between the heading and the rice figure records that one manuscript copy gives a different rice total but that the entries from the gold line downward are identical."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumai_upper_p154_left",
   "sequence": 803,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴舞藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumai",
   "image": "images/upper_p154_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 154,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百八十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Comprehensive Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Tsurumai, printed 舞鶴)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Tsurumai domain: five-year average tax total, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Tsurumai (鶴舞, printed 舞鶴) domain block from the facing page and closes its five-year average tax reckoning. The carried-over item ends in gold 2 shu, ei 45.6 mon and copper cash 200 mon; the composite total that follows is 224.33273 koku of hulled rice together with 3 ryō 2 bu in gold, 23 kan 608.569 mon in ei and 74 kan 86 mon in copper cash. That rice total reconciles exactly with the facing page, where the five-year average land tax of 224.02948 koku and the miscellaneous tax rice of 0.30325 koku are printed separately. The demographic half of the page records 13,514 households and 63,858 people, split 32,337 male and 31,521 female, with a partial breakdown of 219 samurai and 557 sotsu households, 37 shrine-priest households and 1 shrine-land household, 311 temples and 159 temple-land households, and 17 chōri, 34 eta and 67 hinin households."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsurumai_upper_p155_right",
   "sequence": 804,
   "domain_canonical": "鶴舞藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "舞鶴藩",
   "domain_en": "Tsurumai",
   "image": "images/upper_p155_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 155,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "二百八十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（舞鶴）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Maizuru [as printed]; the name is a compositor's transposition of Tsurumai)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "status-group population counts",
   "page_summary_en": "Book page 284 of fascicle four continues the population return for Tsurumai domain in Kazusa, whose block opens with a maru-marker three pages earlier; the running header and that marker both print the name with its two characters transposed, as 舞鶴藩. Under the single 内 (\"of which\") at the head of the page the survey breaks the domain's people out by status: shizoku 1,188 (546 male, 642 female), sotsu 2,136 (1,065 male, 1,071 female), shrine personnel 189, residents of shrine land 10, temple personnel 448, residents of temple land 730, chōri 94, eta 146 and hinin 218 — 5,159 persons in all, every sub-total reconciling with its male and female components. The page closes with 332 shrines, an explicit 村數シレス (\"village count not known\"), a parenthetical 船艦不記 (\"warships not recorded\"), and the governor's own household of four persons, one male and three female."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuyama_upper_p220_left",
   "sequence": 805,
   "domain_canonical": "福山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福山藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p220_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 220,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福山）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview Table, Fascicle Five (Fukuyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Assessed yield, reclaimed land, and regular land tax",
   "page_summary_en": "This is the opening leaf of the Fukuyama Domain entry in fascicle five of the Hansei Ichiran. It gives a nominal assessed yield (草高) of 110,000 koku, an additional 2,728.682 koku covering both supplementary assessment (込高) and newly opened paddy (新田高), and a combined total (〆高) of 112,728.682 koku, which reconciles exactly. A separate item records roughly 354 chō of newly reclaimed foreshore (新涯地), broken down into 215 chō 3 tan 4 se 8 bu still exempt from collection until the soil recovers — worth 1,108.631 koku of rice — and about 118 chō 6 tan of tidally flooded ground whose assessment is not yet fixed, plus a separately listed 18 chō 5 tan of new dry field awaiting survey. The regular land tax (正租) is 49,017.48582 koku of rice, about 44.6 percent of the nominal assessment, with an editor's note that one manuscript copy lacks the sub-unit characters 二勺."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuyama_upper_p221_right",
   "sequence": 806,
   "domain_canonical": "福山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福山藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p221_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 221,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福山）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Fukuyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Land-tax and miscellaneous-tax receipts, with a marginal breakdown of the excise duties",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-five revenue account of Fukuyama Domain in Bingo Province. The regular land tax in cash stands at 23,488 ryō plus 298.489 ei-mon, and the miscellaneous taxes at 2,799.2311 koku of rice and 9,601 ryō plus 76.747 ei-mon; the two are then totalled under the mark 〆 at 51,816.71692 koku of rice and 33,089 ryō plus 375.236 ei-mon, the cash totals reconciling exactly against their components. A note in small type warns that the seven lines that follow were written in the margin of the manuscript the compilers worked from, and those lines open a parenthesis that itemises the miscellaneous cash tax: duties on tatami facing and rush matting at 1,604 ryō, on cotton goods at 1,551 ryō, on tobacco at 92 ryō, on salt at 768 ryō, and a payment on branded sake at 35 ryō. Their sum, 4,052 ryō and 864.879 ei-mon, matches the printed total to the last unit and fixes the conversion the account uses at 1,000 ei-mon to the ryō."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuyama_upper_p221_left",
   "sequence": 807,
   "domain_canonical": "福山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福山藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p221_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 221,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Fukuyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Households, status categories, religious houses, and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the household and population return for Fukuyama Domain in fascicle five of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran. The domain reports 38,727 households in total, of which the survey itemises only the special-status categories: 799 shizoku houses, 1,546 sotsuzoku houses, 292 Buddhist temples, 103 Shinto priest houses, 7 hermitages, 648 halls enshrining Buddhist images, 159 houses registered before temple gates, 853 eta households and 109 hinin households, with the numbers of mountain ascetics and of komuso headships left unrecorded. The population is given as 185,858 persons, split into 96,694 male and 88,163 female — a sum of 184,857, which falls 1,001 short of the stated total. Four lines printed in red in the original manuscript, reproduced here at the left of the leaf, explain why the compilers distrusted these figures: Fukuyama's submitted report was \"extremely jumbled and unclear,\" so the editors took the clear final sheet and discarded the discrepant one, and the month and day of the survey were never specified."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuyama_upper_p222_right",
   "sequence": 808,
   "domain_canonical": "福山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福山藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p222_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 222,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle 5 (Fukuyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukuyama status-group population, shrines, ship, governor's household",
   "page_summary_en": "This is a continuation leaf of the Fukuyama domain block in fascicle 5 of the Hansei ichiran, carrying the tail of the domain's population breakdown under an 內 (\"of which\") head whose parent total stands on the preceding leaf. The status groups printed here are shizoku 4,423 (2,183 male / 2,240 female), sotsu 4,818 (2,682 / 2,136), temple-and-hermitage residents 1,173 (694 monks' side / 479, of whom 4 nuns), shrine households 506 (264 / 242), persons on the temple-gate religious registers 778 (488 / 290), eta 3,849 (2,011 / 1,838), chasen 819 (424 / 395), and hinin 588 (289 / 299); every male-plus-female pair sums exactly to its printed total. The page then records 2,325 shrines, one sailing vessel — the Junpū-maru, a wooden hikona-type craft built at Tomo-no-tsu in Bingo — and the governor's household of 5 persons (1 male, 4 female). No maru-marker appears anywhere on the leaf, so all of it belongs to Fukuyama; the left margin carries a printed bracket marking where a fusen slip was pasted on the manuscript and a note that the slip's text is reproduced at the end of the volume."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuyama_lower_p215_right",
   "sequence": 809,
   "domain_canonical": "福山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福山藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuyama",
   "image": "images/lower_p215_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 215,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（福山）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Nine (Fukuyama)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officials and troop strength",
   "page_summary_en": "The page opens the Fukuyama domain entry in fascicle nine of the 1869–70 Dajōkan survey, but its first four columns still belong to Fukui: 右常備 closes the standing-force list carried over from the preceding leaf, then 砲兵一隊 五十三人 and 步兵十一小隊 七百三十七人 are restated as the reserve and closed by 右豫備. After the ○福山藩 marker, Fukuyama's establishment is set out as 知事 one man, 大參事 two (Okada Sō and Miura Misaki), 權大參事 two corrected in smaller type to one (Takeda Heinosuke), 少參事 five (Ōmori Kōji, Kawamura Tsukumo, Kurai Shinobuo, Yūzaki Shinzō, Hamano Shōkichi), and 權少參事 with no count printed but two names (Miyadera Yasuki and Murakami Hansai). The troop heading 兵隊 is followed by a bracketed note giving three infantry companies and, reckoned at forty-eight men to a platoon, twenty-four platoons — 1,152 infantry. The printed page number is 406."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuchiyama_upper_p224_right",
   "sequence": 810,
   "domain_canonical": "福知山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福知山藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuchiyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p224_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 224,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五　（福知山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Five (Fukuchiyama) [running head]",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukuchiyama land assessment, land and cash taxes, and household count",
   "page_summary_en": "This page opens Fukuchiyama Domain's fascicle-five entry with the maru-marker ○福知山藩, whose parenthetical note gives the original assessed yield (honkoku) as 32,000 koku. The domain's surveyed yield (kusadaka) is 32,933.5668 koku, an increment of 933.5668 koku over the honkoku that the small note 新開共 at the foot of the column attributes to newly opened fields; the regular land tax in rice is 13,724.19 koku, the miscellaneous tax 123.1536 koku of rice plus 198.625 ryō in cash, and the household count 7,668. A double-column note converts the cash tax to 49.06073 koku of rice at a rice-note price of 567.8 monme per koku and a note rate of 140 monme per ryō, and the three rice figures sum exactly to the printed grand total of 13,896.404 koku. The four columns to the right of the marker are the tail of the preceding entry for Funai Domain: its Ryūkyū-matting product line at 1,167 ryō, raw wax at 199 ryō, and the closing product totals of 15,385.1987 koku of rice and soybeans and 1,949 ryō in cash."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukuchiyama_upper_p224_left",
   "sequence": 811,
   "domain_canonical": "福知山藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福知山藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukuchiyama",
   "image": "images/upper_p224_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 224,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福知山）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Fukuchiyama)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukuchiyama households and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-5 entry for Fukuchiyama Domain begun on the facing right-hand page, and carries no maru-marker of its own. The right third gives household counts by status — 276 shizoku, 284 sotsu, 7 shrine-priest households, 57 temples, 10 shugendo practitioners, 36 hinin and 321 eta — and the remainder of the page gives the domain population of 31,130 (15,677 male, 15,453 female), broken down by the same statuses: 845 shizoku, 609 sotsu, 29 shrine personnel, 135 temple personnel, 161 hinin, 1,734 eta and 33 shugendo practitioners, each with its own male/female split. Every split sums exactly to its parent total, and the seven status groups together account for 3,546 persons, leaving some 27,584 commoners unenumerated here. Two details go beyond the project's existing extraction: a note beneath the temple-personnel figures recording 2 nuns counted outside the 135, and the editorial line 原本不書 against 神社, meaning the shrine count is not written in the original manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukumoto_upper_p226_right",
   "sequence": 812,
   "domain_canonical": "福本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福本藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukumoto",
   "image": "images/upper_p226_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 226,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（福本）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Fukumoto)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukumoto domain: assessed yield, land tax, sundry tax, households",
   "page_summary_en": "This page belongs entirely to Fukumoto, a small Harima-province branch house of the Ikeda of Tottori; the maru-marker ○福本藩 stands near the top right, with only the running head and the printed page number 426 to its right, so no preceding domain's data appears here. A gloss under the domain name lists its lands as ten villages in Jintō district, fourteen in Jinsai, and one in Innami — twenty-five villages in three districts — assessed at a base yield of 10,573.2038 koku, or 11,573.052 koku once the re-surveyed new-field increment is added. A four-line note that the compilers mark as standing outside the ruled column in the original divides that total: 7,073.052 koku is Fukumoto's own allotment and the remaining 4,500 koku is made up in stipendiary rice from the head house, Tottori. The regular land tax comes to 5,002.166 koku of rice and 43.15 koku of soybeans, sundry taxes to 87 ryō 2 bu plus 169.625 mon in eiraku reckoning, and the domain counts 1,686 households, among them 96 shizoku and 80 sotsu."
  },
  {
   "id": "fukumoto_upper_p226_left",
   "sequence": 813,
   "domain_canonical": "福本藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "福本藩",
   "domain_en": "Fukumoto",
   "image": "images/upper_p226_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 226,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "四百二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（吹上）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 5 (Fukiage)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Fukumoto population breakdown and the opening of the Fukiage land-and-tax entry",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of the page closes Fukumoto domain's fascicle-5 entry with its demographic block: a total population of 7,194, split into 3,691 men and 3,403 women, followed by status sub-counts of 361 shizoku (188 men, 173 women), 170 sotsu (95 men, 75 women), 23 Buddhist clergy, 3 shrine attendants and 2 shrine maidens, with the governor's own household of three (one man, two women) noted parenthetically. Fukumoto's shrine and temple returns are recorded only as 不詳細, with no figures given. The maru-marker ○吹上藩 then opens Fukiage domain, whose first fiscal lines follow: an assessed gross yield (kusadaka) of 13,707.76742 koku including added, newly reclaimed and re-surveyed land; a main land tax of 3,230.53773 koku of rice plus 497,398.28 mon in cash; and miscellaneous taxes of 191.53882 koku of rice. Two figures on the page do not agree with the project's extracted dataset: the sotsu total reads 170 here rather than 178, and the male and female population sub-counts fall 100 short of the printed total of 7,194."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagashima_upper_p162_left",
   "sequence": 814,
   "domain_canonical": "長島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長島藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagashima",
   "image": "images/upper_p162_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 162,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "二百九十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（長島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview Table, Fascicle Four (Nagashima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nagashima domain kokudaka deductions and net totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of PDF page 162, printed page 299, continues the fascicle-4 land account of Nagashima domain (長島藩, Ise) and carries no maru-marker, so every column on it belongs to Nagashima. It closes a deduction list of five lines — 込高 2,771.09251 koku, 無地高 428.964 koku, an unlabelled 73.188 koku of river-head new paddy breached by a storm tide and now lost land, 永引 2,822.0715 koku, and an unlabelled 2,287.983 koku of flood-damaged ground being written off by annual instalments — whose printed subtotal 小以 of 8,383.29901 koku the five entries reproduce to the last 才. Under the heading 差引當時 the net assessment 正殘高 stands at 9,918.41899 koku; a separately administered holding within Suenoe (周准) District in Kazusa Province is entered at 6,893.6576 koku, less 506.95047 koku of 無地高, leaving 正高 6,386.70713 koku, and the two net figures sum exactly to the grand total 正高〆 of 16,305.12612 koku. The last column carries only the heading 平均, whose figures run on to the following page."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagashima_upper_p163_right",
   "sequence": 815,
   "domain_canonical": "長島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長島藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagashima",
   "image": "images/upper_p163_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 163,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（長島）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration at a Glance, Fascicle Four (Nagashima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nagashima tax receipts, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of PDF 163 in the upper volume, printed book page 300, continues the fascicle-four entry for Nagashima domain in Ise. No maru-marker appears on the sheet: the ○長島藩 marker stands on the preceding PDF page and the next marker, ○成羽藩, opens on the facing left-hand page, so every column here belongs to Nagashima. The domain reports a regular land tax of 18,098 bales 1 to 5 sho 8 go 2 shaku 2 sai, a miscellaneous tax of 244 bales 2 sho 8 go in rice plus 518 ryo 3 bu 11 monme 7 fun 9 rin in cash, 1,653 commoner households (1,586 farming and 67 merchant) noted as lying within the lands administered in Ise Province, and 8,070 commoner residents (7,794 farmers, 3,829 male and 3,965 female; 276 merchants, 137 male and 139 female). Five narrow columns then count the religious and outcaste populations separately from that total: one Shinto priest household with 3 persons, 27 temples with 142 persons (82 monks and 60 women), 10 hermitages with 15 persons (4 monks and 11 nuns), one Shugendo household with 4 persons, and 7 hinin-ban watch households with 34 persons."
  },
  {
   "id": "nagashima_upper_p163_left",
   "sequence": 816,
   "domain_canonical": "長島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "長島藩",
   "domain_en": "Nagashima",
   "image": "images/upper_p163_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 163,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（成羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (Nariwa)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Nagashima's Kazusa branch territory, temple lands, outcaste and retainer counts; opening of the Nariwa block",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 301 completes the fascicle-4 return for 長島藩 (Nagashima, Ise) and then opens the return for 成羽藩 (Nariwa, Bitchū). The Nagashima columns record 30 eta households with 133 persons (64 male, 69 female); a separately counted administered territory in Kazusa Province with 1,047 households and 5,604 persons (2,782 male, 2,822 female); 21 temples with 58 monks; 105 households and 494 persons on temple lands; 147 shizoku households with 652 persons; 123 sotsu households with 502 persons; 38 light-sotsu households with 53 persons; and 8 shrines. The maru-marker ○成羽藩 then begins Nariwa's block, which on this page carries only the kusadaka heading and the figure 12,746.20731 koku, with an interlinear note giving the five-year average land-tax rate as roughly 30.5 percent. Every male-plus-female pair on the page sums exactly to its printed total, and Nariwa's own household, population and retainer figures follow on printed page 302."
  },
  {
   "id": "naegi_upper_p164_left",
   "sequence": 817,
   "domain_canonical": "苗木藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "苗木藩",
   "domain_en": "Naegi",
   "image": "images/upper_p164_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 164,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（苗木）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Four (Naegi)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Naegi domain land yield, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf opens the Hansei ichiran entry for Naegi Domain (苗木藩) in Mino province, fascicle four of the 1870 Dajokan survey. Under the kusadaka heading the domain's assessed yield is 14,780.9022 koku, against an actual rice revenue (genseki) of 4,434.276 koku plus a further 482.1013 koku booked as interest on rice lent out in the domain's former territory; the printed total is 4,916.4073 koku, which exceeds the sum of those two components by 0.03 koku. The demographic block records 3,955 households and 23,748 people (12,425 male, 11,323 female). Within that population the page itemises 112 shizoku households with 608 people, 76 sotsu households with 333 people, 22 outcaste households with 171 people (18 eta and 153 hinin), and 22 shrine-family households with 96 people."
  },
  {
   "id": "nanokaichi_upper_p165_right",
   "sequence": 818,
   "domain_canonical": "七日市藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "七日市藩",
   "domain_en": "Nanokaichi",
   "image": "images/upper_p165_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 165,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（七日市）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Four (Nanokaichi)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Land assessment and tax revenue (fascicle 4)",
   "page_summary_en": "This right-hand page of fascicle four opens the block for Nanokaichi domain (七日市藩) in Kōzuke and carries, to the right of its marker, the last three fields of the preceding Naegi (苗木) block: 15 temples with 44 clergy and no nunneries or married-priest temples, 33 villages, and one platoon of troops plus 50 raw recruits to be added to the ranks after selection. For Nanokaichi the table prints a nominal assessed yield of 10,014 koku and a gross assessment (草高) of 11,113.28 koku including newly registered holdings, followed by an 内 (\"of which\") pair of 3,078.04235 koku in rice and 1,822,425.666 mon in cash. The regular land tax, given as a five-year average from kinoe-ne to tsuchinoe-tatsu (1864 to 1868), is 2,138.6802 koku of rice together with 1,746,137.17 mon of cash reckoned as 218.26733 koku of rice, for a printed total of 2,356.94733 koku; miscellaneous taxes over the same five years average 105.4402 koku. The cash-to-rice conversion works out at almost exactly 8,000 mon per koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "muramatsu_upper_p167_left",
   "sequence": 819,
   "domain_canonical": "村松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "村松藩",
   "domain_en": "Muramatsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p167_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 167,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（村松）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Muramatsu)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Muramatsu tax receipts, commodity levies and household/status counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This page completes the Muramatsu domain entry in fascicle four, carrying over from the facing recto. The five-year-average rice revenue of 20,125.65227 koku is split into land tax (正租) of 20,052.09367 koku and miscellaneous tax (雜稅) of 73.5586 koku, first as a small breakdown at the gutter edge and then again as full-size fields; the domain also reports 315 ryō 3 shu in service silver from the lands it administered and 3,743,682 mon in levies on its products, which are listed as lead, tea, striped cotton cloth, raw silk, osmunda fern and whetstone. The household series counts 367 shizoku, 457 sotsu, 6,716 peasant, 17 shrine-attendant, 63 temple, 31 yamabushi and 4 hermitage households, summing exactly to the printed total of 7,655. The shizoku population is given as 1,785 persons, divided into 846 men and 939 women."
  },
  {
   "id": "muramatsu_upper_p168_right",
   "sequence": 820,
   "domain_canonical": "村松藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "村松",
   "domain_en": "Muramatsu",
   "image": "images/upper_p168_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 168,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（村松）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (Muramatsu)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Muramatsu population by status, outcaste households, and shrines",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-4 population return for Muramatsu domain in Echigo and carries no maru-marker, so every entry belongs to Muramatsu. It records the remaining status groups: 2,102 sotsu (991 male, 1,111 female), 32,609 peasants (16,467 male, 16,142 female), 110 shrine personnel, 218 Buddhist clergy, 152 mountain ascetics and 4 hermitage residents, under a printed subtotal of 36,980 persons that also absorbs the status rows carried over from the preceding leaf. A supplement headed 外 then lists the outcaste population separately — 2 hinin households holding 8 people and 26 eta households holding 196 people, 28 households and 204 persons in all. The grand total is 37,184 persons, and the domain is credited with 335 Shinto shrines."
  },
  {
   "id": "muraoka_upper_p168_left",
   "sequence": 821,
   "domain_canonical": "村岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "邨岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Muraoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p168_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 168,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（邨岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Muraoka)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Muramatsu's military corps roster and the opening of Muraoka's land-and-tax entry",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand page of fascicle four closes the Muramatsu (村松藩) entry and opens that of Muraoka (邨岡藩). For Muramatsu it prints 129 villages, with the district assignment left undetermined, followed by a parenthesised roster of eight corps: Enryū 480 men in eight platoons, Kosho 180 in three, Gyobu 180 in three, Hōrai 56 in one, Daiha 50, the Central Force 75, Scouts 32 and the Reserve 49, which sum exactly to the printed total of 1,102 men. Left of the circle-marker Muraoka's land figures begin with an assessed 草高 of 11,000 koku plus 10.4728 koku of dragon-year (1868) newly opened paddy, giving a combined 合高 of 11,010.4728 koku. Its five-year average land tax, stated in hulled rice, is 3,628.2955 koku; the 內 breakdown of that figure is cut off at the page edge and continues overleaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "muraoka_upper_p169_right",
   "sequence": 822,
   "domain_canonical": "村岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "邨岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Muraoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p169_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 169,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（邨岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle 4 (Muraoka)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Muraoka land tax, miscellaneous taxes, rice and cash totals, products, household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-4 revenue entry for Muraoka domain (printed 邨岡藩), the small Yamana barony in Tajima; no maru-marker appears anywhere on the page, so every column belongs to Muraoka. The land tax is given as a five-year average split into 1,800 koku paid in rice (米納) and 1,828.2955 koku paid in cash (金納), alongside dry-field rent and miscellaneous imposts (畠方雜租) of 249.334 koku valued at 6,291,040 mon, miscellaneous taxes on mulberry plots, dry fields and mountain and river land of 2,640,028 mon, and corvee money (夫錢) of 1,174,614 mon. The printed totals are 3,628.2957 koku of rice and 10,105,682 mon in cash, and the three cash components sum exactly to that cash total. The page closes with the domain's products — raw silk thread, silk floss and cattle, on which the survey records no cash tax — and household counts of 72 shizoku and 82 sotsu."
  },
  {
   "id": "muraoka_upper_p169_left",
   "sequence": 823,
   "domain_canonical": "村岡藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "邨岡藩",
   "domain_en": "Muraoka",
   "image": "images/upper_p169_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 169,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（邨岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Muraoka)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Muraoka households and population by status, with shrine tax-exempt land",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-four return for Muraoka domain, printed 邨岡 in the running header, on book page 313; no maru-marker appears, so the whole page belongs to the domain carried over from the facing page. The household block closes with 2,937 commoner households, 5 Shinto-priest households, 9 households of watchmen posted outside the villages, 12 temples and 38 outcaste households, against a printed grand total of 3,155 households that also absorbs the shizoku and sotsu households printed on the facing page. The 人員 population block then records 304 shizoku, 247 sotsu, 14,844 commoners, 5 shrine priests, 8 shrine maidens, 18 monks, 6 family members of Ikkō-sect clergy, 48 village watchmen and 188 outcastes, each with a male/female split that reconciles exactly with its own subtotal, though the printed 惣計 of 15,670 persons stands two above the 15,668 the components sum to. A heading for tax-exempt land held by shrines, temples and others follows, with shrine exempt land assessed at 2.3317 koku."
  },
  {
   "id": "uwajima_upper_p171_right",
   "sequence": 824,
   "domain_canonical": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_en": "Uwajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p171_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 171,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇和島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han System Overview, Fascicle Four (Uwajima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Uwajima's kokudaka, tax revenue and paper products, opening after the close of Mutsuura's population return",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 316 opens with the last five items of Mutsuura domain's return, carried over from page 315: 347 eta (176 male, 171 female), 19 hinin (12 male, 7 female), one kazoku household of three persons counted separately from the domain's 2,362 households, six districts holding thirty villages, and a single rifle platoon of sixty men with nine officers. The circle marker ○宇和島藩 then begins Uwajima domain (Iyo, Date house), assessed at a kusadaka of 100,000 koku with the komidaka noted as unknown. On a five-year average Uwajima's regular land tax came to 47,878.322 koku of actual rice and its miscellaneous taxes to 36,369 ryō 2 bu 2 shu plus 52.726 mon in ei, which the survey converts at eight ryō to the koku into 4,546.20971 koku, giving a grand total of 52,424.53171 koku. The products column begins with paper: 33,000 bundles of senka paper and 700 bundles of medium filter paper, a list that runs on across the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "uwajima_upper_p171_left",
   "sequence": 825,
   "domain_canonical": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_en": "Uwajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p171_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 171,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇和島）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran-hyō, Fascicle 4 (Uwajima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Uwajima products and tax figures",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-4 產物 (products) return for Uwajima Domain in Iyo province. Fifteen commodities are listed with quantities, among them 78,000 bundles of hanshi paper, 42,000 bundles of medium hoshi paper and 17,000 bundles of lower-grade sukigami; 1,000,000 kin of wax; 35,000 bales of white charcoal against 20,000 of black; and the dried marine exports 50,000 kin of squid, 3,000 kin of abalone and 1,500 kin of sea cucumber. The list closes with the cash value of the tax on the foregoing, 25,215 ryō 2 bu. A second heading, 諸税數大圖, then opens a summary of the various tax figures, under which four levies in kind are recorded: 2,124 kin of tea, 133 bundles of paper-mulberry wood, 44 kan 602.607 momme of silk floss and 918 kan 228.5 momme of hemp fibre."
  },
  {
   "id": "uwajima_upper_p172_right",
   "sequence": 826,
   "domain_canonical": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇和島",
   "domain_en": "Uwajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p172_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 172,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇和島）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Four (Uwajima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Uwajima dues in kind and their cash reckoning",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues fascicle four of the Hansei Ichiran for Uwajima domain, recording dues rendered in kind and then the cash entries that follow them. Six commodities are entered: firewood 145 bundles, rice bran 40 koku, yard matting 1,701 sheets, straw 11,042 bundles, bracken-fibre rope 505 bundles, and katsu straw 235 bundles; a note then values that whole list at 1,600 ryō in cash. A separate cash item of 9,554 ryō 2 shu together with 52.726 mon in ei-sen follows, carrying an internal sub-amount of 555 ryō 3 bu 1 shu with 60.17 mon. A thirty-character note enumerates fourteen trades — carpenters, plasterers, sawyers, coopers, tatami-makers, shingle-roofers, tile-burners, stonecutters, blacksmiths, small-rope makers, cloth-stretchers, dyers, ship-carpenters and day-labourers — and the licence silver entered beneath it is 89 ryō 3 shu with 18.536 mon. No maru-marker appears anywhere on the leaf, so every column belongs to Uwajima."
  },
  {
   "id": "uwajima_upper_p173_right",
   "sequence": 827,
   "domain_canonical": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_en": "Uwajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p173_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 173,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇和島）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, fascicle four (Uwajima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Uwajima mountain and timber levies, the grand total of money revenue, and the one-tenth household stipend",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-four fiscal return for Uwajima domain; no maru-marker appears, so the whole page belongs to Uwajima. It closes the cedar-mountain land tax carried over from the preceding page, then totals the mountain levies, timber-wholesaler levies, mountain-duty silver, the one-percent shipping fee and the hallmarked-silver cash at 1,426 ryō 1 shu together with 54.97 mon of Eiraku cash. The grand total of the domain's money revenue is 36,369 ryō 2 bu 2 shu plus 52.726 mon, of which 3,636 ryō 3 bu 3 shu plus 30.273 mon — exactly one tenth, and the division reconciles to the last 毛 — is set aside as the household stipend. The five-year average yield in kind is 119,695 bales 3 to 2 sho 2 go of rice and beans at four to to the bale, and the money figure of 36,369 ryō 2 bu 2 shu with 52.726 mon is restated at the left edge of the leaf as a fresh item whose closing label runs onto the next page."
  },
  {
   "id": "uwajima_upper_p173_left",
   "sequence": 828,
   "domain_canonical": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_en": "Uwajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p173_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 173,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（宇和島）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Regulations Overview, Fascicle 4 (Uwajima)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Uwajima stipend outlays, household and population totals, status breakdown",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf closes the fascicle-4 return for Uwajima domain (Iyo province). It first totals the domain's products and taxes, then names the two items charged to hereditary house stipends: 11,969.2322 bales of rice and beans, and 3,636 ryō 3 bu 3 shu in gold together with 30.273 mon in ei-copper cash. It then gives the domain's civil registration: 33,253 households and 169,512 persons. Within those totals the return itemises 548 shizoku households (1,309 men, 1,337 women), 970 sotsu households (2,020 men, 2,006 women), 150 shrine households (398 shrine attendants, 10 shrine maidens, 403 women), and 194 temples (444 monks, 17 women)."
  },
  {
   "id": "uwajima_upper_p174_right",
   "sequence": 829,
   "domain_canonical": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇和島藩",
   "domain_en": "Uwajima",
   "image": "images/upper_p174_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 174,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十二",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（臼杵）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Administration, Fascicle 4 (Usuki)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Uwajima commoner households by status; Usuki entry opens",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of the leaf close the Uwajima entry in fascicle 4 by tabulating commoner households by status: 29,301 farmer households (78,217 men, 73,589 women), 1,334 townsman households (2,232 men, 2,088 women), 622 eta households (2,253 men, 2,149 women), 317 mountain-ascetic households (454 ascetics, 426 women) and 17 hinin households (86 men, 74 women), together with 149 shrines and 121 halls. A note states that districts and villages are not itemised, and a bracketed line records 683 infantry in twelve companies and 241 artillerymen. The ○臼杵藩 marker then opens the Usuki entry, whose first figures are a nominal yield (草高) of 50,060-odd koku with the included yield left unitemised and taken from the yield schedule, and a five-year average actual yield (現石) of 35,271.50897 koku. The running header names Usuki even though most of the data printed on the leaf still belongs to Uwajima."
  },
  {
   "id": "usuki_upper_p174_left",
   "sequence": 830,
   "domain_canonical": "臼杵藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "臼杵藩",
   "domain_en": "Usuki",
   "image": "images/upper_p174_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 174,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（臼杵）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (Usuki)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Usuki tax revenue, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Usuki domain entry in fascicle 4 of the Hansei Ichiran, with no maru-marker on the page: the tax figures and the household and population figures all belong to Usuki. The domain reported regular land tax (正租) of 32,104.2692 koku of actual rice and miscellaneous tax (雜税) of 2,790.3072 koku, plus a cash component of 3,015 ryō 1 bu 3 shu and 180 mon in chōsen copper, which the compilers converted at 8 ryō per koku into 376.93257 koku of rice. Usuki counted 15,849 households and 77,827 people in all, of whom 860 households and 3,741 people were shizoku, 760 households and 3,129 people were sotsu, 14,091 households and 69,941 people were commoners, and 48 households and 265 people were Shinto priestly families. The status list breaks off after the priestly households at the foot of the page, leaving 90 households and 751 people unaccounted for against the printed totals."
  },
  {
   "id": "usuki_upper_p175_right",
   "sequence": 831,
   "domain_canonical": "臼杵藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "臼杵藩",
   "domain_en": "Usuki",
   "image": "images/upper_p175_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 175,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（上田）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Ueda)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Usuki clergy, shrine and outcaste populations; opening of Ueda's yield and tax entries",
   "page_summary_en": "The right two-thirds of the page closes the fascicle-four return for Usuki domain in Bungo: 58 temple households holding 410 clergy (3 of them nuns) together with 36 male and 129 female lay household members, 618 shrines, 32 shugen (mountain-ascetic) households totalling 176 people (77 male, 99 female), 259 eta (128 male, 131 female) whose household count the return marks as unknown, 43 hinin households totalling 183 people (90 male, 93 female), and 2 kazoku, namely the governor and his wife. A parenthetical line gives Usuki 900 troops, and a further note records that districts and villages were not entered in the return. The maru-marker ○上田藩 then opens Ueda domain in Shinano, whose first four columns give a nominal assessed yield of 53,000 koku, an additional 7,120.7015 koku of newly registered reclaimed land with no included yield, and a five-year average regular tax of 22,102.11344 koku of actual rice."
  },
  {
   "id": "ueda_upper_p175_left",
   "sequence": 832,
   "domain_canonical": "上田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "上田",
   "domain_en": "Ueda",
   "image": "images/upper_p175_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 175,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（上田）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Table Four (Ueda)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Ueda miscellaneous and product tax receipts",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf, printed book-page 325, continues the Ueda domain entry in fascicle four of the Hansei Ichiran and carries no maru-marker, so every figure on it belongs to Ueda. The first block, headed 雜稅 (miscellaneous taxes), reports 309.29896 koku of hulled rice, 133,314.151 mon in ei-cash, 3,018 ryō 3 bu 3 shu in gold, and 212,932.4 mon in copper cash, followed by a note assigning those receipts to raw silk, silkworm eggs, paper, mulberry-field licence fees, the kuchimai surcharge rice, and other minor imposts. The second block, headed 諸雜稅幷物産稅 五ヶ年平均 (five-year average of the various miscellaneous taxes together with the product tax), reports 298.06895 koku of rice, 8 ryō 2 bu 3 shu in gold, 133,291.151 mon in ei-cash, and 86,588 mon in copper cash; a printed brace ties all four of those columns to an interlinear note naming mulberry-field licence fees, cut fields, thicket and woodland, and other miscellaneous tax revenue. A cursive 〆 closes the entry before the running header in the left margin."
  },
  {
   "id": "ueda_upper_p176_right",
   "sequence": 833,
   "domain_canonical": "上田藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "上田藩",
   "domain_en": "Ueda",
   "image": "images/upper_p176_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 176,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十六",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（上田）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Ueda)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Ueda domain households and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-4 return for Ueda domain (上田藩) in Shinano. It closes the cash-tax entry with 3,010 ryō 1 bu in gold, 23 mon in ei-currency and 175 mon in copper cash, glossed by a bracketed marginal note stating that these are the dues on producers and dealers in raw silk and kuchi-ito silk, in silkworm eggs, and in other sundry taxed items. It then records domain totals of 11,519 households and 62,572 persons and breaks the population down by status: 429 samurai households (1,886 persons), 391 sotsu households (1,744), 52 Shinto-priest households (236), 103 temples (208), 40 shugendō households (151) and 10,393 commoner households (57,108). The male and female sub-counts reconcile with every status total except the samurai line, where 879 men and 1,070 women sum to 1,949 against a printed 1,886, and the six status figures together fall 1,239 persons and 111 households short of the domain totals printed at the head of the page."
  },
  {
   "id": "utsunomiya_upper_p176_left",
   "sequence": 834,
   "domain_canonical": "宇都宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇都宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Utsunomiya",
   "image": "images/upper_p176_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 176,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇都宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Utsunomiya)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Utsunomiya assessed yield and five-year-average tax revenue",
   "page_summary_en": "The page opens with the closing fields of the preceding domain's fascicle-four entry — 108 eta households holding 894 people (448 male, 446 female), 3 hinin shelters holding 13 people (7 male, 6 female), a district-and-village count returned as \"not ascertained,\" and 327 troops — all of which fall to the right of the maru-marker and so belong to Ueda Domain. The marker ○宇都宮藩 then opens Utsunomiya's entry. Utsunomiya reports an original assessment (motodaka) of 70,850 koku against a current assessed yield (kusadaka) of 91,298.98025 koku, the latter noted as including supplementary komidaka. Under the heading \"five-year average,\" the domain returns a regular land tax of 15,808.511 koku of hulled rice plus 6,106,877.996 mon in cash, and miscellaneous taxes of 2,097.96311 koku of rice, 435,679.496 mon, and 193 ryō 2 bu 1 shu in gold."
  },
  {
   "id": "utsunomiya_upper_p177_right",
   "sequence": 835,
   "domain_canonical": "宇都宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇都宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Utsunomiya",
   "image": "images/upper_p177_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 177,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百二十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇都宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Administration, Fascicle Four (Utsunomiya)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Utsunomiya tax dues in grain and oil-seed, with the cash commutation notes",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues Utsunomiya Domain's fascicle-four return of dues received, listing eleven commodity and cash lines and two summarizing notes. The largest entries are soybeans at 639.54973 koku, barnyard millet at 338.49787 koku and perilla oil-seed at 241.91767 koku, and a note to their left records that these three items were taken in as substitute eiraku cash. A second group of six smaller lines follows — soybeans 8.23441 koku, perilla 3.99982 koku, coarse glutinous rice 8.4105 koku, unhulled rice 3.405 koku, fine glutinous rice 14.867 koku and unhulled rice 0.02 koku — closed by a note that rice was sent in substitute and the dues collected in substitute eiraku cash. At the head of the leaf stand two money lines carried over from the preceding page: silver of 4,290.009 monme and cash of 1,369,706 mon."
  },
  {
   "id": "utsunomiya_upper_p177_left",
   "sequence": 836,
   "domain_canonical": "宇都宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇都宮藩",
   "domain_en": "Utsunomiya",
   "image": "images/upper_p177_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 177,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百二十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇都宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 4 (Utsunomiya)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Households and population by status",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf carries the household and population return for Utsunomiya Domain in the fourth fascicle of the 1870 Hansei Ichiran survey. It opens with the two domain totals — 10,557 households and 59,908 persons — and then breaks the population down by status: 562 shizoku households (2,913 persons, 1,356 male and 1,557 female), 329 sotsu households (1,181 persons, 711 male and 470 female), and 8,774 commoner households (53,309 persons, 26,720 male and 26,589 female). A separate heading, 知事實家ヨリ引取候分, covers persons taken into the domain from the governor's natal house: 34 shizoku households (143 persons) and 8 sotsu households (25 persons). Six small religious and occupational categories close the page — 59 yamabushi, 8 blind persons, 1 monkey-handler, 2 shrine mediums, 7 zatō, and 4 novice monks. The listed status counts fall short of the two domain totals by 850 households and 2,256 persons, so the breakdown continues onto the following leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "utsunomiya_upper_p178_right",
   "sequence": 837,
   "domain_canonical": "宇都宮藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇都宮",
   "domain_en": "Utsunomiya",
   "image": "images/upper_p178_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 178,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百三十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第四（宇都宮）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Four (Utsunomiya)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Religious, kazoku and outcast-status households; shrine and temple buildings",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-four return for Utsunomiya Domain, covering the religious and marginal-status population and the domain's religious structures. It records 108 Shinto priestly (社家) households with a printed population of 474 — the reprint marks that figure with a compositor's sic sign, because the male and female sub-counts of 236 and 263 sum to 499 — together with 267 temples housing 198 residents (183 monks, 2 nuns, 10 male servants, 3 lay devotees), and a separately entered 475 temple-gate-front registered households holding 1,583 people. The status categories follow: 60 eta households (332 persons), 4 households of leprosy sufferers (38 persons), 2 hinin households (40 persons), 2 beggar households (9 persons), one licensed ritual dancer, and a single kazoku household of 7. The remainder of the page counts buildings — 997 shrines, 328 halls, 87 hermitages, 38 lodges, 10 sub-temples and 1 small pagoda — plus one priest's-residence plot and one post-horse freight weighing station."
  },
  {
   "id": "uto_upper_p179_left",
   "sequence": 838,
   "domain_canonical": "宇土藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "宇土藩",
   "domain_en": "Uto",
   "image": "images/upper_p179_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 179,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百三十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第四（宇土・延岡）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran-hyō, fascicle 4 (Uto · Nobeoka)",
   "table_number": 4,
   "page_topic": "Yields, retainer strength and religious buildings for Uto and Nobeoka",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf, printed book page 333 of fascicle 4, closes the Uto (宇土) entry and opens the Nobeoka (延岡) entry. Uto's assessed yield is 30,000 koku, with the survey-increase and included yields marked as unknown, and the compiler records that Uto's regular land tax, miscellaneous taxes, household count and population were all unavailable; the only figures given are its retainer strength — 159 samurai, 231 foot-samurai, 159 rank-and-file soldiers and 175 rural militia, totalling 724 men — and 15 shrine and temple buildings. Nobeoka follows with a base yield of 70,000 koku, an assessed yield of 81,815.07308 koku, and 10,499.82411 koku recorded as 前々出高, the yield added at the survey before last. The parenthesised military line at the far right of the sheet — 85 foot soldiers, 17 artillerymen, 102 in all — stands to the right of the ○宇土藩 marker and therefore closes the preceding Ushiku (牛久) entry rather than belonging to Uto."
  },
  {
   "id": "kuwana_upper_p186_left",
   "sequence": 839,
   "domain_canonical": "桑名藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "桑名藩",
   "domain_en": "Kuwana",
   "image": "images/upper_p186_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 186,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百四十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（桑名）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Kuwana)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kuwana domain: assessed yield, land and miscellaneous taxes, households",
   "page_summary_en": "This verso opens the Kuwana domain (桑名藩) entry in fascicle 5 of the 1870 Hansei ichiran, the maru-marker giving its nominal enfeoffment as 60,000 koku. The survey then records a gross assessed yield (草高) of 60,560.325 koku including newly reclaimed fields, a regular land tax (正税) of 27,871.3234 koku of rice plus 610 ryō 1 bu in cash with 141.4 mon in ei-currency, and a fixed-rate (定免) assessment of 22,825.901 koku against that tax. Miscellaneous taxes (雑税) come to 46.221 koku of rice and 102 ryō in cash, together with 132.33 mon in ei and 324 kan 113.6 mon of levied copper coin, of which 5.253 koku is the fixed annual payment. Households number 13,624, and the 内 that closes the page introduces the status-by-status breakdown carried onto the following recto. The two columns printed to the right of the maru-marker — a governor's household of 8 persons (2 male, 6 female) and a declaration of no warships — close the preceding entry for Kurume domain (久留米藩)."
  },
  {
   "id": "kuwana_upper_p187_right",
   "sequence": 840,
   "domain_canonical": "桑名藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "桑名藩",
   "domain_en": "Kuwana",
   "image": "images/upper_p187_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 187,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百四十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（桑名）",
   "page_header_en": "Survey of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Kuwana)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kuwana population by status, with temple, shrine and outcaste household counts",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the fascicle-five return for Kuwana domain (桑名藩) at printed page 348, and carries no maru-marker, so every column belongs to Kuwana. It records a total population of 64,848 (32,714 male, 32,134 female), of which the return itemises seven non-commoner statuses: 7,086 shizoku and sotsuzoku living in 1,726 households, 113 shrine personnel in 21 priestly households, 728 temple personnel (362 monks, 11 nuns, 50 laymen, 305 laywomen), 58 Shugendō practitioners, 30 hall residents, 429 eta in 95 households, and 204 ban-hinin in 44 households. The religious establishments number 114 temples, 15 Shugendō temples, 22 halls and 24 shrines. Two editorial notes flag variant manuscripts — one gives 113 temples and another 160, and one gives 27 shrines rather than 24 — and both add that these figures date from the period when the domain was still assessed at 100,000 koku, before its post-Boshin reduction."
  },
  {
   "id": "kuroishi_upper_p189_left",
   "sequence": 841,
   "domain_canonical": "黒石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "黑石藩",
   "domain_en": "Kuroishi",
   "image": "images/upper_p189_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 189,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十三",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（黑石）",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — Kuroishi (黑石藩)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "kokudaka breakdown and land-tax totals for Kuroishi domain",
   "page_summary_en": "This half-page continues the fascicle-5 fiscal entry for Kuroishi domain (黑石藩), a Tsugaru branch house in Mutsu; no domain marker appears on the leaf, and the running header names Kuroishi as the block's owner. Under the heading 內譯 the assessed yield is itemised into a base holding (本高) of 4,000 koku, 6,260.2 koku divided off from the Hirosaki main house (本家ゟ分割), and 2,991.685 koku of newly reclaimed and re-assessed paddy (新田改出高), for 13,251.885 koku in all. The tax columns then give a regular land tax (正稅) of 7,015.363 koku of rice plus 67 ryō and 730 ei-mon in cash, and miscellaneous taxes (雜稅) of 1,083.156 koku — labelled 小物成米 — plus 602 ryō and 1 kan 211 ei-mon; the printed combined total (正雜稅合計) of 8,098.519 koku and 670 ryō 941 ei-mon reconciles exactly with those components. A final entry records the hereditary house stipend (家祿) at 890.852 koku and 67 ryō 94 ei-mon, and the 1928 collator notes in the margin that those two lines were written outside the ruled columns of the original manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "kuroishi_upper_p190_right",
   "sequence": 842,
   "domain_canonical": "黒石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "黑石",
   "domain_en": "Kuroishi",
   "image": "images/upper_p190_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 190,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（黑石）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 5 (Kuroishi)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kuroishi households, population by status, villages and shrines",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Kuroishi-han entry in fascicle 5 of the Hansei ichiran. No maru-marker appears anywhere on the page, and the running header reads 藩制一覽表第五（黑石）, so every column belongs to Kuroishi. The domain is credited with 2,629 households — of which 178 shizoku, 165 sotsu, 6 shrine households and 21 temple-and-hermitage households are itemised — and a population of 15,932, split 8,115 male and 7,817 female. The itemised status groups are 1,094 shizoku (518 male, 576 female), 747 sotsu (377 male, 370 female), 39 shrine personnel (23 male, 16 female) and 119 clergy and their household members (84 male, 35 female), with a further 26 chūgen and komono servants recorded 外ニ, outside the sotsu count. The page closes with 51 villages, 6 shrines, and a parenthetical editorial note that the original manuscript did not record the governor's family."
  },
  {
   "id": "kuroishi_lower_p202_left",
   "sequence": 843,
   "domain_canonical": "黒石藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "黑石藩",
   "domain_en": "Kuroishi",
   "image": "images/lower_p202_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol2",
   "pdf_page": 202,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百八十一",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第九（黑石、黑羽）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 9 (Kuroishi, Kurobane)",
   "table_number": 9,
   "page_topic": "Domain officer roster (fascicle 9)",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle 9 of the Hansei ichiran prints each domain's officer roster, and this half-leaf (book page 381) carries the whole of Kuroishi's alongside the tail of Kururi's and the opening line of Kurobane's. The four name columns at the right edge complete Kururi's six acting senior councillors — two were printed on the facing half-leaf, four here (Terada Chūhei, Hirosawa Kichirō, Murata Sōtarō, Shinozaki Ryūzō) — and are followed by Kururi's junior councillorship, printed 二人（一人）, two posts with only one name given, and its acting junior councillor Masuda Rensō. Kuroishi, opened by the ○黑石藩 marker, records one governor (no name printed), one senior councillor (Sasaki Osamu), two acting senior councillors (Karaushi Kosui and Karaushi Tōri), one junior councillor (Osaka Seiitsu) and two acting junior councillors (Sakaki Shigetoshi and Yamazaki Den), then closes with 兵隊未詳 — its troop strength not recorded. Kurobane's block begins at the far left with its own ○ marker and the bare label 知事, its figures continuing on the following half-leaf."
  },
  {
   "id": "kujira_upper_p191_left",
   "sequence": 844,
   "domain_canonical": "櫛羅藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "櫛羅",
   "domain_en": "Kujira",
   "image": "images/upper_p191_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 191,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十七",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五（櫛羅）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Overview, Fascicle Five (Kujira)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Land tax and miscellaneous tax totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This left-hand leaf closes the fascicle-5 tax entry for Kujira domain (Yamato province, Nagai house). The printed table gives miscellaneous taxes of 197.925 koku of rice, 735.5 ryō in gold, and 48.29 ei-mon in copper. The editor then warns that the next ten lines were written in red ink in the margin of the original manuscript, and those lines carry a fuller account: regular land tax of 4,205.75568 koku, miscellaneous-tax rice of 329.875 koku, cash of 115 ryō 1 bu 3 shu plus 5.6 ei-mon, that cash converted to 19.24052 koku of rice, and a grand total of 4,554.8712 koku, which is the exact sum of the three rice figures. A closing caveat records that the cash was converted either at six ryō or at five ryō one bu to the koku — the second rate would yield 21.98916 koku instead — and that the compiler could not determine which rate was correct."
  },
  {
   "id": "kujira_upper_p192_right",
   "sequence": 845,
   "domain_canonical": "櫛羅藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "櫛羅藩",
   "domain_en": "Kujira",
   "image": "images/upper_p192_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
