   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百五十八",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（黒川）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions Survey, Fascicle 5 (Kurokawa)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kujira household and population returns; Kurokawa entry opens with its kokudaka",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes the fascicle-5 return for Kujira Domain (Yamato) and opens the return for Kurokawa Domain. Kujira reports 519 households and 2,273 persons, broken down into 104 samurai households (406 persons), 36 sotsu households (114), 2 shrine-priest households (30), 353 eta households (1,582) and 24 enbo households (99); the household figures sum exactly to 519, and the population figures sum to 2,273 once the 42 residents of the domain's 40 Buddhist temples are added, the temples themselves being marked 算外, outside the household count. The domain also returns 68 Shinto shrines, and a parenthetical records four members of the governor's family (two male, two female) counted separately. Left of the ○黒川藩 marker, Kurokawa's entry begins with a kokudaka of 11,839.1099 koku, annotated as covering honden, shinden, the komidaka increment and granted lands, followed by an editor's note that the next three lines stand in vermilion in the original manuscript."
  },
  {
   "id": "kurokawa_upper_p192_left",
   "sequence": 846,
   "domain_canonical": "黒川藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "黑川藩",
   "domain_en": "Kurokawa",
   "image": "images/upper_p192_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 192,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "三百五十九",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（黑川）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle Five (Kurokawa)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Kurokawa domain land assessment, five-year average tax, households, population, shrines and temples",
   "page_summary_en": "Printed page 359 continues the fascicle-five return for Kurokawa domain in Echigo; the ○黑川藩 marker and the domain's kusadaka of 11,839.1099 koku stand on the facing page 358. A parenthetical note carried over from that page — flagged there by the editor as originally written in red ink — itemises the additions inside that assessment: 15.4044 koku of komidaka and 1,823.7055 koku of resurveyed new paddy plus direct dry-field and paddy increase, which together come to 1,839.1099 koku above a 10,000-koku base. This page then records a write-off of 452.2004 koku for wasteland and sundry heads, a two-entry total of 12,291.3103 koku, and a remainder of 11,386.9095 koku, followed by the five-year average tax take of 4,542.2632 koku in regular land tax and 205.8296 koku in miscellaneous taxes, 4,748.0928 koku in all as the gendaka. It closes with 2,022 households and 9,757 people (4,891 male, 4,866 female), 149 shrines and 16 temples, the temple population given as 25 men with the women unrecorded."
  },
  {
   "id": "yagyu_upper_p198_right",
   "sequence": 847,
   "domain_canonical": "柳生藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "柳生藩",
   "domain_en": "Yagyū",
   "image": "images/upper_p198_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 198,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（柳生）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei ichiran, Table Five (Yagyū)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yagyū domain land assessment, taxes, households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "Fascicle five of the Hansei ichiran for Yagyū, a 10,000-koku domain in Yamato, whose holdings the page places in Soekami and Yamabe districts and inside Sōraku district in Yamashiro. The survey reports a surveyed yield (草高) of 9,593.75198 koku, a regular land tax (正税) of 5,779.38599 koku, and a miscellaneous tax (雑税) of 998.735 monme of silver, which the page itself converts to 16 ryō 2 bu 2 shu plus 20.583 mon at the stated rate of 60 monme to the ryō. Households number 1,394 across 22 villages — 110 of them shizoku and 31 sotsu — with 25 shrines and 36 temples counted apart from that total, and a note explains that the households and persons of the villages attached to the domain's mortuary temple were reckoned separately and added in. The population is given as 6,858, of whom 413 are shizoku (211 men, 202 women); the printed male and female figures for the whole domain, 3,099 and 3,005, fall 754 short of the stated total."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamagami_upper_p199_left",
   "sequence": 848,
   "domain_canonical": "山上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山上藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamagami",
   "image": "images/upper_p199_left.jpg",
