   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（山上）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Yamagami)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Yamagami land assessment, five-year average taxes, and household total",
   "page_summary_en": "This page closes the survey block of the preceding domain and opens that of Yamagami (山上藩), a small Ōmi holding whose maru-marker ○山上藩 stands in the middle of the leaf. To the right of the marker the earlier domain's last three entries print: its governor's family is recorded as 不記 (not entered), its 穢多 population as 14 persons (8 male, 6 female), and its prison-house guards as 6 persons, a total the printed male-female split of 6 and 2 does not reconcile with. Left of the marker Yamagami's own figures begin: a base assessment (草高) of 13,043.928 koku plus 429.62194 koku of newly opened and reassessed paddy (込高), summed on the page to 13,473.54994 koku. The five-year averages that follow give a regular land tax (正租) of 4,474.18528 koku of rice and miscellaneous taxes (雑税) of 423.17692 koku of rice, 18 ryō in gold, and 564.83 mon in eiraku cash, against 2,168 households; the household breakdown opens with 内 at the left edge and continues on the facing page."
  },
  {
   "id": "yamagami_upper_p200_right",
   "sequence": 849,
   "domain_canonical": "山上藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "山上藩",
   "domain_en": "Yamagami",
   "image": "images/upper_p200_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
