   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "三百七十四",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覧表第五 (山家)",
   "page_header_en": "Domain Survey (藩制一覧表), Fascicle 5 — running head reads \"Yamaga\" (山家), but the figures on this leaf close out the previous domain, Yamagami (山上藩): households by status, population by status and sex, shrines, districts and villages",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "households, population by status and sex, shrines, districts and villages",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf completes the fascicle-5 social-structure block for Yamagami domain (山上藩, Ōmi province, whose 草高 of 13,043.988 koku and 2,168 households are recorded on the facing page). It counts 9,769 people in all — 4,987 male and 4,782 female — and breaks that total down by status: 276 shizoku in 84 households, 78 sotsu in 17 households, 48 monks and 8 nuns attached to 43 temples, 3 hermitages and 1 Gyōnin-sect house, 6 shrine attendants in 4 shrine households, and 524 eta in 112 households. The eta figure reconciles only when the single monk printed beneath the sex split is added: 278 men plus 245 women plus 1 monk. The domain's territory is given as 7 districts and 37 villages with 88 shrines, 46 of them branch shrines. The last column is the maru-marker ○山家藩, opening the block for the next domain, Yamaga."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuo_upper_p212_left",
   "sequence": 850,
   "domain_canonical": "松尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松尾藩",
