   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Hansei Ichiran, Fascicle 5 (Matsuo)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsuo domain: village-reported assessed yield, regular and miscellaneous tax receipts, and totals",
   "page_summary_en": "This page continues the fascicle-5 fiscal entry for Matsuo domain (Kazusa province). It opens with the qualifier \"according to the statement submitted by the villages\" and gives an assessed yield of 53,228.77292 koku, then divides the domain's receipts into regular land tax (正租: 12,942.576 koku of rice, 1,492 kan 275 mon 2 bu in ei-cash, 15 kan 391 mon in copper cash) and miscellaneous taxes (雑税: 401.693 koku of rice, 646 kan 520 mon 4 bu in ei-cash, 127 kan 119 mon in copper cash), plus two payments in kind, 0.312 koku of rapeseed and 214 bales 3 to 5 sho 3 go of salt. The closing 合計 line totals 13,344.269 koku of rice and 2,138 kan 795 mon 6 bu of ei-cash, and both reconcile exactly with the printed components; the copper-cash total of 142 kan 514 mon exceeds its two components by 4 mon, a discrepancy internal to the source. No maru-marker appears on the leaf, so every column belongs to Matsuo."
  },
  {
   "id": "matsuo_upper_p213_right",
   "sequence": 851,
   "domain_canonical": "松尾藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "松尾藩",
   "domain_en": "Matsuo",
   "image": "images/upper_p213_right.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 213,
   "page_side": "R",
   "book_page": "四百",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第五（松尾）",
   "page_header_en": "Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle Five (Matsuo)",
   "table_number": 5,
   "page_topic": "Matsuo domain households and population",
   "page_summary_en": "This leaf continues the Matsuo Domain entry in fascicle five of the Hansei Ichiran, with no domain marker on the page: the two rightmost columns close the domain's product list at 0.312 koku of tea seed and 214 bales of salt, after which the household and population returns begin. Matsuo reports 9,224 households in all, of which 350 are warrior (士族) houses, 330 are foot-soldier (卒族) houses, 238 are temples, 36 are watchman-outcast houses, 4 are mountain-ascetic houses and 3 are eta houses; Shinto priestly houses are entered as 不詳, not ascertained. The population stands at 47,724, split 24,971 male and 22,743 female, with 1,644 persons in warrior families (804 male, 840 female), 953 in foot-soldier families (533 male, 420 female) and 216 in clerical households (213 male, of whom 191 are ordained monks, and 3 female). The male and female figures for every status group sum correctly to their own totals, but the domain-wide male and female counts fall ten persons short of the printed population total, an inconsistency in the source itself rather than a transcription error."
  },
  {
   "id": "tsuruga_upper_p216_left",
   "sequence": 852,
   "domain_canonical": "敦賀藩",
   "domain_hi_name": "敦賀",
   "domain_en": "Tsuruga",
