   "image": "images/upper_p045_left.jpg",
   "volume": "vol1",
   "pdf_page": 45,
   "page_side": "L",
   "book_page": "六十五",
   "page_header_kanji": "藩制一覽表第一（西大路）",
   "page_header_en": "Han Institutions at a Glance, Table (fascicle) One — (Nishiōji)",
   "table_number": 1,
   "page_topic": "Tail of Niimi han's fascicle-1 return, then the opening of Nishiōji han's",
   "page_summary_en": "This left half-leaf (printed page 65) carries the end of Niimi han's fascicle-1 return and the start of Nishiōji han's. Right of the ○西大路藩 marker, Niimi's figures run: a combined samurai subtotal of 341 households and 1,204 people (642 male, 562 female), which matches the 124 shizoku and 217 sotsu households printed on the facing page; a domain total of 3,071 households and 15,126 people (7,904 male, 7,222 female); 132 outcaste (eta) households with 594 people; 22 villages; 181 shrines with 41 shrine-servant households totalling 203 people; 63 temples with 71 monks and 10 nuns; and 8 Shugendō households with 31 people. Left of the marker, Nishiōji's entry opens with a nominal assessed yield of 17,004.5 koku, a supplementary yield of 39.1725 koku, a five-year-average land tax of 6,862 koku, and 2,261 households with 9,106 people, of which 225 samurai-class households. The parenthetical breakdown of that last figure — 85 shizoku and 125 sotsu households — sums to 210 rather than 225, a discrepancy printed in the source itself."
  }
 ]
}